terial on a material with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor version-used", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor pinned", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.latest-active default listing shows one entry per material after a mint, not the frozen history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.a STUB MaterialProxy over the versioned surface exercises every function through its exact signature", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.KeepCurrent — an identical save on a used version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a USED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNUSED version updates version 1 in place", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.MintNextVersion — a structure change of a USED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.MintNextVersion — a structure change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.removeSample on a sample with a used version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.removeSample on a sample with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.removeSample succeeds when no version is in use, then the id is unknown", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.removeSample succeeds when no version is pinned, then the id is unknown", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.latest-active default listing shows one entry per sample after a mint, not the frozen history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.a STUB SampleProxy over the versioned surface exercises every function through its exact signature", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.a sample layer keeps resolving its pinned material version after the material mints a newer one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests.pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.boundVersions collects the versioned bindings of the setup (samples yes, presets no)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.versionRefs collects the versioned bindings of the setup (samples yes, presets no)", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a bound version appears in versionsInUse and BLOCKS removal of that sample", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.pinning an experiment's bound sample version BLOCKS removal of that sample", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.editing a USED sample version mints the next version instead of rewriting it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.editing a PINNED sample version mints the next version instead of rewriting it", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.committing from a scene captures the ordered chain including the detector kind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and DataFilePath attachments", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Lifecycle.decideVersioning", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Lifecycle.VersionUsage", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"], "preserves_obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Lifecycle.usageOf", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"], "preserves_obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.boundVersions", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"], "preserves_obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.versionsInUseSeam", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S22-PIN"], "preserves_obligations": ["S22-PIN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories"}
{"number": 66, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.2b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [65], "how_to": "The two store suites become contract suites that any store runs (001 §C 'Contract tests': each library proxy's suite runs against the in-memory store AND SQLite `:memory:`; .spec-md §9). This step moves facts and adds no store; every fact keeps its name and its assertions, except the one named in (1). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs`: `[<AbstractClass>] type MaterialProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshProxy : unit -> MaterialProxy`, a store holding the Built-in catalogue's materials over which no fact removes a sample-referenced material, and `abstract composedProxies : unit -> ReferencingSamples * MaterialProxy`, a store holding the Built-in catalogue's materials whose removal consults the Built-in catalogue's samples. The test-local record `ReferencingSamples = { activeSampleIds : unit -> SampleId list; removeSample : SampleId -> unit }` is the two things the facts do to those samples; a removal that fails, fails the fact. `proxyWithPinned` (step 65) becomes a member over `freshProxy` that pins through `pinMaterialVersion`. These 22 facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `listMaterials ActiveOnly returns the seeded built-in entries with distinct ids`; `searchMaterials with the empty query matches every seeded entry`; `searchMaterials filters by name fragment case-insensitively`; `searchMaterials dispersion facets partition the library`; `tryGetMaterial hits a known id and misses a minted one`; `resolveVersion hits version 1 of a seed, misses a non-existent version, and misses an unknown id`; `saveMaterial on a new id inserts version 1 active — appears in listing and resolves at v1`; `saveMaterial rejects a blank name as InvalidMaterial and persists nothing`; `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a physics change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a physics change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `latest-active default listing shows one entry per material after a mint, not the frozen history`; `markMaterialInactive hides an entry from the offers yet keeps it resolvable, and markMaterialActive revives it`; `supersedeMaterial behaves as inactive — hidden from offers, present under include-inactive, resolvable by version`; `the lifecycle verbs reject an unknown id with a diagnostic reason`; `removeMaterial on a material referenced by seeded samples is blocked and leaves the store unchanged`; `removeMaterial on a material with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor pinned`; `the referencing lookup is live — removing the referencing sample unblocks the material`; `a MaterialProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)`; `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`. `removeMaterial on a material referenced by seeded samples is blocked and leaves the store unchanged` asserts that `activeSampleIds ()` still holds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`, where it asserted that `listSamples ActiveOnly` answered `Ok`. `type MaterialProxyTests () = inherit MaterialProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store: `freshProxy` is `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])`, and `composedProxies` builds `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()`, `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (samplesReferencing samples)` and `ReferencingSamples` over that samples store. The facts over no store stay members of `MaterialProxyTests` alone: `a STUB MaterialProxy over the versioned surface exercises every function through its exact signature`; `referencedMaterials covers films, repeated cells, the substrate plate, and the lower half-space`; `referencedMaterialVersions keeps every referenced material version, a repeated cell once`. The values the facts share (`glass`, `otherPhysics`, `glassPhysicsChanged`, `glassRenamed`, `v1Id`, `v2Id`, `minted`) move unchanged into a private module above the classes. (2) `CategoryProxyTests.fs` likewise: `[<AbstractClass>] type CategoryProxyContract ()` declares `abstract stores : unit -> CategoryProxy * MaterialProxy`, a category store holding the Built-in catalogue's categories and a materials store holding its materials, whose entries the category store's removal consults. Its facts are `the real store add/rename/remove of an unreferenced user category round-trips with fixed Guids`; `the real store rejects a duplicate add — a seeded built-in id and a re-added user id`; `the real store rejects a blank-name add and update as InvalidCategory and persists nothing`; `the real store renames a built-in category — built-ins ARE renamable`; `the real store rejects updateCategory and removeCategory on an unknown id`; `the real store refuses to remove a built-in category and leaves the store unchanged`; `the real store blocks removeCategory on a user category a material references and leaves both stores unchanged`; `the referencing lookup is live — removing the referencing material unblocks the category`; the first six use only the category store. `type CategoryProxyTests () = inherit CategoryProxyContract ()` answers `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore (materialsReferencingCategory materials)` over `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])`, which the six facts that built `categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` read alike, because no Built-in material is in a user category. Its own facts are `a CategoryProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)`; `a STUB CategoryProxy over a fixed category list exercises all four functions through their exact signatures`; `a STUB CategoryProxy surfaces CategoryStillReferenced when a user category is in use`; `a category resolves by id and by name through the list it is given`. (3) The in-memory classes keep the names `MaterialProxyTests` and `CategoryProxyTests`, so every fact keeps its id: xUnit v3 reports an inherited fact under the concrete class that runs it. The abstract contracts hold no discoverable test of their own and get no `ADD_TEST`. Both files keep their compile positions, so no project file changes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MaterialProxyContract` and `CategoryProxyContract` MUST be abstract classes holding the store facts, `MaterialProxyTests` and `CategoryProxyTests` MUST be their in-memory subclasses, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every MaterialProxyTests and CategoryProxyTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.removeMaterial on a material referenced by seeded samples is blocked and leaves the store unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-CONTRACT-SUITES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories"}
{"number": 67, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.2c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [65], "how_to": "The versioned history of one entry, read and written in one place that every SQLite library store calls (001 §C 'Versions are immutable', 'Hybrid shape'; .spec-md §5 `LibraryDbContext`). In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (steps 62-64), after step 64's members, a type extension on `LibraryDbContext` whose members each carry step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark. They run inside `LibraryDatabase.run` (step 62), which catches every exception. They stage changes on the context and never save, so a store ends its `run` with one `SaveChanges ()` and an operation's writes land together or not at all. (1) Reads, every row read through `toStoredVersion` (step 63), whose failure is answered: `tryLatestStored (id : LibraryEntryId) : Result<StoredEntryVersion option, StorageError>`, the version the entry's `LatestVersion` row names, `None` without that row; `tryStoredVersion (id : LibraryEntryId) (version : VersionNumber) : Result<StoredEntryVersion option, StorageError>`, whatever its lifecycle; `storedVersionsOf (id : LibraryEntryId) : Result<StoredEntryVersion list, StorageError>`, ascending by version; and `latestStoredOfKind (kind : LibraryEntryKind) : Result<StoredEntryVersion list, StorageError>`, the latest version of every entry of the kind, in no promised order. (2) Writes: `stageVersion (stored : StoredEntryVersion) : Result<unit, StorageError>` adds the version's row (`versionRow`, step 63), or overwrites every column of the tracked row holding its id and version, and makes the version's facet and sample-material rows exactly its envelope's `facetRows` and `sampleMaterialRows` (step 64); `stageLatest (id : LibraryEntryId) (version : VersionNumber) : unit` makes the entry's `LatestVersion` row name the version, adding the row when absent; and `stageRemoval (id : LibraryEntryId) : unit` removes the entry's latest row and every version row, whose facet, sample-material and pulled-source rows the cascade removes (step 60). (3) The version rule's outcomes, so no store re-implements them: `stageNewEntry (content : LibraryEntryContent) : Result<unit, StorageError>` seals the content (`sealed`, step 30) and stages it as its entry's version and latest under `{ lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned }`; `stageEdit (latest : StoredEntryVersion) (decision : VersionDecision) (content : LibraryEntryContent) : Result<unit, StorageError>` takes the edited value's content at the latest's version and stages nothing for `KeepCurrent`, the sealed content under the latest's state for `MutateInPlace`, and for `MintNextVersion` the sealed `{ content with version = latest.envelope.content.version.next }` under `{ ActiveEntry; VersionUnpinned }`, made the latest. No cache, retry, query option or other member is added. (4) The fixture. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains `freshLibraryDatabase () : LibraryDatabase`: a new `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\")` holding every envelope of `catalogueData ()` as its version 1 and latest under `{ lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned }`, staged through `stageVersion` and `stageLatest` in one `run`. An error fails the calling fact with its `describe`; the caller disposes the database. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.2. (5) Facts, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`, each disposing what it opens. (a) `the fixture library database holds every Built-in entry as its version 1 and latest`: for each kind of `LibraryEntryKind.all`, `latestStoredOfKind` answers exactly the ids of the catalogue's envelopes of that kind, each version 1, equal to its envelope, active and unpinned; and `tryLatestStored` of a test-local GUID answers `None`. (b) `staging a version overwrites its row and its relational rows, and the latest names the staged version`: `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s version 1, restaged pinned with the `SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId` structure (its content resealed), answers pinned through `tryStoredVersion` and has exactly the langasite and silicon sample-material rows at version 1; a renamed version 2 of `MaterialIds.silicon`, staged with `stageLatest`, is what `tryLatestStored` answers, while `tryStoredVersion` of version 1 still answers the catalogue's envelope and `storedVersionsOf` answers versions 1 and 2 in order. (c) `stageEdit keeps, mutates or mints exactly as its decision says`: over Silicon's latest, `KeepCurrent` changes no row; `MutateInPlace` of a renamed Silicon rewrites version 1 under its state and its `BuiltInProvenance`; `MintNextVersion` of a further renamed Silicon adds version 2, active and unpinned, as the latest; and `stageNewEntry` of a test-local material's content makes its version 1 the latest. (d) `staging a removal deletes every version of the entry and its relational rows`: after (b)'s version 2, `stageRemoval` of Silicon leaves no version, latest or facet row of it, while every other entry keeps its latest row.", "acceptance": "After the operations land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the fixture library database holds every Built-in entry as its version 1 and latest`, `staging a version overwrites its row and its relational rows, and the latest names the staged version`, `stageEdit keeps, mutates or mints exactly as its decision says` and `staging a removal deletes every version of the entry and its relational rows`; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.the fixture library database holds every Built-in entry as its version 1 and latest", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-ROW-OPERATIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.staging a version overwrites its row and its relational rows, and the latest names the staged version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-ROW-OPERATIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.stageEdit keeps, mutates or mints exactly as its decision says", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-ROW-OPERATIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.staging a removal deletes every version of the entry and its relational rows", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-ROW-OPERATIONS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories"}
{"number": 68, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.2d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain"], "depends_on": [65], "how_to": "Before a second materials store exists, the in-memory store's version payload and refusal texts become members that both stores call (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'; .spec-md §6). A move: every text and the payload stay exactly as they are. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs`, above the store: `MaterialMetadata` (`MaterialStore.fs:MaterialMetadata`) becomes public, with a one-line doc, and `type MaterialEntry with member this.versionPayload : VersionPayload<MaterialComplexity, MaterialMetadata>` replaces the store's local `payloadOf`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`, where every holder of these texts can reach them: directly after `MaterialError`, `type MaterialError with` gains `static member unknownMaterial (id : MaterialId) : MaterialError` (`unknown material id '<id>'`, the text both the in-memory store's local `unknown` and `MaterialLibrary.fs:resolveMaterialWithDisp` build today, so both call it) and `static member stillReferenced (entry : MaterialEntry) (samples : EntryName list) : MaterialError` (quoting and sorting the names as `removeMaterial` does); beside step 65's `unknownMaterialVersion`, `static member versionsPinned (entry : MaterialEntry) (versions : VersionNumber list) : MaterialError` (step 65's pinned refusal). The in-memory store and `resolveMaterialWithDisp` call them and build no refusal text themselves. Each doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.2. No behaviour, message or fact changes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MaterialStore.fs` MUST declare `MaterialEntry.versionPayload`, `MaterialLibrary.fs` MUST declare `unknownMaterial`, `stillReferenced` and `versionsPinned` on `MaterialError`, and neither the in-memory store nor `resolveMaterialWithDisp` MUST build a refusal text of its own; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories"}
{"number": 69, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S2.2e", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0001", "name": "MaterialProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [66, 67, 68, "STORE_XDUO_0001"], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests"], "how_to": "The materials store over the library database (001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`', 'Hybrid shape'; .spec-md §0.2 Storage row, §4 'Errors and IO'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `MaterialError` gains `MaterialStoreUnavailableErr of reason : string`, the store beneath the proxy failed, carrying the failure's `describe`, because no case names a database failure. Every complete match on `MaterialError` gains it: `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:MaterialError.caption`, the library-error arm of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:runFailureCaption`, and `CatalogueImport.fs`'s material reason (step 37). The `MaterialProxy` doc names `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase` beside the in-memory store. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs`, `module MaterialDatabaseStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type MaterialProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : MaterialProxy`, unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` (ELEV019), carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite materials store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]`. Every field is one `database.run` over step 67's operations, ends a write with one `SaveChanges ()`, and answers every `StorageError`, and every `LibraryEntryError` a decoder answers, as `MaterialStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. An entry is a material when its latest row's kind is `MaterialEntryKind`; an id held by another kind is no material. The fields: `listMaterials scope` decodes (`toMaterialEntry`, step 25) the latest version of every material, `ActiveOnly` keeping those whose state is `ActiveEntry`, sorted by id as the in-memory map lists them; `searchMaterials q` is `byQuery q` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:byQuery`) over `listMaterials ActiveOnly`'s entries; `tryGetMaterial id` decodes the latest version; `resolveVersion mvid` decodes the named version, whatever its lifecycle; `saveMaterial entry` runs `entry.validate` first, then with no version under the id stages `stageNewEntry` of `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry VersionNumber.first UserProvenance entry`, so a material first saved here is a user entry; under an entry of another kind it answers `DuplicateMaterialIdErr` naming the id and that kind's `extension`; otherwise it stages `stageEdit` of the latest with the `decideVersioning` of the latest entry's `versionPayload` and `entry.versionPayload` over the latest's pin (steps 65, 68) and `ofMaterialEntry` at the latest's version under the latest's provenance, which an edit keeps; `markMaterialInactive`, `markMaterialActive` and `supersedeMaterial` restage the latest version with `InactiveEntry`, `ActiveEntry` and `InactiveEntry`, or answer `unknownMaterial`; `pinMaterialVersion mvid` restages the named version `VersionPinned`, or answers `unknownMaterialVersion`; `removeMaterial id` answers `unknownMaterial` without a material, then `stillReferenced` naming each sample whose latest version is `ActiveEntry` and holds a sample-material row naming the material at any version, as `samplesReferencing` (`ElementId.fs:samplesReferencing`) reads the active samples, each read through `toStoredVersion` and `toSample` for its name; then `versionsPinned` naming its pinned versions (`storedVersionsOf`); else it stages `stageRemoval`. Every refusal but the cross-kind `DuplicateMaterialIdErr` is a member of steps 65 and 68. No cache, retry, second connection or provenance other than the stored one and `UserProvenance` is added, and no product root composes the store in this section (`AppContext.create` composes the database stores in S2.4, .spec-md §0.1). (3) Tests, in `MaterialProxyTests.fs`: `type MaterialProxySqliteTests () = inherit MaterialProxyContract ()` runs every contract fact (step 66) over `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase` of a `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67) per store. `ReferencingSamples` lists the ids of the active latest sample entries (`latestStoredOfKind SampleEntryKind`) and removes one by `stageRemoval` and `SaveChanges` through `run`. The class implements `IDisposable` and disposes every database it opened. Its own facts: `a material first saved through the database store is a user entry, and an edit keeps the stored provenance`: read through `run` and `tryLatestStored`, a minted material saved once is version 1 under `UserProvenance`; Silicon renamed keeps version 1 under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`; and Silicon pinned, then given the Langasite complexity, has version 2 as its latest, unpinned, under the same provenance. `a database failure below the materials store is MaterialStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers `Error (MaterialStoreUnavailableErr _)`.", "acceptance": "After the database store lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every MaterialProxyContract fact under `MaterialProxySqliteTests` and its own `a material first saved through the database store is a user entry, and an edit keeps the stored provenance` and `a database failure below the materials store is MaterialStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 24; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.listMaterials ActiveOnly returns the seeded built-in entries with distinct ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.searchMaterials with the empty query matches every seeded entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.searchMaterials filters by name fragment case-insensitively", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.searchMaterials dispersion facets partition the library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.tryGetMaterial hits a known id and misses a minted one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.resolveVersion hits version 1 of a seed, misses a non-existent version, and misses an unknown id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.saveMaterial on a new id inserts version 1 active — appears in listing and resolves at v1", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.saveMaterial rejects a blank name as InvalidMaterial and persists nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.MutateInPlace — a physics change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.MintNextVersion — a physics change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.latest-active default listing shows one entry per material after a mint, not the frozen history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.markMaterialInactive hides an entry from the offers yet keeps it resolvable, and markMaterialActive revives it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.supersedeMaterial behaves as inactive — hidden from offers, present under include-inactive, resolvable by version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.the lifecycle verbs reject an unknown id with a diagnostic reason", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.removeMaterial on a material referenced by seeded samples is blocked and leaves the store unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.removeMaterial on a material with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor pinned", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.the referencing lookup is live — removing the referencing sample unblocks the material", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.a MaterialProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.a material first saved through the database store is a user entry, and an edit keeps the stored provenance", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.a database failure below the materials store is MaterialStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.MaterialDatabaseStore.MaterialProxy.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-MATERIALS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories"}
{"number": 70, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.2f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain"], "depends_on": [69], "how_to": "Before a second category store exists, the in-memory category store's refusal texts become members both stores call (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'; .spec-md §6). A move: every text stays as it is. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`, directly above the in-memory category store (`MaterialLibrary.fs:CategoryProxy.createInMemoryStore`'s augmentation), `type CategoryError with` gains `static member unknownCategory (id : CategoryId) : CategoryError` (the store's local `unknown`), `static member duplicateCategory (existing : MaterialCategory) : CategoryError` (the id already names `existing`), `static member builtInNotRemovable (category : MaterialCategory) : CategoryError` and `static member stillReferenced (category : MaterialCategory) (materials : EntryName list) : CategoryError` (quoting and sorting the names as `removeCategory` does). The store calls them and builds no refusal text itself. Each doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.2. No behaviour, message or fact changes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MaterialLibrary.fs` MUST declare `unknownCategory`, `duplicateCategory`, `builtInNotRemovable` and `stillReferenced` on `CategoryError`, and the in-memory category store MUST build no refusal text of its own; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories"}
{"number": 71, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S2.2g", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0003", "name": "CategoryProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [69, 70, "STORE_XDUO_0003"], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests"], "how_to": "The category store over the library database, with the built-in-not-removable rule read from the provenance (001 §C 'What it holds': categories; 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`'; .spec-md §0.2 Storage row). (1) `MaterialLibrary.fs`: `CategoryError` gains `CategoryStoreUnavailableErr of reason : string`, the category store beneath the proxy failed, carrying the failure's `describe`. Every complete match on `CategoryError` gains it: `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:CategoryError.caption` and `CatalogueImport.fs`'s category reason (step 37). The `CategoryProxy` doc names `CategoryProxy.createInDatabase` beside the in-memory store. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CategoryDatabaseStore.fs`, `module CategoryDatabaseStore`, compiled directly after `MaterialDatabaseStore.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type CategoryProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : CategoryProxy` carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite category store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]`. As in step 69, every field is one `run` over step 67's operations with one `SaveChanges ()` per write, and every `StorageError` or decoder `LibraryEntryError` is `CategoryStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. An entry is a category when its latest row's kind is `CategoryEntryKind`. The fields: `listCategories ()` decodes (`toMaterialCategory`) the latest version of every category, whatever its lifecycle, sorted by id as the in-memory map lists them; `addCategory c` runs `c.validate` first, answers `duplicateCategory` of the category already holding the id, `DuplicateCategoryIdErr` naming the id and the `extension` of another kind holding it, and otherwise stages `stageNewEntry` of `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialCategory VersionNumber.first provenance c`, where a `BuiltInCategory` is filed under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` (step 32, the one built-in catalogue) and a `UserCategory` under `UserProvenance`, because the origin derives from the provenance (step 24); `updateCategory c` runs `c.validate`, answers `unknownCategory` without a category, builds `ofMaterialCategory` at the latest's version under the latest's provenance, which an update keeps, so a category whose origin disagrees with that provenance is `InvalidCategoryErr` carrying the builder's `describe`, and stages `stageEdit` of the latest with the `decideVersioning` of the stored and the incoming category's `{ physics = visibility; metadata = name }` over the latest's pin; nothing pins a category in this section, so an update acts in place as the in-memory store's does; `removeCategory id` answers `unknownCategory` without a category, `builtInNotRemovable` when its decoded origin is `BuiltInCategory` (a built-in catalogue's entry is protected), and `stillReferenced` naming each material whose latest version, active or not, has the category, as `materialsReferencingCategory` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:materialsReferencingCategory`) reads `IncludeInactive`, read inside the same `run`; else it stages `stageRemoval`. Every refusal but the cross-kind `DuplicateCategoryIdErr` is step 70's member. No cache, retry or category pin verb is added. (3) Tests, in `CategoryProxyTests.fs`: `type CategoryProxySqliteTests () = inherit CategoryProxyContract ()` runs the contract's facts (step 66) over one `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` per fact, `stores` answering `CategoryProxy.createInDatabase` and `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase` (step 69) of it, and implements `IDisposable` to dispose it. Its own facts: `a category's provenance follows its origin, and an update keeps it`: read through `run` and `tryLatestStored`, a `UserCategory` added is version 1 under `UserProvenance`; a `BuiltInCategory` added is version 1 under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` and refuses `removeCategory` with `BuiltInNotRemovableErr`; Glass renamed keeps version 1 and its built-in provenance; and Glass updated with `origin = UserCategory` answers `InvalidCategoryErr` and leaves the row as it was. `a database failure below the category store is CategoryStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers `Error (CategoryStoreUnavailableErr _)`.", "acceptance": "After the database store lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every CategoryProxyContract fact under `CategoryProxySqliteTests` and its own `a category's provenance follows its origin, and an update keeps it` and `a database failure below the category store is CategoryStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 10; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CategoryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the real store add/rename/remove of an unreferenced user category round-trips with fixed Guids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the real store rejects a duplicate add — a seeded built-in id and a re-added user id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the real store rejects a blank-name add and update as InvalidCategory and persists nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the real store renames a built-in category — built-ins ARE renamable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the real store rejects updateCategory and removeCategory on an unknown id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the real store refuses to remove a built-in category and leaves the store unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the real store blocks removeCategory on a user category a material references and leaves both stores unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.the referencing lookup is live — removing the referencing material unblocks the category", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.a category's provenance follows its origin, and an update keeps it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests.a database failure below the category store is CategoryStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CategoryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CategoryDatabaseStore.CategoryProxy.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CategoryDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S22-SQLITE-CATEGORIES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.2 -- Pinned replaces VersionsInUse; SQLite materials and categories"}
{"number": 72, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain"], "depends_on": [65], "how_to": "Before a second samples store exists, the in-memory samples store's version payload, search filter and refusal texts become members that both stores call (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'; .spec-md §6; the S2.2 rule of steps 68 and 70). A move: every text, filter and payload stays exactly as it is. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/SampleStore.fs`, above the store: `SampleMetadata` (`SampleStore.fs:SampleMetadata`) becomes public, with a one-line doc, and `type Sample with member this.versionPayload : VersionPayload<SampleStructure, SampleMetadata>` replaces the store's local `payloadOf`: the structure is the physics, and the name, the description and the `SubstrateKind` facet are the metadata. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `SampleQuery` (`ElementId.fs:SampleQuery`) gains `member this.selectFrom (samples : Sample list) : Sample list`, the store's `searchSamples` filter moved whole: the samples whose name contains `text` case-insensitively (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`), then, when `substrate` is `Some`, those of that `SubstrateKind`, in the order given. Directly after `SampleError` (`ElementId.fs:SampleError`), `type SampleError with` gains `static member unknownSample (id : SampleId) : SampleError` (the store's local `unknown`, `unknown sample id '<id>'`), `static member unknownSampleVersion (version : SampleVersionId) : SampleError` (step 65's pin refusal, an `UnknownSampleIdErr` naming the id and the version as `v<n>`) and `static member versionsPinned (sample : Sample) (versions : VersionNumber list) : SampleError` (step 65's `SampleVersionPinnedErr`, naming the sample, its id, the count and the versions as `v1, v2`). (3) The in-memory store's `searchSamples` is `q.selectFrom` over its latest active samples, and the store builds no refusal text, filter or payload of its own. Each new doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.3. No behaviour, message or fact changes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `SampleStore.fs` MUST declare `Sample.versionPayload` over a public `SampleMetadata`, `ElementId.fs` MUST declare `SampleQuery.selectFrom` and `unknownSample`, `unknownSampleVersion` and `versionsPinned` on `SampleError`, and the in-memory samples store MUST build no refusal text, search filter or payload of its own; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SampleStore.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 73, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [65], "how_to": "The samples suite becomes a contract suite that any samples store runs (001 §C 'Contract tests': each library proxy's suite runs against the in-memory store AND SQLite `:memory:`; .spec-md §9), as step 66 did for materials. This step moves facts and adds no store; every fact keeps its name and its assertions. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs`: `[<AbstractClass>] type SampleProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshProxy : unit -> SampleProxy`, a store holding the Built-in catalogue's samples, each at version 1, active and unpinned. `proxyWithPinned` (step 65) becomes a member over `freshProxy` that pins through `pinSampleVersion`. These 21 facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `listSamples ActiveOnly returns the seeded samples with distinct ids`; `searchSamples with the empty query matches every seeded sample`; `searchSamples filters by name fragment case-insensitively`; `searchSamples filters by substrate kind, composing with the text facet`; `tryGetSample hits a known id and misses a minted one`; `resolveVersion hits version 1 of a seed, misses a non-existent version, and misses an unknown id`; `saveSample on a new id inserts version 1 active — appears in listing and resolves at v1`; `saveSample rejects a blank name as InvalidSample and persists nothing`; `saveSample rejects a structurally-empty sample (no films, no substrate) as InvalidSample even when named`; `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a structure change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `latest-active default listing shows one entry per sample after a mint, not the frozen history`; `markSampleInactive hides a sample from the offers yet keeps it resolvable, and markSampleActive revives it`; `supersedeSample behaves as inactive — hidden from offers, present under include-inactive, resolvable by version`; `the lifecycle verbs reject an unknown id with a diagnostic reason`; `removeSample on a sample with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeSample succeeds when no version is pinned, then the id is unknown`; `a SampleProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)`; `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`. `type SampleProxyTests () = inherit SampleProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store: `freshProxy` is `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()` (step 65). The facts over no samples store stay members of `SampleProxyTests` alone: `a Mirror's supportedEmission is unclearable: every candidate collapses to EmitReflectedOnly`; `a Plate is constrainable: clearing R via Emission.withReflected Placement.RayGroupOff leaves T on`; `a STUB SampleProxy over the versioned surface exercises every function through its exact signature`; `a sample layer keeps resolving its pinned material version after the material mints a newer one`; `defaultSupportedEmission pins a Mirror to EmitReflectedOnly; a ThinFilm and a Plate emit both`; `the seeded EUV multilayer is the one Mirror; seeded thin films and plates support both`; `validateSample accepts a Plate that carries a substrate and a non-blank name`; `validateSample leaves a ThinFilm with no substrate Ok`; `validateSample rejects a Plate whose structure.substrate is None as InvalidSample`. The values the facts share (`plate`, `otherStructure`, `platePhysicsChanged`, `plateRenamed`, `v1Id`, `v2Id`, `minted`, `emptyStructure`, `plateMissingSubstrate`) move unchanged into a private module above the classes. (2) The in-memory class keeps the name `SampleProxyTests`, so every fact keeps its id: xUnit v3 reports an inherited fact under the concrete class that runs it. The abstract contract holds no discoverable test of its own and gets no `ADD_TEST`. The file keeps its compile position, so no project file changes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `SampleProxyContract` MUST be an abstract class holding the 21 store facts and `SampleProxyTests` its in-memory subclass; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every SampleProxyTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 74, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S2.3c", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0002", "name": "SampleProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [67, 69, 72, 73, "STORE_XDUO_0002"], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests"], "how_to": "The samples store over the library database (001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`', 'Hybrid shape': the sample-version → material-version keys; .spec-md §0.2 Storage row, §4 'Errors and IO'), step 69's rule for samples. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `SampleError` gains `SampleStoreUnavailableErr of reason : string`, the store beneath the proxy failed, carrying the failure's `describe`, because no case names a database failure. Every complete match on `SampleError` gains it: `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:SampleError.caption` and `CatalogueImport.fs`'s sample reason (step 37). The `SampleProxy` doc names `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` beside the in-memory store. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs`, `module SampleDatabaseStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `CategoryDatabaseStore.fs` (step 71): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type SampleProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : SampleProxy`, unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` (ELEV019), carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite samples store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]`. Every field is one `database.run` over step 67's operations, ends a write with one `SaveChanges ()`, and answers every `StorageError`, and every `LibraryEntryError` a decoder answers, as `SampleStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. An entry is a sample when its latest row's kind is `SampleEntryKind`; an id held by another kind is no sample. The fields: `listSamples scope` decodes (`toSample`, step 25) the latest version of every sample, `ActiveOnly` keeping those whose state is `ActiveEntry`, sorted by id as the in-memory map lists them; `searchSamples q` is `q.selectFrom` (step 72) over `listSamples ActiveOnly`'s samples; `tryGetSample id` decodes the latest version; `resolveVersion svid` decodes the named version, whatever its lifecycle; `saveSample sample` runs `sample.validate` first, then with no version under the id stages `stageNewEntry` of `LibraryEntryContent.ofSample VersionNumber.first UserProvenance sample`, so a sample first saved here is a user entry; under an entry of another kind it answers `DuplicateSampleIdErr` naming the id and that kind's `extension`; otherwise it stages `stageEdit` of the latest with the `decideVersioning` of the latest sample's `versionPayload` and `sample.versionPayload` over the latest's pin (steps 65, 72) and `ofSample` at the latest's version under the latest's provenance, which an edit keeps. `stageVersion` (step 67) writes each staged version's sample-material rows from its structure's `referencedMaterialVersions` (steps 61, 64), so a saved, mutated or minted version keys exactly the material versions its own structure names. `markSampleInactive`, `markSampleActive` and `supersedeSample` restage the latest version with `InactiveEntry`, `ActiveEntry` and `InactiveEntry`, or answer `unknownSample`; `pinSampleVersion svid` restages the named version `VersionPinned`, or answers `unknownSampleVersion`; `removeSample id` answers `unknownSample` without a sample, then `versionsPinned` naming its pinned versions (`storedVersionsOf`), else it stages `stageRemoval`, whose cascade removes the sample-material rows (step 60). Nothing structural references a sample, so removal consults the pin alone, as the in-memory store does. Every refusal but the cross-kind `DuplicateSampleIdErr` is a member of step 72. No cache, retry, second connection or provenance other than the stored one and `UserProvenance` is added, and no product root composes the store in this section (`AppContext.create` composes the database stores in S2.4, .spec-md §0.1). (3) Tests, in `SampleProxyTests.fs`: `type SampleProxySqliteTests () = inherit SampleProxyContract ()` runs every contract fact (step 73) over `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` of a `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67) per store. The class implements `IDisposable` and disposes every database it opened. Its own facts: `a sample first saved through the database store is a user entry, and an edit keeps the stored provenance and keys the material versions of its own structure`: read through `run`, `tryLatestStored` and `tryStoredVersion`, a copy of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId`'s sample under `newSampleId ()` saved once is version 1 under `UserProvenance`; `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` renamed keeps version 1 under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`; pinned through `pinSampleVersion` and then given the `SampleIds.langasiteSiliconId` structure, it has version 2 as its latest, unpinned, under the same provenance, whose sample-material rows are exactly `MaterialVersionId.firstOf` of `MaterialIds.langasite` and `MaterialIds.silicon`, while version 1 keeps those of `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial`; and a sample saved under a test-local GUID that a material saved through `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase` (step 69) of the same database already holds answers `DuplicateSampleIdErr` naming `.material-json`. The GUID is bound once and wrapped where it is born, as a `MaterialId` and as a `SampleId`. `a database failure below the samples store is SampleStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers `Error (SampleStoreUnavailableErr _)`.", "acceptance": "After the database store lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every SampleProxyContract fact under `SampleProxySqliteTests` and its own `a sample first saved through the database store is a user entry, and an edit keeps the stored provenance and keys the material versions of its own structure` and `a database failure below the samples store is SampleStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 23; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.listSamples ActiveOnly returns the seeded samples with distinct ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.searchSamples with the empty query matches every seeded sample", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.searchSamples filters by name fragment case-insensitively", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.searchSamples filters by substrate kind, composing with the text facet", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.tryGetSample hits a known id and misses a minted one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.resolveVersion hits version 1 of a seed, misses a non-existent version, and misses an unknown id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.saveSample on a new id inserts version 1 active — appears in listing and resolves at v1", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.saveSample rejects a blank name as InvalidSample and persists nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.saveSample rejects a structurally-empty sample (no films, no substrate) as InvalidSample even when named", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.MintNextVersion — a structure change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.latest-active default listing shows one entry per sample after a mint, not the frozen history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.markSampleInactive hides a sample from the offers yet keeps it resolvable, and markSampleActive revives it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.supersedeSample behaves as inactive — hidden from offers, present under include-inactive, resolvable by version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.the lifecycle verbs reject an unknown id with a diagnostic reason", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.removeSample on a sample with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.removeSample succeeds when no version is pinned, then the id is unknown", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.a SampleProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.a sample first saved through the database store is a user entry, and an edit keeps the stored provenance and keys the material versions of its own structure", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests.a database failure below the samples store is SampleStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SampleProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SampleDatabaseStore.SampleProxy.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SAMPLES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 75, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [52], "how_to": "The user-sources facts of `SourceLibraryTests` become a contract suite that any user-sources store runs (001 §C 'Contract tests'; .spec-md §9; the S2.3 brief's 'proxy part of SourceLibraryTests'), as step 66 did for materials. This step moves facts and adds no store. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs`: the helper `userSource` takes `(id : ElementValueId)` in place of a `string`, so a fixture holds its id elevated where it is born (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'): each caller passes a text id as `ElementValueId \"<text>\"` and a minted one as `newSourceId ()` itself. `[<AbstractClass>] type SourceProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshSources : unit -> SourceProxy`, a user-sources store holding no user source. These two facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `the user-sources store inserts, replaces by id, and removes`; `the user-sources store refuses a blank name, a non-positive wavelength, and a protected source`. `the user-sources store inserts, replaces by id, and removes` saves its source under `newSourceId ()` where it used the text id `src-user-1`, because the database keys every entry by a GUID (001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'; step 20); its assertions are unchanged. `type SourceLibraryTests () = inherit SourceProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store: `freshSources` is `SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`. The other facts stay members of `SourceLibraryTests` alone: `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal`; `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`; `the live Library offers and resolves a user source after the seeded ones`; `the live Library resolves a sample created in the samples store`; `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`; `the seeded sources are protected, uniquely identified, and cover the lasers and the lithography lines`; `the seeded tree lists every seeded source under Sources`. The private helpers (`nm`, `userSource`, `sourceIds`) move unchanged into a private module above the classes. (2) The in-memory class keeps the name `SourceLibraryTests`, so every fact keeps its id. The abstract contract gets no `ADD_TEST`, and the file keeps its compile position.", "acceptance": "After the move, `SourceProxyContract` MUST be an abstract class holding the two user-sources store facts and `SourceLibraryTests` its in-memory subclass, and `SourceLibraryTests.fs` MUST NOT contain `src-user-1`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every SourceLibraryTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests.the user-sources store inserts, replaces by id, and removes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-SOURCE-SUITE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 76, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [67, 75], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests"], "how_to": "The user-sources store over the library database (001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`', 'Versions are immutable', 'Pinned replaces VersionsInUse'; .spec-md §0.2 Storage row, §4). User sources are versioned in the database while the proxy's surface stays unversioned, because an experiment binds a source by its entry id (`ElementId.fs:SourceProxy`): a save follows `decideVersioning` against the latest version's pin, and every read answers the latest version. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `SourceError` (`ElementId.fs:SourceError`) gains `SourceVersionPinnedErr of reason : string`, a removal refused while any version of the source is pinned (step 65's rule for materials and samples), and `SourceStoreUnavailableErr of reason : string`, the store beneath the proxy failed, carrying the failure's `describe`. Its one complete match, `SourceError.reason`, gains both, and `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:SourceError.caption` reads it unchanged. Directly after `SourceError`, `type SourceError with static member unknownSource (id : ElementValueId) : SourceError` holds the in-memory store's text (`unknown source id '<id>'`), which `SourceProxy.createInMemory`'s `removeSource` now calls; its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.3. The `SourceProxy` doc names `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` beside the in-memory store, says that `listSources` lists in creation order in memory and by name in the database, and names the two new refusals, which the in-memory store never answers because it holds no pin and no database. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SourceDatabaseStore.fs`, `module SourceDatabaseStore`, compiled directly after `SampleDatabaseStore.fs` (step 74): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type SourceProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : SourceProxy` carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite user-sources store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]`. As in step 69, every field is one `run` over step 67's operations with one `SaveChanges ()` per write, and every `StorageError` or decoder `LibraryEntryError` is `SourceStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. A user source is an entry whose latest row's kind is `SourceEntryKind` and whose provenance's `protection` (step 24) is `UserManaged`; a built-in source is a preset, which the preset store serves (`ElementId.fs:LibraryEntryStore`). The fields: `listSources ()` decodes (`toSourcePreset`, step 25) the latest version of every user source, whatever its lifecycle, because the surface has none, ordered by name and then by id; `tryGetSource id` answers `None` for an id that is no GUID (`ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24) or names no user source, else the decoded latest version; `saveSource source` runs `source.validate` first, so a blank name, a bad wavelength or a `ProtectedBuiltIn` source is refused exactly as today (`InvalidSourceErr`, `ProtectedSourceRefusedErr`); then an id that is no GUID is `InvalidSourceErr` naming it, because the database keys every entry by a GUID; an id held by a built-in source is `ProtectedSourceRefusedErr` naming that source; an id held by another kind is `InvalidSourceErr` naming the id and that kind's `extension`; with no version under the id it stages `stageNewEntry` of `LibraryEntryContent.ofSourcePreset VersionNumber.first UserProvenance source`; otherwise it builds `ofSourcePreset` at the latest's version under the latest's provenance and stages `stageEdit` of the latest with the `decideVersioning` of the stored and the incoming content's `{ physics = payload; metadata = name }` over the latest's pin, so a wavelength or tuning change of a pinned version mints the next version and a rename never versions; a builder refusal is `InvalidSourceErr` carrying its `describe`; `removeSource id` answers `unknownSource` without a user source under the id, then `SourceVersionPinnedErr` naming the source, its id and its pinned versions as `v1, v2` (`storedVersionsOf`), else it stages `stageRemoval`. No pin verb is added, because the proxy's surface stays unversioned. No cache, retry or provenance other than the stored one and `UserProvenance` is added. (3) Tests, in `SourceLibraryTests.fs`: `type SourceProxySqliteTests () = inherit SourceProxyContract ()` runs both contract facts (step 75) over `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` of a `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` per store, so the Built-in catalogue's protected sources are present and never listed, and implements `IDisposable` to dispose every database it opened. Its own facts: `a user source is versioned in the database, the proxy answers its latest, and a pinned source is not removable`: a user source saved under `newSourceId ()` is version 1 under `UserProvenance`, unpinned (read through `run` and `tryLatestStored`); with version 1 restaged pinned through `run` (`tryStoredVersion`, `stageVersion`, `SaveChanges`), a save with another wavelength makes version 2 the latest, unpinned, while `tryStoredVersion` of version 1 keeps the first wavelength; `tryGetSource` and `listSources` answer version 2's source; a rename then mutates version 2 in place, so no version 3 exists; and `removeSource` answers `SourceVersionPinnedErr` naming `v1`, after which `tryGetSource` still answers the source. `the database user-sources store holds user sources only and refuses an id it cannot hold`: a `UserManaged` source saved under `PresetIds.source600` answers `ProtectedSourceRefusedErr`, under `SampleIds.multilayerQwId.toElementValueId` `InvalidSourceErr` naming `.sample-json`, and under the test-local text id `not-a-guid` `InvalidSourceErr`; `tryGetSource PresetIds.source600` answers `Ok None`; `removeSource PresetIds.source600` answers `UnknownSourceIdErr`; and `tryLatestStored` of that preset still answers the catalogue's version 1 envelope. `a database failure below the user-sources store is SourceStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers `Error (SourceStoreUnavailableErr _)`.", "acceptance": "After the database store lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including both SourceProxyContract facts under `SourceProxySqliteTests` and its own `a user source is versioned in the database, the proxy answers its latest, and a pinned source is not removable`, `the database user-sources store holds user sources only and refuses an id it cannot hold` and `a database failure below the user-sources store is SourceStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SourceDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests.the user-sources store inserts, replaces by id, and removes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SOURCES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests.the user-sources store refuses a blank name, a non-positive wavelength, and a protected source", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SOURCES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests.a user source is versioned in the database, the proxy answers its latest, and a pinned source is not removable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SOURCES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests.the database user-sources store holds user sources only and refuses an id it cannot hold", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SOURCES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests.a database failure below the user-sources store is SourceStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SOURCES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SourceDatabaseStore.SourceProxy.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SourceDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-SOURCES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 77, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [58], "how_to": "Before a second preset store exists, the preset store's refusal gets a case of its own and a member both stores call (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy', 'Error DUs carry diagnostic payload'; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO'). `LibraryUnavailableErr` (`ElementId.fs:LibraryError`) says the Library could not be read, yet the in-memory preset store (`ElementId.fs:LibraryEntryStore`, built by the `createInMemory` that step 58 renamed) answers it for an id it already holds, as 'the only fitting existing case'. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: `LibraryError` gains `PresetRefusedErr of reason : string`, the preset store refused an entry, and `LibraryUnavailableErr`'s doc says the store beneath the proxy failed. Directly after `LibraryError`, `type LibraryError with static member entryAlreadyHeld (entry : LibraryEntry) : LibraryError` answers `PresetRefusedErr` with today's text (`library entry '<id>' is already present`), and the in-memory store's `addEntry` calls it; its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.3. The `LibraryEntryStore` and builder docs say a duplicate is `PresetRefusedErr`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: the library reason (step 37), the one complete match on `LibraryError`, gains the case, so an import's refused preset still answers `ImportRejectedErr` with the same reason. Any other complete match on `LibraryError` the build reports gains it the same way. (3) Tests. `LibraryProxyTests` gains `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds`: over `Library.createInMemory ()`, `addEntry` of `BuiltinCatalogue.preset` of `PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, `PresetIds.polarizerLp` and `PresetIds.source600` each answers `Ok ()`; `entriesForKind` answers exactly the detector for `Detector`, the polarizer for `LinearPolarizer` and the source for `LightSource`; `tryGetEntry` answers each for its id and `Ok None` for a fresh `newSourceId ()`; and a second `addEntry` of the detector answers `Error (PresetRefusedErr reason)` whose reason names its id, after which `entriesForKind Detector` still answers the one detector.", "acceptance": "After the case lands, `ElementId.fs` MUST declare `PresetRefusedErr` on `LibraryError` and `LibraryError.entryAlreadyHeld`, which the in-memory preset store calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-PRESET-REFUSAL"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 78, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [47, 77], "how_to": "The Library suite becomes a contract suite that any live Library and any preset store run (001 §C 'Contract tests' and 'the `LibraryProxy` live view, and the preset … stores'; .spec-md §9; the S2.3 brief: the preset store's contract lives in `LibraryProxyTests`), as step 66 did for materials. This step moves facts and adds no store. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs`: the test-local record `LiveLibraryStores = { library : LibraryProxy; samples : SampleProxy; sources : SourceProxy }` is a live Library with the samples and user-sources stores it composes. `[<AbstractClass>] type LibraryProxyContract ()` declares `abstract liveStores : unit -> LiveLibraryStores`, a live Library over stores holding the Built-in catalogue and no user source, and `abstract emptyPresetStore : unit -> LibraryEntryStore`, a preset store holding nothing. These 10 facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `entriesForKind Sample returns only SampleItems`; `entriesForKind Detector returns only DetectorItems`; `entriesForKind LinearPolarizer returns ONLY the ideal LP (not the CPs)`; `entriesForKind CircularPolarizer returns EXACTLY the two CP presets (not the LP)`; `tryGetEntry hits a known id and misses an unknown id`; `libraryTrees returns at least one tree and every leaf entry id resolves`; `every seeded sample round-trips store-lookup by its Guid entry id`; `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once`; `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds`; `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds`. The first 7 read `(this.liveStores ()).library` where they read the module-level `proxy` (`BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, step 52), so they prove the live view the composition roots build rather than the fixture's preset double; their assertions are unchanged. `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once` saves its user source and its sample through the record's `sources` and `samples` where it composed `liveLibrary` over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` itself; `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds` and `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds` (step 77) build their store with `emptyPresetStore ()`. `type LibraryProxyTests () = inherit LibraryProxyContract ()` is the in-memory composition: `liveStores` answers `liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples sources` over a new `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` and a new `SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`, with those `samples` and `sources`, as `AppContext.create` composes them (step 44), and `emptyPresetStore` is `Library.createInMemory ()`. The facts over no store stay members of `LibraryProxyTests` alone: `ElementId round-trips through its value accessor`; `a MINTED SampleId round-trips create-store-lookup through a proxy of the same shape`; `a STUB proxy of the same shape drives the same kind-constraint logic`; `a Sample entry's fullDescription is exactly its curated description`; `a non-Sample entry's fullDescription is prose built from its kind`; `every seeded entry has a non-empty fullDescription`; `expandedFilms mirrors RepeatBuilder.expand (count copies of the cell, order preserved)`; `forKinds maps each entry case to its valid catalogue kinds`; `the By kind tree groups entries by kind, then facet, then leaf`; `the seeded sample ids are distinct, non-empty Guids`. The module-level `proxy` goes. (2) The in-memory class keeps the name `LibraryProxyTests`, so every fact keeps its id. The abstract contract gets no `ADD_TEST`, and the file keeps its compile position.", "acceptance": "After the move, `LibraryProxyContract` MUST be an abstract class holding the 10 live-Library and preset-store facts and `LibraryProxyTests` its in-memory subclass; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every LibraryProxyTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.entriesForKind Sample returns only SampleItems", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-LIBRARY-SUITE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.entriesForKind Detector returns only DetectorItems", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-LIBRARY-SUITE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.entriesForKind LinearPolarizer returns ONLY the ideal LP (not the CPs)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-LIBRARY-SUITE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.entriesForKind CircularPolarizer returns EXACTLY the two CP presets (not the LP)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-LIBRARY-SUITE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.tryGetEntry hits a known id and misses an unknown id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-LIBRARY-SUITE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.libraryTrees returns at least one tree and every leaf entry id resolves", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-LIBRARY-SUITE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxyTests.every seeded sample round-trips store-lookup by its Guid entry id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S23-LIBRARY-SUITE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 79, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [74, 76, 78], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests"], "how_to": "The preset store and the live Library over the library database (001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`: … the `LibraryProxy` live view, and the preset … stores'; the S2.3 brief: the preset store holds detectors, polarizers and built-in sources; .spec-md §0.2 Storage row, §4). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/PresetDatabaseStore.fs`, `module PresetDatabaseStore`, compiled directly after `SourceDatabaseStore.fs` (step 76): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. (a) `type LibraryEntryStore with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : LibraryEntryStore` carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite preset store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]`. As in step 69, every field is one `run` over step 67's operations with one `SaveChanges ()` per write, and every `StorageError` or decoder `LibraryEntryError` is `LibraryUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. A preset is an entry whose latest row's kind is `DetectorEntryKind` or `PolarizerEntryKind`, or `SourceEntryKind` with a provenance whose `protection` is `ProtectedBuiltIn` (step 24); a user source belongs to the user-sources store (step 76) and a sample to the samples store (step 74). `proxy.entriesForKind kind` decodes (`toSourcePreset`, `toDetectorPreset`, `toPolarizerPreset`, wrapped as `SourceItem`, `DetectorItem`, `PolarizerItem`) the latest version of every preset whose state is `ActiveEntry`, keeps those whose `forKinds` holds the kind, and orders them by name and then by id; `proxy.libraryTrees ()` answers `[ LibraryTree.byKind offered ]` (step 47) over the active presets of every kind in that order; `proxy.tryGetEntry id` answers `None` for an id that is no GUID or names no preset, else the decoded latest version whatever its lifecycle, so a retired preset a table element binds still resolves (001 §B 'Mark `InactiveEntry` (still resolvable)'); `addEntry entry` answers `PresetRefusedErr` naming the entry for a `SampleItem` (the samples store keeps it) and for a `UserManaged` `SourceItem` (the user-sources store keeps it), then `LibraryError.entryAlreadyHeld` (step 77) when any entry holds the id, and otherwise stages `stageNewEntry` of `ofSourcePreset`, `ofDetectorPreset` or `ofPolarizerPreset` at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` (step 32, the one built-in catalogue) for a `ProtectedBuiltIn` preset and `UserProvenance` for a `UserManaged` one, because the protection derives from the provenance (step 24); a builder refusal is `PresetRefusedErr` carrying its `describe`. (b) `type LibraryProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : LibraryProxy` is `liveLibrary` (`ElementId.fs:liveLibrary`) over `(LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase database).proxy`, `SampleProxy.createInDatabase database` (step 74) and `SourceProxy.createInDatabase database` (step 76): the live view composed once, reusing `liveLibrary` and its derived tree (step 47) with no logic of its own; it calls no EF Core API, so it carries no boundary mark. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`: the `LibraryEntryStore` and `liveLibrary` docs name the database builders beside the in-memory store, in one line each. No cache, retry, lifecycle verb, protection rule or ordering option is added, and no product root composes the stores in this section (S2.4). (3) Tests, in `LibraryProxyTests.fs`: `type LibraryProxySqliteTests () = inherit LibraryProxyContract ()` runs the 10 contract facts (step 78): `liveStores` answers `LibraryProxy.createInDatabase`, `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` and `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` of one `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()`, and `emptyPresetStore` answers `LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase` of a new `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\")` (step 62). The class implements `IDisposable` and disposes every database it opened. Its own facts: `the database preset store keeps detectors, polarizers and built-in sources, filed under their provenance`: over an empty database, `addEntry` of a `BuiltinCatalogue.sample` entry and of a `UserManaged` source under `newSourceId ()` each answers `PresetRefusedErr` and stores nothing; a `UserManaged` copy of `PresetIds.polarizerLp` under a fresh GUID id (`newSourceId ()`, step 20) is stored under `UserProvenance` and the intensity detector under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` (read through `run` and `tryLatestStored`), and both are offered for their kinds; and a user source saved through `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` of the same database is neither offered for `LightSource` nor resolved by the preset store. `an inactive preset is not offered but still resolves`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()`, with `PresetIds.polarizerLp`'s latest version restaged `InactiveEntry` through `run`, `entriesForKind LinearPolarizer` answers `Ok []`, no leaf of the preset store's tree names it, and `tryGetEntry` still answers it. `the database live view offers a user source after the built-in sources and resolves it until it is removed`: over `LibraryProxy.createInDatabase` of `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()`, a user source saved through `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` of the same database is the last `LightSource` entry, after exactly the catalogue's built-in sources (compared as a set, because the database orders them by name), resolves through `tryGetEntry`, and no longer resolves once removed. `a database failure below the preset store is LibraryUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database, `entriesForKind`, `libraryTrees`, `tryGetEntry` and `addEntry` of the preset store each answer `Error (LibraryUnavailableErr _)`.", "acceptance": "After the database stores land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every LibraryProxyContract fact under `LibraryProxySqliteTests` and its own `the database preset store keeps detectors, polarizers and built-in sources, filed under their provenance`, `an inactive preset is not offered but still resolves`, `the database live view offers a user source after the built-in sources and resolves it until it is removed` and `a database failure below the preset store is LibraryUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 14; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/PresetDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.entriesForKind Sample returns only SampleItems", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.entriesForKind Detector returns only DetectorItems", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.entriesForKind LinearPolarizer returns ONLY the ideal LP (not the CPs)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.entriesForKind CircularPolarizer returns EXACTLY the two CP presets (not the LP)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.tryGetEntry hits a known id and misses an unknown id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.libraryTrees returns at least one tree and every leaf entry id resolves", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.every seeded sample round-trips store-lookup by its Guid entry id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.the database preset store keeps detectors, polarizers and built-in sources, filed under their provenance", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.an inactive preset is not offered but still resolves", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.the database live view offers a user source after the built-in sources and resolves it until it is removed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests.a database failure below the preset store is LibraryUnavailableErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.PresetDatabaseStore.LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/PresetDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.PresetDatabaseStore.LibraryProxy.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/PresetDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S23-SQLITE-PRESETS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 80, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.3i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [79], "how_to": "The catalogue import writes into the database stores as it writes into the in-memory doubles (the S2.3 brief: 'CatalogueImport (S1.6) writes into either'; 001 §B '`SeedingProxy` / `seedAll` become `CatalogueImport`: the same seam shape'; .spec-md §6 'Import seam'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: the four save adapters and the four reason matches move out of `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory` (step 40) into `static member ofStores (categories : CategoryProxy) (materials : MaterialProxy) (samples : SampleProxy) (presets : LibraryEntryStore) : CatalogueImportProxy`, unchanged: each save calls its store's write verb (`addCategory`, `saveMaterial`, `saveSample`, `addEntry`) and maps the store's error to `ImportRejectedErr` with its reason. `createInMemory ()` builds its four in-memory stores as today and answers `InMemoryCatalogueStores` whose `proxy` is `CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores` of them; its body keeps no adapter. The doc of `ofStores` is one to three lines: any four stores, the in-memory doubles or the database stores (spec 0050 S2.3). No field, bundle type or ordering is added, and no product root composes the database stores in this section (S2.4). (2) Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`: `importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores`: over a new `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\")`, `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` (steps 38, 40) of `CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores` over `CategoryProxy.createInDatabase`, `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase`, `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` and `LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase` of that database (steps 71, 69, 74, 79) answers `Ok ()`; each catalogue row's decoded value is then what the database stores answer for its id (`listCategories`, `tryGetMaterial`, `tryGetSample` and the preset store's `tryGetEntry`), compared with `=`, as `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value` (step 40) checks the in-memory stores; `latestStoredOfKind` (step 67) answers exactly one version 1 per catalogue row of each kind; and a second import answers `ImportRejectedErr`. The fact disposes the database.", "acceptance": "After the move, `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory` MUST build its proxy through `CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores` and hold no save adapter of its own; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S23-IMPORT-EITHER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S23-IMPORT-EITHER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.3 -- SQLite samples, sources, presets and the live library"}
{"number": 81, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.4a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [38], "how_to": "Every location the app reads gets one Domain shape and one set of defaults (001 §G 'Locations', 'Every path is overridable'; 001 §C 'Settings'; .spec-md §3.9, §5 `DataLocations`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`, module `WorkbenchSettings`, after the `WorkbenchSettings` record (`WorkbenchSettings.fs:87-101`), opening `Softellect.Sys.Primitives` for `ConnectionString` and `FolderName`, the types `AppSettingsProvider` reads and `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate` takes (step 62): the record `DataLocations = { libraryConnection : ConnectionString; backupsFolder : FolderName; preferencesFolder : FolderName; kitsFolder : FolderName; exportsFolder : FolderName; cataloguesFolder : FolderName; shippedCatalogueFolder : FolderName }`. Its doc is one to three lines: every location of 001 §G, each an `appsettings.json` key read once at the composition root (spec 0050 S2.4). Each field has a one-line doc: the library database's SQLite connection string; its `Backups` folder; the per-user preferences folder; the suggested parent of kit folders; the exports folder; the catalogue-export folder; the shipped catalogue. (a) `static member shippedCatalogueDefault : FolderName` is `FolderName \"Catalogue\"`, the shipped catalogue as a folder relative to the install folder (001 §G '`<install>\\Catalogue\\`'). (b) `static member defaultsUnder (documents : FolderName) : DataLocations` answers the 001 §G defaults as configured text, environment variables unexpanded, `documents` being the user's Documents folder the composition root passes: `libraryConnection` = `ConnectionString \"Data Source=%LOCALAPPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/library.db\"`; `backupsFolder` = `FolderName \"%LOCALAPPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Backups\"` (001 §G: `Backups\\` beside the database); `preferencesFolder` = `FolderName \"%APPDATA%/Softellect/Berreman/OpticalConstructor\"`; `kitsFolder`, `exportsFolder` and `cataloguesFolder` = `Optical Constructor/Kits`, `Optical Constructor/Exports` and `Optical Constructor/Catalogues` under `documents` through `FolderName.combine`; `shippedCatalogueFolder` = `shippedCatalogueDefault`. This is the one place the default texts are written. It reads no environment and touches no disk. `WorkbenchSettings` and `WorkbenchSettings.defaults` are unchanged, so nothing that builds settings reaches a location by default (.spec-md §3.9). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs`, on the `type CatalogueProxy with` extension that holds `createBuiltIn` (step 38): `static member createBuiltInUnder (shipped : FolderName) : CatalogueProxy` answers `CatalogueProxy.create` over `shipped`'s `Builtin` subfolder, the one place the `Builtin` name is written. `createBuiltIn ()` becomes `createBuiltInUnder` of `DataLocations.shippedCatalogueDefault` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, so its own `Path.Combine` is deleted and the shipped folder's name has one home. Each doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.4. No environment expansion, existence check, cache or fallback folder is added: resolving configured text is AppConfig's (step 82). (3) Tests. `WorkbenchSettingsTests` gains `DataLocations.defaultsUnder holds the 001 §G locations as configured text`: over `FolderName \"D:/Docs\"` (test-local text, never a real folder), every field of `DataLocations.defaultsUnder` equals the text above, the three Documents folders being `FolderName.combine`d under it, and `shippedCatalogueFolder` is `DataLocations.shippedCatalogueDefault`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given`: `createBuiltInUnder` over `Catalogue` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` reads `Ok` the same catalogue as `CatalogueProxy.create` over `Catalogue/Builtin` there, the path spelled out in the fact, and over a fresh empty folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"CatalogueFolderTests\")` answers `CatalogueIoErr`.", "acceptance": "After the locations land, `WorkbenchSettings.fs` MUST declare `DataLocations` with `defaultsUnder` and `shippedCatalogueDefault`, and `CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn` MUST read through `createBuiltInUnder`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `DataLocations.defaultsUnder holds the 001 §G locations as configured text` and `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests.DataLocations.defaultsUnder holds the 001 §G locations as configured text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LOCATIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LOCATIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.WorkbenchSettings.DataLocations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "obligations": ["S24-LOCATIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CatalogueFolderStore.CatalogueProxy.createBuiltInUnder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "obligations": ["S24-LOCATIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 82, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.4b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [81], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests"], "how_to": "The composition root reads every location from `appsettings.json` through the settings doors, and the test run pins its own (001 §G 'Every path is overridable'; 001 §C 'Settings': the connection string is the `OpticalConstructorSqlite` entry; .spec-md §3.9). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`. (a) Module `ConfigKey` (`AppConfig.fs:22`) gains six appSettings literals, each with a one-line doc naming its `DataLocations` field: `libraryBackupsFolder` = `\"LibraryBackupsFolder\"`, `preferencesFolder` = `\"PreferencesFolder\"`, `kitsFolder` = `\"KitsFolder\"`, `exportsFolder` = `\"ExportsFolder\"`, `cataloguesFolder` = `\"CataloguesFolder\"` and `shippedCatalogueFolder` = `\"ShippedCatalogueFolder\"`. `sqliteConnectionString` (`\"OpticalConstructorSqlite\"`, the connectionStrings entry) is the library connection and keeps its name. (b) Module `AppConfig` gains `readDataLocations (provider : AppSettings.AppSettingsProvider) (install : FolderName) (documents : FolderName) : DataLocations`, documented in one to three lines: each location is read once, a missing or refused one is written back as its default (`DataLocations.defaultsUnder documents`, step 81), and the answer has environment variables expanded and a relative folder rooted at `install`. It works in this order. The connection string is `provider.tryGetConnectionString` on `ConfigKey.sqliteConnectionString`: `Ok (Some value)` is kept; `Ok None` and `Error _` write the default back through `provider.trySetConnectionString` and use it, and an `Error` of the read or of the write-back is named in a `Logger.logWarn`, as `readSetting` (`AppConfig.fs:117`) names a refused value. Each folder is `readSetting provider (AppSettings.ConfigKey ConfigKey.<key>) defaults.<field> FolderName.tryCreate _.configValue`, STL's `FolderName` door (`Softellect.Sys.AppSettings`), so a missing or refused folder is logged and its default written back exactly as today's four keys are. The configured texts, gathered as a `DataLocations`, are then resolved by the private `resolveLocations (install : FolderName) (configured : DataLocations) : DataLocations`: `System.Environment.ExpandEnvironmentVariables` over the connection string and over each folder, and a folder that is not rooted after expansion (`Path.IsPathRooted`) combined under `install`. Each value is elevated where it is born (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). This is the IO boundary; Domain reads no environment. It does not save: its caller saves once, as `loadWorkbenchSettings` does today. `loadWorkbenchSettings` (`AppConfig.fs:136`) and its callers are unchanged in this step; step 83 makes it read the locations. (2) The test run's settings. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/appsettings.json`, a `Content` item of `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` with `CopyToOutputDirectory` `PreserveNewest` and no comment. A project's own copy item wins over a referenced project's item of the same target path (MSBuild removes the transitive item by `TargetPath`), so it replaces the App's `appsettings.json` (`OpticalConstructor.App.fsproj` `Content`) in the test output. That file is what the headless session's real `App` startup reads (`TestApp.fs:31-35`, `Program.fs:48`, `SmokeTests`), and from step 88 that startup opens the configured library. It holds `connectionStrings.OpticalConstructorSqlite` = `Data Source=:memory:` and, in `appSettings`, `LibraryBackupsFolder` = `TestRun/Backups`, `PreferencesFolder` = `TestRun/Preferences`, `KitsFolder` = `TestRun/Kits`, `ExportsFolder` = `TestRun/Exports`, `CataloguesFolder` = `TestRun/Catalogues` and `ShippedCatalogueFolder` = `Catalogue`: relative folders, so each resolves under the test output, and the build-copied catalogue. No test run therefore reaches `%LOCALAPPDATA%`, `%APPDATA%` or `Documents` (.spec-md §3.9, §4 \"Tests' data\"). (3) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs`, `module AppConfigTests`, compiled directly after `LauncherTests.fs`. Every settings file of (a)-(c) is `appsettings.json` in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"AppConfigTests\")`, opened through `AppSettings.AppSettingsProvider.tryCreate (FileName <path>)`; `install` and `documents` are folders under that fresh folder; nothing is created at a resolved location. (a) `readDataLocations writes every missing location back as its default and answers it expanded`: over `{ \"appSettings\": {}, \"connectionStrings\": {} }`, the answer's `libraryConnection` is the expansion of the default connection string and each folder the expansion of its default (`shippedCatalogueFolder` being `Catalogue` under `install`); after `trySave` the file holds the default texts verbatim, `%LOCALAPPDATA%` and `%APPDATA%` unexpanded. (b) `readDataLocations keeps a configured location, expands its variables and roots a relative folder at the install folder`: with a process environment variable the fact sets to a folder under its own test folder (a name no other code reads, removed in a `finally`), a configured `Data Source=%<variable>%/lib.db`, a configured `%<variable>%/Backups` and a configured relative `Kits` answer the expanded connection string, the expanded folder and `Kits` under `install`, and the file still holds the configured texts. (c) `readDataLocations replaces a refused folder with its default and writes the default back`: a configured `KitsFolder` that `FolderName.tryCreate` refuses (it holds `|`) answers the default kits folder, and the default is written back over it. (d) `the test run's appsettings.json keeps the library in memory and every folder under the test output`: inside `HeadlessSession.run`, so the session's `App` startup, the only other writer of that file, has finished, `readDataLocations` over the test output's own `appsettings.json` with `install` = `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` answers `Data Source=:memory:`, five folders under the test output, and `Catalogue` there as the shipped catalogue.", "acceptance": "After the reader lands, `AppConfig.readDataLocations` MUST read every location through `ConfigKey` and the test output's `appsettings.json` MUST hold the test run's locations; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over AppConfigTests, including `readDataLocations writes every missing location back as its default and answers it expanded`, `readDataLocations keeps a configured location, expands its variables and roots a relative folder at the install folder`, `readDataLocations replaces a refused folder with its default and writes the default back` and `the test run's appsettings.json keeps the library in memory and every folder under the test output`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/appsettings.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests.readDataLocations writes every missing location back as its default and answers it expanded", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SETTINGS-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests.readDataLocations keeps a configured location, expands its variables and roots a relative folder at the install folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SETTINGS-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests.readDataLocations replaces a refused folder with its default and writes the default back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SETTINGS-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests.the test run's appsettings.json keeps the library in memory and every folder under the test output", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SETTINGS-READ"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.AppConfig.readDataLocations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "obligations": ["S24-SETTINGS-READ"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 83, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.4c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [82], "how_to": "The app scope is composed over the configured locations, and every test scope over locations under the test output (001 §G; .spec-md §3.9: `AppContext.create` receives every location from settings). The stores stay in memory in this step; step 88 moves them onto the database. (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`: `loadWorkbenchSettings ()` (`AppConfig.fs:136`) becomes `loadWorkbenchSettings () : WorkbenchSettings * DataLocations`. Over the ONE provider it already creates, it reads the four workbench keys as today and the locations through `readDataLocations` (step 82), `install` being `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` and `documents` `Environment.GetFolderPath Environment.SpecialFolder.MyDocuments`, then saves once. When the file cannot be opened it logs as today and answers `WorkbenchSettings.defaults` with `resolveLocations install (DataLocations.defaultsUnder documents)`, so startup never blocks on configuration. Its doc and the module doc say it reads the locations too. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `create (settings)` becomes `static member create (locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings) : AppContext`. `experimentExport` writes into `locations.exportsFolder` through `ExperimentExportFile.createCsvFolder` (`ExperimentExportFile.fs:50`) with the clock it has today; the `Environment.GetFolderPath` and `Path.Combine` at `AppContext.fs:110-112` are deleted, because the exports default now lives in `DataLocations.defaultsUnder` (a move). The `experimentExport` field doc names the configured exports folder. No field is added and nothing else changes. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, module `Startup` (`Program.fs:48`, `:59`): `let workbenchSettings, dataLocations = AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings ()` and `let context = AppContext.create dataLocations workbenchSettings`; the two docs say so in no more words. (4) Tests. New fixture `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs`, `module TestAppScope` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, compiled directly after `TestApp.fs`, no comment in the project file. `testLocations (owner : FolderName) : DataLocations` holds `ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\"` and every folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"TestAppScope\", owner.value)` (`Backups`, `Preferences`, `Kits`, `Exports`, `Catalogues`), with `DataLocations.shippedCatalogueDefault` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` as the shipped catalogue. `freshAppContext (owner : FolderName) : AppContext` is `AppContext.create (testLocations owner) WorkbenchSettings.defaults`. Each doc is one line citing .spec-md §3.9. Every test composition goes through them, its owner the test module's name, and keeps its assertions: `AppContextTests` (`freshContext` and the verbatim-settings fact), `LauncherTests` (`freshContext`), `TableAndElementRotationTests`, `WireUiCompositionTests`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests` and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` (each `AppContext.create WorkbenchSettings.defaults`). `AppContextTests` gains `create writes experiment exports into the configured exports folder`: `testLocations`' `exportsFolder` is emptied first; an `ExportedRun` with one two-point series exported through `freshAppContext`'s `experimentExport` answers `Ok ()` and leaves exactly one `experiment-*.csv` in that folder.", "acceptance": "After the locations reach the app scope, `AppContext.create` MUST take `(locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings)` and write exports into `locations.exportsFolder`, `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT call `Environment.GetFolderPath`, and every UI test composition MUST go through `TestAppScope`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create writes experiment exports into the configured exports folder`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create writes experiment exports into the configured exports folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SCOPE-LOCATIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.AppContext.create", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-SCOPE-LOCATIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-SCOPE-LOCATIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 84, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.4d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [62], "how_to": "`LibraryDatabase` (step 62) learns what the composition root, the backups and the restore need of its one open handle (001 §C 'No migrations', 'Settings': 'Back up library now…' (`VACUUM INTO`) and 'Restore library…'; 001 §G; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO'). In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`: (1) Before `LibraryDatabase`, `LibraryDatabaseOrigin` = `CreatedLibraryDatabase` | `OpenedLibraryDatabase`, its doc one line: whether `openOrCreate` created and stamped the schema or found it stamped. It is never stored, so it has no tag. (2) `openOrCreate` records it, `CreatedLibraryDatabase` when `EnsureCreated` created the schema and it wrote the stamp and `OpenedLibraryDatabase` when it read a matching stamp, and `member this.origin : LibraryDatabaseOrigin` answers it. For a file database whose `DataSource` names a directory that does not exist, `openOrCreate` first creates that directory (`Directory.CreateDirectory`), inside its catch: SQLite creates a file but not its folder, and the default library lives in a folder nobody has made (001 §G). (3) `member this.vacuumInto (target : FileName) : Result<unit, StorageError>` holds the handle's lock and runs `VACUUM INTO` with `target`'s full path as a bound parameter on the handle's connection: SQLite writes a consistent, compacted copy of the live library, stamp included. A target that exists is refused by SQLite and answered as `LibraryDatabaseExn`, and that file is left as it was. It creates no folder; its caller does. (4) `member this.restoreFrom (backup : FileName) (beforeRestore : FileName) : Result<unit, StorageError>` holds the lock and works in this order. It opens `backup` through its own `SqliteConnection` (`Mode=ReadOnly`, pooling off) and reads its `SchemaStamp` row; a file without the table or the row, or with a stamp other than `LibrarySchemaVersion.current`, answers `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr` exactly as `openOrCreate` does, and nothing is written. Otherwise it runs `VACUUM INTO beforeRestore` as (3) does, then copies the backup into the live database through SQLite's online backup (`SqliteConnection.BackupDatabase` from the backup's connection into the handle's connection), so every store over this handle reads the restored library at once and nothing is reopened. It disposes the backup's connection whatever the outcome. (5) `vacuumInto` and `restoreFrom` carry step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark; every exception inside them, and the folder creation in `openOrCreate`, is caught and answered as `LibraryDatabaseExn`, never thrown. Each new member's doc is one to three lines citing 001 §C and spec 0050 S2.4. No retry, lock timeout, cache or second connection kept open is added. (6) Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`, every file in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryDatabaseTests\")` as step 62 keeps them, each fact disposing what it opens. The rows are `LibraryCatalogueImportRow`s, which no foreign key constrains. `openOrCreate says whether it created the library database or opened an existing one`: `:memory:` is `CreatedLibraryDatabase`; a new file is `CreatedLibraryDatabase` and, after that handle is disposed, a second `openOrCreate` of it is `OpenedLibraryDatabase`. `openOrCreate creates the missing folder of a new library database file`: a `Data Source` two folders deep inside a folder that does not exist opens `Ok`, and the file exists afterwards. `vacuumInto writes a stamped copy of the library and refuses a target that exists`: after a row is saved, `vacuumInto` a new file answers `Ok`, and `openOrCreate` of that file is `OpenedLibraryDatabase` holding the row; a second `vacuumInto` the same file answers `Error (LibraryDatabaseExn _)` and the file still opens with the row. `restoreFrom backs up the live library, then replaces it with a backup's under the same handle, and refuses another schema`: over a live file database holding row A, a backup is taken with `vacuumInto` and row B saved; `restoreFrom` the backup into a new `beforeRestore` file answers `Ok`, the same handle then holds A and not B, and `beforeRestore` holds A and B. A backup whose stamp a plain connection set to 2 answers `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr { foundOpt = Some (LibrarySchemaVersion 2); expected = LibrarySchemaVersion.current })`, writes no `beforeRestore` file and leaves the live library as it was.", "acceptance": "After the handle grows, `LibraryDatabase` MUST answer its `origin` and offer `vacuumInto` and `restoreFrom`, and `openOrCreate` MUST create a missing database folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `openOrCreate says whether it created the library database or opened an existing one`, `openOrCreate creates the missing folder of a new library database file`, `vacuumInto writes a stamped copy of the library and refuses a target that exists` and `restoreFrom backs up the live library, then replaces it with a backup's under the same handle, and refuses another schema`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.openOrCreate says whether it created the library database or opened an existing one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-DATABASE-HANDLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.openOrCreate creates the missing folder of a new library database file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-DATABASE-HANDLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.vacuumInto writes a stamped copy of the library and refuses a target that exists", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-DATABASE-HANDLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.restoreFrom backs up the live library, then replaces it with a backup's under the same handle, and refuses another schema", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-DATABASE-HANDLE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryDatabaseStore.LibraryDatabaseOrigin", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S24-DATABASE-HANDLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryDatabaseStore.LibraryDatabase.vacuumInto", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S24-DATABASE-HANDLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryDatabaseStore.LibraryDatabase.restoreFrom", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "obligations": ["S24-DATABASE-HANDLE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 85, "anchor": "ADD_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S2.4e", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0003", "name": "LibraryBackupProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [84], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests"], "how_to": "The Library window's backup seam, as a functional proxy with an in-memory double (001 §C 'Settings': 'Back up library now…' and 'Restore library…'; .spec-md §4: every proxy has an in-memory implementation of the same shape; §10.5: Restore library first backs up the current database, so restoring that backup is the undo). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryBackup.fs`, `module LibraryBackup` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `WorkbenchSettings.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. (1) `LibraryBackupName` = `LibraryBackupName of string` with `.value`: one backup's file name in the backups folder, without the folder. (2) `LibraryBackupError` = `LibraryBackupFailedErr of reason : string` (a backup or the listing failed) | `LibraryRestoreFailedErr of reason : string` (a restore failed or was refused; the library is unchanged) | `UnknownLibraryBackupErr of reason : string` (the named backup is not among the listed ones), each case documented, with `member this.describe : string` rendering the condition and the reason in step 39's form. (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] LibraryBackupProxy = { backUpLibrary : unit -> Result<LibraryBackupName, LibraryBackupError>; listBackups : unit -> Result<LibraryBackupName list, LibraryBackupError>; restoreLibrary : LibraryBackupName -> Result<LibraryBackupName, LibraryBackupError> }`. Its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §C, and each field has a one-line doc: `backUpLibrary` takes a backup of the whole library and answers its name; `listBackups` answers every backup, newest first; `restoreLibrary` refuses a name `listBackups` does not answer, otherwise backs up the current library, replaces the library with the named backup and answers the pre-restore backup's name. (4) `static member createInMemory () : LibraryBackupProxy` is the test double: it keeps the names it minted, `backup-1`, `backup-2`, … in minting order; `listBackups` answers them newest first; `restoreLibrary` of a held name mints a pre-restore backup and answers it, and of any other name answers `UnknownLibraryBackupErr` naming it and mints nothing. It holds no library content; the content is the database store's (step 86). (5) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs`, compiled directly after `LibraryDatabaseTests.fs`. `[<AbstractClass>] type LibraryBackupProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshBackups : unit -> LibraryBackupProxy`, a store holding no backup, and these facts: `a new backup store lists no backup`: `listBackups` answers `Ok []`. `each backup is listed, newest first`: two `backUpLibrary` calls answer two distinct names, and `listBackups` answers them second first. `restoring a listed backup first backs up the current library and answers that backup`: after one backup, `restoreLibrary` of its name answers `Ok before` with a third name, and `listBackups` answers `[ before; first ]`. `restoring an unknown backup is UnknownLibraryBackupErr and takes no backup`: after one backup, `restoreLibrary (LibraryBackupName \"no-such-backup\")` answers `Error (UnknownLibraryBackupErr _)` and the listing is unchanged. `type LibraryBackupProxyTests () = inherit LibraryBackupProxyContract ()` answers `LibraryBackupProxy.createInMemory ()`.", "acceptance": "After the seam lands, `LibraryBackup.fs` MUST declare `LibraryBackupProxy` with `createInMemory`, and `LibraryBackupProxyContract` MUST hold the backup-store facts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every LibraryBackupProxyContract fact under `LibraryBackupProxyTests`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryBackup.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests.a new backup store lists no backup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-BACKUP-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests.each backup is listed, newest first", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-BACKUP-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests.restoring a listed backup first backs up the current library and answers that backup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-BACKUP-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests.restoring an unknown backup is UnknownLibraryBackupErr and takes no backup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-BACKUP-PROXY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryBackup.LibraryBackupProxy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryBackup.fs", "obligations": ["S24-BACKUP-PROXY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 86, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S2.4f", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0003", "name": "LibraryBackupProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [84, 85], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests"], "how_to": "The backup store over the library database and its backups folder (001 §C 'Settings': 'Back up library now…' (`VACUUM INTO`), 'Restore library…'; 001 §G: `Backups\\` beside the database; the S2.4 brief: a timestamped file in `Backups/`). New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs`, `module LibraryBackupStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `PresetDatabaseStore.fs` (step 79): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. (1) `LibraryBackupTime` = `LibraryBackupTime of DateTime` with `.value` and `member this.fileStamp : string`, the invariant-culture `yyyyMMdd-HHmmss`: when a backup was taken, which names it. Its creator passes the clock, the composition root the system clock and tests a fixed one, as `ExperimentExportFile.createCsvFolder` takes `now` (`ExperimentExportFile.fs:50`). (2) The naming rule, private to the module: a backup is `library-<stamp>.db`; when that file exists, `library-<stamp>-2.db`, then `-3` and on, the first that does not exist, so two backups in one second never meet (a restore backs up in the same second it was asked for). The listing reads back only files named so and orders them newest first by the stamp and then the number, a name without a number counting as 1; any other file in the folder is not a backup and is not listed. (3) `type LibraryBackupProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) (backups : FolderName) (now : unit -> LibraryBackupTime) : LibraryBackupProxy`, unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` (ELEV019), marked `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the library backup store (001 §C): VACUUM INTO and the online restore over the backups folder\")>]`. `backUpLibrary` creates `backups` when missing, names the backup by (2) and runs `database.vacuumInto` (step 84) into it. `listBackups` answers `Ok []` for a missing folder. `restoreLibrary name` answers `UnknownLibraryBackupErr` naming it when the listing does not hold it; otherwise it names the pre-restore backup by (2), runs `database.restoreFrom` of `name` under `backups` into it, and answers that name. A `StorageError` of a backup or of the listing is `LibraryBackupFailedErr`, of a restore `LibraryRestoreFailedErr`, each carrying the error's `describe`; an IO exception at the folder is caught here and answered the same way. The `LibraryBackupProxy` doc names `createInDatabase` beside the in-memory double in one line. (4) Tests, in `LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs`: `type LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests () = inherit LibraryBackupProxyContract ()` runs the four contract facts over a FILE database, `library.db` in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryBackupProxyTests\")` with `Backups` beside it, and a fixed clock, so every name past the first carries a number. The class implements `IDisposable` and disposes every database it opened. Where a fact needs entries, its database is filled by `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` through `CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores` over its database stores (step 80). Its own facts: `a backup is a library database holding the library as it was when taken`: after a backup, a user sample saved through `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` of the live database (step 74); the backup file opens through `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate` as `OpenedLibraryDatabase`, and its samples store resolves every Built-in sample and not the user's. `restoring through the backup store brings the backup's library back to every store over the same database`: after a backup, a user sample saved, then `restoreLibrary` of the backup answers `Ok before`; the SAME `SampleProxy` the sample was saved through no longer resolves it and still resolves every Built-in sample, and the `before` backup holds the user's sample. `a backup of another schema is refused with LibraryRestoreFailedErr and changes nothing`: a backup file whose stamp a plain `SqliteConnection` (pooling off) set to 2 answers `Error (LibraryRestoreFailedErr reason)`, `reason` naming both versions; the listing gains no backup and the live library is unchanged. `backups taken in the same second get numbered names and only backup files are listed`: three backups under the fixed clock are named `library-<stamp>.db`, `library-<stamp>-2.db` and `library-<stamp>-3.db` and listed in the reverse order, and a file `notes.txt` in the folder is not listed. `a database failure below the backup store is a typed backup error, never a throw`: after one backup, the database is disposed; `backUpLibrary` answers `Error (LibraryBackupFailedErr _)` and `restoreLibrary` of the listed backup `Error (LibraryRestoreFailedErr _)`, never a throw.", "acceptance": "After the database backup store lands, a test MUST instantiate the real `LibraryBackupProxy.createInDatabase` over a file database; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every LibraryBackupProxyContract fact under `LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests` and its own `a backup is a library database holding the library as it was when taken`, `restoring through the backup store brings the backup's library back to every store over the same database`, `a backup of another schema is refused with LibraryRestoreFailedErr and changes nothing`, `backups taken in the same second get numbered names and only backup files are listed` and `a database failure below the backup store is a typed backup error, never a throw`, the count rising by 9; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.a new backup store lists no backup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.each backup is listed, newest first", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.restoring a listed backup first backs up the current library and answers that backup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.restoring an unknown backup is UnknownLibraryBackupErr and takes no backup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.a backup is a library database holding the library as it was when taken", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.restoring through the backup store brings the backup's library back to every store over the same database", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.a backup of another schema is refused with LibraryRestoreFailedErr and changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.backups taken in the same second get numbered names and only backup files are listed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests.a database failure below the backup store is a typed backup error, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryBackupProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryBackupProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryBackupStore.LibraryBackupTime", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryBackupStore.LibraryBackupProxy.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs", "obligations": ["S24-SQLITE-BACKUPS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 87, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.4g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [86], "how_to": "The remedy for a library of another schema: recreate it, the old file kept in `Backups` first (001 §C 'No migrations': the remedy is to recreate the database from the catalogues; the S2.4 brief: the old file is first copied into `Backups/`, then deleted and recreated; .spec-md §7 '`Test` EF table + migration → library model'). In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs` (step 86): `type LibraryDatabase with static member recreate (connectionString : ConnectionString) (backups : FolderName) (now : unit -> LibraryBackupTime) : Result<LibraryDatabase, StorageError>`, marked `StorageBoundary` as step 86's member is, its doc one to three lines. It reads the connection string through `SqliteConnectionStringBuilder`. An in-memory library (`DataSource` `:memory:` or `Mode` `Memory`) has no file, so it answers `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate connectionString`. For a file library whose file exists, it creates `backups` when missing, copies the file to the next backup name of step 86's rule (`File.Copy`, never overwriting), then deletes the file and any `-wal`, `-shm` and `-journal` file beside it, and answers `openOrCreate connectionString`, which creates and stamps a new library (`CreatedLibraryDatabase`, step 84). A missing file is simply created. Every IO failure is caught and answered as `FileIoExn`; a failed copy deletes nothing. It runs on a file no handle holds: its caller has none, because `openOrCreate` disposed the connection when it answered the mismatch (step 62). No retry, rename-instead-of-copy or migration is added. Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`, under step 84's folder: `recreate copies the old library file into the backups folder, then creates a new stamped library`: a file library whose stamp a plain connection set to 2 (step 62's way) answers `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr` from `openOrCreate`; `recreate` under a fixed clock answers `Ok` a `CreatedLibraryDatabase` stamped 1 and holding no entry; `Backups` beside it holds exactly `library-<stamp>.db`, whose stamp a plain connection reads as 2; and no `-wal` or `-shm` file of the old library is left. `recreate of an in-memory library creates a new one and copies nothing`: `recreate` of `Data Source=:memory:` answers a `CreatedLibraryDatabase` and creates no backups folder.", "acceptance": "After the remedy lands, `LibraryDatabase.recreate` MUST keep the old file in the backups folder before it creates a new library; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `recreate copies the old library file into the backups folder, then creates a new stamped library` and `recreate of an in-memory library creates a new one and copies nothing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.recreate copies the old library file into the backups folder, then creates a new stamped library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-RECREATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.recreate of an in-memory library creates a new one and copies nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S24-RECREATE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryBackupStore.LibraryDatabase.recreate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs", "obligations": ["S24-RECREATE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 88, "anchor": "WIRE", "ac": "AC-S2.4h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [80, 81, 83, 84], "how_to": "The app runs on the library database (001 §C, §G; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`: it composes the SQLite library proxies over the configured locations; §3.9; §7: a mismatch is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `create` becomes `static member create (locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings) : Result<AppContext, StorageError>`. It opens `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate locations.libraryConnection` (step 62) and answers an error as it is, so a library of another schema is shown and never silently recreated. Over the open database it composes the stores: `materials` = `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase` (step 69), `samples` = `SampleProxy.createInDatabase` (step 74), `sources` = `SourceProxy.createInDatabase` (step 76), `categories` = `CategoryProxy.createInDatabase` (step 71) and `library` = `LibraryProxy.createInDatabase` (step 79). When `database.origin` is `CreatedLibraryDatabase` (step 84) it imports the shipped Built-in catalogue, `(CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores categories materials samples (LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase database)).importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltInUnder locations.shippedCatalogueFolder)` (steps 80, 81); an `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe`, and the app starts with what was imported, as step 44 does. An opened library is not imported again: importing on every start, by manifest hash, is S3.1's. `experiments`, `experimentData`, `experimentCollections`, `scenes`, `experimentExport` and `settings` are as in step 83. The in-memory store construction and `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory` go from `create`, with the opens nothing needs any more. The `create` doc says, in one to three lines, that it opens or creates the configured library database, imports the Built-in catalogue into a new one and answers an open failure (001 §C; spec 0050 S2.4); the record and field docs that say in-memory store say database store. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: `Startup.context` (`Program.fs:59`) is now the `Result`. `LauncherWindow(context : AppContext)` (`Program.fs:134`) becomes `LauncherWindow(opened : Result<AppContext, StorageError>)`, and `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` (`Program.fs:216`) passes `Startup.context`. On `Ok context` it is today's launcher. On `Error e` it shows, between the title and the buttons, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherLibraryErrorText` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, with the text `The library could not be opened: <e.describe>`, and the four surface buttons are built with `IsEnabled` false and no click handler, because no window opens without the library. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588-594`): `static member launcherLibraryErrorText : ConstructorUiId = ConstructorUiId \"LauncherLibraryErrorText\"` with a one-line doc. (4) Tests. `TestAppScope.freshAppContext` (step 83) answers the `Ok` context and fails the calling fact with the error's `describe` otherwise; each call opens its own `:memory:` library, so every composition over it runs on the database with the Built-in catalogue imported. `TestAppScope` gains `fileLocations (owner : FolderName) : DataLocations`: every location of `testLocations` moved into a fresh folder under the owner's (a GUID name, so no run meets another's files), and `libraryConnection` `Data Source=<that folder>/library.db`. `LauncherTests.withLauncher` passes `Ok (freshAppContext …)`, and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' `LauncherWindow(ctx)` becomes `LauncherWindow(Ok ctx)`. `TableAndElementRotationTests`, `WireUiCompositionTests` and `WireUi0040CompositionTests` compose through `TestAppScope.freshAppContext` since step 83 and keep their code; their facts now run on the database. `AppContextTests` gains `create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again`: two `AppContext.create` over the same `fileLocations`; the first lists every Built-in sample, and a Built-in sample is removed through it; the second, over the same file, does not list that sample, so it opened the library without importing again, and lists every other Built-in sample. And `create answers LibrarySchemaMismatchErr for a library of another schema and leaves the file as it was`: a file library is created through `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate` and disposed, and its stamp set to 2 through a plain `SqliteConnection` (pooling off); `AppContext.create` over it answers `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr _)`, and the stamp is still 2. `LauncherTests` gains `a library that fails to open is shown on the launcher and the four buttons are disabled`: `LauncherWindow(Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr { foundOpt = Some (LibrarySchemaVersion 2); expected = LibrarySchemaVersion.current }))` shows `launcherLibraryErrorText` naming both versions, each of the four buttons is disabled, and raising `Click` on Main opens no window.", "acceptance": "After the switch, `AppContext.create` MUST answer `Result<AppContext, StorageError>` over the configured library database, and `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT call `MaterialProxy.createInMemory`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemory`, `SourceProxy.createInMemory` or `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again`, `create answers LibrarySchemaMismatchErr for a library of another schema and leaves the file as it was` and `a library that fails to open is shown on the launcher and the four buttons are disabled`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-APP-ON-DATABASE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create answers LibrarySchemaMismatchErr for a library of another schema and leaves the file as it was", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-APP-ON-DATABASE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a library that fails to open is shown on the launcher and the four buttons are disabled", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-APP-ON-DATABASE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.AppContext.create", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-APP-ON-DATABASE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-APP-ON-DATABASE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 89, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S2.4i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [87, 88], "how_to": "The Launcher offers the remedy for a library of another schema (001 §C 'No migrations'; the S2.4 brief: the Launcher offers 'Recreate library from catalogues', the old file first copied into `Backups/`; .spec-md §10.5: the old library kept in `Backups` is the undo, so the action asks no confirmation). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `create`'s composition over an open database (step 88) moves into `static member private compose (locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings) (database : LibraryDatabase) : AppContext`, which `create` calls. `static member recreateLibrary (locations : DataLocations) (settings : WorkbenchSettings) : Result<AppContext, StorageError>` is `LibraryDatabase.recreate locations.libraryConnection locations.backupsFolder (fun () -> LibraryBackupTime DateTime.Now)` (step 87) composed the same way, so a recreated library imports the Built-in catalogue as any new one does. Its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §C. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: `LauncherWindow(opened)` (step 88) becomes `LauncherWindow(locations : DataLocations, settings : WorkbenchSettings, opened : Result<AppContext, StorageError>)`, and `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` passes `Startup.dataLocations`, `Startup.workbenchSettings` and `Startup.context`. The window's content is built by one local function of the outcome. On `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr _)` it also shows, under the error text, a button carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherRecreateLibraryButton` as its `Name` and `AutomationId` and the label `Recreate library from catalogues`; any other error shows no such button, because recreating cannot remedy it. Its click runs `AppContext.recreateLibrary locations settings`: `Ok context` replaces the window's content with the launcher over `context`, the four buttons enabled; `Error e` shows `e.describe` in the error text and keeps the button. (3) `UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `static member launcherRecreateLibraryButton : ConstructorUiId = ConstructorUiId \"LauncherRecreateLibraryButton\"` with a one-line doc. (4) Tests. `LauncherTests.withLauncher` passes `TestAppScope.testLocations`, `WorkbenchSettings.defaults` and `Ok (freshAppContext …)`, step 88's fact passes `testLocations` and the defaults beside its error, and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher passes `testLocations` of its owner, the defaults and `Ok ctx`. In `LauncherTests`: `acceptance: Recreate library from catalogues keeps the old file in Backups, opens a new library and enables the buttons` (trait `ui-smoke`, as the file's click-driven facts are): over `TestAppScope.fileLocations`, a library created through `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate` and disposed has its stamp set to 2 by a plain connection; the launcher over `AppContext.create` of those locations shows the recreate button; raising its `Click` removes `launcherLibraryErrorText` and the button, enables the four buttons, leaves exactly one `library-*.db` in `backupsFolder` whose stamp a plain connection reads as 2, and the library file's stamp reads 1. `the launcher offers Recreate library from catalogues for a schema mismatch only`: with `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr …)` the button is present with its label; with `Error (LibraryDatabaseExn (exn \"disk full\"))` the error text shows and no recreate button exists.", "acceptance": "After the remedy is offered, `AppContext.recreateLibrary` MUST compose over `LibraryDatabase.recreate`, and the launcher MUST show `launcherRecreateLibraryButton` for `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr` alone; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: Recreate library from catalogues keeps the old file in Backups, opens a new library and enables the buttons`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the launcher offers Recreate library from catalogues for a schema mismatch only`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: Recreate library from catalogues keeps the old file in Backups, opens a new library and enables the buttons", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S24-LAUNCHER-RECREATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the launcher offers Recreate library from catalogues for a schema mismatch only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LAUNCHER-RECREATE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.AppContext.recreateLibrary", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "obligations": ["S24-LAUNCHER-RECREATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-LAUNCHER-RECREATE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 90, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S2.4j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [86, 89], "how_to": "'Back up library now…' and 'Restore library…' in the Library window, over the app scope's backup store (001 §C 'Settings'; .spec-md §10: discoverability (both are Library-window buttons), pre-confirmation (Restore library asks), action buttons (the Restore / Cancel pair; restoring the pre-restore backup is the undo); the S2.4 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the record gains `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy`, its doc one line: the library's backup store, `Backups` beside the database (001 §G). `compose` (step 89) sets it to `LibraryBackupProxy.createInDatabase database locations.backupsFolder (fun () -> LibraryBackupTime DateTime.Now)` (step 86). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowContext` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:153`) gains `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy` with a one-line doc. (b) Beside `LibraryRemoveGate`, `LibraryRestoreGate` = `NoPendingLibraryRestore` | `PendingLibraryRestore of backups : LibraryBackupName list * pickedOpt : LibraryBackupName option`, documented as the restore panel: closed, or open over the listed backups with the picked one, if any. `LibraryWindowError` (`:70`) gains `LibraryBackupRefusedErr of LibraryBackupError`, and its `caption` renders it through `LibraryBackupError.caption`. (c) `LibraryWindowModel` gains `restoreGate : LibraryRestoreGate` (opening `NoPendingLibraryRestore`) and `backupStatus : ControlCaption option` (opening `None`), each with a one-line doc. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains, each documented: `BackUpLibraryNow`; `RequestLibraryRestore`; `PickLibraryBackup of LibraryBackupName`; `ConfirmLibraryRestore`; `CancelLibraryRestore`. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `BackUpLibraryNow` calls `context.libraryBackups.backUpLibrary ()`: `Ok name` sets `backupStatus` to `Library backed up to <name>.` and clears `lastError`; `Error e` sets `lastError` to `LibraryBackupRefusedErr e` and clears `backupStatus`. `RequestLibraryRestore` calls `listBackups ()`: `Ok backups` opens the panel over them with nothing picked, disarms the remove and lifecycle gates and clears `lastError` and `backupStatus`; `Error e` sets `lastError`. `PickLibraryBackup name` picks `name` when the panel is open and lists it, and is inert otherwise. `ConfirmLibraryRestore` with a pick calls `restoreLibrary picked`: `Ok before` closes the panel, clears the selection (`selectedEntryId`, `selectedNodeOpt`, `viewedVersion`), because the restored library may not hold the selected entry, and sets `backupStatus` to `Library restored from <picked>. The library before the restore is backed up as <before>.`; `Error e` sets `lastError` and keeps the panel open. Without a pick, or with the panel closed, it is inert. `CancelLibraryRestore` closes the panel and changes nothing else. A message that arms the remove or the lifecycle gate also closes the panel, so at most one confirmation is ever pending (the rule of `requestLifecycle`, `:540`). (f) The view. In the verbs area, after the entry verbs and in Browse and Select mode alike, `verbButton ConstructorUiId.libraryBackUpNowButton (ControlCaption \"Back up library now…\")` and `verbButton ConstructorUiId.libraryRestoreButton (ControlCaption \"Restore library…\")`. While the panel is open, a block carrying `libraryRestorePanel` holds the prompt `Restore the whole library from a backup. The current library is backed up first.`, one `verbButton (ConstructorUiId.libraryBackupRow name.uiKey) (ControlCaption name.value)` per backup in the listed order, the picked one on `positiveBackground` (or `No backup yet.` when there is none), and one row with `actionButton ConstructorUiId.libraryRestoreConfirmButton (ControlCaption \"Restore\") positiveBackground` and `actionButton ConstructorUiId.libraryRestoreCancelButton (ControlCaption \"Cancel\") negativeBackground`: the look of the Select / Close pair (`:1013-1014`, `actionButton` at `:1040`), a visible gap and distinct colours. `backupStatus`, when `Some`, shows in a `TextBlock` carrying `libraryBackupStatusText`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type LibraryBackupName with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (the name's text) and `type LibraryBackupError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`), each with a one-line doc. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group (`UiIds.fs:498-523`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S2.4: `libraryBackUpNowButton` (`\"LibraryBackUpNowButton\"`), `libraryRestoreButton` (`\"LibraryRestoreButton\"`), `libraryRestorePanel` (`\"LibraryRestorePanel\"`), `libraryBackupRow (backup : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"LibraryBackupRow_{backup.value}\"`), `libraryRestoreConfirmButton` (`\"LibraryRestoreConfirmButton\"`), `libraryRestoreCancelButton` (`\"LibraryRestoreCancelButton\"`) and `libraryBackupStatusText` (`\"LibraryBackupStatusText\"`). (5) Threading, so every Library window, opened from the launcher, the strip or a Select session, has the store. `LibraryWindow` (`LibraryWindow.fs:34`) takes `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy` after `categories` and sets the context field. `EditorLaunchers.openLibraryWindow` and `openLibrarySelectWindow` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:158`, `:169`) take it after the `CategoryProxy`, and `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it to `LibraryWindow`. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `libraryBackups : LibraryBackupProxy`, which `initWith` sets to `LibraryBackupProxy.createInMemory ()` for the test scenes as it sets `experimentExport` (`:520`); the strip's `OpenLibraryWindow` (`:1841`) and the Select open (`:3278`) pass `model.libraryBackups`. `Program.fs`'s `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` thread `libraryBackups = context.libraryBackups` by record update beside `sources`, and the launcher's Library button passes `context.libraryBackups`. Every test construction passes one: `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` and its two `LibraryWindow(...)`, `LightSourceEditorTests`' `libraryContext`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' `libraryContext` and `ScrollExtentTests`' `LibraryWindow(...)` pass `LibraryBackupProxy.createInMemory ()`; `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` passes `ctx.libraryBackups`; `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording launchers and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' Select-open stub take the extra argument. A doc that lists the window's or the launchers' stores names the backup store in no more words. (6) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`. Pure facts over `stubContext` with `LibraryBackupProxy.createInMemory ()`: `the backup and restore UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the seven ids' texts. `BackUpLibraryNow reaches the backup store and shows the backup's name`: after `BackUpLibraryNow`, the store lists one backup and `backupStatus` names it. `a refused backup shows its reason as the window message and no status`: over a backup proxy whose fields answer `LibraryBackupFailedErr`, `lastError` is `LibraryBackupRefusedErr` carrying it and `backupStatus` is `None`. `RequestLibraryRestore opens the panel over the backups, and Restore stays inert until one is picked`: after two backups, `RequestLibraryRestore` opens the panel over both, newest first, and `ConfirmLibraryRestore` before a pick leaves the model unchanged. `confirming a picked backup restores it, names the pre-restore backup, closes the panel and clears the selection`: an entry selected, a backup picked and confirmed; the panel is closed, the selection empty, the store lists the pre-restore backup first, and `backupStatus` names both backups. `Cancel closes the restore panel and restores nothing, and arming Remove closes it too`: `CancelLibraryRestore` closes the panel and the store lists no new backup, and `RequestRemoveSelectedEntry` on a selected sample closes an open panel. And `acceptance: the Library window backs up and restores the app-scope library through its buttons` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations …)` a `LibraryWindow` composed from the context's stores and `libraryBackups`; clicks on Back up library now…, then a user sample saved through `ctx.samples`, then clicks on Restore library…, the backup's row and Restore: `ctx.samples` no longer resolves the user sample, `libraryBackupStatusText` names the pre-restore backup, and `Backups` holds two backups.", "acceptance": "After the backup verbs are wired, every Library window, opened from the launcher, the strip or a Select session, MUST carry the app scope's `LibraryBackupProxy` and offer `libraryBackUpNowButton` and `libraryRestoreButton`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Library window backs up and restores the app-scope library through its buttons`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the backup and restore UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `BackUpLibraryNow reaches the backup store and shows the backup's name`, `a refused backup shows its reason as the window message and no status`, `RequestLibraryRestore opens the panel over the backups, and Restore stays inert until one is picked`, `confirming a picked backup restores it, names the pre-restore backup, closes the panel and clears the selection` and `Cancel closes the restore panel and restores nothing, and arming Remove closes it too`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the backup and restore UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.BackUpLibraryNow reaches the backup store and shows the backup's name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a refused backup shows its reason as the window message and no status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.RequestLibraryRestore opens the panel over the backups, and Restore stays inert until one is picked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.confirming a picked backup restores it, names the pre-restore backup, closes the panel and clears the selection", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.Cancel closes the restore panel and restores nothing, and arming Remove closes it too", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.acceptance: the Library window backs up and restores the app-scope library through its buttons", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindowView.LibraryWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.EditorLaunchers", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S24-LIBRARY-BACKUP-UI"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S2.4 -- Database location, settings, backup and restore; the app runs on the database"}
{"number": 91, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [90], "how_to": "A divergent entry is imported as a flagged fork under a new id whose provenance keeps the original id (001 §B 'Per-entry import decision', 'Same id and version, different hash'; the S3.1 brief). The provenance case is the flag, so the entry file, its database row and a kit's snapshot all carry it. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `EntryProvenance` (step 24) gains a fifth case, `ForkProvenance of EntryForkInfo`, declared together with `and EntryForkInfo = { originalId : LibraryEntryId; originalVersion : VersionNumber; originalProvenance : EntryProvenance }`: the entry, version and provenance the fork was taken from, a pulled source's licence and citation included. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.1. A fork belongs to the user: `protection` answers `UserManaged` and `categoryOrigin` answers `UserCategory`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (step 63): `kindValue` answers 5 for a fork, and `catalogueIdOpt` answers `None`, because a fork ships in no catalogue. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json` (step 30): the provenance definition gains a fifth shape, exactly what the serializer writes for `ForkProvenance`. Its `originalId` is a GUID, its `originalVersion` a positive version, and its `originalProvenance` a `$ref` to the provenance definition itself, so a fork of a fork validates. The entry schemas keep version 1, because no entry file has been released. Any other complete match on `EntryProvenance` that FS0025 reports answers a fork as it answers `UserProvenance`. No other case, member or schema changes. (4) Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` also covers a `ForkProvenance` whose original is `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`: it is `UserManaged` and `UserCategory`. `EntryFileJsonTests`' `every provenance round-trips through an entry file` gains a material under a `ForkProvenance` of a `SourcePullProvenance`, and one under a fork of that fork. Each round-trips through its entry file, and its decoder answers the material.", "acceptance": "After the fork provenance lands, `EntryProvenance` MUST declare `ForkProvenance of EntryForkInfo`, which `protection` answers as `UserManaged`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` and `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-FORK-PROVENANCE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.every provenance round-trips through an entry file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-FORK-PROVENANCE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryForkInfo", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S31-FORK-PROVENANCE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 92, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [91], "how_to": "The start-up import compares a catalogue's manifest hash before it reads any entry file (001 §B 'Import on every start'; 001 Summary: 'a manifest-hash comparison makes that cheap'). The catalogue seam therefore reads the manifest on its own. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs`: `CatalogueProxy` (step 32) gains `readManifest : unit -> Result<CatalogueManifest, CatalogueError>` before `readCatalogue`. Its doc says that it reads and checks the manifest and opens no entry file. `createInMemory` answers the held catalogue's `manifest`, or `CatalogueIoErr` while nothing has been written, as its `readCatalogue` does. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs`: `create`'s `readManifest` is the first part of `readCatalogue` in step 33's order. It reads the folder and its `.catalogue-json` (`CatalogueIoErr`) and parses the manifest with `LibraryFileText.parseCatalogueManifest` (`CatalogueFileRejectedErr`). `readCatalogue` calls it and then reads the entry files, so the two share one body. (3) On the same extension, `static member builtInFolderUnder (shipped : FolderName) : FolderName` answers the `Builtin` subfolder of `shipped`. `createBuiltInUnder` (step 81) becomes `create` over it, so `Builtin` is still written in one place; the start-up import (steps 98, 100) logs the shipped catalogue under this folder. Each doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.1. No cache, existence check or other field is added. (4) Tests. `CatalogueProxyTests` gains `the in-memory catalogue reads its manifest alone`: before a write, `readManifest` answers `CatalogueIoErr`; after it, the written catalogue's `manifest`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `readManifest reads the manifest without opening an entry file`. Over a written folder, `readManifest` equals `readCatalogue`'s manifest. After one entry file is deleted, `readCatalogue` answers `MissingEntryFileErr` and `readManifest` still answers that manifest. A folder whose `.catalogue-json` was deleted answers `CatalogueIoErr`. `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given` (step 81) also checks that `builtInFolderUnder` of `Catalogue` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` is its `Catalogue/Builtin` subfolder.", "acceptance": "After the manifest read lands, `CatalogueProxy` MUST declare `readManifest`, which the folder store answers without opening an entry file; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the in-memory catalogue reads its manifest alone`, `readManifest reads the manifest without opening an entry file` and `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests.the in-memory catalogue reads its manifest alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-MANIFEST-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.readManifest reads the manifest without opening an entry file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-MANIFEST-READ"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-MANIFEST-READ"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueFiles.CatalogueProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-MANIFEST-READ"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 93, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [92], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests"], "how_to": "The per-entry decision table of 001 §B as pure Domain data and functions (001 §B 'Per-entry import decision'; .spec-md §3.7, §5 `CatalogueImport`, `ImportDecision`; the S3.1 brief). No seam, store or caller changes in this step. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `LibraryEntryContent` gains `member this.referencedEntryIds : Set<LibraryEntryId>`. For a material it holds the category in `categoryOpt`. For a sample it holds the materials of its payload's structure (`ElementId.fs:SampleStructure.referencedMaterials`), each through `toLibraryEntryId` (step 24). Every other kind references nothing. Its doc says that these are the entries this one names, so that an import never leaves a reference dangling. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, before `CatalogueImportProxy`. Each type and case has a one-line doc citing 001 §B, and the module doc names the table (spec 0050 S3.1). (a) `HeldEntryVersion = { version : VersionNumber; contentHash : ContentHash }` is one version the library holds. `HeldEntry = { id : LibraryEntryId; kind : LibraryEntryKind; name : EntryName; latest : VersionNumber; lifecycle : EntryLifecycle; provenance : EntryProvenance; versions : HeldEntryVersion list }` is what the library holds for one id: the kind, name, lifecycle and provenance of its latest version, and every version, ascending. (b) `ImportOrigin` = `CatalogueImportOrigin of id : CatalogueId * name : CatalogueName` says where the incoming entries come from. (c) `LatestMove` = `MoveLatestVersion` | `KeepLatestVersion`. (d) `ImportAction` = `AddIncomingEntry` | `ReuseHeldEntry` | `AddIncomingVersion of LatestMove` | `ForkIncomingEntry` | `RebindToHeldEntry of LibraryEntryId` | `SkipIncomingEntry` | `RetireHeldEntry`. (e) `ImportStatus` holds the six rows of 001 §B in its order: `EntryIdNotHeld of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope` | `SameContentHash of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * held : HeldEntry` | `VersionNotHeld of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * held : HeldEntry` | `DivergentContent of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * held : HeldEntry` | `NameCollision of incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope * sameName : HeldEntry list` | `EntryUnlisted of held : HeldEntry`. (g) `ImportDecision = { origin : ImportOrigin; status : ImportStatus; defaultAction : ImportAction; alternatives : ImportAction list }` is one row, and `ImportChoice = { decision : ImportDecision; action : ImportAction }` is a confirmed row. `ImportSplit = { awaiting : ImportDecision list }`; every row requires confirmation. (3) Members of `ImportDecision`. `static member decide (origin : ImportOrigin) (incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope) (heldOpt : HeldEntry option) (sameName : HeldEntry list) : ImportDecision` reads `sameName` (the held entries of the incoming kind and name) only when `heldOpt` is `None`, and applies the rules in this order. A held entry of another kind is `DivergentContent`, because one id cannot name two kinds. A held version equal to the incoming version with an equal hash is `SameContentHash`, defaulting to `ReuseHeldEntry` with no alternative. The same version with another hash is `DivergentContent`, defaulting to `ForkIncomingEntry` with `[ SkipIncomingEntry ]`. A version the entry does not hold is `VersionNotHeld`, defaulting to `AddIncomingVersion move` with `[ SkipIncomingEntry ]`. Here `move` is `MoveLatestVersion` only when the incoming provenance is `BuiltInProvenance c`, the origin is `CatalogueImportOrigin (c, _)`, and the incoming version is above `held.latest`: a protected built-in arriving from its own catalogue (001 §B: 'the local latest moves only for a protected built-in from a catalogue'). Otherwise `move` is `KeepLatestVersion`. Without a held entry, a non-empty `sameName` is `NameCollision`, defaulting to `AddIncomingEntry` (side by side), with one `RebindToHeldEntry` per same-name entry in its order and then `SkipIncomingEntry`. Otherwise the row is `EntryIdNotHeld`, defaulting to `AddIncomingEntry` with `[ SkipIncomingEntry ]`. `static member unlisted (origin : ImportOrigin) (held : HeldEntry) : ImportDecision` is `EntryUnlisted`, defaulting to `RetireHeldEntry` with no alternative. `member this.entryId : LibraryEntryId` and `member this.kind : LibraryEntryKind` read the incoming content, or the held entry for `EntryUnlisted`. `member this.byDefault : ImportChoice` is the row with its default action. `member this.rowName : EntryName` is the name the import dialog shows: the incoming name, or the held name for `EntryUnlisted`. For `NameCollision` it is `<name> — from <catalogue name>` (001 §B 'Si — from A'), a caption only: the entry keeps its own name and hash. `static member split (decisions : ImportDecision list) : ImportSplit` MUST return all decisions in `awaiting`, preserving input order, including `SameContentHash` and independent rows. No store is read, nothing is applied, and no other member is added. (4) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs` (`module ImportDecisionTests`), appended to the compile list after `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` with no comment. Its envelopes come from `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`, and a changed one is sealed through `LibraryEntryContent.sealed` (step 30). Its held entries are test-local `HeldEntry` records built from those envelopes. The origin is `CatalogueImportOrigin (CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue, CatalogueName \"Built-in\")` unless a fact says otherwise. (a) `a new id is added, or skipped`. (b) `the same id with the same hash is reused and offers nothing else`. (c) `a version not held is added, and only a protected built-in from its own catalogue moves the latest`: Silicon's version 2 under the Built-in origin moves the latest. The same envelope under the origin of a test-local `Lab` catalogue keeps it, as do a user material's version 2 and a built-in version 2 when the held latest is 3. (d) `the same id and version with another hash, or an id held as another kind, is a divergence forked by default`. (e) `a new id with a held entry's name collides, side by side by default, with a re-binding to each held entry`: a `Lab` material named `Silicon` against two held `Silicon` entries offers one `RebindToHeldEntry` for each, in order, and then `SkipIncomingEntry`, and its `rowName` is `Silicon — from Lab`. (f) `an active entry its catalogue no longer lists is retired`. (g) `every decision row awaits confirmation`: `split` of one row per status MUST return all six rows in order. (h) `a row naming an entry that awaits a choice waits with it`: `split` of a colliding category, a new material in that category, a new sample of that material and an unrelated new source MUST answer all four rows as awaiting, in input order. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` gains `an entry's references are its category and its materials`: Silicon's content names exactly its `categoryOpt`'s category, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s names exactly `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial`, and a source names nothing.", "acceptance": "After the table lands, `CatalogueImport.fs` MUST declare `ImportDecision` with `decide`, `unlisted` and `split`, and no store or caller MUST change; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a new id is added, or skipped`, `the same id with the same hash is reused and offers nothing else`, `a version not held is added, and only a protected built-in from its own catalogue moves the latest`, `the same id and version with another hash, or an id held as another kind, is a divergence forked by default`, `a new id with a held entry's name collides, side by side by default, with a re-binding to each held entry`, `an active entry its catalogue no longer lists is retired`, `every decision row awaits confirmation`, `a row naming an entry that awaits a choice waits with it` and `an entry's references are its category and its materials`, the count rising by 9; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a new id is added, or skipped", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.the same id with the same hash is reused and offers nothing else", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a version not held is added, and only a protected built-in from its own catalogue moves the latest", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.the same id and version with another hash, or an id held as another kind, is a divergence forked by default", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a new id with a held entry's name collides, side by side by default, with a re-binding to each held entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.an active entry its catalogue no longer lists is retired", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.every decision row awaits confirmation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a row naming an entry that awaits a choice waits with it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.an entry's references are its category and its materials", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.ImportDecision", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.HeldEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S31-DECISION-TABLE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 94, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [92, 93], "how_to": "The import seam reads what the library holds and writes whole entry versions, so an imported entry keeps its own version, provenance and hash (001 §B 'Per-entry import decision'; '`SeedingProxy` / `seedAll` become `CatalogueImport`: the same seam shape, fed from parsed files; the in-memory implementation stays as the test double'; the S3.1 brief: the apply function writes through the stores, and nothing else writes; S2.3 interpretation 9). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `CatalogueImportError` keeps its three cases and gains `InvalidImportChoiceErr` (a choice whose action its row does not offer), `DanglingReferenceErr` (a written entry names an entry the same apply skips or re-binds) and `EntryHashingErr` (an entry could not be sealed), each `of reason : string` naming the entry. `describe` gains a line for each, in step 39's form. (2) `EntryVersionPut = { envelope : LibraryEntryEnvelope; latest : LatestMove }` is one version to store. (3) `CatalogueImportProxy` stays `[<ReferenceEquality>]`, and five fields replace its four save fields. `tryHeldEntry : LibraryEntryId -> Result<HeldEntry option, CatalogueImportError>` answers what the library holds for an id (step 93). `heldEntriesNamed : LibraryEntryKind -> EntryName -> Result<HeldEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers the held entries of the kind whose latest version has the name. `heldEntriesOf : CatalogueId -> Result<HeldEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers the held entries whose latest provenance is `BuiltInProvenance` of the catalogue. `putEntryVersion : EntryVersionPut -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` stores the envelope as a version of its entry, `ActiveEntry` and unpinned. It becomes the entry's latest when the entry had none or the put says `MoveLatestVersion`. It answers `ImportRejectedErr` for a version the entry already holds and for an id held as another kind, so a put never overwrites. `retireEntry : LibraryEntryId -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` marks the entry's latest version `InactiveEntry`; an id not held is `ImportRejectedErr`. The record's doc states this contract in one to three lines. (4) `ofStores` (step 80) keeps its signature and becomes the in-memory implementation of (3). A closure-local map, as in `CatalogueProxy.createInMemory` (`CatalogueFiles.fs`, step 32), holds each put entry's envelopes in ascending version order, its latest version and the lifecycle of that latest. The five fields read and write that map. A put of an id the map does not hold first decodes the envelope with its kind's decoder (step 25) and pushes the value through the store's write verb, as step 80's adapters do: `UndecodableEntryErr`, or `ImportRejectedErr` with the store's reason, stops the put before the map changes. So the four stores hold every new entry; a later version or a retirement is the seam's own. Its doc says so in one to three lines. `createInMemory ()` keeps its signature and body. (5) On the proxy, `member this.decideCatalogue (catalogue : CatalogueData) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` uses the origin `CatalogueImportOrigin (catalogue.manifest.id, catalogue.manifest.name)`. For each envelope, in row order, it calls `tryHeldEntry`. When that answers `None`, it calls `heldEntriesNamed` for the envelope's kind and name. It then calls `ImportDecision.decide` (step 93). Then each entry of `heldEntriesOf catalogue.manifest.id` that is `ActiveEntry` and named by no manifest row is `ImportDecision.unlisted`. The first read error stops it. (6) `[<ReferenceEquality>] CatalogueImportContext = { proxy : CatalogueImportProxy; sealEntry : LibraryEntryContent -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, CatalogueImportError>; newEntryId : unit -> LibraryEntryId }` follows the `*Context` convention (AGENTS.md): the seam plus the providers that a fork needs. Domain does not hash (step 26), and the id is injected so that a test is deterministic. Three members: (a) `member this.apply (choices : ImportChoice list) : Result<ImportOutcome, CatalogueImportError>` uses `EntryRebinding = { incoming : LibraryEntryId; held : LibraryEntryId }`, `EntryFork = { original : LibraryEntryId; fork : LibraryEntryId }` and `ImportOutcome = { rebindings : EntryRebinding list; forks : EntryFork list }`. It first checks every choice: its action MUST be the row's `defaultAction` or one of its `alternatives`, else `InvalidImportChoiceErr`. A choice that writes its incoming entry (an add, a version or a fork) whose content's `referencedEntryIds` names the `entryId` of a choice that skips or re-binds is `DanglingReferenceErr` naming both. Nothing is written before these checks pass. It then writes in reference order: categories, materials, samples, sources, polarizers and detectors, in choice order within a kind, with every `RetireHeldEntry` last. `AddIncomingEntry` puts the envelope with `MoveLatestVersion`, and `AddIncomingVersion move` puts it with `move`. `ForkIncomingEntry` takes the incoming content with `id = newEntryId ()`, `version = VersionNumber.first` and `provenance = ForkProvenance { originalId; originalVersion; originalProvenance }` of the incoming content (step 91). It seals that content through `sealEntry`, puts it with `MoveLatestVersion`, and records the `EntryFork`. `RebindToHeldEntry h` records the `EntryRebinding` and writes nothing. `ReuseHeldEntry` and `SkipIncomingEntry` write nothing. `RetireHeldEntry` calls `retireEntry`. The first failure stops the apply, and the writes before it stay (step 40's rule). (b) `member this.importCatalogue (catalogue : CatalogueData) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` MUST run `decideCatalogue` and return every row, without calling `apply` or writing any entry. The caller MUST confirm the complete choice list before `apply` (.spec-md §3.7). (c) `member this.importFrom (catalogue : CatalogueProxy) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` reads it (`CatalogueUnreadableErr`) and imports it. The proxy's `importCatalogue` and `importFrom` (step 40) are deleted, because these replace them. (7) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`, `module CatalogueImportStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `LibraryBackupStore.fs` (step 86), with one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It holds `type CatalogueImportContext with static member create (proxy : CatalogueImportProxy) : CatalogueImportContext`. Its `sealEntry` is `LibraryEntryContent.sealed` (step 30), mapping a `StorageError` to `EntryHashingErr` with its `describe`. Its `newEntryId` mints a new GUID. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.1. (8) Callers. `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 41) imports the loaded catalogue through `(CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy).importCatalogue`. The test fixture MUST explicitly confirm all returned defaults through `apply` before answering the stores; any error MUST fail the fixture with its diagnostic. `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:DefaultStores.create` (steps 42, 58) imports through `(CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy).importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`; an `Error e` is logged as today. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`' compose (steps 88, 89) imports into a created database through `(CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores …)).importFrom`, over the same stores and catalogue as today. Production composition MUST retain the returned decisions without applying defaults; the startup report and Launcher handoff consume them in steps 98–112. The test-only DefaultStores and all test fixtures MUST explicitly apply their chosen defaults, so test setup is deliberate confirmation, not production startup policy. No retry, cache, option or other field is added. (9) Tests. In `CatalogueImportProxyTests`, `recordingProxy` holds an empty library: `tryHeldEntry` answers `None`, both lists answer `[]`, and it records every put and retirement on its tape, refusing a put when the fact's predicate says so. Its facts drive `CatalogueImportContext.create` over it, with `newEntryId` replaced by a fixed test-local id. `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures`: the tape is every category envelope, then every material, sample, source, polarizer and detector envelope, each put once with `MoveLatestVersion`, in row order within a kind. `importCatalogue stops at the first rejected entry and answers its ImportRejectedErr`: refusing every material leaves every category put and nothing else. `every import error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases. `a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)` holds over the new proxy. The class gains three facts. `apply refuses an action its row does not offer, and a write that would leave a reference dangling, before it writes`: a choice of `ReuseHeldEntry` on an `EntryIdNotHeld` row answers `InvalidImportChoiceErr`, and a sample added while its material is skipped answers `DanglingReferenceErr`; in both cases the tape stays empty. `apply forks a divergent entry under a minted id whose provenance keeps the original`: the one put is the fixed id at version 1, under `ForkProvenance` of the original's id, version and provenance, with the hash that `sealed` gives that content, and the outcome names the fork. `apply writes nothing for a reuse, a skip or a re-binding, answers the binding, and retires after every put`: over a retired row, an add, a reuse, a skip and a re-binding, given in that order, the tape holds the add's put and then the retirement, and the outcome holds the one re-binding. `an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr` moves to `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests`, over `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, because only the in-memory double decodes: the import answers `UndecodableEntryErr (MissingEntryFieldErr _)` after the category alone is put. `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests`' other facts import through `CatalogueImportContext.create` of `createInMemory ()`'s proxy and keep their assertions. `importing a catalogue the stores already hold is refused` becomes `importing a catalogue the stores already hold reuses every entry and writes nothing`: a second `importCatalogue` through the same context MUST answer every `SameContentHash` row, whose explicitly confirmed defaults write nothing, and every store lists what it listed. `LibraryDatabaseTests`' `importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores` imports through `CatalogueImportContext.create` over `ofStores` of the four database stores. Its second import through the same context MUST return every reuse row; explicitly applying their defaults MUST leave the stores unchanged. All tape, failure and decoded-entry assertions in this step MUST call `importCatalogue`/`importFrom` to obtain the complete rows, assert the tape is empty, and then explicitly `apply` the chosen defaults before asserting writes or the first write error. Test fixture imports MUST use that same two-phase sequence; no production helper MAY confirm for a user. TestAppScope.freshAppContext and the AppContextTests population fixtures MUST explicitly confirm the complete default choices returned by importFrom after creating their database context. Tests asserting startup identification MUST retain the unconfirmed context instead. These test-only callers MUST be updated together with the import seam.", "acceptance": "After the seam is reshaped, `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST declare `tryHeldEntry`, `heldEntriesNamed`, `heldEntriesOf`, `putEntryVersion` and `retireEntry` and no save field, and `CatalogueImportContext` MUST declare `apply`, `importCatalogue` and `importFrom`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `apply refuses an action its row does not offer, and a write that would leave a reference dangling, before it writes`, `apply forks a divergent entry under a minted id whose provenance keeps the original`, `apply writes nothing for a reuse, a skip or a re-binding, answers the binding, and retires after every put`, `an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr` and `importing a catalogue the stores already hold reuses every entry and writes nothing`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.importCatalogue stops at the first rejected entry and answers its ImportRejectedErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every import error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.a CatalogueImportProxy compares by reference (the [<ReferenceEquality>] contract)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.apply refuses an action its row does not offer, and a write that would leave a reference dangling, before it writes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.apply forks a divergent entry under a minted id whose provenance keeps the original", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.apply writes nothing for a reuse, a skip or a re-binding, answers the binding, and retires after every put", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importFrom fills empty in-memory stores with the whole Built-in catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importFrom an unreadable catalogue imports nothing and answers CatalogueUnreadableErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importing a catalogue the stores already hold is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importing a catalogue the stores already hold reuses every entry and writes nothing", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CatalogueImportStore.CatalogueImportContext.create", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "obligations": ["S31-ENVELOPE-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 95, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S3.1e", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0008", "name": "CatalogueImportProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [94, "STORE_XDUO_0008"], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests"], "how_to": "The import seam over the library database (001 §B; 001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite `create`', 'Contract tests'; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`). Imported built-ins now reach the database as their own envelopes, provenance included (S2.3 interpretation 9). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportError` gains `ImportStoreUnavailableErr of reason : string`, raised when the store beneath the seam failed, with a `describe` line. `ofStores`' body moves into `createInMemory`, whose signature is unchanged, and `ofStores` is deleted; its doc moves with it. The database has its own implementation now, so no product code pushes catalogue values through the database stores. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs` (step 94) gains `type CatalogueImportProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : CatalogueImportProxy`. It carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite import seam (001 §B, §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]`. Every field is one `database.run` (step 62) over step 67's operations. A write ends with one `SaveChanges ()`, and every `StorageError` is answered as `ImportStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. `tryHeldEntry id` answers `None` without the entry's `LatestVersion` row. Otherwise it reads the latest through `tryLatestStored` for its kind, name, lifecycle and provenance, and the versions from the `Version` and `ContentHash` columns of the entry's `EntryVersion` rows, ascending. Step 63 writes those columns from the very envelope, so no payload is parsed for them. `heldEntriesNamed kind name` answers, as `tryHeldEntry` does, every entry whose latest row (`LatestVersion` joined to `EntryVersion` on id and version) has `Kind` = `kind.value` and `Name` = `name.value`. `heldEntriesOf c` does the same for latest rows whose `CatalogueId` is `c`. `putEntryVersion put` answers `ImportRejectedErr` naming the id and the version when `tryStoredVersion` finds that version, and naming both kinds when the latest is another kind. Otherwise it stages `stageVersion { envelope = put.envelope; state = { lifecycle = ActiveEntry; pin = VersionUnpinned } }`, then `stageLatest` when the put says `MoveLatestVersion` or the entry has no latest. `retireEntry id` answers `ImportRejectedErr` without a latest; otherwise it restages the latest with `InactiveEntry` and keeps its pin. No cache, retry, transaction option or second connection is added. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`' compose imports into a created database through `(CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase database)).importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltInUnder locations.shippedCatalogueFolder)`. The `LibraryEntryStore.createInDatabase` that only this import composed goes. (4) Tests: `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` becomes the import seam's contract suite (the step 66 pattern). `[<AbstractClass>] type CatalogueImportContract ()` declares `abstract freshImport : unit -> ImportStoreSet`. The test-local `ImportStoreSet = { context : CatalogueImportContext; categories : CategoryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; samples : SampleProxy; presets : LibraryProxy }` holds empty stores and the import context over them. The four store facts become its `[<Fact>]` members with their assertions. `importFrom fills empty in-memory stores with the whole Built-in catalogue` is renamed `importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue`; the others are `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value`, `importing a catalogue the stores already hold reuses every entry and writes nothing` and `importFrom an unreadable catalogue imports nothing and answers CatalogueUnreadableErr`. The contract gains `putEntryVersion refuses a version the entry holds and an id held as another kind`: a second put of a version that `importFrom` added, and a put of a sample envelope under a material's id, each answer `ImportRejectedErr`, and `tryHeldEntry` answers what it answered before. `type CatalogueImportInMemoryTests () = inherit CatalogueImportContract ()` keeps the class name over `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` and keeps `an entry that does not decode stops the import with UndecodableEntryErr` as its own member. `type CatalogueImportSqliteTests () = inherit CatalogueImportContract ()` implements `IDisposable`, disposing every database it opened. Its `freshImport` opens `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\")` and composes `createInDatabase` with the four database stores (steps 69, 71, 74, 79). Its own facts: `the database import holds every Built-in envelope byte for byte under its own provenance`: after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, `latestStoredOfKind` of every kind answers exactly the catalogue's envelopes of that kind, equal, `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` included. `a database failure below the import seam is ImportStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers it. `LibraryDatabaseTests`' `importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores` moves into the contract's renamed fact, which this class runs. `every import error renders its condition and its payload` covers `ImportStoreUnavailableErr`. The AppContext importFrom call MUST retain its complete decisions without applying them; the test-side population helpers MUST explicitly apply the complete default choice list before checking populated stores. No production path MAY silently confirm those rows. TestAppScope.freshAppContext and the AppContextTests population fixtures MUST explicitly confirm the complete default choices returned by importFrom after creating their database context. Tests asserting startup identification MUST retain the unconfirmed context instead. These test-only callers MUST be updated together with the import seam.", "acceptance": "After the database seam lands, `CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase` MUST exist, `ofStores` MUST NOT, and `AppContext.fs` MUST compose the import over `createInDatabase`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every `CatalogueImportContract` fact over both `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests`, `the database import holds every Built-in envelope byte for byte under its own provenance` and `a database failure below the import seam is ImportStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 7; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importFrom fills empty in-memory stores with the whole Built-in catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.importFrom fills an empty library database through the database stores", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.importing a catalogue the stores already hold reuses every entry and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.importFrom an unreadable catalogue imports nothing and answers CatalogueUnreadableErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.putEntryVersion refuses a version the entry holds and an id held as another kind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.putEntryVersion refuses a version the entry holds and an id held as another kind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.the database import holds every Built-in envelope byte for byte under its own provenance", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a database failure below the import seam is ImportStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every import error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy.ofStores", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"], "preserves_obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CatalogueImportStore.CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "obligations": ["S31-SQLITE-IMPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 96, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [95], "how_to": "Every row of 001 §B's table over both stores (the S3.1 brief: 'one fact per decision row over the in-memory stores and the same rows over SQLite :memory:'; 001 Summary: 'user entries are never touched'). This step adds facts only. Each is a `[<Fact>]` member of `CatalogueImportContract` (step 95), so `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` both run it. A fact sets up the library through `putEntryVersion` and builds its catalogues with `CatalogueData.tryCreate` (step 32), sealing changed contents through `LibraryEntryContent.sealed`. It replaces the context's `newEntryId` with a fixed test-local id, MUST plan through `importCatalogue`, assert no writes for the complete row list, and explicitly confirm chosen rows through `apply`. Every assertion reads `tryHeldEntry` or `heldEntriesNamed`, and the catalogue `Lab` is a test-local id. (a) `a new id is imported after confirmation as its own latest version`. (b) `the same id with the same hash is reused and nothing is written`: a held envelope stays its entry's only version. (c) `a version not held is added after confirmation, and the latest moves only for a protected built-in from its own catalogue`. Silicon's version 2, imported in a catalogue under `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, becomes the latest. A user material's version 2 in `Lab` is held while its latest stays 1, and so is a built-in's version 2 in `Lab`. (d) `the same id and version with another hash awaits a choice, and forking imports it under a new id that keeps the original`. Silicon's version 1 with another description is answered as one `DivergentContent` row, and nothing changes. Applying its `byDefault` holds the fixed id at version 1 under `ForkProvenance` of Silicon's version 1, and Silicon is unchanged. On a fresh store, applying `SkipIncomingEntry` writes nothing. (e) `a new id with a held entry's name awaits a choice; side by side keeps both and a re-binding writes nothing`. A `Lab` material named `Silicon` awaits as `NameCollision`. Its default leaves `heldEntriesNamed` holding both entries. On a fresh store, `RebindToHeldEntry` of Silicon's id writes nothing and answers that binding. (f) `an active built-in its catalogue no longer lists is retired after confirmation and stays held`: a Built-in catalogue without Silicon leaves Silicon `InactiveEntry` with its versions. (g) `a user entry is never touched by a catalogue import`. A user material is put. A Built-in catalogue that does not list it retires nothing, and a `Lab` catalogue that lists its version 2 keeps its latest at 1. (h) `a row that names an entry awaiting a choice waits with it and nothing of either is written` : a `Lab` category named like a held category and a new `Lab` material in it both await, and neither is held. `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` gains `an imported version is what the database stores answer, and a retired built-in stays resolvable`. After (c)'s Built-in version 2, `materials.tryGetMaterial MaterialIds.silicon` answers the version 2 value, and `resolveVersion` of version 1 the version 1 value. After (f), `listMaterials ActiveOnly` omits Silicon and `resolveVersion` still answers it. No product code changes. Every row-status fact MUST exercise the unchanged-library state before confirmation and its named outcome after confirmation. Dependency and unrelated-source rows MUST all remain pending together.", "acceptance": "After the rows land, every 001 §B row MUST have a `CatalogueImportContract` fact run by both `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a new id is imported after confirmation as its own latest version`, `the same id with the same hash is reused and nothing is written`, `a version not held is added after confirmation, and the latest moves only for a protected built-in from its own catalogue`, `the same id and version with another hash awaits a choice, and forking imports it under a new id that keeps the original`, `a new id with a held entry's name awaits a choice; side by side keeps both and a re-binding writes nothing`, `an active built-in its catalogue no longer lists is retired after confirmation and stays held`, `a user entry is never touched by a catalogue import`, `a row that names an entry awaiting a choice waits with it and nothing of either is written` over both stores and `an imported version is what the database stores answer, and a retired built-in stays resolvable`, the count rising by 17; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a new id is imported after confirmation as its own latest version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a new id is imported after confirmation as its own latest version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the same id with the same hash is reused and nothing is written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.the same id with the same hash is reused and nothing is written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a version not held is added after confirmation, and the latest moves only for a protected built-in from its own catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a version not held is added after confirmation, and the latest moves only for a protected built-in from its own catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the same id and version with another hash awaits a choice, and forking imports it under a new id that keeps the original", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.the same id and version with another hash awaits a choice, and forking imports it under a new id that keeps the original", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a new id with a held entry's name awaits a choice; side by side keeps both and a re-binding writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a new id with a held entry's name awaits a choice; side by side keeps both and a re-binding writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.an active built-in its catalogue no longer lists is retired after confirmation and stays held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.an active built-in its catalogue no longer lists is retired after confirmation and stays held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a user entry is never touched by a catalogue import", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a user entry is never touched by a catalogue import", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a row that names an entry awaiting a choice waits with it and nothing of either is written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a row that names an entry awaiting a choice waits with it and nothing of either is written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.an imported version is what the database stores answer, and a retired built-in stays resolvable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-ROWS-BOTH-STORES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 97, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [96], "how_to": "The catalogue-import log (001 §B 'Import on every start': the hash 'recorded in the database'; 001 §C 'What it holds': 'the catalogue-import log'; .spec-md §3.8: a registered catalogue folder is an import-log row). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`. `CatalogueImportTime of DateTime` (UTC) and `CatalogueEntryCount of int` each carry `.value`. `CatalogueImportLogEntry = { catalogueId : CatalogueId; folder : FolderName; manifestHash : ContentHash; importedAt : CatalogueImportTime; entryCount : CatalogueEntryCount }` records which catalogue was absorbed, from which folder, under which manifest hash, when, and with how many entries. `FolderName` is `Softellect.Sys.Primitives.FolderName`, as `DataLocations` holds it (step 81). Each doc is one line. `CatalogueImportProxy` gains three fields. `loggedImports : unit -> Result<CatalogueImportLogEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers every row, ordered ordinally by folder. `logImport : CatalogueImportLogEntry -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` adds the catalogue's row, or replaces it. `forgetImport : CatalogueId -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` removes the row; an unlogged id changes nothing and answers `Ok ()`. The record's doc names the log. `createInMemory` keeps the log in a closure-local map keyed by catalogue id. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`. `type CatalogueImportLogEntry with member this.importRow : LibraryCatalogueImportRow` and `type LibraryCatalogueImportRow with member this.toLogEntry : CatalogueImportLogEntry` map step 60's columns `CatalogueId`, `Folder`, `ManifestHash`, `ImportedAtUtc` and `EntryCount`. Each carries step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark, as `versionRow` and `toStoredVersion` (step 63) do. `createInDatabase`'s three fields work over `CatalogueImports`: they list the rows, add or overwrite the tracked row, and remove it, each in one `run`. (3) Tests. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `recordingProxy` gains an empty log. `CatalogueImportContract` gains `the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id`: two entries are logged under folders `b` and `a` and listed `a` first. Logging the first again with another hash replaces its row. Forgetting it leaves the other, and forgetting it again answers `Ok ()`. Every listed entry equals the one logged, its time included.", "acceptance": "After the log lands, `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST declare `loggedImports`, `logImport` and `forgetImport` over both stores; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id` over both `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.the import log records, replaces and forgets a catalogue by its id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportLogEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S31-IMPORT-LOG"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 98, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [97], "how_to": "Under 001 §B and .spec-md §3.7, startup MUST identify every row before confirmation. In OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs, CatalogueImportContext MUST gain hashManifest : CatalogueManifest -> Result<ContentHash, CatalogueImportError>, now : unit -> CatalogueImportTime and openCatalogue : FolderName -> CatalogueProxy. OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs MUST supply manifestHash, the clock and CatalogueProxy.create at the IO boundary; tests MUST replace the clock. PendingCatalogueImport MUST contain entry : CatalogueImportLogEntry and decisions : ImportDecision list. FolderImportResult MUST have CatalogueUnchanged of CatalogueImportLogEntry, CatalogueImported of CatalogueImportLogEntry (a settled result), and CatalogueAwaitsChoices of PendingCatalogueImport. FolderImportReport MUST hold folder and outcome; StartupImportReport MUST hold folders and expose pending in folder order. importFolder MUST read and hash the manifest and return CatalogueUnchanged without reading entry files or writing anything when its logged hash matches. Otherwise it MUST read the catalogue, obtain every decision through importCatalogue, and return CatalogueAwaitsChoices containing all rows, including Reuse and unrelated additions. It MUST NOT apply a row, retire an entry or log the changed hash. importOnStart MUST process the shipped folder first, then logged folders other than the built-in catalogue in log order, returning each folder error without stopping other folders; a loggedImports failure MUST be returned. No retries or extra cache are added. In CatalogueImportContract, both implementations MUST exercise the five declared facts: (a) first startup returns all rows pending with no writes; after the fixture explicitly applies every default and logs the successful import, the next unchanged start MUST skip entry reads even if an entry file was deleted; (b) a changed built-in version MUST leave held versions and latest unchanged before confirmation, then add the new version and move latest after explicit apply and log; (c) a mixed collision, Reuse and new-source catalogue MUST return all rows pending, write neither source nor log, and do the same after cancellation and another start; (d) logged folders MUST be reported in order, a changed valid folder pending and an unreadable folder an error, without either being logged; (e) after confirmation, user entries MUST retain the version/latest/retirement safeguards of the per-entry table. Fresh GUID-named folders MUST live under AppContext.BaseDirectory/CatalogueImportTests. Step 99 MUST replace the fixture's explicit apply-and-log sequence with settle, preserving the same observations.", "acceptance": "After startup identifies a changed catalogue, every decision row MUST remain pending and library entries, latest pointers, lifecycle and import log MUST stay unchanged until confirmation; unchanged manifest hashes MUST skip entry reads; both-store CatalogueImportContract facts and the required gates MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.the start-up import logs the shipped catalogue and skips it, reading no entry file, while its manifest hash is unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.the start-up import logs the shipped catalogue and skips it, reading no entry file, while its manifest hash is unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a changed built-in catalogue mints the new version and moves the latest on the next start", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a changed built-in catalogue mints the new version and moves the latest on the next start", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a changed catalogue holds every row without writes or logging until confirmation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a changed catalogue holds every row without writes or logging until confirmation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.every logged folder is re-checked on start, and a failing one is reported without stopping the others", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.every logged folder is re-checked on start, and a failing one is reported without stopping the others", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a user entry is never touched by the start-up import", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a user entry is never touched by the start-up import", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.StartupImportReport", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S31-STARTUP-IMPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 99, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.1i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [98], "how_to": "Extra read-only catalogue folders, and settling a catalogue whose rows waited (001 §B 'Extra catalogue folders: read-only folders on a share or a git checkout', 'nothing is overwritten silently'; .spec-md §3.8; the S3.1 brief: registering imports the folder and logs it; unregistering removes the log row and keeps its entries). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportError` gains `CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr of reason : string`, with its `describe` line. (2) `member this.registerFolder (folder : FolderName) : Result<FolderImportResult, CatalogueImportError>` on `CatalogueImportContext` reads the folder's manifest through `openCatalogue` and `readManifest`. A manifest whose catalogue is `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, or already in `loggedImports`, is `CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr` naming the folder, the catalogue and the folder it is logged under. Otherwise the answer is `importFolder folder` (step 98). The folder is only read, so its permissions stay its own. (3) `member this.settle (pending : PendingCatalogueImport) (choices : ImportChoice list) : Result<ImportOutcome, CatalogueImportError>` completes an awaiting import once its rows are chosen; the import dialog (S3.2) calls it. Every pending row MUST have exactly one choice, matched by `entryId`, and no choice may name a row the pending import does not hold; otherwise the answer is `InvalidImportChoiceErr`. It then runs `apply`, and on success logs `{ pending.entry with importedAt = now () }`, so the next start skips the catalogue. (4) `member this.registeredFolders () : Result<CatalogueImportLogEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` on `CatalogueImportProxy` is `loggedImports` without the `CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` row. Unregistering a folder is `forgetImport` (step 97): its row goes, and every entry it brought stays, because user data never vanishes silently. Each doc is one to three lines. (5) Tests, new members of `CatalogueImportContract` over folders made as in step 98. (a) `registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder`: after the shipped start, registering a `Lab` folder answers `CatalogueImported`, its entries are held, and `registeredFolders` lists exactly its row. (b) `registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused`: a folder holding the Built-in catalogue, and the `Lab` folder a second time, each answer `CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr`, and nothing changes. (c) `unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it`: after `forgetImport`, the `Lab` entries are still held, and the next start's report has no `Lab` row. (d) `settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused`, over step 98 (c)'s setup. Settling with no choice answers `InvalidImportChoiceErr` and logs nothing. Settling with every pending row's `byDefault` MUST hold both `Lab glass` materials and the new source, then log the catalogue, and the next start answers `CatalogueUnchanged`. `every import error renders its condition and its payload` (`CatalogueImportProxyTests`) covers the new case. Registration MUST return all rows as CatalogueAwaitsChoices and leave entries and log unchanged. Every registration fixture in this step MUST explicitly call settle over the complete pending list before asserting registeredFolders, duplicate registration or unregister behavior; settle MUST replace step 98 fixtures' explicit apply-and-log sequence. A partial selection including only the collision MUST fail before any write.", "acceptance": "After registration lands, `CatalogueImportContext` MUST declare `registerFolder` and `settle` and `CatalogueImportProxy` `registeredFolders`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder`, `registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused`, `unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it`, `settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused` over both stores and `every import error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.registering a catalogue folder imports and logs it, and lists it as the one registered folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.registering the Built-in catalogue or a registered catalogue again is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.unregistering a folder forgets it and keeps its entries, and the next start no longer reads it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.settling a pending import applies the chosen rows and logs the catalogue, and an incomplete choice is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every import error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-REGISTRATION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 100, "anchor": "WIRE", "ac": "AC-S3.1j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [99], "how_to": "The app imports its catalogues on every start (001 §B 'Import on every start'; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`: it imports the catalogues on start; §3.7, §3.8; the S3.1 brief: the rows that need a choice are held in the AppContext for S3.2's dialog). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the record gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` is the library's import seam over the database, through which the Library window registers folders. `pendingImports : PendingCatalogueImport list` holds the start-up imports whose rows wait for a choice. `compose` (step 89) builds `catalogueImports = CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase database)` (steps 95, 98). It runs `catalogueImports.importOnStart (CatalogueProxy.builtInFolderUnder locations.shippedCatalogueFolder)` (step 92) on every start, created or opened, so step 88's `CreatedLibraryDatabase` branch and its import are deleted. An `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe` and leaves `pendingImports` empty. For an `Ok report`, every folder report whose outcome is an `Error e` is logged naming the folder and `e.describe`, and `pendingImports` is `report.pending`. The app MUST start with its held database state and pending decisions; no new catalogue row is applied before the Launcher confirms it. `create`'s and `recreateLibrary`'s docs say, in no more words, that every start imports the shipped catalogue and the registered folders by manifest hash. `LibraryDatabase.origin` (step 84) keeps its members, because the facts in `LibraryDatabaseTests` and the backup suites still read it. (2) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE': the parenthesis naming `CatalogueImportProxy.importFrom` (step 58) names `CatalogueImportContext.importOnStart`, which imports `Catalogue/Builtin/` and every registered catalogue folder on every start. (3) Tests, in `AppContextTests`. Each uses `TestAppScope.fileLocations` (step 88) of the module, with `shippedCatalogueFolder` set to a fresh folder under the test output. That folder's `Builtin` subfolder is written through `CatalogueProxy.create` (step 33) from `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`. `create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one`: the first create lists Silicon with its description. The `Builtin` folder is rewritten with Silicon's version 2, whose description differs and whose name, and so file name, is unchanged. The second create's `materials.tryGetMaterial MaterialIds.silicon` answers the new description, and `resolveVersion` of version 1 answers the old one. A third create over the unchanged folder leaves the Built-in row of `catalogueImports.proxy.loggedImports ()` exactly as the second create logged it. `create holds every changed-catalogue row pending and writes nothing before confirmation`. After the first create, a user material named `Lab glass` is saved through its `materials`. The `Builtin` folder is rewritten with a new-id material named `Lab glass` and a new source added, both under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. The second create's pendingImports MUST hold one catalogue with every row, including the collision, reuse rows and the new source; neither the new material nor the source is held and the import log is unchanged. The step-88 facts `create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again` and `create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores` keep their assertions, because an unchanged manifest is skipped. Each AppContext fixture that needs a populated catalogue MUST explicitly settle every pending import before reading its library. The first-create, changed-version and reopen facts MUST assert no entry/log mutation before settlement, then retain their original post-confirmation values and counts. Startup MUST never invoke that fixture confirmation path. In OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs, freshAppContext MUST explicitly settle every pending catalogue with its full default choice list before returning a populated test context. Tests of unconfirmed startup MUST call AppContext.create directly. File-backed fixtures MUST use the same explicit sequence; product composition MUST never call this test helper.", "acceptance": "After the wiring, `AppContext.create` MUST run `importOnStart` over the shipped catalogue on every start and hold its awaiting rows in `pendingImports`, and `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT read `LibraryDatabase.origin`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one` and `create holds every changed-catalogue row pending and writes nothing before confirmation`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-APP-IMPORTS-ON-START"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create holds every changed-catalogue row pending and writes nothing before confirmation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-APP-IMPORTS-ON-START"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 101, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.1k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [100], "how_to": "'Register catalogue folder…' in the Library window (001 §B 'Extra catalogue folders'; .spec-md §3.8; §10: discoverability ('Register catalogue folder…' is in the Library window) and action buttons; the S3.1 brief). Unregister has no undo and needs none: it keeps every entry, and registering the folder again restores the row. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowContext` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:153`) gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `libraryBackups` (step 90), with a one-line doc. (b) `LibraryWindowError` gains `CatalogueImportRefusedErr of CatalogueImportError`, and its `caption` renders it through `CatalogueImportError.caption`. (c) `LibraryWindowModel` (`:229`) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `importStatus : ControlCaption option` opens as `None`. `pendingImports : PendingCatalogueImport list` opens as `[]`; it holds the registrations whose rows wait for the import dialog. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains `RegisterCatalogueFolder of FolderName` and `UnregisterCatalogueFolder of CatalogueId`, each documented. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `RegisterCatalogueFolder folder` calls `context.catalogueImports.registerFolder folder` (step 99), and each outcome clears `lastError`. `Ok (CatalogueImported entry)` sets `importStatus` to `Registered catalogue folder <folder> (<n> entries).`. `Ok (CatalogueAwaitsChoices pending)` appends `pending` to `pendingImports` and sets `importStatus` to `Review <folder>; <k> entries await confirmation. Nothing has been imported or registered.`. `Ok (CatalogueUnchanged entry)` sets it to `Catalogue folder <folder> is unchanged.`. `Error e` sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr e` and clears `importStatus`. `UnregisterCatalogueFolder id` calls `context.catalogueImports.proxy.forgetImport id`. `Ok ()` sets `importStatus` to `Unregistered <folder>. Its entries stay in the library.`, naming the folder its `registeredFolders` row had, and `Error e` sets `lastError`. Neither message arms or disarms a gate. (f) The view. `verbButton` (`:1020`) becomes `verbButtonOn (id : ConstructorUiId) (label : ControlCaption) (onPressed : PointerPressedEventArgs -> unit)`, and `verbButton id label onClick` is `verbButtonOn id label (fun _ -> onClick ())`, so the look keeps one body. A private `pickCatalogueFolder (owner : Window) (onPicked : FolderName -> unit) : unit` opens `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync` with `FolderPickerOpenOptions(Title = \"Register catalogue folder\", AllowMultiple = false)`. On a confirmed pick it passes the first folder's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FolderName`, posted on the UI thread. It is wrapped so that a host without a provider changes nothing, in the shape of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`. In the verbs row (`verbsRow`, `:1104`), after the entry verbs and in Browse and Select mode alike, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton (ControlCaption \"Register catalogue folder…\")` resolves the owner window from the press, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton` does, and dispatches `RegisterCatalogueFolder` on a confirmed pick. When `context.catalogueImports.proxy.registeredFolders ()` answers at least one row, a block carrying `libraryCatalogueFoldersPanel`, titled `Catalogue folders`, follows the verbs. It holds one row per folder carrying `libraryCatalogueFolderRow entry.catalogueId.uiKey`: the folder, `imported <yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm> UTC`, `<n> entries`, and `verbButton (ConstructorUiId.libraryUnregisterCatalogueButton entry.catalogueId.uiKey) (ControlCaption \"Unregister\")`. `importStatus`, when `Some`, shows in a `TextBlock` carrying `libraryImportStatusText`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type CatalogueId with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (its GUID's text, as `CategoryId.uiKey` is) and `type CatalogueImportError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`), each with a one-line doc. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group (`UiIds.fs:498-523`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.1: `libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton` (`\"LibraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton\"`), `libraryCatalogueFoldersPanel` (`\"LibraryCatalogueFoldersPanel\"`), `libraryCatalogueFolderRow (catalogue : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"LibraryCatalogueFolderRow_{catalogue.value}\"`), `libraryUnregisterCatalogueButton (catalogue : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"LibraryUnregisterCatalogueButton_{catalogue.value}\"`) and `libraryImportStatusText` (`\"LibraryImportStatusText\"`). (4) Threading, along step 90's `libraryBackups` path, so that every Library window has the app scope's import seam. `LibraryWindow` (`LibraryWindow.fs:34`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `libraryBackups` and sets the context field. `EditorLaunchers.openLibraryWindow` and `openLibrarySelectWindow` take it after the `LibraryBackupProxy`, and `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext`. `initWith` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:475`) sets it to `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `DefaultStores.DefaultStoreSet` (`:430`) gains `catalogueImports`, the context its stores were imported through (step 94), and `initTableAndElementRotation` and `initMain` set it by record update beside `sources`. The strip's `OpenLibraryWindow` and the Select open pass `model.catalogueImports`. `Program.fs`' `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` thread `catalogueImports = context.catalogueImports` beside `libraryBackups`, and the launcher's Library button passes it. Every test construction passes one. `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` and its two `LibraryWindow(...)`, `LightSourceEditorTests`' `libraryContext`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' `libraryContext` and `ScrollExtentTests`' `LibraryWindow(...)` pass `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` passes `ctx.catalogueImports`. `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording launchers and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' Select-open stub take the extra argument. A doc that lists the window's or the launchers' stores names the import seam in no more words. (5) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`. The pure facts run over `stubContext` with an in-memory import context and a catalogue folder written through `CatalogueProxy.create` into a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryWindowTests\")`, holding one user source. `the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the five ids' texts. `RegisterCatalogueFolder holds every row for confirmation and names it in the status`: afterwards pendingImports MUST contain every row, registeredFolders MUST be empty, tryHeldEntry MUST not hold the source, and importStatus MUST name the folder. `a folder is held for the import dialog without imports or registration before confirmation`: a source with the folder's source name is put first under another id; `pendingImports` holds the one collision, `registeredFolders` is empty, and `importStatus` counts one entry waiting. `a refused registration shows its reason as the window message`: registering the same folder twice sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr (CatalogueAlreadyRegisteredErr _)`. `UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries`: `registeredFolders` is empty, the source is still held, and `importStatus` names the folder. `acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries` (trait `ui-smoke`) runs over `AppContext.create` of `TestAppScope.fileLocations`. The folder is registered through `ctx.catalogueImports.registerFolder`, and a `LibraryWindow` is composed from the context's stores, `libraryBackups` and `catalogueImports`. The window shows `libraryCatalogueFolderRow` for the folder. A press on its Unregister verb, made as the file's other acceptance facts press a verb, removes the row, `libraryImportStatusText` names the folder, and `ctx.sources.tryGetSource` still resolves the folder's source. Every setup requiring an already registered catalogue, including the ui-smoke fixture and duplicate-registration/unregister facts, MUST explicitly settle its complete pending row list before exercising that behavior. Registration itself MUST remain read-only until dialog Apply; Cancel MUST preserve both entries and log.", "acceptance": "After the Library window is wired, every Library window, opened from the launcher, the strip or a Select session, MUST carry the app scope's `CatalogueImportContext` and offer `libraryRegisterCatalogueFolderButton`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `RegisterCatalogueFolder holds every row for confirmation and names it in the status`, `a folder is held for the import dialog without imports or registration before confirmation`, `a refused registration shows its reason as the window message`, `UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the catalogue-folder UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.RegisterCatalogueFolder holds every row for confirmation and names it in the status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a folder is held for the import dialog without imports or registration before confirmation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a refused registration shows its reason as the window message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.UnregisterCatalogueFolder forgets the folder and keeps its entries", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.acceptance: the Library window lists a registered catalogue folder, and Unregister removes it and keeps its entries", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindowView.LibraryWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.EditorLaunchers", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S31-LIBRARY-REGISTER-UI"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.1 -- Import on every start and the per-entry decision table"}
{"number": 102, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [101], "how_to": "A dropped entry file is an import origin of its own, and one entry is decided on its own (001 §H 'A library entry: its `-json` file, dropped onto the Library or Materials window (§B decision table)'; 001 §B 'one table for catalogues, kit snapshots and single dropped files'; the S3.2 brief). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `ImportOrigin` (step 93) gains `DroppedFileOrigin of file : FileName`, documented as an entry file dropped onto the Library or Materials window, held by its leaf name (`FileName.leafName`). (2) `member this.describe : string` on `ImportOrigin` is its honest render (ELEV002): the catalogue's name for `CatalogueImportOrigin` and the file's text for `DroppedFileOrigin`. `ImportDecision.rowName` (step 93) reads it, so a name collision from a dropped file is `<name> — from <file>`, and one from a catalogue stays `<name> — from <catalogue name>`. (3) `ImportDecision.decide` keeps its rules. Its latest-move condition names `CatalogueImportOrigin (c, _)`, so an entry from a dropped file never moves the latest: a version not held is `AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion`. Its doc says so in one line. (4) On `CatalogueImportProxy`, `member this.decideEntry (origin : ImportOrigin) (incoming : LibraryEntryEnvelope) : Result<ImportDecision, CatalogueImportError>` holds the per-envelope body of `decideCatalogue` (step 94 (5)): `tryHeldEntry`, then `heldEntriesNamed` for the envelope's kind and name when nothing is held, then `ImportDecision.decide`. `decideCatalogue` calls it for every envelope in row order and keeps its unlisted rows, so one body decides catalogue rows, dropped files (step 104) and S4.2's kit snapshots. No store is read or written beyond that body, and no other member changes. (5) Tests: `ImportDecisionTests` gains `a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision`. Under `DroppedFileOrigin (FileName \"Silicon.material-json\")`, Silicon's built-in version 2 against its held version 1 is `VersionNotHeld` defaulting to `AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion`. A user material named `Silicon` under `DroppedFileOrigin (FileName \"lab-silicon.material-json\")` against the held Silicon is `NameCollision` whose `rowName` is `Silicon — from lab-silicon.material-json`. `describe` answers `Built-in` for the class's catalogue origin and `lab-silicon.material-json` for that file's. The facts over `decideCatalogue` keep their assertions.", "acceptance": "After the origin lands, `ImportOrigin` MUST hold `DroppedFileOrigin`, and `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST declare `decideEntry`, which `decideCatalogue` calls for every envelope; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a dropped file keeps the latest and names itself in a collision", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROP-ORIGIN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.ImportDecision", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S32-DROP-ORIGIN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-DROP-ORIGIN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 103, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [102], "how_to": "One library entry file is read on its own (001 §H: a single entry file is dropped in; 001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout'; the S3.2 brief: dropped files are parsed by S1.4's reader). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: on `LibraryEntryKind` (step 24), `static member tryOfFileName (file : FileName) : LibraryEntryKind option` answers the kind whose `extension` equals the file's extension (`FileName.tryGetExtension`), compared with `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` (the Windows rule of step 26), and `None` otherwise, a `.catalogue-json` included. Its doc is one line citing 001 §A. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs` (steps 33, 92): `type LibraryFileText with static member readEntryFile (kind : LibraryEntryKind) (file : FileName) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` reads the file's text as UTF-8 (a missing or unreadable file is `FileIoExn`; every .NET IO exception is caught here) and answers `LibraryFileText.parseEntry kind` of it (step 30), so the file's schema, version and hash are checked. It is the per-row read of `CatalogueProxy.create`'s `readCatalogue` (step 33), moved: `readCatalogue` calls `readEntryFile row.kind` for each manifest row and maps its error to `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` naming the file, as before, and the folder's entry files are the top-level files for which `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName` answers a kind. One body reads an entry file, and one rule names its kind. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.2. (3) Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` gains `a file's extension names its entry kind, ignoring case`: `Silicon.material-json` is `MaterialEntryKind`, `C:/lab/Glass.CATEGORY-JSON` is `CategoryEntryKind`, a stem followed by each of the six kinds' `extension` answers that kind, and `.catalogue-json`, `notes.txt` and `Silicon` answer `None`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `readEntryFile reads one entry file through its schema, version and hash checks`, over a folder written as the class's other facts write one: each entry file read with its row's kind answers the catalogue's envelope; a file name that does not exist answers `FileIoExn`; the sample's file read as `MaterialEntryKind` answers `SchemaValidationErr`; and the source's file with a number changed inside its payload, its hash kept, answers `ContentHashMismatchErr`. The class's facts over `readCatalogue` keep their assertions.", "acceptance": "After the read is shared, `LibraryFileText.readEntryFile` MUST be the one read of an entry file, which `readCatalogue` calls, and `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName` the one rule naming a file's kind; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a file's extension names its entry kind, ignoring case` and `readEntryFile reads one entry file through its schema, version and hash checks`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a file's extension names its entry kind, ignoring case", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-FILE-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.readEntryFile reads one entry file through its schema, version and hash checks", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-FILE-READ"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CatalogueFolderStore.LibraryFileText.readEntryFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-FILE-READ"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 104, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [103], "how_to": "Dropped entry files are decided against the library, and nothing is written (001 §H; 001 §B 'nothing is overwritten silently'; .spec-md §3.7: a dropped file always opens the dialog; the S3.2 brief: dropping one or more entry files of any kind parses them and opens the dialog). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `CatalogueImportError` gains `DroppedFileRefusedErr of reason : string` (a dropped file is not a library entry file, does not read, or contradicts another dropped file) and `UnresolvedReferenceErr of reason : string` (a dropped entry names an entry neither held nor dropped), each with a `describe` line in step 39's form. (2) `CatalogueImportContext` (steps 94, 98) gains `readEntryFile : LibraryEntryKind -> FileName -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, CatalogueImportError>`, documented as reading one entry file. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`' `create` fills it with `LibraryFileText.readEntryFile` (step 103), a `StorageError` becoming `DroppedFileRefusedErr` that names the file with the error's `describe`. `create`'s signature is unchanged, and a fact replaces the field by record update. (3) `member this.decideDroppedFiles (files : FileName list) : Result<ImportDecision list, CatalogueImportError>` on `CatalogueImportContext` works in this order. (a) A file's kind is `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName` (step 103). A file without one is refused as `<file>: not a library entry file`, and every other file is read through `readEntryFile`, a refusal keeping its reason. When any file is refused, the answer is one `DroppedFileRefusedErr` whose reason lists every refused file with its reason, one line each in drop order, so every bad file is named at once. (b) Two files holding one id and version are one entry when their hashes agree, the first file kept, and `DroppedFileRefusedErr` naming both files when they differ. (c) Every id in an entry's `content.referencedEntryIds` (step 93) MUST be the id of a dropped entry or be held (`proxy.tryHeldEntry` answers `Some`). Otherwise the answer is `UnresolvedReferenceErr` naming the entry, its file and the missing id, so an applied drop never leaves a reference dangling. (d) Each remaining entry, in drop order, is `proxy.decideEntry (DroppedFileOrigin file.leafName) envelope` (step 102). An empty list answers `Ok []`, and the first read error of the proxy is the answer. Nothing is written: the import dialog applies the rows (steps 107, 108). No retry, cache or option is added. (4) Tests: new `[<Fact>]` members of `CatalogueImportContract`, so each runs over the in-memory seam and SQLite `:memory:`. Each fact first runs `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` through `freshImport ()`'s context, whose `readEntryFile` is the real reader. Its files are written into a fresh folder, a GUID name under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"CatalogueImportTests\")`, through each envelope's `fileText` (step 30) and `writeAtomically` (step 33), named by `content.fileName`, from envelopes sealed with `LibraryEntryContent.sealed`. `dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name`: a new user material's file and Silicon's built-in file, dropped in that order, answer an `EntryIdNotHeld` row whose origin is `DroppedFileOrigin` of the first file's leaf name and a `SameContentHash` row, and `tryHeldEntry` of the new material still answers `None`. `a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file`: `notes.txt`, a `missing.material-json` that does not exist and the user material's file answer one `DroppedFileRefusedErr` whose reason names `notes.txt` and `missing.material-json` and not the material's file. `two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ`: the material's file and a copy of it under another name answer one row; the material's file and the file of a changed content at the same id and version answer `DroppedFileRefusedErr` naming both files. `a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr`: a test-local user sample whose structure names a new user material, dropped alone, answers `UnresolvedReferenceErr` naming the material's id; dropped after the material's file, the two answer two `EntryIdNotHeld` rows in drop order. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `every import error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After dropped files are decided, `CatalogueImportContext` MUST declare `readEntryFile` and `decideDroppedFiles`, which writes nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name`, `a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file`, `two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ`, `a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr` over both stores and `every import error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.dropped entry files are decided against the library, each under its own file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a dropped file that is not a library entry file or does not read is refused, naming every such file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.two dropped files of one id and version are one row when equal and refused when they differ", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a dropped entry naming an entry neither held nor dropped is UnresolvedReferenceErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every import error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-DROPPED-DECISIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 105, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [104], "how_to": "The import seam answers a held version's envelope, so the import dialog can show what an incoming entry would change (001 §B: 'with an explicit \"use my Si instead\" re-binding and a diff preview'; the S3.2 brief: the override picker carries a diff preview of the two payloads). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportProxy` gains `tryHeldEnvelope : LibraryEntryId -> VersionNumber -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope option, CatalogueImportError>`, documented as the envelope of one held version, whatever its lifecycle, and `None` when that version is not held. The in-memory double answers it from its map (step 94 (4)), and `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `recordingProxy` (step 94) answers `None`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `createInDatabase` (step 95) answers it in one `database.run` through `tryStoredVersion id version` (step 67), `Some stored` answering `stored.envelope` and every `StorageError` `ImportStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`, as its other fields do. No other field, cache or query is added. (3) Tests: `CatalogueImportContract` gains `tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held`. After `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` and a put of Silicon's version 2 (a changed description, sealed) with `KeepLatestVersion`, `tryHeldEnvelope MaterialIds.silicon.toLibraryEntryId` answers the catalogue's envelope at version 1 and the put's at version 2, and `None` at version 3; a test-local GUID answers `None`.", "acceptance": "After the read lands, both implementations of `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST answer `tryHeldEnvelope`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held` over both stores, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-HELD-ENVELOPE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.tryHeldEnvelope answers every held version's envelope and nothing for a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-HELD-ENVELOPE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-HELD-ENVELOPE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 106, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [105], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests"], "how_to": "The line diff of two entry files, which the import dialog's preview shows (001 §B 'a diff preview'; the S3.2 brief). An entry file is canonical text (step 27: sorted keys, two-space indents), so a line diff of two files compares their payloads field by field. No diff package is added. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/EntryTextDiff.fs`, `module EntryTextDiff` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `CatalogueFiles.fs` (step 32), with one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `EntryTextLine of string`, with `.value`, is one line of an entry file. `EntryDiffLine` = `SameEntryLine of EntryTextLine` | `RemovedEntryLine of EntryTextLine` | `AddedEntryLine of EntryTextLine` is one line of a comparison: the held side's lines are removed and the incoming side's added. `static member diffLines (held : EntryTextLine list) (incoming : EntryTextLine list) : EntryDiffLine list` on `EntryDiffLine` keeps the common leading and trailing lines as `SameEntryLine`. It compares the lines between them by their longest common subsequence, a dynamic-programming table over that middle alone, so a small edit to a long tabulated file stays cheap. Between two kept lines, the held side's other lines come first as `RemovedEntryLine` and then the incoming side's as `AddedEntryLine`, each in its own order. So the `SameEntryLine` and `RemovedEntryLine` lines, in order, are the held text, and the `SameEntryLine` and `AddedEntryLine` lines are the incoming text. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.2. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs` (step 30): `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.diffFrom (held : LibraryEntryEnvelope) : Result<EntryDiffLine list, StorageError>` renders both envelopes' `fileText` and splits each at `\\n`, dropping the empty segment after the final line end. It answers `EntryDiffLine.diffLines` of the held lines and this envelope's lines, and a `fileText` failure passes through. Its doc is one line. (3) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs` (`module EntryTextDiffTests`), appended to the compile list after `ImportDecisionTests.fs` (step 93) with no comment. `equal texts diff as unchanged lines only`: two equal three-line lists answer three `SameEntryLine`s in order, and two empty lists answer `[]`. `a changed line is removed and then added between the unchanged lines`: `a b c d` against `a x c d` answers `SameEntryLine a`, `RemovedEntryLine b`, `AddedEntryLine x`, `SameEntryLine c`, `SameEntryLine d`; and `a b c` against `a c` answers `SameEntryLine a`, `RemovedEntryLine b`, `SameEntryLine c`. `lines added or removed at either end leave the rest unchanged`: `x a b` against `a b` answers `RemovedEntryLine x` and then two `SameEntryLine`s; `a b` against `a b y` answers two `SameEntryLine`s and then `AddedEntryLine y`; and `a b` against `c d` answers `RemovedEntryLine a`, `RemovedEntryLine b`, `AddedEntryLine c`, `AddedEntryLine d`. In every case of the three facts, the held and the incoming texts are recovered from the answer as (1) says. `EntryFileJsonTests` gains `two versions of an entry diff by the lines of their files`: Silicon's built-in envelope and a sealed copy whose description differs answer exactly two `RemovedEntryLine`s, the held file's `contentHash` and `descriptionOpt` lines, and two `AddedEntryLine`s, the copy's; every other line of the file is a `SameEntryLine`.", "acceptance": "After the diff lands, `EntryDiffLine.diffLines` MUST answer the lines of its rule and `LibraryEntryEnvelope.diffFrom` MUST diff two entry files; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal texts diff as unchanged lines only`, `a changed line is removed and then added between the unchanged lines`, `lines added or removed at either end leave the rest unchanged`, `two versions of an entry diff by the lines of their files`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/EntryTextDiff.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests.equal texts diff as unchanged lines only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests.a changed line is removed and then added between the unchanged lines", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests.lines added or removed at either end leave the rest unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryTextDiffTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryTextDiffTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.two versions of an entry diff by the lines of their files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.EntryTextDiff.EntryDiffLine", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/EntryTextDiff.fs", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.EntryFileJson.LibraryEntryEnvelope.diffFrom", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "obligations": ["S32-ENTRY-DIFF"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 107, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [106], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests"], "how_to": "The import dialog's pure MVU (001 §B 'The decisions show as one dialog with a row per entry, and nothing is overwritten silently'; 001 §O 'Import dialog: one row per entry, its status, the default action and an override'; .spec-md §3.7, §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 the Apply / Cancel pair; the S3.2 brief). It reaches the import seam only on Apply. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `brush`, `messageColor`, `positiveBackground`, `negativeBackground`, `verbButton` and `actionButton` (the view section, `MaterialsWindowView.fs:877-924`) lose `private`. Their docs say, in no more words, that the import dialog uses the same look: one declaration serves both, the spec 0048 R2 rule `LibraryWindowView.fs` follows for `LifecycleAction`. No body changes, and no other view's copy is touched. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView`, compiled directly after `MaterialsWindowView.fs` and before `MaterialsWindow.fs` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment. The module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §B and spec 0050 S3.2, and every type, case and field has a one-line doc. (a) `ImportDialogRequest` = `SettlePendingCatalogue of PendingCatalogueImport` (a catalogue whose rows wait, step 98) | `ApplyDroppedEntries of decisions : ImportDecision list` (dropped entry files, step 104): what the dialog decides. S4.2 adds a kit snapshot's case. `member this.decisions : ImportDecision list` is the pending import's `decisions` or the dropped ones. `member this.heading : ControlCaption` is `Import from <folder>: <k> entries need a decision.` (`entry.folder` of the pending import) or `Import <n> dropped entry files.`. (b) `ImportDialogApplied = { request : ImportDialogRequest; choices : ImportChoice list; outcome : ImportOutcome }` is what an Apply did. `member this.summary : ControlCaption` is `Imported <folder> (decisions applied: <n>).` or `Imported the dropped entry files (decisions applied: <n>).`, `n` counting the choices. Every opener shows it as its status, so the text is written once. (c) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ImportDialogContext = { imports : CatalogueImportContext; request : ImportDialogRequest; onApplied : ImportDialogApplied -> unit; requestClose : unit -> unit }`, in the shape of `MaterialsWindowContext` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:154`): the composition root bakes the seam, the opener's callback and the window's close, and tests substitute recording stubs. (d) `ImportDiffState` = `NoImportDiffShown` | `ImportDiffShown of LibraryEntryId`: at most one row shows its diff. (e) `ImportDialogModel = { context : ImportDialogContext; choices : ImportChoice list; diff : ImportDiffState; lastError : CatalogueImportError option }`. `initImportDialog (context : ImportDialogContext) : ImportDialogModel` opens with the `byDefault` (step 93) of every decision of `context.request.decisions`, in order, no diff shown and no error. Rows are told apart by their decision's `entryId`, the key `settle` matches choices by (step 99). (f) `ImportDialogMsg`, each case documented: `DecideImportRow of LibraryEntryId` (the row takes its default action), `OverrideImportRow of LibraryEntryId * ImportAction` (the row takes one of its `alternatives`), `ToggleImportDiff of LibraryEntryId`, `ApplyImportChoices` and `CancelImportDialog`. (g) `updateImportDialog (msg : ImportDialogMsg) (m : ImportDialogModel) : ImportDialogModel`. `DecideImportRow id` sets the row's action to its `defaultAction`. `OverrideImportRow (id, action)` sets it when `action` is one of the row's `alternatives` and is inert otherwise, including for a row the dialog does not hold. Both clear `lastError`. `ToggleImportDiff id` shows that row's diff, or hides it when it is the one shown. `ApplyImportChoices` is the only message that reaches the seam: for `SettlePendingCatalogue p` it calls `context.imports.settle p m.choices` (step 99), and for `ApplyDroppedEntries _` it calls `context.imports.apply m.choices` (step 94). `Ok outcome` calls `context.onApplied { request = context.request; choices = m.choices; outcome = outcome }`, then `context.requestClose ()`, and clears `lastError`. `Error e` sets `lastError` to `Some e`, and the dialog stays open with its choices. `CancelImportDialog` calls `context.requestClose ()` and nothing else. (h) `importDialogView (m : ImportDialogModel) (dispatch : ImportDialogMsg -> unit) : IView` is a `DockPanel`. Docked at the bottom is one horizontal row of `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importApplyButton (ControlCaption \"Apply\") positiveBackground` and `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importCancelButton (ControlCaption \"Cancel\") negativeBackground`: one row, the boxes' margin as the gap, distinct colours, the look of the Select / Close pair. Above it, when `lastError` is `Some e`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importDialogMessage` shows `e.caption` (step 101) in `messageColor`. Docked at the top, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importDialogHeading` shows `request.heading` and the line `Nothing is imported until you press Apply.`. A `ScrollViewer` fills the rest; its vertical `StackPanel` carries `importDecisionList` and holds one block per choice. A row's block carries `importDecisionRow entryId.uiKey` and holds, in order: a line with the decision's `rowName`, its `kind.caption`, `version <v>` (the incoming content's version, or the held latest for `EntryUnlisted`) and `status.caption`; the line `Default: <decision.actionCaption decision.defaultAction>`; a `WrapPanel` holding one box per offered action, the default first and then the `alternatives` in order, each carrying `importActionOption entryId.uiKey action.uiKey` with `decision.actionCaption action` as its label. The chosen one is an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others are `verbButton`s. Pressing the default dispatches `DecideImportRow`, and an alternative `OverrideImportRow`. The `WrapPanel` sits in the vertical block, so it wraps at the window's width (AGENTS.md: never in a horizontal `StackPanel`). When the row has a diff base, a `verbButton` carrying `importDiffToggle entryId.uiKey`, labelled `Show diff` or `Hide diff` while shown, dispatches `ToggleImportDiff`. While shown, a block carrying `importDiffPreview entryId.uiKey` lists the lines of `incoming.diffFrom held` (step 106), one `TextBlock` each, prefixed `  `, `- ` or `+ `, with removed lines in `messageColor` and added lines in `Color.FromRgb(0uy, 110uy, 0uy)`. The held envelope is read through `context.imports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope` (step 105) as the view renders, as the library windows' views re-query their stores. An error shows one line with its `describe`, and `None` the line `The held version is not in the library.`. The diff base is: for `DivergentContent (incoming, held)`, the held version equal to the incoming version when `held.versions` holds it, else `held.latest`; for `VersionNotHeld (incoming, held)`, `held.latest`; for `NameCollision (incoming, sameName)`, the entry the row's `RebindToHeldEntry` names when that is its action, else the first of `sameName`, at its latest. `EntryIdNotHeld`, `SameContentHash` and `EntryUnlisted` rows have none. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type LibraryEntryId with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`, its GUID's text, as `CategoryId.uiKey`; `type LibraryEntryKind with member this.caption : ControlCaption`: `Material`, `Sample`, `Source`, `Polarizer`, `Detector`, `Category`; `type ImportStatus with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, in step 93's order: `New entry`, `Already in the library`, `New version of a held entry`, `Differs from the held version`, `Same name as a held entry`, `No longer in its catalogue`; `type ImportAction with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`: `add`, `reuse`, `version-latest`, `version-kept`, `fork`, `rebind-<guid>`, `skip`, `retire`; `type ImportDecision with member this.actionCaption (action : ImportAction) : ControlCaption`: `Add` (`Side by side` on a `NameCollision`), `Reuse the held entry`, `Add version, made latest`, `Add version, latest kept`, `Fork as a new entry`, `Use my <name> instead` (001 §B; the name of the same-name entry it names, or `Use the held entry instead` on any other status), `Skip` and `Mark inactive`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a group after the Materials window's, under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.2: `importDialogWindow` (`\"ImportDialogWindow\"`), `importDialogHeading` (`\"ImportDialogHeading\"`), `importDecisionList` (`\"ImportDecisionList\"`), `importDecisionRow (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportDecisionRow_{entry.value}\"`), `importActionOption (entry : ConstructorUiKey) (action : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportActionOption_{entry.value}_{action.value}\"`), `importDiffToggle (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportDiffToggle_{entry.value}\"`), `importDiffPreview (entry : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportDiffPreview_{entry.value}\"`), `importDialogMessage` (`\"ImportDialogMessage\"`), `importApplyButton` (`\"ImportApplyButton\"`) and `importCancelButton` (`\"ImportCancelButton\"`). (5) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs` (`module ImportDialogTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`), appended to the compile list after `LibraryWindowTests.fs` with no comment. Its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and its dialog context records `onApplied` and `requestClose`. Its rows come from `decideDroppedFiles` (step 104) over files written as step 104's facts write them, in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"ImportDialogTests\")`: a new user material, a user material named `Silicon` (a `NameCollision`) and Silicon's built-in version 2 with a changed description (a `VersionNotHeld`). `the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the ten ids' texts. `the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied`: three rows in drop order, each choice its `byDefault`, no diff shown, and `tryHeldEntry` of the new material answers `None`. `an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert`: `OverrideImportRow` of the collision with its `RebindToHeldEntry` takes it; of the new material with `ForkIncomingEntry`, which it does not offer, it is inert; and `DecideImportRow` restores the collision's default. `Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes`: with the collision overridden by `SkipIncomingEntry`, `ApplyImportChoices` leaves the new material held, Silicon held at versions 1 and 2 with latest 1, and no second `Silicon`; it records one `onApplied` whose `choices` are the model's and whose `summary` is `Imported the dropped entry files (decisions applied: 3).`, and one close. `Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue`: a test-local `PendingCatalogueImport`, whose entry names a test-local catalogue id and folder and whose one decision is the collision `decideEntry` gives under `CatalogueImportOrigin (that id, CatalogueName \"Lab\")`, applied through `ApplyImportChoices`, holds both `Silicon` materials, and `proxy.loggedImports ()` holds a row for that catalogue id. `a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open`: the rows of a dropped new material and a dropped sample that names it, with the material overridden by `SkipIncomingEntry`, answer `lastError = Some (DanglingReferenceErr _)` on Apply, with no `onApplied`, no close and nothing held. `Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing`: `CancelImportDialog` records one close, no `onApplied`, and nothing is held. `each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers`: `importDialogView` mounted headless, as `LibraryWindowTests` mounts a view, shows in the collision's row `Silicon — from <its file>`, `Material`, `version 1`, `Same name as a held entry` and `Default: Side by side`, and the options `Side by side`, `Use my Silicon instead` and `Skip` by their `importActionOption` ids; the new material's row has no `importDiffToggle`. `a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload`: pressing the version row's `importDiffToggle` shows `importDiffPreview` holding a `- ` line with the held description and a `+ ` line with the incoming one; pressing it again hides it.", "acceptance": "After the dialog's MVU lands, `ImportDialogView` MUST reach the import seam only on `ApplyImportChoices`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied`, `an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert`, `Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes`, `Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue`, `a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open`, `Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing`, `each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers`, `a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload`, the count rising by 9; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.the import dialog UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.the dialog opens one row per decision with its default action chosen and nothing applied", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.an override takes one of the row's alternatives, Decide restores the default, and an action the row does not offer is inert", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.Apply hands every row's choice to the import seam once, reports it and closes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.Apply on a pending catalogue settles it and logs the catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.a refused Apply shows its reason and keeps the dialog open", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.Cancel closes the dialog and applies nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.each row shows its name, kind, version, status, default action and every action it offers", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.a row's diff preview shows the lines that differ between the held and the incoming payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.ImportDialogRequest", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.ImportDialogContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.updateImportDialog", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-MVU"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 108, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [107], "how_to": "The import dialog's window, and the one drop seam of the library windows (the S3.2 brief: a new window with its own view and window files; 001 §H; .spec-md §4 'UI': every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `ImportDialogView.fs`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment. (a) `type ImportDialogWindow(imports : CatalogueImportContext, request : ImportDialogRequest, onApplied : ImportDialogApplied -> unit)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `MaterialsWindow` (`MaterialsWindow.fs:29`) does. Its title is `Import decisions`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.importDialogWindow`; it asks for 900 × 640 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`). It runs `Program.mkProgram` over `initImportDialog`, `updateImportDialog` and `importDialogView` (step 107) with the context `{ imports = imports; request = request; onApplied = onApplied; requestClose = this.Close }`. Closing it any other way than Apply applies nothing, because only `ApplyImportChoices` reaches the seam. Its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §B and spec 0050 S3.2. (b) `module EntryFileDrop` holds `acceptEntryFiles (window : Window) (onDropped : FileName list -> unit) : unit`, the one drop seam of the Library and Materials windows (001 §H). It calls `DragDrop.SetAllowDrop(window, true)` and adds two handlers through `DragDrop.AddDragOverHandler` and `DragDrop.AddDropHandler`. The drag-over handler sets `e.DragEffects` to `DragDropEffects.Copy` when `e.DataTransfer.Contains DataFormat.File`, and to `DragDropEffects.None` otherwise. The drop handler takes `e.DataTransfer.TryGetFiles ()` and calls `onDropped` with each item's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FileName`, in order, when there is at least one. It is an IO edge in the shape of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`: each handler body is wrapped so that a platform failure changes nothing, and headless facts send the windows' drop message directly (steps 110, 111). Its doc is one to three lines. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the import dialog leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"ImportDialog\"` over an `ImportDialogWindow` whose request is `ApplyDroppedEntries` of one `EntryIdNotHeld` row per envelope of `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`, each `ImportDecision.decide (DroppedFileOrigin <its file name>) envelope None []`, and one `NameCollision` row against two same-name held entries, so the list is longer than the screen and one row's options are wide. Its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`, and `onApplied` is `ignore`. (3) `ImportDialogTests` gains `acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it` (trait `ui-smoke`). Over the class's in-memory context and two dropped rows (step 107), an `ImportDialogWindow` with a recording `onApplied` is shown headless. It shows `importDialogHeading`, `importDecisionList` holding both rows, and `importApplyButton` and `importCancelButton` with equal tops, Cancel to the right of Apply with a gap between them. Pressing Apply's centre, as the file's other facts press a box, holds both entries, records one `onApplied`, and closes the window.", "acceptance": "After the window lands, `ImportDialogWindow` MUST call `WindowFit.keepOnScreen`, and `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles` MUST be the one drop seam; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import dialog leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the import dialog leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.acceptance: the import dialog window renders its rows with Apply and Cancel in one row, and Apply imports the chosen entries and closes it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S32-DIALOG-WINDOW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 109, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.2h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [108], "how_to": "Every Materials window carries the app's import seam, the one a Sample editor opens in Select state included, so a file dropped on it is decided against the app library (001 §H: dropped onto the Library or Materials window; the S3.2 brief). This step threads the seam and changes no behaviour; step 110 reads it. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `MaterialsWindowContext` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:154`) gains `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories`, documented as the import seam that dropped entry files are decided and applied through. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`: `MaterialsWindow` (`MaterialsWindow.fs:29`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories` and sets the context field. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SampleEditorWindow.fs`: `SampleEditorWindow` (`SampleEditorWindow.fs:30`) takes `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` after `categories` and passes it to the Select-state `MaterialsWindow` that its `openMaterialsSelect` builds (`SampleEditorWindow.fs:69`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs`: the Sample editor it opens (`LibraryWindow.fs:77`) gets the window's `catalogueImports` (step 101). (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `EditorLaunchers.openMaterialsWindow` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:150`) takes the `CatalogueImportContext` after the `CategoryProxy`; `EditorLaunchers.defaults` passes it to `MaterialsWindow` (`:193`); and the strip's `OpenMaterialsWindow` (`:1832`) passes `model.catalogueImports` (step 101). The field's doc names the import seam in no more words. (6) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: the launcher's Materials button passes `context.catalogueImports`. (7) Every test construction passes one. `MaterialsWindowTests`' `stubContext` (`MaterialsWindowTests.fs:180`) and its `MaterialsWindow(...)` mounts (`:702`, `:1044`), `SampleEditorWindowTests`' `SampleEditorWindow(...)` mounts, `EmbeddedChartTests`' `MaterialsWindow(...)` (`EmbeddedChartTests.fs:230`), `ScrollExtentTests`' `MaterialsWindow(...)` and `SampleEditorWindow(...)`, `WindowLauncherTests`' windows (`WindowLauncherTests.fs:453`, `:488`, `:545`) and `WireUi0040CompositionTests`' Sample editors (`WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:306`, `:352`) pass `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:47`, `:57`, `:149`) passes `ctx.catalogueImports`, and `MainWorkbenchTests`' recording `openMaterialsWindow` (`MainWorkbenchTests.fs:106`) takes the extra argument. `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' launchers, a record update of `EditorLaunchers.defaults` (`WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs:136`), keep their code. A doc that lists the window's stores names the import seam in no more words. No assertion changes: the facts whose constructions change keep what they assert, among them `Library and Materials windows: the facet rows wrap, nothing is clipped`, `Material, Sample, Category and Source editors leave everything reachable`, `the Materials and Library strip buttons reach their launchers as pure launches`, `the initial projection lists every stored material as a selectable entry leaf with the live count`.", "acceptance": "After the threading, every `MaterialsWindow` and `SampleEditorWindow` construction MUST pass a `CatalogueImportContext`, and no assertion MUST change; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SampleEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SampleEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/EmbeddedChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WindowLauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.Library and Materials windows: the facet rows wrap, nothing is clipped", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.Material, Sample, Category and Source editors leave everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests.the Materials and Library strip buttons reach their launchers as pure launches", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the initial projection lists every stored material as a selectable entry leaf with the live count", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.MaterialsWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SampleEditorWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.EditorLaunchers", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-IMPORTS-THREADED"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 110, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.2i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [109], "how_to": "Dropping entry files onto the Materials window opens the import dialog over them (001 §H; .spec-md §3.7: a dropped file always opens the dialog; §10.1 discoverability: the dialog opens on a dropped entry file; §10.4: the dialog's completion message updates the window's model, whose projections re-query the store, so no reload is needed; the S3.2 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) `MaterialsWindowContext` gains `openImportDialog : ImportDecision list -> unit`, documented as opening the import dialog over the rows of dropped entries (the composition root bakes the window; tests record). (b) `MaterialsWindowModel` gains `importStatus : ControlCaption option` and `importError : CatalogueImportError option`, each opening `None`, each with a one-line doc. (c) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `DropMaterialEntryFiles of FileName list` and `MaterialsImportApplied of summary : ControlCaption`. (d) `updateMaterialsWindow`. `DropMaterialEntryFiles files` calls `context.catalogueImports.decideDroppedFiles files` (step 104). `Ok []` leaves the model as it was. `Ok decisions` calls `context.openImportDialog decisions` and clears `importStatus` and `importError`. `Error e` sets `importError` to `Some e` and clears `importStatus`; no dialog opens. `MaterialsImportApplied summary` sets `importStatus` to `Some summary` and clears `importError`; the next render re-queries the store, so an added material is listed. Neither arms or disarms a gate or changes the mode. (e) The view: after `messageRow` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:messageRow`), when either is set, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialsImportStatusText` shows `importError`'s `caption` (step 101) in `messageColor`, or else `importStatus`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`. The context's `openImportDialog` is `fun decisions -> ImportDialogWindow(catalogueImports, ApplyDroppedEntries decisions, fun applied -> dispatch (MaterialsImportApplied applied.summary)).Show()` (step 108). `member _.DropEntryFiles (files : FileName list) : unit` dispatches `DropMaterialEntryFiles files`: the semantic seam that the drop and the tests share, as `Retarget` is the launcher's. After `Program.run`, `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles this (fun files -> dispatch (DropMaterialEntryFiles files))` (step 108). The class doc names the drop in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group: `materialsImportStatusText` (`\"MaterialsImportStatusText\"`) under a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S3.2. (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`. `stubContext` (step 109) passes a recording `openImportDialog`. Files are written as step 104's facts write them, into a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"MaterialsWindowTests\")`. `dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`: `DropMaterialEntryFiles` of a new user material's file records one `openImportDialog` holding one `EntryIdNotHeld` row, `importError` stays `None`, and the context's import seam does not hold the material. `a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog`: `DropMaterialEntryFiles [ notes.txt ]` sets `importError` to `Some (DroppedFileRefusedErr _)` and records no dialog. `an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status`: `MaterialsImportApplied` of a summary sets `importStatus` to it and clears `importError`. `the Materials window accepts dropped files`: a `MaterialsWindow` mounted as the class mounts one answers `DragDrop.GetAllowDrop` true. `acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations …)`, a `MaterialsWindow(ctx.materials, ctx.categories, ctx.catalogueImports)` is shown headless. After `window.DropEntryFiles` of a new user material's file, exactly one `ImportDialogWindow` opens, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent` as `LauncherTests.clickAndObserve` observes. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, `ctx.materials.tryGetMaterial` resolves the material, and `materialsImportStatusText` shows the summary.", "acceptance": "After the drop is wired, a file dropped on the Materials window MUST be decided through `decideDroppedFiles` and open `ImportDialogWindow`, applying nothing before Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`, `a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog`, `an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status`, `the Materials window accepts dropped files`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.dropping entry files on the Materials window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.a refused drop on the Materials window shows its reason and opens no dialog", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.an applied import of dropped files is the Materials window status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the Materials window accepts dropped files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.acceptance: a material file dropped on the Materials window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.MaterialsWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-MATERIALS-DROP"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 111, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.2j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [110], "how_to": "Dropping entry files onto the Library window opens the import dialog over them, and so does a registered folder whose rows wait (001 §H; 001 §B 'Extra catalogue folders'; .spec-md §3.7, §3.8, §10.1, §10.4; S3.1 step 101 holds such a registration in `pendingImports` for this dialog). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowContext` gains `openImportDialog : ImportDialogRequest -> unit`, documented as `MaterialsWindowContext`'s is. (b) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `DropLibraryEntryFiles of FileName list`, `ReviewPendingImports` and `LibraryImportApplied of ImportDialogApplied`. (c) `updateLibraryWindow`. `DropLibraryEntryFiles files` calls `context.catalogueImports.decideDroppedFiles files`: `Ok []` is inert; `Ok decisions` calls `context.openImportDialog (ApplyDroppedEntries decisions)` and clears `lastError` and `importStatus`; `Error e` sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr e` (step 101) and clears `importStatus`. The `RegisterCatalogueFolder` arm for `Ok (CatalogueAwaitsChoices pending)` (step 101) also calls `context.openImportDialog (SettlePendingCatalogue pending)`. `ReviewPendingImports` opens the dialog over the first of `pendingImports`, and is inert when there is none. `LibraryImportApplied applied` sets `importStatus` to `applied.summary` and clears `lastError`. For `SettlePendingCatalogue p` it also removes from `pendingImports` the import whose `entry.catalogueId` is `p.entry.catalogueId`, because `settle` logged it and `registeredFolders` now lists it. None of these arms or disarms a gate. (d) The view: while `pendingImports` is not empty, the verbs row (`LibraryWindowView.fs:verbsRow`), in Browse and Select mode alike and after step 101's `Register catalogue folder…`, holds `verbButton ConstructorUiId.libraryReviewImportsButton (ControlCaption \"Review imports…\")`, which dispatches `ReviewPendingImports`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs`. The context's `openImportDialog` is `fun request -> ImportDialogWindow(catalogueImports, request, fun applied -> dispatch (LibraryImportApplied applied)).Show()`. `member _.DropEntryFiles (files : FileName list) : unit` dispatches `DropLibraryEntryFiles files`, and after `Program.run`, `EntryFileDrop.acceptEntryFiles this (fun files -> dispatch (DropLibraryEntryFiles files))`. The class doc names the drop in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group: `libraryReviewImportsButton` (`\"LibraryReviewImportsButton\"`) under a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S3.2. (4) Every other construction of `LibraryWindowContext` passes `openImportDialog`: `LibraryWindowTests`' `stubContext` a recording stub, and `LightSourceEditorTests`' and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' `libraryContext` `ignore`. (5) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`, over `stubContext` with step 101's in-memory import context; files and catalogue folders are written as step 101's facts write them. `dropping entry files on the Library window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`: `DropLibraryEntryFiles` of a new user source's file records one `ApplyDroppedEntries` request holding one `EntryIdNotHeld` row; `lastError` stays `None`, and the source is not held. `a refused drop on the Library window shows its reason as the window message`: `DropLibraryEntryFiles [ notes.txt ]` sets `lastError` to `CatalogueImportRefusedErr (DroppedFileRefusedErr _)` and records no request. `a registration whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog, and Review imports reopens it`: over step 101's awaiting-folder setup, `RegisterCatalogueFolder` records one `SettlePendingCatalogue` request over the model's pending import, and `ReviewPendingImports` records it again. `a settled registration leaves the pending list and its summary is the status`: after that, the pending import settled through `context.catalogueImports.settle` with its `byDefault` choices, `LibraryImportApplied` of the result empties `pendingImports`, sets `importStatus` to its `summary`, and `registeredFolders` lists the folder. `the Library window accepts dropped files`: a `LibraryWindow` mounted as the class mounts one answers `DragDrop.GetAllowDrop` true. `acceptance: a source file dropped on the Library window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations …)`, a `LibraryWindow` composed from the context's stores, `libraryBackups` and `catalogueImports` is shown headless. After `window.DropEntryFiles` of a new user source's file, exactly one `ImportDialogWindow` opens, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent`. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, `ctx.sources.tryGetSource` resolves the source, and `libraryImportStatusText` (step 101) shows the summary.", "acceptance": "After the drop is wired, a file dropped on the Library window and a registration whose rows await MUST open `ImportDialogWindow`, applying nothing before Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a source file dropped on the Library window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `dropping entry files on the Library window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing`, `a refused drop on the Library window shows its reason as the window message`, `a registration whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog, and Review imports reopens it`, `a settled registration leaves the pending list and its summary is the status`, `the Library window accepts dropped files`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.dropping entry files on the Library window decides them and opens the import dialog, applying nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a refused drop on the Library window shows its reason as the window message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a registration whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog, and Review imports reopens it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a settled registration leaves the pending list and its summary is the status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the Library window accepts dropped files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.acceptance: a source file dropped on the Library window opens the import dialog, and Apply adds it to the app library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.LibraryWindowView.LibraryWindowContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S32-LIBRARY-DROP"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 112, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.2k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [111], "how_to": "The start-up imports whose rows wait open the import dialog from the Launcher (001 §B; .spec-md §3.7: rows that need a choice wait in the one import dialog, their default pre-selected, and nothing in them applies unconfirmed; §10.1: the dialog opens at start when a catalogue row needs a choice; S3.1 step 100 holds them in `AppContext.pendingImports`). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow` (steps 88, 89): (1) For `Ok context`, the window keeps the imports still waiting in one local mutable list, started from `context.pendingImports`; the window is the IO edge (AGENTS.md: mutation only at the IO boundary). While the list is not empty, the content shows, between the title and the surface buttons, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherPendingImportsText` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, with the text `Library entries waiting for an import decision: <n>.` (`n` summing the `decisions` of the list), and a `Button` carrying `launcherReviewImportsButton` the same way, labelled `Review imports…`. Its click opens `ImportDialogWindow(context.catalogueImports, SettlePendingCatalogue head, onApplied)` (step 108) over the head of the list. `onApplied` removes from the list the import whose `entry.catalogueId` is the applied request's, and rebuilds the content through step 89's local content function, so the notice counts what still waits and goes when nothing does. Cancel leaves the list as it was. (2) The first time the launcher opens (`Opened`), when the list is not empty, it opens the dialog over its head, so the choice is asked at start; the launcher never applies a row itself. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `launcherPendingImportsText` (`\"LauncherPendingImportsText\"`) and `launcherReviewImportsButton` (`\"LauncherReviewImportsButton\"`), each with a one-line doc. (4) Tests, in `LauncherTests`. `a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice`: in `withLauncher` (the fixture explicitly settles the Built-in catalogue before opening the launcher) neither id is present, and the buttons are still the four surfaces. `acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it` (trait `ui-smoke`): over `TestAppScope.fileLocations`, a first `AppContext.create` saves a user material `Lab glass` through its `materials`; the `Builtin` folder under the locations' `shippedCatalogueFolder` is rewritten with a new-id material named `Lab glass` (step 100's `create holds every changed-catalogue row pending and writes nothing before confirmation` setup); and a second `AppContext.create` holds one pending import containing every catalogue decision row. `LauncherWindow(locations, WorkbenchSettings.defaults, Ok ctx)` shown headless opens exactly one `ImportDialogWindow`, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent`, and `launcherPendingImportsText` reads `Library entries waiting for an import decision: <all pending rows>.`. Pressing the dialog's `importCancelButton` closes it and keeps the notice. Clicking `launcherReviewImportsButton` opens a dialog again. Pressing its `importApplyButton` closes it, removes the notice and the button, and leaves both `Lab glass` materials held. A third `AppContext.create` over the same locations holds no pending import. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher, whose context holds no pending import, keeps its code. The headless startup acceptance fact MUST also run on a fresh empty database with a nonconflicting catalogue: the dialog MUST show every Add and Reuse row, Cancel MUST leave entries and the log unchanged, and Apply MUST settle the whole list. Mixed-conflict coverage MUST remain. The test MUST derive its displayed row count from the complete decisions list, not a collision count; fixture population elsewhere MUST explicitly settle first.", "acceptance": "After the launcher is wired, a start-up import whose rows await MUST open `ImportDialogWindow` from the launcher and stay waiting until Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s13 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a launcher with no pending import shows no import notice", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S32-LAUNCHER-PENDING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: a start-up catalogue whose rows await a choice opens the import dialog from the launcher; Cancel keeps it waiting and Apply settles it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S32-LAUNCHER-PENDING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S32-LAUNCHER-PENDING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.2 -- The import dialog and single-file drop"}
{"number": 113, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [112], "how_to": "Licence attribution is a fact of an entry's provenance, decided once in Domain (001 §B 'Licence attribution: CC-BY entries show their attribution in the Library and Materials windows and in the Details view'; the S3.3 brief: an entry whose provenance licence requires attribution shows its citation, and CC0 shows the licence name only). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, after `EntryProvenance` and `EntryForkInfo` (steps 24, 91), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3: (1) `EntryAttribution` = `LicenceAndCitation of licence : EntryLicence * citation : EntryCitation` | `LicenceNameOnly of licence : EntryLicence` is what an entry shows about its licence. Its `member this.text : string` is the honest render (ELEV002): `Licence <licence> — cite: <citation>` and `Licence <licence>`. (2) `type EntryLicence with member this.attributionWith (citation : EntryCitation) : EntryAttribution` holds the one CC-BY rule. A licence whose SPDX identifier starts with `CC-BY` (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`: `CC-BY-4.0`, `CC-BY-SA-4.0`, `CC-BY-NC-4.0` …) obliges its user to credit the source, so it answers `LicenceAndCitation`. Every other licence, `CC0-1.0` included, answers `LicenceNameOnly`. No other licence family, table or option is added. (3) `type EntryProvenance with member this.attributionOpt : EntryAttribution option`. `SourcePullProvenance info` answers `Some (info.licence.attributionWith info.citation)`. `ForkProvenance fork` answers `fork.originalProvenance.attributionOpt`, so a fork of a pulled entry, and a fork of that fork, keep its credit (S3.1 interpretation 2). `BuiltInProvenance`, `UserProvenance` and `KitImportProvenance` answer `None`, because they carry no licence. (4) `EntryAttributionLine = { entryName : EntryName; attribution : EntryAttribution }` is one credited entry as a surface lists it, with `member this.text : string` = `<entry name>: <attribution text>`. (5) `type LibraryEntry with member this.attributedEntryIds : LibraryEntryId list` names the entries a surface showing the entry credits: the entry's own id (`entry.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24; none for a non-GUID id), then, for a `SampleItem`, every material its structure references (`ElementId.fs:188` `SampleStructure.referencedMaterials`) through `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId`, in that set's order. A sample's own provenance carries no licence, but the optical constants of its layers may. (6) The fixture `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains, each with a one-line doc, the builders both suites use for licensed and user entries, so no fact copies them. `licensedMaterialContent (id : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) (licence : EntryLicence) (citation : EntryCitation) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's Silicon (`MaterialIds.silicon`, decoded from `catalogueData ()`) under `id` and `name`, built with `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry VersionNumber.first` under `SourcePullProvenance { source = MaterialSourceName \"Test optical constants\"; record = MaterialSourceRecordId \"test/<name>\"; sourceVersion = MaterialSourceVersion \"2026-11-01\"; licence = licence; citation = citation }`. `userMaterialContent (id : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the same Silicon under `UserProvenance`. `userCategoryContent (id : CategoryId) (name : CategoryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's Glass category (`CategoryIds.glass`) under `id`, `name` and `UserCategory`, built with `ofMaterialCategory VersionNumber.first UserProvenance`. `sampleContentOver (id : SampleId) (material : MaterialId) (name : EntryName) : LibraryEntryContent` is the catalogue's `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` sample under `id`, `name` and `UserProvenance`, its films replaced by one 100 nm `SingleLayer` of version 1 of `material`. `putSealedEntries (context : CatalogueImportContext) (contents : LibraryEntryContent list) : unit` seals each content through `context.sealEntry` and puts it through `context.proxy.putEntryVersion` with `MoveLatestVersion`, in order. A builder or seam error fails the calling fact with its `describe`. (7) Tests, in `LibraryEntryFilesTests`. `a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone`: `CC-BY-4.0`, `cc-by-sa-4.0` and `CC-BY-NC-4.0` answer `LicenceAndCitation`, `CC0-1.0` and `MIT` answer `LicenceNameOnly`, and the two texts are exactly `Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: <citation>` and `Licence CC0-1.0`. `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none`: a `SourcePullProvenance` under `CC-BY-4.0`, a fork of it and a fork of that fork answer the same `LicenceAndCitation`; a `SourcePullProvenance` under `CC0-1.0` answers `LicenceNameOnly`; `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`, `UserProvenance` and a `KitImportProvenance` of a test-local `KitId` answer `None`; and an `EntryAttributionLine` named `PTB glass` renders `PTB glass: <its attribution's text>`. `an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials`: a source preset of the catalogue answers its own id alone, and the `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` sample answers its own id followed by `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial` in the order of its `referencedMaterials`.", "acceptance": "After the attribution lands, `EntryProvenance.attributionOpt` MUST answer a pulled entry's licence attribution, through any fork, and `None` for every other provenance; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone`, `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none`, `an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a CC-BY licence attributes with its citation and any other licence by its name alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.an entry's attributed ids are its own and its sample's materials", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryAttribution", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryAttributionLine", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 114, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [113], "how_to": "The library answers the credit a list of entries owes, so the three surfaces that show it read one body (001 §B 'Licence attribution'; the S3.3 brief: the Library window, the Materials window and the Details view of a bound element). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, on `CatalogueImportProxy`: `member this.attributionLinesOf (ids : LibraryEntryId list) : Result<EntryAttributionLine list, CatalogueImportError>`. For each distinct id, in the order given, it calls `tryHeldEntry` (step 94). An id the library does not hold adds nothing. A held entry adds `{ entryName = held.name; attribution = a }` when `held.provenance.attributionOpt` (step 113) is `Some a`: the latest version's provenance is the entry's credit. The first read error is the answer. It writes nothing. Its doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. No cache, per-version lookup or other member is added. Tests: `CatalogueImportContract` gains `attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked`, so it runs over the in-memory seam and SQLite `:memory:`. After `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` through `freshImport ()`'s context, `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries` (step 113) puts `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` under `CC-BY-4.0` and the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`, `licensedMaterialContent` `RII glass` under `CC0-1.0`, a fork of `PTB glass` named `PTB glass (fork)` (its content under a test-local id and `ForkProvenance` of `PTB glass`'s id, version and provenance), and `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass`. `attributionLinesOf` of `Lab glass`, `MaterialIds.silicon`, `PTB glass`, `RII glass`, the fork, a test-local GUID and `PTB glass` again answers exactly three lines, in this order: `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`, `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0` and the fork's line, which carries `PTB glass`'s licence and citation.", "acceptance": "After the read lands, `CatalogueImportProxy.attributionLinesOf` MUST answer one line per held, licensed entry in the order asked; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked` over both stores, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.attributionLinesOf names each held entry whose provenance carries a licence, in the order asked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ATTRIBUTION-READ"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 115, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [114], "how_to": "The import seam lists the user's entries and pins a version of any kind, which every export needs (001 §B 'Export: … Exporting pins the exported versions (§C)'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned — a one-way flag — when a kit first references it, or when it is exported'; the S3.3 brief: exporting pins every exported version through S2.2's pin verbs). S2.2's verbs (`pinMaterialVersion`, `pinSampleVersion`, step 65) cover two kinds, and the source, preset and category stores have none (S2.3 interpretation 4). So the kind-neutral pin lives on the envelope seam (step 94), and its database half shares one body with those verbs. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: `CatalogueImportProxy` gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `heldUserEntries : unit -> Result<HeldEntry list, CatalogueImportError>` answers every held entry whose latest provenance is not a built-in (`provenance.protection` is `UserManaged`: user, kit-import, pulled and forked entries), whatever its lifecycle, each as `tryHeldEntry` answers it. `pinEntryVersion : LibraryEntryId -> VersionNumber -> Result<unit, CatalogueImportError>` pins one held version, one way. It answers `Ok ()` also when the version is already pinned, and `ImportRejectedErr` naming the id and the version when that version is not held. The record's doc names both in no more words. (2) The in-memory double (`createInMemory`, step 95). `heldUserEntries` answers the map's entries whose latest provenance is `UserManaged`, in the map's id order. `pinEntryVersion` answers `ImportRejectedErr` for a version the map does not hold. For a held material or sample version it decodes the envelope (step 25), as its put does, and calls the bundled store's `pinMaterialVersion` or `pinSampleVersion` (step 65); a refusal is `ImportRejectedErr` with the store's reason. For every other kind it answers `Ok ()`, because the in-memory category, source and preset stores hold no pin. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`: the operations' extension (step 67) gains `stagePin (id : LibraryEntryId) (version : VersionNumber) : Result<StoredEntryVersion option, StorageError>` under the same `StorageBoundary` mark. It calls `tryStoredVersion id version`; a held version is restaged through `stageVersion` with `pin = VersionPinned` and its lifecycle kept, and is answered as it was found; a version not held answers `None`. It stages and never saves. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs`' `pinMaterialVersion` (step 69) and `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs`' `pinSampleVersion` (step 74) call it in place of their own restage and keep their refusals, so one body pins a version row. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`' `createInDatabase` (step 95). `heldUserEntries` answers, in one `database.run` and as `heldEntriesOf` does, every entry whose latest row (`LatestVersion` joined to `EntryVersion`) has `Protection` = `UserManaged.value`, in no promised order. `pinEntryVersion id version` is one `run` of `stagePin` and one `SaveChanges ()`; `None` is `ImportRejectedErr` naming the id and the version. Every `StorageError` is `ImportStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`, as for its other fields. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs`: `recordingProxy` (step 94) answers `heldUserEntries` with `[]` and `pinEntryVersion` with `Ok ()`. No cache, retry, unpin verb or other field is added: a pin is one-way (001 §C). (6) Tests. `CatalogueImportContract` gains two facts, so each runs over both stores; their entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `putSealedEntries` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. `heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in`: before any put it answers `[]`. After `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass`, `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` and a fork of `PTB glass` (as step 114's fact builds it) are put, and `Lab glass` is retired through `retireEntry`, it answers exactly those three ids, compared as a set, each with its own name. `pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held`: `Lab glass`'s version 1 is pinned through `pinEntryVersion`, and a second pin of it answers `Ok ()`. The material, decoded and given the catalogue Langasite's complexity, saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial` then resolves at versions 1 and 2, and version 1 keeps Silicon's complexity. A put `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack`, its version 1 pinned the same way, makes `samples.removeSample` answer `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. Version 3 of `Lab glass` and version 1 of a test-local GUID answer `ImportRejectedErr`. `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` gains `pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle`. Over a database the fact opens as the class's `freshImport` does, after `importFrom` of the Built-in catalogue and `retireEntry` of one built-in source, `pinEntryVersion` of version 1 of one entry of each of the six kinds, that source included, leaves each of those rows `VersionPinned`, read through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`. The source stays `InactiveEntry`, and every other entry's version 1 stays `VersionUnpinned`. The inherited `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` and `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` (steps 66, 73) run unchanged over the shared `stagePin`.", "acceptance": "After the seam grows, both implementations of `CatalogueImportProxy` MUST answer `heldUserEntries` and `pinEntryVersion`, and the database pin verbs MUST share `stagePin`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in` and `pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held` over both stores and `pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SampleDatabaseStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.heldUserEntries answers every entry whose latest version is not a built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.pinEntryVersion pins a held version so that its next physics edit mints a version, and refuses a version not held", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.pinEntryVersion pins the version row of every kind, keeping its lifecycle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S33-EXPORT-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 116, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [115], "how_to": "One library entry exports to its own `-json` file, and exporting pins the version it writes (001 §B 'Export: any entry → its `-json` file … Exporting pins the exported versions'; 001 §A: the file name is the entry's name made filesystem-safe plus its kind's extension; the S3.3 brief). Export lives on the import context, the library-exchange seam that every library window already carries (steps 101, 109), so no new context is threaded. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, before `CatalogueImportContext`: `LibraryExportError` is an `*Error` union, each case documented. `ExportedEntryNotHeldErr of reason : string` is an entry to export that the library does not hold, named by its id. `ExportLibraryRefusedErr of CatalogueImportError` is a seam failure while reading or pinning. `ExportFileWriteErr of reason : string` is an entry file that could not be written, naming the file. `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: a fixed phrase naming the condition, a colon, then the reason or the wrapped error's `describe`. (2) On `CatalogueImportProxy`: `member this.tryLatestEnvelope (id : LibraryEntryId) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope option, CatalogueImportError>` is `tryHeldEntry id` and then `tryHeldEnvelope id held.latest` (step 105); an id not held answers `None`. (3) `CatalogueImportContext` (steps 94, 98, 104) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `writeEntryFile : FileName -> LibraryEntryEnvelope -> Result<unit, LibraryExportError>` writes one entry's file. `exportFolderOpt : FolderName option` is the folder the export dialogs open in (001 §G 'Exports': the catalogue-export folder), `None` where no location is configured. `member this.exportEntry (id : LibraryEntryId) (file : FileName) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, LibraryExportError>` reads the latest envelope through `tryLatestEnvelope`: `None` is `ExportedEntryNotHeldErr` naming the id, and a read error is `ExportLibraryRefusedErr`. It then pins that version through `proxy.pinEntryVersion` (step 115) before anything is written, so the file always names a frozen version. It then writes the file through `writeEntryFile` and answers the envelope written. The member doc says so in one to three lines. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `create`, its signature unchanged, fills `writeEntryFile` with the envelope's `fileText` (step 30) written through `LibraryFileText.writeAtomically` (step 33). The file is therefore byte-identical to the catalogue's and the database's copy of the entry (001 §C 'Hybrid shape'). A `StorageError` is `ExportFileWriteErr` naming the file, with the error's `describe`. `create` sets `exportFolderOpt` to `None`; the composition root sets the configured folder (step 118). No overwrite check is added, because the save dialog's own prompt guards the chosen file (steps 119, 120). (5) Tests. Each file goes into a fresh folder, a GUID name under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryExportTests\")`. `CatalogueImportContract` gains two facts, so each runs over both stores. `exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse`: after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())` and `putSealedEntries` of `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` (step 113), `exportEntry` of it to `<folder>/Lab glass.material-json` answers the held envelope. The context's `readEntryFile MaterialEntryKind` (step 104) reads that file back equal, and `decideDroppedFiles` of it answers one `SameContentHash` row. The material, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial`, then resolves at versions 1 and 2. `exportEntry` of `MaterialIds.silicon` to `<folder>/Silicon.material-json` writes a file whose text equals `Catalogue/Builtin/Silicon.material-json` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, byte for byte. `exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing`: a test-local GUID answers `ExportedEntryNotHeldErr` naming it, and the folder holds no file. `CatalogueImportProxyTests` gains `every export error renders its condition and its payload`: each of the three cases, over a distinct test-local reason or a wrapped `ImportRejectedErr`, renders a distinct text holding its reason or the wrapped error's `describe`.", "acceptance": "After single-entry export lands, `CatalogueImportContext.exportEntry` MUST pin the latest version before it writes that entry's file; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse` and `exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing` over both stores and `every export error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.exporting one entry pins its latest version and writes its entry file, which a drop decides as a reuse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.exporting an entry the library does not hold is refused and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.every export error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.CatalogueImportContext", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.LibraryExportError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "obligations": ["S33-ENTRY-EXPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 117, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [116], "how_to": "A selection, a category or the whole of the user's library exports to a catalogue folder: one `.catalogue-json` manifest and one file per entry (001 §B 'Export: … a selection or a category → a catalogue folder'; 001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout': uniqueness per kind within a catalogue is checked on export; 001 §C '\"Export my library\" writes the user entries to a catalogue folder, which the recreated database imports'; the S3.3 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`. (a) `CatalogueExportTarget = { folder : FolderName; name : CatalogueName }` is where a catalogue export goes and the name its manifest carries. (b) `LibraryExportError` (step 116) gains three cases, each documented and each with a `describe` line. `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr of CatalogueError`: the entries do not form a catalogue (`InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr` from `CatalogueData.tryCreate`), or the folder write failed. `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr of reason : string`: the target folder already holds a catalogue manifest, naming the folder. `EmptyLibraryExportErr of reason : string`: there is nothing to export. (c) `CatalogueImportContext` gains `newCatalogueId : unit -> CatalogueId`, documented as the id an exported catalogue is minted under and injected as `newEntryId` is. (d) `member this.exportEntries (ids : LibraryEntryId list) (target : CatalogueExportTarget) : Result<CatalogueData, LibraryExportError>` works in this order, and nothing is pinned or written before its last two steps. (i) An empty list is `EmptyLibraryExportErr` naming the folder. (ii) Each distinct id's latest envelope is read through `tryLatestEnvelope` (`ExportedEntryNotHeldErr`, `ExportLibraryRefusedErr`). (iii) The user entries they reference join them. Every id in an exported content's `referencedEntryIds` (step 93) that is not yet exported, and for which `tryHeldEntry` answers a `UserManaged` entry, joins at its latest version, and its own references are followed the same way. A referenced built-in does not join, because every library imports the shipped catalogue. So a sample over Silicon exports alone, and an export of user entries never meets a built-in's file name. (iv) The per-kind name check comes first among the refusals: `CatalogueData.tryCreate (this.newCatalogueId ()) target.name VersionNumber.first envelopes` (step 32). Its refusal is `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr`, so two exported entries of one kind and one file name are refused, naming both (step 26's `DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`). (v) `(this.openCatalogue target.folder).readManifest ()` (steps 92, 98). `Ok manifest` or `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` is `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr` naming the folder, so an export never overwrites a catalogue. Any other answer (no folder, no manifest) goes on; the writer creates a missing folder. (vi) Every envelope's version is pinned through `proxy.pinEntryVersion` (step 115). (vii) `writeCatalogue` writes the data (step 33: the entry files, then the manifest, each atomically; a folder holding an entry file the catalogue does not name is refused, and those pins stay, which only makes the next physics edit mint a version). The answer is the data written. (e) `member this.exportUserLibrary (target : CatalogueExportTarget) : Result<CatalogueData, LibraryExportError>` is `exportEntries` over every id `proxy.heldUserEntries ()` answers, inactive entries included, so a recreated library gets back everything the user owned (001 §C). A library holding no user entry is `EmptyLibraryExportErr`. A catalogue holds one version of each entry, its latest, because the folder names each entry's file by its name (001 §A). Each member doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `create`, its signature unchanged, fills `newCatalogueId` with a new GUID. `type CatalogueExportTarget with static member ofFolder (folder : FolderName) : CatalogueExportTarget` names the target by the folder's last segment (`Path.GetFileName` of the path without its trailing separator), so a chosen folder `…/Lab catalogue` exports as the catalogue `Lab catalogue`. The export dialogs call it (steps 119, 120). Its doc is one line. No merge into an existing catalogue, version bump of a re-export, progress report or option is added: each target folder becomes a new catalogue. (3) Tests. Each target is a fresh GUID folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryExportTests\")`, not created beforehand. Entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `putSealedEntries` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. `CatalogueImportContract` gains six facts, so each runs over both stores. `a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry`: `userCategoryContent` `Lab category`, `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` with its `categoryOpt` set to that category, and `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack` over `Lab glass`. `exportEntries [ Lab stack ]` answers data whose envelopes are exactly those three, each equal to its held latest envelope. `CatalogueProxy.create` over the folder reads it back equal, its manifest named `target.name`. `proxy.decideCatalogue` of it answers three `SameContentHash` rows, each defaulting to `ReuseHeldEntry`, and `importCatalogue` of it MUST answer the same three reuse rows; explicit confirmation of their defaults MUST leave `heldUserEntries` unchanged. `a catalogue export pins every exported version`: after (E1)'s export, `Lab glass`, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial`, resolves at versions 1 and 2, and `samples.removeSample` of `Lab stack` answers `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. `a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing`: two `userMaterialContent`s named `Lab glass` under two ids answer `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr (InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr (DuplicateEntryFileNameErr reason))`, whose reason names both entries (step 26). The target folder does not exist, and the first material, given Langasite's complexity and saved, still resolves at version 1 alone. `a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue`: after `Lab glass` is exported to the target, exporting `Lab stack` to it answers `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr` naming the folder, and every file's text in it is unchanged. `Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in`: over `Lab category`, `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and a `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` retired through `retireEntry`, `exportUserLibrary` answers data whose ids are exactly `heldUserEntries ()`'s four, none under `BuiltInProvenance`, and the folder reads back equal. `an export with nothing to write is refused`: `exportEntries []`, and `exportUserLibrary` over a library holding only the Built-in catalogue, each answer `EmptyLibraryExportErr`, and the target folder does not exist. `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` gains `a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind`: over a database the fact opens as the class's `freshImport` does, `Lab category`, `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and a user source (the catalogue's first source under a fresh GUID id and `UserManaged`, built with `ofSourcePreset` under `UserProvenance`) are put. `exportEntries` of those four and of one built-in polarizer and one built-in detector leaves each exported version row `VersionPinned`, read through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`, while an unexported built-in source stays `VersionUnpinned`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `a catalogue export target is named by its folder`: `ofFolder (FolderName \"D:/Exports/Lab catalogue\")` and `ofFolder (FolderName \"D:/Exports/Lab catalogue/\")` each answer the folder as given and `CatalogueName \"Lab catalogue\"`. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `every export error renders its condition and its payload` (step 116) covers the three new cases.", "acceptance": "After catalogue export lands, `exportEntries` and `exportUserLibrary` MUST check per-kind file-name uniqueness before they pin, pin before they write, and never overwrite a catalogue folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry`, `a catalogue export pins every exported version`, `a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing`, `a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue`, `Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in`, `an export with nothing to write is refused` over both stores, `a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind`, `a catalogue export target is named by its folder` and `every export error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 14; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export pins every exported version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export pins every exported version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.an export with nothing to write is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.an export with nothing to write is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S33-CATALOGUE-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests.a catalogue export target is named by its folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueFolderTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueFolderTests", "discovery_