{"number": 118, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S3.3f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [117], "how_to": "The two library windows share one verb box and one folder picker, and the app's import context suggests the configured catalogue-export folder (001 §G 'Exports' and 'Every path is overridable'; S2.4 interpretation 10: the catalogue-export location is carried in `DataLocations` until its reader arrives; spec 0048 R2 and S3.2 interpretation 6: the lower declaration serves both windows). Both windows behave as before. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) The body of `verbButton` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:889`, public since step 107) moves into the new public `verbButtonOn (id : ConstructorUiId) (label : ControlCaption) (onPressed : PointerPressedEventArgs -> unit) : IView`, which hands the press to `onPressed`, and `verbButton id label onClick` becomes `verbButtonOn id label (fun _ -> onClick ())`. (b) The public `pickLibraryFolder (owner : Window) (title : ControlCaption) (startOpt : FolderName option) (onPicked : FolderName -> unit) : unit` is step 101's `pickCatalogueFolder` body, moved, with the title and the start folder as parameters. It opens `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync` with `FolderPickerOpenOptions(Title = title.value, AllowMultiple = false)`. For `Some folder`, `SuggestedStartLocation` is resolved through `StorageProviderExtensions.TryGetFolderFromPathAsync`, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile` (`:3376`) resolves its folder. A confirmed pick passes the first folder's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FolderName`, posted on the UI thread, and a host without a provider changes nothing. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`: its private `verbButton` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1020`) and step 101's private `verbButtonOn` and `pickCatalogueFolder` are deleted. Every call uses `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` or `MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn`, and Register catalogue folder… calls `MaterialsWindowView.pickLibraryFolder owner (ControlCaption \"Register catalogue folder\") None`. The look, the ids and the messages are unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the compose that `create` and `recreateLibrary` share (steps 89, 100) builds `catalogueImports` as `CatalogueImportContext.create` with `exportFolderOpt` (step 116) set to `Some locations.cataloguesFolder` (`DataLocations.cataloguesFolder`, step 81) by record update, so every library window the app opens suggests it. Every other composition (`DefaultStores`, `initWith`, the tests) keeps `None`. (4) Tests. `AppContextTests` gains `the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports`: over an app context composed through `TestAppScope` (step 83: `testLocations`, `freshAppContext`), `catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` is `Some` of those locations' `cataloguesFolder`, and `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`'s `exportFolderOpt` is `None`. Every `LibraryWindowTests`, `MaterialsWindowTests` and `ImportDialogTests` fact passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the shared pieces land, `LibraryWindowView.fs` MUST declare no `verbButton`, `verbButtonOn` or `pickCatalogueFolder` of its own, and the app's `catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` MUST be the configured catalogues folder; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-SHARED-WINDOW-PIECES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-SHARED-WINDOW-PIECES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.pickLibraryFolder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-SHARED-WINDOW-PIECES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 119, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.3g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [118], "how_to": "The Materials window exports the selected material to its file and the shown materials to a catalogue folder, and credits a licensed material (001 §B 'Export', 'Licence attribution'; 001 §G 'Exports'; the S3.3 brief: the buttons go in the Library and Materials windows, with messages and ids; a single-entry export goes through a save dialog defaulting to the catalogues folder; a category exports to a catalogue folder; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each a one-line doc: `type LibraryExportError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`); `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.exportedCaption (file : FileName) : ControlCaption` = `Exported <name> version <n> to <file>; that version is now pinned.`; and `type CatalogueData with member this.exportedCaption (folder : FolderName) : ControlCaption` = `Exported <k> entries to the catalogue folder <folder>; their versions are now pinned.`, `k` counting its envelopes. Both windows render their export outcomes through these alone. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) The public `pickEntryExportFile (owner : Window) (startOpt : FolderName option) (envelope : LibraryEntryEnvelope) (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` is the save dialog, an IO edge in `pickLibraryFolder`'s shape (step 118): `owner.StorageProvider.SaveFilePickerAsync` with `Title = \"Export library entry\"`, `SuggestedFileName = envelope.content.fileName.value`, `DefaultExtension` the kind's extension without its leading dot, one `FilePickerFileType` whose pattern is `*` plus that extension, `ShowOverwritePrompt = true`, and `startOpt` resolved as `pickLibraryFolder` resolves it. A confirmed file's `Path.LocalPath` is passed as a `FileName`, posted on the UI thread. (b) The public `attributionPanel (id : ConstructorUiId) (lines : EntryAttributionLine list) : IView list` answers nothing for no line, else one vertical `StackPanel` carrying `id` that holds one wrapping `TextBlock` per line (`line.text`, max width 380). (c) `MaterialsWindowModel` gains `entryExportStatus : ControlCaption option` and `entryExportError : LibraryExportError option`, both `None` when the window opens, each with a one-line doc. (d) `member this.exportableSelection : LibraryEntryEnvelope option` is, in Browse mode, the selected material's latest envelope through `context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope id.toLibraryEntryId` (step 116), and `None` in Select mode, without a selection, for a material the seam does not hold, or on a read error. (e) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `ExportSelectedMaterial of FileName` (the selected material's latest version to the file chosen in the save dialog) and `ExportShownMaterials of CatalogueExportTarget` (the materials the window shows, its text filter and facets applied, to a catalogue folder; a category facet makes it that category's export). (f) `updateMaterialsWindow`. `ExportSelectedMaterial file` is inert without a selection, and otherwise calls `context.catalogueImports.exportEntry id.toLibraryEntryId file`. `ExportShownMaterials target` calls `exportEntries` over `m.filteredEntries` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:476`), each `e.id.toLibraryEntryId`, and `target`. `Ok` sets `entryExportStatus` to the outcome's `exportedCaption` and clears `entryExportError`; `Error e` sets `entryExportError` to `Some e` and clears `entryExportStatus`. Neither arms or disarms a gate, or changes the selection or the mode. (g) The view. In the verbs row (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:971`), in Browse mode and after Categories…: while `exportableSelection` is `Some envelope`, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.materialsExportButton (ControlCaption \"Export…\")` resolves the owner window from the press, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton` does, and calls `pickEntryExportFile owner context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt envelope (fun file -> dispatch (ExportSelectedMaterial file))`. While `filteredEntries` is not empty, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.materialsExportShownButton (ControlCaption \"Export shown to catalogue…\")` calls `pickLibraryFolder owner (ControlCaption \"Export to catalogue folder\") context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` and dispatches `ExportShownMaterials (CatalogueExportTarget.ofFolder folder)` (step 117). After step 110's import status, when either is set, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialsExportStatusText` shows `entryExportError`'s caption in `messageColor`, or else `entryExportStatus`. The view panel (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:1096`), after the description, holds `attributionPanel ConstructorUiId.materialsAttributionPanel` over `context.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf [ shownEntry.id.toLibraryEntryId ]` (step 114), and nothing on a read error. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group (`UiIds.fs:525`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.3: `materialsExportButton` (`\"MaterialsExportButton\"`), `materialsExportShownButton` (`\"MaterialsExportShownButton\"`), `materialsExportStatusText` (`\"MaterialsExportStatusText\"`) and `materialsAttributionPanel` (`\"MaterialsAttributionPanel\"`). (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`. The export and attribution facts compose `stubContext` (step 110) over the in-memory double: with `let stores = CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, the context takes `stores.materials`, `stores.categories` and `CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy`, the Built-in catalogue is imported through its `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and test entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries`. Files go into fresh GUID folders under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"MaterialsWindowTests\")`. `the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids`: the four ids' texts. `ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version`: with `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` selected (`SelectEntry`), `ExportSelectedMaterial` of `<folder>/Lab glass.material-json` writes the file, which the context's `readEntryFile` reads back equal to the held envelope. `entryExportStatus` is `Exported Lab glass version 1 to <file>; that version is now pinned.`, and `Lab glass`, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through `stores.materials`, resolves at versions 1 and 2. `ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category`: `userCategoryContent` `Lab category` holds `Lab glass` and `Lab quartz` (their `categoryOpt` set to it), and `Other glass` stays in Silicon's category. With the material-category facet applied to `Lab category` (`ApplyFacetValue`), `ExportShownMaterials` of a target folder writes a catalogue holding exactly the two materials and the category, and the status counts 3 entries. `a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing`: with a committed text filter `Lab glass` showing two user materials of that name, `ExportShownMaterials` sets `entryExportError` to `Some (ExportCatalogueRefusedErr _)`, the status is `None`, and the target folder does not exist; a following `ExportSelectedMaterial` that succeeds clears the error. `a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only`: `exportableSelection` is the held envelope of the selected `Lab glass`, `None` without a selection, and `None` for a Select-mode model over the same context and selection. `the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone`: `materialsWindowView` mounted headless, as the class's mounting facts mount the window's view, with `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` (`CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`) selected, shows `materialsAttributionPanel` holding the text `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`. With `RII glass` (`CC0-1.0`) selected it holds `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0` and no `cite:`, and with `Lab glass` selected no `materialsAttributionPanel` is present.", "acceptance": "After the Materials window is wired, its Export… and Export shown to catalogue… verbs MUST export through `exportEntry` and `exportEntries`, and its view panel MUST show the selected material's attribution; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids`, `ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version`, `ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category`, `a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing`, `a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only`, `the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests.the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.pickEntryExportFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialsWindowView.attributionPanel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "obligations": ["S33-MATERIALS-EXPORT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 120, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.3h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [119], "how_to": "The Library window exports the selected entry, the shown entries and the user's whole library, and credits the licensed materials of a selected sample (001 §B 'Export', 'Licence attribution'; 001 §C '\"Export my library\" writes the user entries to a catalogue folder'; .spec-md §10.1: 'Export my library…' is in the Library window; the S3.3 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`. (a) `LibraryWindowError` gains `LibraryExportRefusedErr of LibraryExportError`, documented, and its `caption` renders it through `LibraryExportError.caption` (step 119). (b) `LibraryWindowModel` gains `entryExportStatus : ControlCaption option`, `None` when the window opens, with a one-line doc. (c) `member this.exportableSelection : LibraryEntryEnvelope option` is, in Browse mode, the selected entry's latest envelope through `entry.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId` (step 24) and `context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope` (step 116), and `None` otherwise, as step 119's is. (d) `LibraryWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry of FileName`, `ExportShownLibraryEntries of CatalogueExportTarget` and `ExportMyLibrary of CatalogueExportTarget`. (e) `updateLibraryWindow`. `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry file` is inert without an `exportableSelection`, and otherwise calls `context.catalogueImports.exportEntry` of its id and `file`. `ExportShownLibraryEntries target` calls `exportEntries` over the ids of `m.filteredEntries` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:518`), each `e.entryId.tryToLibraryEntryId`. `ExportMyLibrary target` calls `exportUserLibrary target` (step 117). `Ok` sets `entryExportStatus` to the outcome's `exportedCaption` (step 119) and clears `lastError`; `Error e` sets `lastError` to `Some (LibraryExportRefusedErr e)` and clears `entryExportStatus`. None of them arms or disarms a gate, or changes the selection or the mode. (f) The view. In the verbs row (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1104`), in Browse mode and after step 101's Register catalogue folder… and step 111's Review imports…, through `MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn` and the pickers of steps 118 and 119 opened at `context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt`: `libraryExportButton` (`Export…`) while `exportableSelection` is `Some`, dispatching `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry`; `libraryExportShownButton` (`Export shown to catalogue…`) while `filteredEntries` is not empty, dispatching `ExportShownLibraryEntries`; and `libraryExportMyLibraryButton` (`Export my library…`), always, its picker titled `Export my library to a catalogue folder`, dispatching `ExportMyLibrary`. Each catalogue target is `CatalogueExportTarget.ofFolder` of the picked folder. `entryExportStatus`, when `Some`, shows in a `TextBlock` carrying `libraryExportStatusText` after step 101's `libraryImportStatusText`. The view panel (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1240`), after the description, holds `MaterialsWindowView.attributionPanel ConstructorUiId.libraryAttributionPanel` over `context.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf entry.attributedEntryIds` (steps 113, 114), and nothing on a read error, so a selected sample credits the licensed materials of its layers. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Library window group (`UiIds.fs:498`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.3: `libraryExportButton` (`\"LibraryExportButton\"`), `libraryExportShownButton` (`\"LibraryExportShownButton\"`), `libraryExportMyLibraryButton` (`\"LibraryExportMyLibraryButton\"`), `libraryExportStatusText` (`\"LibraryExportStatusText\"`) and `libraryAttributionPanel` (`\"LibraryAttributionPanel\"`). (3) Tests, in `LibraryWindowTests`. The export and attribution facts compose `stubContext` (steps 101, 111) over the in-memory double: with `let stores = CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, the context takes `samples = stores.samples`, `materials = stores.materials`, `library = stores.libraryEntries` and `catalogueImports = CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy`, the Built-in catalogue is imported through its `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and test entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries`. Files go into fresh GUID folders under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"LibraryWindowTests\")`. `the export and attribution UiIds of the Library window are the stable intent-named ids`: the five ids' texts. `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry writes the selected entry's file and pins its version`: with `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack` over `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` selected (`SelectLibraryEntry`), `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry` of `<folder>/Lab stack.sample-json` writes the file, which the context's `readEntryFile` reads back equal to the held envelope. `entryExportStatus` is `Exported Lab stack version 1 to <file>; that version is now pinned.`, and `stores.samples.removeSample` of `Lab stack` answers `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. `ExportShownLibraryEntries writes the shown entries and the user materials they reference`: with the text filter `Lab stack` committed (`CommitLibraryTextFilter`), `ExportShownLibraryEntries` of a target folder writes a catalogue holding exactly `Lab stack` and `Lab glass`, and the status counts 2 entries. `ExportMyLibrary writes every user entry to a catalogue folder`: over `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass`, `ExportMyLibrary` writes a catalogue whose ids are exactly `heldUserEntries ()`'s three, none under `BuiltInProvenance`. `a refused Library export shows its reason as the window message`: over a library holding only the Built-in catalogue, `ExportMyLibrary` sets `lastError` to `Some (LibraryExportRefusedErr (EmptyLibraryExportErr _))`, `entryExportStatus` is `None`, and the target folder does not exist. `the Library window shows the citation of a CC-BY material of the selected sample`: `libraryWindowView` mounted headless, as the class's mounting facts mount the window's view, with `PTB stack` (a `sampleContentOver` `PTB glass`, `CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`) selected, shows `libraryAttributionPanel` holding `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`; with a built-in source selected no `libraryAttributionPanel` is present. `Export my library over the app library writes a catalogue folder that a new library registers with every user entry`: over `AppContext.create` of one `TestAppScope.fileLocations` scope, a user material `Lab glass` saved through the context's `materials.saveMaterial` and a sample `Lab stack` over it saved through `samples.saveSample` reach the database seam. `stubContext` updated with the app context's stores and `catalogueImports` takes `ExportMyLibrary` of a target folder under the test output, and its status counts 2 entries. Over a second, fresh scope, a second `AppContext.create`'s `catalogueImports.registerFolder` of that folder MUST answer CatalogueAwaitsChoices with both rows and no entry/log writes; after the fixture explicitly confirms the complete list through settle, materials.tryGetMaterial and samples.tryGetSample MUST resolve both entries unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the Library window is wired, its Export…, Export shown to catalogue… and Export my library… verbs MUST export through `exportEntry`, `exportEntries` and `exportUserLibrary`, and its view panel MUST credit the licensed materials of a selected sample; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the export and attribution UiIds of the Library window are the stable intent-named ids`, `ExportSelectedLibraryEntry writes the selected entry's file and pins its version`, `ExportShownLibraryEntries writes the shown entries and the user materials they reference`, `ExportMyLibrary writes every user entry to a catalogue folder`, `a refused Library export shows its reason as the window message`, `the Library window shows the citation of a CC-BY material of the selected sample`, `Export my library over the app library writes a catalogue folder that a new library registers with every user entry`, the count rising by 7; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the export and attribution UiIds of the Library window are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.ExportSelectedLibraryEntry writes the selected entry's file and pins its version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.ExportShownLibraryEntries writes the shown entries and the user materials they reference", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.ExportMyLibrary writes every user entry to a catalogue folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.a refused Library export shows its reason as the window message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.the Library window shows the citation of a CC-BY material of the selected sample", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests.Export my library over the app library writes a catalogue folder that a new library registers with every user entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-LIBRARY-EXPORT"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 121, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S3.3i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [120], "how_to": "The Details bay credits the licensed entries of the selected element's binding: the bound entry and, for a sample, the materials of its layers (001 §B 'Licence attribution': in the Details view; the S3.3 brief: the Details view of a bound element). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, in the `type TableAndElementRotationModel with` block that holds `detailsState` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3187`): the public `member model.detailsAttributionLines : EntryAttributionLine list`. For `ElementSelected i` whose element has a bound entry (`boundEntry`, `:2449`), it is `model.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf entry.attributedEntryIds` (steps 101, 113, 114). It is `[]` on a read error, for an unbound element, and without an element selection. `detailsState` appends each line's `text` on its own line after the title and the out-of-band warning, so the Details bay (`BayNames.details`) shows the credit under what the element is. Its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) Tests, in `LayerBandsControlsTests`, over `initMain ()`, whose `catalogueImports` is the in-memory double its stores were imported through (step 101's `DefaultStores`). Step 113's `putSealedEntries` puts `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` (`CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`), `licensedMaterialContent` `RII glass` (`CC0-1.0`), and `sampleContentOver` `PTB stack` and `RII stack` over them; the double pushes each new entry into the model's stores. `the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation`: after `AddElement Sample` and the class's `bind` of the new element to `PTB stack`, `detailsAttributionLines` is exactly one line whose text is `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`. Bound to `RII stack`, it is `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0`, and bound to `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s sample, it is `[]`. `the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material`: the Details bay, mounted headless as `the Details bay renders the bound multilayer sample's bands and description` mounts it but without the `ui-smoke` trait, shows a `layerBandsTitle` whose text holds `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test` for an element bound to `PTB stack`.", "acceptance": "After the Details bay is wired, `detailsAttributionLines` MUST credit a bound entry and the licensed materials of a bound sample, and the Details bay MUST show them; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation` and `the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests.the Details of a bound sample credit its CC-BY material with its citation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-DETAILS-ATTRIBUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests.the Details bay shows the citation of a bound sample's CC-BY material", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S33-DETAILS-ATTRIBUTION"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S3.3 -- Export, Export my library and licence attribution"}
{"number": 122, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [121], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests"], "how_to": "The kit's identity and its kit file, as pure Domain data (001 §E 'The kit file holds the kit id (GUID), name, author, created and modified times, notes, … and the sendExclude globs'; 001 §A 'A file that exists once per folder is named by its extension alone: .kit-json'; 001 §P 'a ClockProvider'; .spec-md §3.11, §5 'Kit module'). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`: `module Kit` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `EntryTextDiff.fs` (step 106): one `<Compile Include=\"Kit.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. It opens `LibraryEntryFiles` (step 24: `KitId`, `FileStem`, `FileSchemaVersion`) and `Softellect.Sys.Primitives` (`FileExtension`, `FileName`, `FolderName`). Every type follows `AGENTS.md`: single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool` appears, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.1. `KitId` is step 24's type and MUST NOT be declared again (ELEV014). In this order: (1) `ClockTime of DateTime`, an instant the injected clock answers, in UTC. (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ClockProvider = { now : unit -> ClockTime }`, the injected clock (.spec-md §4 'Time comes from ClockProvider'): the composition root passes the system clock, a test a fixed or stepping one. No system clock is declared here; the code that first opens a kit in the app composes it. (3) `KitError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the folder or the file: `KitIoErr` (a kit's file or folder could not be read, written, listed or deleted), `NotAKitFolderErr` (the folder, or the folder's `.kit-json`, does not exist), `KitAlreadyExistsErr` (a folder asked to become a kit already holds a `.kit-json`), `KitFileRejectedErr` (a kit file's text failed its parse, schema or version check) and `InvalidKitNameErr` (a blank kit name). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form, a fixed phrase naming the condition, a colon and the reason: `a kit file could not be read or written: <reason>`, `the folder is not a kit: <reason>`, `the folder is already a kit: <reason>`, `a kit file was refused: <reason>` and `the kit name is not valid: <reason>`. Later steps add cases, each with its line. (4) `KitName of string`, the kit's display name. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<KitName, KitError>` keeps the text as given and refuses one that is empty or white space with `InvalidKitNameErr`. `member this.fileStem : FileStem` is `FileStem.ofText this.value`: the filesystem-safe name rule is step 24's, reached through this member, and no second rule is written (.spec-md §3.11). (5) `KitAuthor of string` (any text, empty allowed), `KitNotes of string` (free text, empty when there are none) and `SendExcludeGlob of string` (a glob such as `**/*.dng` that Send kit… leaves out, 001 §E; S6 reads it). (6) `KitFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; id : KitId; name : KitName; author : KitAuthor; created : ClockTime; modified : ClockTime; notes : KitNotes; sendExclude : SendExcludeGlob list }`, the `.kit-json`. Its static members mirror `CatalogueManifest`'s (step 26): `currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` is 1; `extension : FileExtension` is `.kit-json`, the one place that text is written; `fileName : FileName` is `(FileStem.ofText \"\").withExtension KitFile.extension`, because a file that exists once per folder is named by its extension alone; and `create (id : KitId) (name : KitName) (author : KitAuthor) (now : ClockTime) : KitFile` answers `KitFile.currentSchemaVersion`, `created` and `modified` both `now`, `KitNotes \"\"` and no glob. The id is minted by the caller (S5.2's New kit…), never here. S8.3 adds the naming template and S9.2 the import profiles. (7) `KitFolder of FolderName`, a folder that is or becomes a kit (001 §A 'KitFolder (the folder path type)'). (8) `KitAccess` = `ReadWriteKitAccess` | `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, how a kit is opened (001 §E 'an open read-only choice'). No `bool` stands for it and no member maps it to one (ELEV012). No other type, member or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs`, `module KitTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. `a kit name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `KitName.tryCreate \"Optics: QZ/LR\"` answers the text unchanged, and its `fileStem` is `FileStem \"Optics_ QZ_LR\"`, equal to `FileStem.ofText \"Optics: QZ/LR\"`; `\"\"` and `\"   \"` answer `InvalidKitNameErr`. `a new kit file is created and modified at one instant, with no notes and no send exclusions`: `KitFile.create` over `KitId (Guid.Parse \"6f1c2a9e-3b7d-4e25-9a41-0c8d5e7f2b16\")`, that name, `KitAuthor \"Test author\"` and `ClockTime` of `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)` answers schema version 1, that id, name and author, `created` and `modified` equal to the instant, `KitNotes \"\"` and an empty `sendExclude`. `the kit file is named by its extension alone`: `KitFile.extension` is `FileExtension \".kit-json\"` and `KitFile.fileName` is `FileName \".kit-json\"`. `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text that contains the reason.", "acceptance": "After `Kit.fs` lands, `KitFile.create` MUST answer a kit file created and modified at the given instant, `KitName.tryCreate` MUST refuse a blank name and `KitFile.fileName` MUST be `.kit-json`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `a new kit file is created and modified at one instant, with no notes and no send exclusions`, `the kit file is named by its extension alone`, `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a kit name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a new kit file is created and modified at one instant, with no notes and no send exclusions", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.the kit file is named by its extension alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every kit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ClockProvider", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 123, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [122], "how_to": "How a kit names what it holds, and the one hash of bytes (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths (forward slashes) plus the SHA-256 recorded at attach time', 'Absolute paths are never stored'; 001 §A 'Kit extensions'; 001 §P: `KitProxy` covers 'kit, items, setups, experiments, studies and fit runs'; .spec-md §5). (1) In `Kit.fs`, after `KitAccess` (step 122), each doc one to three lines: (a) `KitRelativePath of string`, a path inside a kit, with forward slashes. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<KitRelativePath, KitError>` replaces every `\\` with `/` and then refuses, with `InvalidKitPathErr` naming the text: an empty or white-space text; a rooted path (a leading `/`); a path holding a `:` (a drive such as `C:/data` or `C:data`); and a path any of whose `/`-separated segments is empty, `.` or `..`. Otherwise it answers the forward-slashed text, so a path is never absolute and never escapes the kit. No other normalisation is added. (b) `KitFileKind` = `ItemKitFile` | `SetupKitFile` | `ExperimentKitFile` | `StudyKitFile` | `FitRunKitFile`: the kit files that exist many times, one per item, setup, experiment, study and fit run (001 §A; the `.kit-json` is not a kind, because it has its own verbs). `member this.extension : FileExtension` answers `.item-json`, `.setup-json`, `.experiment-json`, `.study-json` and `.fitrun-json`; `member this.fileNameOf (stem : FileStem) : FileName` is `stem.withExtension this.extension` (step 24); `static member all : KitFileKind list` lists the five in that order. The kinds are stored only as their extensions, so no int tag, `tryOfWire` or other member is added. The sections that bring each kind's format (S4.3 experiments and setups, S7.1 items, S11 studies and fit runs) add no case and no proxy verb. (c) `KitFileText of string`, the text of a file in a kit: a kit file the app owns, or a lab file it only reads (001 §E), UTF-8 without a byte-order mark. One type serves both, because two would need a conversion each way (ELEV006). (d) `KitDataFile = { path : KitRelativePath; text : KitFileText; contentHash : ContentHash }`: a lab file as read, with the SHA-256 of its bytes as stored (001 §E). (e) `KitError` gains `MissingKitFileErr of reason : string` (the kit holds no file at that name or path) and `InvalidKitPathErr of reason : string`, rendered `the kit holds no such file: <reason>` and `the path is not inside the kit: <reason>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `ContentHash` (step 24) gains `static member ofBytes (bytes : byte[]) : ContentHash`, the lowercase hex (`Convert.ToHexStringLower`) SHA-256 (`SHA256.HashData`) of the bytes. Its doc says it is the one SHA-256 body of the app, used for an entry's canonical content and for a kit's files. `ContentHash`'s doc names both uses. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`: `contentHashOf` (step 27) hashes the UTF-8 bytes of the compact canonical rendering through `ContentHash.ofBytes`, and its own `SHA256.HashData` / `Convert.ToHexStringLower` lines are deleted: a move, so every hash is unchanged and step 27's frozen hash literal (`CanonicalJsonTests`, `the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen`) still holds. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122): `a kit-relative path keeps forward slashes and refuses an absolute or escaping path`: `data\\raw\\run 1.csv` answers `data/raw/run 1.csv`, and `data/raw/run 1.csv` and `.kit-json` are kept as given; `\"\"`, `\"  \"`, `/data/a.csv`, `C:/a.csv`, `C:a.csv`, `../a.csv`, `data/../../a.csv`, `data/./a.csv` and `data//a.csv` each answer `InvalidKitPathErr`. `every kit file kind renders its 001 extension and names its files`: the five extensions exactly as above, `all` in that order, and `ExperimentKitFile.fileNameOf (FileStem \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL\")` is `FileName \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL.experiment-json\"`. `every kit error renders its condition and its payload` (step 122) also covers the two new cases. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` (step 24) gains `the content hash of bytes is their lowercase SHA-256`: `ContentHash.ofBytes` of the UTF-8 bytes of `abc` is `ContentHash \"ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad\"`, and of no bytes `ContentHash \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\"`.", "acceptance": "After the path, kind and hash types land, `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` MUST refuse every absolute or escaping path and `contentHashOf` MUST hash through `ContentHash.ofBytes` with every hash unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit-relative path keeps forward slashes and refuses an absolute or escaping path`, `every kit file kind renders its 001 extension and names its files`, `the content hash of bytes is their lowercase SHA-256` and the widened `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a kit-relative path keeps forward slashes and refuses an absolute or escaping path", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every kit file kind renders its 001 extension and names its files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.the content hash of bytes is their lowercase SHA-256", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every kit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitRelativePath", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitFileKind", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitDataFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.ContentHash.ofBytes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PATHS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 124, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [123], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests"], "how_to": "The `.kit-json` text: canonical JSON, validated against its own schema on read, a version mismatch a typed error (001 §B 'No up-converters … The same holds for kit files'; the S4.1 brief: kit.schema.json is validated on read; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats', §6 'JSON + schema'). It reuses the stack of steps 27-31, and the two bodies a second format would copy move to one home each. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`. (a) `type JsonNode with member this.canonicalFileText : string` is the indented canonical rendering (step 27) followed by one `\\n`: the form of every file the app writes. `LibraryEntryEnvelope.fileText` (step 30) and `CatalogueManifest.fileText` (step 31), in `EntryFileJson.fs`, now render through it, and the code that appended the `\\n` in each is deleted. (b) `parseVersionedText<'Value> (validate : JsonElement -> Result<unit, StorageError>) (extension : FileExtension) (expected : FileSchemaVersion) (text : string) : Result<'Value, StorageError>` holds the read order of `LibraryFileText.parseCatalogueManifest` (step 31), moved: parse the text (`MalformedJsonErr`); `validate` the root element (`SchemaValidationErr`); compare its top-level `schemaVersion` with `expected` before anything binds (`UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` of `{ fileExtension = extension; found; expected }`, step 30); bind through `options` (`MalformedJsonErr`). Every throwing .NET call is caught there. It is marked `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"a versioned file's text, parsed, validated and bound at the storage seam (spec 0050 S4.1)\")>]`, because its signature carries the text. `parseCatalogueManifest` now calls it with `SchemaValidation.validateCatalogueManifest`, `CatalogueManifest.extension` and `CatalogueManifest.currentSchemaVersion`, and its own body is deleted, so step 31's facts stay green unchanged. (2) The schema. New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/library-catalogue.schema.json` (step 31), with `$id` `https://berreman/schema/kit.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1 (`then`): every key of `KitFile` is present (`schemaVersion`, `id`, `name`, `author`, `created`, `modified`, `notes`, `sendExclude`) and no other (`additionalProperties: false`); `id` is the GUID string of `library-common.schema.json` (step 30), referenced by its `$id`; `name` is a string holding a non-white-space character (the pattern `\\S`); `author` and `notes` are strings; `created` and `modified` are strings; and `sendExclude` is an array of non-empty strings. A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside step 30's `schema/library-*.schema.json` items of `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateKitFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith` (step 29), its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as step 30's entry schemas do (`SchemaValidation.fs:17-21`: `JsonSchema.FromText` registers an `$id` only once). (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs`, `module KitFolderStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `CatalogueImportStore.fs` (step 94): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit`. (a) `type KitFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` (step 27) rendered by `canonicalFileText`, so a kit file is indented canonical JSON with sorted keys, LF line ends and one final `\\n`. The two instants are written by the serializer's own ISO 8601 form, which keeps every tick and the `Z` of a UTC instant. (b) `type KitFileText with member this.parseKitFile : Result<KitFile, StorageError>` is `parseVersionedText validateKitFile KitFile.extension KitFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value`. There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs`, `module KitFileJsonTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its kit file is `KitFile.create` over `KitId (Guid.Parse \"6f1c2a9e-3b7d-4e25-9a41-0c8d5e7f2b16\")`, the name `Optics: QZ/LR — µ` and `KitAuthor \"Test author\"`, with `created` at `ClockTime` of `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc).AddTicks 1234567L` and `modified` one day later, the notes `Two lines\\nof notes` and the globs `**/*.dng` and `data/raw/big/**`. `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text`: `fileText` then `parseKitFile` answers an equal kit file; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys in ordinal order (`author`, `created`, `id`, `modified`, `name`, `notes`, `schemaVersion`, `sendExclude`), keeps `µ` and `—` unescaped, and writes `created` as `2026-11-03T12:00:00.1234567Z`; writing the parsed kit file again gives the same text. `a kit file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` set to 2, both with its body intact and as `{ \"schemaVersion\": 2 }` alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = KitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`: the text without `name`, with an extra key `colour`, with `name` set to `\"   \"`, and with `id` set to `not-a-guid`, each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; the text `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After the kit file's text lands, `KitFileText.parseKitFile` MUST validate against `schema/kit.schema.json` and refuse another schema version with `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, and the entry, manifest and kit file texts MUST render through `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a kit file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 3, with every `EntryFileJsonTests` fact (steps 30-31) passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests.a kit file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE-TEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests.a kit file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE-TEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE-TEXT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE-TEXT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateKitFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE-TEXT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitFolderStore.KitFileText.parseKitFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FILE-TEXT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 125, "anchor": "ADD_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S4.1d", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0004", "name": "KitProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [123], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests"], "how_to": "The kit-folder seam in Domain: its record over the kit file, and its in-memory double over a shared in-memory folder (001 §P: `KitProxy`, built per opened folder; 001 §F 'New kit…: … An empty folder is initialised; a folder that already has files keeps them, and .kit-json plus the app's subfolders are added'; .spec-md §4: every proxy has an in-memory implementation of the same shape; §5 `KitProxy`: 'Fields grow as kinds land'). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`: `module KitFolders` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `Kit.fs` (step 122): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `Kit` and `LibraryEntryFiles`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.1. (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitProxy = { initialiseKit : KitFile -> Result<unit, KitError>; readKitFile : unit -> Result<KitFile, KitError>; writeKitFile : KitFile -> Result<unit, KitError> }`, the functional-proxy convention of `ElementId.fs:583` (`SourceProxy`): one proxy per kit folder, built once where the folder is opened. Each field has a one-line doc. `initialiseKit` makes the folder a kit: it refuses a folder that already holds a `.kit-json` with `KitAlreadyExistsErr` and writes nothing; otherwise it keeps every file and folder the folder holds and adds the folders `data` and `library` and the kit file. `readKitFile` answers the kit file, or `NotAKitFolderErr` when there is none. `writeKitFile` replaces the kit file whole, or answers `NotAKitFolderErr`, writing nothing, when the folder is not a kit yet, so `initialiseKit` is the one way a folder becomes a kit. (2) `InMemoryKitFolder`, one in-memory kit folder that every in-memory proxy built over it shares, as two windows share one folder. Its content (the kit file, texts by their kit-relative path, the folders that exist and, from step 129, the lock) is state private to it, mutated only inside its members and the proxies' closures, the boundary as in `ElementId.fs:1101` (`SourceProxy.createInMemory`). Its public surface is: `static member create () : InMemoryKitFolder`, a folder that exists and holds nothing; `member this.placeLabFile (path : KitRelativePath) (text : KitFileText) : Result<unit, KitError>`, an outside writer placing or replacing a text at a path and adding its parent folders (the `.kit-json` path is refused with `InvalidKitPathErr`, because only `initialiseKit` and `writeKitFile` write the kit file); and `member this.paths () : KitRelativePath list`, every file and folder it holds (the `.kit-json`, each text and each of its parent folders, each folder added), in ordinal order. One map of texts by path serves every text a later step stores, so a kit file of a kind (step 127) is the text at its file name and a lab file is the text at its path, as in a real folder. (3) `type KitProxy with static member createInMemory (folder : InMemoryKitFolder) : KitProxy`, the double (.spec-md §4). Its three fields follow (1) over the folder's state; the folder it names in an error's reason is `in-memory kit folder`. No caching, retry or other field is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests` (test code is outside the ELEV scope). It declares, each with a one-line doc: a test-local record `KitTestFolder = { openProxy : unit -> KitProxy; placeLabFile : string -> string -> unit; paths : unit -> string list }`, one folder as the facts see it: `openProxy` builds a NEW proxy over the same folder each call, as a second window or process would; `placeLabFile path text` is an outside writer (an instrument, another editor) placing a file at a kit-relative path; `paths` lists every file and folder under the kit, kit-relative with forward slashes, in ordinal order. `steppingClock () : ClockProvider` starts at `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)` and advances one second per call. `newKitFile (clock : ClockProvider) : KitFile` is `KitFile.create` over `KitId (Guid.Parse \"6f1c2a9e-3b7d-4e25-9a41-0c8d5e7f2b16\")`, `Optics: QZ/LR` and `KitAuthor \"Test author\"` at `clock.now ()`. `[<AbstractClass>] type KitProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshFolder : unit -> KitTestFolder`, a folder that exists and holds nothing, and holds the contract facts; `type KitProxyTests () = inherit KitProxyContract ()` answers a fresh `InMemoryKitFolder.create ()` whose `openProxy` is `KitProxy.createInMemory` over it, whose `placeLabFile` goes through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` and `placeLabFile`, and whose `paths` renders `paths ()`. The facts: `a folder holds no kit until it is initialised`: `readKitFile` of a fresh folder answers `NotAKitFolderErr`, `writeKitFile` answers `NotAKitFolderErr`, and `paths` is empty. `initialising an empty folder writes the kit file, data and library, and nothing else`: after `initialiseKit (newKitFile clock)`, `paths` is exactly `.kit-json`, `data` and `library`, and `readKitFile` answers the kit file given. `initialising a folder that holds files keeps every one of them`: with `notes.txt` and `raw/run 1.csv` placed first, `initialiseKit` answers `Ok`, and `paths` is exactly `.kit-json`, `data`, `library`, `notes.txt`, `raw` and `raw/run 1.csv` (.spec-md §3.13: AT-1 builds its kit around its lab folder). `a folder that already holds a kit is not initialised again`: a second `initialiseKit`, of another kit file and through a second proxy, answers `KitAlreadyExistsErr`; `readKitFile` still answers the first and `paths` is unchanged. `the kit file is replaced in place and read back equal`: `writeKitFile` of the kit file with `notes = KitNotes \"Reviewed\"` and `sendExclude = [ SendExcludeGlob \"**/*.dng\" ]` answers `Ok`, and `readKitFile` of a second proxy answers it.", "acceptance": "After the seam lands, `KitFolders.fs` MUST declare `KitProxy` with exactly `initialiseKit`, `readKitFile` and `writeKitFile`, `InMemoryKitFolder` and `KitProxy.createInMemory`, and `KitProxyContract` MUST hold the kit-file facts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a folder holds no kit until it is initialised`, `initialising an empty folder writes the kit file, data and library, and nothing else`, `initialising a folder that holds files keeps every one of them`, `a folder that already holds a kit is not initialised again`, `the kit file is replaced in place and read back equal` under `KitProxyTests`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a folder holds no kit until it is initialised", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.initialising an empty folder writes the kit file, data and library, and nothing else", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.initialising a folder that holds files keeps every one of them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a folder that already holds a kit is not initialised again", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.the kit file is replaced in place and read back equal", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PROXY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PROXY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.InMemoryKitFolder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-PROXY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 126, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S4.1e", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0004", "name": "KitProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [124, 125], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests"], "how_to": "The folder implementation of `KitProxy` (001 §P 'KitProxy.create (folder : KitFolder)'; 001 §E 'Writes are atomic (write *.tmp, then replace)'; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO', 'Stored formats'; §5). (1) One atomic writer of bytes. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs` (step 33), `type FileName with member this.writeBytesAtomically (bytes : byte[]) : Result<unit, StorageError>` holds the body of `LibraryFileText.writeAtomically`, moved: write the bytes to `<file>.tmp` beside the file, then move it over the file (`File.Move(tmp, file, true)`); on a failure delete the `.tmp` and answer `FileIoExn`. `LibraryFileText.writeAtomically` keeps its signature and now writes the text's UTF-8 bytes without a byte-order mark through it, so one body writes every file atomically and step 33's facts stay green unchanged. (2) In `KitFolderStore.fs` (step 124): `type KitProxy with static member create (folder : KitFolder) : KitProxy`, unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` (ELEV019). Building it touches nothing in the folder. `initialiseKit kitFile`: a `.kit-json` (`KitFile.fileName`) already in the folder is `KitAlreadyExistsErr` naming the folder, and nothing is written; otherwise it creates the folder when missing, then `data` and `library` (each is kept when it is there), and writes `kitFile.fileText` (step 124) through `writeBytesAtomically` LAST, so a folder is a kit only once it is whole. Every file the folder held is kept. `readKitFile`: a missing folder or a missing `.kit-json` is `NotAKitFolderErr` naming the folder; otherwise the bytes are read and decoded as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped, and `parseKitFile` (step 124) answers the kit file. Its `StorageError` is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming `.kit-json`, the folder and the error's `describe` (step 33), so another schema version is reported with both versions. `writeKitFile kitFile`: a missing `.kit-json` is `NotAKitFolderErr` and nothing is written; otherwise the text replaces it through `writeBytesAtomically`. Every .NET IO exception is caught here and answered `KitIoErr` naming the file or folder and the exception's message; a `FileIoExn` of the writer is `KitIoErr` in the same way. Nothing above the proxy handles an exception (.spec-md §4). A declaration whose signature carries a bare primitive for that IO is marked on itself with `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof IoBoundary, …)>]`. (3) The `KitProxy` doc names `KitProxy.create` beside the in-memory double in one line. Tests, in `KitProxyTests.fs`. `type KitProxyFolderTests () = inherit KitProxyContract ()`, in `KitProxyTests.fs`, runs every contract fact over a real folder: `freshFolder` creates a new folder `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitProxyFolderTests\", <a new GUID>)`, never under `%TEMP%` (the `ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs:24` precedent); `openProxy` is `KitProxy.create (KitFolder (FolderName folder))`; `placeLabFile` creates the parent folders and writes the text as UTF-8 without a byte-order mark; `paths` enumerates every file and folder recursively, relative to the folder, `\\` replaced by `/`, in ordinal order. Its own facts: `a folder that does not exist is not created by its proxy, and initialising it creates it`: `KitProxy.create` over a folder path that does not exist, then `readKitFile`, answers `NotAKitFolderErr` and the folder still does not exist; `initialiseKit` then creates it holding exactly `.kit-json`, `data` and `library`. `a kit file of another schema version or of broken text is refused, naming the kit file`: after `initialiseKit`, the `.kit-json` rewritten by the test with `schemaVersion` set to 2 makes `readKitFile` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` whose reason names `.kit-json` and both versions; the file rewritten as `{` answers `KitFileRejectedErr` naming `.kit-json`; neither throws, and the file is left as the test wrote it.", "acceptance": "After the folder store lands, a test MUST instantiate the real `KitProxy.create` over a folder under the test output, and `LibraryFileText.writeAtomically` MUST write through `FileName.writeBytesAtomically`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every `KitProxyContract` fact under `KitProxyFolderTests` and its own `a folder that does not exist is not created by its proxy, and initialising it creates it` and `a kit file of another schema version or of broken text is refused, naming the kit file`, the count rising by 7, with every `CatalogueFolderTests` fact (step 33) passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a folder holds no kit until it is initialised", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.initialising an empty folder writes the kit file, data and library, and nothing else", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.initialising a folder that holds files keeps every one of them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a folder that already holds a kit is not initialised again", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.the kit file is replaced in place and read back equal", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a folder that does not exist is not created by its proxy, and initialising it creates it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a kit file of another schema version or of broken text is refused, naming the kit file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitFolderStore.KitProxy.create", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CatalogueFolderStore.FileName.writeBytesAtomically", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-FOLDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 127, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [126], "how_to": "The kit files that exist many times, one verb set for every kind (001 §A 'The kit root is flat: every kit file sits at the root, and its kind is its extension'; the S4.1 brief: list, read, write and delete kit files per kind, generic over the kind's extension so later kinds add no verbs). (1) `KitProxy` (step 125) gains four fields, each with a one-line doc. `listKindFiles : KitFileKind -> Result<FileStem list, KitError>` answers the stems of the files at the kit root whose names end with the kind's extension (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`), in ordinal order; a file of another kind, the `.kit-json`, a `*.tmp` and a file in a subfolder are not listed. `readKindFile : KitFileKind -> FileStem -> Result<KitFileText, KitError>` answers the text of `kind.fileNameOf stem` (step 123), or `MissingKitFileErr` naming it. `writeKindFile : KitFileKind -> FileStem -> KitFileText -> Result<unit, KitError>` creates or replaces that file whole. `deleteKindFile : KitFileKind -> FileStem -> Result<unit, KitError>` deletes it, or answers `MissingKitFileErr` naming it and changes nothing. The stem is the caller's, made safe by step 24's rule (`FileStem.ofText`) before the call, so a name keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md §3.11). The text is the caller's; each kind's format arrives with its shapes, as the kit file's did in step 124. (2) `KitProxy.createInMemory` (step 125) implements them over the folder's one map of texts, at the root path `kind.fileNameOf stem`. (3) `KitProxy.create` (step 126) implements them over the folder's root: the listing reads the folder's top-level file names; a read decodes UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped; a write goes through `writeBytesAtomically` (step 126) as UTF-8 without a byte-order mark; IO exceptions are `KitIoErr` as in step 126. Tests. New `KitProxyContract` facts (step 125), so both classes run them: `kit files of every kind are listed, read, replaced and deleted by their names`: after `initialiseKit`, for each kind of `KitFileKind.all`, `writeKindFile` of the stems `QZ-LR` and `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` with distinct texts, then `listKindFiles` answers the two in ordinal order, `readKindFile` answers each text, a second `writeKindFile` of `QZ-LR` replaces its text, and `deleteKindFile` of the other leaves `listKindFiles` answering `QZ-LR` alone; files of the other kinds and the `.kit-json` are never listed under a kind, and `paths` holds each file at its name. `reading or deleting a missing kit file is MissingKitFileErr and changes nothing`: `readKindFile` and `deleteKindFile` of a stem never written answer `MissingKitFileErr`, and `paths` is unchanged. `replacing a kit file leaves only its new text and no temporary file`: after `writeKindFile` of `QZ-LR` as a setup and its replacement, `paths` holds `QZ-LR.setup-json` once and no path ending with `.tmp`, and `readKindFile` answers the new text. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains `a replace that fails keeps the old file whole, removes its temporary file and is KitIoErr`: while the test holds `QZ-LR.setup-json` open with `FileShare.None`, `writeKindFile` of a new text answers `KitIoErr`; once the test lets go, the file holds its old text and the folder holds no `*.tmp`.", "acceptance": "After the per-kind verbs land, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST list, read, write and delete kit files of every `KitFileKind` by stem; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `kit files of every kind are listed, read, replaced and deleted by their names`, `reading or deleting a missing kit file is MissingKitFileErr and changes nothing`, `replacing a kit file leaves only its new text and no temporary file` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` and `a replace that fails keeps the old file whole, removes its temporary file and is KitIoErr`, the count rising by 7; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.kit files of every kind are listed, read, replaced and deleted by their names", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.kit files of every kind are listed, read, replaced and deleted by their names", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.reading or deleting a missing kit file is MissingKitFileErr and changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.reading or deleting a missing kit file is MissingKitFileErr and changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.replacing a kit file leaves only its new text and no temporary file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.replacing a kit file leaves only its new text and no temporary file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a replace that fails keeps the old file whole, removes its temporary file and is KitIoErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S41-KIND-FILES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 128, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [127], "how_to": "Reading a lab file by its kit-relative path with its SHA-256 (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths (forward slashes) plus the SHA-256 recorded at attach time'; 'Lab files are read-only for the app'; the S4.1 brief: read a data file by relative path with its SHA-256). Copy-in and the attachment that records the hash are S4.2's. (1) `KitProxy` gains `readDataFile : KitRelativePath -> Result<KitDataFile, KitError>` with a one-line doc: the file at that path inside the kit, its text, and `ContentHash.ofBytes` (step 123) of its bytes as stored, or `MissingKitFileErr` naming the path. Any file of the kit can be read so, under `data/` or anywhere else; nothing is written. (2) `KitProxy.createInMemory` answers the text at the path in the folder's map, hashed as its UTF-8 bytes. (3) `KitProxy.create` joins the path's segments under the kit folder with the platform's separator, reads the bytes, hashes them, and decodes the text as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark (EF BB BF) dropped from the text, never from the hashed bytes. A missing file is `MissingKitFileErr`; an IO exception is `KitIoErr` as in step 126. Tests. A new `KitProxyContract` fact: `a lab file is read by its kit-relative path with the SHA-256 of its bytes`: with `data/raw/run 1.csv` placed as `phi,I\\n0,0.5\\n`, `readDataFile` of that path answers its path, its text and the test's own `Convert.ToHexStringLower (SHA256.HashData (Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes text))`; `readDataFile` of `data/raw/none.csv` answers `MissingKitFileErr`; `paths` is unchanged. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains `a lab file with a byte-order mark reads without it and hashes its bytes as stored`: a file written by the test as the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `a,b\\n` reads as the text `a,b\\n` with the hash of all its bytes, byte-order mark included; and `a lab file another process holds open is KitIoErr, never a throw`: while the test holds `data/run.csv` open with `FileShare.None`, `readDataFile` answers `KitIoErr`.", "acceptance": "After the lab-file read lands, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST answer a lab file's text and the SHA-256 of its stored bytes by its kit-relative path; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a lab file is read by its kit-relative path with the SHA-256 of its bytes` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, `a lab file with a byte-order mark reads without it and hashes its bytes as stored` and `a lab file another process holds open is KitIoErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a lab file is read by its kit-relative path with the SHA-256 of its bytes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-DATA-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a lab file is read by its kit-relative path with the SHA-256 of its bytes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-DATA-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a lab file with a byte-order mark reads without it and hashes its bytes as stored", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-DATA-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a lab file another process holds open is KitIoErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-DATA-FILES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S41-DATA-FILES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 129, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [128], "how_to": "One window per kit, guarded by `.oc/lock` (001 §E 'a .oc/lock (machine, user, process, time) warns across processes and machines, with an open read-only choice'; 001 §A '.oc/ app-owned cache and lock; safe to delete'; the S4.1 brief: a foreign live lock is KitLockedErr carrying the holder, and the caller can then open read-only). (1) In `Kit.fs`, declared above `KitError` (step 122), each doc one to three lines: `MachineName of string` and `UserName of string`; `KitLockOwner = { machine : MachineName; user : UserName; processId : ProcessId }`, who opened a kit, where `ProcessId` is `Softellect.Sys.Primitives.ProcessId` (STL `Sys/Primitives.fs:802`), reused and not declared again (ELEV014); and `KitLockHolder = { owner : KitLockOwner; acquiredAt : ClockTime }`, with `member this.describe : string` = `<user> on <machine> (process <id>) since <yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss> UTC`, the time in the invariant culture. `KitError` gains `KitLockedErr of holder : KitLockHolder`, rendered `the kit is open elsewhere: <holder's describe>`. (2) `KitProxy` gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `acquireLock : ClockTime -> Result<KitLockHolder, KitError>` takes the kit's lock for this proxy at that time and answers the holder. `releaseLock : unit -> Result<unit, KitError>` gives it back. Both implementations keep one rule. A lock is this proxy's when this proxy took it; any other lock is foreign, even one taken in the same process, because two windows on one kit are two holders. Acquiring while this proxy holds the lock answers its holder again and writes nothing. Acquiring when there is no lock, or a stale one, writes `{ owner = <this proxy's owner>; acquiredAt = time }` into `.oc/lock`, creating `.oc` when missing (`.oc` is created on the first write that needs it and never before), and answers it. Acquiring against a foreign live lock answers `KitLockedErr` of its holder and writes nothing; the caller can then open the kit read-only (step 131). Releasing deletes `.oc/lock` when this proxy holds it and the file still names its holder, and keeps `.oc`; otherwise it does nothing. No verb breaks another's lock: 001 §E offers read-only instead. (3) `KitProxy.createInMemory`: the n-th proxy built over one `InMemoryKitFolder`, counting from 1, is owned by `{ machine = MachineName \"in-memory\"; user = UserName \"in-memory\"; processId = ProcessId n }`. The folder holds the lock, which `paths` lists as `.oc/lock` under `.oc`. Every in-memory lock is live. (4) `KitProxy.create`: the owner is `Environment.MachineName`, `Environment.UserName` and `ProcessId.getCurrentProcessId ()`, read when the proxy is built. In `KitFolderStore.fs`, `type KitLockHolder with member this.lockFileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` by `canonicalFileText` (step 124), and `type KitFileText with member this.parseLockHolder : Result<KitLockHolder, StorageError>` binds it through `CanonicalJson.options` (`MalformedJsonErr`). No schema covers it, because `.oc/` is cache. A lock is stale when its text does not bind, or when it names this machine (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`) and a process id with no running process (`Process.GetProcessById` raises `ArgumentException`); every other lock is live. Taking it writes the holder's text to `.oc/lock-<a new GUID>.tmp` and moves that file to `.oc/lock` without overwriting (`File.Move(tmp, lock, false)`), deleting a stale lock first, so two openers racing never both hold it: the one whose move fails deletes its `.tmp`, reads the winner and answers `KitLockedErr` of it. Releasing reads `.oc/lock` and deletes it only when it binds to this proxy's holder. IO exceptions are `KitIoErr` as in step 126. Tests. `KitTests` gains `a lock holder renders who holds the lock, on which machine and since when`: a holder of `UserName \"lab\"` on `MachineName \"BENCH-1\"`, process 4242, acquired at `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)`, renders `lab on BENCH-1 (process 4242) since 2026-11-03 12:00:00 UTC`; and `every kit error renders its condition and its payload` covers `KitLockedErr`. New `KitProxyContract` facts, each over proxies A, B and C from `openProxy` on one initialised folder and times from `steppingClock`: `a second proxy cannot take a held lock and is told who holds it, until it is released`: A's `acquireLock` answers a holder; B's answers `KitLockedErr` of exactly that holder; after A's `releaseLock`, B's answers a holder of B's owner at B's time. `a proxy that holds the lock keeps it when it asks again, and another proxy's release leaves it`: A's second `acquireLock` answers A's first holder, its time unchanged; B's `releaseLock` answers `Ok`, and C's `acquireLock` still answers `KitLockedErr` of A's holder. `the lock is written in the cache folder only when it is first taken, and its release keeps the folder`: after `initialiseKit`, `paths` holds no `.oc`; after A's `acquireLock` it holds `.oc` and `.oc/lock`; after A's `releaseLock` it holds `.oc` and no `.oc/lock`. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains, each writing `.oc/lock` itself through `lockFileText` where a holder is needed: `the folder lock names this machine, this user and this process`: the holder `acquireLock` answers is owned by `Environment.MachineName`, `Environment.UserName` and this process, and `.oc/lock` parses to it; `a lock left on this machine by a process that has ended is taken over`: a lock of this machine and process 2147483647 (`Int32.MaxValue`, never a Windows process id, which are multiples of 4) is replaced, and `acquireLock` answers this proxy's holder; `a lock taken on another machine is live`: a lock of `MachineName \"another-machine\"` and this process answers `KitLockedErr` of it and stays; and `an unreadable lock is taken over`: a `.oc/lock` holding `not a lock` is replaced, and `acquireLock` answers this proxy's holder.", "acceptance": "After the lock lands, a second `KitProxy` over a locked kit MUST answer `KitLockedErr` carrying the holder while the first holds it, in both implementations, and the folder lock MUST be taken without overwriting a live one; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a lock holder renders who holds the lock, on which machine and since when`, the widened `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`, `a second proxy cannot take a held lock and is told who holds it, until it is released`, `a proxy that holds the lock keeps it when it asks again, and another proxy's release leaves it`, `the lock is written in the cache folder only when it is first taken, and its release keeps the folder` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, `the folder lock names this machine, this user and this process`, `a lock left on this machine by a process that has ended is taken over`, `a lock taken on another machine is live`, `an unreadable lock is taken over`, the count rising by 11; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a lock holder renders who holds the lock, on which machine and since when", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every kit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a second proxy cannot take a held lock and is told who holds it, until it is released", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a second proxy cannot take a held lock and is told who holds it, until it is released", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a proxy that holds the lock keeps it when it asks again, and another proxy's release leaves it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a proxy that holds the lock keeps it when it asks again, and another proxy's release leaves it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.the lock is written in the cache folder only when it is first taken, and its release keeps the folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.the lock is written in the cache folder only when it is first taken, and its release keeps the folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.the folder lock names this machine, this user and this process", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a lock left on this machine by a process that has ended is taken over", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a lock taken on another machine is live", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.an unreadable lock is taken over", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitLockHolder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitLockOwner", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-LOCK"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 130, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [129], "how_to": "The external-change check (001 §E 'on activation, files changed outside the app (another editor, git, a sync) are offered for reload'; the S4.1 brief: the stamps recorded at load against the folder now, giving the changed kit files). The kit files are the `.kit-json` and every root file of a `KitFileKind.all` extension; lab files, `.oc/` and `*.tmp` files are never stamped. The offer itself is S5.3's. (1) `KitProxy` gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `recordStamps : unit -> Result<unit, KitError>` records the stamp of every kit file now, replacing any earlier record. `changedKitFiles : unit -> Result<FileName list, KitError>` answers the file name of every kit file whose stamp now differs from the recorded one, or that exists on one side only (added or removed), in ordinal order. The record lives inside the proxy and is never written to the folder (.spec-md §3.12: a read-only open writes no stamp). This proxy's own `initialiseKit`, `writeKitFile` and `writeKindFile` set the written file's entry to its new stamp and `deleteKindFile` removes it, so only other writers' changes are answered. Before any `recordStamps` the record is empty, and every kit file present is answered. (2) `KitProxy.create`: a stamp is `ContentHash.ofBytes` (step 123) of the file's bytes, so a file rewritten with the same bytes is not a change. `KitProxy.createInMemory`: a stamp is the content itself, the kit file by equality and a text by its text, which answers the same as the folder for every contract fact. The record of each is private to its closure. Tests. New `KitProxyContract` facts: `kit files another writer adds, changes or removes are reported, and this proxy's own writes are not`: after A's `initialiseKit`, A's `writeKindFile` of `X` as an experiment and A's `recordStamps`, A's `writeKindFile` of `own` as a setup leaves A's `changedKitFiles` empty; then B writes `Y` as a setup, replaces `X`'s text, deletes `own` and writes the kit file with new notes, and A's `changedKitFiles` answers exactly `.kit-json`, `X.experiment-json`, `Y.setup-json` and `own.setup-json`, in that order. `recording the stamps again clears the report, and lab files are never reported`: after those changes, A's `recordStamps` makes `changedKitFiles` answer `Ok []`; placing `data/new.csv` and `notes.txt` leaves it empty; and a new proxy C, which never recorded, answers every kit file present.", "acceptance": "After the change check lands, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST answer the kit files another writer added, changed or removed since `recordStamps`, and none of their own writes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `kit files another writer adds, changes or removes are reported, and this proxy's own writes are not` and `recording the stamps again clears the report, and lab files are never reported` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.kit files another writer adds, changes or removes are reported, and this proxy's own writes are not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-CHANGE-CHECK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.kit files another writer adds, changes or removes are reported, and this proxy's own writes are not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-CHANGE-CHECK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.recording the stamps again clears the report, and lab files are never reported", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-CHANGE-CHECK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.recording the stamps again clears the report, and lab files are never reported", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-CHANGE-CHECK"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S41-CHANGE-CHECK"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 131, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.1j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [130], "how_to": "What logic receives: the opened kit (001 §P 'Logic receives a KitContext'; the S4.1 brief: KitContext holds the proxy, the loaded KitFile, the access and the clock, and a read-only KitContext writes nothing at all, not even .oc/; .spec-md §3.12). In `KitFolders.fs`, after `KitProxy.createInMemory`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.1: (1) `KitError` (step 122, in `Kit.fs`) gains `KitReadOnlyErr of reason : string` (a write asked of a kit opened read-only, the reason naming the verb), rendered `the kit is open read-only: <reason>`. (2) `type KitProxy with member this.readOnlyView : KitProxy` answers the same proxy with every write refused: `initialiseKit`, `writeKitFile`, `writeKindFile`, `deleteKindFile` and `acquireLock` answer `KitReadOnlyErr` naming the field and write nothing; `releaseLock` answers `Ok ()` and does nothing; `readKitFile`, `listKindFiles`, `readKindFile`, `readDataFile`, `recordStamps` and `changedKitFiles` pass through, because they write nothing. A field a later step adds that writes is refused here too. (3) `KitContext = { proxy : KitProxy; kitFile : KitFile; access : KitAccess; clock : ClockProvider }`. `static member openKit (proxy : KitProxy) (access : KitAccess) (clock : ClockProvider) : Result<KitContext, KitError>` opens the kit in this order. Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` the context's proxy is `proxy.readOnlyView`; under `ReadWriteKitAccess` it is `proxy`. It reads the kit file (an error passes through and nothing is written). Under `ReadWriteKitAccess` it acquires the lock at `clock.now ()`; `KitLockedErr` passes through with nothing written, and the caller can open the kit again read-only. Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` no lock is taken. It then records the stamps (step 130); on an error there it releases the lock it took and passes the error through. `member this.close () : Result<unit, KitError>` releases the lock (the read-only view releases nothing). `member this.saveKitFile (kitFile : KitFile) : Result<KitContext, KitError>` sets `modified` to `this.clock.now ()`, writes the kit file through the context's proxy and answers the context holding it, so a read-only context answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. `modified` is when the app last wrote the kit file; the writes of the other kit files leave the `.kit-json` alone, so a git-managed kit does not churn it on every save. No other member is added: logic reads and writes the kit's other files through `context.proxy`. Tests. New `KitProxyContract` facts: `opening a kit read-write reads its kit file and takes the lock, and closing it releases the lock`: over an initialised folder, `openKit` of A with `ReadWriteKitAccess` answers a context holding the kit file and `ReadWriteKitAccess`, and `paths` holds `.oc/lock`; its `close ()` answers `Ok` and `paths` holds no `.oc/lock`. `a kit open elsewhere refuses a read-write open and allows a read-only one`: with A opened read-write, `openKit` of B with `ReadWriteKitAccess` answers `KitLockedErr` and `paths` is unchanged, and `openKit` of B with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` answers a context holding the same kit file and `ReadOnlyKitAccess`. `a read-only kit context writes nothing, not even the cache folder`: over a folder initialised with one experiment file written, with no lock taken, the read-only context's `proxy.initialiseKit`, `proxy.writeKitFile`, `proxy.writeKindFile`, `proxy.deleteKindFile` and `proxy.acquireLock` and its `saveKitFile` each answer `KitReadOnlyErr`; its `proxy.readKindFile` answers the experiment's text; its `close ()` answers `Ok`; and `paths` is exactly what it was before the open, with no `.oc`. `saving the kit file through the context stamps its modified time`: over a folder initialised with `newKitFile clock`, `openKit` of A with `ReadWriteKitAccess` and the same stepping clock, then `saveKitFile` of the opened kit file with `notes = KitNotes \"Reviewed\"`, answers a context whose kit file's `modified` is two seconds after its `created` (the clock answered the creation, then the lock, then the save) and whose `created` is unchanged, and B's `readKitFile` answers that kit file. `opening a folder that is not a kit writes nothing`: `openKit` of a fresh folder answers `NotAKitFolderErr` under both accesses, and `paths` stays empty. `every kit error renders its condition and its payload` (step 122) covers `KitReadOnlyErr`.", "acceptance": "After `KitContext` lands, `KitContext.openKit` MUST take the lock only under `ReadWriteKitAccess`, and a read-only context MUST write nothing, not even `.oc`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening a kit read-write reads its kit file and takes the lock, and closing it releases the lock`, `a kit open elsewhere refuses a read-write open and allows a read-only one`, `a read-only kit context writes nothing, not even the cache folder`, `saving the kit file through the context stamps its modified time`, `opening a folder that is not a kit writes nothing` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` and the widened `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 10; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.opening a kit read-write reads its kit file and takes the lock, and closing it releases the lock", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.opening a kit read-write reads its kit file and takes the lock, and closing it releases the lock", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a kit open elsewhere refuses a read-write open and allows a read-only one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a kit open elsewhere refuses a read-write open and allows a read-only one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a read-only kit context writes nothing, not even the cache folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a read-only kit context writes nothing, not even the cache folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.saving the kit file through the context stamps its modified time", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.saving the kit file through the context stamps its modified time", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.opening a folder that is not a kit writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.opening a folder that is not a kit writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every kit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy.readOnlyView", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S41-KIT-CONTEXT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.1 -- The kit file, KitFolder, KitProxy and KitContext"}
{"number": 132, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [131], "how_to": "The pure shapes of an attachment and of copying a lab file in (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths (forward slashes) plus the SHA-256 recorded at attach time', 'Attaching a file from outside the kit copies it into data/, keeping its name and suffixing on collision', 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open and before each fit'; the S4.2 brief: `DataAttachment` is a `KitRelativePath` plus the `ContentHash` recorded at attach, and a file from outside is copied into `data/` or a chosen folder inside it, keeping its name, with ` (2)`, ` (3)`… on collision; .spec-md §5 `Kit` module). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs` (steps 122-131), after `KitDataFile` (step 123), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2, every type following `AGENTS.md` (single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool`). (1) `KitDataFolder of KitRelativePath`, a folder of the kit that lab files are copied into: `data` or a folder inside it (001 §A 'data/ … raw lab files (default home for attachments)'). `static member root : KitDataFolder` is `data`, the folder `initialiseKit` creates (step 125). `static member tryCreate (path : KitRelativePath) : Result<KitDataFolder, KitError>` keeps `data` and every path that starts `data/` (ordinal) and refuses any other with `InvalidKitPathErr` naming it. (2) `member this.copyTargetFor (leaf : FileName) (taken : KitRelativePath list) : Result<KitRelativePath, KitError>` on `KitDataFolder` is the one collision rule. It answers the first of `<folder>/<leaf>`, `<folder>/<stem> (2)<extension>`, `<folder>/<stem> (3)<extension>`, … that no path of `taken` equals ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`, the Windows rule). The extension is the text from the leaf's last `.` when that `.` is not its first character, and empty otherwise: `run 1.csv` gives `run 1 (2).csv`, `archive.tar.gz` gives `archive.tar (2).gz`, `README` gives `README (2)` and `.hidden` gives `.hidden (2)`. Each candidate is made through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123), so a leaf that cannot be a kit path answers its `InvalidKitPathErr`. `taken` is every file and folder directly in the folder, and the rule reads nothing. (3) `type KitFolder with member this.tryKitPathOf (file : FileName) : KitRelativePath option` answers the kit-relative path of an absolute file name that lies inside the folder, and `None` otherwise. Both texts have every `\\` turned into `/`, and the folder's text loses a trailing `/`. When the file's text starts with the folder's text followed by `/`, ignoring case, the rest goes through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate`, whose `Ok` is the answer. Every other name is `None`, the folder itself and a sibling folder sharing a prefix (`C:/kits/a` against `C:/kits/ab/x.csv`) included. It touches no disk. (4) `LabFileSource = { file : FileName; content : FileByteContent }`, a lab file as the user picked it: its absolute name and its bytes. `FileByteContent` is `Softellect.Sys.Primitives.FileByteContent` (STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`), reused, not declared again (ELEV014). (5) `DataAttachment = { path : KitRelativePath; contentHash : ContentHash }`, the data file an experiment references: its path inside the kit and the SHA-256 recorded at attach (.spec-md §5). It never holds an absolute path. `type KitDataFile with member this.attachment : DataAttachment` answers the file's path and hash. (6) `DataAttachmentStatus` = `AttachedDataUnchanged` | `AttachedDataChanged of current : ContentHash` | `AttachedDataMissing`: unchanged, data changed since attach, or missing (001 §E). `member this.statusAgainst (currentOpt : KitDataFile option) : DataAttachmentStatus` on `DataAttachment` answers `AttachedDataMissing` for `None`, `AttachedDataUnchanged` for a file whose `contentHash` equals the recorded one, and `AttachedDataChanged` of the file's hash for any other. No other type, member, option or rule is added. Tests, new facts in `KitTests` (step 122). `a data folder is the kit's data folder or a folder inside it`: `KitDataFolder.root` is `data`; `tryCreate` keeps `data` and `data/raw/run 1`, and refuses `raw`, `library`, `datax` and `.oc/data` with `InvalidKitPathErr`. `a copy keeps its file name and takes the first free numbered suffix, ignoring case`: under `root`, `run 1.csv` with nothing taken answers `data/run 1.csv`; with `data/run 1.csv` taken, `data/run 1 (2).csv`; with that and `data/RUN 1 (2).CSV` taken, `data/run 1 (3).csv`. `archive.tar.gz`, `README` and `.hidden`, each taken once, answer `data/archive.tar (2).gz`, `data/README (2)` and `data/.hidden (2)`. Under `data/raw`, `a.csv` answers `data/raw/a.csv`, and a leaf `C:a.csv` answers `InvalidKitPathErr`. `a file is inside the kit when its absolute name lies under the kit folder`: over `KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/kits/Optics\")`, `C:/kits/Optics/data/run 1.csv`, `c:\\KITS\\optics\\data\\run 1.csv` and `C:/kits/Optics/notes.txt` answer `data/run 1.csv`, `data/run 1.csv` and `notes.txt`. `C:/kits/Optics`, `C:/kits/OpticsB/data/a.csv`, `D:/lab/a.csv` and `C:/kits/Optics/../a.csv` answer `None`. A folder text ending in `/` answers as the same folder. `an attachment records its data file's path and hash, and its status compares that hash with the file now`: a `KitDataFile` at `data/a.csv` with the hash of the UTF-8 bytes of `abc` (`ContentHash.ofBytes`, step 123) answers an attachment with that path and hash. That attachment against `Some` of the same file is `AttachedDataUnchanged`, against a file with the hash of `abd` is `AttachedDataChanged` of that hash, and against `None` is `AttachedDataMissing`.", "acceptance": "After the attachment shapes land, `KitDataFolder.copyTargetFor` MUST keep a lab file's name and take the first free ` (n)` suffix ignoring case, `KitFolder.tryKitPathOf` MUST locate only names inside the kit folder, and `DataAttachment.statusAgainst` MUST answer unchanged, changed or missing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a data folder is the kit's data folder or a folder inside it`, `a copy keeps its file name and takes the first free numbered suffix, ignoring case`, `a file is inside the kit when its absolute name lies under the kit folder`, `an attachment records its data file's path and hash, and its status compares that hash with the file now`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a data folder is the kit's data folder or a folder inside it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a copy keeps its file name and takes the first free numbered suffix, ignoring case", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a file is inside the kit when its absolute name lies under the kit folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.an attachment records its data file's path and hash, and its status compares that hash with the file now", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitDataFolder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitFolder.tryKitPathOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.LabFileSource", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.DataAttachment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.DataAttachmentStatus", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitDataFile.attachment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH-SHAPES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 133, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [132], "how_to": "Copy-in and location, the two kit verbs an attach needs, in both implementations (001 §E 'Attaching a file from outside the kit copies it into data/, keeping its name and suffixing on collision', 'Lab files are read-only for the app', 'Writes are atomic (write *.tmp, then replace)'; 001 §P '`KitProxy` … copy-in'; the S4.1 brief: copy a file in (S4.2)). (1) `KitProxy` (`KitFolders.fs`, steps 125-131) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `tryKitPathOf : FileName -> KitRelativePath option` answers the kit-relative path of an absolute file name that lies inside the kit, through `KitFolder.tryKitPathOf` (step 132), so both implementations share one rule. `copyInFile : KitDataFolder -> FileName -> FileByteContent -> Result<KitDataFile, KitError>` writes the bytes as a NEW file in the data folder. Its name is the leaf name given, or the one `copyTargetFor` (step 132) picks over every file and folder directly in that folder. It creates the folder and its parents when missing, and answers the file exactly as `readDataFile` (step 128) reads it back. It never replaces a file, because the app never writes a lab file (001 §E). (2) `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 125) gains `member this.kitFolder : KitFolder`, the folder it stands for, `KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/in-memory-kit\")`, against which its proxies locate names. It also gains `member this.removeLabFile (path : KitRelativePath) : Result<unit, KitError>`, an outside writer deleting a file: `MissingKitFileErr` when absent, and the `.kit-json` path refused with `InvalidKitPathErr`, as `placeLabFile` refuses it. `KitProxy.createInMemory`: `tryKitPathOf` is `folder.kitFolder.tryKitPathOf`. `copyInFile` decodes the bytes as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped and stores the text at the chosen path in the folder's one map of texts, adding its parent folders, so `readDataFile` then answers it hashed as its UTF-8 bytes, as step 128's double does. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs`: the body of `FileName.writeBytesAtomically` (step 126) becomes one private body over `ExistingFilePolicy` (`Softellect.Sys.Primitives.ExistingFilePolicy`, STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`, reused). It writes `<file>.tmp`, then moves it onto the file, replacing it under `OverwriteExistingFile` (`File.Move(tmp, file, true)`) and never under `RefuseExistingFile` (`File.Move(tmp, file, false)`). On any failure it deletes the `.tmp` and answers `FileIoExn`. `writeBytesAtomically` calls it with `OverwriteExistingFile`, so step 126's facts stay green unchanged. New `member this.writeNewBytesAtomically (bytes : byte[]) : Result<unit, StorageError>` calls it with `RefuseExistingFile`. A declaration whose signature carries the bytes is marked as step 126's is. (4) `KitFolderStore.fs`, `KitProxy.create` (steps 126-131): `tryKitPathOf` is the `tryKitPathOf` of the folder it was built over. `copyInFile` joins the data folder's segments under the kit folder with the platform's separator and creates the folder when missing. The names of its files and folders are the taken paths. The bytes go to the chosen path through `writeNewBytesAtomically`, and the answer is built from those bytes by the decode and hash of `readDataFile` (step 128), one body for both. Every IO exception and `FileIoExn` is `KitIoErr` naming the file, as in step 126. (5) `KitProxy.readOnlyView` (step 131) refuses `copyInFile` with `KitReadOnlyErr` naming it, writing nothing, and passes `tryKitPathOf` through. No retry, overwrite option, cache or other field is added. Tests, in `KitProxyTests.fs`. `KitTestFolder` (step 125) gains three fields, each with a one-line doc. `absoluteName : string -> FileName` is the absolute name of a kit-relative path in this folder: under `kitFolder` in memory, and `Path.Combine` of the folder and the path on disk. `outsideName : string -> FileName` is an absolute name outside the kit: under `C:/outside` in memory, and on disk under a sibling folder `outside-<GUID>` of the kit folder, never created. `removeLabFile : string -> unit` is an outside writer deleting a file. New `KitProxyContract` facts, so `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` both run them, each over an initialised folder (step 125): `a copied-in file keeps its name and bytes, and a taken name gets the next free suffix`: `copyInFile KitDataFolder.root (FileName \"run 1.csv\")` of the UTF-8 bytes of `phi,I\\n0,0.5\\n` answers `data/run 1.csv` with that text and the hash of those bytes, and `readDataFile` of it answers the same. A second copy of other bytes under the same leaf answers `data/run 1 (2).csv`, and a third `data/run 1 (3).csv`, while `data/run 1.csv` keeps its text. `paths` holds the three and no `*.tmp`. `copying into a new folder inside data creates it`: a copy into `KitDataFolder.tryCreate` of `data/raw/2026-11-03` creates that folder and its parent, and `paths` lists `data/raw`, `data/raw/2026-11-03` and the file. `a file inside the kit is located by its absolute name, and one outside it is not`: `tryKitPathOf (absoluteName \"data/run 1.csv\")` answers `data/run 1.csv` whether or not the file exists, and `tryKitPathOf (outsideName \"run 1.csv\")` answers `None`. `a read-only kit refuses a copy-in and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView`, `copyInFile` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and `paths` is unchanged. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains `a copied-in file holds exactly the bytes given, a byte-order mark included`: copied-in bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `a,b\\n` are the file's bytes exactly, and the answer's text is `a,b\\n` with the hash of all the bytes; and `the new-file writer refuses a file that exists, keeps it whole and leaves no temporary file`: over a file `x.csv` the test wrote, `writeNewBytesAtomically` of other bytes answers `FileIoExn`, the file keeps its bytes, and the folder holds no `*.tmp`.", "acceptance": "After copy-in lands, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST copy a lab file's bytes into the kit's data folder under its own name or the next free suffix, never replacing a file, and MUST locate names inside the kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a copied-in file keeps its name and bytes, and a taken name gets the next free suffix`, `copying into a new folder inside data creates it`, `a file inside the kit is located by its absolute name, and one outside it is not`, `a read-only kit refuses a copy-in and writes nothing` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, `a copied-in file holds exactly the bytes given, a byte-order mark included` and `the new-file writer refuses a file that exists, keeps it whole and leaves no temporary file`, the count rising by 10, with every step 126 and step 127 fact passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a copied-in file keeps its name and bytes, and a taken name gets the next free suffix", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a copied-in file keeps its name and bytes, and a taken name gets the next free suffix", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.copying into a new folder inside data creates it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.copying into a new folder inside data creates it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a file inside the kit is located by its absolute name, and one outside it is not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a file inside the kit is located by its absolute name, and one outside it is not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a read-only kit refuses a copy-in and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a read-only kit refuses a copy-in and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a copied-in file holds exactly the bytes given, a byte-order mark included", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.the new-file writer refuses a file that exists, keeps it whole and leaves no temporary file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.InMemoryKitFolder", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.CatalogueFolderStore.FileName.writeNewBytesAtomically", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs", "obligations": ["S42-COPY-IN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 134, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [133], "how_to": "Attaching a lab file and checking it later, as two Domain members over the proxy (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths … plus the SHA-256 recorded at attach time', 'Attaching a file from outside the kit copies it into data/', 'Lab files are read-only for the app', 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open and before each fit'; the S4.2 brief: a file inside the kit is recorded in place, and a status function compares the recorded hash with the file now). In `KitFolders.fs`, after `KitProxy.readOnlyView` (step 131), on one `type KitProxy with` extension, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2: (1) `member this.attachLabFile (target : KitDataFolder) (source : LabFileSource) : Result<DataAttachment, KitError>`. When `tryKitPathOf source.file` answers a path, the file is recorded in place: the answer is the `attachment` (step 132) of `readDataFile` of that path, nothing is written and `source.content` is not used. Otherwise the file is copied in: the answer is the `attachment` of `copyInFile target source.file.leafName source.content` (step 133). So an attachment always holds the kit-relative path and the hash of the bytes the kit holds, and no absolute path is kept. (2) `member this.attachmentStatus (attachment : DataAttachment) : Result<DataAttachmentStatus, KitError>` reads `readDataFile attachment.path` through `attachment.statusAgainst` (step 132). `MissingKitFileErr` is `AttachedDataMissing`, a read file is compared by its hash, and every other error passes through. It writes nothing, so a read-only kit answers it too. No cache, retry or other member is added. Tests: new `KitProxyContract` facts (step 125), so both classes run them, over an initialised folder. `attaching a file inside the kit records it in place and writes nothing`: with `data/run 1.csv` placed as `phi,I\\n0,0.5\\n`, `attachLabFile KitDataFolder.root { file = absoluteName \"data/run 1.csv\"; content = <the UTF-8 bytes of other text> }` answers `data/run 1.csv` with `readDataFile`'s hash, and `paths` and every text are unchanged. `attaching a file from outside copies it into data, and another of that name gets a suffix`: `attachLabFile` of `outsideName \"run 1.csv\"` with the UTF-8 bytes of `phi,I\\n0,0.5\\n` answers `data/run 1.csv` with the hash of those bytes. A second outside file with that leaf and other bytes answers `data/run 1 (2).csv`, and the first copy keeps its text. `an attachment whose file changed since attach is flagged, and one whose file is gone is missing`: over an attachment made as in the previous fact, `attachmentStatus` answers `AttachedDataUnchanged`. After the outside writer places other text at its path, it answers `AttachedDataChanged` of that text's hash as `readDataFile` gives it. After `removeLabFile` of the path, it answers `AttachedDataMissing`. The same three answers come through `readOnlyView`.", "acceptance": "After attach lands, `KitProxy.attachLabFile` MUST record a file inside the kit in place and copy one from outside into the data folder, and `KitProxy.attachmentStatus` MUST answer unchanged, changed or missing, in both implementations; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `attaching a file inside the kit records it in place and writes nothing`, `attaching a file from outside copies it into data, and another of that name gets a suffix`, `an attachment whose file changed since attach is flagged, and one whose file is gone is missing` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.attaching a file inside the kit records it in place and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.attaching a file inside the kit records it in place and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.attaching a file from outside copies it into data, and another of that name gets a suffix", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.attaching a file from outside copies it into data, and another of that name gets a suffix", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.an attachment whose file changed since attach is flagged, and one whose file is gone is missing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.an attachment whose file changed since attach is flagged, and one whose file is gone is missing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy.attachLabFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy.attachmentStatus", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S42-ATTACH"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number":135,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S4.2d","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[134],"how_to":"An experiment's data file becomes a kit attachment, read through the kit by its relative path (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths …', 'Absolute paths are never stored'; the S4.2 brief: `Experiments.DataFilePath`, an absolute path string today, is replaced by `DataAttachment` in `Experiment.dataFileOpt` and `attachDataFile`; `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` and `ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate` read through the kit by relative path; no kit file stores an absolute path). This is one step because the record field's type changes every consumer at once. (1) Domain. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs` opens `Kit`. `DataFilePath` (`Experiments.fs:DataFilePath`) is deleted. `Experiment.dataFileOpt` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) becomes `DataAttachment option` (step 132), and `attachDataFile` (`Experiments.fs:attachDataFile`) takes `(attachment : DataAttachment)`. Their docs say the attachment is a kit-relative path and its hash (spec 0050 S4.2). (b) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs`, after `DataFileText` (`MeasuredData.fs:DataFileText`): `type Kit.KitFileText with member this.dataFileText : DataFileText` hands a kit file's text to the measured-data parsers, in one direction only (ELEV006). Its doc is one line. (c) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs`: `ExperimentDataProxy` (`ExperimentDataProxy.fs:ExperimentDataProxy`) opens `Kit` and becomes `{ attachDataFile : FileName -> Result<DataAttachment, KitError>; attachmentStatus : DataAttachment -> Result<DataAttachmentStatus, KitError>; tryLoadIntensity : DataAttachment -> Result<IntensitySeries, ExperimentDataError>; tryLoadEllipsometric : DataAttachment -> Result<EllipsometricSeries, ExperimentDataError> }`, still `[<ReferenceEquality>]`. Each field has a one-line doc: attach a picked file to the kit, in place inside it and copied into `data/` otherwise; the attachment's status now; and the two loads by the attachment's kit path. The module and record docs say, in one to three lines each, that the seam reads through one kit (spec 0050 S4.2). Their paragraphs about the DECLARED lifecycle and a future file adapter are deleted, because that lifecycle ended at spec 0038 step 36. (d) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: the last parameter of `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`) becomes `(attachment : DataAttachment)`, passed to the loads. Nothing else changes. (e) The docs of `ExperimentCollectionStore.fs` that name `DataFilePath` say `DataAttachment`. (2) Storage. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs`, `createFileBacked ()` (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:createFileBacked`) becomes `createFileBacked (kit : KitProxy) : ExperimentDataProxy`. `attachDataFile file` reads the picked file into a `FileByteContent` where the bytes are read (`File.ReadAllBytes`; any exception is caught there and answered `KitIoErr` naming the file and the exception's message), then answers `kit.attachLabFile KitDataFolder.root` of `{ file = file; content = <that content> }` (step 134). `attachmentStatus` is `kit.attachmentStatus` (step 134). `loadThrough` (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:loadThrough`) reads `kit.readDataFile attachment.path` (step 128). A `KitError` is `MalformedDataFileErr` with today's text form, `could not read the <kind> data file '<kit path>': <describe>`, staying within the four-case channel, and the file's `text.dataFileText` goes to the parser unchanged. The module doc says, in one to three lines, that the seam reads through the kit it is built over and that the picked file's read is its one IO of its own. (3) Ui. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`, where `AppContext` composes `experimentData` (`AppContext.fs:AppContext.create`; `compose` since step 89), and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`'s `defaultExperimentProxies`: `experimentData` is `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked (KitProxy.createInMemory (InMemoryKitFolder.create ()))`, the session's in-memory kit, as the scene and collection seams beside it are in-memory stores. The `experimentData` field doc says so in one line. (b) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type KitError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` is its `describe` (step 122), with a one-line doc, beside the other error captions. (c) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. `ExperimentFileStatus` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:ExperimentFileStatus`) gains `DataFileAttachFailed of reason : ControlCaption`, captioned `Attach failed — <reason>`. `AttachDataFileTo` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TableAndElementRotationMsg`) carries `Experiments.ExperimentId * FileName`, the picked file, and its doc says the kit records it. Its update arm calls `model.experimentData.attachDataFile`. On `Error e` the experiment keeps what it had, and its status is `DataFileAttachFailed e.caption`. On `Ok attachment` it is today's arm over `attachDataFile experimentId attachment` and `loadAndValidate … attachment`. `pickDataFile` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`) passes `FileName file.Path.LocalPath`, and its `onPicked` takes a `FileName`. `dataFileRow` shows `file: <the attachment's kit path>`. Every comment that names `DataFilePath` names the attachment or the picked file. (d) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs`: the `type Experiments.DataFilePath with` extension (`UserEnvironment.fs:443-447`) is deleted, because `FileName.tryGetFolderName` (STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`) gives the same answer. `rememberFolder`'s `selectedFile` and `DataFilePick.FilePicked` (`UserEnvironment.fs:rememberFolder`, `UserEnvironment.fs:DataFilePick`) take a `FileName`. (e) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`: `handoffFileCaption` shows the attachment's kit path, and `validateExperiment` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`) passes the attachment to `loadAndValidate`. The doc of `SolverHandoffWindow.fs` names the measured-data seam over the kit where it names the step-36 load seam. (4) The project-file comments that name `DataFilePath`, in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, name the data attachment in no more words. Nothing is added. (5) Tests. Each fixture attachment is born as a `DataAttachment` with a `data/…` path and a test-local 64-character lowercase hex hash literal. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: the mock is keyed by the attachment's path, answers `attachDataFile` with an attachment at `data/<leaf>` and `attachmentStatus` with `AttachedDataUnchanged`. `a mock ExperimentDataProxy loads canned intensity and ellipsometric series through their exact signatures` and `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError from both fields, never a throw` keep their assertions over attachments at `data/run-intensity.csv`, `data/run-ellipsometric.csv` and `data/nowhere.csv`. `ExperimentDataStoreTests` builds each proxy as `createFileBacked (KitProxy.create (KitFolder (FolderName <a new GUID folder under the class's testDir>)))` and places each fixture text at `data/<name>` itself, its attachment being `readDataFile`'s. Its four facts keep their names and assertions, the missing-file one over an attachment whose path holds no file. It gains `createFileBacked copies a picked file from outside the kit into data and records one inside the kit in place`: a picked file the test wrote outside the kit folder attaches as `data/<its name>` holding its bytes, and a picked file the test wrote inside the kit's `data` folder attaches in place, writing nothing; and `createFileBacked answers KitIoErr for a picked file it cannot read and attaches nothing`: a picked name that does not exist answers `KitIoErr` naming it, and the kit holds nothing new. `ExperimentProxyTests`: `DataFilePath elevates a raw path and attachDataFile binds one per experiment` becomes `attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment`, over an attachment at `data/run1.csv`. `ExperimentCollectionProxyTests`' `a stub ExperimentCollectionProxy over a fixed map exercises saveCollection, tryLoadCollection, and listCollections through their exact signatures` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`' `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and DataFilePath attachments`, renamed `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments`, carry attachments at `data/run1.csv`, `data/e1-transmitted.csv` and `data/e3-dark.csv`, and keep their assertions. `InverseConstructorTests`: `mockIntensity` and `mockEllipsometric` answer `attachDataFile` with `data/<the picked file's leaf>` and `attachmentStatus` with `AttachedDataUnchanged`. The facts dispatch `AttachDataFileTo` with a `FileName` and assert the attachment's path, `data/measured.csv` and `data/run.csv`, keeping every other assertion: `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status`, `the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path`, `a named collection round-trips through save, list, and load` and the `ui-smoke` fact `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing`. It gains `a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment`: over a mock whose `attachDataFile` answers `KitIoErr`, `AttachDataFileTo` leaves the experiment's `dataFileOpt` `None` and its status `DataFileAttachFailed`, whose caption holds the reason. `DataFilePickerFolderTests`' five facts that pick a file (`a confirmed selection records the file's folder under the purpose key`, `a cancel leaves the persisted folder untouched`, `the next open passes the persisted folder as the picker start folder`, `a re-pick in a new folder replaces the persisted folder`, `a bare filename with no directory part leaves the folder map untouched`) pick a `FileName` and keep their assertions. `SolverHandoffWindowTests`' `withFile` attaches `data/<name>`, and its mocks gain the two fields and are keyed by the attachment's path; `ScrollExtentTests`' `noData` gains the two fields. Every fact of both keeps its assertions. After this step, `git grep -n -w DataFilePath -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor \":(exclude)*/MuellerReconstruction.fs\" \":(exclude)*/MuellerDataStore.fs\"` finds nothing. The two excluded files keep spec 0044's history note, because they belong to S9's removals.","acceptance":"After the switch, `Experiment.dataFileOpt` MUST hold a `DataAttachment`, `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` MUST read and attach through the kit it is built over, and `git grep -n -w DataFilePath -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor \":(exclude)*/MuellerReconstruction.fs\" \":(exclude)*/MuellerDataStore.fs\"` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `createFileBacked copies a picked file from outside the kit into data and records one inside the kit in place`, `createFileBacked answers KitIoErr for a picked file it cannot read and attaches nothing`, the renamed `attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment` and `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing`; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffWindow.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataFilePickerFolderTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.a mock ExperimentDataProxy loads canned intensity and ellipsometric series through their exact signatures","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError from both fields, never a throw","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked round-trips a known intensity file through the step-34 parser","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked round-trips a known ellipsometric file through the step-34 parser","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error from both fields, never a throw","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked delegates parse semantics: an existing but empty file is the parser's EmptyDataFileErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked copies a picked file from outside the kit into data and records one inside the kit in place","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked answers KitIoErr for a picked file it cannot read and attaches nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.DataFilePath elevates a raw path and attachDataFile binds one per experiment","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.a stub ExperimentCollectionProxy over a fixed map exercises saveCollection, tryLoadCollection, and listCollections through their exact signatures","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and DataFilePath attachments","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.a named collection round-trips through save, list, and load","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests.a confirmed selection records the file's folder under the purpose key","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataFilePickerFolderTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests.a cancel leaves the persisted folder untouched","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataFilePickerFolderTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests.the next open passes the persisted folder as the picker start folder","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataFilePickerFolderTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests.a re-pick in a new folder replaces the persisted folder","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataFilePickerFolderTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests.a bare filename with no directory part leaves the folder map untouched","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataFilePickerFolderTests.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.DataFilePath","op":"retire","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"],"preserves_obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.attachDataFile","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentData.ExperimentDataProxy","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.UserEnvironment.DataFilePick","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.UserEnvironment.rememberFolder","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ExperimentFileStatus","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.AttachDataFileTo","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MeasuredData.KitFileText.dataFileText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.KitError.caption","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S42-DATA-SEAM"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 136, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [135], "how_to": "An experiment's attachment is checked when its experiments are opened (001 §E 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open'; the S4.2 brief: the status function runs on open). Today the constructor opens experiments by loading a saved collection (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, the `CollectionLoad` arm of `updateTableAndElementRotation`), and that arm clears every status. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `ExperimentFileStatus` (step 135) gains `DataFileChangedSinceAttach`, captioned `Data changed since attach — attach it again to validate it`, and `DataFileMissingFromKit of path : ControlCaption`, captioned `Data file missing — <path>`, each with a one-line doc. (2) The `CollectionLoad` arm, on `Ok (Some snapshot)`, sets `experimentDataStatus` to one status for each loaded experiment that has an attachment, through `model.experimentData.attachmentStatus` (step 135). `AttachedDataUnchanged` validates it as attaching does (`loadAndValidate`, giving `DataFileValidated` or the error's status). `AttachedDataChanged _` is `DataFileChangedSinceAttach`. `AttachedDataMissing` is `DataFileMissingFromKit` of the kit path. An `Error e` is `AttachedFileParseError e.caption`, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:fileStatus` maps a read failure today. An experiment without an attachment has no status. The validation of the attach arm and of this arm is one private function, so it is written once. Its comment cites 001 §E in one line, where the clear-on-load comment stood. No other arm, field or message changes. Tests, in `InverseConstructorTests`. `loading a collection re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged`: a collection saved with an attachment and loaded into a fresh model sharing the collection store, over a mock whose `attachmentStatus` answers `AttachedDataUnchanged`, gives that experiment the status `DataFileValidated` with the mock's point count. `loading a collection flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`: a collection of two experiments, attached at `data/a.csv` and `data/b.csv`, loaded over a mock whose `attachmentStatus` answers `AttachedDataChanged` for the first and `AttachedDataMissing` for the second, gives them the statuses `DataFileChangedSinceAttach` and `DataFileMissingFromKit`, whose caption names `data/b.csv`, and the loaded experiments keep their attachments.", "acceptance": "After a collection loads, every loaded experiment with an attachment MUST carry a status computed through `attachmentStatus`: validated when unchanged, `DataFileChangedSinceAttach` when its data changed and `DataFileMissingFromKit` when it is gone; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `loading a collection re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged` and `loading a collection flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.loading a collection re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S42-OPEN-STATUS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.loading a collection flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S42-OPEN-STATUS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ExperimentFileStatus", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S42-OPEN-STATUS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 137, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [136], "how_to": "What a kit references in the library, as data (001 §E 'Library closure snapshot: every library version the kit references is copied into library/ when first referenced, built-ins included'; the S4.2 brief: a kit first references a library version by binding a sample, material or preset). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, directly before `LibraryEntryContent` (step 25), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2. `LibraryVersionRef = { entryId : LibraryEntryId; version : VersionNumber }` is one version of one library entry, with `member this.describe : string` = `<GUID> v<n>`. `EntryReference` = `EntryVersionReference of LibraryVersionRef` (a version named exactly, as a sample or a material is bound) | `EntryLatestReference of LibraryEntryId` (an entry named by its id alone, as a preset is bound and a material names its category), with `member this.entryId : LibraryEntryId` and `member this.describe : string` (`<GUID> v<n>` or `<GUID> (latest)`). `LibraryEntryContent` gains `member this.references : EntryReference list`. A material answers its `categoryOpt` as one `EntryLatestReference`. A sample answers its `structure.referencedMaterialVersions` (step 61), in that set's order, each as the `EntryVersionReference` of its material's `toLibraryEntryId` (step 24) and version. Every other kind answers nothing. `referencedEntryIds` (step 93) becomes the set of the `entryId`s of `references`, so the references are walked in one place and its answers are unchanged. `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.libraryVersionRef : LibraryVersionRef` is the content's id and version. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs` opens `LibraryEntryFiles`. `VersionRef` (`Lifecycle.fs:VersionRef`) gains `member this.entryReference : EntryReference`, the `EntryVersionReference` of the material's or the sample's id and version. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `ElementBinding` (`Experiments.fs:ElementBinding`) gains `member this.entryReferenceOpt : EntryReference option`. `BoundByVersion v` is `Some v.entryReference`, `BoundByEntryId id` is `id.tryToLibraryEntryId` (step 24) as an `EntryLatestReference`, and `Unbound` is `None`. `Experiment` gains `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list`, its setup's bindings in setup order, each once: what a kit snapshots when it records the experiment. Each doc is one to three lines. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006), and no other member is added. Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests` gains `an entry's references name a material's category at its latest and a sample's material versions`: Silicon's content (`BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`) answers exactly one `EntryLatestReference` of its `categoryOpt`'s category. `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s content answers the `EntryVersionReference`s of `MaterialIds.glass152` and `MaterialIds.vacuumMaterial` at version 1. A source's content answers `[]`. `an entry's references are its category and its materials` (step 93) passes unchanged. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `an experiment references the library versions its setup binds, each once`: an experiment whose setup binds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, `PresetIds.source600` twice and one unbound element answers exactly the `EntryVersionReference` of that sample at version 1 and the `EntryLatestReference` of the source's GUID.", "acceptance": "After the references land, `LibraryEntryContent.references` MUST name a material's category and a sample's material versions, `referencedEntryIds` MUST be their ids, and `Experiment.libraryReferences` MUST answer the setup's bindings once each; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an entry's references name a material's category at its latest and a sample's material versions` and `an experiment references the library versions its setup binds, each once`, the count rising by 2, with `an entry's references are its category and its materials` passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.an entry's references name a material's category at its latest and a sample's material versions", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-REFERENCES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.an experiment references the library versions its setup binds, each once", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-REFERENCES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.LibraryVersionRef", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S42-REFERENCES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryReference", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S42-REFERENCES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Lifecycle.VersionRef.entryReference", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs", "obligations": ["S42-REFERENCES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ElementBinding.entryReferenceOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S42-REFERENCES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.libraryReferences", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S42-REFERENCES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 138, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [137], "how_to": "The kit's `library/` folder holds one snapshot file per library version (001 §A '`library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json` — snapshot of every library version the kit uses'; 001 §C 'The library file, the database payload and a kit's snapshot of an entry are byte-identical, and the hash proves it'; the S4.1 brief: write and list snapshots (S4.2)). (1) `Kit.fs`: `KitError` gains `SnapshotExistsErr of reason : string`, rendered `the kit already holds this library snapshot: <reason>`. `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.snapshotFileName : FileName` is `<id>@v<n><kind extension>`: the GUID in its lowercase `D` form, the version number and `content.schema.kind.extension` (step 24), as in `<GUID>@v1.material-json`. `member this.snapshotPath : KitRelativePath` is that name under `library`. Each doc is one line citing 001 §A. (2) `KitProxy` gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `listSnapshots : unit -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope list, KitError>` answers every snapshot the kit holds, ordered ordinally by file name, each read through its kind's schema, version and hash checks. `writeSnapshot : LibraryEntryEnvelope -> Result<unit, KitError>` writes the envelope's entry file at its `snapshotPath`, creating `library` when missing. A snapshot already at that name is `SnapshotExistsErr` naming it, and nothing is written, because a snapshot is immutable. `readOnlyView` (step 131) refuses `writeSnapshot` with `KitReadOnlyErr` and passes `listSnapshots` through. (3) `KitProxy.createInMemory`: the private state of `InMemoryKitFolder` gains the snapshots, envelopes by file name, and `paths` lists each as `library/<name>` beside the `library` folder. (4) `KitProxy.create` (`KitFolderStore.fs`). `writeSnapshot` renders `fileText` (step 30) and writes its UTF-8 bytes, without a byte-order mark, through `writeNewBytesAtomically` (step 133), so the snapshot is byte for byte the catalogue's and the database's text; a `StorageError` from `fileText` is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file. `listSnapshots` answers `Ok []` when there is no `library` folder. Otherwise it reads every top-level file of `library` for which `LibraryEntryKind.tryOfFileName` (step 103) answers a kind; other files, `*.tmp` included, are no snapshot. It decodes the bytes as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped and parses them with `LibraryFileText.parseEntry` of that kind (step 30). A refusal, or a parsed envelope whose `snapshotFileName` is not the file's name ignoring case, is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming `library/<file>` and the reason. IO exceptions are `KitIoErr` as in step 126. No cache, overwrite or other field is added. Tests. `KitTests` gains `a snapshot is named by its entry id and version and its kind's extension, under library`: the `snapshotFileName` of Silicon's built-in envelope is Silicon's GUID text followed by `@v1.material-json`, and its `snapshotPath` is that name under `library`; and `every kit error renders its condition and its payload` covers `SnapshotExistsErr`. New `KitProxyContract` facts, over an initialised folder and envelopes of `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`: `a snapshot is written once under its id and version and listed back`: `writeSnapshot` of Silicon's and of `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`'s envelopes, then `listSnapshots`, answers both, equal, in file-name order, and `paths` holds `library/<each name>`. `a second snapshot of one version is refused and changes nothing`: a second `writeSnapshot` of Silicon's envelope, and of a sealed copy at version 1 with another description, each answer `SnapshotExistsErr`, and `listSnapshots` still answers the first. `a read-only kit refuses a snapshot and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView`, `writeSnapshot` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and `paths` is unchanged. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains `a snapshot file is byte for byte its catalogue entry file`: the snapshot file of Silicon's envelope equals `Catalogue/Builtin/Silicon.material-json` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` byte for byte; `a snapshot that does not read, or is not named for its own id and version, is refused naming the file`: a `library/<Silicon's snapshot name>` the test writes as `{`, and Silicon's file the test copies under the snapshot name of another GUID, each make `listSnapshots` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file; and `files under library that are not entry files are not snapshots`: `library/notes.txt` and `library/x.material-json.tmp` beside one snapshot leave `listSnapshots` answering that snapshot alone.", "acceptance": "After the snapshot files land, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST write a library version once as `library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json`, refuse a second write of that name, and list every snapshot through its schema, version and hash checks, and the folder snapshot MUST be byte for byte the catalogue entry file; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a snapshot is named by its entry id and version and its kind's extension, under library`, `a snapshot is written once under its id and version and listed back`, `a second snapshot of one version is refused and changes nothing`, `a read-only kit refuses a snapshot and writes nothing` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, `a snapshot file is byte for byte its catalogue entry file`, `a snapshot that does not read, or is not named for its own id and version, is refused naming the file`, `files under library that are not entry files are not snapshots` and the widened `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 10; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a snapshot is named by its entry id and version and its kind's extension, under library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every kit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a snapshot is written once under its id and version and listed back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a snapshot is written once under its id and version and listed back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a second snapshot of one version is refused and changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a second snapshot of one version is refused and changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a read-only kit refuses a snapshot and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a read-only kit refuses a snapshot and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a snapshot file is byte for byte its catalogue entry file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a snapshot that does not read, or is not named for its own id and version, is refused naming the file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.files under library that are not entry files are not snapshots", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.InMemoryKitFolder", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.LibraryEntryEnvelope.snapshotFileName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT-FILES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 139, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [137, 138], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests"], "how_to": "A kit snapshots every library version it references, closure and built-ins included, and the library pins each (001 §E 'Library closure snapshot: every library version the kit references is copied into library/ when first referenced, built-ins included, because the receiver may run another catalogue version'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned — a one-way flag — when a kit first references it'; the S4.2 brief: its entry file is written byte-identical to `library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json`, and the version is PINNED in the database (S2.2)). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`: `module KitLibrary` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `CatalogueImport.fs` (step 37), because it reads the import seam: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. It opens `Kit`, `KitFolders`, `LibraryEntryFiles` and `CatalogueImport`. Each type and member has a doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2. (1) `KitLibraryError`, an `*Error` union: `KitLibraryKitErr of KitError`, `KitLibraryImportErr of CatalogueImportError`, and `UnheldEntryErr of reason : string`, a reference that neither the library nor the kit's snapshots hold, naming its `describe`. `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form, a wrapped error by its own `describe`. (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitLibraryContext = { kit : KitContext; imports : CatalogueImportContext }`: one opened kit (step 131) and the library's import seam (step 94), the `*Context` convention. (3) `member this.snapshotReferences (references : EntryReference list) : Result<LibraryVersionRef list, KitLibraryError>` works in this order. Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` it answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr \"snapshotReferences\")`, reading, pinning and writing nothing. It lists the kit's snapshots (`kit.proxy.listSnapshots`, step 138). It resolves each reference to one envelope. `EntryVersionReference r` is the kit's own snapshot of `r` when it holds one, and otherwise `imports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope r.entryId r.version` (step 105). `EntryLatestReference id` is `imports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope id` (step 116), and otherwise the kit's highest-version snapshot of `id`. Neither is `UnheldEntryErr`. It walks each resolved envelope and then its `content.references` (step 137), depth first and in order, so a sample brings its material versions and each material its category, and every version is visited once. Each visited version the kit holds no snapshot of is pinned through `imports.proxy.pinEntryVersion` and then written through `kit.proxy.writeSnapshot` (step 138). It pins first, as `exportEntry` (step 116) pins before it writes, so a written snapshot always names a pinned version. A version the kit already holds is neither rewritten nor pinned, even when the library's copy of that version differs: the kit keeps its snapshot (001 §E). The answer is every version written, in visit order. The first failure stops it, and what it wrote stays, so calling it again completes the work. Its callers are the writers of kit content that binds library versions: the kit's experiment and setup files pass what they bind (an experiment's `libraryReferences`, step 137) once a constructor session holds a kit (S4.3), as S7.1's items and S11.5's promotion do in their sections. No cache, retry or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs`, `module KitLibraryTests`, appended at the end of the compile list of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj` with no comment. Its library is `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 94), and its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create` over that seam with `pinEntryVersion` wrapped by a test-local recorder of every pin, in order. Its kit is `KitProxy.createInMemory` over a fresh `InMemoryKitFolder`, initialised with a test-local kit file and opened through `KitContext.openKit` with a stepping clock. `referencing a sample snapshots it with its materials and their categories, each once, and pins each`: `snapshotReferences` of the `EntryVersionReference` of `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` at version 1 answers, in order, the sample's version, then each of its materials followed by that material's category, each version once. `listSnapshots` answers exactly their catalogue envelopes, and the recorder holds the same versions in the same order. `referencing a version the kit already holds writes and pins nothing`: the same call again answers `Ok []`, records no pin and leaves `paths` unchanged. `a preset referenced by its id snapshots the library's latest version`: the `EntryLatestReference` of the GUID of `PresetIds.source600` answers that source's version 1 and writes its envelope. `a version the kit holds is kept even when the library's differs, and one the library lacks resolves from the kit`: with the kit already holding a sealed copy of Silicon at version 1 whose description differs, a reference to Silicon at version 1 answers `[]`, records no pin and leaves that copy as the kit's snapshot. With the kit holding the snapshot of a test-local user material that the library does not hold, a reference to it at its version answers `[]`. `a reference neither the library nor the kit holds is UnheldEntryErr and writes nothing`: a reference to a test-local GUID answers `UnheldEntryErr` naming it, and the recorder and `paths` are unchanged. `a read-only kit refuses to snapshot and pins nothing`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, the call answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged. `a snapshot pins its version rows in the library database` runs over SQLite: with the import seam `CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase` (step 95) of `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67), disposed by the fact, after the multilayer sample's reference every answered version reads `VersionPinned` through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`, and every other catalogue version stays `VersionUnpinned`. `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload`: each case, over a distinct test-local reason or a wrapped `KitIoErr` or `ImportRejectedErr`, renders a distinct text that holds its reason or the wrapped error's `describe`.", "acceptance": "After snapshotting lands, `KitLibraryContext.snapshotReferences` MUST write every referenced version and its closure once into `library/`, pin each in the library before writing it, keep a version the kit already holds, and refuse under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `referencing a sample snapshots it with its materials and their categories, each once, and pins each`, `referencing a version the kit already holds writes and pins nothing`, `a preset referenced by its id snapshots the library's latest version`, `a version the kit holds is kept even when the library's differs, and one the library lacks resolves from the kit`, `a reference neither the library nor the kit holds is UnheldEntryErr and writes nothing`, `a read-only kit refuses to snapshot and pins nothing`, `a snapshot pins its version rows in the library database`, `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.referencing a sample snapshots it with its materials and their categories, each once, and pins each", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.referencing a version the kit already holds writes and pins nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a preset referenced by its id snapshots the library's latest version", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a version the kit holds is kept even when the library's differs, and one the library lacks resolves from the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a reference neither the library nor the kit holds is UnheldEntryErr and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a read-only kit refuses to snapshot and pins nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a snapshot pins its version rows in the library database", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.every kit library error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.KitLibraryError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.KitLibraryContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S42-SNAPSHOT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 140, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [139], "how_to": "A kit's snapshot is an import origin of its own, and the decision table keeps the kit's copy unless the user adds it (001 §E 'Resolution on open (the §B decision table, applied to the snapshot): same id, version and hash → the database entry; missing locally → the snapshot read-only, with \"Add to my library\"; divergence → reported; the kit keeps its snapshot; name-only collision → side by side, with the explicit re-binding', 'nothing changes in the database unconfirmed'; .spec-md §3.7: a kit's snapshot always opens the dialog). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`: (1) `ImportOrigin` (steps 93, 102) gains `KitSnapshotOrigin of kit : KitName` (step 122), documented as the library snapshot of the named kit. `describe` answers the kit's name, so a collision row reads `Silicon — from <kit>` (`rowName`, step 102). (2) `ImportDecision.decide` keeps every rule for the other origins and the order in which it tells the rows apart. Under `KitSnapshotOrigin` it sets the actions so that applying a row's default writes nothing. `SameContentHash` stays `ReuseHeldEntry`. `EntryIdNotHeld` defaults to `SkipIncomingEntry` (the kit's copy, read-only), with `[ AddIncomingEntry ]` (Add to my library). `VersionNotHeld` defaults to `SkipIncomingEntry`, with `[ AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion ]`; the latest never moves, because the move condition names `CatalogueImportOrigin` (step 102). `DivergentContent` defaults to `SkipIncomingEntry`, with `[ ForkIncomingEntry ]`. `NameCollision` defaults to `SkipIncomingEntry`, with `AddIncomingEntry` and then one `RebindToHeldEntry` per same-name entry, in its order. A category offers no re-binding, because a kit binds samples, materials and presets, and a material names its category by id. `mode` and `split` are unchanged. The doc of `decide` says so in one to three lines. (3) Any other complete match on `ImportOrigin` that FS0025 reports answers the kit as `describe` does. Tests: `ImportDecisionTests` (step 93) gains two facts, under `KitSnapshotOrigin (KitName \"Optics kit\")` and the class's envelopes. `a kit snapshot keeps the kit's copy by default and offers to add it to the library`: a new id is `EntryIdNotHeld`, defaulting to `SkipIncomingEntry` with `[ AddIncomingEntry ]`. The held version is `SameContentHash`, reusing it. Silicon's built-in version 2 is `VersionNotHeld`, defaulting to `SkipIncomingEntry` with `[ AddIncomingVersion KeepLatestVersion ]`. Silicon's version 1 with another description is `DivergentContent`, defaulting to `SkipIncomingEntry` with `[ ForkIncomingEntry ]`. The origin's `describe` is `Optics kit`. `a kit snapshot named like a held entry sits side by side, re-binding an entry but never a category`: a new material named `Silicon` against two held `Silicon` entries is `NameCollision`, defaulting to `SkipIncomingEntry`, with `AddIncomingEntry` and then one `RebindToHeldEntry` per held entry in order; its `rowName` is `Silicon — from Optics kit`. A new category named like a held category offers `[ AddIncomingEntry ]` alone. The class's other facts keep their assertions.", "acceptance": "After the kit origin lands, `ImportDecision.decide` under `KitSnapshotOrigin` MUST default every row to keeping the kit's copy or reusing the held entry, and MUST offer adding, forking or re-binding as 001 §E says; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit snapshot keeps the kit's copy by default and offers to add it to the library` and `a kit snapshot named like a held entry sits side by side, re-binding an entry but never a category`, the count rising by 2, with every other `ImportDecisionTests` fact passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a kit snapshot keeps the kit's copy by default and offers to add it to the library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-KIT-ORIGIN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests.a kit snapshot named like a held entry sits side by side, re-binding an entry but never a category", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportDecisionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportDecisionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-KIT-ORIGIN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.ImportDecision", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S42-KIT-ORIGIN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 141, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [140], "how_to": "Resolution on open: the kit's snapshots decided against the library, row by row, writing nothing (001 §E 'Resolution on open'; the S4.2 brief: pure Domain, REUSING S3.1's decision function over the snapshots against the database; the rows go to S3.2's dialog, and nothing in the database changes unconfirmed). In `KitLibrary.fs` (step 139): `member this.resolveSnapshots () : Result<ImportDecision list, KitLibraryError>` on `KitLibraryContext` lists the kit's snapshots (`kit.proxy.listSnapshots`, step 138) and answers, in that order, `imports.proxy.decideEntry (KitSnapshotOrigin kit.kitFile.name) envelope` (steps 102, 140) for each. So one body decides catalogue rows, dropped files and a kit's snapshots. It only reads, so a read-only context answers it, and a kit without snapshots answers `Ok []`. Its doc says that a kit's opener calls it after `KitContext.openKit` (step 131) and MUST show every snapshot row in the import dialog, including an all-Reuse list. Only a kit with no snapshot rows MAY open without this dialog. No other member, cache or option is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), whose kits hold snapshots written through `writeSnapshot` and whose library holds the Built-in catalogue. `a snapshot the library holds byte for byte is reused`: Silicon's catalogue envelope resolves as `SameContentHash`, defaulting to `ReuseHeldEntry`. `a snapshot the library lacks stays in the kit read-only, with Add to my library offered`: a test-local user material that the library does not hold resolves as `EntryIdNotHeld`, defaulting to `SkipIncomingEntry` with `[ AddIncomingEntry ]`. `a divergent snapshot is reported and the kit keeps it`: in another kit, Silicon at version 1 with another description resolves as `DivergentContent`, defaulting to `SkipIncomingEntry`, and `listSnapshots` still answers the kit's copy. `a snapshot named like a held entry offers side by side and an explicit re-binding`: a user material named `Silicon` under a new id resolves as `NameCollision`, whose `rowName` names the kit file's name and whose alternatives end with the `RebindToHeldEntry` of Silicon's id. `resolving the snapshots writes nothing, through a read-only kit too`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, a kit holding the snapshots of the first, second and fourth facts resolves to the same rows in listing order, and `paths` and every held entry are unchanged.", "acceptance": "After resolution lands, `KitLibraryContext.resolveSnapshots` MUST answer one `KitSnapshotOrigin` row per snapshot through `CatalogueImportProxy.decideEntry` and MUST write nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a snapshot the library holds byte for byte is reused`, `a snapshot the library lacks stays in the kit read-only, with Add to my library offered`, `a divergent snapshot is reported and the kit keeps it`, `a snapshot named like a held entry offers side by side and an explicit re-binding`, `resolving the snapshots writes nothing, through a read-only kit too`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a snapshot the library holds byte for byte is reused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-RESOLUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a snapshot the library lacks stays in the kit read-only, with Add to my library offered", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-RESOLUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a divergent snapshot is reported and the kit keeps it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-RESOLUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a snapshot named like a held entry offers side by side and an explicit re-binding", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-RESOLUTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.resolving the snapshots writes nothing, through a read-only kit too", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-RESOLUTION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.KitLibraryContext.resolveSnapshots", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S42-RESOLUTION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 142, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [141], "how_to": "The session's library: the library's stores overlaid with the kit's read-only snapshots, so the kit opens on any machine (001 §E 'So the kit opens on any machine', 'missing locally → the snapshot read-only', 'divergence → … the kit keeps its snapshot'; the S4.2 brief: the session's library is the database view overlaid with the kit's read-only snapshot entries, a LibraryProxy composition). In `KitLibrary.fs`, each type and member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2: (1) `EntryReplacement = { incoming : LibraryEntryId; held : LibraryEntryEnvelope }` is a kit entry the user re-bound to a held entry ('use my Si instead', 001 §B). `KitLibraryOverlay = { snapshots : LibraryEntryEnvelope list; replacements : EntryReplacement list }`. `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitLibraryStores = { library : LibraryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; samples : SampleProxy; categories : CategoryProxy }` is the library stores a constructor session reads. (2) `member this.openOverlay (rebindings : EntryRebinding list) : Result<KitLibraryOverlay, KitLibraryError>` on `KitLibraryContext` lists the kit's snapshots and reads each re-binding's held entry through `imports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope rebinding.held`; one that is not held is `UnheldEntryErr`. The re-bindings are the `ImportOutcome.rebindings` of a confirmed resolution (step 143). It writes nothing. (3) The overlay rule, one member per store, as type extensions after the record: `type LibraryProxy with member this.overlaidWith (overlay : KitLibraryOverlay) : LibraryProxy`, and the same member on `MaterialProxy`, `SampleProxy` and `CategoryProxy`. Every write field passes through to the store unchanged. A read of one version of an entry (`resolveVersion`) answers the held entry for a replaced entry; otherwise the kit's snapshot of that version when the kit holds one, so a divergent version is the kit's (001 §E); otherwise the store's. A read by id (`tryGetMaterial`, `tryGetSample`, `tryGetEntry`) answers the held entry for a replaced entry; otherwise the store's; otherwise the kit's highest-version snapshot of the id. Listings: `LibraryProxy.entriesForKind` answers the store's entries followed by the kit's snapshot-only entries offered for the kind (`LibraryEntry.forKinds`), one per id at its highest version, with a replaced or store-held id left out. `libraryTrees` is `[ LibraryTree.byKind <those entries> ]` (step 47), over the five kinds step 47 names, distinct by id. `CategoryProxy.listCategories` answers the store's categories followed by the kit's snapshot-only ones. `listMaterials`, `searchMaterials`, `listSamples` and `searchSamples` pass through, because the Materials and Library windows show the library (001 §F). A snapshot reaches a domain value only through step 25's decoders, so no entry id becomes a kind's id anywhere else. A decoder's refusal is the store's own unavailable case (`LibraryUnavailableErr`, `MaterialStoreUnavailableErr`, `SampleStoreUnavailableErr`, `CategoryStoreUnavailableErr`, steps 69-79), naming the snapshot and the refusal's `describe`. (4) `member this.overlaidWith (overlay : KitLibraryOverlay) : KitLibraryStores` on `KitLibraryStores` overlays each of its four stores. No cache, write-back or other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests`. `a kit opened against an empty library resolves every entry from its snapshots`: a kit is snapshotted (step 139) from the Built-in library with the references of the multilayer sample and of the 600 nm source preset. It is then opened read-only by a second proxy over the same folder, in a second context over EMPTY in-memory stores and seam (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, step 95), whose `KitLibraryStores` hold a live library composed over those stores as `LibraryProxyTests` composes one (step 78). `resolveSnapshots` answers `EntryIdNotHeld` for every snapshot. Over `openOverlay []`, every snapshot resolves, each equal to its catalogue value: the sample through `samples.resolveVersion` and `library.tryGetEntry`, each material version through `materials.resolveVersion`, each category through `categories.listCategories`, and the preset through `library.tryGetEntry` and `entriesForKind LightSource`. `the session resolves a divergent version to the kit's snapshot`: over the Built-in library, for a kit holding Silicon at version 1 with another description, `materials.resolveVersion` of Silicon at version 1 answers the kit's description, and `tryGetMaterial` of Silicon answers the library's latest. `a re-bound entry resolves to the held entry`: over the Built-in library, a test-local sample the kit alone holds, re-bound to `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` through `openOverlay`, resolves to the multilayer through `samples.tryGetSample` and `library.tryGetEntry`, and `entriesForKind Sample` offers no entry of the kit sample's id. `the overlay passes every write to the library and never lists a kit entry in it`: `samples.saveSample` of a new sample through the overlaid stores holds it in the underlying store, and no listing of the underlying stores answers a kit entry.", "acceptance": "After the overlay lands, `KitLibraryStores.overlaidWith` MUST answer every kit snapshot the library lacks read-only, the kit's copy of a divergent version and the held entry for a re-bound one, passing every write to the library; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit opened against an empty library resolves every entry from its snapshots`, `the session resolves a divergent version to the kit's snapshot`, `a re-bound entry resolves to the held entry`, `the overlay passes every write to the library and never lists a kit entry in it`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a kit opened against an empty library resolves every entry from its snapshots", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-OVERLAY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.the session resolves a divergent version to the kit's snapshot", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-OVERLAY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a re-bound entry resolves to the held entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-OVERLAY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.the overlay passes every write to the library and never lists a kit entry in it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-OVERLAY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.KitLibraryOverlay", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S42-OVERLAY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.KitLibraryStores", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S42-OVERLAY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.EntryReplacement", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S42-OVERLAY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 143, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [142], "how_to": "Confirming a kit's resolution: the chosen rows are applied, and what they add is pinned, because the kit references it (001 §E 'One dialog shows all rows; nothing changes in the database unconfirmed'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned … when a kit first references it'; the S4.2 brief). In `KitLibrary.fs`: `member this.confirm (choices : ImportChoice list) : Result<ImportOutcome, CatalogueImportError>` on `KitLibraryContext` runs `imports.apply choices` (step 94). Its checks refuse an action a row does not offer (`InvalidImportChoiceErr`), and a written entry that names one kept in the kit or re-bound (`DanglingReferenceErr`), before anything is written. Then, for every choice whose action is `AddIncomingEntry` or `AddIncomingVersion _`, it pins the incoming envelope's version through `imports.proxy.pinEntryVersion`, in choice order. A fork has a new id that the kit does not reference, so it is not pinned. The answer is `apply`'s outcome, whose `rebindings` the opener passes to `openOverlay` (step 142). It answers `CatalogueImportError`, the import dialog's error channel (step 107). Its doc is one to three lines. Nothing else is written, and the kit's files are untouched. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests`, each over a kit snapshotted from the Built-in library (step 139) with the references of the multilayer sample and of the 600 nm source preset, and then opened read-only by a second proxy over the same folder, in a second context over an empty in-memory library whose `pinEntryVersion` is recorded. The kit's files are never written by a confirmation. `adding a kit's entry to the library holds it and pins the version the kit references`: choosing `AddIncomingEntry` for the 600 nm source row holds the source in the library (`tryHeldEntry`) and records its version's pin. `adding a sample while its material stays in the kit is refused and writes nothing`: choosing `AddIncomingEntry` for the multilayer sample while its materials keep `SkipIncomingEntry` answers `DanglingReferenceErr`, and nothing is held or pinned. `confirming the kit's defaults writes nothing, and a re-binding is answered for the session`: confirming every row's `byDefault` (step 93) holds and pins nothing. Over the Built-in library and a kit holding a user material named `Silicon` under a new id, the `RebindToHeldEntry` choice of Silicon's id answers that re-binding in the outcome and writes nothing. `once added, a kit's entries resolve as reused`: after confirming `AddIncomingEntry` for every row, a second `resolveSnapshots` answers `SameContentHash` for each.", "acceptance": "After confirmation lands, `KitLibraryContext.confirm` MUST apply only the chosen rows, pin every version a choice adds, answer the re-bindings and write nothing for the kit's defaults; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `adding a kit's entry to the library holds it and pins the version the kit references`, `adding a sample while its material stays in the kit is refused and writes nothing`, `confirming the kit's defaults writes nothing, and a re-binding is answered for the session`, `once added, a kit's entries resolve as reused`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.adding a kit's entry to the library holds it and pins the version the kit references", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-CONFIRM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.adding a sample while its material stays in the kit is refused and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-CONFIRM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.confirming the kit's defaults writes nothing, and a re-binding is answered for the session", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-CONFIRM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.once added, a kit's entries resolve as reused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S42-CONFIRM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.KitLibraryContext.confirm", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S42-CONFIRM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 144, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.2m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [143], "how_to": "The kit's resolution rows go to the one import dialog (001 §E 'One dialog shows all rows; nothing changes in the database unconfirmed'; .spec-md §10.1 'The import dialog opens … on a kit whose snapshot needs decisions', §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 the Apply / Cancel pair; step 107: 'S4.2 adds a kit snapshot's case'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs` (step 107): `ImportDialogRequest` gains `ResolveKitSnapshot of kit : KitLibraryContext * decisions : ImportDecision list`, documented as a kit's snapshot rows (step 141). `decisions` answers its rows. `heading` is `Open kit <kit name>: <k> library entries need a decision.`, `k` counting every snapshot row, including `SameContentHash`. `ImportDialogApplied.summary` is `Opened the library of kit <kit name> (decisions applied: <n>).`. For this case, `ApplyImportChoices` calls `kit.confirm m.choices` (step 143), and its `Ok` and `Error` are handled as the other cases' are, so `onApplied` receives the outcome, whose re-bindings the opener overlays (step 142). Every other message, the rows, the diff preview and the Apply / Cancel row are unchanged, and Cancel applies nothing. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, `ImportDecision.actionCaption` (step 107): under `KitSnapshotOrigin` (step 140), `SkipIncomingEntry` reads `Keep the kit's copy (read-only)`; `AddIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library`, or `Add to my library, side by side` on a `NameCollision`; `AddIncomingVersion _` reads `Add this version to my library`; and `ForkIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library as a fork`. Every other action, and every action under another origin, keeps its caption. The dialog opens for a kit wherever the app opens one, and this step adds no window, id or message. (3) Tests, in `ImportDialogTests` (step 107). Each runs over a kit snapshotted (step 139) from `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` with the multilayer sample's references, then opened read-only by a second proxy over the same folder and resolved (step 141) by a second `KitLibraryContext` over an empty in-memory library whose `pinEntryVersion` is recorded. The request is `ResolveKitSnapshot` of that context and its rows, with the class's recording `onApplied` and `requestClose`. `a kit snapshot request names the kit and opens every row on the kit's default`: `initImportDialog` holds every row on `SkipIncomingEntry`, and `heading` names the kit and counts every row. `applying a kit snapshot request confirms through the kit library and closes`: `OverrideImportRow` of each row to `AddIncomingEntry`, then `ApplyImportChoices`, holds every entry in the library, records each version's pin, and calls `onApplied` once, with a summary naming the kit, and `requestClose` once. With only the sample overridden, Apply leaves `lastError` `DanglingReferenceErr`, the dialog open and nothing held. `a kit snapshot row offers to keep the kit's copy or to add it to my library`: the sample row's `actionCaption` of its default is `Keep the kit's copy (read-only)` and of `AddIncomingEntry` is `Add to my library`; a collision row's `AddIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library, side by side`; and under the class's catalogue origin `SkipIncomingEntry` keeps its caption `Skip`.", "acceptance": "After the kit case lands, the import dialog MUST show a kit's snapshot rows on the kit's defaults and confirm them through `KitLibraryContext.confirm` only on Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a kit snapshot request names the kit and opens every row on the kit's default`, `applying a kit snapshot request confirms through the kit library and closes`, `a kit snapshot row offers to keep the kit's copy or to add it to my library`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.a kit snapshot request names the kit and opens every row on the kit's default", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S42-DIALOG"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.applying a kit snapshot request confirms through the kit library and closes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S42-DIALOG"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests.a kit snapshot row offers to keep the kit's copy or to add it to my library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportDialogTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S42-DIALOG"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.ImportDialogRequest", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S42-DIALOG"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportDialogView.updateImportDialog", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S42-DIALOG"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.2 -- Attachments by relative path and hash; the library snapshot and its resolution"}
{"number": 145, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [144], "how_to": "Opening a folder the user picked, in Domain: initialise it when it holds no kit, open it otherwise (001 §F 'New kit…: … An empty folder is initialised; a folder that already has files keeps them, and .kit-json plus the app's subfolders are added'; 001 §E 'an open read-only choice'; the S4.3 brief: Main and Inverse open a kit through a `KitFolderPicker` seam, a Domain record, followed by S4.1's initialise-or-open; .spec-md §3.10). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, beside `KitFolder.tryKitPathOf` (step 132): `type KitFolder with member this.namedKitFile (id : KitId) (author : KitAuthor) (now : ClockTime) : Result<KitFile, KitError>` is `KitFile.create id <name> author now` (step 122), the name being `KitName.tryCreate` of the folder's leaf: its text with every `\\` turned into `/` and trailing `/` removed, after the last `/`. A blank leaf (a drive root such as `C:/`) answers `InvalidKitNameErr`. It touches no disk. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`, after `KitContext` (step 131): (a) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitFolderPicker = { pickKitFolder : unit -> Async<KitFolder option> }`, how the app asks the user for a kit folder; `None` when the user cancels. The brief writes the field `unit -> KitFolder option`; it answers `Async` because Avalonia's folder dialog (`IStorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync`) completes asynchronously on the UI thread, and blocking the dispatcher on it deadlocks. The App passes the Avalonia dialog (steps 150, 154); headless tests pass a folder under the test output (step 154); S5.2's start screen calls the same seam. (b) `type KitContext with static member openOrInitialise (proxy : KitProxy) (clock : ClockProvider) (newKitFile : ClockTime -> Result<KitFile, KitError>) : Result<KitContext, KitError>` is `KitContext.openKit proxy ReadWriteKitAccess clock` (step 131); on `NotAKitFolderErr` only it calls `newKitFile (clock.now ())`, then `proxy.initialiseKit` of that kit file (step 125), then `openKit` read-write again. Every other error passes through and nothing is written, `KitLockedErr` included: the caller may then open the kit with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` (001 §E). A folder that is a kit keeps its kit file, and `newKitFile` is not called. (c) `static member createInMemory (kitFile : KitFile) (clock : ClockProvider) : KitContext`: a new `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 125) holding exactly what `initialiseKit kitFile` leaves (the kit file, `data` and `library`), and a context over the folder's first proxy holding that kit file, `ReadWriteKitAccess` and the clock. It takes no lock and records no stamp, because no other proxy can reach the folder, so it cannot fail and answers the context. It is the kit of a scene that opened no folder (step 150). No other member, option or verb is added, and `KitProxy` gains no field. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `a new kit is named for its folder`: `namedKitFile` over `KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/kits/Optics QZ\")`, over `C:\\kits\\Optics QZ\\` and over `C:/kits/Optics QZ/` answers a kit file named `Optics QZ` with the given id, author and instant (`created` equal to `modified`); over `C:/` it answers `InvalidKitNameErr`. New `KitProxyContract` facts (step 125), so `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` both run them, each passing `newKitFile clock` (step 125) wrapped in `Ok` as the new kit file: `opening a folder that holds no kit initialises it and opens it read-write`: over a fresh folder, `openOrInitialise` of proxy A answers a context holding that kit file and `ReadWriteKitAccess`, and `paths` is exactly `.kit-json`, `.oc`, `.oc/lock`, `data` and `library`. `opening a folder that is a kit keeps its kit file`: over a folder initialised with the kit file whose notes are `KitNotes \"first\"`, `openOrInitialise` of A whose new kit file has another id answers the first kit file, and B's `readKitFile` answers it unchanged. `a kit open elsewhere is not opened or initialised again`: with A opened through `openOrInitialise`, B's `openOrInitialise` answers `KitLockedErr` of A's holder, a test-local counter of its new-kit calls stays 0, and `paths` is unchanged; `KitContext.openKit` of B with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` then answers a context. `KitProxyTests` (in memory only) gains `an in-memory kit context holds its kit file and writes through its own folder`: `KitContext.createInMemory` of `newKitFile clock` answers a context holding that kit file and `ReadWriteKitAccess`; its `proxy.readKitFile` answers that kit file, and `proxy.writeKindFile ExperimentKitFile (FileStem \"E1\")` of a text, then `readKindFile`, answers that text.", "acceptance": "After the open seam lands, `KitContext.openOrInitialise` MUST initialise a folder that holds no kit and open a kit read-write keeping its kit file, passing `KitLockedErr` through with nothing written, and `KitFolder.namedKitFile` MUST name a new kit for its folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a new kit is named for its folder`, `opening a folder that holds no kit initialises it and opens it read-write`, `opening a folder that is a kit keeps its kit file`, `a kit open elsewhere is not opened or initialised again` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, and `an in-memory kit context holds its kit file and writes through its own folder`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a new kit is named for its folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.opening a folder that holds no kit initialises it and opens it read-write", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.opening a folder that holds no kit initialises it and opens it read-write", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.opening a folder that is a kit keeps its kit file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.opening a folder that is a kit keeps its kit file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a kit open elsewhere is not opened or initialised again", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a kit open elsewhere is not opened or initialised again", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.an in-memory kit context holds its kit file and writes through its own folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitFolder.namedKitFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitFolderPicker", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitContext.openOrInitialise", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitContext.createInMemory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPEN-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 146, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [145], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests"], "how_to": "An experiment persists as its own kit file, `<name>.experiment-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .experiment-json', 'A file that exists many times is named by its own identity'; the S4.3 brief: each kit file kind has a JSON schema and a schema version and is written atomically through KitProxy, and until S8.3 / S9.1 give experiments template names the name is its ExperimentId, e.g. `E3`; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 124's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`); no second parser or writer is written. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (a) `ExperimentId` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentId`) gains `member this.fileStem : FileStem`, `FileStem.ofText` (step 24) of `E<n>`, so `ExperimentId 3` is stored as `E3.experiment-json`. (b) After `Experiment` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`): `ExperimentFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; experiment : Experiment }`, the `.experiment-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1. `type Experiment with member this.experimentFile : ExperimentFile` is the experiment at the current schema version. A file is read back as its `experiment` field; no member converts the other way (ELEV006). (2) Schema. New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/kit.schema.json` (step 124), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/experiment.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1 (`then`): the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `experiment` (`additionalProperties: false`); `experiment` holds exactly `id` (a positive integer), `setup` (an array), `varied`, `measurement`, `range` (an object), `dataFileOpt` and `sourceWaveLengthOpt`; `dataFileOpt` is `null` or an object holding exactly `path` (a non-empty string) and `contentHash` (the content-hash definition of `library-common.schema.json`, step 30, referenced by its `$id`). The descriptors, bindings, range and wavelength are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one, as step 30's payloads are. A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/kit.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateExperimentFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith` (step 29), its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateKitFile` (step 124) does. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`, `module KitContentFiles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `KitFolderStore.fs` (step 124): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the kit's content files, their texts and their typed reads and writes (spec 0050 S4.3). (a) `type ExperimentFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` (step 27) rendered by `canonicalFileText` (step 124): indented canonical JSON, LF line ends, one final `\\n`. (b) `type KitFileText with member this.parseExperimentFile : Result<ExperimentFile, StorageError>` is `parseVersionedText validateExperimentFile ExperimentKitFile.extension ExperimentFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value` (steps 123, 124). There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs`, `module KitContentFileJsonTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its fixtures are two test-local experiments written as records, as `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs` writes its E1 / E2 / E3: E1 varies a polarizer's R1 over a setup binding the 1 mm glass plate sample by its version 1 (`BoundByVersion`), the 600 nm source preset by its entry id (`BoundByEntryId` of `PresetIds.source600`, step 20) and one `Unbound` element, carries a `DataAttachment` at `data/run 1.csv` with a test-local 64-character lowercase hex hash, and sets its source to 632.8 nm (`WaveLength.nm`); E3 is a dark line with no varied element, no attachment and no wavelength. `an experiment is stored under its id`: `(ExperimentId 3).fileStem` is `FileStem \"E3\"`, and `ExperimentKitFile.fileNameOf` of it is `FileName \"E3.experiment-json\"`. `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`: `experimentFile`, `fileText`, then `parseExperimentFile` answers an equal file for E1 and for E3; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys as `experiment` then `schemaVersion`, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text. `an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: E1's text with `schemaVersion` set to 2, with its body intact and as `{ \"schemaVersion\": 2 }` alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = ExperimentKitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds`: E1's text without `experiment`, with an extra top-level key `notes`, with `experiment.id` set to 0, and with `dataFileOpt.contentHash` set to `abc`, each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; the text `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After the experiment file lands, `ExperimentFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseExperimentFile` reads back equal, validated against `schema/experiment.schema.json`, another schema version being `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, and `ExperimentId.fileStem` MUST name an experiment `E<n>`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment is stored under its id`, `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment is stored under its id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentId.fileStem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateExperimentFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitFileText.parseExperimentFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.ExperimentFile.fileText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-EXPERIMENT-FILE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 147, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [146], "how_to": "A saved scene persists as its own kit file, `<scene name>.setup-json`, in today's `Scene.SceneSnapshot` shape (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .setup-json'; the S4.3 brief: a scene is <scene name>.setup-json, in today's Scene.SceneSnapshot shape, which S8.2 replaces with slots). The stack is step 146's. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`, which opens `LibraryEntryFiles` (step 24); each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (a) `SceneName` (`Scene.fs:SceneName`) gains `member this.fileStem : FileStem`, `FileStem.ofText this.value`: the name keeps the lab's characters and only the characters Windows forbids become `_` (.spec-md §3.11, step 24's one rule). (b) `SceneSnapshot` (`Scene.fs:SceneSnapshot`) gains `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list` (step 137): the `placement.valueId` of each element that names a library entry (`ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24) as an `EntryLatestReference`, in element order, each once; an unbound element and a value id that names no entry give none. It is what a kit snapshots when it records the scene (step 149). (c) After `SceneSnapshot`: `SceneFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; name : SceneName; scene : SceneSnapshot }`, the `.setup-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1. The name is kept inside the file because the file stem is the name made filesystem-safe and can differ from it. (2) Schema. New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/setup.schema.json`, draft 2020-12, `$id` `https://berreman/schema/setup.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1: the root holds exactly `schemaVersion`, `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\\S`) and `scene`; `scene` holds exactly `elements` (an array), `view`, `snap` and `pivot`; their shapes are bound by the serializer. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/experiment.schema.json`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateSceneFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy`. (3) `KitContentFiles.fs` (step 146): `type SceneFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf` rendered by `canonicalFileText`) and `type KitFileText with member this.parseSceneFile : Result<SceneFile, StorageError>` = `parseVersionedText validateSceneFile SetupKitFile.extension SceneFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value`. Tests, in `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 146). Its fixture scene is written as a record, as `SceneRoundTripTests.fs` writes its source model's elements: a light source bound to the 600 nm source preset (`PresetIds.source600`), a linear polarizer bound to the linear-polarizer preset, a detector that is unbound and sits on the polarizer's reflected beam, a view panned and zoomed off `Table.defaultView`, `SnapToBeam` and `PivotAtIncidentFace`. `a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe`: `SceneName \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL\"` has the file stem of the same text, `SceneName \"a: b/c\"` has `FileStem \"a_ b_c\"`, and `SetupKitFile.fileNameOf` of the first is `FileName \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL.setup-json\"`. `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`: a `SceneFile` of `SceneName \"Bench: A\"` and the fixture, by `fileText` and `parseSceneFile`, answers an equal file; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys as `name`, `scene`, `schemaVersion`, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text. `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` set to 2, with its body intact and alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = SetupKitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`: the text without `name`, with `name` set to `\"   \"`, with `scene` lacking `pivot`, and with an extra top-level key, each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`. `a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest`: the fixture's `libraryReferences` is exactly the `EntryLatestReference`s of the source preset's and the linear-polarizer preset's GUIDs, in that order; a scene binding the source preset twice references it once; and a scene of unbound elements references nothing.", "acceptance": "After the setup file lands, `SceneFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseSceneFile` reads back equal, validated against `schema/setup.schema.json`, another schema version being `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `SceneName.fileStem` MUST keep the lab's characters, and `SceneSnapshot.libraryReferences` MUST name each bound entry once; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe`, `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`, `a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/setup.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a setup file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Scene.SceneFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Scene.SceneName.fileStem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Scene.SceneSnapshot.libraryReferences", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateSceneFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitFileText.parseSceneFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-FILE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 148, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [147], "how_to": "A kit's experiments and scenes are read and written by typed members over the per-kind verbs (001 §P '`KitProxy` … setups, experiments'; step 127: a kind adds no proxy verb; the S4.3 brief: committing, editing and removing an experiment and saving and loading a scene write and read kit files, and SceneRoundTripTests and ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests are re-pointed at kit files). In `KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146-147), on one `type KitProxy with` extension, each member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3: (1) `member this.writeExperiment (experiment : Experiment) : Result<unit, KitError>` renders `experiment.experimentFile.fileText` and writes it with `writeKindFile ExperimentKitFile experiment.id.fileStem` (step 127), replacing a file of that name whole. A `StorageError` of the rendering is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the error's `describe`. (2) `member this.deleteExperiment (id : ExperimentId) : Result<unit, KitError>` is `deleteKindFile ExperimentKitFile id.fileStem`. (3) `member this.readExperiments () : Result<Experiment list, KitError>` reads every stem `listKindFiles ExperimentKitFile` answers, with `readKindFile`, and parses it with `parseExperimentFile`. A refusal, or a file whose experiment's `id.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case, is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason, and the whole read answers it, so the constructor never opens a kit with an experiment left out. The answer is ordered by `id`. (4) `member this.writeScene (name : SceneName) (scene : SceneSnapshot) : Result<unit, KitError>` writes `{ schemaVersion = SceneFile.currentSchemaVersion; name = name; scene = scene }` by `fileText` with `writeKindFile SetupKitFile name.fileStem`, a rendering error mapped as in (1). Two names with one stem (they differ only in characters Windows forbids) share one file, and the later write replaces it. (5) `member this.readScene (name : SceneName) : Result<SceneSnapshot, KitError>` reads `readKindFile SetupKitFile name.fileStem` and answers the parsed file's `scene`; a missing file is `MissingKitFileErr` (step 127) and a refusal is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file. (6) `member this.readSceneNames () : Result<SceneName list, KitError>` parses every setup file and answers the names they hold, in ordinal order; a refused file refuses the read as in (3). Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) every write answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and every read passes, because the members call the proxy's verbs. No cache, retry or other member is added. Tests. `SceneRoundTripTests` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` drop their in-memory stores and run over a kit folder: each fact makes `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"<class>\", <a new GUID>)` (the `KitProxyFolderTests` precedent, step 126), builds `KitProxy.create` over it and calls `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file. Each module doc says so in one to three lines. `SceneRoundTripTests` keeps `sceneName` and its fixture elements. `createInMemory round-trips capture-save-load-restore reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings, and view state` becomes `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state`: `writeScene` of `Experiment A` and the captured scene, then `readSceneNames` answers `[ Experiment A ]`, `readScene` answers the captured scene, the folder holds `Experiment A.setup-json`, and `restoreScene` of it onto `initTableAndElementRotation ()` keeps every assertion. `saveScene overwrites a scene stored under the same name (upsert)` becomes `writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file`, with the same assertions over `readSceneNames` and `readScene`. `tryLoadScene returns None for a name that was never saved` becomes `reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr`. `saveScene rejects a directly-constructed blank name as InvalidScene` is deleted: the store that re-validated a name is gone, and `SceneName.tryCreate` keeps its facts (step 151). It gains `a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file`: `Broken.setup-json` written by the test as `{` makes `readSceneNames` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming it. `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` keeps `e1`, `e2` and `e3`; `collectionName`, `snapshotOf` and its `ExperimentCollectionStore` open go. `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments` becomes `a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes and data attachments`: `writeExperiment` of E3, E1 and E2, then `readExperiments` answers `[ e1; e2; e3 ]`, and the folder holds `E1.experiment-json`, `E2.experiment-json` and `E3.experiment-json`. `saveCollection overwrites a collection stored under the same name (upsert)` becomes `writing an experiment again replaces its kit file`: E1, then E1 with `CaptureReflected`, reads back as the second. `tryLoadCollection returns None for a name that was never saved` becomes `a kit with no experiment files reads no experiments`: a fresh kit answers `Ok []`. `listCollections enumerates every saved collection and each loads back value-identically` becomes `deleting an experiment removes its kit file and keeps the others`: after E1, E2 and E3, `deleteExperiment (ExperimentId 2)` leaves `readExperiments` answering `[ e1; e3 ]`, and a second delete answers `MissingKitFileErr`. `saveCollection rejects a directly-constructed blank name as InvalidCollection and stores nothing` is deleted, because experiments are named by their ids. It gains `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file`: `E5.experiment-json` written as `{`, and `E6.experiment-json` holding E1's file text, each make `readExperiments` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file; and `a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView`, `writeExperiment`, `deleteExperiment` and `writeScene` answer `KitReadOnlyErr`, the folder's files and bytes are unchanged, and `readExperiments` answers what the kit holds.", "acceptance": "After the typed members land, `KitProxy.writeExperiment`, `deleteExperiment`, `readExperiments`, `writeScene`, `readScene` and `readSceneNames` MUST write, read and delete the kit's experiment and setup files, a file that does not read refusing the whole read, and `SceneRoundTripTests` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` MUST run over kit folders; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state`, `writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file`, `reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr`, `a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file`, `a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes and data attachments`, `writing an experiment again replaces its kit file`, `a kit with no experiment files reads no experiments`, `deleting an experiment removes its kit file and keeps the others`, `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file`, `a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.createInMemory round-trips capture-save-load-restore reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings, and view state", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.saveScene overwrites a scene stored under the same name (upsert)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.tryLoadScene returns None for a name that was never saved", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.saveScene rejects a directly-constructed blank name as InvalidScene", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes and data attachments", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.saveCollection overwrites a collection stored under the same name (upsert)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.writing an experiment again replaces its kit file", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.tryLoadCollection returns None for a name that was never saved", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.a kit with no experiment files reads no experiments", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.listCollections enumerates every saved collection and each loads back value-identically", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.deleting an experiment removes its kit file and keeps the others", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.saveCollection rejects a directly-constructed blank name as InvalidCollection and stores nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.deleteExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readExperiments", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeScene", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readScene", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readSceneNames", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-KIT-CONTENT-VERBS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 149, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [148], "how_to": "A kit's experiment and scene files are recorded with the library versions they reference (001 §E 'Library closure snapshot: every library version the kit references is copied into library/ when first referenced'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned … when a kit first references it'; step 139: `snapshotReferences`' callers are the writers of kit content that binds library versions). In `KitContentFiles.fs`, on a `type KitLibraryContext with` extension (step 139), each member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3: (1) `member this.recordExperiment (experiment : Experiment) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>` calls `this.snapshotReferences experiment.libraryReferences` (steps 137, 139), then `this.kit.proxy.writeExperiment experiment` (step 148), a `KitError` wrapped as `KitLibraryKitErr`. The snapshots come first, so a written file never references a version the kit lacks; on a failure the file is not written and what the snapshot wrote stays (step 139). (2) `member this.recordScene (name : SceneName) (scene : SceneSnapshot) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>` does the same with `scene.libraryReferences` (step 147) and `writeScene` (step 148). Removing an experiment snapshots nothing and keeps the kit's snapshots, which other files may reference: it calls `deleteExperiment` directly (step 152). No other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), over its Built-in library, its recorder of pins and its in-memory kit opened read-write. `recording an experiment snapshots the library versions it binds, then writes its file`: an experiment whose setup binds the multilayer sample (`SampleIds.multilayerQwId`) at version 1 and the 600 nm source preset by its entry id, recorded through `recordExperiment`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding the sample, its materials, their categories and the source preset, each once; the recorder holds every one of those versions; and `kit.proxy.readExperiments ()` answers the experiment. `recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind`: a scene whose elements bind the 600 nm source preset and the multilayer sample by value id, beside one unbound detector, recorded through `recordScene` under `Bench`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding the source, the multilayer at its latest version, its materials and their categories, and `readScene` answers the scene. `a reference the library and the kit cannot resolve records nothing`: an experiment binding a test-local GUID by entry id answers `UnheldEntryErr` naming it, `readExperiments` answers `[]`, and `paths` is unchanged. `a read-only kit records nothing`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, `recordExperiment` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the recording members land, `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` and `recordScene` MUST snapshot every library version the file references, pinning it, before they write the file, and write nothing when a reference cannot be resolved; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `recording an experiment snapshots the library versions it binds, then writes its file`, `recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind`, `a reference the library and the kit cannot resolve records nothing`, `a read-only kit records nothing`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording an experiment snapshots the library versions it binds, then writes its file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-RECORD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-RECORD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a reference the library and the kit cannot resolve records nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-RECORD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a read-only kit records nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-RECORD"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-RECORD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordScene", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-RECORD"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 150, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [149], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests"], "how_to": "Opening a picked folder for a constructor window, in the Ui (the S4.3 brief: the picker is followed by S4.1's initialise-or-open, and a foreign lock offers Open read-only; step 141's doc: a kit's opener resolves its snapshots after `KitContext.openKit`; .spec-md §3.10, §3.12). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening`, compiled directly before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (1) `type ClockProvider with static member system : ClockProvider` answers `ClockTime DateTime.UtcNow` at each call: the clock the app composes where it first opens a kit (step 122 leaves it to that code). (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] OpenedKit = { library : KitLibraryContext; experimentData : ExperimentData.ExperimentDataProxy; experiments : Experiment list; scenes : SceneName list; decisions : ImportDecision list; overlay : KitLibraryOverlay }`: a kit opened for a constructor window. `library` is the opened `KitContext` with the library's import seam (step 139); `experimentData` the measured-data seam over that kit (`ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked`, step 135); `experiments` and `scenes` what the window shows of the kit, read at open; `decisions` its snapshot rows (step 141); `overlay` the session's library overlay (step 142). `member this.pendingDecisions : ImportDecision list` MUST be all snapshot decisions in their original order, including `SameContentHash`. `member this.withRebindings (rebindings : EntryRebinding list) : Result<OpenedKit, KitLibraryError>` answers the opened kit whose overlay is `library.openOverlay rebindings` (step 142), after a confirmed resolution (step 156). (3) `openKitAt (folder : KitFolder) (access : KitAccess) (clock : ClockProvider) (author : KitAuthor) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : Result<OpenedKit, KitLibraryError>`, in this order. The proxy is `KitProxy.create folder` (step 126). Under `ReadWriteKitAccess` the context is `KitContext.openOrInitialise proxy clock (folder.namedKitFile (KitId (Guid.NewGuid ())) author)` (step 145): the kit id is minted here, where the app first makes a kit. Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` it is `KitContext.openKit proxy ReadOnlyKitAccess clock`, which never initialises. A `KitError` is `KitLibraryKitErr`, so `KitLockedErr` reaches the caller unchanged inside it. Over the open context it then reads `readExperiments ()` and `readSceneNames ()` (step 148), resolves `{ kit = context; imports = imports }.resolveSnapshots ()` (step 141) and opens `openOverlay []` (step 142). When any of these fails the context is closed (`close`, step 131) and the failure is the answer, so a kit whose files do not read is never left locked; a close that fails is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying its `describe`, and the first error is answered. (4) `type KitFolderPicker with static member ofWindow (owner : TopLevel) (suggested : FolderName) : KitFolderPicker` (step 145) is the Avalonia folder dialog: `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync` titled `Choose a kit folder`, one folder, its `SuggestedStartLocation` the `suggested` folder when `TryGetFolderFromPathAsync` resolves it. It answers `Some (KitFolder (FolderName path))` of the chosen folder's `TryGetLocalPath ()`, and `None` on Cancel, for a folder with no local path, or when the provider throws (a host without one). It is the IO edge in the shape of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`, nothing above it handles an exception, and it creates no folder. (5) `scratchKit () : KitContext` is `KitContext.createInMemory (KitFile.create (KitId (Guid.NewGuid ())) (KitName \"Scratch kit\") (KitAuthor \"\") (ClockProvider.system.now ())) ClockProvider.system` (steps 122, 145): the kit of a scene that opened no folder, the test scenes and the TestWindows heads; nothing it holds outlives the scene. No cache, retry or other declaration is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs`, `module KitOpeningTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Each fact makes its folders under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitOpeningTests\", <a new GUID>)` and opens them with `ClockProvider.system`, `KitAuthor \"test\"` and an import context over the Built-in library (`BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`, step 94). `opening an empty folder initialises a kit named for it and opens it read-write`: over a folder named `Optics QZ` that does not exist yet, `openKitAt` read-write answers an opened kit whose kit file is named `Optics QZ` and whose context is read-write, with no experiment, scene or decision; the folder holds `.kit-json`, `data`, `library` and `.oc/lock`; after `close` it holds no `.oc/lock`. `opening a kit reads its experiments and scenes`: a kit given one experiment through `writeExperiment` and a scene `Bench` through `writeScene`, then closed, answers that experiment and `[ Bench ]` when opened again. `a kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr inside the open's error, and opening it read-only writes nothing`: with the kit opened, a second read-write `openKitAt` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr _)` naming this process; `openKitAt` with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` answers an opened kit whose context is read-only, and every file of the folder keeps its bytes. `a kit whose experiment file does not read is refused and left unlocked`: `E1.experiment-json` written by the test as `{` makes `openKitAt` answer `KitLibraryKitErr (KitFileRejectedErr _)` naming it, and the folder holds no `.oc/lock`. `a kit holding a snapshot the library lacks opens with a pending row, and its overlay serves the entry`: a kit whose `library/` holds the snapshot of a test-local user material (written through `writeSnapshot`, step 138) answers one pending `EntryIdNotHeld` row and an overlay whose `snapshots` hold that envelope; a kit holding only Silicon's catalogue snapshot MUST answer that SameContentHash row as pending, without writing to the library. `the scratch kit is an empty in-memory kit opened read-write`: `scratchKit ()` answers a read-write context whose proxy lists no experiment or setup file.", "acceptance": "After `KitOpening.fs` lands, `KitOpening.openKitAt` MUST initialise or open a picked folder, read its experiments and scenes, resolve its snapshots and answer an opened kit, closing the kit on any failure and passing `KitLockedErr` through inside `KitLibraryKitErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening an empty folder initialises a kit named for it and opens it read-write`, `opening a kit reads its experiments and scenes`, `a kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr inside the open's error, and opening it read-only writes nothing`, `a kit whose experiment file does not read is refused and left unlocked`, `a kit holding a snapshot the library lacks opens with a pending row, and its overlay serves the entry`, `the scratch kit is an empty in-memory kit opened read-write`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening an empty folder initialises a kit named for it and opens it read-write", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening a kit reads its experiments and scenes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.a kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr inside the open's error, and opening it read-only writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.a kit whose experiment file does not read is refused and left unlocked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.a kit holding a snapshot the library lacks opens with a pending row, and its overlay serves the entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.the scratch kit is an empty in-memory kit opened read-write", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.OpenedKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.openKitAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.scratchKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.KitFolderPicker.ofWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.ClockProvider.system", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S43-OPENING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 151, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [150], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneProxyTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests"], "how_to": "`Scene.SceneProxy` and its in-memory store are deleted, because a scene now persists as a kit file (001 §R '`Scene.SceneProxy` and `ExperimentCollectionProxy` (in-memory seams), replaced by `KitProxy`'; the S4.3 brief: AppContext loses scenes, and SceneProxyTests' facts move to kit-file tests). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`: `SceneProxy` (`Scene.fs:SceneProxy`) and its `type SceneProxy with … createInMemory` extension are deleted. The module doc becomes one to three lines: the constructor scene as data, kept in a kit as `<scene name>.setup-json` (spec 0050 S4.3). Every doc sentence that names the proxy, a declared seam, a future storage cycle or `.ocproj` goes; each remaining doc keeps one to three lines. `SceneStoreError`, `SceneName`, `SnapMode`, `SceneElement`, `SceneSnapshot` and step 147's members stay. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the `scenes` field (`AppContext.fs:AppContext`) and its composition, with their comments, are deleted. (3) The comment above `Scene.fs`'s `<Compile>` in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` is cut to the words that stay true, naming no proxy, and nothing is added (AGENTS.md). A doc in `ExperimentDataProxy.fs` that still names `Scene.SceneProxy` or `SceneProxyTests` drops the name. (4) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneProxyTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` entry and the comment above it in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`. Its facts on the shapes that stay move into `SceneRoundTripTests` unchanged, with the `SnapMode` open they need: `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a blank name as InvalidScene carrying a reason`, `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a null name as InvalidScene`, `SceneName.tryCreate accepts a non-blank name and round-trips its value`, `SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement`. `a SceneProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)` and `a stub SceneProxy over a fixed map exercises saveScene, tryLoadScene, and listScenes through their exact signatures` are deleted with the proxy; step 148's kit-file facts cover what a scene store does. The comment above `SceneRoundTripTests.fs`'s `<Compile>` names the kit file instead of the proxy, in no more words. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' `the finalized app scope carries every store proxy — the step-027 scene seam is composed at the root` drops its `ctx.scenes.listScenes ()` match and keeps its other assertions; its module doc and the comment beside it in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` stop naming the scene seam.", "acceptance": "After the scene seam is deleted, `Scene.fs` MUST declare no `SceneProxy`, `AppContext` MUST compose no scene store, and the `SceneName` and `SnapMode` facts MUST run in `SceneRoundTripTests`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a blank name as InvalidScene carrying a reason`, `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a null name as InvalidScene`, `SceneName.tryCreate accepts a non-blank name and round-trips its value`, `SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement` under `SceneRoundTripTests`, the count falling by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the finalized app scope carries every store proxy — the step-027 scene seam is composed at the root`; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMovementTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FacetedTreeControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RayPositionControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererTestTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RotationControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToBeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToReflectedTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneProxyTests.SceneName.tryCreate rejects a blank name as InvalidScene carrying a reason", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SceneName.tryCreate rejects a blank name as InvalidScene carrying a reason", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneProxyTests.SceneName.tryCreate rejects a null name as InvalidScene", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SceneName.tryCreate rejects a null name as InvalidScene", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneProxyTests.SceneName.tryCreate accepts a non-blank name and round-trips its value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SceneName.tryCreate accepts a non-blank name and round-trips its value", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneProxyTests.SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneProxyTests.a SceneProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneProxyTests.a stub SceneProxy over a fixed map exercises saveScene, tryLoadScene, and listScenes through their exact signatures", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests.the finalized app scope carries every store proxy — the step-027 scene seam is composed at the root", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Scene.SceneProxy", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Scene.SceneProxy.createInMemory", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.AppContext.scenes", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S43-NO-SCENE-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 152, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [151], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionProxyTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests"], "how_to": "The constructor works inside a kit: it holds a `KitContext` in place of the collection seam, and committing, editing and removing an experiment write and delete its kit file (001 §S4 'today's experiments and scenes persist into the kit'; 001 §R; the S4.3 brief; .spec-md §0.1 `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` 'Hosts a KitContext in place of the scene and collection seams'). The windows work in their scratch kit until step 154 opens a picked folder. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs`: `ExperimentCollectionProxy` and its `createInMemory` extension (`ExperimentCollectionStore.fs:ExperimentCollectionProxy`), `ExperimentCollectionError` and `CollectionName.tryCreate` are deleted, because nothing saves, lists or loads a named collection any more. `CollectionName` (with `.value`) and `ExperimentCollectionSnapshot` stay: they are the collection the solver hand-off shows (`SolverHandoffView.fs:SolverHandoffContext`), which S11.5 retires. The module doc becomes one to three lines saying so (spec 0050 S4.3), every doc sentence naming the proxy, `Scene.SceneProxy`, a future store or `.ocproj` goes, and the comment above its `<Compile>` in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` is cut to the words that stay true. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `TableAndElementRotationModel` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TableAndElementRotationModel`) loses `experimentCollections`, `collectionName`, `savedCollections` and `collectionStatus`, and gains `kit : KitContext` (the kit the constructor works in) and `kitStatus : ControlCaption option` (the last kit read or write that needs telling), each with a one-line doc; `experimentData`'s doc says it reads through `kit`. The `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentCollectionStore` and its comment go. (b) `defaultExperimentProxies` is deleted. `initWith` loses its `experimentData` and `experimentCollections` parameters: it sets `kit` to `KitOpening.scratchKit ()` (step 150), `experimentData` to `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` over that kit's proxy (step 135) and `kitStatus` to `None`. `initTableAndElementRotation`, `initMainWith`, `initInverse` and `initMain` keep their signatures and stop passing the two proxies. (c) `type TableAndElementRotationModel with member model.loadKit (opened : OpenedKit) : TableAndElementRotationModel` (step 150), its doc one to three lines: the model working in an opened kit. It sets `kit` to `opened.library.kit`, `experimentData` to `opened.experimentData`, `experimentCollection` to `Experiments.ExperimentCollection.ofLoaded opened.experiments` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentCollection`) and `kitStatus` to `None`, and computes `experimentDataStatus` as step 136's `CollectionLoad` arm did: one status per loaded experiment with an attachment, through `experimentData.attachmentStatus` and the one private validation function, moved here unchanged, so a changed or missing data file is flagged when the kit opens (001 §E). (d) Writing through the kit. The kit's library is `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }` (steps 101, 139). `ExpCommit` computes the committed collection as today; when the draft committed (the collection changed), the experiment the draft now edits (`draft.editingId`, `Experiments.fs:commit`) is recorded through `recordExperiment` (step 149): on `Ok` the model takes the new collection and `kitStatus` is `None`; on `Error e` the model keeps its collection and `kitStatus` is `Some (ControlCaption $\"Not saved to the kit — {e.describe}\")`. `ExpRemove id` calls `model.kit.proxy.deleteExperiment id` (step 148): `Ok` or `MissingKitFileErr` removes the experiment (its file is gone either way); any other error keeps it and sets `kitStatus` the same way. `AttachDataFileTo` (step 135): the experiment carrying its new attachment is recorded through `recordExperiment` before the model takes it; on an error the experiment keeps what it had, its data status is unchanged, and `kitStatus` names the error. `ExpEdit`, `ExpNew` and the draft messages write nothing. (e) `CollectionSetName`, `CollectionSave` and `CollectionLoad` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TableAndElementRotationMsg`) and their arms are deleted. (f) `collectionBuilderView` loses its name field, Save button, status line and saved list. It shows `kitStatus`, when `Some`, in a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.kitStatus`, and then the inverse `Data files:` section unchanged. Its doc and the section comment above it say the experiments are kept in the kit; every comment that names the collection store, `SceneProxy` or `.experimentCollections` names the kit. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: `collectionNameField`, `saveCollectionButton` and `savedCollections` (`UiIds.fs:165-168`) are deleted, and `collectionStatus` becomes `kitStatus` (`\"KitStatus\"`) under a doc line naming the kit status line and the data files. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `ConstructorUiId.savedCollection` (`ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:70`) and the `CollectionName.caption` extension (`:250`) are deleted. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `experimentData` and `experimentCollections` (`AppContext.fs:AppContext`) and their composition go, because the measured-data seam reads through the kit a window works in; the record doc names what remains. (5) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` stop threading `experimentData` and `experimentCollections`, and their docs and `ConstructorScene`'s stop naming the collection store. (6) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` entry and comment; its five facts test the deleted proxy and `CollectionName.tryCreate`, and step 148's kit-file facts in `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` cover what the store did. The `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj` comment above `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs` names the kit files, and that file's doc names no proxy. (a) `TestAppScope` (step 83) gains, each with a one-line doc citing .spec-md §3.10: `freshKitFolder (owner : FolderName) : KitFolder`, a new GUID-named folder under `testLocations owner`'s `kitsFolder`, not created; and `openedKitIn (owner : FolderName) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : OpenedKit`, `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) over `freshKitFolder owner` read-write with `ClockProvider.system` and `KitAuthor \"test\"`, failing the calling fact with the error's `describe` otherwise. (b) `InverseConstructorTests`: `inverse ()` is `initInverse` over the class's stores, then `loadKit (TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName \"InverseConstructorTests\") m.catalogueImports)`, so its facts run over a folder kit; the mocks are set by record update after it, and every fact keeps its assertions. `a named collection round-trips through save, list, and load` becomes `committed experiments and their attachments are kept in the kit and reopen with it`: after the commit and the attach of `withIntensityExperiment`, `readExperiments` of the model's kit answers the model's experiments, and, the kit closed, an inverse model loaded from `openKitAt` of the same folder holds equal experiments with the attachment. `saving a collection with a blank name reports a typed status and stores nothing` and `loading an unknown collection reports a typed status and leaves the live collection alone` are deleted with the collection builder; step 153's scene facts cover a blank name and a miss. Step 136's `loading a collection re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged` and `loading a collection flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing` become `opening a kit re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged` and `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`: the experiments are written into a folder kit, the kit opened through `openKitAt`, and the model loaded through `loadKit` of that opened kit with the mock as its `experimentData`, with the same assertions. It gains `a commit, an attach and a removal write the kit's experiment files`: a commit writes `E1.experiment-json`, the attach rewrites it with the attachment, and `ExpRemove` deletes it and drops the experiment; and `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why`: over a model whose kit is its own kit's read-only view (`{ m.kit with proxy = m.kit.proxy.readOnlyView; access = ReadOnlyKitAccess }`), `ExpCommit` leaves the collection as it was and `kitStatus` holds `KitReadOnlyErr`'s text. `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing` drops its two collection messages and keeps rendering. (c) `AppContextTests.surfaceOf` drops its two record-update fields. (d) `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`: `the finalized app scope carries every store proxy — the step-027 scene seam is composed at the root` is deleted, because the app scope composes no scene or experiment store and `AppContextTests`' `create carries the settings record it was given, verbatim` pins its settings; the solver hand-off its factory opens reads through `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked (KitOpening.scratchKit ()).proxy`; its module doc and the `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` comments naming `ExperimentCollectionProxy` say the kit. (e) `SolverHandoffWindowTests.baseExperiment` sets its model's `catalogueImports` to `(TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"SolverHandoffWindowTests\")).catalogueImports`, a library holding the presets it binds, so its commit records them; every fact keeps its assertions. After this step `git grep -n -E \"SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the constructor holds its kit, `TableAndElementRotationModel` MUST hold `kit` and no collection store, a commit, an attach and a removal MUST write and delete the experiment's kit file (a failed write keeping the experiment and showing `kitStatus`), `loadKit` MUST flag changed and missing data, and `git grep -n -E \"SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, the count falling by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing`; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `committed experiments and their attachments are kept in the kit and reopen with it`, `opening a kit re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged`, `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`, `a commit, an attach and a removal write the kit's experiment files`, `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why`, the count falling by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementM