{"number": 153, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [152], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests"], "how_to": "Saving and loading a scene write and read its kit file (the S4.3 brief; 001 §P: every user step is a semantic message, and the same messages back the buttons; .spec-md §4 'UI'). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `sceneName : ControlCaption` (the scene name being typed, raw text until `SceneName.tryCreate` validates it at save, as the draft's label is) and `savedScenes : Scene.SceneName list` (the kit's scenes, by name), each with a one-line doc. `initWith` sets them to `ControlCaption \"\"` and `[]`; `loadKit` (step 152) sets `savedScenes` to `opened.scenes`. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each with a one-line doc: `SceneSetName of ControlCaption` (edit the name), `SceneSave` (save the table as a scene of that name in the kit) and `SceneLoad of Scene.SceneName` (put the kit's scene of that name on the table). (3) Arms. `SceneSetName name` sets `sceneName`. `SceneSave`: `SceneName.tryCreate model.sceneName.value` (`Scene.fs:SceneName`); a blank name sets `kitStatus` to `Save failed — <reason>` and writes nothing. Otherwise `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordScene name model.captureScene` (step 149; `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:captureScene`): on `Ok` `savedScenes` holds the name once, in ordinal order, and `kitStatus` is `Saved scene '<name>'.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `SceneLoad name`: `model.kit.proxy.readScene name` (step 148); `Ok scene` is `restoreScene scene model` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:restoreScene`) with `kitStatus` `Loaded scene '<name>'.`; `Error e` leaves the table alone and sets `kitStatus` to `Load failed — <e.describe>`. (4) The view: `collectionBuilderView` shows first, under the heading `Scene:`, one horizontal row: the name field, a `TextBox` carrying `ConstructorUiId.sceneNameField` that dispatches `SceneSetName` on Enter and on lost focus (the old collection name field's commit), and the `workbenchButton` `Save scene` (`ConstructorUiId.saveSceneButton`, dispatching `SceneSave`); then the `kitStatus` line (step 152); then, when `savedScenes` is not empty, `Saved scenes:` and a `WrapPanel` named `ConstructorUiId.savedScenes` holding one `workbenchButton` per name (`ConstructorUiId.savedScene name`, captioned by the name, dispatching `SceneLoad name`); then the inverse `Data files:` section. It shows in both modes. (5) Ids. `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, beside `kitStatus` (step 152), under one doc line naming the scene row: `sceneNameField` (`\"SceneNameField\"`), `saveSceneButton` (`\"SaveSceneButton\"`) and `savedScenes` (`\"SavedScenes\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, where `savedCollection` and the collection caption stood: `static member savedScene (name : Scene.SceneName) : ConstructorUiId` (`SavedScene_<name>`) and `type Scene.SceneName with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, each with a one-line doc. No other message, field or id is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs`, `module SceneSaveLoadTests`, compiled directly after `InverseConstructorTests.fs` with no comment. Its model is `initMain ()` loaded through `loadKit (TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName \"SceneSaveLoadTests\") m.catalogueImports)` (step 152), whose import seam holds the Built-in catalogue. `a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table`: with a linear polarizer added (`AddElement Placement.LinearPolarizer`, pre-bound to its preset), `SceneSetName (ControlCaption \"Bench: A\")` then `SceneSave` makes `savedScenes` `[ Bench: A ]` and `kitStatus` `Saved scene 'Bench: A'.`; the kit folder holds `Bench_ A.setup-json` and the preset's snapshot under `library/`; after `RemoveSelected`, `SceneLoad` of that name puts back the saved elements; and a model loaded from the same folder opened again (the first kit closed) lists `Bench: A`. `saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing`: `SceneSetName (ControlCaption \"   \")` then `SceneSave` sets `kitStatus` to a text starting `Save failed`, leaves `savedScenes` empty and writes no setup file. `loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone`: `SceneLoad (SceneName \"nowhere\")` sets `kitStatus` to a text starting `Load failed` and leaves `elements` as they were. `the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes` (trait `ui-smoke`): `mainView` over a model with one saved scene and the Experiments bay selected renders headless without throwing, holding `sceneNameField`, `saveSceneButton`, `savedScenes` and the scene's `savedScene` button.", "acceptance": "After scene save and load land, `SceneSave` MUST record the table as a setup file of the kit with its library snapshots and `SceneLoad` MUST restore a kit scene onto the table, each reporting a refusal in `kitStatus`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table`, `saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing`, `loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMovementTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FacetedTreeControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RayPositionControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererTestTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RotationControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToBeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToReflectedTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SceneSetName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SceneSave", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SceneLoad", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.sceneName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.savedScenes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.sceneNameField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.saveSceneButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.savedScenes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.savedScene", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S43-SCENE-SAVE-LOAD"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 154, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S4.3j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [153], "how_to": "Main and Inverse open a kit the user picks, and each constructor window works in its kit until it closes (the S4.3 brief: Program.fs MainConstructorWindow and InverseConstructorWindow take a KitContext; the Launcher's Main and Inverse open a kit through the KitFolderPicker seam, followed by S4.1's initialise-or-open; headless tests substitute the seam with a folder under the test output; .spec-md §3.10; §10.5: Close kit loses nothing, because kit writes are immediate and atomic). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: (1) `MainConstructorWindow(context : AppContext, opened : OpenedKit)` and `InverseConstructorWindow(context : AppContext, opened : OpenedKit)`: the opened kit (step 150) carries the `KitContext` (`opened.library.kit`) with what was read when it opened, because a window cannot fail and the reads and the resolution precede it. `ConstructorScene` gains `storesOf (context : AppContext) (opened : OpenedKit) : KitLibraryStores`, `{ library = context.library; materials = context.materials; samples = context.samples; categories = context.categories }.overlaidWith opened.overlay` (step 142), so the kit's snapshot entries resolve in its window. Each window's seed is today's (`initMainWith` / `initInverse` over those four stores and `context.experiments`, with the record update threading `sources`, `experimentExport`, `libraryBackups` and `catalogueImports`), then `.loadKit opened` (step 152). When the window closes (`Closed`) it releases the kit (`opened.library.kit.close ()`); an `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (2) `LauncherWindow(locations, settings, opened, pickerFor : TopLevel -> KitFolderPicker)` (steps 88, 89, 112): the new argument builds the folder picker over the launcher, and `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` passes `fun owner -> KitFolderPicker.ofWindow owner Startup.dataLocations.kitsFolder` (step 150; 001 §G: the suggested parent of kit folders). Main and Inverse no longer build a window directly: a click starts `(pickerFor this).pickKitFolder ()` on the UI thread (`Async.StartImmediate`); `None` does nothing; `Some folder` calls one local function of the folder, the mode (`ForwardConstructor` / `InverseConstructor`, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:ConstructorMode`) and the access, which calls `KitOpening.openKitAt folder access ClockProvider.system (KitAuthor Environment.UserName) context.catalogueImports` with `ReadWriteKitAccess`. On `Ok opened` it shows `MainConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for the forward mode and `InverseConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for the inverse one. On `Error e` no window opens, and the launcher shows, between the title and the surface buttons, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherKitErrorText` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, reading `The kit could not be opened: <e.describe>`; the next successful open removes it. Steps 155 and 156 call the same local function. Materials and Library are unchanged: they need no kit (001 §F). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588`): `static member launcherKitErrorText : ConstructorUiId = ConstructorUiId \"LauncherKitErrorText\"` with a one-line doc. (4) Tests. `TestAppScope` (step 152) gains `kitPickerOf (folder : KitFolder) : KitFolderPicker`, answering `Some folder` at once, with a one-line doc. Every fact that builds a constructor window passes `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` of its module's name over its context's `catalogueImports` and keeps its assertions: `WireUiCompositionTests` (`WireUiCompositionTests.fs:113`), `WireUi0040CompositionTests` (`WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:175`), `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:120`, `:121`), `AppContextTests`' two-window acceptance (`AppContextTests.fs:137`, `:140`, one kit each), `TableAndElementRotationTests` (`TableAndElementRotationTests.fs:224`) and `LauncherTests`' single-instance fact (`LauncherTests.fs:215`). `MainWorkbenchTests.mainWith` loads its model over `TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName \"MainWorkbenchTests\")`, so the workbench it mounts has the window's shape (`MainWorkbenchTests.fs:89`). Every `LauncherWindow(...)` in `LauncherTests` and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` passes `fun _ -> TestAppScope.kitPickerOf (TestAppScope.freshKitFolder <owner>)`. In `LauncherTests`, `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene` and `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene` keep their assertions over a fresh folder and also find `.kit-json` in it. It gains, each with trait `ui-smoke`: `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`: a folder whose kit holds one experiment (written through `openKitAt`, `writeExperiment` and `close`) opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow`, and closing it removes `.oc/lock`; `a cancelled pick opens nothing`: a picker answering `None` opens no window and creates no folder; and `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window`: a folder whose `E1.experiment-json` holds `{` opens no window, shows `launcherKitErrorText` naming `E1.experiment-json`, and holds no `.oc/lock`.", "acceptance": "After the windows take an opened kit, the launcher's Main and Inverse MUST open the folder the picker answers as a kit (initialising it when needed) in the forward and inverse constructor, show a kit that cannot be opened in `launcherKitErrorText`, and a closed window MUST release its kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene`, `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene`, `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`, `a cancelled pick opens nothing`, `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window`, the count rising by 3; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a cancelled pick opens nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.MainConstructorWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.InverseConstructorWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.launcherKitErrorText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S43-WINDOWS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 155, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S4.3k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [154], "how_to": "A kit open elsewhere is offered read-only (001 §E 'a .oc/lock … warns across processes and machines, with an open read-only choice'; the S4.3 brief: a foreign lock offers 'Open read-only'; .spec-md §10.5: the opposing pair Open read-only / Cancel shares one row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; §3.12: a read-only open writes nothing). (1) In `Program.fs`' `LauncherWindow`, when the open of a picked folder (step 154) answers `Error (KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr holder))`, no window opens; `launcherKitErrorText` reads `The kit is open elsewhere: <holder.describe>.` (step 129), and under it one horizontal row holds `Open read-only` (`ConstructorUiId.launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton`, background `MaterialsWindowView.positiveBackground`) and, 12 px to its right, `Cancel` (`ConstructorUiId.launcherCancelKitOpenButton`, background `MaterialsWindowView.negativeBackground`; both colours public since step 107), each carrying its id as `Name` and `AutomationId`. `Open read-only` calls step 154's local function for the same folder and mode with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, and on success removes the text and the row. `Cancel` removes them and opens nothing. Every other error keeps step 154's text with no row. A window opened read-only works in the read-only context, so each kit write it asks answers `KitReadOnlyErr` in its `kitStatus` (step 152); S5.3 adds the title marker and disables those messages. (2) `UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton` (`\"LauncherOpenKitReadOnlyButton\"`) and `launcherCancelKitOpenButton` (`\"LauncherCancelKitOpenButton\"`), each with a one-line doc. (3) Tests, in `LauncherTests`, each holding the picked kit open through an `openKitAt` of its own, as a second window would, and closing it at the end, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing`: clicking Main shows the holder's text naming this process and both buttons with equal tops, `Cancel` to the right of `Open read-only` with a gap; clicking `Open read-only` opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow` and removes the row, and every file of the folder keeps its bytes, the other holder's `.oc/lock` included; closing that window leaves the `.oc/lock` in place. `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`: clicking `Cancel` removes the text and the row and opens no window. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher keeps its code.", "acceptance": "After the read-only offer lands, a picked kit whose lock another holder owns MUST show the holder with Open read-only and Cancel on one row, and Open read-only MUST open the constructor over the kit's read-only context writing nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing` and `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-READ-ONLY-OFFER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-READ-ONLY-OFFER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S43-READ-ONLY-OFFER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S43-READ-ONLY-OFFER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.launcherCancelKitOpenButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S43-READ-ONLY-OFFER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 156, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S4.3l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [155], "how_to": "Opening a kit resolves its library snapshot first, in the one import dialog when a row needs a decision (001 §E 'Resolution on open … One dialog shows all rows; nothing changes in the database unconfirmed'; .spec-md §10.1 'The import dialog opens … on a kit whose snapshot needs decisions'; §10.3 identify → confirm; step 141's doc: a kit whose rows all reuse MUST still show every row before confirmation; step 144: `ResolveKitSnapshot`). (1) In `Program.fs`' `LauncherWindow`, step 154's local function, on `Ok opened`: when `opened.pendingDecisions` (step 150) is empty the window opens as before. Otherwise it opens `ImportDialogWindow(context.catalogueImports, ResolveKitSnapshot (opened.library, opened.decisions), onApplied)` (steps 108, 144) and no constructor window yet. `onApplied applied` calls `opened.withRebindings applied.outcome.rebindings` (step 150): `Ok resolved` opens the constructor window over `resolved` in the asked mode; `Error e` closes the kit and shows `launcherKitErrorText` with `e.describe`. When the dialog closes without an Apply (its `Closed` with no `onApplied` before it, tracked by one local flag at this IO edge), the kit is closed (`close`, step 131) and nothing opens, so a cancelled resolution leaves the kit unlocked and the library unchanged. A read-only open (step 155) resolves the same way, because resolution writes nothing to the kit (step 141). No message or id is added. (2) Tests, in `LauncherTests`, with trait `ui-smoke`; the kits are written through `openKitAt`, `writeSnapshot` (step 138) and `close`. `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`: over a kit whose `library/` holds the snapshot of a test-local user material the app's library does not hold, clicking Main opens exactly one `ImportDialogWindow` and no constructor window; pressing its `importApplyButton`, the rows on their defaults (keep the kit's copy), opens one `MainConstructorWindow`, and the app's library still does not hold the material (`context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryHeldEntry` answers `None`). `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit`: over the same kind of kit, pressing `importCancelButton` opens no constructor window and leaves no `.oc/lock`. `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening`: over a kit holding only Silicon's Built-in snapshot, clicking Main MUST open one ImportDialogWindow displaying the Reuse row and no constructor. Cancel MUST release the kit without library writes; opening again and pressing Apply MUST open one MainConstructorWindow with database entries and the import log unchanged. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher keeps its code. After this step `git grep -n -E \"SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy\" -- Berreman/` still finds nothing. The declared opener acceptance fact MUST include an all-Reuse snapshot: every row MUST be visible; no constructor MUST open before Apply; Cancel MUST close the pending kit without changing database entries or log; applying defaults MUST open with no database writes. An empty snapshot list alone MAY bypass the dialog.", "acceptance": "After resolution on open lands, a picked kit whose snapshot has a row that is not `SameContentHash` MUST open the import dialog before the constructor, Apply MUST open the constructor over the resolved overlay and Cancel MUST open nothing and release the kit, and `git grep -n -E \"SceneProxy|ExperimentCollectionProxy\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`, `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit`, `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening`, the count rising by 3; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-RESOLVE-ON-OPEN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-RESOLVE-ON-OPEN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S43-RESOLVE-ON-OPEN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S43-RESOLVE-ON-OPEN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.3 -- Today's experiments and scenes persist in the kit; the in-memory seams go"}
{"number": 157, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.4a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [156], "how_to": "The design history and the project report leave `Report.fs`, because each exists only over the `.ocproj` aggregate (001 §R '`.ocproj`: `ProjectFile`, the `ProjectJson` project aggregate and the `Project` record'; the S4.4 brief: a module that also serves another live surface keeps that surface and loses only the project path). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs`: the module `DesignHistory` (`Report.fs:DesignHistory`: `ChangeKind`, `DiffIdentity`, `DiffItem`, `ProjectDiff`, `historyFolder`, `appendRevision`, `layerDiff`, `diffRevisions`) and the module `Report` (`Report.fs:Report`: `ReportFormat`, `reportsDir`, `ReportChart`, `reportDocument`, `generate`) are deleted with their docs. Nothing outside `Report.fs` and `ExportImportTests.fs` names them, and no window ever called `generate`. The module `MaterialLibrary` (`Report.fs:MaterialLibrary`) stays unchanged in this step: the metadata-only material file is a surface of its own, and step 160 gives it its own schema. Every `open` left unused goes, `Giraffe.ViewEngine`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.Export` and `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project` among them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`: the `Giraffe.ViewEngine.StrongName` package reference and the three-line comment above it (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:73-76`) are deleted, because the report HTML was Storage's only use of it; the central `PackageVersion` in the root `Directory.Build.targets` is not touched. The comment above `RecentFiles.fs`'s `<Compile>` (`:32-34`) is cut to the words that stay true, naming no report, design history or `ChartHandle` dependency of `Report`; nothing is added (AGENTS.md). `Export.fs`'s `ChartHandle` and `exportChartImage` (`Export.fs:Export`) stay as Export's own chart-image surface (§I.7). (3) Tests: in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs`, `AC-I11 appendRevision twice yields two numbered snapshots and diffRevisions returns a ProjectDiff` is deleted with the fixtures only it used (`filmThickness`, `vacuumSystem`, `light`, `node` and `sampleProject`, `ExportImportTests.fs:141-183` in today's tree) and the opens they alone needed (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory` and any other left unused). The module doc (`:23-24`) drops its design-history clause. Every other fact of the class keeps its name and assertions. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"DesignHistory|appendRevision|diffRevisions|ProjectDiff|ReportFormat|Giraffe\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the design history and the project report leave `Report.fs`, `git grep -n -E \"DesignHistory|appendRevision|diffRevisions|ProjectDiff|ReportFormat|Giraffe\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` MUST find nothing and the material file's import and export MUST behave as before; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, every other ExportImportTests fact unchanged, the count falling by 1; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExportImportTests.AC-I11 appendRevision twice yields two numbered snapshots and diffRevisions returns a ProjectDiff", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory.ChangeKind", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory.DiffIdentity", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory.DiffItem", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory.ProjectDiff", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory.historyFolder", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory.appendRevision", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.DesignHistory.diffRevisions", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.Report.ReportFormat", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.Report.generate", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-REPORT-MODULES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.4 -- The .ocproj aggregate is deleted"}
{"number": 158, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.4b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [157], "how_to": "The whole-project undo and redo go, because their only state is the aggregate (001 §R '`.ocproj`'; the S4.4 brief names `History.fs`; .spec-md §8: this spec adds no undo history). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/History.fs` (`History.fs:History`: `EditHistory` with `ofPresent`, `push`, `undo` and `redo`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:36`); the comment above `RecentFiles.fs`'s `<Compile>` loses its undo/redo words and gains none. Nothing else in the product names the module. (2) Tests: in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs`, `AC-I7 undo restores the pre-edit project and redo restores the edit` and `AC-I7 undo on empty history returns the input unchanged` (`HistoryTests.fs:48-66`) are deleted with `open OpticalConstructor.Storage.History`. The fixtures `projectWith`, `preEdit` and `edited` stay, because `AC-I6 writeAutosave leaves the .ocproj untouched and writes a distinct .autosave` uses them until step 159. The module doc (`:19-22`) keeps only its autosave sentence and gains none. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"EditHistory|Storage.History\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the edit history is deleted, `git grep -n -E \"EditHistory|Storage.History\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent` and `AC-I6 writeAutosave leaves the .ocproj untouched and writes a distinct .autosave` unchanged, the count falling by 2; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/History.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.HistoryTests.AC-I7 undo restores the pre-edit project and redo restores the edit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.HistoryTests.AC-I7 undo on empty history returns the input unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.History.EditHistory", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.History.EditHistory.ofPresent", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.History.push", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.History.undo", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.History.redo", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-EDIT-HISTORY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.4 -- The .ocproj aggregate is deleted"}
{"number": 159, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.4c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [158], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.RoundTripTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests"], "how_to": "The `.ocproj` file and its autosave sidewrite go: no window ever saved or opened one (001 §0, §R; .spec-md §7: '`.ocproj`, `recent.json`, autosave files — compatibility break accepted'). Kits replace them (S4.1–S4.3). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs` (`ProjectFile.fs:ProjectFile`: `extension`, `FileName.saveProject`, `FileName.openProject`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:24`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs`: the `Autosave` module (`RecentFiles.fs:Autosave`: `autosaveSuffix`, `FileName.autosavePath`, `FileName.writeAutosave`) is deleted, with `open OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectFile`, `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project` and any other open left unused. `RecentFiles` keeps `maxRecent`, `prefsPath`, `bump`, `loadRecent` and `FileName.pushRecent` unchanged, as S5.1 replaces them. Its module doc (`RecentFiles.fs:11-17`) becomes one to three lines saying what stays: the most-recently-used list, kept in the per-user `recent.json` through the shared options; `loadRecent`'s doc (`:47`) says 'paths' for '`.ocproj` paths'. No comment in the file names autosave, `saveProject` or `.ocproj`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`: every comment that names `ProjectFile` or autosave (`:16-19`, `:25-27`, `:32-34`) is cut to the words that stay true; nothing is added (AGENTS.md). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs` is in scope for its module doc only: a sentence of it that still names `FileName.openProject` or `ProjectFile.fs` as a precedent (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:19-20` today, in the doc step 135 rewrote) goes. (5) `.gitignore`: the `*.autosave` rule, its two-line comment and the blank line after them (`.gitignore:341-344`) are deleted. (6) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/RoundTripTests.fs` (`RoundTripTests.fs:RoundTripTests`, the `.ocproj` round trip and its load-time refusals) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`. What it proved holds for kit files in `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 146): `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds`. In `HistoryTests.fs`, `AC-I6 writeAutosave leaves the .ocproj untouched and writes a distinct .autosave` (`HistoryTests.fs:90-110`) is deleted with the fixtures only it used (`filmThickness`, `vacuumSystem`, `light`, `node`, `projectWith`, `preEdit`, `edited`) and every open left unused (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectFile`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.Autosave` and the engine opens). The class keeps `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent` with its assertions; only its paths change, written as kit folders, not `.ocproj` files: `C:\\kits\\a`, `C:\\kits\\b`, `C:\\KITS\\A` and `C:\\kits\\f<i>`, so the head is `C:\\kits\\f20` and the last `C:\\kits\\f5`. Its module doc becomes one line naming `RecentFiles.bump`'s most-recent-first rule. Afterwards `git grep -n -i -E \"ProjectFile|autosave\" -- Berreman/ .gitignore` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the project file and the autosave are deleted, `git grep -n -i -E \"ProjectFile|autosave\" -- Berreman/ .gitignore` MUST find nothing and `.gitignore` MUST hold no `*.autosave` rule; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent` over kit-folder paths and every KitContentFileJsonTests fact, the count falling by 4; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs", ".gitignore", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/RoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.RoundTripTests.AC-I1 saveProject then openProject reproduces the project value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/RoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.RoundTripTests.AC-I2 a schema-violating document returns SchemaValidationErr and binds nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/RoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.RoundTripTests.AC-I3 a schemaVersion mismatch is rejected without migration", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/RoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.HistoryTests.AC-I6 writeAutosave leaves the .ocproj untouched and writes a distinct .autosave", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.HistoryTests.R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectFile.extension", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectFile.saveProject", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectFile.openProject", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.Autosave.autosaveSuffix", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.Autosave.autosavePath", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.Autosave.writeAutosave", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-FILE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.4 -- The .ocproj aggregate is deleted"}
{"number": 160, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.4d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [159], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.TableViewTests"], "how_to": "The project codec, its schema and the aggregate record go (001 §R '`.ocproj`: … the `ProjectJson` project aggregate and the `Project` record. Kits replace them, and the JSON + schema stack is reused (§B)'; the S4.4 brief: the serializer options already live in the canonical-JSON module, step 21, so `ProjectJson.fs` goes whole). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectJson.fs` (`ProjectJson.fs:ProjectJson`: `schemaVersion`, `ProjectJsonText` with `value` and `parseProject`, `serializeProject`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:23`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs`: `projectSchemaFile`, the project-schema lazy and `validate` (`SchemaValidation.fs:31-36` and `:61-76` in today's tree; `validate` answers `validateWith` over the project schema since step 29) are deleted; `tryLoadSchema`, `collectMessages`, `validateWith` and the per-kind validators stay. The module doc (`:9-12`) becomes one to three lines naming no project. (3) `schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json` is deleted with its `Content` item (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:58-60`). The one live reader of it moves with what it reads: the material file's `materialEntry` check (`Report.fs:materialEntrySchema`, which wraps the project schema's `$defs` today). New `schema/material-metadata.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 with `$id` `https://berreman/schema/material-metadata.json`, root `\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/materialEntry\"`, and `$defs` holding `materialEntry`, `dispersionModel`, `thermoOptic` and `unitOfMeasure` exactly as the project schema holds them (they are `materialEntry`'s whole reference closure), is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` in the project schema's place. In `Report.fs`, `materialEntrySchema` becomes the lazy `tryLoadSchema` of that file (`SchemaValidation.fs:tryLoadSchema`, through a private `FileName` bound once, as `projectSchemaFile` was) and `validateEntryElement` answers `validateWith materialEntrySchema element` (step 29's one evaluation body), so its refusal carries the evaluation's messages. The `MaterialLibrary` module doc and `materialEntrySchema`'s doc each become one to three lines naming the new file and no project schema. `importMaterials`, `exportMaterials` and the DTO are otherwise unchanged. (4) Domain: `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Project.fs` (`Project.fs:Project`: `OpticalConstructorProject`, `schemaDefAnchors`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj:42`); the comment above `Groups.fs`'s `<Compile>` (`:43-45`) loses 'compiles after Project'. `BeamTree`, `SourceSpec`, `Placement` and `Table` stay: other code uses them. (5) Docs that name the record: `Sidecar.fs`'s module doc (`Sidecar.fs:12-14`) and `SidecarTests.fs`'s (`SidecarTests.fs:14-15`) lose the sentence about the canonical project; every comment in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` that names `ProjectJson` is cut to the words that stay true. Sidecar itself is unchanged. (6) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line: `AC-C1 a fresh project table is 1.2 x 2.0 x 0.10 m` moves unchanged into `TableViewTests`, with any open it needs, and the other facts go with the codec (`AC-A2 a valid canonical project validates on load`, `AC-D6 round-trip preserves the defaultUnit label and the canonical SI datum`, `AC-A5 the canonical SI magnitudes are stored verbatim`, `AC-B9 beam tree and systems round-trip through the schema-validated canonical project`, `AC-B9 the filled beamNode $def rejects a malformed incident shape on load`, `AC-C1 the edited table size round-trips through the schema-validated canonical project`). In `PlacementTests.fs`, `AC-A6 a project carrying placement round-trips through the canonical JSON and passes schema validation` is deleted with the fixtures only it used (`PlacementTests.fs:149-175`: `vacuumSystem`, `light`, `rootNode`, `okOr`) and the opens left unused (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.Errors` and any other); the module doc drops its AC-A6 clause. A placement's round trip is held for kit files by `SceneRoundTripTests`' `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state` (step 148). `StackEditTests.fs` loses `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project` (`StackEditTests.fs:11`), which names nothing it uses. `ExportImportTests` gains `a material entry outside the materialEntry definition is SchemaValidationErr`: `validateEntryElement` of an element whose `category` is `NotACategory` (with a GUID `id` and a `name`) answers `Error (SchemaValidationErr messages)` with `messages` not empty. (7) The record's census also names `History.fs` (deleted at step 158), `ProjectFile.fs` and `RoundTripTests.fs` (deleted at step 159), and `RecentFiles.fs` and `HistoryTests.fs` (emptied of it at step 159); they are in scope only so the retirement covers its whole census, and nothing more changes in them. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"ProjectJson|OpticalConstructorProject|schemaDefAnchors|optical-constructor-project|Domain.Project\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the codec, the project schema and the record are deleted, `git grep -n -E \"ProjectJson|OpticalConstructorProject|schemaDefAnchors|optical-constructor-project|Domain.Project\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing, and `MaterialLibrary.validateEntryElement` MUST validate against `schema/material-metadata.schema.json`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a material entry outside the materialEntry definition is SchemaValidationErr`, `AC-C1 a fresh project table is 1.2 x 2.0 x 0.10 m` under TableViewTests and every other ExportImportTests fact, the count falling by 6; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/material-metadata.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Sidecar.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Project.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacementTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TableViewTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StackEditTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SidecarTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/History.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/RoundTripTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.AC-C1 a fresh project table is 1.2 x 2.0 x 0.10 m", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/TableViewTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.TableViewTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.TableViewTests.AC-C1 a fresh project table is 1.2 x 2.0 x 0.10 m", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.AC-A2 a valid canonical project validates on load", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.AC-D6 round-trip preserves the defaultUnit label and the canonical SI datum", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.AC-A5 the canonical SI magnitudes are stored verbatim", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.AC-B9 beam tree and systems round-trip through the schema-validated canonical project", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.AC-B9 the filled beamNode $def rejects a malformed incident shape on load", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.AC-C1 the edited table size round-trips through the schema-validated canonical project", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PlacementTests.AC-A6 a project carrying placement round-trips through the canonical JSON and passes schema validation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacementTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExportImportTests.a material entry outside the materialEntry definition is SchemaValidationErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExportImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectJson.schemaVersion", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectJson.ProjectJsonText", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectJson.ProjectJsonText.value", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectJson.ProjectJsonText.parseProject", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectJson.serializeProject", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validate", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project.OpticalConstructorProject", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project.schemaDefAnchors", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"], "preserves_obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.MaterialLibrary.validateEntryElement", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S44-PROJECT-CODEC"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.4 -- The .ocproj aggregate is deleted"}
{"number": 161, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.4e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [160], "how_to": "Nothing under `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` names `.ocproj` any more (001 §T 'From section 4: `git grep -n -i -F \"ocproj\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` finds nothing'; the S4.4 brief). Comments, schema descriptions and test literals only; no behaviour changes. (1) The groups file: `OpticalConstructor.Storage/GroupsLibrary.fs`'s module doc (`GroupsLibrary.fs:13-25`) becomes one to three lines: the per-user groups and experiment-collections file, read and written through the shared options and validated on load through `validateWith`, a `schemaVersion` mismatch being `SchemaValidationErr`. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Groups.fs`' `GroupsLibrary` doc (`Groups.fs:180-182`) loses its clause 'it is kept apart from any per-project `.ocproj`'. `schema/optical-constructor-groups.schema.json`'s `description` (`:5`) loses 'kept apart from any per-project .ocproj,'; nothing else in the schema changes. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/GroupsRoundTripTests.fs`' doc (`GroupsRoundTripTests.fs:20`) loses 'independent of any `.ocproj`;'. (2) The environment file's two old-file facts, `an old environment.json carrying a recentFiles array still loads, field ignored, no migration` and `load reads an old on-disk environment.json with a recentFiles array without falling back to defaults` (`EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs:383`, `:395`), graft `[ \"C:/kits/a\", \"C:/kits/b\" ]` and `[ \"C:/kits/a\" ]` for their `.ocproj` names; their assertions are unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs` and `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` are in scope because steps 151 and 152 rewrote their `.ocproj` wording (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj:141-155` today): a comment line of them that still names `.ocproj` loses those words and keeps what stays true, gaining none (AGENTS.md). (4) `.gitignore`: the `*.binz` comment (`.gitignore:336-338`) drops its last sentence, 'Canonical `.ocproj` project files remain committable.', because the sidecars stay (`Sidecar.fs:Sidecar`) and no project file exists; the rule is unchanged. Afterwards `git grep -n -i -F \"ocproj\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` finds nothing, which S5.1 onward asserts as an invariant.", "acceptance": "After the last `.ocproj` wording goes, `git grep -n -i -F \"ocproj\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/` MUST find nothing and `.gitignore` MUST still ignore `*.binz`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an old environment.json carrying a recentFiles array still loads, field ignored, no migration` and `load reads an old on-disk environment.json with a recentFiles array without falling back to defaults` over their new literals and every GroupsRoundTripTests fact, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/GroupsLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Groups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/optical-constructor-groups.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", ".gitignore", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/GroupsRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EnvironmentRoundTripTests.an old environment.json carrying a recentFiles array still loads, field ignored, no migration", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-NO-OCPROJ"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EnvironmentRoundTripTests.load reads an old on-disk environment.json with a recentFiles array without falling back to defaults", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs", "obligations": ["S44-NO-OCPROJ"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S4.4 -- The .ocproj aggregate is deleted"}
{"number": 162, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.1a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [161], "how_to": "The history's cap is a setting of its own (001 §F 'up to `KitHistoryLimit` = 100 folders (`appsettings.json`)'; the S5.1 brief: KitHistoryLimit = 100, carried in WorkbenchSettings; .spec-md §8: the only configuration knobs are the 001 §G locations and `KitHistoryLimit`). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`, module `WorkbenchSettings`: (1) `WorkbenchSettingsError` (`WorkbenchSettings.fs:15-18`) gains `NonPositiveKitHistoryLimitErr of value : int` as its last case; its doc stops counting the settings it guards ('All three thresholds' becomes words true of every one: each is a count or a cap). (2) After `ThicknessBucketCap` (`WorkbenchSettings.fs:73-81`), `KitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit of int`, written as `ThicknessBucketCap` is: `member this.value`, `static member defaultValue : KitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit 100`, and `static member tryCreate (v : int) : Result<KitHistoryLimit, WorkbenchSettingsError>` answering `KitHistoryLimit v` for a positive `v` and `NonPositiveKitHistoryLimitErr v` otherwise. Its doc is one to three lines: the most kits the kit history keeps; over it the oldest unstarred kit is dropped and a starred one never is (001 §F, spec 0050 S5.1). The `WorkbenchSettings` record is unchanged in this step; step 163 carries the limit. No other type, case or member is added. Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs`: `KitHistoryLimit accepts a positive count, defaults to 100 and refuses a non-positive count with the typed error carrying the value`: `KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate` of 1, 100 and 5000 answers each value, `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue.value` is 100, and 0 and -1 answer `NonPositiveKitHistoryLimitErr` carrying the value.", "acceptance": "After the limit lands, `KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate` MUST accept a positive count and refuse any other with `NonPositiveKitHistoryLimitErr` carrying it, and `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue` MUST be 100; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `KitHistoryLimit accepts a positive count, defaults to 100 and refuses a non-positive count with the typed error carrying the value`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests.KitHistoryLimit accepts a positive count, defaults to 100 and refuses a non-positive count with the typed error carrying the value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-LIMIT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.WorkbenchSettings.KitHistoryLimit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "obligations": ["S51-LIMIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.WorkbenchSettings.WorkbenchSettingsError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S51-LIMIT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 163, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.1b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [162], "how_to": "The app reads the limit from `appsettings.json` and carries it in the workbench settings (001 §F 'up to `KitHistoryLimit` = 100 folders (`appsettings.json`)'; 001 §G 'Every path is overridable in appsettings.json'; the S5.1 brief: a ConfigKey in AppConfig.fs with a settings door, carried in WorkbenchSettings). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`: the `WorkbenchSettings` record (`WorkbenchSettings.fs:87-93`) gains `kitHistoryLimit : KitHistoryLimit` (step 162) as its last field, and `defaults` (`:95-101`) gains `kitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`; the record's doc adds the kit history limit's 100 to the built-in values it says are written once here. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`. (a) Module `ConfigKey` gains `[<Literal>] let kitHistoryLimit = \"KitHistoryLimit\"` after `thicknessBucketCap`, its doc one line: the appSettings int of 001 §F, the most kits the history keeps, default 100 (`KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`). (b) Module `WorkbenchSettingsDoors` (`AppConfig.fs:64-109`): the three count doors (`QuickPickThreshold`, `TreeAutoBuildThreshold`, `ThicknessBucketCap`) repeat one body today: an invariant-culture `Int32.TryParse`, the type's own int `tryCreate`, and the refusals `not a positive count: '<text>'` and `not a whole number: '<text>'`. That body moves to ONE private extension member of STL's `AppSettings.ConfigValue` declared in this module, `member private this.tryPositiveCount (create : int -> Result<'Setting, WorkbenchSettingsError>) : Result<'Setting, string>`, and the three doors call it, their answers and texts unchanged. `type KitHistoryLimit with` gains the same door: `static member tryCreate (v : AppSettings.ConfigValue) : Result<KitHistoryLimit, string>` through `tryPositiveCount`, and `member this.configValue : AppSettings.ConfigValue` rendering the count as the other doors do. The shared member is private, so it adds no public signature mixing our types with primitives (ELEV010), and no fourth copy of the body is written (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). (c) `AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings` (`AppConfig.fs:136`) builds the record with `kitHistoryLimit = readSetting provider (AppSettings.ConfigKey ConfigKey.kitHistoryLimit) defaults.kitHistoryLimit KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate _.configValue` beside the other keys, so a missing or refused key is logged and written back as 100 by `readSetting` (`AppConfig.fs:117`), and it is saved with them once. A doc that counts the keys it reads stops counting them. The limit's reader is `KitHistory.bump` (step 169), which takes it as a parameter. (3) Census only: the record's other consumers, `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs` and the Ui.Tests files `AppContextTests.fs`, `LauncherTests.fs`, `TableAndElementRotationTests.fs`, `WindowLauncherTests.fs`, `WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs`, `WireUiCompositionTests.fs`, `WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`, read the record or its `defaults` and build no literal of it, so nothing in them changes; they are in scope so the shape change covers its whole census. Every reader a later step added (`TestAppScope.fs`, step 83) is likewise unchanged. (4) Tests. In `OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs`, `defaults equals the record constructed directly from the per-type defaults` (`WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs:22-30`) builds its record with `kitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, and `a settings record assembled from validated values carries the validated thresholds` (`:96-116`) with `kitHistoryLimit = KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate 250 |> okOr KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue` and asserts 250; `the default settings carry a kit history limit of 100` is added: `WorkbenchSettings.defaults.kitHistoryLimit` is `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, whose value is 100. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs` (step 82), `the count doors read a positive whole number and refuse anything else, the kit history limit's included`: with `OpticalConstructor.App` open, `KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate (AppSettings.ConfigValue \"250\")` answers a limit of 250 whose `configValue` is `\"250\"`; `\"0\"` answers `Error \"not a positive count: '0'\"` and `\"ten\"` answers `Error \"not a whole number: 'ten'\"`; and `QuickPickThreshold.tryCreate`, `TreeAutoBuildThreshold.tryCreate` and `ThicknessBucketCap.tryCreate` of `\"0\"` and of `\"ten\"` answer those same two texts, so the one body serves all four doors.", "acceptance": "After the limit is read from `appsettings.json`, `WorkbenchSettings.defaults.kitHistoryLimit` MUST be 100, `AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings` MUST read the `KitHistoryLimit` key through its door, and the four count doors MUST share one parse body; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the default settings carry a kit history limit of 100`, `defaults equals the record constructed directly from the per-type defaults` and `a settings record assembled from validated values carries the validated thresholds`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the count doors read a positive whole number and refuse anything else, the kit history limit's included`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WindowLauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests.the default settings carry a kit history limit of 100", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests.defaults equals the record constructed directly from the per-type defaults", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S51-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests.a settings record assembled from validated values carries the validated thresholds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S51-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests.the count doors read a positive whole number and refuse anything else, the kit history limit's included", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppConfigTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S51-SETTINGS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.WorkbenchSettings.WorkbenchSettings", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S51-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.ConfigKey.kitHistoryLimit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "obligations": ["S51-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.WorkbenchSettingsDoors.KitHistoryLimit.tryCreate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs", "obligations": ["S51-SETTINGS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 164, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.1c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [163], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests"], "how_to": "The kit history as pure Domain data, with its star rules, its eviction and its display order (001 §F 'History': starred kits always at the top, sorted by last open date, then the rest sorted the same way; the cap evicts the oldest UNSTARRED entry and never a starred one; 'Storage': an entry is the folder, kit id, name cache, last opened and `Starred | NotStarred`; .spec-md §3.17: the cases are `StarredKit` / `UnstarredKit`). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs`: `module KitHistory` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `KitFolders.fs` (step 125): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `Kit` (step 122: `KitFolder`, `KitName`, `ClockTime`), `LibraryEntryFiles` (step 24: `KitId`, `FileSchemaVersion`) and `WorkbenchSettings` (`KitHistoryLimit`, step 162). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.1. In this order: (1) `KitStar` = `StarredKit` | `UnstarredKit`, whether the user starred a kit in the history. `member this.value : int` answers 1 and 2, its disk tag, and `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : KitStar option` answers `None` for any other tag (AGENTS.md: a closed set's tag is an int). (2) `KitHistoryEntry = { folder : KitFolder; kitId : KitId; name : KitName; lastOpened : ClockTime; star : KitStar }`, one kit in the history: `name` is the kit's name when it was last opened, kept so a row renders without opening the kit, and `lastOpened` is read from the injected clock (step 169). (3) `KitHistory = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; entries : KitHistoryEntry list }`, the whole history, `entries` held newest open first. `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` is 1 and `static member empty : KitHistory` holds it and no entry. A kit is identified by its folder, compared as today's MRU rule compares paths (`RecentFiles.fs:RecentFiles.bump`: `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` over the text); that comparison is written once, as a private member of `KitHistory`, and no public member answers a `bool` (ELEV010). (4) Members of `KitHistory`, each answering a new history and changing nothing else: `star (folder : KitFolder)` and `unstar (folder : KitFolder)` set the matching entry's `star` to `StarredKit` / `UnstarredKit`, keeping its place, time and other fields; `forget (folder : KitFolder)` removes the matching entry, starred or not (S5.2's Remove from history; .spec-md §10.5: the folder itself is untouched); a folder the history does not hold leaves it equal. `evict (limit : KitHistoryLimit)` drops unstarred entries, the one with the earliest `lastOpened` first and, among equal times, the one later in `entries` first, until the history holds at most `limit.value` entries or no unstarred entry is left; a starred entry is never dropped, so a history holding more stars than the limit keeps them all, and the survivors keep their order. `displayOrder : KitHistoryEntry list` lists the starred entries, then the unstarred ones, each group by `lastOpened` newest first, equal times keeping their order in `entries`. Star, unstar and forget never evict. No cache, `bool` flag, sort option or other member is added; `bump` arrives in step 169, the step that moves it. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs`, `module KitHistoryTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its fixture entries are built directly: kit `x` is the folder `C:/kits/x`, a fixed GUID `KitId`, the name `Kit x`, and a `lastOpened` given as minutes after `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)`. `a kit star round-trips its wire tag`: `StarredKit.value` is 1 and `UnstarredKit.value` is 2, `tryOfWire` is their inverse, and 0 and 3 answer `None`. The history `mixed` holds, in this stored order, unstarred `a` (12:05), starred `b` (12:01), unstarred `c` (12:09), starred `d` (12:07) and unstarred `e` (12:05). `starred kits are listed first, each group newest open first`: `mixed.displayOrder` is `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e`. `star and unstar change only the named kit, matching its folder in any case`: `star` of `C:/KITS/A` stars `a` and leaves every other entry, the stored order and every time unchanged; `unstar` of `C:/kits/a` on that answers `mixed` again; `star` of `C:/kits/zz` answers `mixed` unchanged. `forget removes only the named kit, starred or not`: `forget` of `C:/Kits/B` (starred) and then of `C:/kits/c` (unstarred) leaves `a`, `d` and `e` in their order; `forget` of `C:/kits/zz` answers `mixed` unchanged. `evict drops the oldest unstarred kits down to the limit`: `evict (KitHistoryLimit 4)` of `mixed` drops `e` alone (the later of the two oldest unstarred), `evict (KitHistoryLimit 3)` drops `e` and `a`, leaving `b`, `c`, `d` in their order, and `evict (KitHistoryLimit 5)` answers `mixed` unchanged. `evict never drops a starred kit, even over the limit`: over starred `b`, unstarred `c` and starred `d`, `evict (KitHistoryLimit 1)` drops `c` alone and keeps both stars, two entries over the limit; over `b` and `d` alone it drops nothing.", "acceptance": "After the history model lands, `KitHistory.displayOrder` MUST list the starred kits first and each group newest open first, and `KitHistory.evict` MUST drop only the oldest unstarred kits down to the limit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit star round-trips its wire tag`, `starred kits are listed first, each group newest open first`, `star and unstar change only the named kit, matching its folder in any case`, `forget removes only the named kit, starred or not`, `evict drops the oldest unstarred kits down to the limit` and `evict never drops a starred kit, even over the limit`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.a kit star round-trips its wire tag", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.starred kits are listed first, each group newest open first", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.star and unstar change only the named kit, matching its folder in any case", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.forget removes only the named kit, starred or not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.evict drops the oldest unstarred kits down to the limit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.evict never drops a starred kit, even over the limit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitStar", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistoryEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S51-MODEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 165, "anchor": "ADD_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S5.1d", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0005", "name": "KitHistoryProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [164], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests"], "how_to": "The history's seam in Domain: its record and its in-memory double (001 §P '`KitHistoryProxy` (preferences)' and 'every proxy has an in-memory stub of the same shape'; 001 §F 'a missing folder shows greyed'; the S5.1 brief: a record and an in-memory implementation in Domain, and a 'folder exists' probe feeding the missing state; .spec-md §4, §5 `KitHistoryProxy`). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs`, after `KitHistory` (step 164), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.1: (1) `KitFolderPresence` = `KitFolderPresent` | `KitFolderMissing`, whether a history entry's folder is on disk now; it is never stored, so it has no tag. (2) `KitHistoryError` = `KitHistoryWriteErr of reason : string` (the history could not be written; the reason names the file or folder and the cause), with `member this.describe : string` rendering `the kit history could not be written: <reason>`, a fixed phrase, a colon and the reason (step 39's form). (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitHistoryProxy = { readHistory : unit -> KitHistory; writeHistory : KitHistory -> Result<unit, KitHistoryError>; probeFolder : KitFolder -> KitFolderPresence }`, the functional-proxy convention of `ElementId.fs:583` (`SourceProxy`), built once at the composition root. Each field has a one-line doc: `readHistory` answers the stored history, and the empty history when none is stored or it cannot be read, so it never fails; `writeHistory` replaces the stored history whole; `probeFolder` answers whether a folder exists now, which a history row shows as its missing state. (4) `type KitHistoryProxy with static member createInMemory (presentFolders : KitFolder list) : KitHistoryProxy`, the double (.spec-md §4): it starts holding `KitHistory.empty`; `writeHistory` keeps the given history and answers `Ok ()`; `readHistory` answers the last one kept; `probeFolder` answers `KitFolderPresent` for a folder equal to one of `presentFolders` and `KitFolderMissing` for any other. Its state is private to its closure and mutated only there, as `SourceProxy.createInMemory` (`ElementId.fs:1101`) keeps its store. No cache, retry, verb or other field is added: reading the history, changing it through step 164's members and writing it back is the caller's sequence. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests` (test code is outside the ELEV scope). `[<AbstractClass>] type KitHistoryProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshHistory : unit -> KitHistoryProxy` (a store holding no history, whose probe sees `presentFolder`), `abstract presentFolder : KitFolder` (a folder that exists) and `abstract missingFolder : KitFolder` (one that does not), each with a one-line doc, and holds the contract facts over a test-local two-entry history (`C:/kits/a` starred, `C:/kits/b` unstarred, fixed GUIDs, names `Kit a` and `Kit b`, and instants after `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)` carrying ticks): `a new history store reads the empty history`: `readHistory ()` answers `KitHistory.empty`. `a written history is read back equal`: `writeHistory` of the two-entry history answers `Ok ()` and `readHistory ()` answers it equal. `writing replaces the whole history`: after the two-entry history, writing a one-entry history makes `readHistory ()` answer the one-entry history. `the folder probe answers present for a folder that exists and missing for one that does not`: `probeFolder presentFolder` answers `KitFolderPresent` and `probeFolder missingFolder` answers `KitFolderMissing`. `type KitHistoryProxyTests () = inherit KitHistoryProxyContract ()` answers `KitHistoryProxy.createInMemory [ presentFolder ]`, with `presentFolder` = `KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/in-memory/kits/present\")` and `missingFolder` = `KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/in-memory/kits/missing\")`. `KitHistoryTests` (step 164) gains `a kit history error renders its condition and its reason`: `KitHistoryWriteErr` of a test-local reason renders a text that contains that reason.", "acceptance": "After the seam lands, `KitHistory.fs` MUST declare `KitHistoryProxy` with exactly `readHistory`, `writeHistory` and `probeFolder`, and `KitHistoryProxy.createInMemory`, and `KitHistoryProxyContract` MUST hold the store facts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a new history store reads the empty history`, `a written history is read back equal`, `writing replaces the whole history` and `the folder probe answers present for a folder that exists and missing for one that does not` under `KitHistoryProxyTests`, and `a kit history error renders its condition and its reason`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests.a new history store reads the empty history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests.a written history is read back equal", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests.writing replaces the whole history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests.the folder probe answers present for a folder that exists and missing for one that does not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.a kit history error renders its condition and its reason", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistoryProxy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitFolderPresence", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistoryError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S51-PROXY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 166, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.1e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [165], "how_to": "The history file stores a star as its int tag (AGENTS.md: 'A closed set's wire/disk tag is an integer'; .spec-md §4 'Shapes'; step 28's rule for the options). `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`: `CanonicalJson.options` gains one converter for `KitStar` (step 164), written as step 28's four are and registered with them before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: it writes the case's `value` and reads through `KitStar.tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. No other union changes its form and nothing else in the options changes. Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs` (step 28): `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also covers `KitStar`: `StarredKit` serializes as `1` and `UnstarredKit` as `2`, and each reads back equal; `an unknown disk tag is refused` also reads `3` as a `KitStar` and expects `JsonException`.", "acceptance": "After the converter lands, a `KitStar` MUST be written as its int tag and an unknown tag MUST be refused; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused` over `KitStar`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S51-STAR-TAG"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S51-STAR-TAG"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 167, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.1f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [166], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryJsonTests"], "how_to": "The history file is canonical JSON, validated against its own schema on read, a version mismatch a typed error (001 §F 'Storage'; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats', §6 'JSON + schema'). It reuses step 124's stack and adds no second parser. (1) The schema: new `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit-history.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/kit.schema.json` (step 124), with `$id` `https://berreman/schema/kit-history.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1 (`then`): the keys are `schemaVersion` and `entries` and no other (`additionalProperties: false`); `entries` is an array of objects, each with exactly `folder` (a non-empty string), `kitId` (the GUID string of `library-common.schema.json`, step 30, referenced by its `$id`), `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\\S`), `lastOpened` (a string) and `star` (the integer 1 or 2). A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/kit.schema.json`'s item in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateKitHistory (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith` (step 29), its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateKitFile` does (step 124). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitHistoryStore.fs`, `module KitHistoryStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `KitContentFiles.fs` (step 146): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.1. (a) `KitHistoryText of string` with `.value`, the text of the history file. (b) `type KitHistory with static member fileName : FileName` is `FileName \"kit-history.json\"`, the one place that name is written (the S5.1 brief), and `member this.fileText : Result<KitHistoryText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` (step 27) rendered by `canonicalFileText` (step 124): indented canonical JSON with sorted keys, LF line ends and one final `\\n`, each instant in the serializer's ISO 8601 form and each star as its tag (step 166). (c) `type KitHistoryText with member this.parseKitHistory : Result<KitHistory, StorageError>` is `parseVersionedText validateKitHistory (FileExtension \".json\") KitHistory.currentSchemaVersion this.value` (step 124), `.json` being the history file's extension. There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryJsonTests.fs`, `module KitHistoryJsonTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its history holds, first, the starred `C:/kits/Optics QZ — µ` named `Optics QZ — µ`, opened at `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc).AddTicks 1234567L`, and then the unstarred `D:/lab/Bench 2` named `Bench 2`, opened an hour earlier, each with a fixed GUID. `a kit history round-trips through its canonical text`: `fileText` then `parseKitHistory` answers an equal history; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists the top-level keys (`entries`, `schemaVersion`) and each entry's keys (`folder`, `kitId`, `lastOpened`, `name`, `star`) in ordinal order, keeps `µ` and `—` unescaped, and writes the first entry's `star` as `1` and its `lastOpened` as `2026-11-03T12:00:00.1234567Z`; writing the parsed history again gives the same text; and `KitHistory.empty` round-trips too. `a kit history of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` set to 2, both with its body intact and as `{ \"schemaVersion\": 2 }` alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = FileExtension \".json\"`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed kit history is refused before it binds`: the text with an entry lacking `folder`, with an entry carrying an extra key `colour`, with a `star` of 3, with a `kitId` of `not-a-guid`, with a `name` of `\"   \"` and with an extra top-level key `recent` each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; the text `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After the history text lands, `KitHistory.fileText` and `KitHistoryText.parseKitHistory` MUST round-trip a history through canonical JSON validated by `schema/kit-history.schema.json` and MUST refuse another schema version with `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit history round-trips through its canonical text`, `a kit history of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` and `a schema-invalid or malformed kit history is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit-history.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitHistoryStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryJsonTests.a kit history round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-TEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryJsonTests.a kit history of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-TEXT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed kit history is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-TEXT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitHistoryStore.KitHistoryText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitHistoryStore.fs", "obligations": ["S51-TEXT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitHistoryStore.KitHistory.fileText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitHistoryStore.fs", "obligations": ["S51-TEXT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitHistoryStore.KitHistoryText.parseKitHistory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitHistoryStore.fs", "obligations": ["S51-TEXT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateKitHistory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "obligations": ["S51-TEXT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 168, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S5.1g", "id": "STORE_BigBoy_0005", "name": "KitHistoryProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [165, 167], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests"], "how_to": "The history store over the per-user preferences folder (001 §F 'Storage': the history lives in the per-user preferences, `%APPDATA%\\Softellect\\Berreman\\OpticalConstructor\\`; 001 §G; the S5.1 brief: a Storage create over the DataLocations preferences folder, file kit-history.json, atomic write, and a missing or unreadable file gives an empty history and a logged warning; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO', 'Stored formats'). In `KitHistoryStore.fs` (step 167): `type KitHistoryProxy with static member create (preferences : FolderName) : KitHistoryProxy`, unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` (ELEV019). `preferences` is the composition root's `DataLocations.preferencesFolder` (step 81), passed in by the caller; the store reads no setting. Building it touches nothing. The file is `KitHistory.fileName` under `preferences`. `readHistory ()`: a missing file, a file whose bytes cannot be read, and a text `parseKitHistory` refuses each answer `KitHistory.empty` after one `Logger.logWarn` (`Softellect.Sys.Logging`, as `AppConfig.fs:125` logs) naming the file and the cause (the refusal's `describe`, or the exception's message); the bytes are decoded as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped, and a read never writes, moves or deletes the file. `writeHistory history` creates `preferences` when it is missing, renders `history.fileText` (step 167) and writes its UTF-8 bytes without a byte-order mark through `FileName.writeBytesAtomically` (step 126: `<file>.tmp`, then replace), so no reader sees half a history. A `StorageError` of the render or of the write is `KitHistoryWriteErr` naming the file and the error's `describe`; an IO exception at the folder is `KitHistoryWriteErr` naming the folder and the exception's message. `probeFolder folder` answers `KitFolderPresent` when `Directory.Exists` holds for the folder's text and `KitFolderMissing` otherwise. Every .NET IO exception is caught here, and nothing above the proxy handles one (.spec-md §4). No retry, cache, backup copy or import of `recent.json` is added (.spec-md §7: the kit history starts empty). The `KitHistoryProxy` doc in `KitHistory.fs` names `KitHistoryProxy.create` beside the in-memory double in one line. Tests, in `KitHistoryProxyTests.fs`: `type KitHistoryProxyFolderTests () = inherit KitHistoryProxyContract ()` runs every contract fact (step 165) over real folders under a root `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitHistoryProxyFolderTests\", <a new GUID>)` made per instance, never under `%TEMP%`, `%APPDATA%` or `Documents` (.spec-md §4 'Tests' data'): `freshHistory` is `KitHistoryProxy.create` over `<root>/Preferences`, which does not exist yet; `presentFolder` is `<root>/kits/present`, which the fixture creates; `missingFolder` is `<root>/kits/missing`, never created. Its own facts: `a history written by one store is read back by a new store over the same preferences folder`: a history written through one `create` is read equal through a NEW `create` over the same folder, the write having created the preferences folder, which then holds exactly `kit-history.json` and no `.tmp`. `a missing history file reads as the empty history and creates nothing`: `readHistory ()` over a preferences folder that does not exist answers `KitHistory.empty`, and the folder still does not exist. `an unreadable history file reads as the empty history and is left as it was`: a `kit-history.json` the test writes as `{`, as a valid history's `fileText` with `schemaVersion` set to 2, and as a valid history's `fileText` with a `star` of 3 each read as `KitHistory.empty`, never a throw, and each file keeps its bytes. `a write the preferences folder cannot take is KitHistoryWriteErr, never a throw`: with a FILE at `<root>/Preferences`, `writeHistory` answers `Error (KitHistoryWriteErr reason)` with `reason` naming that path, never a throw.", "acceptance": "After the store lands, a test MUST instantiate the real `KitHistoryProxy.create` over a preferences folder under the test output; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every `KitHistoryProxyContract` fact under `KitHistoryProxyFolderTests` and its own `a history written by one store is read back by a new store over the same preferences folder`, `a missing history file reads as the empty history and creates nothing`, `an unreadable history file reads as the empty history and is left as it was` and `a write the preferences folder cannot take is KitHistoryWriteErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitHistoryStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.a new history store reads the empty history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.a written history is read back equal", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.writing replaces the whole history", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.the folder probe answers present for a folder that exists and missing for one that does not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.a history written by one store is read back by a new store over the same preferences folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.a missing history file reads as the empty history and creates nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.an unreadable history file reads as the empty history and is left as it was", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.a write the preferences folder cannot take is KitHistoryWriteErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitHistoryStore.KitHistoryProxy.create", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitHistoryStore.fs", "obligations": ["S51-STORE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 169, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.1h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [168], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.HistoryTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests"], "how_to": "Opening a kit bumps the kit history, and the 16-entry `recent.json` list goes (001 §F 'Storage': the history replaces the 16-entry recent.json list, and the existing pure MRU logic `RecentFiles.bump` is REUSED and extended over a clock provider; 001 §R 'The 16-entry recent.json list, replaced by the kit history (bump reused)'; .spec-md §0.1, §6 'History MRU', §7: the kit history starts empty). (1) The move. `RecentFiles.bump` (`RecentFiles.fs:RecentFiles.bump`: drop any case-insensitive duplicate, put the new one first, truncate to `maxRecent`) moves into `KitHistory` (step 164) as `member this.bump (limit : KitHistoryLimit) (clock : ClockProvider) (folder : KitFolder) (kitFile : KitFile) : KitHistory`, generalised from file names to entries: the entry matching `folder` (step 164's folder identity) is removed; a new entry `{ folder = folder; kitId = kitFile.id; name = kitFile.name; lastOpened = clock.now (); star = <the removed entry's star, or UnstarredKit when there was none> }` is put first; then `evict limit` (step 164) runs where the truncation ran. The clock is read once. A reopened kit thus keeps its star and refreshes its folder text, id, name and time; the cap drops the oldest unstarred kit and never a star, the just-opened kit included when every other kit is starred, because the limit is the history's ceiling (001 §F 'up to `KitHistoryLimit`'). Its doc cites spec 0050 S5.1. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:35`): `bump` moved in (1), and `maxRecent`, `prefsPath`, `loadRecent` and `FileName.pushRecent` are superseded by step 168's store, which keeps `kit-history.json` where `recent.json` was; nothing in the product called them. The comment above that `<Compile>` line keeps only words true of the line that now follows it and loses every word about recent files; nothing is added. (3) The docs that point at the deleted store point at the kit history instead, in no more words: `OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs`' module doc (`UserEnvironment.fs:7-8`) and `EnvironmentSettings`' doc (`:227-228`) say that recently opened kits are kept by the kit history (`KitHistoryProxy`, spec 0050 S5.1), not here; `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs`' `sample` doc (`EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs:49-51`) and its old-file section comment (`:373-375`) say the same. No comment anywhere names the deleted module or its file, step 164's docs included. Neither file changes behaviour, and the old-environment facts keep their assertions. (4) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj:49`). Its one fact (step 159), `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent`, moves to `KitHistoryTests` as `bump puts the opened kit first, matches its folder in any case and evicts beyond the limit`, over a clock stepping one second per call and a kit file per folder (`KitFile.create`, step 122): bumping `C:\\kits\\b` onto a history holding `C:\\kits\\a` lists `b` then `a`; bumping `C:\\KITS\\A` then lists `C:\\KITS\\A` then `b`, with no duplicate; and twenty distinct `C:\\kits\\f<i>` bumped from `KitHistory.empty` under `KitHistoryLimit 16` leave 16 entries, headed by `f20` and ending with `f5`. `KitHistoryTests` also gains `bump keeps a reopened kit's star and refreshes its folder text, id, name and last open`: a starred `C:/kits/a` named `Old`, bumped as `C:/KITS/A` with a kit file of another id named `New`, is first, starred, named `New`, with the new id, the folder text `C:/KITS/A` and the clock's time, and no other entry of that folder is left. `a bump over the limit drops the oldest unstarred kit and keeps every star`: under `KitHistoryLimit 3`, a history of unstarred `u2` (12:03), unstarred `u1` (12:02) and starred `s` (12:01), bumped with a new `n`, holds `n`, `u2` and `s`: `u1` is dropped and the older star is kept. `a bump into a full starred history never drops a star`: under `KitHistoryLimit 3`, a history of three starred kits bumped with a new `n` equals those three starred kits unchanged, and bumping the last of them instead puts it first, still starred, with all three kept. Afterwards `git grep -n -F -e RecentFiles -e recent.json -e maxRecent -e pushRecent -e loadRecent -e prefsPath -- Berreman/` finds nothing, which S5.2 onward asserts.", "acceptance": "After `bump` moves into the kit history, `KitHistory.bump` MUST put the opened kit first with its star kept and evict the oldest unstarred kit over the limit, and `git grep -n -F -e RecentFiles -e recent.json -e maxRecent -e pushRecent -e loadRecent -e prefsPath -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `bump puts the opened kit first, matches its folder in any case and evicts beyond the limit` (moved from HistoryTests), `bump keeps a reopened kit's star and refreshes its folder text, id, name and last open`, `a bump over the limit drops the oldest unstarred kit and keeps every star` and `a bump into a full starred history never drops a star`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the thirteen s19 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "migrate", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.HistoryTests.R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.bump puts the opened kit first, matches its folder in any case and evicts beyond the limit", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.bump keeps a reopened kit's star and refreshes its folder text, id, name and last open", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.a bump over the limit drops the oldest unstarred kit and keeps every star", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.a bump into a full starred history never drops a star", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistory.bump", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.RecentFiles.bump", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"], "preserves_obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.RecentFiles.maxRecent", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"], "preserves_obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.RecentFiles.prefsPath", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"], "preserves_obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.RecentFiles.loadRecent", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"], "preserves_obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.RecentFiles.pushRecent", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S51-BUMP"], "preserves_obligations": ["S51-BUMP"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.1 -- The kit history over the per-user preferences"}
{"number": 170, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [169], "how_to": "The start screen lists the kit history in its display order, narrowed by a filter, each row carrying whether its folder is on disk (001 §F 'History': each row shows the name, folder, last-open date and the star; a filter box; a missing folder shows greyed; the S5.2 brief: the history list in S5.1's order, a filter box narrows it). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs` (steps 164, 165), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) Between `KitHistoryEntry` and `KitHistory`: `KitHistoryFilter = KitHistoryFilter of string` with `member this.value` and `static member none : KitHistoryFilter` = `KitHistoryFilter \"\"`, the text typed into the start screen's filter box. (2) `KitHistory` gains `member this.entriesMatching (filter : KitHistoryFilter) : KitHistoryEntry list`: `displayOrder` (step 164) keeping only the entries whose name or folder text contains the filter's text trimmed of white space, compared with `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`; a filter that is empty or white space keeps every entry, and the order is always `displayOrder`'s. (3) After `KitFolderPresence` (step 165): `KitHistoryRow = { entry : KitHistoryEntry; presence : KitFolderPresence }`, one row of the start screen's list. (4) `type KitHistory with member this.rowsMatching (filter : KitHistoryFilter) (probe : KitFolder -> KitFolderPresence) : KitHistoryRow list` answers `entriesMatching filter`, each entry paired with `probe entry.folder`, in that order. The probe is `KitHistoryProxy.probeFolder` where the screen lists its rows (step 176), so the history itself stays pure. No sort option, word splitting, cache or `bool` is added. Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs` over step 164's `mixed` history (stored order `a`, `b`, `c`, `d`, `e`; display order `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e`; kit `x` named `Kit x` in `C:/kits/x`): `entriesMatching keeps the kits whose name or folder holds the filter, ignoring case`: `KitHistoryFilter \"kit A\"` answers `a` alone (its name), `\"/C\"` answers `c` alone (its folder), `\"  KITS/  \"` answers all five in display order, and `\"zz\"` answers none. `a blank filter keeps the whole display order`: `KitHistoryFilter.none` and `KitHistoryFilter \"   \"` both answer `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e`. `rowsMatching pairs each listed kit with its folder's presence`: under a probe answering `KitFolderMissing` for `C:/kits/b` and `C:/kits/e` and `KitFolderPresent` for every other folder, `rowsMatching KitHistoryFilter.none` answers `d` present, `b` missing, `c` present, `a` present and `e` missing, and `rowsMatching (KitHistoryFilter \"Kit b\")` answers `b` missing alone.", "acceptance": "After the filter lands, `KitHistory.entriesMatching` MUST keep, in display order, exactly the kits whose name or folder holds the trimmed filter ignoring case, and `KitHistory.rowsMatching` MUST pair each with its folder's presence; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `entriesMatching keeps the kits whose name or folder holds the filter, ignoring case`, `a blank filter keeps the whole display order` and `rowsMatching pairs each listed kit with its folder's presence`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.entriesMatching keeps the kits whose name or folder holds the filter, ignoring case", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-FILTER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.a blank filter keeps the whole display order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-FILTER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.rowsMatching pairs each listed kit with its folder's presence", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-FILTER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistoryFilter", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S52-FILTER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistoryRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S52-FILTER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistory.entriesMatching", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S52-FILTER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistory.rowsMatching", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S52-FILTER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 171, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [170], "how_to": "Two history verbs the start screen needs (001 §F 'a missing folder shows greyed, with Locate… / Remove from history'; 001 §P StarKit, UnstarKit, ForgetKit; step 165: reading the history, changing it through its members and writing it back is the caller's sequence). In `KitHistory.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) `KitHistory` gains `member this.relocate (missing : KitFolder) (found : KitFolder) : KitHistory`, Locate…'s answer. The entry whose folder matches `missing` (step 164's folder identity, the one private comparison) takes `found` as its folder and keeps its kit id, name, last open, star and place; every other entry whose folder matches `found` is dropped, so a folder is listed once. A history that holds no entry of `missing` is answered unchanged. It touches no disk: the row's presence is probed when the screen lists it again (step 176). (2) After `KitHistoryProxy.createInMemory` (step 165): `type KitHistoryProxy with member this.changeHistory (change : KitHistory -> KitHistory) : Result<KitHistory, KitHistoryError>` reads the stored history (`readHistory ()`), applies `change`, writes the result (`writeHistory`) and answers it, or answers the write's error. So the read-change-write sequence is written once for every caller: step 176's star, unstar, forget and locate and step 177's bump. It is unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` and Storage's `create` (ELEV019). No retry, cache, lock or proxy field is added. Tests. `KitHistoryTests` (over `mixed`): `relocate moves a kit's entry to the found folder and keeps its star, name, time and place`: `relocate (KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/KITS/B\")) (KitFolder (FolderName \"D:/moved/b\"))` answers `mixed` with `b`'s folder `D:/moved/b`, still starred, named `Kit b`, opened at 12:01 and second in the stored order, every other entry unchanged. `relocate onto a folder the history holds keeps one entry for that folder`: relocating `C:/kits/a` to `C:/kits/c` answers `a`'s entry at `C:/kits/c` in `a`'s place and no other entry of `C:/kits/c`, four entries in all; relocating `C:/kits/zz` answers `mixed` unchanged. `KitHistoryProxyContract` (step 165) gains `changing the history writes the change and answers what was written`: after `writeHistory` of the contract's two-entry history, `changeHistory (fun h -> h.unstar (KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/kits/a\")))` answers `Ok` of that history with `a` unstarred, and `readHistory ()` answers the same; `KitHistoryProxyTests` and `KitHistoryProxyFolderTests` both run it. `KitHistoryProxyFolderTests` (step 168) gains `a change the preferences folder cannot take is KitHistoryWriteErr, never a throw`: with a FILE at `<root>/Preferences`, `changeHistory (fun h -> h.star (KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/kits/a\")))` answers `Error (KitHistoryWriteErr reason)` with `reason` naming that path, and the file keeps its bytes.", "acceptance": "After the two verbs land, `KitHistory.relocate` MUST move a kit's entry to the found folder keeping its star, name, time and place, and `KitHistoryProxy.changeHistory` MUST write the changed history and answer it or the write's error; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `relocate moves a kit's entry to the found folder and keeps its star, name, time and place` and `relocate onto a folder the history holds keeps one entry for that folder`, `changing the history writes the change and answers what was written` under `KitHistoryProxyTests` and `KitHistoryProxyFolderTests`, and `a change the preferences folder cannot take is KitHistoryWriteErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.relocate moves a kit's entry to the found folder and keeps its star, name, time and place", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-RELOCATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.relocate onto a folder the history holds keeps one entry for that folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-RELOCATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests.changing the history writes the change and answers what was written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-RELOCATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.changing the history writes the change and answers what was written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-RELOCATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests.a change the preferences folder cannot take is KitHistoryWriteErr, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-RELOCATE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistory.relocate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S52-RELOCATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitHistory.KitHistoryProxy.changeHistory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "obligations": ["S52-RELOCATE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 172, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [171], "how_to": "Open kit… opens a folder that is already a kit and never initialises one, so a folder without `.kit-json` can be offered 'Make this a kit' (001 §F 'Open kit…: a folder without .kit-json offers Make this a kit'; the S5.2 brief). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs` (step 150), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) What `openKitAt` does once its context is open (read `readExperiments ()` and `readSceneNames ()`, step 148; resolve `resolveSnapshots ()`, step 141; open `openOverlay []`, step 142; close the context on any failure, logging a failed close and answering the first error) moves unchanged into one private function `openedOver (context : KitContext) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : Result<OpenedKit, KitLibraryError>`, and `openKitAt` calls it after its open, so every answer of `openKitAt` is unchanged. (2) `openExistingKitAt (folder : KitFolder) (clock : ClockProvider) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : Result<OpenedKit, KitLibraryError>` opens `KitContext.openKit (KitProxy.create folder) ReadWriteKitAccess clock` (steps 126, 131), a `KitError` being `KitLibraryKitErr`, and then calls `openedOver`. A folder that holds no `.kit-json`, or does not exist, therefore answers `KitLibraryKitErr (NotAKitFolderErr _)` with nothing written (step 131: opening a folder that is not a kit writes nothing), and a kit open elsewhere answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr _)`. It takes no author, because it never makes a kit. No flag parameter is added to `openKitAt`: initialise-or-open and open-only are two functions over one body (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'). Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ KitOpeningTests.fs` (step 150), over folders under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitOpeningTests\", <a new GUID>)` with that class's clock, author and import context: `opening an existing kit opens it read-write with its kit file and never initialises a folder`: a folder made a kit by `openKitAt` read-write and closed answers, through `openExistingKitAt`, an opened kit whose context is read-write and holds that kit file, the folder holding `.oc/lock` until it is closed; a folder holding only `notes.txt` (written by the test) answers `KitLibraryKitErr (NotAKitFolderErr _)` and still holds exactly `notes.txt`; and a folder that does not exist answers the same error and still does not exist. `opening an existing kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr and writes nothing`: with the kit held open by an `openKitAt` of the fact, `openExistingKitAt` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr holder)` whose holder names this process, and every file of the folder keeps its bytes.", "acceptance": "After the open-only path lands, `KitOpening.openExistingKitAt` MUST open a kit read-write, answer `NotAKitFolderErr` for a folder that is not a kit and `KitLockedErr` for a kit open elsewhere, writing nothing in either case, and `openKitAt` MUST answer as before through the shared body; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening an existing kit opens it read-write with its kit file and never initialises a folder` and `opening an existing kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr and writes nothing`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening an existing kit opens it read-write with its kit file and never initialises a folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-EXISTING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening an existing kit open elsewhere is KitLockedErr and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-EXISTING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.openExistingKitAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-EXISTING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 173, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [172], "how_to": "The two texts a failed kit open shows get one home each, so the start screen and the launcher read the same words (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a re-transcribed constant is a defect; step 154's `The kit could not be opened: <e.describe>` and step 155's `The kit is open elsewhere: <holder.describe>.`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `KitError.caption` (step 135), each with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S5.2: `type KitLibraryError with member this.openFailedCaption : ControlCaption` is `ControlCaption $\"The kit could not be opened: {this.describe}\"`, and `type KitLockHolder with member this.openElsewhereCaption : ControlCaption` is `ControlCaption $\"The kit is open elsewhere: {this.describe}.\"`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow` (steps 154 to 156): wherever it writes `The kit could not be opened: <e.describe>` into `launcherKitErrorText` (step 154) or `The kit is open elsewhere: <holder.describe>.` above the Open read-only row (step 155), it renders `e.openFailedCaption.value` and `holder.openElsewhereCaption.value` instead, so both literals are deleted there and the launcher shows exactly what it showed. Nothing else changes. Tests: `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs` gains `the open captions name the error and the lock holder`: `(KitLibraryKitErr (NotAKitFolderErr \"C:/kits/x\")).openFailedCaption.value` is `The kit could not be opened: ` followed by that error's `describe`; and the holder of `UserName \"lab\"` on `MachineName \"BENCH-1\"`, process 4242, acquired at `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)` (step 129's fixture) renders `The kit is open elsewhere: lab on BENCH-1 (process 4242) since 2026-11-03 12:00:00 UTC.`. `LauncherTests`' facts of steps 154 to 156 keep their assertions.", "acceptance": "After the captions move, `KitLibraryError.openFailedCaption` and `KitLockHolder.openElsewhereCaption` MUST be the one home of the two open-failure texts and `LauncherWindow` MUST render them with no literal of its own; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the open captions name the error and the lock holder`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass, `LauncherTests`' facts of steps 154 to 156 included; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.the open captions name the error and the lock holder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-CAPTIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.KitLibraryError.openFailedCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-CAPTIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.KitLockHolder.openElsewhereCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-CAPTIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 174, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [173], "how_to": "How a picked folder reaches the code and how an opened kit reaches its window leave the launcher for the kit-opening module, so the start screen calls the same code (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; step 154: a click starts the picker on the UI thread with `Async.StartImmediate`, `None` doing nothing; step 156: resolution on open). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs` (step 150), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) `type KitFolderPicker with member this.pickThen (onPicked : KitFolder -> unit) : unit` starts `this.pickKitFolder ()` with `Async.StartImmediate` and calls `onPicked` with the chosen folder; `None` (the user cancelled) calls nothing. It is step 154's body, moved, and adds no posting, retry or exception handling, because `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow` already answers `None` when the dialog cannot open (step 150). It is unique on its receiver beside `ofWindow` (ELEV019). (2) `OpenedKit` (step 150) gains `member this.resolveAndShow (imports : CatalogueImportContext) (show : OpenedKit -> unit) (onFailed : KitLibraryError -> unit) : unit`, step 156's resolution on open, moved. When `this.pendingDecisions` is empty it calls `show this`. Otherwise it shows `ImportDialogWindow(imports, ResolveKitSnapshot (this.library, this.decisions), onApplied)` (steps 108, 144) and no constructor yet; `onApplied applied` calls `this.withRebindings applied.outcome.rebindings` (step 150): `Ok resolved` calls `show resolved`, and `Error e` closes the kit (`this.library.kit.close ()`, step 131) and calls `onFailed e`. When the dialog closes without an Apply (its `Closed` with no `onApplied` before it, tracked by one local flag at this IO edge), the kit is closed and nothing else is called, so a cancelled resolution leaves the kit unlocked and the library unchanged. A close that fails is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying its `describe`, as `openKitAt` logs one. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow`: Main's and Inverse's clicks become `(pickerFor this).pickThen` of step 154's local function for the folder, the mode and `ReadWriteKitAccess`, and that function's `Ok opened` arm becomes `opened.resolveAndShow context.catalogueImports <show the constructor window of the mode> <show e.openFailedCaption in launcherKitErrorText>`, as step 154's open failures are shown. The launcher's own `Async.StartImmediate`, dialog, flag and re-binding code are deleted, and it behaves exactly as before. Tests: `KitOpeningTests` gains `pickThen hands on the folder the picker answers and nothing on a cancel`: a picker answering `Some` of a test-local folder at once calls `onPicked` once with it, and one answering `None` never calls it. `LauncherTests`' facts of steps 154 to 156 (`the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`, `a cancelled pick opens nothing`, the read-only offer and the three resolution facts) keep their assertions and pass over the moved code. The moved resolveAndShow behavior MUST retain step 156's all-Reuse confirmation test: pendingDecisions includes every snapshot row, and only an actually empty snapshot list bypasses the dialog.", "acceptance": "After the pick and the hand-off move, `KitFolderPicker.pickThen` and `OpenedKit.resolveAndShow` MUST be the one home of the picker start and of resolution on open, and `LauncherWindow` MUST call them with no copy of its own; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `pickThen hands on the folder the picker answers and nothing on a cancel`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass, `LauncherTests`' facts of steps 154 to 156 included; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.pickThen hands on the folder the picker answers and nothing on a cancel", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-HAND-OFF"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.KitFolderPicker.pickThen", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HAND-OFF"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.OpenedKit.resolveAndShow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HAND-OFF"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 175, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [174], "how_to": "The app scope composes the kit history once, over the configured preferences folder (the S5.1 mapper's request, its interpretation 12: compose `KitHistoryProxy.create` over `locations.preferencesFolder` where the start screen's proxies are built; .spec-md §0.2: `KitHistoryProxy` is invoked from `AppContext.create` and the start screen; §3.9: every location comes from settings). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the record gains `kitHistory : KitHistoryProxy` as its last field, its doc one line: the kit history the start screen lists and bumps, in the per-user preferences (001 §F, spec 0050 S5.2). The private `compose` (steps 89, 100) sets it to `KitHistoryProxy.create locations.preferencesFolder` (step 168), so `create` and `recreateLibrary` both carry it, and building it touches nothing. No other field, option or cache is added, and the history's cap stays `settings.kitHistoryLimit` (step 163). Every test composition gets it through `TestAppScope` unchanged, over `testLocations`' `Preferences` folder under the test output (step 83). Tests: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs` gains `create composes the kit history over the configured preferences folder`: over `TestAppScope.fileLocations` of the module (step 88), `ctx.kitHistory.readHistory ()` answers `KitHistory.empty`; a one-entry history written through `ctx.kitHistory.writeHistory` answers `Ok ()`, the locations' `preferencesFolder` then holds `kit-history.json`, and a new `KitHistoryProxy.create` over that folder reads the history back equal.", "acceptance": "After the app scope carries the history, `AppContext.kitHistory` MUST be `KitHistoryProxy.create` over the configured preferences folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create composes the kit history over the configured preferences folder`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.create composes the kit history over the configured preferences folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-APP-HISTORY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.AppContext.kitHistory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "obligations": ["S52-APP-HISTORY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 176, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [175], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests"], "how_to": "The start screen's state and its history messages, as a pure Elmish update over injected seams (001 §F 'The history list'; 001 §P StarKit, UnstarKit, ForgetKit and 'every user step is a semantic message'; the S5.2 brief: the messages are pure updates over a start-screen model, with the history and kit proxies injected; .spec-md §4 'UI'). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView`, compiled directly after `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`, because it reads `ConstructorMode` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:246`): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and every type, case and field doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2. It follows `LibraryWindowView.fs`: a context record of injected seams (`LibraryWindowView.fs:LibraryWindowContext`), a model, messages and an update that reaches IO only through the context (`LibraryWindowView.fs:updateLibraryWindow`). (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitStartContext = { kitHistory : KitHistoryProxy; limit : KitHistoryLimit; clock : ClockProvider; author : KitAuthor; imports : CatalogueImportContext; picker : KitFolderPicker; showKit : OpenedKit -> unit }`: the kit history (step 165); its cap (step 162); the clock a bump reads; the author a new kit records (step 122); the library's import seam a kit's snapshot resolves against (step 94); the folder dialog of New kit…, Open kit… and Locate… (step 145); and the hand-off of an opened kit to the screen's window (step 179). This step's messages read `kitHistory` alone; step 177 reads the rest. (2) `KitStartOffer` = `NoKitStartOffer` | `MakeKitOffer of folder : KitFolder` (Open kit… met a folder without `.kit-json`) | `ReadOnlyKitOffer of folder : KitFolder * holder : KitLockHolder` (a kit open elsewhere, step 129): the question the screen asks after an open. (3) `KitRelocation = { missing : KitFolder; found : KitFolder }`: a missing kit's folder and the folder Locate… chose. (4) `KitStartModel = { context : KitStartContext; mode : ConstructorMode; history : KitHistory; filter : KitHistoryFilter; rows : KitHistoryRow list; offer : KitStartOffer; status : ControlCaption option }`: the constructor a chosen kit opens in (Main is `ForwardConstructor`, Inverse `InverseConstructor`); the history as last read or written; the filter's text; the listed rows, always `history.rowsMatching filter context.kitHistory.probeFolder` (step 170); the open question; and the last failure that needs telling. (5) `KitStartMsg`, in this step: `StarKit of KitFolder`, `UnstarKit of KitFolder`, `ForgetKit of KitFolder` (Remove from history), `LocateKit of KitRelocation` and `FilterKitHistory of KitHistoryFilter`; step 177 adds the open messages. (6) `initKitStart (context : KitStartContext) (mode : ConstructorMode) : KitStartModel` reads `context.kitHistory.readHistory ()` once and answers it with `KitHistoryFilter.none`, its rows, `NoKitStartOffer` and no status. (7) `updateKitStart (msg : KitStartMsg) (m : KitStartModel) : KitStartModel`: `StarKit f`, `UnstarKit f`, `ForgetKit f` and `LocateKit r` call `m.context.kitHistory.changeHistory` (step 171) with `star f`, `unstar f`, `forget f` and `relocate r.missing r.found` (steps 164, 171). `Ok history` answers the model holding that history, its rows recomputed and no status; `Error e` keeps the history and rows and sets `status` to `e.notSavedCaption`. `FilterKitHistory filter` holds the filter and recomputes the rows, writing nothing. Remove from history has no undo: the folder is untouched, and opening it again re-adds it (.spec-md §10.5). (8) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type KitHistoryError with member this.notSavedCaption : ControlCaption` is `ControlCaption $\"The kit history was not saved — {this.describe}\"`, with a one-line doc. No view, window, cache, undo history or other message is added here. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs`, `module KitStartTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its fixture context holds a given `KitHistoryProxy`, `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, a clock stepping one second per call from `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)`, `KitAuthor \"test\"`, an import context over the Built-in library (`BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`, step 94), a picker answering `None` and a `showKit` that records each kit it is given. Its history holds, in this stored order, unstarred `a` (12:05), starred `b` (12:01), unstarred `c` (12:09), starred `d` (12:07) and unstarred `e` (12:05), kit `x` named `Kit x` in `C:/kits/x` with a fixed GUID, written into `KitHistoryProxy.createInMemory` over the present folders `C:/kits/a`, `C:/kits/c`, `C:/kits/d` and `C:/kits/a2`. `the start screen opens on the history in display order, each row with its folder's presence`: `initKitStart` over that context and `ForwardConstructor` holds the stored history, `KitHistoryFilter.none`, rows `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e` with `b` and `e` missing, `NoKitStartOffer`, no status and the mode. `starring, unstarring and forgetting a kit write the history and re-list it`: `StarKit` of `C:/kits/a` lists rows `d`, `a`, `b`, `c`, `e` and `readHistory ()` holds `a` starred; `UnstarKit` of it lists `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e` again; `ForgetKit` of `C:/kits/b` removes `b` from the store and the rows. `locating a missing kit re-points its row and keeps its star`: `LocateKit { missing = C:/kits/b; found = C:/kits/a2 }` leaves `b`'s entry starred at `C:/kits/a2` and its row present. `the filter narrows the rows and writes nothing`: `FilterKitHistory (KitHistoryFilter \"kit c\")` lists `c` alone, `FilterKitHistory KitHistoryFilter.none` lists all five again, and `readHistory ()` is unchanged. `a history the store cannot write is shown and the rows are kept`: over a test-local proxy whose `writeHistory` answers `Error (KitHistoryWriteErr \"disk full\")`, `StarKit` keeps the rows and the history, sets a status containing `disk full`, and shows no kit.", "acceptance": "After the start screen's model lands, `initKitStart` MUST list the history's rows in display order with their presence and `updateKitStart` MUST write StarKit, UnstarKit, ForgetKit and LocateKit through `changeHistory`, re-list the rows and show a failed write, and narrow the rows on FilterKitHistory writing nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the start screen opens on the history in display order, each row with its folder's presence`, `starring, unstarring and forgetting a kit write the history and re-list it`, `locating a missing kit re-points its row and keeps its star`, `the filter narrows the rows and writes nothing` and `a history the store cannot write is shown and the rows are kept`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.the start screen opens on the history in display order, each row with its folder's presence", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.starring, unstarring and forgetting a kit write the history and re-list it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.locating a missing kit re-points its row and keeps its star", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.the filter narrows the rows and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a history the store cannot write is shown and the rows are kept", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartOffer", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitRelocation", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartMsg", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.initKitStart", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.updateKitStart", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.KitHistoryError.notSavedCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S52-HISTORY-MESSAGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 177, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [176], "how_to": "Choosing a kit opens it, bumps the history and hands it to the window; a question an open raises becomes an offer (001 §F 'New kit…: choose or create a folder. An empty folder is initialised; a folder that already has files keeps them'; 'Open kit…: a folder without .kit-json offers Make this a kit'; 'Choosing a kit opens the constructor in that mode'; 001 §E 'an open read-only choice'; 001 §P CreateKit, OpenKit; the S5.2 brief: choosing a kit bumps the history and opens the constructor window in the mode the screen was opened for; step 169: `KitHistory.bump` takes the limit, the clock, the folder and the kit file). In `KitStartView.fs` (step 176), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2: (1) `KitStartMsg` gains `CreateKit of KitFolder` (New kit… and Make this a kit), `OpenKit of KitFolder` (Open kit… and a history row), `OpenKitReadOnly of KitFolder` (the read-only offer's Open read-only, and how a test opens a committed kit, .spec-md §3.12), `DismissKitStartOffer` (an offer's Cancel) and `KitOpenFailed of KitLibraryError` (the window reports a kit whose resolution failed, step 179). (2) `updateKitStart`: `CreateKit folder` answers through `KitOpening.openKitAt folder ReadWriteKitAccess m.context.clock m.context.author m.context.imports` (step 150: a folder that holds no kit is initialised keeping every file it holds, a kit is opened); `OpenKit folder` through `KitOpening.openExistingKitAt folder m.context.clock m.context.imports` (step 172); `OpenKitReadOnly folder` through `openKitAt folder ReadOnlyKitAccess …`, which writes nothing to the kit. One private function of the folder, the answer and the model reads every answer, in this order. `Ok opened` bumps the history through `m.context.kitHistory.changeHistory (fun h -> h.bump m.context.limit m.context.clock folder opened.library.kit.kitFile)` (steps 169, 171), then calls `m.context.showKit opened` once, and answers no offer, the bumped history and its rows, and no status; when the bump answers `Error e` the kit is still handed over and `status` is `e.notSavedCaption`. `Error (KitLibraryKitErr (KitLockedErr holder))` answers `ReadOnlyKitOffer (folder, holder)` and no status; `Error (KitLibraryKitErr (NotAKitFolderErr _))` answers `MakeKitOffer folder` and no status; any other `Error e` answers `NoKitStartOffer` and `status` `e.openFailedCaption` (step 173). An error hands nothing over and bumps nothing. `DismissKitStartOffer` answers `NoKitStartOffer`, writing nothing, and `KitOpenFailed e` answers `NoKitStartOffer` and `status` `e.openFailedCaption`. A read-only open bumps the history too, because the user chose the kit. No retry, cache, confirmation or other message is added. Tests, in `KitStartTests` (step 176), over folders under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitStartTests\", <a new GUID>)` and an in-memory history whose present folders are the fact's folders; every kit the fixture's `showKit` recorded, and every kit a fact holds open itself, is closed at its end. `New kit initialises an empty folder, bumps the history and hands the kit over`: `CreateKit` of a folder named `Optics QZ` that does not exist records one shown kit, read-write, whose kit file is named `Optics QZ`; the folder holds `.kit-json`, `data` and `library`; the store's history holds one unstarred entry of that folder with the kit's id and name, opened at the clock's last answer; the rows list it; and no offer or status remains. `Open kit opens an existing kit and bumps it above the others`: over a history holding an older entry of another folder, `OpenKit` of a kit made by `openKitAt` and closed records one shown read-write kit, and the history's first entry is that kit's folder. `Open kit on a folder that is not a kit offers Make this a kit, and accepting it keeps the folder's files`: `OpenKit` of a folder holding `notes.txt` records nothing and answers `MakeKitOffer` of it, the folder still holding exactly `notes.txt`; `CreateKit` of it then records one shown kit, the folder holds `.kit-json`, `data`, `library` and `notes.txt`, and no offer remains; over a second such folder `DismissKitStartOffer` answers no offer and the folder still holds exactly `notes.txt`. `a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only, which opens it and writes nothing to the kit`: with the kit held open by an `openKitAt` of the fact, `OpenKit` records nothing and answers `ReadOnlyKitOffer` whose holder names this process; `OpenKitReadOnly` then records one shown kit whose context is read-only, every file of the folder keeps its bytes, and the history's first entry is the folder. `a kit that cannot be opened is shown and nothing is handed over or bumped`: a kit whose `E1.experiment-json` the test writes as `{` makes `OpenKit` record nothing, answer no offer and a status naming `E1.experiment-json`, leave the history unchanged and hold no `.oc/lock`. `a failed resolution reported by the window is shown`: `KitOpenFailed (KitLibraryKitErr (KitIoErr \"lost\"))` over a model holding a `MakeKitOffer` answers no offer and a status containing `lost`.", "acceptance": "After the open messages land, CreateKit MUST initialise or open a folder, OpenKit MUST open only a kit and offer Make this a kit for any other folder, a kit open elsewhere MUST be offered read-only, and every successful open MUST bump the history and hand the kit to `showKit` once while a failure hands nothing over; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `New kit initialises an empty folder, bumps the history and hands the kit over`, `Open kit opens an existing kit and bumps it above the others`, `Open kit on a folder that is not a kit offers Make this a kit, and accepting it keeps the folder's files`, `a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only, which opens it and writes nothing to the kit`, `a kit that cannot be opened is shown and nothing is handed over or bumped` and `a failed resolution reported by the window is shown`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.New kit initialises an empty folder, bumps the history and hands the kit over", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.Open kit opens an existing kit and bumps it above the others", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.Open kit on a folder that is not a kit offers Make this a kit, and accepting it keeps the folder's files", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only, which opens it and writes nothing to the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a kit that cannot be opened is shown and nothing is handed over or bumped", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a failed resolution reported by the window is shown", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartMsg", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.updateKitStart", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S52-OPEN-MESSAGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 178, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [177], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests"], "how_to": "The start screen's view: New kit…, Open kit…, the status, the offer, the filter box and the history list, every control under a stable id (001 §F 'Start-screen actions', 'History': each row shows the name, folder, last-open date and the star; a filter box; a missing folder shows greyed, with Locate… / Remove from history; 001 §O 'Automation': ids such as `KitHistoryList`, `KitHistoryStarToggle`, `NewKitButton`; .spec-md §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; AGENTS.md: never a wrapping `TextBlock` inside a horizontal `StackPanel`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588`), `// --- The kit start screen (KitStartView, KitStartWindow). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `newKitButton` (`\"NewKitButton\"`), `openKitButton` (`\"OpenKitButton\"`), `kitStartStatusText` (`\"KitStartStatusText\"`), `kitStartOfferText` (`\"KitStartOfferText\"`), `makeThisAKitButton` (`\"MakeThisAKitButton\"`), `openKitReadOnlyButton` (`\"OpenKitReadOnlyButton\"`), `cancelKitStartOfferButton` (`\"CancelKitStartOfferButton\"`), `kitHistoryFilter` (`\"KitHistoryFilter\"`), `kitHistoryList` (`\"KitHistoryList\"`); and, over a row's place in the list (`ConstructorUiPosition`, 0 first), `kitHistoryRow` (`KitHistoryRow_<n>`), `kitHistoryStarToggle` (`KitHistoryStarToggle_<n>`), `kitHistoryLocateButton` (`KitHistoryLocateButton_<n>`), `kitHistoryRemoveButton` (`KitHistoryRemoveButton_<n>`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type KitHistoryEntry with member this.lastOpenedCaption : ControlCaption` is `Last opened <yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm> UTC`, the time in the invariant culture as `KitLockHolder.describe` writes one (step 129); and `type KitFolder with member this.notAKitCaption : ControlCaption` is `<the folder's text> holds no kit.`. (3) `KitStartView.fs`: `kitStartView (m : KitStartModel) (dispatch : KitStartMsg -> unit) : IView`, a pure projection of the model. Its content scrolls as the material editor's does (`MaterialEditorView.fs:twoPane`: a `ScrollViewer` over a `MinWidthPanel`, `WindowLayout.fs:MinWidthPanel`), both scroll bars `Auto` and a minimum width of 520, over one vertical `StackPanel` holding, in order: (a) one row with `New kit…` (`newKitButton`) and `Open kit…` (`openKitButton`), each a `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (public since step 107, the shared look), whose presses call `m.context.picker.pickThen` (step 174) with `CreateKit >> dispatch` and `OpenKit >> dispatch`; (b) when `status` is `Some`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitStartStatusText` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`; (c) for `MakeKitOffer folder`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitStartOfferText` with `folder.notAKitCaption`, and under it one horizontal row of `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton`s: `Make this a kit` (`makeThisAKitButton`, `positiveBackground`, sending `CreateKit folder`) and `Cancel` (`cancelKitStartOfferButton`, `negativeBackground`, sending `DismissKitStartOffer`); for `ReadOnlyKitOffer (folder, holder)` the text is `holder.openElsewhereCaption` (step 173) and the pair is `Open read-only` (`openKitReadOnlyButton`, positive, sending `OpenKitReadOnly folder`) and `Cancel` (the same id and message, negative); the action box's right margin is the gap; (d) a `TextBox` carrying `kitHistoryFilter`, watermark `Filter kits by name or folder`, its text `m.filter.value`, sending `KitHistoryFilter >> FilterKitHistory` on each change (the `CategoryControls.fs:106` shape); (e) a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitHistoryList`, one row per item of `m.rows` at its position `n`: a `DockPanel` whose right side holds a `verbButton` carrying `kitHistoryStarToggle n`, labelled `★` for a starred kit (sending `UnstarKit`) and `☆` otherwise (sending `StarKit`), and, for a missing folder only, `Locate…` (`kitHistoryLocateButton n`, its press calling `m.context.picker.pickThen` with `fun found -> dispatch (LocateKit { missing = <the row's folder>; found = found })`) and `Remove from history` (`kitHistoryRemoveButton n`, sending `ForgetKit` of the row's folder); and whose fill is a `Border` carrying `kitHistoryRow n`, keyed by its id as `verbButton` keys its box, holding three `TextBlock`s: the kit's name (semi-bold), the folder's text (wrapping) and `lastOpenedCaption`. A present row's `Border` sends `OpenKit` of its folder when pressed; a missing row's `Border` has `Opacity` 0.5 and sends nothing, its two buttons staying at full opacity. Every press handler sets `e.Handled` as `verbButton` does, and every id is an AutomationId, never a `Name`, as `MaterialsWindowView.fs:verbButton`'s doc says of variable membership. (4) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs`, `module KitStartWindowTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its screens are mounted as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts a view: a `HostWindow` running `Program.mkSimple` over a model, `updateKitStart` and `kitStartView`, shown headless at 900 × 700. Its context holds an in-memory history holding `KitStartTests`' five entries (step 176) over the present folders `C:/kits/a`, `C:/kits/c` and `C:/kits/d`, an import context over `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`, a picker `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf` of the fact's folder (step 154) and a recording `showKit`; every kit it records is closed at the fact's end. Facts without a trait: `the kit start screen UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the nine fixed ids' texts, and the four positional ids' texts at positions 0 and 3. `the history rows show name, folder and last open in display order, each with its star`: the rows at positions 0 to 4 are `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e`, each `kitHistoryRow n` holding its name, its folder's text and its `lastOpenedCaption` (`Last opened 2026-11-03 12:07 UTC` for `d`), and `kitHistoryStarToggle n` reads `★` for `d` and `b` and `☆` for the rest. `a missing folder's row is greyed with Locate and Remove from history, and a present row offers neither`: rows 1 and 4 (`b`, `e`) have `Opacity` 0.5 and both `kitHistoryLocateButton n` and `kitHistoryRemoveButton n`; rows 0, 2 and 3 have `Opacity` 1 and neither. `each offer shows its text with its two buttons on one row, Cancel to the right`: over the model with `MakeKitOffer` of a test-local folder, `kitStartOfferText` reads its `notAKitCaption`, and `makeThisAKitButton` and `cancelKitStartOfferButton` have equal tops, Cancel's left beyond Make this a kit's right; over `ReadOnlyKitOffer` with step 173's holder the text is its `openElsewhereCaption`, and `openKitReadOnlyButton` and `cancelKitStartOfferButton` sit the same way. `typing into the filter box narrows the list`: setting `kitHistoryFilter`'s text to `kit c` leaves one row, `c`, and clearing it lists five. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing a row's star, its Remove from history and a present row sends StarKit, ForgetKit and OpenKit`: pressing `kitHistoryStarToggle 3` (`a`) stars `a` in the store and pressing the `kitHistoryRemoveButton` of `e`'s row removes `e`; and, over a screen whose history holds one entry of a kit the fact made through `openKitAt` and closed (its folder present), pressing `kitHistoryRow 0` records that kit shown once. `New kit and Open kit open the folder the picker answers`: over a screen whose picker answers a fresh folder, pressing `newKitButton` records one shown kit named for it; over one whose picker answers a folder holding only `notes.txt`, pressing `openKitButton` records nothing and shows `kitStartOfferText`.", "acceptance": "After the view lands, `kitStartView` MUST show New kit…, Open kit…, the status, the offer with its pair on one row, the filter box and one row per listed kit with its name, folder, last open and star, a missing folder's row greyed with Locate… and Remove from history, every control under its `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a row's star, its Remove from history and a present row sends StarKit, ForgetKit and OpenKit` and `New kit and Open kit open the folder the picker answers`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit start screen UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the history rows show name, folder and last open in display order, each with its star`, `a missing folder's row is greyed with Locate and Remove from history, and a present row offers neither`, `each offer shows its text with its two buttons on one row, Cancel to the right` and `typing into the filter box narrows the list`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.the kit start screen UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.the history rows show name, folder and last open in display order, each with its star", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.a missing folder's row is greyed with Locate and Remove from history, and a present row offers neither", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.each offer shows its text with its two buttons on one row, Cancel to the right", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.typing into the filter box narrows the list", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.pressing a row's star, its Remove from history and a present row sends StarKit, ForgetKit and OpenKit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.New kit and Open kit open the folder the picker answers", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.kitStartView", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.newKitButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.openKitButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitStartStatusText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitStartOfferText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.makeThisAKitButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.openKitReadOnlyButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.cancelKitStartOfferButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitHistoryFilter", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitHistoryList", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitHistoryRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitHistoryStarToggle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitHistoryLocateButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitHistoryRemoveButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.KitHistoryEntry.lastOpenedCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.KitFolder.notAKitCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S52-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 179, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.2j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [178], "how_to": "The start screen's window: it composes the screen's context from the app scope and hands an opened kit to the constructor of its mode, through the import dialog when the kit's snapshot needs a decision (001 §F 'Choosing a kit opens the constructor in that mode'; 001 §O: every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`; the S5.2 brief: a new window with its own view and window files in OpticalConstructor.Ui). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the start-screen group (step 178): `kitStartWindow` (`\"KitStartWindow\"`) with a one-line doc. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `AppContext.fs`, the list's last file, because it reads the app scope: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type KitStartWindow(context : AppContext, mode : ConstructorMode, pickerFor : TopLevel -> KitFolderPicker, showConstructor : ConstructorMode -> OpenedKit -> unit)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `LibraryWindow` does (`LibraryWindow.fs:LibraryWindow`); its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §F and spec 0050 S5.2. Its title is `Open a kit — Main` for `ForwardConstructor` and `Open a kit — Inverse` for `InverseConstructor`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.kitStartWindow`; it asks for 720 × 560 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`). It captures the Elmish dispatch from its init command as `LibraryWindow` does, and runs `Program.mkProgram` over `initKitStart`, `updateKitStart` and `kitStartView` (steps 176 to 178) with the context `{ kitHistory = context.kitHistory; limit = context.settings.kitHistoryLimit; clock = ClockProvider.system; author = KitAuthor Environment.UserName; imports = context.catalogueImports; picker = pickerFor this; showKit = <the hand-off> }` (steps 150, 154, 163, 175: the clock, the author and the picker the launcher's open composed). The hand-off of `opened` is `opened.resolveAndShow context.catalogueImports (fun shown -> showConstructor mode shown; this.Close ()) (fun e -> dispatch (KitOpenFailed e))` (step 174): a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first; a shown kit opens the constructor of the screen's mode and closes the screen; a failed re-binding is shown on the screen; and a cancelled dialog releases the kit and keeps the screen open. Closing the screen opens and closes nothing else. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the kit start screen leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"KitStart\"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:assertReachable`) over a `KitStartWindow` whose context is `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"ScrollExtentTests\")` with `kitHistory` replaced by an in-memory history holding forty entries (every fifth folder missing, every seventh kit starred), so the list is longer than the screen; its picker is `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf` of a fresh folder and `showConstructor` ignores its kit. (4) `KitStartWindowTests` (step 178) gains, over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitStartWindowTests\")` with `kitHistory` replaced by a fresh in-memory history, a `showConstructor` that records the mode and the kit, and pickers from `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf`; every recorded kit is closed at the fact's end. Without a trait, `the start screen's title names its mode and it carries its stable id`: the window over `ForwardConstructor` is titled `Open a kit — Main` and over `InverseConstructor` `Open a kit — Inverse`, and each carries `kitStartWindow` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: New kit opens the new kit in the constructor of the screen's mode, bumps the history and closes the screen`: over a fresh folder, pressing `newKitButton` on the Main screen records `ForwardConstructor` with a read-write kit named for the folder, closes the screen, and leaves the history's one entry that folder; the Inverse screen records `InverseConstructor` the same way.", "acceptance": "After the window lands, `KitStartWindow` MUST compose its context from the app scope, be titled by its mode, fit its screen, and hand an opened kit through `resolveAndShow` to the constructor of its mode, closing itself; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: New kit opens the new kit in the constructor of the screen's mode, bumps the history and closes the screen`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the start screen's title names its mode and it carries its stable id` and `the kit start screen leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit start screen leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.the start screen's title names its mode and it carries its stable id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S52-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.acceptance: New kit opens the new kit in the constructor of the screen's mode, bumps the history and closes the screen", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S52-WINDOW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S52-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitStartWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S52-WINDOW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 180, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S5.2k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [179], "how_to": "Both Launcher buttons, Main and Inverse, open the kit start screen, and the launcher's own kit opening goes (001 §F 'Both Launcher buttons, Main and Inverse, open the start screen'; 001 §O 'Launcher: Main / Inverse / Materials / Library. Main and Inverse open the kit start screen'; the S5.2 brief: Main and Inverse open the start screen instead of the picker, and Materials and Library are unchanged; .spec-md §4: superseded code is deleted in the change that replaces it). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`. (a) After `InverseConstructorWindow`, `module private KitConstructorWindows` holds `showConstructorIn (context : AppContext) (mode : ConstructorMode) (opened : OpenedKit) : unit`, showing `MainConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for `ForwardConstructor` and `InverseConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for `InverseConstructor`, step 154's mode match moved out of the launcher's local function; its doc is one line. (b) `LauncherWindow(locations, settings, opened, pickerFor)` keeps its signature (steps 88, 89, 112, 154). Main's click shows `KitStartWindow(context, ForwardConstructor, pickerFor, KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn context)` (step 179), and Inverse's the same with `InverseConstructor`; each click opens one start screen. The launcher's kit opening is deleted whole: step 154's local function of the folder, the mode and the access, the `launcherKitErrorText` block, step 155's holder line with its Open read-only / Cancel row, and their calls of `pickThen`, `resolveAndShow`, `openFailedCaption` and `openElsewhereCaption` (steps 173, 174), whose callers are now the start screen alone. Materials, Library, the library error, the Recreate library button and the pending-imports notice (steps 88, 89, 112) are unchanged, because they need no kit (001 §F). The docs of `LauncherWindow`, `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` say, in no more words, that Main and Inverse open the start screen and that a window works in the kit the start screen opened. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group: `launcherKitErrorText`, `launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton` and `launcherCancelKitOpenButton` (steps 154, 155) are deleted with their docs; the start screen's `kitStartStatusText`, `openKitReadOnlyButton` and `cancelKitStartOfferButton` (step 178) replace them. (3) Tests. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs`, each fact that clicked Main or Inverse to open a kit observes the one `KitStartWindow` the click opens (through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent`, as `clickAndObserve` does) and then presses the start screen's box that the old fact reached through the launcher, at its centre as `LauncherTests.fs:clickBorder` presses one; the launcher's picker (`fun _ -> TestAppScope.kitPickerOf …`, step 154) is the start screen's picker. `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene` and `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene`: the click opens exactly one `KitStartWindow`, titled `Open a kit — Main` (`Open a kit — Inverse`); pressing its `newKitButton` opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow` (`InverseConstructorWindow`), closes the start screen, and leaves `.kit-json` in the fresh folder. `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`: through the start screen's `openKitButton`, every assertion kept. `a cancelled pick opens nothing`: pressing `newKitButton` with a picker answering `None` opens no constructor window, creates no folder and keeps the start screen open. `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window` is renamed `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the start screen and opens no window`: pressing `openKitButton` shows `kitStartStatusText` naming `E1.experiment-json`, opens no constructor window and leaves no `.oc/lock`. `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing` and `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`: through `openKitButton`, the holder's line is `kitStartOfferText` and the pair `openKitReadOnlyButton` / `cancelKitStartOfferButton`, every assertion kept. `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`, `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit` and `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening`: through `openKitButton`, every assertion kept, and Cancel on the dialog keeps the start screen open. `Materials from the launcher then the constructor strip activates ONE single instance` and every Materials, Library, library-error, recreate and pending-import fact keep their code. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`: `the launcher and both constructor states render over ONE root-composed app scope` also shows, asserts and closes `KitStartWindow(ctx, ForwardConstructor, …)` and `KitStartWindow(ctx, InverseConstructor, …)` over the same context, with a picker of a fresh folder and a `showConstructor` that ignores its kit, so ui-smoke renders the screen in both modes. `WireUiCompositionTests` and `WireUi0040CompositionTests` build their constructor windows directly (step 154) and keep their code; `SmokeTests.fs` keeps its code, because `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` (`Program.fs:App`) builds the launcher as before. Afterwards `git grep -n -F -e launcherKitErrorText -e launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton -e launcherCancelKitOpenButton -- Berreman/` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the Launcher is re-wired, its Main and Inverse buttons MUST each open a `KitStartWindow` of their mode whose chosen kit opens the matching constructor window, Materials and Library MUST be unchanged, and `git grep -n -F -e launcherKitErrorText -e launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton -e launcherCancelKitOpenButton -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene`, `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene`, `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`, `a cancelled pick opens nothing`, `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the start screen and opens no window` (renamed from `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window`), `acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing`, `Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing`, `acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library`, `cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit`, `a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening` and `the launcher and both constructor states render over ONE root-composed app scope`, the count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a cancelled pick opens nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the start screen and opens no window", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: a kit open elsewhere offers Open read-only and Cancel in one row, and Open read-only opens it without writing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.Cancel on a kit open elsewhere opens nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first, and Apply opens the constructor over its library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.cancelling a kit's import dialog opens nothing and releases the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a kit whose snapshots the library holds byte for byte confirms every reuse row before opening", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests.the launcher and both constructor states render over ONE root-composed app scope", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.launcherKitErrorText", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.launcherOpenKitReadOnlyButton", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.launcherCancelKitOpenButton", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S52-LAUNCHER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.2 -- The kit start screen and the Launcher"}
{"number": 181, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [180], "how_to": "One spelling per kit folder, so the kit history and the one-window-per-kit rule (step 190) name a kit the same way (001 §E 'Concurrency: one window per kit'; 001 §F: the history holds one entry per folder; step 164: a kit is identified by its folder, compared ignoring case by one private member of `KitHistory`; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, on `KitFolder` (step 122) beside `tryKitPathOf` (step 132), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `member this.canonical : KitFolder` answers the folder's text with every backslash turned into `/`, every trailing `/` removed and the rest upper-cased (`ToUpperInvariant`), so the folder written `C:\\kits\\Optics QZ\\` and the folder written `c:/KITS/optics qz` answer one `KitFolder`. It touches no disk and resolves no relative path. It is a key, never a path to show or open: the history and the windows keep showing a folder as the user chose it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs`: the private folder comparison of `KitHistory` (step 164) compares the two folders' `canonical`s, and its `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` text comparison is deleted, so one rule decides when two folders are one kit. `star`, `unstar`, `forget`, `bump` (step 169) and `relocate` (step 171) keep their code and reach it through that member. No other member, cache or option is added. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs` (step 122) gains `two spellings of one kit folder share one canonical form`: the folders written `C:\\kits\\Optics QZ\\` (backslashes, a trailing one), `C:/kits/Optics QZ` and `c:/KITS/optics qz/` answer equal `canonical`s, each equal to `KitFolder (FolderName \"C:/KITS/OPTICS QZ\")`, and `C:/kits/Optics QY` answers another. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs` (step 164) gains `a kit is matched by its folder in any spelling`: over step 164's `mixed` history, `star` of the folder written `C:\\Kits\\A\\` stars `a` and leaves every other entry, the stored order and every time unchanged, and `forget` of `c:/kits/b/` removes `b` alone. Every earlier `KitHistoryTests` and `KitHistoryProxyTests` fact keeps its assertions.", "acceptance": "After the canonical form lands, `KitFolder.canonical` MUST answer one folder for every spelling of a path and `KitHistory` MUST match folders through it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `two spellings of one kit folder share one canonical form` and `a kit is matched by its folder in any spelling`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitHistory.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.two spellings of one kit folder share one canonical form", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-CANONICAL-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests.a kit is matched by its folder in any spelling", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitHistoryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitHistoryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-CANONICAL-FOLDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitFolder.canonical", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S53-CANONICAL-FOLDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 182, "anchor": "ADD_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S5.3b", "id": "SVC_BigBoy_0001", "name": "ExplorerProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [181], "actions": ["ADD_TEST ExplorerProxyTests"], "how_to": "The seam that shows a folder in Explorer, shared by the Kit menu's Show in Explorer and the Data locations window's Open folder (001 §O 'Kit menu: … Show in Explorer'; 001 §G 'a Launcher Data locations panel shows them, each with Open folder'; the S5.3 brief: Open folder opens Explorer through a seam tests substitute; .spec-md §4: every proxy has an in-memory implementation of the same shape). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`, after `KitFolderPicker` (step 145), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: (1) `ExplorerError` = `MissingFolderErr of reason : string` (the folder does not exist, so nothing is shown) | `ExplorerLaunchErr of reason : string` (the file browser could not be started), each case documented, with `member this.describe : string` rendering `the folder does not exist: <reason>` and `the folder could not be shown: <reason>` (step 39's form). (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ExplorerProxy = { showFolder : FolderName -> Result<unit, ExplorerError> }`, the functional-proxy convention `KitFolderPicker` follows: `showFolder` opens the folder in the system's file browser and answers at once, never waiting for the browser. Its doc and the field's are one line each. (3) `type ExplorerProxy with static member createInMemory (record : FolderName -> unit) : ExplorerProxy`, the test double: it hands every folder it is asked to show to `record` and answers `Ok ()`, starting nothing. The real proxy is step 183's. No folder creation, retry, existence check or other field is added here. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExplorerProxyTests.fs`, `module ExplorerProxyTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. `the in-memory explorer hands every folder it is asked to show to its recorder`: over a recorder appending to a test-local list, `showFolder` of `FolderName \"C:/kits/a\"` and then of `FolderName \"D:/data\"` answers `Ok ()` twice, and the list holds the two folders in that order. `every explorer error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text containing the reason.", "acceptance": "After the seam lands, `KitFolders.fs` MUST declare `ExplorerError`, `ExplorerProxy` with exactly `showFolder`, and `ExplorerProxy.createInMemory`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the in-memory explorer hands every folder it is asked to show to its recorder` and `every explorer error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExplorerProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExplorerProxyTests.the in-memory explorer hands every folder it is asked to show to its recorder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExplorerProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExplorerProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-EXPLORER-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExplorerProxyTests.every explorer error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExplorerProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExplorerProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-EXPLORER-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.ExplorerProxy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S53-EXPLORER-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.ExplorerError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S53-EXPLORER-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.ExplorerProxy.createInMemory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S53-EXPLORER-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 183, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S5.3c", "id": "SVC_BigBoy_0001", "name": "ExplorerProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [182], "how_to": "The real explorer, composed beside the app's other shell seams (step 150: `ClockProvider.system` and `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow` live in `KitOpening.fs`). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, beside `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `type ExplorerProxy with static member system : ExplorerProxy` (step 182). Its `showFolder folder` resolves the folder's text with `Path.GetFullPath`; a folder that does not exist (`Directory.Exists` answers false) answers `MissingFolderErr` naming it and starts nothing; otherwise it starts `explorer.exe` with the full path as its one argument (`ProcessStartInfo(\"explorer.exe\")`, the path added through `ArgumentList`, `UseShellExecute` false), disposes the returned `Process` at once and answers `Ok ()`. Any exception of the resolution or the start is `ExplorerLaunchErr` carrying its message. It is the IO edge, in the shape of `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow`: nothing above it handles an exception, and it creates no folder, because a location that does not exist yet is told, never made (001 §G). No wait for the browser, retry or fallback browser is added. Tests: `ExplorerProxyTests` (step 182) gains `the system explorer refuses a folder that does not exist and starts nothing`: `ExplorerProxy.system`'s `showFolder` of a GUID-named folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"ExplorerProxyTests\")` that the fact never creates answers `Error (MissingFolderErr _)` whose reason names that folder, and the folder still does not exist. No fact asks it to show a folder that exists, because that would open Explorer on the machine running the tests.", "acceptance": "After the real explorer lands, `ExplorerProxy.system` MUST refuse a missing folder with `MissingFolderErr` and start Explorer only for a folder that exists; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the system explorer refuses a folder that does not exist and starts nothing`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExplorerProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExplorerProxyTests.the system explorer refuses a folder that does not exist and starts nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExplorerProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExplorerProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-EXPLORER-SYSTEM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.ExplorerProxy.system", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S53-EXPLORER-SYSTEM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 184, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [183], "actions": ["ADD_TEST KitWindowModelTests", "ADD_TEST KitWindowTests"], "how_to": "The kit window shows its kit: an opened kit carries its folder, and the window's title names the kit, its folder, whether it is read-only and the constructor (001 §O 'the title shows the kit name and folder'; the S5.3 brief: read-only shows in the title; step 155: S5.3 adds the title marker). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit` (step 150) gains `folder : KitFolder` as its first field, documented in one line: the folder the kit was opened from. The private `openedOver` (step 172) takes `(folder : KitFolder)` first and sets it; `openKitAt` and `openExistingKitAt` pass the folder they opened; `withRebindings` keeps it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains, after `kit` (step 152), `kitFolderOpt : KitFolder option`, documented in one line: the kit's folder, `None` for the scratch kit of a scene that opened no folder. `initWith` sets it to `None`; `loadKit` (step 152) sets it to `Some opened.folder`. On the `type TableAndElementRotationModel with` extension that holds `loadKit`, each documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `member model.kitCaption : ControlCaption` is the kit's name (`model.kit.kitFile.name`), then ` (read-only)` when `model.kit.access` is `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, then ` — ` and the folder's text when `kitFolderOpt` is `Some`; and `member model.kitWindowTitle : ControlCaption` is `kitCaption`, ` — Optical Constructor — ` and `Main` for `ForwardConstructor` or `Inverse` for `InverseConstructor`, the words the launcher's buttons use. So a read-write kit `Optics QZ` in `C:/kits/Optics QZ` is titled `Optics QZ — C:/kits/Optics QZ — Optical Constructor — Main`; opened read-only, `Optics QZ (read-only) — C:/kits/Optics QZ — Optical Constructor — Main`; and the scratch kit `Scratch kit — Optical Constructor — Main`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (`Program.fs:71`): the view it runs sets `window.Title <- model.kitWindowTitle.value` and then answers `mainView model dispatch`, so the title follows the model on every change (a mode switch, step 186; a reload's new name, step 187). `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` delete their literal titles (`Program.fs:94`, `:112`), and their docs say the title names the kit. No title setting, format option or cache is added. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs` (step 150) gains `an opened kit carries the folder it was opened from`: `openKitAt` read-write and read-only and `openExistingKitAt` (step 172), over one folder each, answer an opened kit whose `folder` is that folder; each is closed at the end. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs`, `module KitWindowModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its folders are GUID-named under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitWindowModelTests\")`; a kit named `Optics QZ` is made in a folder of that name inside one through `KitOpening.openKitAt` read-write with `ClockProvider.system`, `KitAuthor \"test\"` and an import context over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 94), as `KitOpeningTests` makes its kits; a fact's model is `initMain ()` loaded with `loadKit` of the opened kit; every kit a fact opens is closed at its end. `the window title names the kit, its folder and the constructor`: the loaded model is titled `Optics QZ — <the folder's text> — Optical Constructor — Main`, and with `constructorMode = InverseConstructor` it ends `— Inverse`. `a kit opened read-only is marked in the title`: the kit closed and opened again with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` titles the model `Optics QZ (read-only) — <the folder's text> — Optical Constructor — Main`. `a scene that opened no folder is titled by its kit alone`: `initMain ()` is titled `Scratch kit — Optical Constructor — Main`. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs`, `module KitWindowTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, gains, without a trait, `a constructor window is titled by its kit`: `MainConstructorWindow(ctx, opened)` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitWindowTests\")` and `TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName \"KitWindowTests\") ctx.catalogueImports` (step 152), shown headless, is titled `<the kit's name> — <its folder's text> — Optical Constructor — Main`, and `InverseConstructorWindow` over a second such kit ends `— Inverse`; both windows are closed, which releases their kits (step 154). Every other fact that builds a constructor window keeps its code and its assertions.", "acceptance": "After the title lands, `OpenedKit.folder` MUST name the folder a kit was opened from, and a constructor window's title MUST be its model's `kitWindowTitle`, naming the kit, `(read-only)` for a kit opened read-only, the folder and the constructor; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an opened kit carries the folder it was opened from`, `the window title names the kit, its folder and the constructor`, `a kit opened read-only is marked in the title` and `a scene that opened no folder is titled by its kit alone`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a constructor window is titled by its kit`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.an opened kit carries the folder it was opened from", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the window title names the kit, its folder and the constructor", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only is marked in the title", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a scene that opened no folder is titled by its kit alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a constructor window is titled by its kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.OpenedKit.folder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitFolderOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitWindowTitle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.MainConstructorWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.InverseConstructorWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S53-TITLE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 185, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [184], "how_to": "A kit opened read-only refuses every write message, and the controls that send them are withheld (the S5.3 brief: read-only shows in the title and disables every write message; step 155: a window opened read-only answers `KitReadOnlyErr` in its `kitStatus`, and S5.3 disables those messages; .spec-md §3.12: a read-only open writes nothing). The write messages are those whose arms write the kit: `ExpCommit`, `ExpRemove` and `AttachDataFileTo` (step 152) and `SceneSave` (step 153). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: on the extension that holds `kitCaption` (step 184), `member model.kitWrites : ControlAvailability` answers `ControlOffered` for `ReadWriteKitAccess` and `ControlWithheld` for `ReadOnlyKitAccess` (`RotationControls.fs:19`), the one place the kit's access decides a control. In `updateTableAndElementRotation`, each of the four write messages first matches `model.kitWrites`: `ControlWithheld` answers the model unchanged except `kitStatus = Some (ControlCaption \"The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.\")`, calls no proxy and writes nothing; `ControlOffered` runs the arm steps 152 and 153 wrote, unchanged. One private function holds that guard, and the four arms call it. Every other message, the draft's and `SceneLoad` included, is unchanged. (2) The view withholds those controls under `ControlWithheld`. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`: `ExperimentControlsState` gains `removalAvailability : ControlAvailability` after `addAvailability` (`ExperimentControls.fs:227`), documented in one line (whether a collected experiment's Remove is offered), `ControlOffered` in `emptyExperimentControls` (`:248`); `rowActionButton` (`:727`) takes a `ControlAvailability` after its background and sets `Border.isEnabled` and the 0.4 opacity of a withheld box as `actionButton` (`:696`) does; `collectionRow` (`:745`) takes the availability its Remove passes, its View passing `ControlOffered`; and `collectionBlock` passes `state.removalAvailability`. (b) In `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, the experiment-controls state the Experiments bay builds sets `addAvailability` to `ControlWithheld` when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld` and to today's rule otherwise, and `removalAvailability` to `model.kitWrites`. `attachDataFileButton` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3419`) takes `model.kitWrites` and, withheld, sets `Border.isEnabled` false and opacity 0.4 and opens no picker. `workbenchButton` (`:3237`) becomes a call of a new private `availableWorkbenchButton (availability : ControlAvailability)` with `ControlOffered`, so one body draws both, and the scene row's `Save scene` (step 153) is `availableWorkbenchButton model.kitWrites`. No other control is withheld, and nothing is hidden: a read-only window shows what the kit holds. (3) Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184) gains `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`: a kit holding experiment `E1` (written through `writeExperiment`, step 148) and closed is opened read-only and loaded into `initMain ()`; with a draft ready to commit (a linear polarizer added and chosen, as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:filledExperiments` builds one), `ExpCommit`, `ExpRemove (ExperimentId 1)`, `AttachDataFileTo` of `ExperimentId 1` and a data file under the fact's folder, and `SceneSetName (ControlCaption \"Bench\")` then `SceneSave` each leave the experiments and `savedScenes` as they were and set `kitStatus` to `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.`, and every file of the folder keeps its bytes. `a kit's access decides whether its writes are offered`: `kitWrites` is `ControlOffered` for the kit opened read-write and `ControlWithheld` for it opened read-only. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs`: `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why` (step 152) keeps its assertions over a model whose kit's proxy is `readOnlyView` and whose `access` stays `ReadWriteKitAccess`, so the write still reaches the proxy and fails there; only its fixture line changes. `KitWindowTests` (step 184) gains `a read-only window withholds every write control`: `mainView` mounted as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts a view (`:107`), over the inverse model (`initInverse`, so the Data files section shows) loaded from a kit holding `E1` opened read-only, with the Experiments bay selected and a draft ready to commit: `experimentAddButton`, the `experimentRemoveButton` and the `attachDataFile` of `E1`, and `saveSceneButton` are disabled; over the same kit opened read-write they are enabled.", "acceptance": "After the read-only gate lands, under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` the messages `ExpCommit`, `ExpRemove`, `AttachDataFileTo` and `SceneSave` MUST answer the read-only status and write nothing, and the controls sending them MUST be withheld; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` and `a kit's access decides whether its writes are offered`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a read-only window withholds every write control` and `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-READ-ONLY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit's access decides whether its writes are offered", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-READ-ONLY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-READ-ONLY"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S53-READ-ONLY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitWrites", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-READ-ONLY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.ExperimentControlsState.removalAvailability", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "obligations": ["S53-READ-ONLY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 186, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [185], "how_to": "The Kit menu's verbs and the mode switch, as semantic messages over an injected shell (001 §O 'Kit menu: … Show in Explorer, … Close kit'; 001 §F 'Inside a kit the mode can be switched'; the S5.3 brief: a forward / inverse toggle in the kit window that keeps the kit and the model, through the WindowMode.fs vocabulary if it fits, otherwise a two-case union; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message; §10.5: Close kit loses nothing, because kit writes are immediate and atomic). `WindowMode.fs`'s `LibraryWindowMode` (`WindowMode.fs:65`) is the Browse / Select state of a catalogue window and does not fit, so the switch uses the two-case `ConstructorMode` the model already holds (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:246`, the model's `constructorMode`). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: (1) After `EditorLaunchers` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:143`): `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitWindowShell = { explorer : ExplorerProxy; requestClose : unit -> unit }`, what the Kit menu reaches outside the model, each field documented in one line: the explorer that shows the kit's folder (step 182), and closing the window that hosts the workbench, which releases its kit as it closes (step 154), as `LibraryWindowView.fs:172`'s `requestClose` closes its window. `static member inert : KitWindowShell` holds `ExplorerProxy.createInMemory ignore` and a `requestClose` that does nothing: the shell of the test scenes, so no scene starts Explorer or closes a window by default. (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitShell : KitWindowShell` after `kitFolderOpt` (step 184), documented in one line; `initWith` sets it to `KitWindowShell.inert`, and the windows compose the real one in step 189. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `SwitchConstructorMode of ConstructorMode` (the kit bar's switch), `ShowKitInExplorer` (Show in Explorer) and `CloseKit` (Close kit). (4) Arms. `SwitchConstructorMode mode` answers the model with `constructorMode = mode` and nothing else changed: the kit, the table, the experiments, the draft and the open bay stay, and the chart and Data files gating follow the mode (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2907`, `experimentChartVisible`). `ShowKitInExplorer` with `kitFolderOpt = Some folder` calls `model.kitShell.explorer.showFolder` of the folder's `FolderName`; `Ok ()` answers the model unchanged and `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `The kit folder could not be shown — <e.describe>`; with `None` it answers the model unchanged, because a kit with no folder has nothing to show. `CloseKit` calls `model.kitShell.requestClose ()` and answers the model unchanged; the window's `Closed` handler releases the kit (step 154), and nothing needs saving, because every kit write is already on disk. No confirmation, cache or other message is added. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184), over a loaded model whose `kitShell` records the folders shown and the closes asked: `switching the constructor keeps the kit, the table and the experiments`: over the model with a committed experiment and the Experiments bay open, `SwitchConstructorMode InverseConstructor` answers `constructorMode = InverseConstructor` with `kit`, `elements`, `experimentCollection` and `ribbon` equal to before and the title ending `— Inverse`, and switching back to `ForwardConstructor` answers the first model. `Show in Explorer asks the explorer for the kit's folder`: the recorder holds exactly the kit's folder. `a kit folder the explorer cannot show is told in the kit status`: over an explorer answering `Error (MissingFolderErr \"gone\")`, `kitStatus` contains `gone`. `a scene that opened no folder shows nothing in Explorer`: over `initMain ()` with a recording shell, the recorder stays empty and the model is unchanged. `Close kit asks the window to close and changes nothing else`: the shell's close is asked once, the model equals the one before, and the folder still holds `.oc/lock` until the fact closes the kit.", "acceptance": "After the Kit menu's messages land, `SwitchConstructorMode` MUST change only `constructorMode`, `ShowKitInExplorer` MUST ask the shell's explorer for the kit's folder and tell a refusal in `kitStatus`, and `CloseKit` MUST ask the shell to close the window and change nothing else; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `switching the constructor keeps the kit, the table and the experiments`, `Show in Explorer asks the explorer for the kit's folder`, `a kit folder the explorer cannot show is told in the kit status`, `a scene that opened no folder shows nothing in Explorer` and `Close kit asks the window to close and changes nothing else`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.switching the constructor keeps the kit, the table and the experiments", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Show in Explorer asks the explorer for the kit's folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit folder the explorer cannot show is told in the kit status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a scene that opened no folder shows nothing in Explorer", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Close kit asks the window to close and changes nothing else", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell.inert", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitShell", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SwitchConstructorMode", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ShowKitInExplorer", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CloseKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-MENU-MESSAGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 187, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [186], "how_to": "Kit files changed outside the app are offered for reload, with Reload and Keep mine (001 §E 'on activation, files changed outside the app (another editor, git, a sync) are offered for reload'; 001 §O 'Kit menu: … Reload changes'; the S5.3 brief: on window activation run S4.1's external-change check; changed files are listed with Reload (re-read them into the model) and Keep mine; Reload changes in the Kit menu runs the same check on demand; step 130: `changedKitFiles` answers the kit files whose stamp differs from the recorded one, and never the proxy's own writes). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: (1) Before the model: `KitCheckOrigin` = `KitCheckOnActivation` (the window was activated) | `KitCheckOnRequest` (the Kit menu's Reload changes). (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitChanges : FileName list` after `kitShell` (step 186), documented in one line: the kit files changed outside the app that the kit bar offers to reload, in `changedKitFiles`' order, empty when nothing is offered; `initWith` sets it to `[]`. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `CheckKitChanges of KitCheckOrigin`, `ReloadKitChanges` (the offer's Reload) and `KeepMyKitChanges` (the offer's Keep mine). (4) What `loadKit` sets from a kit's content (`kit`, `experimentCollection` through `ExperimentCollection.ofLoaded` (`Experiments.fs:324`), `savedScenes` (step 153) and `experimentDataStatus` through the one private validation function, steps 152 and 184) moves into one private function of the kit context, its experiments and its scene names, which `loadKit` calls with `opened`'s, so a reload sets exactly what an open sets; `loadKit` keeps setting `experimentData` and `kitFolderOpt` itself. (5) Arms. A model whose `kitFolderOpt` is `None` answers all three unchanged, because nothing outside the app can change a scratch kit. `CheckKitChanges origin` calls `model.kit.proxy.changedKitFiles ()` (step 130): `Ok []` sets `kitChanges` to `[]` and, for `KitCheckOnRequest` only, `kitStatus` to `No kit file changed outside the app.`; `Ok files` sets `kitChanges` to `files` and changes nothing else, so an open offer is replaced by the current list; `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `The kit could not be checked for changes — <e.describe>`. `ReloadKitChanges` reads `model.kit.proxy.readKitFile ()` (step 125), `readExperiments ()` and `readSceneNames ()` (step 148), then calls `recordStamps ()` (step 130); when all answer `Ok`, the model holds the re-read kit file in `kit` (its proxy, `access` and `clock` kept) and the re-read experiments and scene names through (4), the draft starting fresh as an open's does, `kitChanges` is `[]` and `kitStatus` is `None`; the first `Error e` keeps the model and its offer and sets `kitStatus` to `The kit could not be reloaded — <e.describe>`. `KeepMyKitChanges` calls `recordStamps ()`: `Ok ()` sets `kitChanges` to `[]`, so the same changes are not offered again and the window's next write of such a file replaces it; `Error e` keeps the offer and sets the check's status text. None of the three writes a kit file, so a read-only kit is offered reloads too (step 131: `recordStamps` and `changedKitFiles` pass through `readOnlyView`). No merge, per-file choice, diff, file watcher or timer is added: the check runs when the window is activated (step 189) and on request (step 188). Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184). Another writer is `KitProxy.create` over the kit's folder (step 126), which takes no lock, writing through `writeExperiment` (step 148) and `writeKitFile` (step 125); its experiment `E2` is the committed experiment with `id = ExperimentId 2`. `files another writer changed are offered, and the window's own writes are not`: after `ExpCommit` of an experiment through the model, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` offers nothing; after the other writer writes `E2` and the kit file named `Renamed`, it offers exactly `.kit-json` and `E2.experiment-json`. `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`: `ReloadKitChanges` then leaves the model holding `E2`, the kit named `Renamed` (its title starting `Renamed`) and no offer, and a second check offers nothing. `Keep mine keeps the model and clears the offer until the next change`: `KeepMyKitChanges` instead leaves the experiments and the kit's name as they were and no offer; a second check offers nothing; and a further write of the other writer is offered again. `a requested check with nothing changed says so, and an activation check stays silent`: over an unchanged kit, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnRequest` sets `kitStatus` to `No kit file changed outside the app.`, and `KitCheckOnActivation` leaves `kitStatus` `None`. `a kit opened read-only is offered changes and reloads them`: over the kit opened read-only, the other writer's `E2` is offered and `ReloadKitChanges` reads it in, and the window's proxy writes no file. `InverseConstructorTests`' and `SceneSaveLoadTests`' facts that load a kit through `loadKit` (steps 152, 153) keep their assertions over the moved body.", "acceptance": "After reload lands, `CheckKitChanges` MUST offer exactly the kit files another writer changed, `ReloadKitChanges` MUST re-read the kit file, experiments and scenes into the model and clear the offer, and `KeepMyKitChanges` MUST clear the offer keeping the model; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `files another writer changed are offered, and the window's own writes are not`, `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`, `Keep mine keeps the model and clears the offer until the next change`, `a requested check with nothing changed says so, and an activation check stays silent` and `a kit opened read-only is offered changes and reloads them`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.files another writer changed are offered, and the window's own writes are not", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Keep mine keeps the model and clears the offer until the next change", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a requested check with nothing changed says so, and an activation check stays silent", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only is offered changes and reloads them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitCheckOrigin", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitChanges", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CheckKitChanges", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ReloadKitChanges", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.KeepMyKitChanges", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-RELOAD"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 188, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [187], "how_to": "The kit bar above the workbench: the kit, the Kit menu, the constructor and its switch, the reload offer and the kit status, in a file of its own (001 §O 'Kit menu: Send kit…, Show in Explorer, Copy experiments from another kit…, Reload changes, Close kit', of which S6 adds Send kit… and Copy experiments…; .spec-md §4: new surfaces live in their own files, and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` hosts them through messages; §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; AGENTS.md: never a wrapping `TextBlock` inside a horizontal `StackPanel`). The Kit menu is the bar's verb row, not an Avalonia `Menu`: a popup is not provable headless, which is why the element menu is a model-driven overlay (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:117`), and the ribbon's bay order is fixed (Add first, Details last, spec 0046). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the start-screen group (step 178), `// --- The kit window's kit bar (KitWindowView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `kitBar` (`\"KitBar\"`), `kitCaptionText` (`\"KitCaptionText\"`), `kitShowInExplorerButton` (`\"KitShowInExplorerButton\"`), `kitReloadChangesButton` (`\"KitReloadChangesButton\"`), `kitCloseButton` (`\"KitCloseButton\"`), `kitModeText` (`\"KitModeText\"`), `kitSwitchModeButton` (`\"KitSwitchModeButton\"`), `kitChangesText` (`\"KitChangesText\"`), `kitChangesReloadButton` (`\"KitChangesReloadButton\"`) and `kitChangesKeepMineButton` (`\"KitChangesKeepMineButton\"`); the doc of `kitStatus` (step 152) says it is the kit bar's status line. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView`, compiled directly after `KitStartView.fs` (step 176): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3. `kitWindowView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView` is a `DockPanel` whose top child is the kit bar and whose fill is `mainView model dispatch` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3938`), so the bar stays in view while the page scrolls. The bar is one vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitBar`, margin 8, 6, 8, 2, holding in order: (a) a `DockPanel` whose left child is the semi-bold `TextBlock` `Kit:` and whose fill is a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitCaptionText` with `model.kitCaption` (step 184); (b) a `WrapPanel` holding the Kit menu's verbs, each a `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (public since step 107): `Show in Explorer` (`kitShowInExplorerButton`, sending `ShowKitInExplorer`, present only when `kitFolderOpt` is `Some`), `Reload changes` (`kitReloadChangesButton`, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnRequest`) and `Close kit` (`kitCloseButton`, `CloseKit`), then a `TextBlock` carrying `kitModeText` reading `Main constructor` or `Inverse constructor`, and the verb `kitSwitchModeButton` labelled `Switch to Inverse` in the forward constructor (sending `SwitchConstructorMode InverseConstructor`) and `Switch to Main` in the inverse one (sending `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor`); (c) when `kitChanges` is not empty, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitChangesText`, `Changed outside the app: <the file names joined by \", \">. Reload them, or keep your version?`, and under it one horizontal `StackPanel` of two `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton`s: `Reload` (`kitChangesReloadButton`, `positiveBackground`, `ReloadKitChanges`) and `Keep mine` (`kitChangesKeepMineButton`, `negativeBackground`, `KeepMyKitChanges`), the action box's right margin being the gap; (d) when `kitStatus` is `Some`, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitStatus` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`. Every id is an AutomationId, never a `Name`, as `MaterialsWindowView.fs:verbButton`'s doc says of variable membership. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `collectionBuilderView` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3484`) no longer shows the `kitStatus` line (step 152), because the kit bar shows it whichever bay is open, and one control carries the id; its doc and the section comment say so. (4) Tests. `KitWindowTests` (step 184) mounts its screens as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts a view (`:107`), over `kitWindowView`, headless at 1000 × 700, each model loaded from a folder kit with a recording `kitShell` (step 186). Without a trait: `the kit window UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the ten new ids' texts. `the kit bar shows the kit, its Kit menu and the constructor`: `kitCaptionText` reads the model's `kitCaption`; `kitShowInExplorerButton`, `kitReloadChangesButton` and `kitCloseButton` are present; `kitModeText` reads `Main constructor` and `kitSwitchModeButton` `Switch to Inverse`, and over the inverse model `Inverse constructor` and `Switch to Main`; over `initMain ()`, the scratch kit, `kitShowInExplorerButton` is absent. `a changed kit offers Reload and Keep mine on one row, Keep mine to the right`: over a model whose `kitChanges` holds `.kit-json` and `E2.experiment-json`, `kitChangesText` names both, and the two buttons have equal tops, `kitChangesKeepMineButton`'s left beyond `kitChangesReloadButton`'s right; with no changes neither button exists. `the kit status shows in the kit bar whichever bay is open`: a model whose `kitStatus` is `Some` shows exactly one control carrying `kitStatus`, with the Add bay open and with the Experiments bay open. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does (`:69`): `pressing the kit bar's buttons sends their messages`: `kitSwitchModeButton` switches the model to the inverse constructor (`kitModeText` then reads `Inverse constructor`), `kitShowInExplorerButton` hands the kit's folder to the recording explorer, `kitReloadChangesButton` shows `No kit file changed outside the app.` in `kitStatus`, and `kitCloseButton` asks the recording close once. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable`: `assertReachable \"KitWindow\"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over `filledExperiments ()` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:114`) updated, as a record, to a kit marked `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, a test-local `kitFolderOpt`, three file names in `kitChanges` and a `kitStatus`, so the bar is at its tallest. `InverseConstructorTests`' and `SceneSaveLoadTests`' facts keep their assertions: they read `kitStatus` from the model, and the builder still renders.", "acceptance": "After the kit bar lands, `kitWindowView` MUST show above `mainView` the kit's caption, the Kit menu (Show in Explorer, Reload changes, Close kit), the constructor with its switch, the reload offer with Reload and Keep mine on one row and the kit status, every control under its `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing the kit bar's buttons sends their messages`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit window UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the kit bar shows the kit, its Kit menu and the constructor`, `a changed kit offers Reload and Keep mine on one row, Keep mine to the right`, `the kit status shows in the kit bar whichever bay is open` and `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the kit window UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-BAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the kit bar shows the kit, its Kit menu and the constructor", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-BAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a changed kit offers Reload and Keep mine on one row, Keep mine to the right", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-KIT-BAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the kit status shows in the kit bar whichever bay is open", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests