{"number": 189, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S5.3i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [188], "how_to": "The constructor windows run the kit window: the kit bar over the workbench, the real shell, and the change check on every activation (001 §E 'on activation, files changed outside the app … are offered for reload'; the S5.3 brief: on window activation, run S4.1's external-change check; 001 §O: the title shows the kit name and folder). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (`Program.fs:71`), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: (1) It runs `Program.mkProgram` instead of `Program.mkSimple`, capturing the Elmish dispatch from its init command as `LibraryWindow` does (`LibraryWindow.fs:90`): init answers `seed ()` with `kitShell = { explorer = ExplorerProxy.system; requestClose = window.Close }` (steps 183, 186) and `Cmd.ofEffect` storing the dispatch; update is `updateTableAndElementRotation` with `Cmd.none`. (2) Its view keeps setting `window.Title <- model.kitWindowTitle.value` (step 184) and answers `KitWindowView.kitWindowView model dispatch` (step 188) in place of `mainView`, so the kit bar shows above the workbench. (3) `window.Activated.Add (fun _ -> dispatch (CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation))` (step 187), so every activation, the first included, checks the kit; the first finds nothing, because opening the kit recorded its stamps (step 131). `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` keep their constructors and their `Closed` release (step 154), and their docs say they run the kit window. No timer, file watcher or polling is added. Tests, in `KitWindowTests` (step 184), each over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitWindowTests\")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152), with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: activating a constructor window offers the kit files changed outside the app, and Reload reads them in`: a shown `MainConstructorWindow` holds `kitBar` and no `kitChangesText`; another writer (`KitProxy.create` over the kit's folder, step 126) writes an experiment `E2` through `writeExperiment` (step 148), an experiment committed in a scratch `initMain ()` model and given `id = ExperimentId 2`; a second `Window` is shown and activated, then the constructor window is activated again (`Activate ()`), and `kitChangesText` names `E2.experiment-json`; pressing `kitChangesReloadButton` at its centre removes the offer, and, its Experiments tab pressed, the collection holds `E2`'s row. `Close kit closes the window and releases the kit`: pressing `kitCloseButton` closes the window (its `Closed` raised once), and the kit's folder holds no `.oc/lock`. Neither fact presses `kitShowInExplorerButton`, because a real window's explorer is the system's.", "acceptance": "After the windows run the kit window, a constructor window MUST show the kit bar above the workbench, use the system explorer and its own close, and check its kit for outside changes on every activation; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: activating a constructor window offers the kit files changed outside the app, and Reload reads them in` and `Close kit closes the window and releases the kit`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: activating a constructor window offers the kit files changed outside the app, and Reload reads them in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-WINDOW-HOST"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.Close kit closes the window and releases the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-WINDOW-HOST"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.MainConstructorWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S53-WINDOW-HOST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.InverseConstructorWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S53-WINDOW-HOST"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 190, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [189], "how_to": "One window per kit: choosing a kit whose window is open brings that window forward instead of opening the kit again (001 §E 'Concurrency: one window per kit'; the S5.3 brief: opening a kit that is already open activates its window). The windows meet in the host-layer registry that already keeps Materials and Library single-instance (`WindowLauncher.fs:108`, `WindowRegistry`; `WindowLauncher.fs:191`, `WindowLauncher.create`), keyed by the kit's canonical folder (step 181); no second registry is written. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs`: `WindowKey` (`WindowLauncher.fs:34`) gains `KitWindowKey of KitFolder`, documented in one line: a constructor window, keyed by its kit's canonical folder. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `KitWindowPresence` = `KitWindowActivated` (a window held the kit and was brought forward) | `NoKitWindowOpen` (no window holds it). `type KitFolder with member this.windowKey : WindowLauncher.WindowKey` is `KitWindowKey this.canonical`, and `member this.activateKitWindow () : KitWindowPresence` calls `openOrActivate this.windowKey` of `WindowLauncher.create` over a factory that answers `WindowNotRegisteredErr` of its key (`WindowLauncher.fs:66`), `SelectWindowModality.defaultValue` and `BrowseOpen`: `Ok (ActivatedWindow _)` is `KitWindowActivated`, and every other answer is `NoKitWindowOpen`, because that factory never builds a window. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs` (steps 176, 177): `KitStartContext` gains `activateKitWindow : KitFolder -> KitWindowPresence` after `showKit`, documented in one line. In `updateKitStart`, `CreateKit folder`, `OpenKit folder` and `OpenKitReadOnly folder` first call `m.context.activateKitWindow folder`: `KitWindowActivated` answers the model with no offer and no status, and opens, bumps and hands over nothing, because the kit's window holds it and its history entry was bumped when that window opened; `NoKitWindowOpen` runs step 177's open unchanged. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs` (step 179) composes `activateKitWindow = fun folder -> match folder.activateKitWindow () with KitWindowActivated -> this.Close (); KitWindowActivated | NoKitWindowOpen -> NoKitWindowOpen`, so the screen closes when it brought a kit's window forward, as it closes when it hands a kit over. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`: `rootWindowFactory` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:44`), exhaustive over `WindowKey`, answers `KitWindowKey _` with `Error (WindowFactoryFailedErr (key, \"a kit window opens over its opened kit\"))`, because a constructor window is built by the kit hand-off (step 191), never by the root factory; its doc says so in no more words. (6) Tests. `KitStartTests`' fixture context (step 176) and `KitStartWindowTests`' contexts (step 178) pass `activateKitWindow = fun _ -> NoKitWindowOpen`, and every earlier fact keeps its assertions. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs` gains `a kit whose window is open is activated, not opened, bumped or handed over`: over a kit made by `openKitAt` and closed, and a context whose `activateKitWindow` answers `KitWindowActivated` for that folder and records each call, `OpenKit`, `CreateKit` and `OpenKitReadOnly` of the folder each record one activation and no shown kit, answer no offer and no status, leave the history unchanged and leave the folder without `.oc/lock`. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs` gains `two spellings of one kit folder are one window key, and no window holds a new kit`: the `windowKey`s of `C:/kits/a` and of the same folder written with backslashes, a trailing one and in upper case are equal, and `activateKitWindow ()` of a GUID-named folder under the test output answers `NoKitWindowOpen`.", "acceptance": "After the registry key lands, `KitFolder.activateKitWindow` MUST bring forward a window registered under the kit's canonical folder and answer `NoKitWindowOpen` otherwise, and the start screen's open messages MUST activate such a window instead of opening the kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit whose window is open is activated, not opened, bumped or handed over` and `two spellings of one kit folder are one window key, and no window holds a new kit`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a kit whose window is open is activated, not opened, bumped or handed over", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.two spellings of one kit folder are one window key, and no window holds a new kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.WindowLauncher.WindowKey.KitWindowKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.KitWindowPresence", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.KitFolder.windowKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.KitFolder.activateKitWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartContext.activateKitWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 191, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S5.3k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [190], "how_to": "Every constructor window registers under its kit, so a second choice of the kit brings it forward (001 §E 'one window per kit'; step 190's registry key; step 180: `KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn` shows the window of a mode over an opened kit). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn` (step 180), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3, opens the window of the mode through `WindowLauncher.create` over a factory that builds `MainConstructorWindow(context, opened)` or `InverseConstructorWindow(context, opened)`, `context.settings.selectWindowModality` and `BrowseOpen`, under `opened.folder.windowKey` (steps 184, 190): `Ok (CreatedWindow _)` is the open; `Ok (ActivatedWindow _)` or `Ok (RetargetedWindow _)`, a window that already holds the kit, closes the opened kit again (`opened.library.kit.close ()`, step 131) so the one window keeps the kit; and `Error (WindowFactoryFailedErr (_, reason))` closes the opened kit and is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying the reason, as `openKitAt` logs a failed close (step 150). The registry forgets the window when it closes (`WindowLauncher.fs:225`), so the kit opens again after Close kit. No other code changes. Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs`, with trait `ui-smoke`, through the start screen as step 180's facts go: `acceptance: choosing a kit whose window is open activates that window and opens no second one`: Main's start screen over a picker answering a fresh folder, pressing `newKitButton`, opens one `MainConstructorWindow`; Inverse's start screen over a picker answering the same folder, pressing `openKitButton`, opens no constructor window and closes the screen, and the folder's `.oc/lock` still names this process; the same happens through a picker answering that folder written with backslashes and in upper case. `a kit can be opened again once its window is closed`: once that window is closed, Main's start screen pressing `openKitButton` over the folder opens one `MainConstructorWindow`. Each fact closes the windows it opened, so no registry key outlives it.", "acceptance": "After the windows register, choosing a kit whose constructor window is open MUST bring that window forward, open no second one and keep its lock, and a closed window's kit MUST open again; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: choosing a kit whose window is open activates that window and opens no second one` and `a kit can be opened again once its window is closed`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: choosing a kit whose window is open activates that window and opens no second one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW-WIRE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.a kit can be opened again once its window is closed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW-WIRE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S53-ONE-WINDOW-WIRE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 192, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [191], "how_to": "What the Data locations window lists, as data (001 §G 'Every path is overridable in appsettings.json; a Launcher Data locations panel shows them, each with Open folder'; .spec-md §5 `DataLocations`: every path 001 §G names; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`, after `DataLocations` (step 81), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `DataLocationKind` = `LibraryDatabaseLocation` | `LibraryBackupsLocation` | `PreferencesLocation` | `KitsLocation` | `ExportsLocation` | `CataloguesLocation` | `ShippedCatalogueLocation`, one per field of `DataLocations`, each case documented in one line naming its field; it is never stored, so it has no tag. `static member all : DataLocationKind list` lists them in that order, the order of the record's fields. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs`, beside `LibraryDatabase.recreate` (step 87), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `type LibraryDatabase with static member tryFileOf (connectionString : ConnectionString) : FileName option` reads the connection string through `SqliteConnectionStringBuilder` and answers `None` for an in-memory library (`DataSource` `:memory:` or `Mode` `Memory`) and otherwise `Some` of the `DataSource`'s full path (`Path.GetFullPath`). It is `recreate`'s in-memory test and file read, moved: `recreate` calls it and its own copy is deleted, so one rule says where a library's file is. It touches no file. No other member is added. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs` (step 62) gains `tryFileOf answers the library's file, and nothing for an in-memory library`: `Data Source=:memory:` and `Data Source=lib;Mode=Memory;Cache=Shared` answer `None`, and `Data Source=<a folder under the test output>/library.db` answers that file's full path; `recreate`'s facts (step 87) keep their assertions. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs` (step 81) gains `every location is a data location kind, in the order of its field`: `DataLocationKind.all` holds the seven cases once each, in the order above.", "acceptance": "After the location kinds land, `DataLocationKind.all` MUST list the seven 001 §G locations in field order and `LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf` MUST be the one rule for a library's file, `recreate` calling it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `tryFileOf answers the library's file, and nothing for an in-memory library` and `every location is a data location kind, in the order of its field`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests.tryFileOf answers the library's file, and nothing for an in-memory library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryDatabaseTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATION-KINDS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests.every location is a data location kind, in the order of its field", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.WorkbenchSettingsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATION-KINDS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.WorkbenchSettings.DataLocationKind", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATION-KINDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.WorkbenchSettings.DataLocationKind.all", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATION-KINDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LibraryBackupStore.LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATION-KINDS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 193, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [192], "actions": ["ADD_TEST DataLocationsTests", "ADD_TEST DataLocationsWindowTests"], "how_to": "The Data locations screen: its rows, its message and its view, as a pure Elmish update over injected seams (001 §G 'a Launcher Data locations panel shows them, each with Open folder'; the S5.3 brief: it lists every DataLocations entry with its path and Open folder, which opens Explorer through a seam tests substitute; .spec-md §4 'UI'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type DataLocationKind with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Library database`, `Library backups`, `Preferences`, `Kit folders (suggested parent)`, `Exports`, `Catalogue exports` and `Shipped catalogue`) and `member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`LibraryDatabase`, `LibraryBackups`, `Preferences`, `Kits`, `Exports`, `Catalogues` and `ShippedCatalogue`); and `ConstructorUiId.dataLocationRow`, `dataLocationPathText` and `dataLocationOpenFolderButton`, each over a `DataLocationKind` (`DataLocationRow_<key>`, `DataLocationPath_<key>`, `DataLocationOpenFolder_<key>`). `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the kit-bar group (step 188), `// --- The Data locations window (DataLocationsView, DataLocationsWindow). ---`, holding `dataLocationsStatusText` (`\"DataLocationsStatusText\"`) with a one-line doc. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView`, compiled directly after `KitWindowView.fs` (step 188): one `<Compile>` line and no comment; its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3. It follows `KitStartView.fs` (step 176). (a) `DataLocationRow = { kind : DataLocationKind; path : ControlCaption; folderOpt : FolderName option }`: what a listed location shows and the folder Open folder opens, `None` when there is none. (b) `type DataLocations with member this.rows : DataLocationRow list` answers one row per `DataLocationKind.all` (step 192), in that order: the library database row shows `LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf this.libraryConnection`'s full path and opens its folder (`Path.GetDirectoryName`), and for an in-memory library shows `In memory (<the connection string>)` with no folder; every other row shows its folder's text and opens that folder. It reads no disk: a folder that does not exist yet is listed, and Open folder tells it. (c) `[<ReferenceEquality>] DataLocationsContext = { locations : DataLocations; explorer : ExplorerProxy }` (step 182). (d) `DataLocationsModel = { context : DataLocationsContext; rows : DataLocationRow list; status : ControlCaption option }`. (e) `DataLocationsMsg` = `OpenDataLocationFolder of DataLocationKind`. (f) `initDataLocations (context : DataLocationsContext) : DataLocationsModel` answers `context.locations.rows` and no status. (g) `updateDataLocations (msg : DataLocationsMsg) (m : DataLocationsModel) : DataLocationsModel`: for the row of the kind, a folder is handed to `m.context.explorer.showFolder`, `Ok ()` clearing `status` and `Error e` setting it to `The folder could not be opened — <e.describe>`; a row without a folder answers the model unchanged. (h) `dataLocationsView (m : DataLocationsModel) (dispatch : DataLocationsMsg -> unit) : IView`, a pure projection: a `ScrollViewer` over a `MinWidthPanel` of minimum width 480, both scroll bars `Auto`, as `kitStartView` scrolls (step 178), over a vertical `StackPanel` holding the status, when `Some`, as a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `dataLocationsStatusText` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`, then one `DockPanel` per row carrying `dataLocationRow kind`, whose right side holds, for a row with a folder, the `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` `Open folder` (`dataLocationOpenFolderButton kind`, sending `OpenDataLocationFolder kind`) and whose fill is a vertical `StackPanel` of the semi-bold `kind.caption` and a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `dataLocationPathText kind` with the path. No edit field, copy button or cache is added: the locations are edited in `appsettings.json` (001 §G). (3) Tests. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataLocationsTests.fs`, `module DataLocationsTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over `DataLocations` built in the fact with folders under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"DataLocationsTests\")` and a recording explorer: `the rows list every location in order, the library by its file`: over a file library `Data Source=<folder>/library.db` the seven rows follow `DataLocationKind.all`, the library row shows the file's full path and opens `<folder>`, and the kits row shows and opens the kits folder. `an in-memory library is listed without a folder`: over `Data Source=:memory:` the library row reads `In memory (Data Source=:memory:)` and has no folder. `Open folder hands the row's folder to the explorer`: `OpenDataLocationFolder KitsLocation` records the kits folder and leaves no status, and over the in-memory library `OpenDataLocationFolder LibraryDatabaseLocation` records nothing. `a folder the explorer cannot open is told`: over an explorer answering `Error (MissingFolderErr \"gone\")`, the status contains `gone`. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs`, `module DataLocationsWindowTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounts the view as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts one (`:107`), headless at 800 × 600, over `TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName \"DataLocationsWindowTests\")` (step 83) and a recording explorer. Without a trait: `the Data locations UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: `dataLocationsStatusText` and the three ids of `KitsLocation`. `every location is listed with its path, and Open folder only where there is a folder`: each kind's `dataLocationRow` and `dataLocationPathText` exist, the kits row's path is the test kits folder's text, and the in-memory library's row has no `dataLocationOpenFolderButton` while every other row has one. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing Open folder hands that location's folder to the explorer`: pressing the exports row's button records the exports folder.", "acceptance": "After the Data locations view lands, `DataLocations.rows` MUST list the seven locations with their paths and folders, the in-memory library without one, and `updateDataLocations` MUST hand a row's folder to the context's explorer and tell a refusal; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the rows list every location in order, the library by its file`, `an in-memory library is listed without a folder`, `Open folder hands the row's folder to the explorer` and `a folder the explorer cannot open is told`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Open folder hands that location's folder to the explorer`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Data locations UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `every location is listed with its path, and Open folder only where there is a folder`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataLocationsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests.the rows list every location in order, the library by its file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataLocationsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests.an in-memory library is listed without a folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataLocationsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests.Open folder hands the row's folder to the explorer", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataLocationsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests.a folder the explorer cannot open is told", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataLocationsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataLocationsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests.the Data locations UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests.every location is listed with its path, and Open folder only where there is a folder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests.pressing Open folder hands that location's folder to the explorer", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView.DataLocationRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView.DataLocationsContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView.DataLocationsModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView.DataLocationsMsg", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView.initDataLocations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView.updateDataLocations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsView.dataLocationsView", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsView.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataLocationsStatusText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.dataLocationRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.dataLocationPathText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.dataLocationOpenFolderButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 194, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S5.3n", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [193], "how_to": "The Data locations window, single-instance in the host registry (001 §G; .spec-md §4: every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`; Materials and Library are single-instance through the same registry, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:182`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Data locations group (step 193): `dataLocationsWindow` (`\"DataLocationsWindow\"`) with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs`: `WindowKey` (`WindowLauncher.fs:34`) gains `DataLocationsWindowKey`, documented in one line: the single-instance Data locations window. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `KitStartWindow.fs` (step 179): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type DataLocationsWindow(locations : DataLocations, explorer : ExplorerProxy)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `KitStartWindow` does; its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §G and spec 0050 S5.3. Its title is `Data locations`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.dataLocationsWindow`; it asks for 720 × 460 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`); it runs `Program.mkSimple` over `initDataLocations { locations = locations; explorer = explorer }`, `updateDataLocations` and `dataLocationsView` (step 193). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`: `rootWindowFactory` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:44`) answers `DataLocationsWindowKey` with `DataLocationsWindow(TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName \"WireUiFinalCompositionTests\"), ExplorerProxy.createInMemory ignore)`, and `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff` adds `DataLocationsWindowKey` to the keys it opens, so ui-smoke renders the window. (5) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the Data locations window leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"DataLocations\"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `DataLocationsWindow` over `TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName \"ScrollExtentTests\")` and `ExplorerProxy.createInMemory ignore`. `DataLocationsWindowTests` (step 193) gains, without a trait, `the Data locations window is titled and carries its stable id`: the window is titled `Data locations` and carries `dataLocationsWindow` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`; and, with trait `ui-smoke`, `the Data locations window opens once through the registry`: two `openOrActivate DataLocationsWindowKey` through `WindowLauncher.create` over a factory building the window answer `CreatedWindow` and then `ActivatedWindow` of the same window, which is then closed.", "acceptance": "After the window lands, `DataLocationsWindow` MUST run the Data locations screen titled `Data locations`, fitted to its screen and single-instance under `DataLocationsWindowKey`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Data locations window opens once through the registry` and the widened `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Data locations window is titled and carries its stable id` and `the Data locations window leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the Data locations window leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests.the Data locations window is titled and carries its stable id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests.the Data locations window opens once through the registry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataLocationsWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataLocationsWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests.the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-WINDOW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataLocationsWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataLocationsWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.WindowLauncher.WindowKey.DataLocationsWindowKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataLocationsWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-WINDOW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 195, "anchor": "WIRE_UI", "ac": "AC-S5.3o", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.App", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [194], "how_to": "The Launcher's footer opens Data locations (001 §O 'A footer link opens Data locations'; 001 §G; .spec-md §10.1: the Launcher's footer link opens Data locations). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588`): `launcherDataLocationsLink` (`\"LauncherDataLocationsLink\"`) with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow(locations, settings, opened, pickerFor)` (steps 88, 89, 154, 180): its footer, the bottom-docked row of the version line (`Program.fs:179-189`), gains on its left a link-styled `Button` reading `Data locations` (transparent background, no border, underlined text, font size 11) carrying `launcherDataLocationsLink` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, whose click opens `DataLocationsWindow(locations, ExplorerProxy.system)` (steps 183, 194) through `WindowLauncher.create` over that factory, `settings.selectWindowModality` and `BrowseOpen`, under `DataLocationsWindowKey`, so a second click brings the open window forward. The link is in every outcome's content and always enabled, a library that failed to open included, because the locations do not depend on the library (step 88). The `LauncherWindow` doc names the link in no more words; no other launcher control changes. (3) Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs`, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: the Data locations link opens one Data locations window listing the configured locations`: over `TestAppScope.testLocations`, raising `Click` on `launcherDataLocationsLink` as the file's launcher facts click opens exactly one `DataLocationsWindow`, whose kits row's `dataLocationPathText` reads the test kits folder's text, and a second click opens no other window; the window is closed at the end. `the Data locations link stays enabled when the library fails to open`: over `Error (LibrarySchemaMismatchErr …)`, as step 88's fact builds the launcher, `launcherDataLocationsLink` is enabled while the four surface buttons are disabled. No fact presses Open folder through the launcher, because its explorer is the system's.", "acceptance": "After the footer link lands, the Launcher MUST show `launcherDataLocationsLink`, enabled in every outcome, opening one Data locations window over the configured locations; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Data locations link opens one Data locations window listing the configured locations` and `the Data locations link stays enabled when the library fails to open`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.acceptance: the Data locations link opens one Data locations window listing the configured locations", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-LINK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests.the Data locations link stays enabled when the library fails to open", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-LINK"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-LINK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.launcherDataLocationsLink", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S53-LOCATIONS-LINK"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S5.3 -- The kit window: title, Kit menu, lock, reload and mode; Data locations"}
{"number": 196, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S6a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [195], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests"], "how_to": "What travels when a kit is sent, as pure Domain data (001 §H 'Send kit… writes one <kit name>.zip (excluding .oc/ and sendExclude)'; 001 §E 'Large lab files (e.g. 24 MB DNG images) may stay in the kit … Send kit… honours sendExclude (e.g. **/*.dng)'; 001 §A '.oc/ app-owned cache and lock; safe to delete; never sent'; the S6 brief: the globs use a small pure matcher in Domain supporting **, * and ?, and no package is added, because STL pins no globbing package). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6, and every type follows `AGENTS.md` (single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool`). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`. (a) Directly before `KitRelativePath` (step 123): `KitPathRole` = `KitAppCachePath` (the path is the app's cache folder or lies under it) | `KitContentPath` (any other path). (b) `KitRelativePath` gains: `static member appCacheFolder : KitRelativePath`, the text `.oc`, the app-owned cache and lock folder (001 §A); `member this.pathRole : KitPathRole`, `KitAppCachePath` when the path's first `/`-separated segment equals `appCacheFolder`'s text ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`); `member this.parentOpt : KitRelativePath option`, the text before the last `/`, `None` for a path at the kit root; and `member this.leafName : FileName`, the text after the last `/` (the whole text at the root). (c) The lock names its folder through `appCacheFolder`: the lock path of `KitFolderStore.fs` (step 129) and the `.oc` and `.oc/lock` entries of `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 129, `KitFolders.fs`), so the text `.oc` is written once in product code. Every answer of those members is unchanged. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs`: `module KitArchive` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `KitHistory.fs` (step 164): one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. It opens `Kit`, `LibraryEntryFiles` (step 24: `FileStem`) and `Softellect.Sys.Primitives`. In this order: (a) `GlobPathMatch` = `GlobPathMatched` | `GlobPathUnmatched`. (b) `type SendExcludeGlob with member this.matchOf (path : KitRelativePath) : GlobPathMatch`, the one glob matcher (`SendExcludeGlob`, step 122). The glob's `\\` become `/`, and the glob and the path are split at `/` into segments. A glob segment `**` matches zero or more whole path segments. In any other glob segment `*` matches zero or more characters and `?` exactly one character, never across a `/`, and every other character matches itself ignoring case (the Windows rule `copyTargetFor` follows, step 132). A glob matches the whole path from the kit root: `**/*.dng` matches `IMG_0001.DNG` and `data/raw/a.dng`; `data/raw/big/**` matches everything under `data/raw/big` but not that folder; `*.csv` matches `run.csv` but not `data/run.csv`. It is a recursive match over the two segment lists and, inside a segment, over the two character lists; no regular expression, brace, character class or negation is added. (c) `KitSendChoice` = `SentWithKit` | `LeftOutOfSend`. (d) `KitTreeEntry` = `KitTreeFile of KitRelativePath` | `KitTreeFolder of KitRelativePath`, one file or folder under a kit, with `member this.path : KitRelativePath`. (e) `type KitFile with member this.sendChoiceOf (path : KitRelativePath) : KitSendChoice` answers `LeftOutOfSend` for a `KitAppCachePath` path and for a path that, or any folder holding it (its chain of `parentOpt`), a glob of `sendExclude` answers `GlobPathMatched`; `SentWithKit` otherwise. So a glob that names a folder leaves out the folder and everything in it. `member this.sentEntries (tree : KitTreeEntry list) : KitTreeEntry list` keeps, in order, the entries whose path is `SentWithKit`. (f) `type KitName with member this.zipFileName : FileName` is `this.fileStem.withExtension (FileExtension \".zip\")` (steps 24, 122): the one place `.zip` is written, so a kit named `Optics: QZ/LR` is sent as `Optics_ QZ_LR.zip`. No other type, member or option is added; S8.3's naming template and S9.2's import profiles add nothing here. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs`, `module KitArchiveTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment; every path is made through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate`. `a glob matches whole segments with a double star, and characters with star and question mark inside one segment, ignoring case`: `**/*.dng` matches `IMG_0001.DNG`, `data/raw/a.dng` and `data/a.Dng`, and not `data/a.dngx`; `data/raw/big/**` matches `data/raw/big/x.dng` and `data/raw/big/y/z.csv`, and not `data/raw/big` or `data/raw/bigger/x`; `*.csv` matches `run.csv` and not `data/run.csv`; `data/run ?.csv` matches `data/run 1.csv` and not `data/run 10.csv`; `data\\raw\\*.csv` matches `data/raw/a.csv`; `**` matches `.kit-json` and `data/raw/a.csv`. `the app cache is never sent, and a glob leaves out what it matches and everything inside a folder it matches`: over a kit file whose `sendExclude` is `**/*.dng` and `data/scratch`, `.oc`, `.oc/lock` and `.OC/planner/x.json` are `LeftOutOfSend`; so are `data/raw/IMG_0001.DNG`, `data/scratch` and `data/scratch/a.csv`; `.kit-json`, `data`, `data/raw`, `data/run 1.csv`, `library/x.material-json` and `.ocx/a` are `SentWithKit`. `the sent entries keep the tree's order and drop what is left out` : a tree, in ordinal order, of the folders `.oc`, `data`, `data/raw` and `library` and the files `.kit-json`, `.oc/lock`, `data/raw/IMG_0001.DNG`, `data/run 1.csv` and `notes.txt` answers, under the glob `**/*.dng`, every entry but `.oc`, `.oc/lock` and the DNG, in the tree's order; with no glob it answers every entry but `.oc` and `.oc/lock`. `a kit is sent as a zip named for it`: `(KitName \"Optics: QZ/LR\").zipFileName` is `FileName \"Optics_ QZ_LR.zip\"`. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `a kit path knows its folder, its leaf and whether it is the app's cache`: `data/raw/run 1.csv` has `parentOpt` `Some data/raw`, `leafName` `FileName \"run 1.csv\"` and `KitContentPath`; `.kit-json` has `parentOpt` `None` and `leafName` `FileName \".kit-json\"`; `appCacheFolder` is `.oc` and `KitAppCachePath`; `.oc/lock` is `KitAppCachePath` and `.ocx` `KitContentPath`.", "acceptance": "After the send rule lands, `SendExcludeGlob.matchOf` MUST match `**`, `*` and `?` as specified, `KitFile.sendChoiceOf` MUST leave out the app cache and every path a glob or a matched folder covers, and the lock MUST name `.oc` through `KitRelativePath.appCacheFolder`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a glob matches whole segments with a double star, and characters with star and question mark inside one segment, ignoring case`, `the app cache is never sent, and a glob leaves out what it matches and everything inside a folder it matches`, `the sent entries keep the tree's order and drop what is left out`, `a kit is sent as a zip named for it` and `a kit path knows its folder, its leaf and whether it is the app's cache`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests.a glob matches whole segments with a double star, and characters with star and question mark inside one segment, ignoring case", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests.the app cache is never sent, and a glob leaves out what it matches and everything inside a folder it matches", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests.the sent entries keep the tree's order and drop what is left out", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests.a kit is sent as a zip named for it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a kit path knows its folder, its leaf and whether it is the app's cache", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitPathRole", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitRelativePath.appCacheFolder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitRelativePath.pathRole", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitRelativePath.parentOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitRelativePath.leafName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.GlobPathMatch", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.SendExcludeGlob.matchOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitSendChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitTreeEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitFile.sendChoiceOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitFile.sentEntries", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitName.zipFileName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RULE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number": 197, "anchor": "ADD_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S6b", "id": "FILE_BigBoy_0001", "name": "KitArchiveProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [196], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests"], "how_to": "The zip / unzip seam in Domain: its record, its in-memory double over an in-memory disk, and its contract facts (001 §P '`KitArchiveProxy` (zip / unzip)'; 'every proxy has an in-memory stub of the same shape'; the S6 brief: a record and an in-memory implementation in Domain, a Storage create over System.IO.Compression; unzip refuses any entry that escapes the target folder; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO'; §10.2: per zipped file progress with Cancel). The proxy does IO only; what is sent and what is received is decided by step 196's rule and step 198's members. In `KitArchive.fs` (step 196), after `KitName.zipFileName`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) `KitArchiveError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `KitArchiveIoErr` (a kit folder, a file in it, a zip or a folder to extract into could not be listed, read, written or removed), `KitZipEntryEscapesErr` (a zip entry's name is not a path inside the folder it would be extracted into), `KitZipTargetNotEmptyErr` (the folder to extract into already holds a file or folder), `KitZipInsideKitErr` (the zip would be written inside the kit it holds) and `KitZipHoldsNoKitErr` (a zip holds no `.kit-json` at its root). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `a kit archive could not be read or written: <reason>`, `a zip entry is not a path inside the folder: <reason>`, `the folder to extract into is not empty: <reason>`, `the zip would be written inside the kit it holds: <reason>` and `the zip holds no kit: <reason>`. (2) `type KitTreeEntry with` (step 196): `static member tryOfZipEntryName (name : string) : Result<KitTreeEntry, KitArchiveError>`, the one reading of a zip entry's name: a name ending in `/` is a folder and any other a file; the name without that `/` goes through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123), whose refusal (an empty, rooted, drive-holding, `.`- or `..`-holding name) is `KitZipEntryEscapesErr` naming the entry as written; and `member this.zipEntryName : string`, the path's text for a file and that text followed by `/` for a folder. So every entry name is kit-relative and forward-slashed, and no entry can name a place outside the folder it is extracted into. (3) `KitArchiveFileCount of int`, how many files an archive job handles; `KitArchiveProgress = { filesDone : KitArchiveFileCount; filesTotal : KitArchiveFileCount }`, told after each file, the total being the job's file entries. (4) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitArchiveObserver = { reportArchiveProgress : KitArchiveProgress -> unit; cancellation : CancellationToken }`: told after each file, and asked before each file whether the job is cancelled, the rule of `JobRunner.fs:runLoop` (the token is checked between steps). `static member unobserved : KitArchiveObserver` tells nobody and is never cancelled (`CancellationToken.None`). (5) `KitArchiveOutcome` = `KitArchiveFinished of files : KitArchiveFileCount` | `KitArchiveCancelled` (the job stopped before its next file and left nothing behind). (6) `KitZipJob = { kit : KitFolder; entries : KitTreeEntry list; zip : FileName }` and `KitUnzipJob = { zip : FileName; entries : KitTreeEntry list; target : KitFolder }`. (7) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitArchiveProxy = { listKitTree : KitFolder -> Result<KitTreeEntry list, KitArchiveError>; writeKitZip : KitZipJob -> KitArchiveObserver -> Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>; listZipEntries : FileName -> Result<KitTreeEntry list, KitArchiveError>; extractKitZip : KitUnzipJob -> KitArchiveObserver -> Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError> }`, the functional-proxy convention of `KitProxy` (step 125), each field with a one-line doc. `listKitTree` answers every file and folder under the kit folder, kit-relative, in ordinal order of path; a folder that is not there is `KitArchiveIoErr` naming it. `writeKitZip` writes a zip at `job.zip` holding, in order, each entry under its `zipEntryName`, a file with its bytes and a folder empty. Before each file it reads `observer.cancellation`; cancelled, it answers `KitArchiveCancelled` and no zip is written, a zip already at that name keeping its content. After each file it reports progress. The zip appears only once every file is in it, replacing a zip of that name; a file it cannot read is `KitArchiveIoErr` naming it, and no zip is written. `listZipEntries` reads every entry name through `tryOfZipEntryName`, in the zip's order, the first refusal answering its `KitZipEntryEscapesErr`; a zip that is not there or does not read is `KitArchiveIoErr`. `extractKitZip` refuses a target that holds anything with `KitZipTargetNotEmptyErr` and writes nothing; otherwise it creates the target when it is missing and writes each entry of `job.entries` under it, a folder created and a file with the bytes the zip holds under its `zipEntryName`. Before each file it reads the cancellation; cancelled, it removes everything it created, the target too when it created it, and answers `KitArchiveCancelled`. After each file it reports progress; a failure removes what it created and is `KitArchiveIoErr`. (8) `InMemoryArchiveDisk`, the double's disk, shared by every proxy built over it as two windows share one disk. Its state (files by absolute name with their bytes, the folders placed, and each zip as its entries with each file's bytes) is private, mutated only inside its members and the proxies' closures, the boundary of `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 125). A name is compared with every `\\` turned into `/`, a trailing `/` removed, ignoring case. Its public surface is: `static member create () : InMemoryArchiveDisk`; `member this.placeFile (file : FileName) (content : FileByteContent) : unit`, an outside writer placing or replacing a file, every folder holding it existing from then on; `member this.placeFolder (folder : FolderName) : unit`; `member this.tryDiskFile (file : FileName) : FileByteContent option`; and `member this.paths () : FileName list`, every file, folder and zip it holds, forward-slashed, in ordinal order. `FileByteContent` is `Softellect.Sys.Primitives.FileByteContent` (STL `Sys/Primitives.fs:461`), reused as step 132 does. (9) `type KitArchiveProxy with static member createInMemory (disk : InMemoryArchiveDisk) : KitArchiveProxy`, the four fields of (7) over the disk; `listKitTree` locates the disk's names inside the kit folder through `KitFolder.tryKitPathOf` (step 132), so it shares the kit's one location rule. No caching, retry, overwrite option or other field is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`. It declares, each with a one-line doc, a test-local record `KitArchiveTestDisk = { archive : KitArchiveProxy; root : string; placeFile : string -> byte[] -> unit; placeFolder : string -> unit; files : string -> (string * byte[]) list; paths : string -> string list }` (`placeFile` and `placeFolder` take a path relative to `root`; `files` and `paths` list every file with its bytes, and every file and folder, under a folder relative to `root`, kit-relative and forward-slashed, in ordinal order); a test-local `sampleKit (disk : KitArchiveTestDisk) : unit` placing under `kit`: `.kit-json`, `data/run 1.csv` (`phi,I\\n0,0.5\\n`), `data/raw/IMG_0001.DNG` (the bytes 0 to 255), `library/x.material-json`, `notes.txt` and the empty folder `data/empty`; and `[<AbstractClass>] type KitArchiveProxyContract ()` with `abstract freshDisk : unit -> KitArchiveTestDisk`, holding the contract facts. `type KitArchiveProxyTests () = inherit KitArchiveProxyContract ()` answers a disk over `InMemoryArchiveDisk.create ()` whose root is `C:/disk`. The facts, each over `sampleKit`: `a kit folder is listed as every file and folder under it, kit-relative, in ordinal order`: `listKitTree` of `<root>/kit` answers exactly the folders `data`, `data/empty`, `data/raw` and `library` and the five files, in ordinal order. `a zip of the given entries extracts into an empty folder byte for byte, each file reported once`: `writeKitZip` of that tree to `<root>/out/kit.zip` under an observer recording each progress answers `KitArchiveFinished` of 5, the progress reading 1 to 5 of 5; `listZipEntries` answers the tree; `extractKitZip` of it into `<root>/received`, which does not exist, answers `KitArchiveFinished` of 5, and `paths` and `files` of `received` equal those of `kit`. `extracting into a folder that holds anything is refused and writes nothing` : with `received/notes.txt` placed, `extractKitZip` answers `KitZipTargetNotEmptyErr` and `paths` of `received` is exactly `notes.txt`. `a zip job cancelled before its next file writes no zip`: an observer whose token's source is cancelled on the first progress makes `writeKitZip` answer `KitArchiveCancelled`, `listZipEntries` of its zip answer `KitArchiveIoErr`, and `paths` of `out` hold no zip. `an extraction cancelled before its next file removes everything it wrote`: over a written zip, an extraction cancelled on its first progress answers `KitArchiveCancelled`, and `received` does not exist. `a kit folder or a zip that is not there is KitArchiveIoErr` : `listKitTree` of `<root>/none` and `listZipEntries` of `<root>/none.zip` answer `KitArchiveIoErr`. `KitArchiveTests` (step 196) gains `a zip entry name is a kit-relative path, a folder's ending in a slash, and an escaping name is refused`: `data/run 1.csv` reads as `KitTreeFile` and `data/raw/` as `KitTreeFolder` of `data/raw`, and each entry's `zipEntryName` gives its name back; `../evil.txt`, `/etc/x`, `C:/x.txt`, `a/../../b.txt`, `a\\..\\..\\b.txt`, `./a` and `` each answer `KitZipEntryEscapesErr` naming the entry; and `every kit archive error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text containing the reason.", "acceptance": "After the seam lands, `KitArchive.fs` MUST declare `KitArchiveProxy` with exactly `listKitTree`, `writeKitZip`, `listZipEntries` and `extractKitZip`, `InMemoryArchiveDisk` and `KitArchiveProxy.createInMemory`, and `KitArchiveProxyContract` MUST hold the archive facts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit folder is listed as every file and folder under it, kit-relative, in ordinal order`, `a zip of the given entries extracts into an empty folder byte for byte, each file reported once`, `extracting into a folder that holds anything is refused and writes nothing`, `a zip job cancelled before its next file writes no zip`, `an extraction cancelled before its next file removes everything it wrote` and `a kit folder or a zip that is not there is KitArchiveIoErr` under `KitArchiveProxyTests`, and `a zip entry name is a kit-relative path, a folder's ending in a slash, and an escaping name is refused` and `every kit archive error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a kit folder is listed as every file and folder under it, kit-relative, in ordinal order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a zip of the given entries extracts into an empty folder byte for byte, each file reported once", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.extracting into a folder that holds anything is refused and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a zip job cancelled before its next file writes no zip", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.an extraction cancelled before its next file removes everything it wrote", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a kit folder or a zip that is not there is KitArchiveIoErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests.a zip entry name is a kit-relative path, a folder's ending in a slash, and an escaping name is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests.every kit archive error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveProxy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitTreeEntry.tryOfZipEntryName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitTreeEntry.zipEntryName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveFileCount", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveProgress", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveObserver", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveOutcome", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitZipJob", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitUnzipJob", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.InMemoryArchiveDisk", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveProxy.createInMemory", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number": 198, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S6c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [197], "how_to": "Send and receive as two Domain members over the seam, and the two dialogs they need (001 §H 'Send kit… writes one <kit name>.zip (excluding .oc/ and sendExclude), and Open kit from zip… extracts it. There is no separate bundle format'; 001 §E; 001 §P `SendKit`, `OpenKitZip`; the S6 brief: Send kit… goes through a save dialog, Open kit from zip… chooses a zip and a target folder). In `KitArchive.fs` (steps 196-197), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) On one `type KitArchiveProxy with` extension, beside `createInMemory`: (a) `member this.sendKit (kitFile : KitFile) (kit : KitFolder) (zip : FileName) (observer : KitArchiveObserver) : Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>`. When `kit.tryKitPathOf zip` (step 132) answers a path, the zip would lie inside the kit it holds: the answer is `KitZipInsideKitErr` naming the zip, and nothing is listed or written. Otherwise it lists `listKitTree kit` and answers `writeKitZip { kit = kit; entries = kitFile.sentEntries tree; zip = zip } observer` (step 196), so the zip leaves out `.oc` and every path the kit file's globs leave out. (b) `member this.receiveKit (zip : FileName) (target : KitFolder) (observer : KitArchiveObserver) : Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>` lists `listZipEntries zip`. A zip holding no `KitTreeFile` whose path is the kit file's name (`KitFile.fileName`, step 122, ignoring case) is `KitZipHoldsNoKitErr` naming the zip, and nothing is written. Otherwise it answers `extractKitZip { zip = zip; entries = <the entries whose pathRole is KitContentPath>; target = target } observer`, so an app cache the zip holds is never received: a foreign `.oc/lock` would make the received kit look open elsewhere (step 129). (2) After them: `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitZipPicker = { pickZipToWrite : FileName -> Async<FileName option>; pickZipToOpen : unit -> Async<FileName option> }`, the save dialog of Send kit… and the open dialog of Open kit from zip…, the convention of `KitFolderPicker` (step 145): `pickZipToWrite` is handed the zip name to suggest (`KitName.zipFileName`) and answers the chosen file; each answers `None` when the user cancels. Each field has a one-line doc. `static member none : KitZipPicker` answers `None` to both at once, the picker of a scene that picks nothing. The Avalonia dialogs are step 200's. No other member or option is added. Tests, new `KitArchiveProxyContract` facts (step 197), each over `sampleKit` with `kit/.oc/lock` and `kit/.oc/planner/c.json` also placed and a kit file (`KitFile.create`, step 122) whose `sendExclude` is `**/*.dng`: `sending a kit zips every file and folder but the app cache and what its globs leave out`: `sendKit` to `<root>/out/kit.zip` answers `KitArchiveFinished` of 4, and `listZipEntries` answers exactly `.kit-json`, `data`, `data/empty`, `data/raw`, `data/run 1.csv`, `library`, `library/x.material-json` and `notes.txt`, the four folders as `KitTreeFolder`. `a zip is never written inside the kit it holds` : `sendKit` to `<root>/kit/out/kit.zip` answers `KitZipInsideKitErr` and `paths` of `kit` is unchanged. `a received kit holds every sent file byte for byte`: after that send, `receiveKit` into `<root>/received` answers `KitArchiveFinished` of 4, and `files` of `received` equals `files` of `kit` without `.oc/lock`, `.oc/planner/c.json` and `data/raw/IMG_0001.DNG`. `a zip that holds no kit file is refused and nothing is extracted`: a zip written by `writeKitZip` of the tree without `.kit-json` makes `receiveKit` answer `KitZipHoldsNoKitErr`, and `received` does not exist. `a zip's app cache is not received`: a zip written by `writeKitZip` of the whole tree, `.oc` and `.oc/lock` included, received into `received` leaves no `.oc` among `paths` of `received`.", "acceptance": "After send and receive land, `KitArchiveProxy.sendKit` MUST zip the kit's sent entries and refuse a zip inside the kit, `receiveKit` MUST refuse a zip without `.kit-json` and never extract an app cache, and `KitZipPicker` MUST be declared with `none`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `sending a kit zips every file and folder but the app cache and what its globs leave out`, `a zip is never written inside the kit it holds`, `a received kit holds every sent file byte for byte`, `a zip that holds no kit file is refused and nothing is extracted` and `a zip's app cache is not received` under `KitArchiveProxyTests`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.sending a kit zips every file and folder but the app cache and what its globs leave out", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a zip is never written inside the kit it holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a received kit holds every sent file byte for byte", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a zip that holds no kit file is refused and nothing is extracted", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests.a zip's app cache is not received", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveProxy.sendKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitArchiveProxy.receiveKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive.KitZipPicker", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-RECEIVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number": 199, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S6d", "id": "FILE_BigBoy_0001", "name": "KitArchiveProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [198], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests"], "how_to": "The real archive over System.IO.Compression (the S6 brief: a Storage create over System.IO.Compression; exceptions are mapped at the seam; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO', 'Every kit and catalogue write is atomic: write *.tmp, then replace'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitArchiveStore.fs`, `module KitArchiveStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `KitHistoryStore.fs` (step 167): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6. It opens `System.IO`, `System.IO.Compression`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit` and `OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive`. `type KitArchiveProxy with static member create () : KitArchiveProxy`, unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` (ELEV019), each field following step 197's contract: (a) `listKitTree`: `Directory.EnumerateFileSystemEntries(folder, \"*\", SearchOption.AllDirectories)`, each name made relative to the folder with `\\` turned into `/` and read through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123), a directory as `KitTreeFolder` and a file as `KitTreeFile`, in ordinal order; a missing folder is `KitArchiveIoErr` naming it. (b) `writeKitZip`: it streams into `<zip>.tmp` beside the zip, a `FileStream` (`FileMode.Create`) under a `ZipArchive` in `ZipArchiveMode.Create`: a folder entry is `CreateEntry` of its `zipEntryName` (step 197) and a file entry `CreateEntry(<zipEntryName>, CompressionLevel.Optimal)` with the file's bytes copied in from `File.OpenRead` of its path's segments joined under the kit folder. Entry names come from `zipEntryName` alone. Before each file it reads `observer.cancellation.IsCancellationRequested`: cancelled, it disposes the archive, deletes the `.tmp` and answers `KitArchiveCancelled`. After each file it reports progress. Once the archive is disposed, `File.Move(tmp, zip, true)` puts the zip in place, replacing one of that name, as the save dialog has already asked (step 200). Any exception deletes the `.tmp` and is `KitArchiveIoErr` naming the file or the zip and the exception's message; a zip already at that name keeps its bytes. It streams instead of calling `FileName.writeBytesAtomically` (step 126), because a kit's zip need not fit in memory; the write-then-replace rule is the same. (c) `listZipEntries`: `ZipFile.OpenRead`, each entry's `FullName` through `KitTreeEntry.tryOfZipEntryName` in the archive's order, the first refusal answering its `KitZipEntryEscapesErr`; an IO or `InvalidDataException` is `KitArchiveIoErr` naming the zip. (d) `extractKitZip`: a target that exists and holds any file or folder is `KitZipTargetNotEmptyErr` naming it; otherwise it creates the target when missing, remembering whether it did, opens the zip and, for each entry of `job.entries` in order, creates a folder entry's folder, or copies a file entry's bytes (`archive.GetEntry` of its `zipEntryName`; a missing entry is `KitArchiveIoErr` naming it) into a `FileStream` in `FileMode.CreateNew`, creating its folders. An entry's place is the target joined with its path's `/`-separated segments; every entry being a `KitRelativePath`, no place lies outside the target, and no second check is written. Before each file it reads the cancellation: cancelled, it removes everything it created (the target recursively when it created it, otherwise each file and folder it made) and answers `KitArchiveCancelled`. After each file it reports progress. Any exception removes what it created and is `KitArchiveIoErr`. Every .NET IO and compression exception is caught here; nothing above the proxy handles one (.spec-md §4). A declaration whose signature carries a bare primitive for that IO is marked on itself with `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof IoBoundary, …)>]`, as step 126's are. No package is added: System.IO.Compression ships with .NET. (2) The `KitArchiveProxy` doc (step 197) names `KitArchiveProxy.create` beside the in-memory double in one line. Tests, in `KitArchiveProxyTests.fs`: `type KitArchiveProxyFolderTests () = inherit KitArchiveProxyContract ()` runs every contract fact (steps 197, 198) over a real disk: its root is a new folder `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitArchiveProxyFolderTests\", <a new GUID>)`, never under `%TEMP%` (the `KitProxyFolderTests` precedent, step 126); its archive is `KitArchiveProxy.create ()`; `placeFile` and `placeFolder` create folders and write bytes; `files` and `paths` enumerate recursively. Its own facts: `a zip entry that would escape the folder is refused and nothing is extracted`: for each of `../evil.txt`, `a/../../evil.txt`, `C:/evil.txt` and `..\\evil.txt`, a zip the test writes with `ZipArchive`, holding `.kit-json`, `ok.txt` and that entry, makes `listZipEntries` answer `KitZipEntryEscapesErr` naming the entry and `receiveKit` into `<root>/received` answer the same; `received` does not exist and no `evil.txt` exists under the root or beside it. `a sent kit, received elsewhere and reopened, equals the original kit file by file`: a kit made in `<root>/Optics QZ` through `KitProxy.create` (step 126): `initialiseKit` of a kit file whose `sendExclude` is `**/*.dng`, `writeKindFile` of an experiment file `E1`, `copyInFile` (step 133) into `data/raw` of `run 1.csv` as the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `phi,I\\n0,0.5\\n`, and `data/raw/IMG_0001.DNG` written by the test; it is then opened read-write through `KitContext.openKit` (step 131), so it holds `.oc/lock`, and sent while open to `<root>/exports/Optics QZ.zip`. `receiveKit` into `<root>/received/Optics QZ` answers `Ok`; the received folder opened through `KitContext.openKit (KitProxy.create <it>) ReadOnlyKitAccess` reads a kit file equal to the original's; every file under it equals the original's file of that path byte for byte, the byte-order mark included, and it holds exactly the original's files without `.oc/lock` and the DNG. Both contexts are closed at the end. `the zip's entries are forward-slashed kit-relative names`: `ZipFile.OpenRead` of that zip lists `FullName`s exactly equal to the sent entries' `zipEntryName`s, none holding `\\`, a `:` or a leading `/`. `a zip that cannot replace its file is KitArchiveIoErr and leaves no temporary file`: while the test holds `<root>/exports/k.zip` open with `FileShare.None`, `sendKit` to it answers `KitArchiveIoErr`; once the test lets go, the zip keeps its bytes and `exports` holds no `*.tmp`.", "acceptance": "After the folder archive lands, a test MUST instantiate the real `KitArchiveProxy.create ()` over a folder under the test output, its zips MUST hold forward-slashed kit-relative names and its extraction MUST refuse every escaping entry; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including every `KitArchiveProxyContract` fact under `KitArchiveProxyFolderTests` and its own `a zip entry that would escape the folder is refused and nothing is extracted`, `a sent kit, received elsewhere and reopened, equals the original kit file by file`, `the zip's entries are forward-slashed kit-relative names` and `a zip that cannot replace its file is KitArchiveIoErr and leaves no temporary file`, the count rising by 15; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitArchiveStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitArchive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a kit folder is listed as every file and folder under it, kit-relative, in ordinal order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a zip of the given entries extracts into an empty folder byte for byte, each file reported once", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.extracting into a folder that holds anything is refused and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a zip job cancelled before its next file writes no zip", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.an extraction cancelled before its next file removes everything it wrote", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a kit folder or a zip that is not there is KitArchiveIoErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.sending a kit zips every file and folder but the app cache and what its globs leave out", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a zip is never written inside the kit it holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a received kit holds every sent file byte for byte", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a zip that holds no kit file is refused and nothing is extracted", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a zip's app cache is not received", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a zip entry that would escape the folder is refused and nothing is extracted", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a sent kit, received elsewhere and reopened, equals the original kit file by file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.the zip's entries are forward-slashed kit-relative names", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests.a zip that cannot replace its file is KitArchiveIoErr and leaves no temporary file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitArchiveStore.KitArchiveProxy.create", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitArchiveStore.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-FOLDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number": 200, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S6e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [199], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests"], "how_to": "A zip or an unzip runs off the UI thread with per-file progress and Cancel, through `JobRunner`, and the two dialogs open (.spec-md §10.2: 'Per item: … one zipped file. Each shows a progress bar with Cancel, through JobRunner'; §10.3: one click with Cancel; §6 'Long work: OpticalConstructor.Ui/JobRunner.fs'; the S6 brief: Send kit… through a save dialog defaulting to the exports folder). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob`, compiled directly after `KitOpening.fs` (step 150), before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6. (1) `type KitArchiveFileCount with member this.jobStepCount : JobStepCount` (`JobRunner.fs:JobStepCount`), a file count as the runner's step count; `type KitArchiveProgress with member this.jobProgress (elapsed : JobElapsed) : JobProgress` is `{ completed = this.filesDone.jobStepCount; total = Some this.filesTotal.jobStepCount; elapsed = elapsed }` (`JobRunner.fs:JobProgress`). (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitArchiveJobHandle = { cancelArchiveJob : unit -> unit }`, how a started job is cancelled. (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitArchiveJobHost = { startArchiveJob : (KitArchiveObserver -> Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>) -> KitArchiveJobHandle }`: starts one archive job (step 197) and answers its handle; the job's progress and its end reach the two callbacks the host was built with. (a) `static member posting (post : (unit -> unit) -> unit) (progressed : JobProgress -> unit) (ended : Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError> -> unit) : KitArchiveJobHost` makes a `CancellationTokenSource` per job and runs the job through `JobRunner.startBackground` (`JobRunner.fs:154`) on a thread-pool worker, as `RanToCompletion [ <the job's result> ]`. Its observer's `reportArchiveProgress p` calls `post (fun () -> progressed (p.jobProgress <the elapsed time of a Stopwatch started with the job>))`, and `onDone` calls `post (fun () -> ended <the result>)`; a job that raised (`Error (JobRunExn e)`) ends with `Error (KitArchiveIoErr e.Message)`. The handle's `cancelArchiveJob` cancels the source, which the job reads before its next file. (b) `static member onUiThread (progressed) (ended) : KitArchiveJobHost` is `posting` through Avalonia's `Dispatcher.UIThread.Post`, so a window's messages arrive on its own thread: the host the windows compose. (c) `static member immediate (progressed) (ended) : KitArchiveJobHost` runs the job on the caller's thread before it answers, with a source of its own, calling `progressed` for each file and then `ended`: the host of headless tests. (d) `static member inert : KitArchiveJobHost` runs nothing and answers a handle that does nothing: the default of scenes that run no job. (4) `KitArchiveJobState = { job : JobModel<KitArchiveFileCount>; handleOpt : KitArchiveJobHandle option }`, the one archive job a surface runs: the runner's model (`JobRunner.fs:185`) and the running job's handle. `static member idle : KitArchiveJobState` is `{ job = initModel; handleOpt = None }`; `member this.started (handle : KitArchiveJobHandle) : KitArchiveJobState` passes the job through `updateJob StartRequested` (`JobRunner.fs:233`) and holds the handle; `member this.progressed (progress : JobProgress) : KitArchiveJobState` passes it through `updateJob (ProgressReported progress)`; `member this.cancel () : unit` calls the handle's `cancelArchiveJob` while the job runs. A surface returns to `idle` when its job ends and tells the outcome in its own status, so the view binds the model's `isRunning`, `progress` and `progressText`. (5) `KitArchiveProgressIds = { bar : ConstructorUiId; text : ConstructorUiId; cancel : ConstructorUiId }` and `kitArchiveProgressView (state : KitArchiveJobState) (ids : KitArchiveProgressIds) (cancel : unit -> unit) : IView`, the one progress row of both surfaces: a `DockPanel` whose right child is a `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton` `Cancel` (`negativeBackground`, carrying `ids.cancel`, its press calling `cancel`) and whose fill is a vertical `StackPanel` of a `ProgressBar` carrying `ids.bar` (minimum 0, maximum 1, its value the progress's `fraction`, indeterminate while no progress has come) and a `TextBlock` carrying `ids.text` with `progressText`, or `Starting…` before the first file. Every id is an AutomationId. (6) The dialogs. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: the body of `KitFolderPicker.pickThen` (step 174) moves into `startPick<'Picked> (pick : Async<'Picked option>) (onPicked : 'Picked -> unit) : unit` (start `pick` with `Async.StartImmediate`, call `onPicked` with a chosen value, nothing on `None`), which `pickThen` calls, so one body starts every dialog. In `KitArchiveJob.fs`: `type KitZipPicker with static member ofWindow (owner : TopLevel) (suggested : FolderName) : KitZipPicker` (step 198): `pickZipToWrite name` is `owner.StorageProvider.SaveFilePickerAsync` titled `Send kit`, with `SuggestedFileName` the name, `DefaultExtension` `zip`, one file type `Zip archive` (`*.zip`), `ShowOverwritePrompt` true and `SuggestedStartLocation` the `suggested` folder when `TryGetFolderFromPathAsync` resolves it; `pickZipToOpen ()` is `OpenFilePickerAsync` titled `Open kit from zip`, one file, the same file type and start location. Each answers `Some (FileName path)` of the chosen file's `TryGetLocalPath ()`, and `None` on Cancel, for a file with no local path, or when the provider throws (a host without one): the IO edge in the shape of `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow` (step 150) and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile` (`:3395`); it creates no folder. `member this.pickZipToWriteThen (name : FileName) (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` and `member this.pickZipToOpenThen (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` are `startPick` of the two dialogs. No queue, retry or second job is added: a surface runs one archive job at a time. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs`, `module KitArchiveJobTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. `an immediate job reports each file and then its end on the caller's thread`: `immediate` over recorders, starting a job that reports 1 and 2 of 2 files and answers `Ok (KitArchiveFinished 2)`, has recorded, before `startArchiveJob` answers and on the test's thread, two progresses whose `completed` is 1 and 2 and `total` `Some 2`, then that end. `a posting job hands its cancellation to the run before its next file`: `posting` with a `post` that calls at once, over a job that reports its first file, then waits on a test-local gate and answers `KitArchiveCancelled` when its token is cancelled: once the first progress has arrived (a `ManualResetEventSlim` with a ten-second limit, never a sleep), the fact calls `cancelArchiveJob` and opens the gate, and the recorded end is `Ok KitArchiveCancelled`. `a posting run that raises ends with KitArchiveIoErr carrying its message` : a job raising `IOException \"disk gone\"` ends with `Error (KitArchiveIoErr _)` whose reason contains `disk gone`. `a job state runs from start through progress back to idle`: `idle` is not running and has no progress text; `started` with a recording handle is running; `progressed` of 1 of 3 files reads a progress text starting `1 / 3`; `cancel ()` calls the handle once; `idle` again is not running. `the zip pickers hand on the file the dialog answers and nothing on a cancel`: a `KitZipPicker` whose fields answer `Some` of a test-local zip at once makes `pickZipToWriteThen` and `pickZipToOpenThen` call `onPicked` once with it, and `KitZipPicker.none` never calls it.", "acceptance": "After the job host lands, `KitArchiveJobHost` MUST run an archive job through `JobRunner.startBackground` with per-file progress and a cancel read before each file, `KitArchiveJobState` MUST follow `JobRunner.updateJob`, and `KitZipPicker.ofWindow` MUST open the save and open dialogs; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an immediate job reports each file and then its end on the caller's thread`, `a posting job hands its cancellation to the run before its next file`, `a posting run that raises ends with KitArchiveIoErr carrying its message`, `a job state runs from start through progress back to idle` and `the zip pickers hand on the file the dialog answers and nothing on a cancel`, the count rising by 5, with `pickThen hands on the folder the picker answers and nothing on a cancel` passing as written; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests.an immediate job reports each file and then its end on the caller's thread", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests.a posting job hands its cancellation to the run before its next file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests.a posting run that raises ends with KitArchiveIoErr carrying its message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests.a job state runs from start through progress back to idle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests.the zip pickers hand on the file the dialog answers and nothing on a cancel", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitArchiveJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitArchiveJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitArchiveFileCount.jobStepCount", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitArchiveProgress.jobProgress", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitArchiveJobHandle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitArchiveJobHost", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitArchiveJobState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitArchiveProgressIds", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.kitArchiveProgressView", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitZipPicker.ofWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitZipPicker.pickZipToWriteThen", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitArchiveJob.KitZipPicker.pickZipToOpenThen", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitArchiveJob.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.startPick", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs", "obligations": ["S6-ARCHIVE-JOB"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":201,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S6f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[200],"how_to":"Send kit… as semantic messages of the kit window (001 §P `SendKit`; 001 §O 'Kit menu: Send kit…'; the S5.3 mapper's request: Send kit… joins the kit bar, sending a `TableAndElementRotationMsg`; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message, and the button and the test send the same message; §10.2, §10.4: per-file progress with Cancel, and the completion message updates the model). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) `KitWindowShell` (step 186) gains, each field documented in one line, `zipPicker : KitZipPicker` (the save dialog, step 198), `archive : KitArchiveProxy` (the zip writer, step 197) and `archiveJobs : KitArchiveJobHost` (runs the send off the UI thread, step 200). `inert` holds `KitZipPicker.none`, `KitArchiveProxy.createInMemory (InMemoryArchiveDisk.create ())` and `KitArchiveJobHost.inert`. A record expression that builds a shell in full becomes a record update of `KitWindowShell.inert`: the shell `ConstructorScene.mount` builds in `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs` (step 189) is `{ KitWindowShell.inert with explorer = ExplorerProxy.system; requestClose = window.Close }`, so the windows keep their behaviour until step 233 composes their real archive, and a test shell built in full becomes such an update. (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitSend : KitArchiveJobState` after `kitChanges` (step 187), documented in one line (the window's one send, step 200); `initWith` sets it to `KitArchiveJobState.idle`. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `SendKit of FileName` (send the kit to this zip: the Send kit button's message after its save dialog, and how a test sends a kit), `SendKitProgressed of JobProgress`, `SendKitEnded of Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>` and `CancelSendKit`. (4) Arms. `SendKit zip`: with `kitFolderOpt = None` it sets `kitStatus` to `A kit with no folder cannot be sent.` and starts nothing; while `kitSend.job.isRunning` it answers the model unchanged, one archive job per window; otherwise it calls `model.kitShell.archiveJobs.startArchiveJob (fun observer -> model.kitShell.archive.sendKit model.kit.kitFile folder zip observer)` (step 198), sets `kitSend` to `kitSend.started` of the handle and `kitStatus` to `None`. Sending writes no kit file, so it is not behind the read-only guard (step 185): a kit opened read-only is sent as it is, which is how a reviewer returns a kit (001 §E 'Review round-trip'). `SendKitProgressed p` sets `kitSend` to `kitSend.progressed p`. `SendKitEnded result` sets `kitSend` to `KitArchiveJobState.idle` and `kitStatus` to `The kit was sent: <n> file(s) zipped.` for `Ok (KitArchiveFinished n)`, `Send kit was cancelled: no zip was written.` for `Ok KitArchiveCancelled`, and `The kit could not be sent — <e.describe>` for `Error e`. `CancelSendKit` calls `model.kitSend.cancel ()` and answers the model unchanged; the end message returns it to idle. No queue, retry, overwrite question (the save dialog asks it, step 200) or other message is added. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184), over its folder kits (`openKitAt` under the class's folder) loaded into `initMain ()`, with `kitShell` an update of `KitWindowShell.inert` whose `archive` is `KitArchiveProxy.create ()` (step 199) and whose `archiveJobs` is either `KitArchiveJobHost.immediate` over recorders of the `SendKitProgressed` and `SendKitEnded` messages, which the fact then passes through the update in order, or a test-local deferred host that keeps the job and answers a handle cancelling a source the fact owns. Zips go under the fact's own folder, never inside the kit. `Send kit zips the kit's folder and tells how many files it sent`: `SendKit` of `<fact>/exports/Optics QZ.zip` then the recorded messages leave the zip there; `KitArchiveProxy.create ().listZipEntries` of it holds `.kit-json`, `data` and `library` and no `.oc` entry, though the kit holds `.oc/lock`; `kitStatus` is `The kit was sent: <the zip's file count> file(s) zipped.` and `kitSend` is idle. `a running send shows each zipped file as progress`: after `SendKit` and the first recorded progress only, `kitSend.job.isRunning` holds and its `progressText` starts `1 / `. `a cancelled send writes no zip and says so`: over the deferred host, `SendKit` leaves the job running and no zip; `CancelSendKit` cancels the fact's source; the fact runs the kept job over an observer of that source's token, which answers `Ok KitArchiveCancelled`, and `SendKitEnded` of it sets `kitStatus` to `Send kit was cancelled: no zip was written.`, `kitSend` idle and no zip. `a scratch kit is not sent and no job starts`: over `initMain ()` (the scratch kit), `SendKit` sets `kitStatus` to `A kit with no folder cannot be sent.` and the recorders stay empty. `a send that fails tells why and leaves the window idle`: `SendKit` of a zip inside the kit's folder ends with `kitStatus` containing `inside the kit it holds` and `kitSend` idle. `a kit opened read-only is sent, and its folder is unchanged`: over the kit opened read-only, `SendKit` writes the zip and every file of the kit's folder keeps its bytes.","acceptance":"After the Send kit messages land, `SendKit` MUST start one send of the kit's folder through the shell's job host, `SendKitProgressed` and `SendKitEnded` MUST drive `kitSend` and `kitStatus`, and `CancelSendKit` MUST cancel the running send; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Send kit zips the kit's folder and tells how many files it sent`, `a running send shows each zipped file as progress`, `a cancelled send writes no zip and says so`, `a scratch kit is not sent and no job starts`, `a send that fails tells why and leaves the window idle` and `a kit opened read-only is sent, and its folder is unchanged`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Send kit zips the kit's folder and tells how many files it sent","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a running send shows each zipped file as progress","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a cancelled send writes no zip and says so","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a scratch kit is not sent and no job starts","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a send that fails tells why and leaves the window idle","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only is sent, and its folder is unchanged","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell.zipPicker","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell.archive","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell.archiveJobs","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitSend","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SendKit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SendKitProgressed","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SendKitEnded","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CancelSendKit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-SEND-MESSAGES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number": 202, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S6g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [201], "how_to": "Send kit… in the kit bar's Kit menu, with its progress row (001 §O 'Kit menu: Send kit…, Show in Explorer, Copy experiments from another kit…, Reload changes, Close kit'; 001 §O 'Automation': ids such as `SendKitButton`; the S6 brief: id `SendKitButton`; .spec-md §10.2: a progress bar with Cancel). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the kit-bar group (step 188), each member with a one-line doc: `sendKitButton` (`\"SendKitButton\"`), `sendKitProgressBar` (`\"SendKitProgressBar\"`), `sendKitProgressText` (`\"SendKitProgressText\"`) and `sendKitCancelButton` (`\"SendKitCancelButton\"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs` (step 188), docs one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: the Kit menu's `WrapPanel` gains, first, the verb `Send kit…` (`MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` carrying `sendKitButton`), present when `model.kitFolderOpt` is `Some` and `model.kitSend.job.isRunning` does not hold; its press calls `model.kitShell.zipPicker.pickZipToWriteThen model.kit.kitFile.name.zipFileName (SendKit >> dispatch)` (steps 196, 200, 201), so the dialog suggests `<kit name>.zip` and a cancelled dialog sends nothing. Directly under the verb row, while `model.kitSend.job.isRunning` holds, the bar shows `kitArchiveProgressView model.kitSend { bar = ConstructorUiId.sendKitProgressBar; text = ConstructorUiId.sendKitProgressText; cancel = ConstructorUiId.sendKitCancelButton } (fun () -> dispatch CancelSendKit)` (step 200). Nothing else in the bar changes. Tests, in `KitWindowTests` (step 184), its screens mounted over `kitWindowView` as step 188's are, each model loaded from a folder kit. Without a trait: `the Send kit UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the four ids' texts. `a running send shows its progress bar, its count and Cancel, and hides Send kit`: over a model whose `kitSend` is `started` with a test-local handle and `progressed` by 2 of 5 files, `sendKitProgressText` reads a text starting `2 / 5`, `sendKitProgressBar`'s value is 0.4, `sendKitCancelButton` is present and `sendKitButton` absent; over the idle model `sendKitButton` is present and no progress row exists; over `initMain ()` (the scratch kit) `sendKitButton` is absent. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing Send kit asks for a zip named for the kit and starts the send, and Cancel cancels it`: over a shell whose `zipPicker` records the name it is handed and answers a zip under the fact's folder, and whose `archiveJobs` is a test-local deferred host recording each job and answering a recording handle, pressing `sendKitButton` hands the picker `<the kit's name>.zip`, records one job and shows `sendKitProgressText`; pressing `sendKitCancelButton` calls the handle's cancel once.", "acceptance": "After Send kit joins the kit bar, `sendKitButton` MUST open the save dialog with the kit's zip name and send `SendKit`, and a running send MUST show its progress bar, count and Cancel; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Send kit asks for a zip named for the kit and starts the send, and Cancel cancels it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Send kit UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `a running send shows its progress bar, its count and Cancel, and hides Send kit`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the Send kit UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a running send shows its progress bar, its count and Cancel, and hides Send kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.pressing Send kit asks for a zip named for the kit and starts the send, and Cancel cancels it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.sendKitButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.sendKitProgressBar", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.sendKitProgressText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.sendKitCancelButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S6-SEND-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number": 203, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S6h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [202], "how_to": "The two pure halves of copying experiments between kits: how a copied experiment is named, and which library versions it needs (001 §H 'Between kits: Copy experiments from another kit… brings the experiments with their setups, data files and the items they use'; .spec-md §3.15; the S6 brief: each experiment is copied with the library snapshots it needs, and clashing names get S4.1's suffix rule). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `Experiment` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) gains `static member renumberedFor (taken : ExperimentId list) (incoming : Experiment list) : Experiment list`. An experiment is stored under its id (`E<n>`, `ExperimentId.fileStem`, step 146), so a name clash is an id clash, and the suffix rule of an id-named file is the next free id. In order, an incoming experiment keeps its id when no id of `taken` and no id given to an earlier incoming experiment equals it; otherwise it takes the `next` (`Experiments.fs:139`) of the highest id among `taken`, every incoming id and every id given so far. Only `id` changes, and the order is kept. S8.3 and S9.1, which give experiments template names, carry the rule over to names. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`: the depth-first walk of `KitLibraryContext.snapshotReferences` (step 139) moves into `referenceClosure (resolve : EntryReference -> Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, KitLibraryError>) (references : EntryReference list) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope list, KitLibraryError>`, declared before `KitLibraryContext`'s members: it resolves each reference through `resolve`, then walks each resolved envelope's `content.references` (step 137) depth first and in order, visiting every version (`libraryVersionRef`, step 137) once, and answers the visited envelopes in visit order; the first error stops it. `snapshotReferences` calls it with its own resolution (the kit's snapshot of a version, otherwise the library's held or latest envelope) and then pins and writes the versions the kit lacks exactly as before, so its walk exists once. No other member is added. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `copied experiments keep their ids unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free id`: with `taken` [1; 2], incoming E2 and E3 answer E4 (E2's experiment) and E3, in that order; with `taken` empty the incoming are unchanged; with `taken` [5], incoming E1, E5 and E2 answer E1, E6 and E2; every field but `id` is unchanged. `KitLibraryTests` (step 139) gains `the closure of references walks each entry's references depth first, each version once`: over a resolver reading `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`'s envelopes (`EntryVersionReference` by id and version, `EntryLatestReference` by the highest version, anything else `UnheldEntryErr`), the references [multilayer v1; multilayer v1] (`SampleIds.multilayerQwId`) answer the sample, then each of its materials followed by that material's category, each version once, in the order step 139's first fact writes them; a reference to a test-local GUID answers `UnheldEntryErr`. Every other `KitLibraryTests` fact passes as written.", "acceptance": "After the copy's pure halves land, `Experiment.renumberedFor` MUST keep every free id and give a clashing experiment the next free id, and `KitLibrary.referenceClosure` MUST hold the one depth-first walk that `snapshotReferences` calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `copied experiments keep their ids unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free id` and `the closure of references walks each entry's references depth first, each version once`, the count rising by 2, with every other `KitLibraryTests` fact passing as written; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.copied experiments keep their ids unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-COPY-PLAN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.the closure of references walks each entry's references depth first, each version once", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-COPY-PLAN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.renumberedFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S6-COPY-PLAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.referenceClosure", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S6-COPY-PLAN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number": 204, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S6i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [203], "how_to": "A kit's lab file read whole, as the bytes a copy carries to another kit (the S6 brief: each experiment is copied with the data files it references, into data/, hashes re-recorded; 001 §E 'Lab files are read-only for the app'). `readDataFile` (step 128) answers a decoded text, which would drop a byte-order mark and cannot carry a binary file, so the copy reads bytes. (1) `KitProxy` (`KitFolders.fs`, steps 125-138) gains `readLabFile : KitRelativePath -> Result<LabFileSource, KitError>` with a one-line doc: the file at that path inside the kit as a `LabFileSource` (step 132), its absolute name in the kit folder and its bytes as stored, or `MissingKitFileErr` naming the path. Any file of the kit can be read so. It writes nothing, so `readOnlyView` (step 131) passes it through. A record expression that builds a `KitProxy` in full gains the field. (2) `KitProxy.createInMemory` (step 125): the absolute name is the path under `folder.kitFolder` (step 133), joined with `/`, and the bytes are the UTF-8 bytes of the stored text, as its `readDataFile` hashes them. (3) `KitProxy.create` (`KitFolderStore.fs`, step 126): the path's segments joined under the kit folder with the platform's separator name the file, whose bytes are read whole; a missing file is `MissingKitFileErr` and an IO exception `KitIoErr`, as in step 126. No cache, retry or other field is added. Tests, in `KitProxyTests.fs`. A new `KitProxyContract` fact (step 125), so `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` both run it: `a lab file is read whole by its kit-relative path, with its absolute name in the kit`: over an initialised folder with `data/raw/run 1.csv` placed as `phi,I\\n0,0.5\\n`, `readLabFile` of that path answers `content` equal to the UTF-8 bytes of that text, `file` equal to `absoluteName \"data/raw/run 1.csv\"` (step 133), and `ContentHash.ofBytes` of the content equal to `readDataFile`'s hash; a path never placed answers `MissingKitFileErr`; through `readOnlyView` the same answers come and `paths` is unchanged. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains `a lab file's bytes are read as stored, a byte-order mark included`: a file written by the test as the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `a,b\\n` reads back as exactly those bytes.", "acceptance": "After the whole read lands, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST answer a lab file's absolute name and bytes by its kit-relative path, and `readOnlyView` MUST pass `readLabFile` through; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a lab file is read whole by its kit-relative path, with its absolute name in the kit` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, and `a lab file's bytes are read as stored, a byte-order mark included`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests.a lab file is read whole by its kit-relative path, with its absolute name in the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-LAB-FILE-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a lab file is read whole by its kit-relative path, with its absolute name in the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-LAB-FILE-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests.a lab file's bytes are read as stored, a byte-order mark included", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyFolderTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S6-LAB-FILE-READ"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitFolders.KitProxy.readLabFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "obligations": ["S6-LAB-FILE-READ"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":205,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Optimization","BerremanTests","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[204],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests"],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. One home for the parameter vocabulary that items, item models and the fitter share, compiled early enough for the library entries and the kit (the S7.1 brief: a Parameter's name REUSES `MuellerInverse.ParameterName` and a dial's sign REUSES `MuellerReconstruction.DialSign`; .spec-md §4: a reuse is a move). `MuellerInverse.fs` and `MuellerReconstruction.fs` compile last in Domain, after `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (step 24) and `Kit.fs` (step 122), which must name both types, so both MOVE. This step changes no behaviour. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`: `module ItemModels` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ElementId.fs` and before `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (one `<Compile Include=\"ItemModels.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment). Its module doc is one to three lines: the parameter vocabulary of items and item models (spec 0050 S7.1). (2) `ParameterName` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ParameterName`, the single-case union over `string` with `.value`) moves into it unchanged; its doc keeps its text and adds that spec 0050 S7.1 moved it here. `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels` and declares it no more, so `ParameterAxis.name` and every axis list read the moved type. (3) `DialSign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:DialSign`: `DialPositive` | `DialNegative` with `member this.value : float`, +1 / −1) moves after it unchanged, its doc likewise. `MuellerReconstruction.fs` opens `ItemModels`, and `AnalyzerModel.dialSign` and `physicalAngle` read it as today. (4) The consumers open the module where the compiler asks and change nothing else: `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/DesignParameters.fs`; and in `Berreman/BerremanTests/` `InverseFitHarness.fs`, `MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `OptimizationTests.fs` and `MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`. No alias, re-export or second declaration remains (ELEV014), so `git grep -n -E \"type (ParameterName|DialSign) =\" -- Berreman/` finds only `ItemModels.fs`. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs`, `module ItemModelsTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels`. `the moved parameter name and dial sign keep their values`: `(ParameterName \"c2.retardance\").value` is `c2.retardance`, `DialPositive.value` is 1.0 and `DialNegative.value` is −1.0. No BerremanTests fact changes. `OptimizationTests` (whose fixture builds `ParameterName` values) and `MuellerReconstructionTests` (whose analyzer models carry `DialPositive` and `DialNegative`) are the cheapest BerremanTests classes that exercise the two types, and they run unchanged.","acceptance":"After the move, `ParameterName` and `DialSign` MUST be declared only in `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`, compiled before `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`; unit-tests MUST pass over `OptimizationTests` and `MuellerReconstructionTests` with their numbers unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the moved parameter name and dial sign keep their values`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests","BerremanTests.OptimizationTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/DesignParameters.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/OptimizationTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.the moved parameter name and dial sign keep their values","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-NAME-MOVE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.ParameterName","op":"retire","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-NAME-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-NAME-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.DialSign","op":"retire","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-NAME-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-NAME-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-NAME-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.DialSign","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-NAME-MOVE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":206,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[205],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Define the detector noise data required by 001 §I without moving the bench implementation before 001 §Q / §S10. In OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs, after ParameterName and DialSign from step 205: `ParameterValue of double` with `.value`, one parameter's number in its kind's unit. `ParameterKind` = `AngleParameter` (radians: an azimuth, an axis or dial offset, an ellipticity angle, a rotation uncertainty) | `PhaseParameter` (radians: a retardance) | `FractionParameter` (dimensionless in [0, 1]: an extinction ratio, a diattenuation, a degree of polarization, an element or throughput uncertainty) | `ScaleParameter` (a dimensionless multiplier: an intensity scale, a gain) | `MuellerElementParameter` (one Mueller-matrix element) | `ThicknessParameter` (metres) | `ReadingParameter` (a detector reading in its own units: a dark offset). `ItemParameterAxis = { name : ParameterName; kind : ParameterKind; defaultValue : ParameterValue }` is one parameter a model publishes. Detector model files store their axis descriptors, so ParameterKind MUST carry stable integer wire tags 1 through 7 in the declaration order above and tryOfWire : int -> ParameterKind option, with zero and unrecognized tags returning None. Its text rendering MUST remain separate from its tag. On ItemParameterAxis, declare static member detectorNoiseAxes (rotation : ParameterValue) (element : ParameterValue) (throughput : ParameterValue) : ItemParameterAxis list. It MUST return rotationUncertainty with AngleParameter, then elementUncertainty and throughputUncertainty with FractionParameter, preserving the supplied values. A detector model MUST carry that ItemParameterAxis list; an instantiated item carries the corresponding ordinary Parameter states. Domain MUST NOT declare or reference AngleUncertainty, ElementUncertainty, ThroughputUncertainty or NoiseParam. Their sole declarations MUST remain in Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs until step 339 moves all four to Optimization/BenchNoise.fs. No new noise-budget record, duplicated bench constants, dependency from Domain to Optimization, or product reference to a test assembly is permitted. In ItemModelsTests, add `the detector noise axes keep their declared quantities`: construct elevated test-local rotation, element and throughput values (0.001 radians, 0.02 and 0.03), call detectorNoiseAxes, and assert names, kinds, order and exact defaults. This data-projection test MUST NOT claim to test a promoted bench model. The axis fact MUST verify every ParameterKind tag round-trips and that zero and an unrecognized tag return None.","acceptance":"After detector noise axes are defined, Domain MUST publish the three named axes with the supplied values, without declaring any bench-noise type; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass including `the detector noise axes keep their declared quantities`, the count rising by 1; build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.the detector noise axes keep their declared quantities","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-NOISE-MOVE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterValue","op":"create","obligations":["S71-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterKind","op":"create","obligations":["S71-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemParameterAxis","op":"create","obligations":["S71-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes","op":"create","obligations":["S71-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterKind.value","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterKind.tryOfWire","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-NOISE-MOVE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":207,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71c","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[206],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. What a parameter is, and the parameters the existing models publish (001 §I: 'Each model publishes its parameter axes, so the fitter's ParameterAxis list is generated, not hand-written'; the S7.1 brief: names, kinds, defaults, an item's parameters created from them; .spec-md §3.14: the source preset, the ideal LP / CP presets and the stack `Sample` are models themselves). In `ItemModels.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `Berreman.Media` (`Thickness`), `OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary` and `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Library`. Using step 206's ParameterValue, ParameterKind and ItemParameterAxis, add the three physics type extensions, each member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list. (a) On `SourcePreset` (`ElementId.fs:SourcePreset`), the light source over the preset's λ (001 §I 'Light source | λ or tunable limits (exists) + output polarization (azimuth, ellipticity, degree of polarization) + an intensity scale'): `azimuth` and `ellipticity` (`AngleParameter`, 0), `degreeOfPolarization` (`FractionParameter`, 0) and `intensityScale` (`ScaleParameter`, 1), so the default is unpolarized light at unit scale (001 §N). λ and the tunable limits stay the preset's, as today. (b) On `PolarizerPreset` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`): `[]`, because an ideal LP or CP, or a constant-Mueller compound, has no parameter (001 §I 'Ideal LP / ideal CP | None'). (c) On `Sample` (`ElementId.fs:Sample`): one `ThicknessParameter` per layer of finite thickness, in stack order, defaulting to that thickness in metres. A `SingleLayer` at film position k (1-based) is `film<k>.thickness`; layer j of a `Repeated` group at position k is `film<k>.layer<j>.thickness`, shared by every period; the substrate plate is `substrate.thickness`; a layer of `Thickness.Infinity` publishes nothing. `type Thickness with member this.parameterValueOpt : ParameterValue option` (`Infinity` is `None`) is the one conversion. A sample's materials publish nothing here: a study opens a material version and owns its unknowns (001 §I 'Material parameters as unknowns'; S11.1). No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `ItemModelsTests` (step 206), each comparing axis lists with `=`: `a source preset publishes the light-source parameters, unpolarized at unit scale`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633).parameterAxes` is exactly the four axes above. `an ideal polarizer preset publishes no parameter`: the polarizer of `BuiltinCatalogue.preset PresetIds.polarizerLp` publishes `[]`. `a sample publishes one thickness per finite layer`: `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId).parameterAxes` is one `substrate.thickness` axis at 1e-3 and `SampleIds.glassFilm600Id`'s one `film1.thickness` axis at 6e-7 (each value within 1e-15); a test-local structure of one 5 nm layer and a `Repeated` group over a 10 nm and a 20 nm cell answers `film1.thickness`, `film2.layer1.thickness` and `film2.layer2.thickness` in that order. `a noise budget publishes its three uncertainties at its own values`: ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes over the three elevated test-local inputs of step 206 MUST give those axes, names, kinds and defaults unchanged.","acceptance":"After the vocabulary lands, `SourcePreset.parameterAxes` MUST publish the four light-source parameters at unpolarized unit scale, `PolarizerPreset.parameterAxes` none, `Sample.parameterAxes` one thickness per finite layer and `NoiseParam.parameterAxes` its three uncertainties; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a source preset publishes the light-source parameters, unpolarized at unit scale`, `an ideal polarizer preset publishes no parameter`, `a sample publishes one thickness per finite layer` and `a noise budget publishes its three uncertainties at its own values`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a source preset publishes the light-source parameters, unpolarized at unit scale","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.an ideal polarizer preset publishes no parameter","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a sample publishes one thickness per finite layer","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a noise budget publishes its three uncertainties at its own values","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.SourcePreset.parameterAxes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.PolarizerPreset.parameterAxes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.Sample.parameterAxes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.Thickness.parameterValueOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-AXES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":208,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71d","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[207],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The parameterised item models of 001 §I as data, and the parameters each publishes (001 §I table; the S7.1 brief's payload rows; .spec-md §3.14: every item MUST instantiate an ItemModel entry; source, ideal-polarizer and stack forms reuse the physics of step 207 through typed bindings). In `ItemModels.fs`, after step 207's extensions, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `Berreman.Fields` (`WaveLength`). (1) `PolarizerLeakage` = `ExtinctionRatioLeakage` (its parameter is the extinction ratio T_min / T_max) | `DiattenuationLeakage` (its parameter is the diattenuation (T_max − T_min) / (T_max + T_min)): how a real linear polarizer states its leakage. (2) `RetardanceDispersion` = `ConstantRetardance` (δ is the same at every λ) | `InverseWaveLengthRetardance of WaveLength` (δ is the retardance at that reference λ and scales as λ_ref / λ, a zero-order plate's dispersion): 'dispersive where the model says so'. (3) `BlackBoxNormalisation` = `SixteenElementMueller` (all sixteen elements are parameters) | `FifteenElementsAndScale` (a scale and the fifteen elements normalised by m00). (4) `OpticalForm` = `RealPolarizerModel of PolarizerLeakage` | `RetarderPlateModel of RetardanceDispersion` | `BlackBoxMuellerModel of BlackBoxNormalisation` | `CompoundModel of CompoundComponent list`, with `and CompoundComponent = { form : OpticalForm; offset : Angle }`: what one optical element does to light. A compound is its components in light order, each turned by its fixed offset within the compound, which generalises `ConstantMueller` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerBehavior`) with parameters (001 §I 'CPL = LP · Retarder(axis = 45° + Δ, δ)'). A black-box matrix is held at reference orientation and turned as R(−φ) M R(φ) like any element (001 §I). (5) `ItemModelForm` = `SourcePresetItemModel` | `IdealPolarizerItemModel` | `StackSampleItemModel` | `OpticalElementModel of OpticalForm` | `EmptySlotModel` (the identity, the calibration reference) | `IntensityDetectorModel of ItemParameterAxis list` (records S₀ through a gain and a dark offset) | `MuellerPolarimeterModel of ItemParameterAxis list` (records a full Mueller matrix) | `EllipsometerModel of ItemParameterAxis list` (records Ψ and Δ): the payload of an item-model library entry, a detector's budget being its noise axes' defaults. Evaluating a form to a Mueller matrix or a reading is the run law's (001 §N, S8.1), not this step's. (6) `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` on `OpticalForm` and on `ItemModelForm`. `RealPolarizerModel` publishes `extinctionRatio` (`FractionParameter`, 0) under `ExtinctionRatioLeakage` or `diattenuation` (`FractionParameter`, 1) under `DiattenuationLeakage`, then `axisOffset` (`AngleParameter`, 0), so its defaults are the ideal linear polarizer. `RetarderPlateModel` publishes `retardance` (`PhaseParameter`, π / 2, a quarter wave) and `fastAxisOffset` (`AngleParameter`, 0) under either dispersion. `BlackBoxMuellerModel` publishes, under `SixteenElementMueller`, `m00` … `m33` (`m<row><column>`, row-major, `MuellerElementParameter`) at the identity, and under `FifteenElementsAndScale` `scale` (`ScaleParameter`, 1) followed by the fifteen `m<row><column>` other than `m00` at the identity. `CompoundModel` publishes, for its component k (1-based, light order), each axis of the component's form renamed `c<k>.<name>`, kind and default kept, so a compound inside a compound prefixes twice (`c2.c1.retardance`). `OpticalElementModel f` publishes `f`'s axes; `EmptySlotModel` publishes nothing; `IntensityDetectorModel noise` publishes `gain` (`ScaleParameter`, 1) and `darkOffset` (`ReadingParameter`, 0) followed by `noise` (step 207); `MuellerPolarimeterModel noise` and `EllipsometerModel noise` publish `noise`. The gain's session scope is the study's (001 §L, S11.1). Names are unique within a form. The source, ideal-polarizer and stack forms MUST declare the corresponding typed binding kind and derive their bound parameter axes by calling the SourcePreset, PolarizerPreset and Sample parameterAxes members from step 207; they MUST NOT copy those computations. Their unbound parameterAxes MUST contain no binding-dependent axes; the resolved choice in step 216 supplies them. No evaluator is added here. Tests, in `ItemModelsTests`, comparing names, kinds and defaults (angles within 1e-15): `a real linear polarizer publishes its leakage and its axis offset`: both leakages, defaults 0 and 1, then `axisOffset` 0. `a retarder plate publishes its retardance at a quarter wave and its fast-axis offset`: `retardance` π / 2 and `fastAxisOffset` 0 under `ConstantRetardance` and under `InverseWaveLengthRetardance` of 632.8 nm (`WaveLength.nm`). `a compound publishes its components' parameters under their light-order prefixes` : the compound of a real LP by extinction ratio at 0° and a constant retarder at 45° publishes `c1.extinctionRatio`, `c1.axisOffset`, `c2.retardance` and `c2.fastAxisOffset` with the components' kinds and defaults; that compound as the second component of a compound after a black box publishes `c2.c1.extinctionRatio` among its names. `a black-box Mueller matrix publishes sixteen elements, or a scale and fifteen, at the identity`: sixteen names `m00` … `m33` with 1 on the diagonal and 0 elsewhere; `scale` then fifteen names without `m00`. `an empty slot publishes nothing and each detector its gain, dark offset and noise as its form says`: over `detectorNoiseAxes`, the intensity detector publishes `gain`, `darkOffset`, `rotationUncertainty`, `elementUncertainty` and `throughputUncertainty`, the polarimeter and the ellipsometer the last three, and `EmptySlotModel` `[]`. The detectorNoiseAxes fixture MUST use step 206's constructor over elevated test-local values; the list payload is the model's three noise axes. Every detector MUST publish that list unchanged.","acceptance":"After the forms land, `ItemModelForm` MUST hold the optical element, empty slot and three detector forms, and every form's `parameterAxes` MUST publish the names, kinds and defaults specified, a compound's under `c<k>.` prefixes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a real linear polarizer publishes its leakage and its axis offset`, `a retarder plate publishes its retardance at a quarter wave and its fast-axis offset`, `a compound publishes its components' parameters under their light-order prefixes`, `a black-box Mueller matrix publishes sixteen elements, or a scale and fifteen, at the identity` and `an empty slot publishes nothing and each detector its gain, dark offset and noise as its form says`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel and StackSampleItemModel MUST also be serializable ItemModel forms whose bound axes reuse the named physics members.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a real linear polarizer publishes its leakage and its axis offset","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a retarder plate publishes its retardance at a quarter wave and its fast-axis offset","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a compound publishes its components' parameters under their light-order prefixes","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a black-box Mueller matrix publishes sixteen elements, or a scale and fifteen, at the identity","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.an empty slot publishes nothing and each detector its gain, dark offset and noise as its form says","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.PolarizerLeakage","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.RetardanceDispersion","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.BlackBoxNormalisation","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.OpticalForm","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.CompoundComponent","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelForm","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.OpticalForm.parameterAxes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelForm.parameterAxes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-MODEL-FORMS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":209,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-S71e","id":"STORE_BigBoy_0006","name":"ItemModelProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[208],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests"],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item-model library store's seam in Domain: the entry, its identity, its errors, its record and its in-memory double, with a contract suite any store runs (001 §I '`ItemModel` — parameterised physics, a library entry'; 001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite create', 'Contract tests'; the S7.1 brief: a proxy record, an in-memory implementation and a SQLite create, the S2 pattern; .spec-md §3.3: built-ins are named through well-known ids). In `ItemModels.fs`, after step 208's forms, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1; the file opens `System` (`Guid`). (1) `ItemModelId of Guid` with `.value`, an item model's frozen GUID. `ItemModelVersionId = { itemModelId : ItemModelId; version : VersionNumber }`, one version of one item model, which an item pins (001 §I 'the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'). (2) `ItemModelEntry = { id : ItemModelId; name : EntryName; description : EntryDescription; model : ItemModelForm; protection : EntryProtection }`, shaped like `PolarizerPreset` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`): its protection derives from its provenance at the file seam (step 210). `ItemModelVersion = { version : VersionNumber; entry : ItemModelEntry }`, one stored version, with `member this.versionId : ItemModelVersionId`. (3) `module ItemModelIds`, shaped like `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (no `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]`, no `[<Literal>]`, each a typed value written `Guid.Parse \"…\" |> ItemModelId`), the frozen identities of the eleven built-in item models step 210 ships: `realLinearPolarizerModelId` `940bda4e-db9c-4103-b59c-dab2f3ee5875`; `retarderPlateModelId` `8e9797b7-f0db-443f-b33d-61f9901881cd`; `circularPolarizerModelId` `33486eec-836a-4cbf-ac79-e3f14439ad4b`; `blackBoxMuellerModelId` `852cbb95-e9f8-4963-8098-866303071e67`; `emptySlotModelId` `628b87f6-8e8c-460b-8a91-1815063aa9dd`; `intensityDetectorModelId` `01cfdc64-d07e-4e2b-963e-ea3caa8428e6`; `muellerPolarimeterModelId` `7e74324f-ded2-4607-b9d8-a40d477ac437`; `ellipsometerModelId` `608caa06-1b53-464e-962f-073730270af6`. (4) `ItemModelError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `DuplicateItemModelErr` (the store already holds an item model under the id, naming it and its held version), `InvalidItemModelErr` (the store cannot hold the entry: a protection or an id it refuses, naming why) and `ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr` (the store beneath failed, carrying the failure's `describe`). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `the item model is already held: <reason>`, `the item model cannot be stored: <reason>` and `the item-model store is unavailable: <reason>`. (5) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ItemModelProxy = { listItemModels : unit -> Result<ItemModelVersion list, ItemModelError>; resolveItemModelVersion : ItemModelVersionId -> Result<ItemModelVersion option, ItemModelError>; saveItemModel : ItemModelVersion -> Result<unit, ItemModelError> }`, the functional-proxy convention of `ElementId.fs:SourceProxy`. Its doc states the contract: `listItemModels` answers the latest version of every item model, ordered by name and then by id; `resolveItemModelVersion` answers that exact version or `None`; `saveItemModel` stores a new item model at the given version and refuses an id the store already holds with `DuplicateItemModelErr`, changing nothing, because an item model is never edited in this spec and a later version arrives through the import seam (step 95). (6) `static member createInMemory () : ItemModelProxy`, the in-memory double: a closure-local map from `ItemModelId` to its saved version, mutated only inside the closure as in `CatalogueProxy.createInMemory` (step 32). It holds what it is given, built-ins included, because step 210's in-memory import pushes the shipped item models through it. No cache, retry, removal, edit or other field is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs`, `module ItemModelProxyTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its entries are test-local `UserManaged` item models under test-local GUIDs: `Lab retarder` (a constant retarder) and `Lab polarizer` (a real LP by diattenuation). `[<AbstractClass>] type ItemModelProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshItemModels : unit -> ItemModelProxy`, a store holding no item model, and three `[<Fact>]` members. `an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version`: `Lab retarder` saved at version 2 resolves at version 2 to the saved version, and answers `None` at version 1 and under another id. `the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name`: after `Lab retarder` and `Lab polarizer` are saved, `listItemModels` answers `Lab polarizer` then `Lab retarder`. `saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version`: a second save under `Lab retarder`'s id, at version 3 and with another name, answers `DuplicateItemModelErr` naming the id; version 2 still resolves to the first, and version 3 answers `None`. `type ItemModelProxyTests () = inherit ItemModelProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store (`freshItemModels` is `ItemModelProxy.createInMemory ()`), with its own fact `every item-model error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. ItemModelIds MUST additionally declare sourcePresetItemModelId with the frozen GUID 239b0cfb-9938-5f3b-a767-c4252ea671b6. ItemModelIds MUST additionally declare idealPolarizerItemModelId with the frozen GUID d47e5ce3-3e74-5058-848e-3aa54930e377. ItemModelIds MUST additionally declare stackSampleItemModelId with the frozen GUID 4d13ecb1-2006-576f-99e7-e8bc266e8624.","acceptance":"After the contract lands, `ItemModels.fs` MUST declare `ItemModelProxy` with exactly the fields `listItemModels`, `resolveItemModelVersion` and `saveItemModel`, its in-memory double, the entry types and the eleven `ItemModelIds`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version`, `the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name` and `saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version` under `ItemModelProxyTests` and `every item-model error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests.an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests.the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests.saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests.every item-model error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelId","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelVersionId","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelEntry","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelVersion","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelIds","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelProxy","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ItemModelProxy.createInMemory","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-SEAM"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":210,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[209],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item model becomes a library kind with its file, its schema and its import, and the built-in item models ship in the Built-in catalogue (001 §A 'Library extensions: … .item-model-json'; 001 §B; 001 §I; the S7.1 brief: LibraryEntryKind gains it, `.item-model-json` with a schema, CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel, the built-in item models are written once through the export path and added to Catalogue/Builtin/ with the manifest updated, and there is no code seed; .spec-md §3.14; step 24: 'S7.1 adds the item-model kind'; step 57: a section that adds a built-in kind changes the integrity counts in the step that adds it). The kind, its rows and the facts that count them land together, because `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests` requires every kind of `LibraryEntryKind.all` to have rows. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (steps 24, 25, 137) opens `ItemModels`; each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (a) `LibraryEntryKind` gains `ItemModelEntryKind` after `CategoryEntryKind`: `value` 7 (`tryOfWire 7` answers it), extension `.item-model-json` (001 §A), schema version 1; `all` lists the seven in tag order, and its doc and step 24's 'S7.1 adds' remark say so. (b) Beside step 24's id extensions, `type ItemModelId with member this.toLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId`, the same GUID; after `EntryReference` (step 137), `type ItemModelVersionId with member this.entryReference : EntryReference`, the `EntryVersionReference` of that GUID at that version. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006). (c) `LibraryEntryPayload` gains `ItemModelPayload of ItemModelForm`, of kind `ItemModelEntryKind`. (d) The builder `static member ofItemModel (version : VersionNumber) (provenance : EntryProvenance) (entry : ItemModelEntry) : Result<LibraryEntryContent, LibraryEntryError>`, as step 25's preset builders: an `entry.protection` other than `provenance.protection` is `ProvenanceMismatchErr` naming the entry; otherwise the content holds the entry's id, name, `categoryOpt = None`, `descriptionOpt = Some entry.description` and `ItemModelPayload entry.model`. The decoder `member this.toItemModel : Result<ItemModelEntry, LibraryEntryError>` is marked as step 25's decoders are (`StorageBoundary`: the file's entry GUID becomes the item model's id): another payload is `EntryKindMismatchErr`, no description `MissingEntryFieldErr`, and the protection comes from the provenance. (e) `references` (step 137): an item model answers `[]`, because its components are inline forms, not entries. (2) Every match on `LibraryEntryKind` or `LibraryEntryPayload` the compiler now reports incomplete (FS0025 is an error) gains the case, and no wildcard is added. Among them: `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`' apply order (step 94: item models after detectors); `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs`' `schemaFile` and its per-kind lazies (step 30: `schema/library-item-model.schema.json`); `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`' `facetRows` (step 64: an item model has none); and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`' `LibraryEntryKind.caption` (step 107: `Item model`). (3) The import seam: the brief's 'CatalogueImport gains saveItemModel' is realised on step 94's kind-neutral seam. `InMemoryCatalogueStores` gains `itemModels : ItemModelProxy`, built by `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` with `ItemModelProxy.createInMemory ()` (step 209). A put of an item-model id its map does not hold decodes the envelope with `toItemModel` and pushes `{ version = content.version; entry = … }` through `saveItemModel`, as step 94's adapters push the other kinds; `UndecodableEntryErr`, or an `ItemModelError` answered as `ImportRejectedErr` with its `describe`, stops the put before the map changes. The database seam (`createInDatabase`, step 95) already stores every kind's envelope and is unchanged. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-item-model.schema.json`, written as step 30's per-kind schemas (`$id` `https://berreman/schema/library-item-model.json`, referencing `library-common.schema.json`): `schema` is `{ kind: 7, version: <a positive integer> }` unconditionally; under `schema.version` 1 every key is present and no other, `id` a GUID, `name` a non-empty string, `categoryOpt` `null`, `descriptionOpt` a string, `payload` the item-model case with its form bound by the serializer, `provenance` one of the common shapes and `contentHash` the hash pattern. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside the other library schemas in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. (5) The built-ins go through the export path once, as step 35's did. New throw-away `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` loads the Release x64 build exactly as step 35's tool did (`#I` the `OpticalConstructor.Tests` output, `#r` the Domain and Storage assemblies and what they load, no `#r \"nuget:\"`). It reads the catalogue through `(CatalogueProxy.create (FolderName (Path.Combine(__SOURCE_DIRECTORY__, \"Builtin\")))).readCatalogue ()` (step 33), seals the eleven item models below as `ProtectedBuiltIn` entries at `VersionNumber.first` under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue` through `ofItemModel` and `sealed` (step 30), builds `CatalogueData.tryCreate CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue (CatalogueName \"Built-in\") VersionNumber.first` over the catalogue's envelopes followed by the eleven, and writes it back through the same proxy's `writeCatalogue`. Any `Error` prints its case and exits 1. Build, run `dotnet fsi Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` once from the repository root, and commit the eleven new files and the rewritten `.catalogue-json`; every other entry file is rewritten byte for byte, so git shows no change in it. The catalogue keeps version 1, because no release exists; its manifest hash changes, which is what the start-up import compares (001 §B). The eleven, by `ItemModelIds` member, name, form and description: (a) `realLinearPolarizerModelId`, `Real linear polarizer`, `OpticalElementModel (RealPolarizerModel ExtinctionRatioLeakage)`, described 'A linear polarizer with an extinction ratio and an axis offset; at its defaults it is the ideal linear polarizer.'; (b) `retarderPlateModelId`, `Retarder plate`, `OpticalElementModel (RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance)`, described 'A wave plate with a retardance and a fast-axis offset; at its defaults it is a quarter-wave plate.'; (c) `circularPolarizerModelId`, `Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder)`, `OpticalElementModel (CompoundModel [ { form = RealPolarizerModel ExtinctionRatioLeakage; offset = 0° }; { form = RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance; offset = 45° } ])`, described 'A linear polarizer followed in light order by a retarder whose fast axis sits at 45° plus its own offset.'; (d) `blackBoxMuellerModelId`, `Black-box Mueller matrix`, `OpticalElementModel (BlackBoxMuellerModel SixteenElementMueller)`, described 'A sample known only by its sixteen Mueller elements at reference orientation; at its defaults it is the identity.'; (e) `emptySlotModelId`, `Empty slot (air)`, `EmptySlotModel`, described 'Nothing in the beam: the identity, the calibration reference.'; (f) `intensityDetectorModelId`, `Intensity detector (gain, dark offset and noise)`, `IntensityDetectorModel detectorNoiseAxes`, described 'Records the intensity S0 through a gain and a dark offset, with the decent-lab noise budget.'; (g) `muellerPolarimeterModelId`, `Mueller polarimeter`, `MuellerPolarimeterModel detectorNoiseAxes`, described 'Records a full Mueller matrix, with the decent-lab noise budget.'; (h) `ellipsometerModelId`, `Ellipsometer (noise budget)`, `EllipsometerModel detectorNoiseAxes`, described 'Records Psi and Delta, with the decent-lab noise budget.'. Their files are named by step 24's rule (`Real linear polarizer.item-model-json` and the rest, exactly this step's effects), LF-only, and `git check-ignore` reports none of them. Step 212 deletes the tool. (6) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs` (step 41, linked into the UI suite) gains `itemModels () : ItemModelVersion list`, the catalogue's item-model rows decoded in row order at their versions, and `itemModel (id : ItemModelId) : ItemModelVersion`, failing with the id when the catalogue holds none, each with a one-line doc. (7) Tests. `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests`' `the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present` (step 57) counts 11 item models beside its other kinds. It gains `the shipped item models include every required form under their well-known ids`: `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` holds exactly the eleven above by id, name and form, each at version 1 and `ProtectedBuiltIn`, and each envelope's provenance is `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension` (step 24) covers seven tags, `None` for 0 and 8, and `.item-model-json`. It gains `an item-model builder and decoder are inverse, and a protection its provenance disagrees with is refused`: a test-local `UserManaged` compound under `UserProvenance` decodes to itself through `ofItemModel` and `toItemModel`; a `ProtectedBuiltIn` entry under `UserProvenance` answers `ProvenanceMismatchErr`; and `toItemModel` of Silicon's content answers `EntryKindMismatchErr`. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures` expects the tape to end with every item-model envelope, in row order, after the detectors. The same one-time exporter MUST also write Light source (preset binding).item-model-json under ItemModelIds.sourcePresetItemModelId, form SourcePresetItemModel, version 1 and ProtectedBuiltIn, with a description identifying the typed physics binding it reuses. Its manifest row and hash MUST be produced by the same export path. The same one-time exporter MUST also write Ideal polarizer (preset binding).item-model-json under ItemModelIds.idealPolarizerItemModelId, form IdealPolarizerItemModel, version 1 and ProtectedBuiltIn, with a description identifying the typed physics binding it reuses. Its manifest row and hash MUST be produced by the same export path. The same one-time exporter MUST also write Sample by stack.item-model-json under ItemModelIds.stackSampleItemModelId, form StackSampleItemModel, version 1 and ProtectedBuiltIn, with a description identifying the typed physics binding it reuses. Its manifest row and hash MUST be produced by the same export path. The import-tape fixture MUST first obtain all decisions, assert no writes, and then explicitly apply their defaults as step 94 requires before asserting the expanded item-model tape. In the throw-away export-item-models.fsx ONLY, detectorNoiseAxes MUST be derived from BerremanTests.NoiseParam.decentLab in the built BerremanTests assembly, reading its three values once and passing elevated ParameterValues to ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes. The script MAY reference that test assembly; no product project may do so. It MUST NOT transcribe the bench constants. The persisted catalogue contains the generated axes. Step 212 deletes the exporter, and step 339's parity fact compares the promoted budget with these catalogue defaults. EntryFileJson.fs MUST encode ParameterKind in the detector axis list through its integer value and decode through tryOfWire. An unrecognized tag MUST become the typed file-read error at this serialization boundary, never an unrecognized Domain case or an exception. It MUST use the canonical JSON stack already used for ItemModel payloads.","acceptance":"After the kind lands, `LibraryEntryKind.all` MUST list seven kinds with `ItemModelEntryKind` at tag 7 and `.item-model-json`, an item-model entry MUST seal, write and read back through `library-item-model.schema.json`, the in-memory import MUST push item models through `ItemModelProxy.saveItemModel`, and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/` MUST hold the eleven built-in item models listed in its manifest, none git-ignored; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present`, `the shipped item models include every required form under their well-known ids`, `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`, `an item-model builder and decoder are inverse, and a protection its provenance disagrees with is refused` and `importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-item-model.schema.json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/.catalogue-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Real linear polarizer.item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Retarder plate.item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder).item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Black-box Mueller matrix.item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Empty slot (air).item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Intensity detector (gain, dark offset and noise).item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Mueller polarimeter.item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ellipsometer (noise budget).item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Light source (preset binding).item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Ideal polarizer (preset binding).item-model-json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/Sample by stack.item-model-json"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.the shipped item models include every required form under their well-known ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.an item-model builder and decoder are inverse, and a protection its provenance disagrees with is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.the shipped Built-in catalogue is whole: every file validates, every hash matches its manifest row, ids are unique and every built-in kind is present","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportProxyTests.importCatalogue pushes every entry once, categories then materials then samples then presets, through the exact signatures","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.LibraryEntryKind.ItemModelEntryKind","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.LibraryEntryPayload.ItemModelPayload","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.LibraryEntryContent.ofItemModel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.LibraryEntryContent.toItemModel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.ItemModelId.toLibraryEntryId","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.ItemModelVersionId.entryReference","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.CatalogueImport.InMemoryCatalogueStores.itemModels","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs","obligations":["S71-LIBRARY-KIND"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":211,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-S71g","id":"STORE_BigBoy_0006","name":"ItemModelProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[210],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests"],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item-model store over the library database (001 §C 'The library proxies keep their shapes and gain a SQLite create', 'Contract tests'; the S7.1 brief: a SQLite create with the contract suite run on both; step 76's pattern). New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ItemModelDatabaseStore.fs`, `module ItemModelDatabaseStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `PresetDatabaseStore.fs` (step 79): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type ItemModelProxy with static member createInDatabase (database : LibraryDatabase) : ItemModelProxy` carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, \"the SQLite item-model store (001 §C): every field is one LibraryDatabase.run over the entry-version rows\")>]` and a doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. As in step 76, every field is one `run` (step 62) over step 67's operations with one `SaveChanges ()` per write, and every `StorageError` or decoder `LibraryEntryError` is `ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`. An item model is an entry whose latest row's kind is `ItemModelEntryKind`, built-in or user. `listItemModels ()` decodes (`toItemModel`, step 210) the latest version of every item model (`latestStoredOfKind ItemModelEntryKind`), whatever its lifecycle, as `{ version; entry }`, ordered by name and then by id. `resolveItemModelVersion v` answers `None` when `tryStoredVersion v.itemModelId.toLibraryEntryId v.version` finds no row or a row of another kind, and that version decoded otherwise. `saveItemModel v` answers `DuplicateItemModelErr` naming the id and its latest version when the id holds an item model; `InvalidItemModelErr` naming the id and that kind's `extension` when it holds another kind; `InvalidItemModelErr` carrying the builder's `describe` when `ofItemModel v.version UserProvenance v.entry` refuses, as it does a `ProtectedBuiltIn` entry, because built-ins arrive only through the import seam (step 95); and otherwise it stages `stageNewEntry` of that content. No cache, retry, pin verb, removal or edit is added. Tests, in `ItemModelProxyTests.fs` (step 209): `type ItemModelProxySqliteTests () = inherit ItemModelProxyContract ()` runs the three contract facts over `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase` of an empty `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate (ConnectionString \"Data Source=:memory:\")` per store, and implements `IDisposable`, disposing every database it opened. Its own facts, each over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67) unless it says otherwise and each disposing it: `the database item-model store lists the Built-in item models and resolves each by its version` : `listItemModels` answers exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` (step 210) ordered by name, and `resolveItemModelVersion` of each one's `versionId` answers it. `the database item-model store holds user item models only and refuses an id it cannot hold`: a `ProtectedBuiltIn` entry under a fresh GUID answers `InvalidItemModelErr`; an entry under the GUID of `MaterialIds.silicon` answers `InvalidItemModelErr` naming `.material-json`; an entry under `ItemModelIds.emptySlotModelId` answers `DuplicateItemModelErr`; and `tryLatestStored` of that built-in still answers the catalogue's envelope. `a database failure below the item-model store is ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`: over a disposed database every field answers `Error (ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr _)`.","acceptance":"After the database store lands, `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase` MUST serve the library database's item models and save only user item models; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version`, `the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name` and `saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version` under `ItemModelProxySqliteTests`, and `the database item-model store lists the Built-in item models and resolves each by its version`, `the database item-model store holds user item models only and refuses an id it cannot hold` and `a database failure below the item-model store is ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ItemModelDatabaseStore.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests.an item model is saved at its version and resolved by exactly that version","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-DATABASE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests.the store lists the latest version of every item model, by name","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-DATABASE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests.saving an item model the store already holds is DuplicateItemModelErr and keeps the held version","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-DATABASE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests.the database item-model store lists the Built-in item models and resolves each by its version","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-DATABASE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests.the database item-model store holds user item models only and refuses an id it cannot hold","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-DATABASE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests.a database failure below the item-model store is ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr, never a throw","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelProxySqliteTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-DATABASE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.ItemModelDatabaseStore.ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ItemModelDatabaseStore.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-MODEL-DATABASE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":212,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71h","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[211],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item-model entry file and the import of item models are proved over every form and over both stores (001 §B 'Any entry that cannot serialise is a test failure'; 001 §C 'Contract tests'; .spec-md §9), and the export tool goes. No product source file changes. (0) The throw-away tool is deleted now that the shipped files and their facts are green (steps 210, 211), as step 36 deleted step 35's (.spec-md §3.6; the S7.1 brief: written once, no code seed): `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` is removed, so `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/` holds only `Builtin/`. Nothing references it. (1) `EntryFileJsonTests` (step 30) gains `an item-model entry file round-trips every model form`: content → `sealed` → `fileText` → `parseEntry ItemModelEntryKind` answers an equal envelope whose `toItemModel` answers the entry, for test-local entries holding a real LP under each `PolarizerLeakage`, a retarder under `ConstantRetardance` and under `InverseWaveLengthRetardance` of 632.8 nm, a black box under each `BlackBoxNormalisation`, a compound whose second component is itself a compound, `EmptySlotModel`, and each detector over `detectorNoiseAxes` and over `zeroNoiseAxes`, under `BuiltInProvenance` and `UserProvenance`; and the real LP's file parsed as a `PolarizerEntryKind` answers `SchemaValidationErr`. (2) `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` (step 95): the test-local `ImportStoreSet` gains `itemModels : ItemModelProxy`. `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` fills it with the `itemModels` of its `InMemoryCatalogueStores` (step 210), and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` with `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase` (step 211) of its database. The contract's `importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue` also requires `listItemModels` to answer one version per item-model row, and `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value` requires each item-model row's decoded version to be what `resolveItemModelVersion` answers for its `versionId`. Every other assertion is kept. detectorNoiseAxes MUST be the noise-axis list read from the shipped Mueller-polarimeter model; zeroNoiseAxes MUST be the same axis descriptors with every defaultValue set to the elevated zero. The serializer MUST round-trip lists of axes and MUST NOT bind a NoiseParam. The detector-model round-trip fact MUST assert integer kind tags on disk and reject zero and an unrecognized kind tag with the typed malformed-file error, while retaining all three noise defaults.","acceptance":"After the facts land, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx` MUST NOT exist and `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/` MUST hold only `Builtin/`, every item-model form MUST round-trip through its entry file, and both import stores MUST hold and resolve the Built-in item models; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item-model entry file round-trips every model form` and `importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue` and `every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value` under `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/export-item-models.fsx","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.an item-model entry file round-trips every model form","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ENTRY-FILE-AND-IMPORT"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs","obligations":["S71-ENTRY-FILE-AND-IMPORT"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs","obligations":["S71-ENTRY-FILE-AND-IMPORT"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.importFrom fills empty stores with the whole Built-in catalogue","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs","obligations":["S71-ENTRY-FILE-AND-IMPORT"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.CatalogueImportSqliteTests.every imported entry resolves by its id to its decoded value","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs","obligations":["S71-ENTRY-FILE-AND-IMPORT"]}],"contracts":[],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":213,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[212],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests"],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. An item's identity and the model it instantiates, as pure Domain data in the `Kit` module (001 §I '`Kit.Item` = one PHYSICAL piece: `ItemId` (GUID) and an `ItemLabel` (`LP1`, `CPL2`, `QZ`, `Phone`); the `ItemModel` it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'; 001 §A: the kit module holds `Item`, `ItemId`, `ItemLabel`, `Parameter`, `ParameterState`; 001 §I: the model is always an ItemModel version, with an optional typed binding to preset or sample physics; .spec-md §3.14, §3.17, §5 'Kit module'). `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs` (step 122) opens `ItemModels` (step 205), `Library` and `Placement`; the new types are appended at the end of the file in this order, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1, every case name of two words and no `bool`. (1) `ItemError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the item, the label or the parameter: `InvalidItemLabelErr` (a blank label), `DuplicateItemLabelErr` (another item of the kit has the label's file name), `DuplicateItemIdErr` (another item has the id), `UnknownItemParameterErr` (the item has no parameter of that name) and `InvalidParameterStateErr` (a parameter state breaks its rules, step 214). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `the item label is not valid: <reason>`, `the kit already has an item of that label: <reason>`, `the kit already has an item of that id: <reason>`, `the item has no such parameter: <reason>` and `the parameter state is not valid: <reason>`. (2) `ItemId of Guid` with `.value`, one physical piece's frozen identity, minted by the caller as `KitId` is (step 122). (3) `ItemLabel of string` with `.value`. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<ItemLabel, ItemError>` keeps the text as given and refuses an empty or white-space text with `InvalidItemLabelErr`; `member this.fileStem : FileStem` is `FileStem.ofText this.value` (step 24), the stem of its `<label>.item-json` (001 §A), so a label keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md §3.11). (4) `ItemNotes of string`, free text, empty when there are none. (5) `ItemRevision of int` with `.value`, `static member first : ItemRevision` (1) and `member this.next : ItemRevision`: the revision an item file carries (001 §I 'Revisions'). (6) ItemModelInstance MUST be PresetInstance of model : ItemModelVersionId * preset : ElementValueId | SampleInstance of model : ItemModelVersionId * sample : SampleVersionId | ItemModelVersionInstance of ItemModelVersionId. Every case MUST carry the exact instantiated item-model version. Its entryReferenceOpt MUST always be Some of that model version's entryReference. Its bindingReferenceOpt MUST separately identify the preset or sample physics dependency using the same GUID conversion and snapshot rules as step 137; standalone item models MUST have None. A non-GUID preset binding MUST be rejected by AddItem with InvalidItemModelBindingErr, never erase the model reference. ItemError MUST gain InvalidItemModelBindingErr of reason : string with a diagnostic naming the model and binding.  Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs`, `module KitItemTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. `an item label keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `ItemLabel.tryCreate \"CPL:2\"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem \"CPL_2\"`, equal to `FileStem.ofText \"CPL:2\"`; `\"\"` and `\"  \"` answer `InvalidItemLabelErr`. `an item revision starts at one and counts up`: `ItemRevision.first` is 1 and its `next.next` is 3. `an item's model is referenced as the library snapshots it`: source, ideal-polarizer and sample instances MUST each return their exact ItemModel version plus a separate physics binding reference; a standalone instance MUST return its model version and no binding.  `every item error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. ItemError MUST also declare UnknownKitItemErr of reason : string, rendered as `the kit has no item of that id: <reason>`, and the error-rendering fact MUST cover it; the S6 copy mapping requires this case.","acceptance":"After the item identity lands, `ItemLabel.tryCreate` MUST refuse a blank label and name its file through the shared stem rule, and `ItemModelInstance.entryReferenceOpt` MUST answer the reference the kit snapshots; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item label keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `an item revision starts at one and counts up`, `an item's model is referenced as the library snapshots it` and `every item error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.an item label keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.an item revision starts at one and counts up","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.an item's model is referenced as the library snapshots it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.every item error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemId","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemLabel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemNotes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemRevision","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemModelInstance","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-IDENTITY"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":214,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71j","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[213],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. A parameter and its state (001 §I '`Parameter` = a name plus a `ParameterState`: `Known of value` | `Unknown of start * bounds * prior option` | `Calibrated of value * sigma * fromFitRun`'; the S7.1 brief: the name REUSES `ParameterName`; .spec-md §3.17: the cases are `KnownParameter`, `UnknownParameter` and `CalibratedParameter`). In `Kit.fs`, after `ItemModelInstance` (step 213), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ParameterInterval = { lower : ParameterValue; upper : ParameterValue }`, the bounds a fit searches within. (2) `ParameterSigma of double` with `.value`, one standard deviation in the parameter's unit. (3) `ParameterPrior = { centre : ParameterValue; sigma : ParameterSigma }`, a Gaussian prior. (4) `UnknownParameterData = { start : ParameterValue; bounds : ParameterInterval; priorOpt : ParameterPrior option }`. (5) `FitRunName of string` with `.value`, the fit run a calibration came from, named by its file stem `<study>@<stamp>` (001 §A); S11.3 writes fit runs under it and S11.5 publishes from them. (6) `CalibratedParameterData = { value : ParameterValue; sigma : ParameterSigma; fitRun : FitRunName }`. Records hold the same-typed pairs, because a case tuple repeating a type is ELEV011. (7) `ParameterState` = `KnownParameter of ParameterValue` | `UnknownParameter of UnknownParameterData` | `CalibratedParameter of CalibratedParameterData`. (8) `Parameter = { name : ParameterName; state : ParameterState }`. `static member knownAtDefault (axis : ItemParameterAxis) : Parameter` is the axis's name with `KnownParameter axis.defaultValue`, the one way an item's parameters are made from a model's axes (step 216). `member this.validate : Result<Parameter, ItemError>` answers the parameter when its state keeps the rules and otherwise `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming the parameter and the broken rule: every number is finite (neither NaN nor infinite); an unknown's `bounds.lower` is below its `bounds.upper` and its `start` lies within them, ends included; a prior's and a calibration's `sigma` is above zero. No range by kind is checked here, because a kind's range is its model's (S8.1). No other type or member is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests` (step 213): `a parameter is created known at its axis default`: `Parameter.knownAtDefault` of the `retardance` axis that `(OpticalElementModel (RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance)).parameterAxes` publishes is named `retardance` and `KnownParameter` of π / 2. `a parameter whose state keeps its rules is kept, and one that breaks them is InvalidParameterStateErr`: a known 0.1, an unknown starting at 0.5 within [0, 1] with and without a prior of centre 0.5 and sigma 0.1, an unknown starting on its lower bound, and a calibration of 0.25 with sigma 0.01 from `FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\"` each validate to themselves; a known NaN, an unknown whose bounds are [1, 1], an unknown starting at −0.5 within [0, 1], a prior with sigma 0 and a calibration with sigma −1 each answer `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming the parameter.","acceptance":"After the parameter states land, `Parameter.knownAtDefault` MUST make a known parameter at the axis's default and `Parameter.validate` MUST refuse a non-finite number, an empty or misplaced search interval and a non-positive sigma; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a parameter is created known at its axis default` and `a parameter whose state keeps its rules is kept, and one that breaks them is InvalidParameterStateErr`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.a parameter is created known at its axis default","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.a parameter whose state keeps its rules is kept, and one that breaks them is InvalidParameterStateErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ParameterInterval","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ParameterSigma","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ParameterPrior","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.UnknownParameterData","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.FitRunName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.CalibratedParameterData","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ParameterState","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Parameter","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PARAMETER-STATE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":215,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71k","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[214],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item itself, with its dial mapping and its revision history (001 §I: an item has its own `Parameter` values, an optional photo (a kit file) and notes; 'Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero and a sign (`DialSign` exists). Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'; 'Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history'; the S7.1 brief). In `Kit.fs`, after `Parameter` (step 214), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ItemDial` = `DialMounted of DialSign` (the item turns on a dial: a raw reading maps to the physical angle as `sign · (reading − dialZero)`, the rule of `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle`) | `FixedMounting` (the item is not read off a dial). `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` answers, for `DialMounted`, the one axis `dialZero` (`AngleParameter`, 0), and `[]` for `FixedMounting`, so the zero is an ordinary parameter of the item. (2) `ItemRevisionRecord = { revision : ItemRevision; parameters : Parameter list }`, the values an earlier revision held: the short value history (fit runs keep every vector, 001 §I). (3) `Item = { id : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; model : ItemModelInstance; parameters : Parameter list; dial : ItemDial; photoOpt : KitRelativePath option; notes : ItemNotes; revision : ItemRevision; history : ItemRevisionRecord list }`. The photo is a kit-relative path to a kit file (step 123). `history` lists earlier revisions, oldest first. `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list` MUST be its model's exact entryReferenceOpt followed by bindingReferenceOpt when present, with duplicate references removed: what the kit snapshots and pins when it records the item (step 219). `member this.tryFindParameter (name : ParameterName) : Parameter option`. Two LPs of one model are two items with independent parameters (001 §I), so an item holds its own `parameters` and never shares them. No other member is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests`, over test-local items written as records: `an item references its model's library version once and finds its parameters by name`: an item over `ItemModelVersionInstance` of `ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId` at version 1 answers exactly that version's `entryReference`; each source, ideal-polarizer and stack item MUST also name its model version once and its bound physics dependency; and `tryFindParameter` answers the parameter named `dialZero` and `None` for `nothing`. `a dial-mounted item publishes its dial zero and a fixed one nothing`: `(DialMounted DialNegative).parameterAxes` is the one `dialZero` axis at 0 and `FixedMounting.parameterAxes` is `[]`.","acceptance":"After the item lands, `Item` MUST hold its id, label, model, own parameters, dial, photo, notes, revision and history, `Item.libraryReferences` MUST name its model's version once, and `ItemDial.parameterAxes` MUST publish `dialZero` for a dial-mounted item only; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item references its model's library version once and finds its parameters by name` and `a dial-mounted item publishes its dial zero and a fixed one nothing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.an item references its model's library version once and finds its parameters by name","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.a dial-mounted item publishes its dial zero and a fixed one nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemDial","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemRevisionRecord","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.libraryReferences","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.tryFindParameter","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":216,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71l","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[215],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Adding an item, as a pure update over the kit's items (001 §P: `AddItem` is a semantic message; the S7.1 brief: pure updates for AddItem, an item's parameters are created from the generated axes; 001 §I 'Two LPs of one model are two items with independent parameters'). In `Kit.fs`, after `Item` (step 215), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1. (1) `ItemModelChoice` = `SourcePresetChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * source : SourcePreset` | `PolarizerPresetChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * polarizer : PolarizerPreset` | `StackSampleChoice of model : ItemModelVersion * version : SampleVersionId * sample : Sample` | `LibraryModelChoice of ItemModelVersion`: a model as the library resolved it. `member this.instance : ItemModelInstance` MUST carry the choice's exact model version in every case: PresetInstance (model.versionId, preset.id), SampleInstance (model.versionId, version), or ItemModelVersionInstance model.versionId; `member this.parameterAxes : ItemParameterAxis list` MUST match the model form and typed binding, calling the preset/sample parameterAxes members (step 207) for SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel and StackSampleItemModel, or entry.model.parameterAxes for a standalone form (step 208). (2) `ItemDraft = { id : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; model : ItemModelChoice; dial : ItemDial }`, what `AddItem` gives. `member this.toItem : Item` holds the draft's id, label, `model.instance` and dial; its `parameters` are `Parameter.knownAtDefault` (step 214) of `model.parameterAxes` followed by `dial.parameterAxes`, in that order; `photoOpt = None`, `notes = ItemNotes \"\"`, `revision = ItemRevision.first` and `history = []`. `member this.addTo (items : Item list) : Result<Item, ItemError>` answers `DuplicateItemIdErr` when an item holds the id, `DuplicateItemLabelErr` naming both labels when an item's label `fileStem` equals the draft's ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`), because every `<label>.item-json` shares the kit root on Windows, and MUST validate that each resolved model has the form matching its binding before returning toItem. An absent/mismatched model, a non-GUID preset binding or LibraryModelChoice of an unbound binding-required form MUST yield InvalidItemModelBindingErr before an item is recorded. It writes nothing; the caller records the item (step 219). Every source, ideal-polarizer and sample test draft MUST receive the corresponding BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel from step 210. The declared source/polarizer/sample fact MUST assert a model version in every item and exercise the mismatched-model refusal without changing the kit. No other member, option or default is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests`: `adding an item from a library model creates its parameters known at the model's defaults and its dial zero`: a CPL1 item made by an `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive` holds the parameters `c1.extinctionRatio`, `c1.axisOffset`, `c2.retardance`, `c2.fastAxisOffset` and `dialZero`, each `KnownParameter` of its axis default, its model `ItemModelVersionInstance` of that model's `versionId`, revision 1, no history, no photo and empty notes. `a source preset, an ideal polarizer and a sample give an item their own parameters`: a `SourcePresetChoice` of `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633` with `FixedMounting` holds `azimuth`, `ellipticity`, `degreeOfPolarization` and `intensityScale`; a `PolarizerPresetChoice` of the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer with `DialMounted DialNegative` holds `dialZero` alone; a `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 with its catalogue sample holds `substrate.thickness` at 1e-3 and the `SampleInstance` of the stack item-model version and that sample version. `two items of one model are two items with equal starting parameters`: LP1 and LP2, two drafts over the `ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId` model with distinct test-local ids, are two items whose parameters are equal and whose ids and labels differ. `adding an item whose id or label file name the kit already holds is refused`: over a kit holding LP1, a draft labelled `lp1`, and one labelled `LP:1` beside an item labelled `LP_1`, answer `DuplicateItemLabelErr`, and a draft reusing LP1's id answers `DuplicateItemIdErr`.","acceptance":"After AddItem lands, `ItemDraft.toItem` MUST create every parameter its model and dial publish, known at its default, at revision 1, and `ItemDraft.addTo` MUST refuse an id or a label file name the kit already holds; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `adding an item from a library model creates its parameters known at the model's defaults and its dial zero`, `a source preset, an ideal polarizer and a sample give an item their own parameters`, `two items of one model are two items with equal starting parameters` and `adding an item whose id or label file name the kit already holds is refused`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.adding an item from a library model creates its parameters known at the model's defaults and its dial zero","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.a source preset, an ideal polarizer and a sample give an item their own parameters","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.two items of one model are two items with equal starting parameters","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.adding an item whose id or label file name the kit already holds is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemModelChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemDraft","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemDraft.toItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemDraft.addTo","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ADD-ITEM"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":217,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71o","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[216],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. An item persists as its own kit file, `<label>.item-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .item-json', 'A file that exists many times is named by its own identity'; the S7.1 brief: `<label>.item-json` kit files go through KitProxy with a schema and a version; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 146's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`); no second parser or writer is written. (1) `Kit.fs`, after Item (step 215), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: `ItemFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; item : Item }`, the `.item-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1, and `type Item with member this.itemFile : ItemFile`, the item at the current schema version. A file is read back as its `item` field; no member converts the other way (ELEV006). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/item.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/experiment.schema.json` (step 146), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/item.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1 (`then`): the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `item`; `item` holds exactly `id` (the GUID definition of `library-common.schema.json`, referenced by its `$id`), `label` (a non-empty string), `model`, `parameters` (an array), `dial`, `photoOpt` (`null` or a non-empty string), `notes` (a string), `revision` (a positive integer) and `history` (an array). The model, parameters, dial and history are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one, as step 146's descriptors are. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/experiment.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateItemFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateExperimentFile` (step 146) does. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs` (step 146): `type ItemFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText`, and `type KitFileText with member this.parseItemFile : Result<ItemFile, StorageError>` is `parseVersionedText validateItemFile ItemKitFile.extension ItemFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value` (steps 123, 124). There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Tests, in `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 146): `an item is stored under its label`: `ItemKitFile.fileNameOf` of `(ItemLabel \"CPL1\").fileStem` is `FileName \"CPL1.item-json\"`. `an item file round-trips through its canonical text`: a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive`, with its record initialized to revision 2, c2.retardance unknown under a prior, c2.fastAxisOffset calibrated, the revision-1 parameters in history, a photoOpt of data/photos/CPL1.jpg and notes, and a laser item over `PresetIds.heNe633` with `FixedMounting`, each go `itemFile`, `fileText`, then `parseItemFile` and answer an equal file; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys as `item` then `schemaVersion`, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text. `an item file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` : CPL1's text with `schemaVersion` 2, with its body and as `{ \"schemaVersion\": 2 }` alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = ItemKitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed item file is refused before it binds`: CPL1's text without `item`, with an extra top-level key `notes`, with `item.label` empty, and with `item.revision` 0 each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; the text `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance.","acceptance":"After the item file lands, `ItemFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseItemFile` reads back equal, validated against `schema/item.schema.json`, another schema version being `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item is stored under its label`, `an item file round-trips through its canonical text`, `an item file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` and `a schema-invalid or malformed item file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/item.schema.json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an item is stored under its label","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an item file round-trips through its canonical text","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an item file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed item file is refused before it binds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.itemFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateItemFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.ItemFile.fileText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitFileText.parseItemFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-FILE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":218,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71p","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[217],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests"],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. A kit's items are read and written by typed members over the per-kind verbs (001 §P '`KitProxy` … kit, items, …'; step 127: a kind adds no proxy verb; step 148's members for experiments). In `KitContentFiles.fs`, on step 148's `type KitProxy with` extension, each member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: (1) `member this.writeItem (item : Item) : Result<unit, KitError>` renders `item.itemFile.fileText` (step 217) and writes it with `writeKindFile ItemKitFile item.label.fileStem`, replacing a file of that name whole; a `StorageError` of the rendering is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the error's `describe`. (2) `member this.readItems () : Result<Item list, KitError>` reads every stem `listKindFiles ItemKitFile` answers, with `readKindFile`, and parses it with `parseItemFile`. A refusal, a file whose item's `label.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case, or a second file holding an `ItemId` already read is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason, and the whole read answers it, so a kit never opens with an item left out. The answer is ordered by the label's text (ordinal). Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) a write answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and a read passes, because the members call the proxy's verbs. No delete, cache, retry or other member is added; an item is renamed by no member in this section. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemFileTests.fs`, `module KitItemFileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, whose facts each make `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitItemFileTests\", <a new GUID>)`, build `KitProxy.create` over it and call `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (the `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` precedent, step 148). Its items are CPL1, LP1 and Phone made through `ItemDraft.toItem` (step 216) over the circular-polarizer, real-LP and intensity-detector built-ins. `a kit's item files round-trip, each stored under its label` : after `writeItem` of Phone, CPL1 and LP1, the folder holds `CPL1.item-json`, `LP1.item-json` and `Phone.item-json`, and `readItems` answers CPL1, LP1 and Phone in that order. `writing an item again under its label replaces its file`: CPL1, then a CPL1 record initialized with revision 2 and its prior parameters in history, reads back as the second. This storage fact MUST construct the record directly and MUST NOT depend on the publication behavior introduced in step 235. `an item file that does not read, holds another label or repeats an id refuses the read, naming the file`: `Broken.item-json` written by the test as `{`, `Other.item-json` holding CPL1's file text, and `CPL9.item-json` holding a file whose item is labelled `CPL9` but has LP1's id each make `readItems` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file. `a read-only kit refuses an item write and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView`, `writeItem` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`, the folder's files and bytes are unchanged, and `readItems` answers what the kit holds.","acceptance":"After the typed members land, `KitProxy.writeItem` MUST write each item to `<label>.item-json` and `KitProxy.readItems` MUST read every item file back, ordered by label, a file that does not read, holds another label or repeats an id refusing the whole read; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's item files round-trip, each stored under its label`, `writing an item again under its label replaces its file`, `an item file that does not read, holds another label or repeats an id refuses the read, naming the file` and `a read-only kit refuses an item write and writes nothing`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemFileTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests.a kit's item files round-trip, each stored under its label","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemFileTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-KIT-FILES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests.writing an item again under its label replaces its file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemFileTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-KIT-FILES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests.an item file that does not read, holds another label or repeats an id refuses the read, naming the file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemFileTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-KIT-FILES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests.a read-only kit refuses an item write and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemFileTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemFileTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-ITEM-KIT-FILES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-KIT-FILES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readItems","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-ITEM-KIT-FILES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":219,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71q","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[218],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Writing an item first snapshots and pins the model version it references (001 §I 'the ItemModel it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'; 001 §E 'Library closure snapshot'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned … when a kit first references it'; the S7.1 brief: referencing a model version snapshots and pins it (S4.2); step 139: S7.1's items call `snapshotReferences`). In `KitContentFiles.fs`, on step 149's `type KitLibraryContext with` extension, documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: `member this.recordItem (item : Item) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>` calls `this.snapshotReferences item.libraryReferences` (steps 139, 215), then `this.kit.proxy.writeItem item` (step 218), a `KitError` wrapped as `KitLibraryKitErr`. The snapshots come first, so a written item never references a version the kit lacks; on a failure the file is not written and what the snapshot wrote stays (step 139). The Items panel (S7.2) and Publish calibration (S11.5) record items through it. No other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), over its Built-in library (`BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`, which holds the shipped item models since step 210), its recorder of pins and its in-memory kit opened read-write. `recording an item snapshots its model's library version and pins it, then writes its file`: CPL1 made through `ItemDraft.toItem` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)`, recorded through `recordItem`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding exactly that item model's version 1 envelope, `paths` holding `library/<its GUID>@v1.item-model-json` and `CPL1.item-json`, the recorder holding that version, and `kit.proxy.readItems ()` answering CPL1. `recording a sample item snapshots the sample with its materials and their categories`: a QZ item over `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 snapshots the sample, its glass material and that material's category, each once. `recording a preset item snapshots the preset's latest version`: a laser item over `SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.heNe633` snapshots that preset's version 1. `a read-only kit records no item`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, `recordItem` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance.","acceptance":"After recording lands, `KitLibraryContext.recordItem` MUST snapshot and pin the library version an item's model names, with its closure, before it writes the item's file, and write nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `recording an item snapshots its model's library version and pins it, then writes its file`, `recording a sample item snapshots the sample with its materials and their categories`, `recording a preset item snapshots the preset's latest version` and `a read-only kit records no item`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording an item snapshots its model's library version and pins it, then writes its file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-RECORD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording a sample item snapshots the sample with its materials and their categories","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-RECORD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording a preset item snapshots the preset's latest version","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-RECORD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a read-only kit records no item","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-RECORD-ITEM"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S71-RECORD-ITEM"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":220,"anchor":"WIRE","ac":"AC-S71r","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[219],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The app scope composes the item-model store over its library database for S6 item-copy resolution and the S7 Items panel (.spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`: it composes the SQLite library proxies over the configured locations; 001 §O 'Add item from library model…'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `AppContext` gains `itemModels : ItemModelProxy`, documented in one line (the item-model store over the app's library database, spec 0050 S7.1), set by `compose` (step 89) to `ItemModelProxy.createInDatabase database` (step 211) beside the other database stores, so `create` and `recreateLibrary` carry it. No window reads it in this section, and no other field changes. (2) Tests: `AppContextTests` gains `the app scope serves the Built-in item models from its library database`: `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"AppContextTests\")`'s `itemModels.listItemModels ()` answers exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` ordered by name, because the start-up import (steps 95, 100) brought the shipped item models into its database.","acceptance":"After the composition, `AppContext.itemModels` MUST be the database item-model store of the app scope's library and serve the Built-in item models; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app scope serves the Built-in item models from its library database`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.the app scope serves the Built-in item models from its library database","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S71-APP-ITEM-MODELS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.AppContext.itemModels","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs","obligations":["S71-APP-ITEM-MODELS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":221,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[220],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The item mapping of Copy experiments from another kit… as pure data (001 §H 'brings the experiments with their setups, data files and the items they use. Items map onto existing items where the user says so; otherwise they are added'; .spec-md §3.15: the item mapping MUST be complete in S6; the S7.2 brief: a mapping table lists every item the picked experiments use, each with 'map to existing item' or 'add', the default mapping by identical model and label and otherwise adding; the S7.1 mapper's request: items map by `ItemId` or label). Each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, after the Item declarations from step 215. (a) `type ItemLabel with member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : ItemLabel list) : ItemLabel` answers the first of `<label>`, `<label> (2)`, `<label> (3)`, … whose `fileStem` no label of `taken` has, ignoring case: the suffix form of `KitDataFolder.copyTargetFor` (step 132) on a label, because an item's file is named by its label (step 217). (b) `ItemCopyChoice` = `MapOntoKitItem of ItemId` (the copy uses the target kit's item of that id and brings nothing) | `AddCopiedItem` (the source item is added to the target kit). `ItemCopyRow = { sourceItem : Item; choice : ItemCopyChoice }`, one row of the mapping table. Neither is stored, so neither carries a wire tag. (c) `type Item with member this.defaultCopyChoice (held : Item list) : ItemCopyChoice` is `MapOntoKitItem` of the held item with this item's `id` when there is one, because one id is one physical piece (001 §I); otherwise `MapOntoKitItem` of the first held item whose `model` equals this item's and whose `label` equals its label (ordinal); otherwise `AddCopiedItem`. (d) On `ItemCopyRow`, `static member copyRowsFor (used : Item list) (held : Item list) (chosen : ItemCopyRow list) : ItemCopyRow list` answers one row per item of `used`, in order, whose choice is that of the `chosen` row with the same `sourceItem.id`, or else the item's `defaultCopyChoice held`: the panel keeps what the user chose while the chosen experiments change, and a copy given no row takes the defaults. (e) On `ItemCopyRow`, `static member itemsToAdd (rows : ItemCopyRow list) (held : Item list) : Result<Item list, ItemError>` checks every row before it answers: a `MapOntoKitItem id` whose `id` no held item has is `UnknownKitItemErr` (step 213) naming the source item's label and the id; an `AddCopiedItem` of an item whose `id` a held item has is `DuplicateItemIdErr` naming its label, because a piece the kit holds is mapped, not added twice. Otherwise it answers the `AddCopiedItem` rows' items in order, each relabelled `label.nextFreeAmong` the held labels and the labels given to the earlier added items, every other field kept. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `Experiment` gains `static member itemsUsedBy (experiments : Experiment list) (items : Item list) : Item list`, the items, in their order and each once, one of whose `libraryReferences` (step 215) is among the `libraryReferences` (step 137) of one of the experiments. An experiment's setup binds a preset by its entry id and a sample by its version (`Experiments.fs:ElementBinding`), and an item instantiating that preset or that sample version references the same entry (step 213), so these are the items the experiments use; an item-model item is used by no experiment until setups name items (S8.2). No other type, member or option is added. Tests. In `KitItemTests`: `an added item's label takes the next free suffix among the labels the kit holds`: `CPL1` among `cpl1` and `CPL1 (2)` answers `CPL1 (3)`, among no label `CPL1`, and `LP:1` among `LP_1` answers `LP:1 (2)`. `an item maps by default onto the kit's item of its id, then of its model and label, and is otherwise added`: with the held items LP1 (real-LP model) and CPL1 (circular-polarizer model), a source item of LP1's id labelled `Polarizer A` maps onto LP1; a source `CPL1` of the circular-polarizer model under another id maps onto the held CPL1; a source `CPL1` of the real-LP model and a source `CPL2` of the circular-polarizer model are added. `the mapping rows follow the used items and keep the choices already made`: `copyRowsFor` of the used items LP1 and QZ, with a chosen row adding QZ, answers LP1 at its default and QZ added, in that order; a chosen row of an item not used gives no row. `the items to add are checked before any is answered, and each clashing label is suffixed`: over held `CPL1`, an added source `CPL1` is `CPL1 (2)` and a second added `CPL1` `CPL1 (3)`; an added item whose id the kit holds answers `DuplicateItemIdErr`, a mapping onto an id the kit lacks `UnknownKitItemErr`, and either refusal answers no item. In `ExperimentProxyTests` (steps 137, 203): `the items an experiment uses are those whose model its setup binds, each once`: of the items Laser (`SourcePresetChoice` of `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`), QZ (`StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1), QZ2 (that sample at version 2) and CPL1, an experiment whose setup binds that sample at version 1 and that preset by its entry id uses exactly Laser and QZ, in that order; two experiments binding the preset name Laser once; an experiment binding nothing uses none. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the mapping lands, `ItemCopyRow.copyRowsFor` MUST give each used item the chosen or default choice, `ItemCopyRow.itemsToAdd` MUST refuse a mapping onto a missing item and an added held id and suffix each clashing label, and `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` MUST answer the items whose model the experiments bind; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an added item's label takes the next free suffix among the labels the kit holds`, `an item maps by default onto the kit's item of its id, then of its model and label, and is otherwise added`, `the mapping rows follow the used items and keep the choices already made`, `the items to add are checked before any is answered, and each clashing label is suffixed` and `the items an experiment uses are those whose model its setup binds, each once`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.an added item's label takes the next free suffix among the labels the kit holds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.an item maps by default onto the kit's item of its id, then of its model and label, and is otherwise added","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.the mapping rows follow the used items and keep the choices already made","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.the items to add are checked before any is answered, and each clashing label is suffixed","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.the items an experiment uses are those whose model its setup binds, each once","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemCopyChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemCopyRow","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.defaultCopyChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemCopyRow.copyRowsFor","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemCopyRow.itemsToAdd","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.itemsUsedBy","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MAPPING"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":222,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72d","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[221],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The session's item-model store reads the kit's snapshots as its other library stores do, so a kit's items resolve their models on any machine (001 §E 'So the kit opens on any machine', 'missing locally → the snapshot read-only'; step 142's overlay rule; step 219: recording an item snapshots its item model). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`, after step 142's store extensions, documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2: `type ItemModelProxy with member this.overlaidWith (overlay : KitLibraryOverlay) : ItemModelProxy`. `resolveItemModelVersion v` answers, for an entry the overlay's `replacements` re-bind, the held entry; otherwise the kit's snapshot of exactly that version (`LibraryEntryEnvelope.libraryVersionRef`, step 137) when the overlay holds one, so a divergent version is the kit's (001 §E); otherwise the store's. `listItemModels ()` answers the store's item models followed by the kit's snapshot-only item models, one per id at its highest version, ordered by name and then by id, a re-bound or store-held id left out (step 142's listing rule). `saveItemModel` passes through to the store. A snapshot becomes an item model only through `toItemModel` (step 210), and its refusal is `ItemModelStoreUnavailableErr` naming the snapshot and the refusal's `describe`. `KitLibraryStores` (step 142) is unchanged: the windows compose the overlaid item-model store beside it (step 243). No cache, write-back or other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests`: `a kit's item models resolve from its snapshots against an empty library`: a kit snapshotted (step 139) from the Built-in library with the references of `ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId` and `ItemModelIds.retarderPlateModelId` at version 1, opened read-only by a second proxy over the same folder against EMPTY in-memory stores and seam (`CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, step 95), resolves both versions through `(ItemModelProxy .createInMemory ()).overlaidWith` of its `openOverlay []` (step 142), each equal to `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel` of its id, and `listItemModels` answers the two, by name. `the overlaid item-model store answers the kit's divergent version and passes a save through`: over the Built-in library, for a kit whose snapshot of the circular polarizer at version 1 has another description, `resolveItemModelVersion` of that version answers the kit's description, `listItemModels` answers the store's eight item models and no second circular polarizer, and `saveItemModel` of a test-local user item model through the overlaid store holds it in the underlying store. The item file/schema and snapshot tests MUST cover source, ideal-polarizer and stack items carrying their exact ItemModel version and typed physics binding. recordItem MUST pin and snapshot the model and the full physics closure. Reopening against an empty library MUST resolve the model from its .item-model-json snapshot and then its binding; a missing model MUST be a typed error, never a preset/sample fallback. No fixture MAY construct a bare preset/sample model instance.","acceptance":"After the overlay lands, `ItemModelProxy.overlaidWith` MUST answer a kit's snapshot-only item model and the kit's copy of a divergent version, list the store's item models first and pass a save to the store; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's item models resolve from its snapshots against an empty library` and `the overlaid item-model store answers the kit's divergent version and passes a save through`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a kit's item models resolve from its snapshots against an empty library","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-MODEL-OVERLAY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.the overlaid item-model store answers the kit's divergent version and passes a save through","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-MODEL-OVERLAY"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.ItemModelProxy.overlaidWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-MODEL-OVERLAY"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":223,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72e","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[222],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The constructor window holds its kit's items, read when the kit opens and when it reloads (the S7.1 mapper's request: read `KitProxy.readItems` on open; 001 §O 'Items panel: the list'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit` (steps 150, 184) gains `items : Item list` after `experiments`, documented in one line: the kit's items as read at open, in label order. The private `openedOver` (step 172) reads `readItems ()` (step 218) after `readExperiments ()`; a refusal closes the kit and is the answer, as any failed read is (step 150), so a kit with an unreadable item file is never left locked. `withRebindings` keeps it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitItems : Item list` beside the kit's loaded content (step 187), documented in one line: the kit's items in label order, as the kit last read or wrote them; `initWith` sets it to `[]`. The private function of a kit's content that `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` share (step 187 (4)) takes the items after the experiments and sets `kitItems`: `loadKit` passes `opened.items`; `ReloadKitChanges` reads `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()` after `readExperiments ()`, its `Error e` keeping the model and the offer with step 187's text; the copy message introduced in step 225 MUST pass the model's kitItems. A changed item file is offered for reload by step 130's check, because `.item-json` is a kind of `KitFileKind.all` (step 123). The doc of `loadKit` says, in no more words, that it loads the items. No other field or message changes. Tests. `KitOpeningTests` (step 150) gains `opening a kit reads its items, and an item file that does not read refuses the open`: a kit holding CPL1 and LP1, written through `writeItem` (step 218) and closed, answers `items` CPL1 then LP1 when opened again read-write and read-only; a kit whose `Broken.item-json` the test writes as `{` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitFileRejectedErr _)` naming it, and its folder holds no `.oc/lock`. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184) gains `a loaded kit's items are the window's, and Reload reads an item another writer wrote`: `initMain ()` loaded from a folder kit holding CPL1 holds `kitItems` CPL1; after another writer (step 187's `KitProxy.create` over the folder) writes LP1 through `writeItem`, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` offers `LP1.item-json`, and `ReloadKitChanges` leaves `kitItems` CPL1 then LP1.","acceptance":"After the window holds items, `OpenedKit.items` MUST hold the kit's items read at open, a kit with an unreadable item file MUST not open, and `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` MUST set `kitItems`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening a kit reads its items, and an item file that does not read refuses the open` and `a loaded kit's items are the window's, and Reload reads an item another writer wrote`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening a kit reads its items, and an item file that does not read refuses the open","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-WINDOW-ITEMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a loaded kit's items are the window's, and Reload reads an item another writer wrote","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-WINDOW-ITEMS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.OpenedKit.items","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","obligations":["S72-WINDOW-ITEMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitItems","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-WINDOW-ITEMS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":224,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S6j","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[223,204],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests"],"how_to":"Copying experiments from another kit with the data files they reference and the snapshots they need (001 §H 'Between kits'; .spec-md §3.15: S6 completes the copy with items and explicit mapping before its closing composition; the S6 brief: each experiment is copied with its setup files, the data files it references (into data/, under S4.2's collision rule, hashes re-recorded) and the library snapshots it needs; clashing names get S4.1's suffix rule). An S4.3 experiment carries its setup inside its own file (the `setup` array, step 146) and references no `.setup-json`, so copying the experiment file copies its setup. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146-149), because the copy reads and writes experiment files through its typed members, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) `ExperimentCopyReport = { experiments : Experiment list; dataFiles : DataAttachment list; snapshots : LibraryVersionRef list }`: each copied experiment as written, each data file copied in and each snapshot added. (2) `type KitContext with member this.copyExperimentsFrom (source : KitContext) (ids : ExperimentId list) : Result<ExperimentCopyReport, KitLibraryError>` reads everything it needs before it writes anything, in this order. (a) Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` it answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr \"copyExperimentsFrom\")` and reads nothing. (b) It reads `source.proxy.readExperiments ()` (step 148) and keeps, in the source's order, the experiments whose id `ids` names; an id the source lacks is `KitLibraryKitErr (MissingKitFileErr <its ExperimentKitFile file name>)`. (c) It lists `source.proxy.listSnapshots ()` (step 138) and takes `referenceClosure` (step 203) of the kept experiments' `libraryReferences` (step 137), in order, resolving an `EntryVersionReference` to the source's snapshot of that version and an `EntryLatestReference` to the source's highest-version snapshot of that entry; a reference the source holds no snapshot of is `UnheldEntryErr` naming its `describe`. Of that closure it keeps the versions `this.proxy.listSnapshots ()` holds no snapshot of. (d) It reads, through `source.proxy.readLabFile` (step 204), each distinct `dataFileOpt` path of the kept experiments, in order of first appearance. (e) It renumbers the kept experiments with `Experiment.renumberedFor` (step 203) over the ids of `this.proxy.readExperiments ()`. (f) It writes, in this order: each kept snapshot through `this.proxy.writeSnapshot` (step 138), byte for byte the source's entry file; each data file through `this.proxy.copyInFile <folder> source.file.leafName source.content` (step 133), where `<folder>` is `KitDataFolder.tryCreate` (step 132) of the path's `parentOpt` (step 196) when that answers `Ok`, and `KitDataFolder.root` otherwise, so a file keeps its data folder, takes the next free suffix on a clash (step 132's rule), and its new attachment (`KitDataFile.attachment`, step 132) records the hash of the bytes the kit now holds; and each renumbered experiment, its `dataFileOpt` replaced by the new attachment of its source path, through `this.proxy.writeExperiment` (step 148). The snapshots and data come first, so a written experiment never references a file the kit lacks. A `KitError` is `KitLibraryKitErr`; the first failure stops the copy, and what it wrote stays. (g) It answers the report. It pins nothing in the library: a version arrives as the source's snapshot, as a received kit's does, and the kit's import dialog resolves it the next time the kit is opened (step 141); a version the kit already holds keeps the kit's snapshot (step 139's rule). The source is only read. This first copy operation is extended with item transfer and mapping by steps 227-229 within S6, before the section's closing composition. No merge, deduplication of equal files across folders, or cache is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs`, `module ExperimentCopyTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its kits are `KitProxy.createInMemory` over fresh `InMemoryKitFolder`s (step 125), initialised with test-local kit files and opened through `KitContext.openKit` with a stepping clock, the source read-only and the target read-write unless a fact says otherwise. The source is filled before its read-only open: its experiments recorded through `{ kit = <it>; imports = <an import context over BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()> }.recordExperiment` (step 149), so its snapshots are the library's, and its data files placed through `placeLabFile` and attached through `attachLabFile` (step 134). E1 binds `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` at version 1 and `PresetIds.source600` by its entry id and attaches `data/raw/run 1.csv`; E2 binds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 and attaches nothing; E3 binds nothing and attaches `data/b.csv`. `a copy brings exactly the chosen experiments, the data files they reference and the snapshots they need`: copying [E1] into an empty target answers a report of E1, its one data file and E1's closure, and leaves the target's `paths` exactly `.kit-json`, `data`, `data/raw`, `data/raw/run 1.csv`, `library` and the `library/<name>` of each version of E1's closure; `readExperiments` answers E1 with an attachment at `data/raw/run 1.csv` whose hash is that of the source's bytes; the source's `paths` and texts are unchanged. `a copied experiment whose id the kit holds takes the next free id`: over a target holding E1 and E2 (written through `writeExperiment`), copying [E2; E3] leaves `readExperiments` answering the target's E1 and E2 unchanged, the source's E3 as E3, and the source's E2 as E4. `a copied data file whose name the kit holds takes the next free suffix, and its hash is re-recorded` : over a target holding `data/raw/run 1.csv` with other text, copying [E1] attaches `data/raw/run 1 (2).csv` with the hash of the source's bytes, and the target's first file keeps its text; with the source's file rewritten by an outside writer after its attach, the copied attachment records the hash of the rewritten bytes. `a data file two copied experiments share is copied once`: a source E5 that attaches `data/raw/run 1.csv` as E1 does, copied with E1, writes one data file, and both copied experiments reference it. `a snapshot the kit already holds is kept and not written again`: over a target already holding one version of E1's closure (written through `writeSnapshot`), copying [E1] reports every other version of the closure and not that one, and the target lists it once. `a copy whose data file the source lacks writes nothing` : a source experiment whose attached file an outside writer removed (`removeLabFile`, step 133) makes the copy answer `KitLibraryKitErr (MissingKitFileErr _)`, and the target's `paths` are unchanged. `a kit opened read-only copies nothing` : over a target opened read-only, the copy answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)` and its `paths` are unchanged. `an experiment the source does not hold is refused and nothing is written`: copying [E9] answers `KitLibraryKitErr (MissingKitFileErr _)` naming `E9.experiment-json`, and the target's `paths` are unchanged.","acceptance":"After the copy lands, `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` MUST write exactly the chosen experiments, renumbered on a clash, the data files they reference with re-recorded hashes, and the source snapshots of their closure the kit lacks, reading everything before writing and the source only read; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a copy brings exactly the chosen experiments, the data files they reference and the snapshots they need`, `a copied experiment whose id the kit holds takes the next free id`, `a copied data file whose name the kit holds takes the next free suffix, and its hash is re-recorded`, `a data file two copied experiments share is copied once`, `a snapshot the kit already holds is kept and not written again`, `a copy whose data file the source lacks writes nothing`, `a kit opened read-only copies nothing` and `an experiment the source does not hold is refused and nothing is written`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copy brings exactly the chosen experiments, the data files they reference and the snapshots they need","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copied experiment whose id the kit holds takes the next free id","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copied data file whose name the kit holds takes the next free suffix, and its hash is re-recorded","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a data file two copied experiments share is copied once","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a snapshot the kit already holds is kept and not written again","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copy whose data file the source lacks writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a kit opened read-only copies nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.an experiment the source does not hold is refused and nothing is written","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.ExperimentCopyReport","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":225,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S6k","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[224],"how_to":"Copy experiments from another kit… as semantic messages of the kit window (001 §O 'Kit menu: … Copy experiments from another kit…'; the S6 brief: pick a kit folder, the source opening read-only, and pick experiments; the S5.3 mapper's request: its kit writes go through the read-only guard of step 185; .spec-md §4 'UI'). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) `KitWindowShell` (steps 186, 201) gains `kitPicker : KitFolderPicker` (the folder dialog that chooses the kit to copy from, step 145), documented in one line; `inert` holds a picker answering `None` at once. (2) Before the model: `KitCopySource = { source : KitContext; experiments : Experiment list; chosen : ExperimentId list }`: the kit chosen to copy from, opened read-only, its experiments as read, and the ids chosen so far, in the source's order. (3) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitCopyOpt : KitCopySource option` after `kitSend` (step 201), documented in one line; `initWith` sets it to `None`. (4) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `OpenCopySource of KitFolder` (the kit the folder dialog chose), `ToggleCopiedExperiment of ExperimentId`, `CopyChosenExperiments` (the panel's Copy) and `CloseCopySource` (the panel's Cancel). (5) Arms. `OpenCopySource` and `CopyChosenExperiments` go through the private read-only guard of step 185 first, so a kit opened read-only answers `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.`, opens nothing and writes nothing; `ToggleCopiedExperiment` and `CloseCopySource` write nothing. `OpenCopySource folder`: when `kitFolderOpt` is `Some own` and `folder.canonical` equals `own.canonical` (step 181), `kitStatus` is `A kit cannot copy experiments from itself.` and nothing opens. Otherwise an open source is closed first (`close ()`, step 131), then `KitContext.openKit (KitProxy.create folder) ReadOnlyKitAccess model.kit.clock` (steps 126, 131: a read-only open writes nothing, not even `.oc`) and its `readExperiments ()` (step 148): `Ok` sets `kitCopyOpt` to `Some { source = <it>; experiments = <them>; chosen = [] }` and `kitStatus` to `None`; an `Error e` closes what was opened, sets `kitCopyOpt` to `None` and `kitStatus` to `The kit could not be opened to copy from — <e.describe>`. `ToggleCopiedExperiment id` adds the id to `chosen`, or removes it, keeping the source's order; without a source it changes nothing. `CopyChosenExperiments` with a source and a non-empty `chosen` calls `model.kit.copyExperimentsFrom src.source src.chosen` (step 224). On `Ok report` it reads `model.kit.proxy.readExperiments ()` and sets the window's content through the private function `loadKit` and the reload share (step 187 (4)), over the kit as it is, those experiments and the current `savedScenes`, as a reload does; it closes the source, sets `kitCopyOpt` to `None` and `kitStatus` to `Copied <n> experiment(s) from <the source kit's name>.`. On an `Error e` of either, the panel stays and `kitStatus` is `The experiments could not be copied — <e.describe>`. Without a source, or with nothing chosen, it changes nothing. `CloseCopySource` closes the source and sets `kitCopyOpt` to `None`, nothing else. The copy is the window's own write, so `changedKitFiles` (step 130) offers none of its files. Steps 227-229 MUST complete item transfer and explicit mapping within S6 before its closing composition. No preview, undo or other message is added here. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184), over its folder kits loaded into `initMain ()`. The source is a second folder kit made by `openKitAt` under the class's folder holding E1 (a dark line) and E2 (attaching a data file through `attachLabFile`), closed before the facts open it. `choosing a kit to copy from opens it read-only and lists its experiments` : `OpenCopySource` of the source folder sets `kitCopyOpt` to its two experiments with nothing chosen, and the source folder holds no `.oc` and keeps every byte. `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source`: then `ToggleCopiedExperiment` of E2 and `CopyChosenExperiments` leave the model's experiments holding E2, the target folder holding `E2.experiment-json` and E2's data file under `data`, `kitCopyOpt` `None`, and `kitStatus` `Copied 1 experiment(s) from <the source's name>.`; `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` then offers nothing. `toggling an experiment twice leaves it unchosen, and Cancel copies nothing`: toggling E1 twice leaves nothing chosen; toggling it and `CloseCopySource` leave `kitCopyOpt` `None` and the target holding no experiment file. `a kit opened read-only neither opens a source nor copies`: over the target opened read-only, `OpenCopySource` sets `kitStatus` to the read-only text and leaves `kitCopyOpt` `None`, and `CopyChosenExperiments` over a model whose `kitCopyOpt` the fact set by record update writes nothing. `a kit cannot copy from itself, and a folder that is no kit is told`: `OpenCopySource` of the window's own folder written with a trailing `/` sets `kitStatus` to `A kit cannot copy experiments from itself.`; of a folder holding only `notes.txt` it sets a `kitStatus` containing `the folder is not a kit` and leaves `kitCopyOpt` `None`. The shared kit-content update MUST receive model.kitItems, loaded by step 223, so copying experiments preserves the loaded item list until the item-transfer update in step 227.","acceptance":"After the copy messages land, `OpenCopySource` MUST open the chosen kit read-only and list its experiments, `ToggleCopiedExperiment` MUST choose and unchoose, `CopyChosenExperiments` MUST copy the chosen experiments into the window's kit and show them, and a kit opened read-only MUST open no source and copy nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `choosing a kit to copy from opens it read-only and lists its experiments`, `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source`, `toggling an experiment twice leaves it unchosen, and Cancel copies nothing`, `a kit opened read-only neither opens a source nor copies` and `a kit cannot copy from itself, and a folder that is no kit is told`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.choosing a kit to copy from opens it read-only and lists its experiments","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.toggling an experiment twice leaves it unchosen, and Cancel copies nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only neither opens a source nor copies","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit cannot copy from itself, and a folder that is no kit is told","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell.kitPicker","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitCopySource","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitCopyOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.OpenCopySource","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ToggleCopiedExperiment","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CopyChosenExperiments","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CloseCopySource","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-MESSAGES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":226,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S6l","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[225],"how_to":"Copy experiments from another kit… in the kit bar: the verb and the panel that picks the experiments (001 §O 'Kit menu'; 'Automation': every new control gets a stable id; .spec-md §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row, with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; AGENTS.md: every control of every window can be scrolled fully on screen). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the kit-bar group (step 188), each member with a one-line doc: `kitCopyExperimentsButton` (`\"KitCopyExperimentsButton\"`), `kitCopySourceText` (`\"KitCopySourceText\"`), `kitCopyExperimentList` (`\"KitCopyExperimentList\"`), `kitCopyChosenButton` (`\"KitCopyChosenButton\"`) and `kitCopyCancelButton` (`\"KitCopyCancelButton\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `attachDataFile` (`ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:65`): `static member kitCopyExperimentToggle (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` = `KitCopyExperimentToggle_<n>`, with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`, docs one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: the Kit menu gains, after Show in Explorer (001 §O's order), the verb `Copy experiments from another kit…` (`MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` carrying `kitCopyExperimentsButton`), present when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlOffered` (step 185) and `kitCopyOpt` is `None`; its press calls `model.kitShell.kitPicker.pickThen (OpenCopySource >> dispatch)` (steps 174, 225). When `kitCopyOpt` is `Some src`, under the verb row and any send progress: a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `kitCopySourceText`, `Copy from <src.source.kitFile.name>: choose the experiments to copy.`; a `ScrollViewer` carrying `kitCopyExperimentList`, vertical scroll bar `Auto`, `MaxHeight` 160, over a vertical `StackPanel` of one `CheckBox` per experiment of `src.experiments`, each carrying `kitCopyExperimentToggle e.id`, its content `E<n> — <e.description>`, checked when `src.chosen` holds its id, and each change sending `ToggleCopiedExperiment e.id`; and one horizontal `StackPanel` of two `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton`s: `Copy` (`kitCopyChosenButton`, `positiveBackground`, `CopyChosenExperiments`), present only when `src.chosen` is not empty, and `Cancel` (`kitCopyCancelButton`, `negativeBackground`, `CloseCopySource`), the action box's right margin being the gap. The list scrolls inside its own height because the bar sits outside the page's `ScrollViewer` (step 188): a source of many experiments never pushes a control out of reach. Every id is an AutomationId. Tests. `KitWindowTests` (step 184), screens mounted as step 188's: without a trait, `the copy UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the five fixed ids' texts and `kitCopyExperimentToggle (ExperimentId 3)`'s text `KitCopyExperimentToggle_3`. `an open source lists its experiments with a toggle each, and Copy and Cancel share a row, Cancel to the right` : over a model whose `kitCopyOpt` holds a source context from a folder kit with E1 and E2 and E2 chosen, `kitCopySourceText` names the source kit, E1's toggle is unchecked and E2's checked, and `kitCopyChosenButton` and `kitCopyCancelButton` have equal tops, Cancel's left beyond Copy's right; with nothing chosen `kitCopyChosenButton` is absent. `a kit opened read-only offers no Copy experiments`: over the kit opened read-only `kitCopyExperimentsButton` is absent, and over it opened read-write present. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing at a box's centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing Copy experiments, a toggle and Copy brings the experiment into the kit`: over a shell whose `kitPicker` answers a source kit folder holding E2 (made by `openKitAt` and closed), pressing `kitCopyExperimentsButton` shows the panel; pressing E2's toggle and then `kitCopyChosenButton` removes the panel, shows `kitStatus` starting `Copied 1 experiment(s)` and leaves `E2.experiment-json` in the window's kit folder. `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable` (step 188) keeps its assertion over a model that also runs a send (`kitSend` started and progressed) and holds an open copy source of forty experiments, so the bar is at its tallest.","acceptance":"After the copy panel lands, `kitCopyExperimentsButton` MUST open the folder dialog for a kit opened read-write, and an open source MUST list its experiments with a toggle each and Copy / Cancel on one row inside a bounded list; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Copy experiments, a toggle and Copy brings the experiment into the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the copy UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `an open source lists its experiments with a toggle each, and Copy and Cancel share a row, Cancel to the right`, `a kit opened read-only offers no Copy experiments` and the changed `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the copy UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.an open source lists its experiments with a toggle each, and Copy and Cancel share a row, Cancel to the right","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a kit opened read-only offers no Copy experiments","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.pressing Copy experiments, a toggle and Copy brings the experiment into the kit","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitCopyExperimentsButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitCopySourceText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitCopyExperimentList","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitCopyChosenButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitCopyCancelButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.kitCopyExperimentToggle","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S6-COPY-VIEW"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":227,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72k","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[226],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. Copying experiments brings the items they use, each mapped onto a kit item or added (001 §H; .spec-md §3.15; the S7.2 brief; the S6 mapper's request: `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` gains the item mapping, its read-then-write order and its report kept). Each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`: `KitLibraryError` (step 139) gains `KitLibraryItemErr of ItemError`, an item the copy could not take, rendered `the items could not be copied: <e.describe>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`: `ExperimentCopyReport` (step 224) gains `items : Item list` after `experiments`, each item added to the kit as written. `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` (step 224) takes `(itemRows : ItemCopyRow list)` after `ids`, the user's choices; an item no row names takes its default (step 221). After reading the kept experiments (224 (b)) it reads `source.proxy.readItems ()` and `this.proxy.readItems ()` (step 218); the used items are `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` of the kept experiments and the source's items, the rows `ItemCopyRow.copyRowsFor used <the kit's items> itemRows`, and the items to add `ItemCopyRow.itemsToAdd rows <the kit's items>` (step 221), a refusal answering `KitLibraryItemErr` before anything is written. The closure (224 (c)) walks the kept experiments' `libraryReferences` followed by the added items' (step 215), so an added item's model snapshot comes with it. The lab files read (224 (d)) are the kept experiments' `dataFileOpt` paths followed by the added items' `photoOpt` paths, each distinct path read once in order of first appearance. The writes (224 (f)) are the snapshots, then every lab file under step 224's folder and suffix rule, then each added item through `this.proxy.writeItem` (step 218), its `photoOpt` replaced by the attachment path of its copied photo, then the experiments, so a written item or experiment never references a file the kit lacks. A mapped item writes nothing, and no experiment changes, because an S4.3 experiment names no item (step 221). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the `CopyChosenExperiments` arm (step 225) passes `[]`, so a window's copy maps and adds each used item by its default until step 228 passes the panel's choices; on `Ok` it reads `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()` with the experiments and sets `kitItems` through step 223's content function. Tests, in `ExperimentCopyTests` (step 224), whose every existing fact passes `[]` and keeps its assertions. The source also holds items recorded through `recordItem` (step 219): `Laser600` (`SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.source600`, used by E1), `ML` (`StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` at version 1, used by E1), `QZ` (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, used by E2) and `CPL1` (the circular-polarizer item model, used by none). `a copy adds the items its experiments use, with their model snapshots`: copying [E1] with no row into an empty target answers a report whose `items` are Laser600 and ML; the target's `readItems` answers them, its `paths` hold `Laser600.item-json` and `ML.item-json` and every snapshot E1's closure needs, and neither QZ nor CPL1 is written. `an item the kit holds by id, or by model and label, is mapped and not added`: over a target holding ML (written through `writeItem`, the same id) and a `Laser600` of the same preset under another id, copying [E1] reports no item and leaves the target's item files unchanged. `an added item whose label the kit holds takes the next free label`: over a target holding an item labelled `ML` of the glass plate, copying [E1] adds the source's ML as `ML (2)`. `the user's choice overrides the default, and a choice the kit cannot take writes nothing`: over the target of the second fact, a row adding Laser600 adds it as `Laser600 (2)` while ML stays mapped; a row mapping ML onto a test-local GUID answers `KitLibraryItemErr (UnknownKitItemErr _)`, and a row adding ML, whose id the target holds, `KitLibraryItemErr (DuplicateItemIdErr _)`, each leaving the target's `paths` unchanged. `an added item's photo is copied with it`: with the source's ML given the photo `data/photos/ml.jpg` (attached through `attachLabFile`), copying [E1] writes `data/photos/ml.jpg` into the empty target and the added ML references it; over a target already holding another `data/photos/ml.jpg`, the copy is `data/photos/ml (2).jpg` and ML references that. `KitLibraryTests`' `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload` (step 139) covers `KitLibraryItemErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the copy brings items, `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` MUST add each used item the rows or the defaults add, with its model snapshot and photo, map the others, refuse a choice the kit cannot take before writing anything, and report the added items; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a copy adds the items its experiments use, with their model snapshots`, `an item the kit holds by id, or by model and label, is mapped and not added`, `an added item whose label the kit holds takes the next free label`, `the user's choice overrides the default, and a choice the kit cannot take writes nothing`, `an added item's photo is copied with it` and the widened `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload`, every existing `ExperimentCopyTests` fact keeping its assertions, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copy adds the items its experiments use, with their model snapshots","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.an item the kit holds by id, or by model and label, is mapped and not added","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.an added item whose label the kit holds takes the next free label","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.the user's choice overrides the default, and a choice the kit cannot take writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.an added item's photo is copied with it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.every kit library error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitLibrary.KitLibraryError.KitLibraryItemErr","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.ExperimentCopyReport.items","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S72-COPY-ITEMS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":228,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72l","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[227],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The copy panel's item mapping as semantic messages of the kit window (the S7.2 brief: after the experiments are picked, a mapping table lists every item they use, each with 'map to existing item' or 'add'; the S6 mapper's request: the kit bar's copy panel gains its choice; .spec-md §4 'UI'). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2: (1) `KitCopySource` (step 225) gains `items : Item list` (the source kit's items, read when it opens) and `itemRows : ItemCopyRow list` (the mapping table, step 221), each documented in one line. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ChooseCopiedItem of ItemId * ItemCopyChoice`, documented in one line: a press of a choice of the mapping table. (3) Arms. `OpenCopySource` (step 225) also reads the source's `readItems ()` after its experiments, an `Error e` closing what was opened with step 225's text; the source opens with its items and no row. `ToggleCopiedExperiment` (step 225) also sets `itemRows` to `ItemCopyRow.copyRowsFor (Experiment.itemsUsedBy <the chosen experiments> src.items) model.kitItems src.itemRows` (step 221), so a row appears at its default with the first chosen experiment that uses its item, keeps the user's choice while used, and goes when no chosen experiment uses it. `ChooseCopiedItem (id, choice)` sets the choice of the row whose `sourceItem.id` is `id`, and changes nothing without such a row or a source; it writes nothing. `CopyChosenExperiments` passes `src.itemRows` where step 227 passed `[]`; its status after an `Ok` that added items is `Copied <n> experiment(s) and added <m> item(s) from <the source kit's name>.`, and with no item added step 225's text; an `Error e` keeps the panel with step 225's text. No preview, undo or other message is added. Every record expression that builds a `KitCopySource` in the tests gains the two fields (`KitWindowModelTests`' read-only copy fact and `KitWindowTests`' open-source fact, steps 225, 226), their assertions unchanged. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests`, over step 225's folder kits: the source, made as step 225's and closed before a fact opens it, holds E1, whose setup binds the `PresetIds.source600` preset by its entry id, and E2, whose setup binds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, recorded through `recordExperiment` (step 149), and the items `Laser600` (`SourcePresetChoice` of that preset) and `QZ` (`StackSampleChoice` of that sample at version 1), recorded through `recordItem` (step 219); the target holds a `Laser600` item of the same preset under another id. `choosing experiments lists the items they use, each at its default`: after `OpenCopySource`, `itemRows` is empty; toggling E2 lists QZ with `AddCopiedItem`; toggling E1 too lists Laser600 with `MapOntoKitItem` of the target's Laser600, then QZ; toggling E2 off leaves Laser600 alone. `the user's choice for an item is kept and copied`: with E1 and E2 chosen, `ChooseCopiedItem` of Laser600 with `AddCopiedItem`, then `CopyChosenExperiments`, leave the target folder holding `Laser600 (2).item-json` and `QZ.item-json`, `kitItems` the target's Laser600, `Laser600 (2)` and QZ, and `kitStatus` `Copied 2 experiment(s) and added 2 item(s) from <the source's name>.`. `a choice the copy refuses keeps the panel and writes nothing`: with QZ written into the target under its own id first, choosing E2 maps QZ onto it by default; `ChooseCopiedItem` of QZ with `AddCopiedItem` and `CopyChosenExperiments` keep the panel, set `kitStatus` starting `The experiments could not be copied`, and write nothing. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the mapping messages land, choosing experiments MUST list the items they use at their defaults, `ChooseCopiedItem` MUST set a row's choice, and `CopyChosenExperiments` MUST copy with the rows and show the added items; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `choosing experiments lists the items they use, each at its default`, `the user's choice for an item is kept and copied` and `a choice the copy refuses keeps the panel and writes nothing`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.choosing experiments lists the items they use, each at its default","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the user's choice for an item is kept and copied","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a choice the copy refuses keeps the panel and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-MESSAGES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitCopySource.items","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitCopySource.itemRows","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ChooseCopiedItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-MESSAGES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":229,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72m","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[228],"how_to":"S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The mapping table in the kit bar's copy panel (the S7.2 brief; 001 §O 'Automation'; .spec-md §4 'UI'; AGENTS.md: every control of every window can be scrolled fully on screen). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the kit-bar group (steps 188, 226): `kitCopyItemList` (`\"KitCopyItemList\"`), with a one-line doc. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `kitCopyExperimentToggle` (step 226): `static member kitCopyItemChoice (sourceItem : ItemId) (choice : ItemCopyChoice) : ConstructorUiId` is `KitCopyItemChoice_<the source GUID>_Add` for `AddCopiedItem` and `KitCopyItemChoice_<the source GUID>_<the kit item's GUID>` for `MapOntoKitItem`, with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S7.2. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`, the copy panel (step 226): when `src.itemRows` is not empty, the `ScrollViewer` carrying `kitCopyExperimentList` holds, below the experiment toggles, the wrapping line `Items the chosen experiments use: add each to this kit, or use an item it already has.` and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitCopyItemList` of one block per row: the line `<source label> — <row.sourceItem.model.entryReferenceOpt's EntryReference.describe>` (step 213) and a `WrapPanel` of the choices `Add` (`AddCopiedItem`) and `Use <label>` for each item of `model.kitItems` (`MapOntoKitItem` of its id), each carrying `kitCopyItemChoice` and sending `ChooseCopiedItem`, the row's choice an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others `verbButton`s (the MaterialsWindowView actionButton / verbButton styling already used by the kit bar). The table shares the experiment list's scroller (`MaxHeight` 160), so the bar's tallest height is unchanged and no control leaves the screen. Its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. Tests. `KitWindowTests` (step 184), screens mounted as step 188's: without a trait, `the copy-mapping UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: `kitCopyItemList`'s text and `kitCopyItemChoice` of a test-local source GUID with `AddCopiedItem` and with `MapOntoKitItem` of a second GUID. `an open source lists the items its chosen experiments use, each with Add and the kit's items, the choice marked`: over a model whose `kitCopyOpt` holds a source with Laser600 mapped onto the kit's Laser600 and QZ added, `kitCopyItemList` holds two blocks; Laser600's `Use Laser600` choice and QZ's `Add` are marked; every choice box is inside `kitCopyExperimentList`. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `pressing a mapping choice and Copy adds or maps the item as chosen`: over a shell whose `kitPicker` answers a source folder kit holding E1 and the item Laser600 (made as in step 228), pressing `kitCopyExperimentsButton`, E1's toggle, Laser600's `Add` choice and `kitCopyChosenButton` leaves `Laser600 (2).item-json` in the window's kit folder beside its own Laser600's file, and `kitStatus` starting `Copied 1 experiment(s) and added 1 item(s)`. `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable` (steps 188, 226) keeps its assertion over a copy source whose forty experiments are chosen and whose twenty items each have a row.","acceptance":"After the mapping table lands, an open copy source MUST list each used item with Add and the kit's items, the choice marked, inside the panel's bounded scroller; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a mapping choice and Copy adds or maps the item as chosen`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the copy-mapping UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `an open source lists the items its chosen experiments use, each with Add and the kit's items, the choice marked` and the changed `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the copy-mapping UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-VIEW","S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.an open source lists the items its chosen experiments use, each with Add and the kit's items, the choice marked","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S72-COPY-VIEW","S6-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.pressing a mapping choice and Copy adds or maps the item as chosen","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S72-COPY-VIEW","S6-COPY"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-VIEW","S6-COPY"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.kitCopyItemList","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.kitCopyItemChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S72-COPY-VIEW"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":230,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S6m","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[229,226],"how_to":"Open kit from zip… as semantic messages of the start screen (001 §F 'Open kit from zip…: choose a target folder, extract, open'; 001 §P `OpenKitZip`; the S6 brief: choose a zip and a target folder, extract, then open as S5.2 does; .spec-md §10.2, §10.4: per-file progress with Cancel, and the completion message updates the model). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs` (steps 176-178), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: (1) `KitStartContext` (step 176) gains, each field documented in one line, `zipPicker : KitZipPicker` (the open dialog of a zip, step 198; the target folder comes from `picker`), `archive : KitArchiveProxy` (step 197) and `archiveJobs : KitArchiveJobHost` (step 200). Every record expression building the context gains the three: `KitStartWindow` (step 179) composes `zipPicker = KitZipPicker.none`, `archive = KitArchiveProxy.create ()` (step 199) and `archiveJobs = KitArchiveJobHost.onUiThread (fun p -> dispatch (OpenKitZipProgressed p)) (fun r -> dispatch (OpenKitZipEnded r))` over the dispatch it captures from its init command, and step 232 gives it the real dialog; the test contexts of `KitStartTests` and `KitStartWindowTests` hold `KitZipPicker.none`, an in-memory archive and `KitArchiveJobHost.inert` unless a fact says otherwise. (2) Before the model: `KitZipOpening = { zip : FileName; target : KitFolder }`, a zip and the folder it is extracted into. (3) `KitStartModel` gains `zipJob : KitArchiveJobState` (the one extraction, step 200) and `zipOpeningOpt : KitZipOpening option` (what it extracts), each documented in one line; `initKitStart` sets `KitArchiveJobState.idle` and `None`. (4) `KitStartMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `OpenKitZip of KitZipOpening` (the button's message after its two dialogs, and how a test opens a zip), `OpenKitZipProgressed of JobProgress`, `OpenKitZipEnded of Result<KitArchiveOutcome, KitArchiveError>` and `CancelOpenKitZip`. (5) `updateKitStart`: `OpenKitZip opening` answers the model unchanged while `zipJob.job.isRunning`; otherwise it calls `m.context.archiveJobs.startArchiveJob (fun observer -> m.context.archive.receiveKit opening.zip opening.target observer)` (step 198) and answers `zipJob` started with the handle, `zipOpeningOpt` `Some opening`, `NoKitStartOffer` and no status. `OpenKitZipProgressed p` passes `zipJob` through `progressed`. `OpenKitZipEnded result` sets `zipJob` to idle and `zipOpeningOpt` to `None`; for `Ok (KitArchiveFinished _)` with `Some opening` it then answers exactly as `OpenKit opening.target` does: `KitOpening.openExistingKitAt` (step 172), then step 177's one private function that reads every open's answer, so the kit is opened read-write, the history bumped and the kit handed to `showKit`, or the open's offer or status is shown. `Ok KitArchiveCancelled` sets `status` to `Open kit from zip was cancelled: nothing was extracted.` and `Error e` to `The zip could not be opened — <e.describe>`. `CancelOpenKitZip` calls `m.zipJob.cancel ()` and answers the model unchanged. No retry, overwrite of a non-empty folder (step 197 refuses it), merge into an existing kit or other message is added. Tests, in `KitStartTests` (step 176), over folders under its class folder, `archive = KitArchiveProxy.create ()` and either `KitArchiveJobHost.immediate` over recorders whose messages the fact passes through `updateKitStart` in order, or a test-local deferred host. The zip is made from a kit opened by `openKitAt`, given an experiment through `writeExperiment` (step 148) and closed, then sent through `KitArchiveProxy.create ().sendKit` (step 198) into `<fact>/exports/<name>.zip`. `Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit into the chosen folder, opens it and bumps the history`: `OpenKitZip` into `<fact>/received/k`, which does not exist, records one shown kit, read-write, whose kit file equals the original's and whose experiments equal the original's; the history's first entry is that folder; `zipJob` is idle and no status remains. `a zip extracted into a folder that holds files is refused, and nothing opens`: into a folder holding `notes.txt`, the status contains `not empty`, nothing is shown, and the folder holds exactly `notes.txt`. `a cancelled extraction opens nothing and leaves no folder`: over the deferred host, `CancelOpenKitZip` cancels the fact's source; the kept job run over an observer of that token answers `Ok KitArchiveCancelled`; `OpenKitZipEnded` of it shows the cancel status, shows no kit, and the target does not exist. `a zip that holds no kit is told, and nothing opens`: a zip written by `writeKitZip` without `.kit-json` ends with a status containing `holds no kit` and nothing shown. `a running extraction shows its progress, and a second Open kit from zip waits for it`: over the deferred host, a second `OpenKitZip` while the first runs leaves the model unchanged and the host holds one job.","acceptance":"After the Open kit from zip messages land, `OpenKitZip` MUST start one extraction through the context's job host and, once it finishes, open the extracted folder as Open kit does, and `CancelOpenKitZip` MUST cancel it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit into the chosen folder, opens it and bumps the history`, `a zip extracted into a folder that holds files is refused, and nothing opens`, `a cancelled extraction opens nothing and leaves no folder`, `a zip that holds no kit is told, and nothing opens` and `a running extraction shows its progress, and a second Open kit from zip waits for it`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit into the chosen folder, opens it and bumps the history","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a zip extracted into a folder that holds files is refused, and nothing opens","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a cancelled extraction opens nothing and leaves no folder","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a zip that holds no kit is told, and nothing opens","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a running extraction shows its progress, and a second Open kit from zip waits for it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartContext.zipPicker","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartContext.archive","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartContext.archiveJobs","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitZipOpening","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartModel.zipJob","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartModel.zipOpeningOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartMsg.OpenKitZip","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartMsg.OpenKitZipProgressed","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartMsg.OpenKitZipEnded","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartMsg.CancelOpenKitZip","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-MESSAGES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":231,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S6n","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[230],"how_to":"Open kit from zip… on the start screen, with its progress row (001 §F 'Start-screen actions: … Open kit from zip…'; 001 §A UI label 'Open kit from zip…'; the S6 brief: id `OpenKitZipButton`; .spec-md §10.2). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the start-screen group (step 178), each member with a one-line doc: `openKitZipButton` (`\"OpenKitZipButton\"`), `openKitZipProgressBar` (`\"OpenKitZipProgressBar\"`), `openKitZipProgressText` (`\"OpenKitZipProgressText\"`) and `openKitZipCancelButton` (`\"OpenKitZipCancelButton\"`). (2) `kitStartView` (step 178), docs one to three lines citing spec 0050 S6: its first row gains, after `Open kit…`, the verb `Open kit from zip…` (`MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` carrying `openKitZipButton`), present while `m.zipJob.job.isRunning` does not hold; its press calls `m.context.zipPicker.pickZipToOpenThen (fun zip -> m.context.picker.pickThen (fun target -> dispatch (OpenKitZip { zip = zip; target = target })))` (steps 174, 200, 230): the zip first, then the folder to extract into, and a cancel of either sends nothing. Directly under that row, while the extraction runs, `kitArchiveProgressView m.zipJob { bar = ConstructorUiId.openKitZipProgressBar; text = ConstructorUiId.openKitZipProgressText; cancel = ConstructorUiId.openKitZipCancelButton } (fun () -> dispatch CancelOpenKitZip)` (step 200). Nothing else on the screen changes. Tests, in `KitStartWindowTests` (step 178), screens mounted as its facts mount them. Without a trait: `the Open kit from zip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the four ids' texts. `a running extraction shows its progress bar, its count and Cancel, and hides Open kit from zip`: over a model whose `zipJob` is started with a test-local handle and progressed by 3 of 4 files, `openKitZipProgressText` reads a text starting `3 / 4`, `openKitZipProgressBar`'s value is 0.75, `openKitZipCancelButton` is present and `openKitZipButton` absent; over the idle model the button is present and no progress row exists. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing at a box's centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` does: `Open kit from zip asks for a zip, then a folder, and starts one extraction of that zip into that folder`: over a context whose `zipPicker` answers a test-local zip and records each call, whose `picker` answers a fresh folder and records each call, and whose `archiveJobs` is a test-local deferred host, pressing `openKitZipButton` asks the zip dialog, then the folder dialog, records one job and shows `openKitZipProgressText`; pressing `openKitZipCancelButton` calls the handle's cancel once.","acceptance":"After Open kit from zip joins the start screen, `openKitZipButton` MUST ask for a zip and then a folder and send `OpenKitZip`, and a running extraction MUST show its progress bar, count and Cancel; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `Open kit from zip asks for a zip, then a folder, and starts one extraction of that zip into that folder`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Open kit from zip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `a running extraction shows its progress bar, its count and Cancel, and hides Open kit from zip`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.the Open kit from zip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S6-ZIP-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.a running extraction shows its progress bar, its count and Cancel, and hides Open kit from zip","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S6-ZIP-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.Open kit from zip asks for a zip, then a folder, and starts one extraction of that zip into that folder","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S6-ZIP-VIEW"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.openKitZipButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.openKitZipProgressBar","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.openKitZipProgressText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.openKitZipCancelButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S6-ZIP-VIEW"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":232,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-S6o","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[231],"how_to":"The start screen opens a real zip dialog, and Open kit from zip… works end to end in the app (001 §F; 001 §G 'Exports: Documents\\Optical Constructor\\Exports\\', where Send kit… writes; the S6 brief: then open as S5.2 does). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs` (step 179): `KitStartWindow(context, mode, pickerFor, zipPickerFor : TopLevel -> KitZipPicker, showConstructor)`, the new argument after `pickerFor`, mirroring it; the composed context's `zipPicker` is `zipPickerFor this` (in place of step 230's `KitZipPicker.none`); its doc says so in one line. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `LauncherWindow` (steps 180, 190, 191): Main's and Inverse's start screens are built with `fun owner -> KitZipPicker.ofWindow owner locations.exportsFolder` (steps 81, 200), so the dialog starts in the exports folder. (3) Every other construction of `KitStartWindow` passes a zip picker: `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit start screen leaves everything reachable` (step 179), `KitStartWindowTests`' window facts and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`' launcher fact (step 180) pass `fun _ -> KitZipPicker.none`, their assertions unchanged. Tests, in `KitStartWindowTests`, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit and opens it in the constructor of the screen's mode`: a kit made by `openKitAt` under the fact's folder, given an experiment and closed, is sent through `KitArchiveProxy.create ().sendKit` into `<fact>/exports/<name>.zip`; a `KitStartWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitStartWindowTests\")` with a fresh in-memory history, `ForwardConstructor`, a picker answering a fresh `<fact>/received/k`, a zip picker answering that zip and a `showConstructor` recording the mode and the kit, is shown; pressing `openKitZipButton` at its centre starts the real extraction on a worker, and the fact runs `Dispatcher.UIThread.RunJobs ()` until the recorder holds a kit or ten seconds pass, never a fixed sleep; the recorder then holds `ForwardConstructor` with a read-write kit whose kit file equals the original's, the received folder holds every sent file, the screen is closed, and the history's one entry is the received folder. The recorded kit is closed at the end. `LauncherTests`' facts keep their assertions: the launcher's start screens are built with the real dialog, which no fact presses.","acceptance":"After the start screen's dialog is wired, `KitStartWindow` MUST take `zipPickerFor`, the launcher MUST pass `KitZipPicker.ofWindow` over the exports folder, and Open kit from zip MUST extract a sent kit and open it in the constructor of the screen's mode; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit and opens it in the constructor of the screen's mode`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests.acceptance: Open kit from zip extracts a sent kit and opens it in the constructor of the screen's mode","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S6-ZIP-WIRE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.App.LauncherWindow","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S6-ZIP-WIRE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":233,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-S6p","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[232],"how_to":"The constructor windows compose the real Send kit… and Copy experiments… seams (the S6 brief: Send kit… through a save dialog defaulting to the DataLocations exports folder; 001 §G: the suggested parent of kit folders is the kits folder; .spec-md §3.9: every location comes from settings). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: `AppContext` gains `locations : DataLocations` (step 81), documented in one line (the locations the app scope was composed over, where its windows' dialogs start), set by `compose` (step 89) from its `locations` argument, so `create` and `recreateLibrary` carry it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (step 189): the shell is `{ KitWindowShell.inert with explorer = ExplorerProxy.system; requestClose = window.Close; zipPicker = KitZipPicker.ofWindow window context.locations.exportsFolder; archive = KitArchiveProxy.create (); archiveJobs = KitArchiveJobHost.onUiThread (fun p -> dispatch (SendKitProgressed p)) (fun r -> dispatch (SendKitEnded r)); kitPicker = KitFolderPicker.ofWindow window context.locations.kitsFolder }` (steps 150, 199, 200, 201, 225), over the dispatch the mount captures from its init command; `mount` takes the `AppContext` for it, which `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` pass. Their docs say, in no more words, that the kit bar sends and copies through the real dialogs. No other seam changes. Tests. `AppContextTests` gains `the app scope carries the locations it was composed over`: `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"AppContextTests\")` holds `locations` equal to `TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName \"AppContextTests\")` (step 83). `KitWindowTests` gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `a constructor window's kit bar offers Send kit, and Copy experiments only to a kit opened read-write`: a shown `MainConstructorWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitWindowTests\")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152) holds `sendKitButton` and `kitCopyExperimentsButton`; over that kit closed and opened again read-only it holds `sendKitButton` and no `kitCopyExperimentsButton`. Neither is pressed, because a real window's dialogs are the system's (the S5.3 Show in Explorer precedent). The windows' consumers keep their assertions.","acceptance":"After the constructor windows are wired, `AppContext.locations` MUST hold the composed locations and the windows' kit shell MUST hold the real save dialog over the exports folder, the real archive and job host and the real kit folder dialog; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `a constructor window's kit bar offers Send kit, and Copy experiments only to a kit opened read-write`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app scope carries the locations it was composed over`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests.the app scope carries the locations it was composed over","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S6-KIT-SHELL-WIRE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a constructor window's kit bar offers Send kit, and Copy experiments only to a kit opened read-write","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S6-KIT-SHELL-WIRE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.AppContext.locations","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs","obligations":["S6-KIT-SHELL-WIRE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.App.MainConstructorWindow","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S6-KIT-SHELL-WIRE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.App.InverseConstructorWindow","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S6-KIT-SHELL-WIRE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S6 -- Send and receive kits; copy experiments between kits"}
{"number":234,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71m","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[233,216],"how_to":"Setting one parameter's state, as a pure update of one item (001 §P: `SetParameterState` is a semantic message; the S7.1 brief: pure updates for SetParameterState; 001 §I: each item has its own parameter values). On `Item` in `Kit.fs` (step 215), documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: `member this.withParameterState (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<Item, ItemError>`. It answers `UnknownItemParameterErr` naming the item's label and the name when no parameter has the name, and the `InvalidParameterStateErr` of `{ name = name; state = state }.validate` (step 214) when the state breaks its rules; otherwise the item with that parameter's state replaced in place, every other parameter, the order, the revision and the history unchanged. A state set this way edits the working revision; only a published revision (step 235) moves the revision. It writes nothing. Tests, in `KitItemTests`, over a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive` (step 216): `setting a parameter's state replaces it in place and keeps the revision`: setting `c2.retardance` to `UnknownParameter` starting at π / 2 within [π / 4, 3π / 4] answers the item with that state at the same position, the other four parameters unchanged and revision 1. `setting the state of a parameter the item lacks, or one that breaks its rules, is refused`: setting `nothing`, and setting `c2.retardance` to an unknown whose bounds are reversed, answer `UnknownItemParameterErr` and `InvalidParameterStateErr`, and the item is as it was. `two items of one model keep independent parameters` : with CPL2 made by the same draft under another id and label, setting CPL1's `c2.fastAxisOffset` to `KnownParameter 0.01` leaves CPL2's parameters equal to the model's defaults.","acceptance":"After SetParameterState lands, `Item.withParameterState` MUST replace one named parameter's state in place, refuse a name the item lacks and a state that breaks its rules, and leave the revision unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `setting a parameter's state replaces it in place and keeps the revision`, `setting the state of a parameter the item lacks, or one that breaks its rules, is refused` and `two items of one model keep independent parameters`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s23 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.setting a parameter's state replaces it in place and keeps the revision","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-SET-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.setting the state of a parameter the item lacks, or one that breaks its rules, is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-SET-PARAMETER-STATE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.two items of one model keep independent parameters","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-SET-PARAMETER-STATE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.withParameterState","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-SET-PARAMETER-STATE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.1 -- Items, parameters and item models"}
{"number":235,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S71n","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[234],"how_to":"Publishing a revision, as a pure update of one item (001 §I 'Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history; \"Publish calibration\" writes the next revision. Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'; the S7.1 brief: publishing a revision, which S11.5 uses). On `Item` in `Kit.fs`, documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1: `member this.publishRevision (published : Parameter list) : Result<Item, ItemError>`. It checks every published parameter first and writes nothing on a refusal: a name the item lacks is `UnknownItemParameterErr`, a name given twice is `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming it, and a state that fails `validate` (step 214) is its `InvalidParameterStateErr`. Otherwise it answers the item whose `history` is the old history followed by `{ revision = this.revision; parameters = this.parameters }`, whose `revision` is `this.revision.next`, and whose parameters take each published state in place, the others unchanged. S11.5's Publish calibration passes `CalibratedParameter` states; any state may be published. No limit, time stamp or other field is added: the history holds every earlier revision's values, which is short because a fit run keeps the rest. Tests, in `KitItemTests`, over a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive` (step 216): `publishing a revision records the values it replaces and counts the revision up`: publishing `c2.retardance` as `CalibratedParameter { value = 1.55; sigma = 0.002; fitRun = FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\" }` answers revision 2 whose history is the one record of revision 1 with the five default parameters, and whose `c2.retardance` is that calibration; publishing `c2.fastAxisOffset` on that answer gives revision 3 with two records, revisions 1 and 2, in that order. `a revision naming a parameter the item lacks, naming one twice or breaking a rule publishes nothing`: publishing `nothing`, `c2.retardance` twice, or a calibration with sigma 0 each answers its error, and the item keeps revision 1 and an empty history.","acceptance":"After publishing lands, `Item.publishRevision` MUST record the replaced values as the current revision's history record, count the revision up and take every published state, and MUST publish nothing when a parameter is unknown, repeated or invalid; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `publishing a revision records the values it replaces and counts the revision up` and `a revision naming a parameter the item lacks, naming one twice or breaking a rule publishes nothing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s23 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.publishing a revision records the values it replaces and counts the revision up","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PUBLISH-REVISION"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.a revision naming a parameter the item lacks, naming one twice or breaking a rule publishes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S71-PUBLISH-REVISION"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.publishRevision","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S71-PUBLISH-REVISION"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.1 -- Items, parameters and item models"}
{"number":236,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[235,220],"how_to":"The item edits the Items panel sends besides AddItem and SetParameterState: a label, notes and a photo (the S7.2 brief: 'plus label, notes and photo edits'; 001 §I: an item has an optional photo (a kit file) and notes; the S7.1 mapper's request: a rename, photo or notes edit is its own member). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) ItemError.UnknownKitItemErr from step 213 MUST be reused unchanged; the copy mapping already consumes it. (2) On `Item` (step 215), beside `withParameterState` (step 234): `member this.withNotes (notes : ItemNotes) : Item` answers the item with those notes; `member this.withPhoto (photoOpt : KitRelativePath option) : Item` answers it with that photo, `None` removing the reference and never a file (001 §E 'Lab files are read-only for the app'); `member this.relabelledAmong (label : ItemLabel) (items : Item list) : Result<Item, ItemError>` answers `DuplicateItemLabelErr` naming both labels when an item of `items` with another `id` has a label whose `fileStem` equals the new one's ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`, the rule of `ItemDraft.addTo`, step 216), and otherwise the item with the new label; the item's own entry in `items` is ignored, so `lp1` may become `LP1`. None of the three changes the parameters, the revision or the history: like `withParameterState` they edit the working revision, and only `publishRevision` moves it (steps 234, 235). (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ItemIdProvider = { mintItemId : unit -> ItemId }`, the provider that mints a new item's identity (AGENTS.md: ambient effects are injected as provider records, as `ClockProvider` is, step 122); its system instance is declared beside `ClockProvider.system` in step 239. No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `KitItemTests` (step 213), over a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive`: `an item's notes and photo are edited in place, keeping its parameters and revision`: `withNotes (ItemNotes \"Mounted 2026-11-01\")` and `withPhoto` of the kit path `data/photos/CPL1.jpg` (`KitRelativePath.tryCreate`, step 123) answer the item with those notes and that photo, and `withPhoto None` removes the photo; the parameters, revision 1 and the empty history are unchanged. `relabelling an item keeps its id and refuses a label whose file name another item holds`: over the items CPL1 and LP1 (an `ItemDraft` over `ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`), relabelling CPL1 `CPL 1` answers the item with its id and the new label, relabelling it `cpl1` answers that label, and relabelling it `lp1` answers `DuplicateItemLabelErr` naming `LP1`. `every item error renders its condition and its payload` (step 213) covers `UnknownKitItemErr`.","acceptance":"After the item edits land, `Item.withNotes` and `Item.withPhoto` MUST edit an item in place, `Item.relabelledAmong` MUST refuse a label whose file name another item holds, and `ItemError` MUST hold `UnknownKitItemErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item's notes and photo are edited in place, keeping its parameters and revision`, `relabelling an item keeps its id and refuses a label whose file name another item holds` and the widened `every item error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.an item's notes and photo are edited in place, keeping its parameters and revision","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.relabelling an item keeps its id and refuses a label whose file name another item holds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.every item error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemError.UnknownKitItemErr","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.withNotes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.withPhoto","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.relabelledAmong","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ItemIdProvider","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDITS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.2 -- The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy"}
{"number":237,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72c","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[236,221],"how_to":"A relabelled item moves to the file of its new label (001 §A: an item is `<label>.item-json`; step 218: no member renamed an item until this section; the S7.2 brief: label edits, writes through KitProxy). In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`, on step 219's `type KitLibraryContext with` extension, documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2: `member this.recordRelabelledItem (previous : Item) (relabelled : Item) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>`, where `relabelled` is `previous` under a new label (`relabelledAmong`, step 236). When the two labels' `fileStem`s differ ignoring case, it records `relabelled` through `this.recordItem` (step 219) and then deletes the old file through `this.kit.proxy.deleteKindFile ItemKitFile previous.label.fileStem` (step 127); when that delete fails, it deletes the new file through the same verb, logs that delete's own failure with `Logger.logError` carrying its `describe`, and answers the first error as `KitLibraryKitErr`, so a failed relabel leaves the item under its old label and never two files of one `ItemId`, which `readItems` refuses (step 218). When the stems are equal ignoring case (`lp1` to `LP1`), the kit root being one Windows folder, it deletes the old file first and then records `relabelled`; when that record fails it writes `previous` back through `this.kit.proxy.writeItem` (step 218), logging that write's own failure, and answers the first error. Under a read-only kit the first write or delete answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and nothing is written. No other member is added. Tests, in `KitLibraryTests` (steps 139, 219), over its Built-in library and its in-memory kit opened read-write, with a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `DialMounted DialPositive` recorded through `recordItem`: `a relabelled item moves to the file of its new label`: relabelled `CPL 1` and recorded through `recordRelabelledItem`, `paths` holds `CPL 1.item-json` and no `CPL1.item-json`, and `kit.proxy.readItems ()` answers the item under its new label and its id. `a relabel that changes only the case rewrites the one file`: an item recorded as `cpl1` and relabelled `CPL1` leaves exactly one item file, `CPL1.item-json`, and `readItems` answers the item labelled `CPL1`. `a relabel whose old file cannot be deleted leaves the item under its old label`: over a context whose proxy is a record update of the in-memory one refusing `deleteKindFile` of the stem `CPL1` with `KitIoErr`, relabelling CPL1 `CPL 1` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitIoErr _)`, and `readItems` answers CPL1 alone under its old label.","acceptance":"After the relabel lands, `KitLibraryContext.recordRelabelledItem` MUST leave the item in the file of its new label alone, rewrite one file for a change of case, and leave the item under its old label when the old file cannot be deleted; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a relabelled item moves to the file of its new label`, `a relabel that changes only the case rewrites the one file` and `a relabel whose old file cannot be deleted leaves the item under its old label`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a relabelled item moves to the file of its new label","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-RELABEL-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a relabel that changes only the case rewrites the one file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-RELABEL-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a relabel whose old file cannot be deleted leaves the item under its old label","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-RELABEL-FILE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordRelabelledItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S72-RELABEL-FILE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.2 -- The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy"}
{"number":238,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[237,223],"how_to":"The constructor's flow strip as model state: which step of the flow the window shows (001 §O 'a left flow strip: Items → Setups → Experiments → Data → Unknowns → Plan → Fit → Results → Publish, each step reachable directly'; the S7.2 brief: in this section its steps are Items, Setups (the table) and Experiments (the existing Experiments bay); .spec-md §3.22: a step appears only when it works). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2: (1) Before the model: `ConstructorFlowStep` = `ItemsFlowStep` | `SetupsFlowStep` | `ExperimentsFlowStep`. `static member all : ConstructorFlowStep list` lists them in 001 §O's order, where S9.3, S11 and S14 insert Data, Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results and Publish when each works. `member this.caption : ControlCaption` is `Items`, `Setups` or `Experiments`. It is window state, never stored, so it carries no wire tag. (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `flowStep : ConstructorFlowStep` after `kitItems` (step 223), documented in one line; `initWith` sets it to `SetupsFlowStep`, so a window opens on the table and the Add bay as today. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ShowFlowStep of ConstructorFlowStep`, documented in one line: a press of a flow-strip step. (4) Arms. `ShowFlowStep ItemsFlowStep` sets `flowStep` alone. `ShowFlowStep SetupsFlowStep` sets `flowStep` and, when `ribbon` is `BayNames.experiments` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:BayNames`), sets `ribbon` to `BayNames.add`, the table's first bay; any other open bay stays. `ShowFlowStep ExperimentsFlowStep` sets `flowStep` and `ribbon = BayNames.experiments`: the Experiments step is the existing Experiments bay. The `SelectBay name` arm of `updateTableAndElementRotation` keeps setting `ribbon` and also sets `flowStep` to `ExperimentsFlowStep` for `BayNames.experiments` and to `SetupsFlowStep` for any other bay, so the strip names the surface the ribbon shows. The forward and inverse constructors show the same strip. No other message or field changes. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184): `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups`: `ConstructorFlowStep.all` is Items, Setups and Experiments with those captions, and `initMain ()` opens on `SetupsFlowStep` with `BayNames.add`. `showing a flow step shows its surface, and the Experiments step is the Experiments bay`: from `initMain ()`, `ShowFlowStep ExperimentsFlowStep` opens `BayNames.experiments`; `ShowFlowStep ItemsFlowStep` then keeps it; `ShowFlowStep SetupsFlowStep` then opens `BayNames.add`; and with `BayNames.details` open, `ShowFlowStep SetupsFlowStep` keeps it. `choosing a ribbon bay keeps the flow strip on Setups or Experiments`: `SelectBay BayNames.experiments` sets `ExperimentsFlowStep` and `SelectBay BayNames.rotation` `SetupsFlowStep`, the kit, the elements and the experiments unchanged.","acceptance":"After the flow state lands, `ShowFlowStep` MUST set the window's step, the Experiments step MUST open the Experiments bay, a ribbon bay choice MUST keep the step on Setups or Experiments, and a window MUST open on Setups; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups`, `showing a flow step shows its surface, and the Experiments step is the Experiments bay` and `choosing a ribbon bay keeps the flow strip on Setups or Experiments`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STATE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.showing a flow step shows its surface, and the Experiments step is the Experiments bay","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STATE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.choosing a ribbon bay keeps the flow strip on Setups or Experiments","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STATE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ConstructorFlowStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.flowStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STATE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ShowFlowStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STATE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.2 -- The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy"}
{"number":239,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72g","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[238],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests"],"how_to":"The Items panel's state and `AddItem`, as semantic messages of the constructor window (001 §O 'Items panel: the list, \"Add item from library model…\"'; 001 §P `AddItem`; the S7.2 brief: a picker over presets, samples and item models, writes through KitProxy; the S7.1 mapper's request: offer `AppContext.itemModels` and the presets and sample versions as `ItemModelChoice`, mint the `ItemId` through an injected provider, send AddItem through `ItemDraft.addTo` and record through `KitLibraryContext.recordItem`; .spec-md §4 'UI'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, beside `ClockProvider.system` (step 150): `type ItemIdProvider with static member system : ItemIdProvider` mints `ItemId (Guid.NewGuid ())` at each call (step 236), documented in one line citing spec 0050 S7.2. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (a) Before the model: `AddItemForm = { itemId : ItemId; offers : ItemModelChoice list; chosenOpt : ItemModelChoice option; labelText : ControlCaption; dial : ItemDial }`: the open form, holding the new item's id, minted when the form opens; the models offered (step 216); the one chosen; the label as typed, a raw caption until `ItemLabel.tryCreate` reads it; and the dial. `member this.itemDraftOpt : ItemDraft option` is `Some { id = itemId; label = <it>; model = <the chosen>; dial = dial }` when a model is chosen and `ItemLabel.tryCreate labelText.value` answers `Ok`, and `None` otherwise. (b) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains, after `flowStep` (step 238), each documented in one line: `itemModels : ItemModelProxy` (the item-model store the form offers, step 209), `itemIds : ItemIdProvider`, `selectedItemOpt : ItemId option` (the item the panel shows) and `addItemFormOpt : AddItemForm option`. `initWith` sets them to `ItemModelProxy.createInMemory ()`, `ItemIdProvider.system`, `None` and `None`. `DefaultStores.DefaultStoreSet` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:430`) gains `itemModels`, the `itemModels` of the in-memory stores it imports the Built-in catalogue into (steps 42, 94, 210), and `initTableAndElementRotation` and `initMain` set it by record update beside `sources` and `catalogueImports` (step 101), so the test scenes offer the eight built-in item models. (c) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `SelectKitItem of ItemId` (a press of an item row), `OpenAddItemForm` (Add item from library model…), `ChooseNewItemModel of ItemModelChoice`, `SetNewItemLabel of ControlCaption`, `SetNewItemDial of ItemDial`, `CancelAddItemForm` and `AddItem of ItemDraft` (001 §P: the form's Add, and how a test adds an item). (d) Arms. `OpenAddItemForm` reads the offers in this order: the standalone forms from `model.itemModels.listItemModels ()` as `LibraryModelChoice`s; sourceModel, polarizerModel and sampleModel MUST be the resolved SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel and StackSampleItemModel versions from that same list, joined to their typed physics offers; the source presets of `model.library.entriesForKind LightSource` (each `SourceItem s` as `SourcePresetChoice (sourceModel, s)`); the polarizer presets of `entriesForKind LinearPolarizer` then `CircularPolarizer` (each `PolarizerItem p` as `PolarizerPresetChoice (polarizerModel, p)`, one per entry id); and the samples of `entriesForKind Sample` (each `SampleItem s` as `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, SampleVersionId.firstOf s.id, s)`, the version an experiment's binding pins, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:descriptorBinding`, so an item and an experiment name one entry). A library listing that fails offers nothing of its kind, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:allowedEntryIds` treats one; an `Error e` of the item-model store sets `kitStatus` to `The item models could not be listed — <e.describe>` and the other offers stay. The form opens with `itemId = model.itemIds.mintItemId ()`, those offers, nothing chosen, an empty label and `FixedMounting`. `SelectKitItem id` sets `selectedItemOpt = Some id` when `kitItems` holds the id, and changes nothing otherwise. `ChooseNewItemModel`, `SetNewItemLabel` and `SetNewItemDial` set the open form's field and change nothing without a form; `CancelAddItemForm` sets `addItemFormOpt = None`; none of these writes. `AddItem draft` is a write message: it goes through step 185's private read-only guard first, so a kit opened read-only answers `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.` and writes nothing. Otherwise `draft.addTo model.kitItems` (step 216): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `The item was not added — <e.describe>` and changes nothing else; `Ok item` is recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordItem item` (step 219): `Ok ()` sets `kitItems` to the items with it in label order (ordinal), `selectedItemOpt = Some item.id`, `addItemFormOpt = None` and `kitStatus = None`; `Error e` keeps the items and sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>` (step 152's text). No remove, duplicate, template or other message is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs`, `module ItemsPanelModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its models are `initMain ()` (the in-memory scratch kit over the Built-in stores, steps 150, 152) with `itemIds` a test-local provider answering fixed GUIDs in turn. `Add item from library model lists the item models, the presets and the samples, and mints the item's id`: `OpenAddItemForm` opens a form whose `itemId` is the provider's first GUID, nothing chosen, an empty label and `FixedMounting`, and whose offers are the eight `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` as `LibraryModelChoice`s ordered by name, then the source presets, then the polarizer presets, then the samples at version 1, in `entriesForKind`'s order. `the add form takes a model, a label and a dial, and Cancel closes it writing nothing`: `ChooseNewItemModel` of the circular-polarizer offer, `SetNewItemLabel (ControlCaption \"CPL1\")` and `SetNewItemDial (DialMounted DialPositive)` set the form, whose `itemDraftOpt` is that draft; with the label `  ` it is `None`; `CancelAddItemForm` closes the form, and `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()` answers `[]`. `AddItem records the item in the kit with its model's snapshot and selects it`: `AddItem` of the CPL1 draft leaves `kitItems` CPL1, CPL1 selected, the form closed and `kitStatus` `None`; `readItems ()` answers CPL1 and `listSnapshots ()` holds the circular polarizer's version 1 envelope. `AddItem of a label the kit holds is told and records nothing`: then `AddItem` of a draft labelled `cpl1` under a new id sets `kitStatus` containing `already has an item of that label`, and `kitItems` and `readItems ()` are unchanged. `a kit opened read-only adds no item`: over the model whose kit is its scratch kit's read-only view (`{ m.kit with proxy = m.kit.proxy.readOnlyView; access = ReadOnlyKitAccess }`, step 152's fixture), `AddItem` of the CPL1 draft sets `kitStatus` to the read-only text, and `readItems ()` answers `[]`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the panel's state lands, `OpenAddItemForm` MUST offer the item models, presets and samples with a minted id, and `AddItem` MUST record a new item through `recordItem`, refusing a label the kit holds and any write under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Add item from library model lists the item models, the presets and the samples, and mints the item's id`, `the add form takes a model, a label and a dial, and Cancel closes it writing nothing`, `AddItem records the item in the kit with its model's snapshot and selects it`, `AddItem of a label the kit holds is told and records nothing` and `a kit opened read-only adds no item`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.Add item from library model lists the item models, the presets and the samples, and mints the item's id","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.the add form takes a model, a label and a dial, and Cancel closes it writing nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.AddItem records the item in the kit with its model's snapshot and selects it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.AddItem of a label the kit holds is told and records nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.a kit opened read-only adds no item","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.ItemIdProvider.system","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.AddItemForm","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.itemModels","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.itemIds","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.selectedItemOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.addItemFormOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SelectKitItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.OpenAddItemForm","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ChooseNewItemModel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetNewItemLabel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetNewItemDial","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CancelAddItemForm","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.AddItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ADD-ITEM"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.2 -- The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy"}
{"number":240,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72h","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[239],"how_to":"`SetParameterState`, the parameter editor and the label, notes and photo edits, as semantic messages of the constructor window (001 §P `SetParameterState`; 001 §O 'a parameter grid (state, value, bounds, σ, provenance)'; the S7.2 brief: plus label, notes and photo edits, writes through KitProxy). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (1) Before the model: `ParameterStateChoice` = `KnownStateChoice` | `UnknownStateChoice`, the two states a user sets by hand (a calibration comes from a fit, S11.5). `ParameterEditField` = `ValueEditField` | `LowerEditField` | `UpperEditField` | `PriorSigmaEditField`. `ParameterEditDraft = { itemId : ItemId; name : ParameterName; choice : ParameterStateChoice; valueText : ControlCaption; lowerText : ControlCaption; upperText : ControlCaption; priorSigmaText : ControlCaption }`, the editor's typed-in texts, raw captions until `tryState` reads them. `static member ofParameter (itemId : ItemId) (parameter : Parameter) : ParameterEditDraft` fills it from the state: a known value is `KnownStateChoice` with that value; an unknown is `UnknownStateChoice` with its start, its bounds and its prior's sigma, the sigma empty without a prior; a calibration is `KnownStateChoice` with its value; a field the state has no number for is empty; numbers are written `ToString(\"R\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`. `member this.withFieldText (field : ParameterEditField) (text : ControlCaption) : ParameterEditDraft` sets one field. `member this.tryState : Result<ParameterState, ItemError>` reads the texts with `Double.TryParse(text, NumberStyles.Float, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`: `KnownStateChoice` is `KnownParameter` of the value; `UnknownStateChoice` is `UnknownParameter { start = value; bounds = { lower; upper }; priorOpt }`, `priorOpt` `None` for an empty sigma and otherwise `Some { centre = value; sigma }`, so a prior is centred on the start; a text a needed number does not read from is `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming the parameter and the field (`value`, `lower`, `upper` or `prior sigma`). The rules of a state stay `Parameter.validate`'s (step 214), which `withParameterState` applies. (2) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `parameterEditOpt : ParameterEditDraft option` after `addItemFormOpt` (step 239), documented in one line; `initWith` sets it to `None`, and `SelectKitItem` (step 239) sets it to `None`. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `SetParameterState of ItemId * ParameterName * ParameterState` (001 §P: the editor's Set, and how a test sets a state), `EditItemParameter of ParameterName` (a press of a parameter row of the selected item), `SetParameterEditChoice of ParameterStateChoice`, `SetParameterEditText of ParameterEditField * ControlCaption`, `CancelParameterEdit`, `RelabelKitItem of ItemId * ItemLabel`, `SetKitItemNotes of ItemId * ItemNotes`, `SetKitItemPhoto of ItemId * FileName` (the photo file the picker answered) and `RemoveKitItemPhoto of ItemId`. (4) Arms. `EditItemParameter name` opens `ParameterEditDraft.ofParameter` of the selected item's parameter of that name and changes nothing without one; `SetParameterEditChoice` and `SetParameterEditText` change the open draft (`withFieldText`) and `CancelParameterEdit` closes it; none of these writes. The six others are write messages: each goes through step 185's read-only guard first, and an id `kitItems` does not hold changes nothing. Each makes the edited item through a Domain member: `SetParameterState (id, name, state)` through `withParameterState name state` (step 234), `RelabelKitItem` through `relabelledAmong label model.kitItems` (step 236), `SetKitItemNotes` through `withNotes`, `RemoveKitItemPhoto` through `withPhoto None`, and `SetKitItemPhoto (id, file)` through `model.experimentData.attachDataFile file` (step 135: a file inside the kit is recorded in place, one outside is copied into `data/`) and then `withPhoto (Some attachment.path)`. A refusal sets `kitStatus` to `The item was not changed — <e.describe>`, or `The photo was not attached — <e.describe>` for the attach, and writes nothing more. The edited item is then recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }`: `recordRelabelledItem item edited` (step 237) for a relabel, `recordItem edited` (step 219) otherwise. `Ok ()` replaces the item in `kitItems` in label order, closes the editor after a `SetParameterState` and sets `kitStatus` to `None`; `Error e` keeps `kitItems` and sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. No undo, publish (S11.5) or dial edit is added: the dial is chosen when the item is added (step 215). Tests, in `ItemsPanelModelTests` (step 239), over its model holding CPL1, added through `AddItem` of step 239's CPL1 draft (the circular-polarizer model, `DialMounted DialPositive`): `SetParameterState sets an item's parameter and records it`: `SetParameterState` of CPL1's `c2.retardance` as `UnknownParameter` starting at π / 2 within [π / 4, 3π / 4] leaves that state in `kitItems` and in `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()`, at revision 1. `a parameter state that breaks its rules is told and nothing is recorded`: the same with the bounds reversed sets `kitStatus` containing `the parameter state is not valid`, and `kitItems` and `readItems ()` are unchanged. `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets`: `EditItemParameter (ParameterName \"c2.retardance\")` opens a draft at `KnownStateChoice` whose value text reads back π / 2 exactly; `SetParameterEditChoice UnknownStateChoice` with the lower, upper and prior-sigma texts `0.7`, `2.4` and `0.1` gives a `tryState` of an unknown starting at π / 2 within [0.7, 2.4] with a prior centred at π / 2 of sigma 0.1; the lower text `abc` gives `InvalidParameterStateErr` naming `lower`; an empty sigma gives no prior; `ofParameter` of a calibration of 1.55 is `KnownStateChoice` at 1.55; `CancelParameterEdit` closes the draft. `relabelling an item renames its kit file, and a label another item holds is told`: `RelabelKitItem` of CPL1 to `CPL 1` leaves `kitItems` labelled `CPL 1` and the kit's item files `CPL 1.item-json` alone; with LP1 added, relabelling `CPL 1` to `lp1` sets `kitStatus` containing `already has an item of that label`. `notes and a photo are recorded with the item, and removing the photo keeps its file`: `SetKitItemNotes` of `Mounted` is read back by `readItems ()`; `SetKitItemPhoto` of a file the fact writes under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"ItemsPanelModelTests\", <a new GUID>, \"CPL1.jpg\")` gives CPL1 the photo `data/CPL1.jpg`, which the kit's `paths` hold; `RemoveKitItemPhoto` removes the photo and `data/CPL1.jpg` stays. `a kit opened read-only edits no item and writes nothing`: over the read-only model of step 239's fact with `kitItems` set to the CPL1 the scratch kit holds, each of the six write messages sets `kitStatus` to the read-only text and the kit's `paths` are unchanged.","acceptance":"After the edit messages land, `SetParameterState`, `RelabelKitItem`, `SetKitItemNotes`, `SetKitItemPhoto` and `RemoveKitItemPhoto` MUST change one item through its Domain member and record it, telling a refusal and writing nothing under a read-only kit, and `ParameterEditDraft.tryState` MUST read the state the editor sets; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SetParameterState sets an item's parameter and records it`, `a parameter state that breaks its rules is told and nothing is recorded`, `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets`, `relabelling an item renames its kit file, and a label another item holds is told`, `notes and a photo are recorded with the item, and removing the photo keeps its file` and `a kit opened read-only edits no item and writes nothing`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.SetParameterState sets an item's parameter and records it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.a parameter state that breaks its rules is told and nothing is recorded","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.relabelling an item renames its kit file, and a label another item holds is told","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.notes and a photo are recorded with the item, and removing the photo keeps its file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.a kit opened read-only edits no item and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ParameterStateChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ParameterEditField","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ParameterEditDraft","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.parameterEditOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetParameterState","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.EditItemParameter","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetParameterEditChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetParameterEditText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CancelParameterEdit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.RelabelKitItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetKitItemNotes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetKitItemPhoto","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.RemoveKitItemPhoto","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-ITEM-EDIT-MESSAGES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.2 -- The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy"}
{"number":241,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[240],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests"],"how_to":"The Items panel, a surface in a file of its own (001 §O 'Items panel: the list, \"Add item from library model…\", a parameter grid (state, value, bounds, σ, provenance), the dial mapping, revisions'; 001 §O 'Automation': ids such as `KitItemList`; the S7.2 brief: ids `KitItemList`, `AddItemButton`, `ItemParameterGrid` and so on; .spec-md §4 'UI': new surfaces live in their own files; §10.5: an opposing pair shares a row with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the kit-bar group (steps 188, 202, 226), `// --- The Items panel (ItemsPanelView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `itemsPanel` (`\"ItemsPanel\"`), `kitItemList` (`\"KitItemList\"`), `addItemButton` (`\"AddItemButton\"`), `addItemOfferList` (`\"AddItemOfferList\"`), `newItemLabelField` (`\"NewItemLabelField\"`), `addItemConfirmButton` (`\"AddItemConfirmButton\"`), `addItemCancelButton` (`\"AddItemCancelButton\"`), `itemLabelField` (`\"ItemLabelField\"`), `itemModelText` (`\"ItemModelText\"`), `itemDialText` (`\"ItemDialText\"`), `itemNotesField` (`\"ItemNotesField\"`), `itemPhotoText` (`\"ItemPhotoText\"`), `itemChoosePhotoButton` (`\"ItemChoosePhotoButton\"`), `itemRemovePhotoButton` (`\"ItemRemovePhotoButton\"`), `itemParameterGrid` (`\"ItemParameterGrid\"`), `parameterEditPanel` (`\"ParameterEditPanel\"`), `parameterEditKnownChoice` (`\"ParameterEditKnownChoice\"`), `parameterEditUnknownChoice` (`\"ParameterEditUnknownChoice\"`), `parameterEditValueField` (`\"ParameterEditValueField\"`), `parameterEditLowerField` (`\"ParameterEditLowerField\"`), `parameterEditUpperField` (`\"ParameterEditUpperField\"`), `parameterEditPriorSigmaField` (`\"ParameterEditPriorSigmaField\"`), `parameterEditSetButton` (`\"ParameterEditSetButton\"`), `parameterEditCancelButton` (`\"ParameterEditCancelButton\"`) and `itemRevisionList` (`\"ItemRevisionList\"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each declaration with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S7.2. Ids: `static member kitItemRow (itemId : ItemId) : ConstructorUiId` is `KitItemRow_<the GUID>`; `addItemOffer (choice : ItemModelChoice)` is `AddItemOffer_<the entry GUID>_v<n>` for an item model or a sample and `AddItemOffer_<the preset's entry id>` for a preset; `newItemDialChoice (dial : ItemDial)` is `NewItemDial_Fixed`, `NewItemDial_Positive` or `NewItemDial_Negative`; `itemParameterRow (name : ParameterName)` is `ItemParameterRow_<the name>`; `itemRevisionRow (revision : ItemRevision)` is `ItemRevisionRow_<n>`. Captions, each `member this.caption : ControlCaption`: `ItemModelChoice` (an item model `<name> v<n>`, a preset its entry name, a sample `<name> v<n>`); `ItemDial` (`Fixed mounting`, `On a dial, sign +1`, `On a dial, sign −1`); `ItemRevisionRecord` (`Revision <n>: <name> <value>, …`, a known value, an unknown's start or a calibration's value). `ParameterGridCells = { state : ControlCaption; value : ControlCaption; bounds : ControlCaption; sigma : ControlCaption; provenance : ControlCaption }` and `type Parameter with member this.gridCells : ParameterGridCells`: a known value is `Known`, its value, `—`, `—`, `Given`; an unknown `Unknown`, its start, `[<lower>, <upper>]`, its prior's sigma or `—`, `To be fitted`; a calibration `Calibrated`, its value, `—`, its sigma, `Fit run <the fit run's name>`. Every number is `ToString(\"G6\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`, in the parameter's own unit (step 207). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `pickDataFile` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3376`) becomes public and takes `(title : ControlCaption)` after the owner, setting the picker options' `Title` to it; `attachDataFileButton` passes `ControlCaption \"Attach measured-data file\"`, today's title, so its picker is unchanged, and its doc says the Items panel's photo uses it too. On the model extension that holds `kitWrites` (step 185): `member model.itemModelCaption (item : Item) : ControlCaption` is the name the window's stores give the item's model: a preset's entry name through `model.library.tryGetEntry`, a sample's `<name> v<n>` through `model.samples.resolveVersion`, an item model's `<name> v<n>` through `model.itemModels.resolveItemModelVersion`, and `(model not in the library)` when the store answers `None` or an error. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ItemsPanelView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.ItemsPanelView`, compiled directly after `KitStartView.fs` (step 176) and before `KitWindowView.fs` (step 188): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and `itemsPanelView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`'s doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. The view is a `ScrollViewer`, both scroll bars `Auto`, over one vertical `StackPanel` carrying `itemsPanel`, margin 8, holding in order: (a) the semi-bold `Items` and the wrapping line `The physical pieces of this kit: each instantiates a library model and holds its own parameters.`; (b) while the kit's writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185) and no form is open, the verb `Add item from library model…` (`addItemButton`, sending `OpenAddItemForm`); (c) with a form open: `Choose a model:` over a `ScrollViewer` carrying `addItemOfferList`, vertical scroll bar `Auto`, `MaxHeight` 220, over the offers grouped under the semi-bold headings `Item models`, `Light sources`, `Polarizers` and `Samples` (a group with no offer shows nothing), each offer a box carrying `addItemOffer` with its caption sending `ChooseNewItemModel`; a `DockPanel` of `Label:` and a `TextBox` carrying `newItemLabelField` showing `labelText` whose every change sends `SetNewItemLabel`; `Dial:` and a `WrapPanel` of the three `newItemDialChoice` boxes (`FixedMounting`, `DialMounted DialPositive`, `DialMounted DialNegative`) with their captions sending `SetNewItemDial`; and one horizontal `StackPanel` of `Add` (`addItemConfirmButton`, `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, present only when the form's `itemDraftOpt` is `Some draft`, sending `AddItem draft`) and `Cancel` (`addItemCancelButton`, on `negativeBackground`, sending `CancelAddItemForm`), the action box's right margin being the gap; (d) a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `kitItemList`, one box per item of `kitItems` carrying `kitItemRow` and reading `<label> — <model.itemModelCaption item> — revision <n>`, sending `SelectKitItem`, or the line `This kit holds no item yet.`; (e) for the selected item: a `DockPanel` of `Label:` and a `TextBox` carrying `itemLabelField`, enabled by `kitWrites`, which on Enter or losing focus sends `RelabelKitItem` of `ItemLabel.tryCreate` of its text when that answers `Ok` with another label (a blank text is ignored, as `ExperimentControls`' number fields ignore an unreadable one); `Model: <itemModelCaption>` (`itemModelText`); `Dial: <dial.caption>` (`itemDialText`), the dial's zero being the `dialZero` row of the grid; `Notes:` and a wrapping `TextBox` carrying `itemNotesField`, accepting returns, enabled by `kitWrites`, which on losing focus sends `SetKitItemNotes` when its text changed; `Photo: <the kit path>` or `No photo` (`itemPhotoText`) with, while writes are offered, the verb `Choose photo…` (`itemChoosePhotoButton`), whose press resolves the owner window as `attachDataFileButton` does and calls `pickDataFile owner (ControlCaption \"Choose item photo\")` sending `SetKitItemPhoto`, and, when a photo is set, `Remove photo` (`itemRemovePhotoButton`, `RemoveKitItemPhoto`); a `Grid` carrying `itemParameterGrid`, six `Auto` columns `Parameter`, `State`, `Value`, `Bounds`, `σ` and `Provenance`, a semi-bold header row and one row per parameter in the item's order, whose first cell is a box carrying `itemParameterRow` with the name sending `EditItemParameter` and whose other cells are the parameter's `gridCells`; with `parameterEditOpt` open for this item, a block carrying `parameterEditPanel`: `Edit <name>`, a `WrapPanel` of `Known` (`parameterEditKnownChoice`) and `Unknown` (`parameterEditUnknownChoice`) sending `SetParameterEditChoice`, the labelled `TextBox`es `Value:` (or `Start:`), and for an unknown `Lower:`, `Upper:` and `Prior σ (blank: none):`, carrying their `parameterEdit…Field` ids, each change sending `SetParameterEditText`, the `describe` of `tryState`'s error in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`, and one horizontal `StackPanel` of `Set` (`parameterEditSetButton`, `positiveBackground`, present only when `tryState` answers `Ok state` and writes are offered, sending `SetParameterState (item.id, name, state)`) and `Cancel` (`parameterEditCancelButton`, `negativeBackground`, `CancelParameterEdit`); and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `itemRevisionList`: `Revision <n> (current)` and then each `history` record, newest first, by its caption, each line carrying `itemRevisionRow` of its revision. A chosen offer, the chosen dial and state, and the selected item's row are `actionButton`s on `positiveBackground` and the others `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton`s, the import dialog's chosen-option look (step 108). Every id is an AutomationId. A `WrapPanel` sits only in a vertical block (AGENTS.md). Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ItemsPanelTests.fs`, `module ItemsPanelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounting `itemsPanelView` in a `HostWindow` as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` (`:107`) mounts a view, headless at 1000 × 700, over `initMain ()` driven through its messages (steps 239, 240). Without a trait: `the Items panel UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the fixed ids' texts, `kitItemRow` of a test-local GUID, `addItemOffer` of the circular polarizer's `LibraryModelChoice` (`AddItemOffer_33486eec-836a-4cbf-ac79-e3f14439ad4b_v1`), `newItemDialChoice (DialMounted DialNegative)`, `itemParameterRow (ParameterName \"c2.retardance\")` (`ItemParameterRow_c2.retardance`) and `itemRevisionRow ItemRevision.first`. `the Items panel lists the kit's items and shows the selected item's model, dial, notes, photo, parameters and revisions`: with CPL1 (circular polarizer, `DialMounted DialPositive`) and LP1 added, CPL1's `c2.fastAxisOffset` published as `CalibratedParameter` of 0.01 with sigma 0.002 from `FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\"` (step 235, set into `kitItems` by record update) and CPL1 selected: `kitItemList` holds CPL1's row then LP1's, CPL1's reading `CPL1 — Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder) v1 — revision 2`; `itemModelText` and `itemDialText` read `Model: Circular polarizer (linear polarizer and retarder) v1` and `Dial: On a dial, sign +1`; the grid holds the five parameter rows, `c2.fastAxisOffset`'s reading `Calibrated`, `0.01`, `—`, `0.002` and `Fit run QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z`; `itemRevisionList` holds revisions 2 and 1. `the add form lists the library models by kind and offers Add and Cancel on one row, Cancel to the right`: after `OpenAddItemForm`, `addItemOfferList` holds the circular polarizer's offer and `addItemConfirmButton` is absent; after a model and the label `CPL1`, `Add` and `Cancel` have equal tops, Cancel's left beyond Add's right. `the parameter editor offers Known and Unknown, and Set and Cancel on one row`: after `EditItemParameter` of CPL1's `c2.retardance` and `SetParameterEditChoice UnknownStateChoice`, the lower, upper and prior fields are present; with the lower text `abc` the Set box is absent and the error is shown; with valid texts Set and Cancel have equal tops, Cancel to the right. `a kit opened read-only offers no item write in the Items panel`: over a model whose kit is the read-only view of a scratch kit holding CPL1 with a photo, `kitItems` CPL1 and CPL1 selected (record updates, as `ItemsPanelModelTests`' read-only facts build them, steps 239, 240), `addItemButton`, `itemChoosePhotoButton` and `itemRemovePhotoButton` are absent and `itemLabelField` and `itemNotesField` are disabled. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` (`:69`) does: `pressing Add item, a model, a label and Add records the item in the kit`: pressing `addItemButton`, the circular polarizer's offer, setting `newItemLabelField`'s text to `CPL1` and pressing `addItemConfirmButton` shows CPL1's `kitItemRow`, and the model's scratch kit's `readItems ()` answers CPL1. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. The addItemOffer id and caption MUST always include the item-model GUID/version; a bound preset or sample MUST add its binding identity so two offers sharing one model remain distinct. Missing model resolution MUST render the typed missing-model condition, not a preset-only caption.","acceptance":"After the panel's view lands, `itemsPanelView` MUST show the kit's items, the add form, the selected item's label, model, dial, notes, photo, parameter grid, editor and revisions under their `ConstructorUiId`s, every write control withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Add item, a model, a label and Add records the item in the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Items panel UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the Items panel lists the kit's items and shows the selected item's model, dial, notes, photo, parameters and revisions`, `the add form lists the library models by kind and offers Add and Cancel on one row, Cancel to the right`, `the parameter editor offers Known and Unknown, and Set and Cancel on one row` and `a kit opened read-only offers no item write in the Items panel`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ItemsPanelView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ItemsPanelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests.the Items panel UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ItemsPanelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S72-ITEMS-PANEL-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests.the Items panel lists the kit's items and shows the selected item's model, dial, notes, photo, parameters and revisions","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ItemsPanelTests.fs","cla