{"number":242,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S72j","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[241],"how_to":"The flow strip on the left of the constructor window, each step reachable directly, and the surface its step shows (001 §O 'a left flow strip …, each step reachable directly'; 001 §O 'Automation'; the S7.2 brief: the flow strip in its own view file, every step reachable directly, with ids; .spec-md §3.22, §4 'UI'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the Items-panel group (step 241), `// --- The constructor's flow strip (FlowStripView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `flowStrip` (`\"FlowStrip\"`), `flowItemsStep` (`\"FlowItemsStep\"`), `flowSetupsStep` (`\"FlowSetupsStep\"`) and `flowExperimentsStep` (`\"FlowExperimentsStep\"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` (step 238) gains `member this.flowUiId : ConstructorUiId`, its box's id (`flowItemsStep`, `flowSetupsStep` or `flowExperimentsStep`), documented in one line. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/FlowStripView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.FlowStripView`, compiled directly after `ItemsPanelView.fs` (step 241) and before `KitWindowView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and `flowStripView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`'s doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. The view is a `Border` carrying `flowStrip`, margin 8, 4, 0, 4, over a vertical `StackPanel` holding one box per step of `ConstructorFlowStep.all`, in order, carrying `step.flowUiId` with `step.caption` and sending `ShowFlowStep step`: the window's step (`model.flowStep`) an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, the others `verbButton`s (step 241's chosen-option look). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs`, `kitWindowView` (step 188): its `DockPanel` holds the kit bar (top), then `FlowStripView.flowStripView model dispatch` docked left, then the step's surface as the fill: `ItemsPanelView.itemsPanelView model dispatch` for `ItemsFlowStep` and `mainView model dispatch` for `SetupsFlowStep` and `ExperimentsFlowStep`, keyed `items` or `workbench` with `Avalonia.FuncUI.DSL.View.withKey`, so a change between the two recreates the surface (the keyed-slot discipline of `Ribbon.fs:ribbonView`) and Setups ↔ Experiments keeps the workbench. Its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. Tests. `KitWindowTests` (step 184), screens mounted as step 188's: without a trait, `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the four ids' texts and each step's `flowUiId`. `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows`: over the loaded model, the three step boxes are present, top to bottom, Items above Setups above Experiments, each left of the surface; on `SetupsFlowStep` `tableElementCanvas` is present and `itemsPanel` absent; on `ItemsFlowStep` `itemsPanel` is present and the canvas absent; on `ExperimentsFlowStep` the Experiments bay's pane (`ConstructorUiId.ribbonPane` of its key) is present. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing the flow strip's steps shows the Items panel, the Experiments bay and the table`: pressing `flowItemsStep` shows `itemsPanel`, pressing `flowExperimentsStep` the Experiments bay's pane, and pressing `flowSetupsStep` the table canvas. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the kit window's Items step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"KitWindowItems\"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over `initMain ()` on `ItemsFlowStep` with three items added through `AddItem` (step 239), the second selected, its first parameter's editor open as unknown, and the add form open. `the kit window: the kit bar and the page stay reachable` (steps 188, 226) keeps its assertion with the strip present.","acceptance":"After the flow strip lands, `kitWindowView` MUST show the flow strip left of the surface, each step a box under its `ConstructorUiId` that shows the Items panel, the table or the Experiments bay; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing the flow strip's steps shows the Items panel, the Experiments bay and the table`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `the kit window's Items step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/FlowStripView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.pressing the flow strip's steps shows the Items panel, the Experiments bay and the table","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Items step leaves everything reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.flowStrip","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.flowItemsStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.flowSetupsStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.flowExperimentsStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ConstructorFlowStep.flowUiId","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.FlowStripView.flowStripView","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/FlowStripView.fs","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView.kitWindowView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S72-FLOW-STRIP-VIEW"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.2 -- The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy"}
{"number":243,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-S72n","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[242,229],"how_to":"The constructor windows' Items panel reads the app's item models with the kit's snapshots, and an item added in a real window is a kit file (the S7.2 brief; the S7.1 mapper's request: offer `AppContext.itemModels`; .spec-md §0.1 `Program.fs`; 001 §E 'So the kit opens on any machine'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: each constructor window's seed (steps 154, 189) threads `itemModels = context.itemModels.overlaidWith opened.overlay` (steps 220, 222) by record update beside `catalogueImports`; `itemIds` stays `initWith`'s `ItemIdProvider.system` (step 239), and the photo picker is the system dialog the view opens (step 241). The docs of `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` say, in no more words, that their Items panel reads the app's item models. No other seam changes. (2) Tests, in `KitWindowTests`, with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: an item added in a constructor window is a kit file with its model's snapshot, and the window reopened lists it`: a shown `MainConstructorWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitWindowTests\")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152): pressing `flowItemsStep`, `addItemButton`, the circular polarizer's offer, setting `newItemLabelField`'s text to `CPL1` and pressing `addItemConfirmButton` shows CPL1's `kitItemRow`; the kit's folder holds `CPL1.item-json` and `library/33486eec-836a-4cbf-ac79-e3f14439ad4b@v1.item-model-json`; the window closed, a second `MainConstructorWindow` over the same folder opened again through `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) shows CPL1's `kitItemRow` once `flowItemsStep` is pressed. The windows' other consumers keep their assertions.","acceptance":"After the windows are wired, a constructor window's Items panel MUST offer the app's item models over the kit's snapshots and record an added item in the kit's folder with its model's snapshot; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: an item added in a constructor window is a kit file with its model's snapshot, and the window reopened lists it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: an item added in a constructor window is a kit file with its model's snapshot, and the window reopened lists it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S72-WIRE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.App.MainConstructorWindow","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S72-WIRE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.App.InverseConstructorWindow","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S72-WIRE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S7.2 -- The Items panel, the flow strip and item mapping on copy"}
{"number":244,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S81a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[243],"how_to":"Every parameter name an item model publishes is written once, as a member of `ParameterName`, so the evaluator of this section reads a value under the very name the model publishes (001 §I 'Each model publishes its parameter axes'; 001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a re-transcribed constant is a defect). No name's text, order, kind or default changes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`, on `ParameterName` (moved there by step 205), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: static members answering the names steps 207, 208 and 215 publish, their texts unchanged: `azimuth`, `ellipticity`, `degreeOfPolarization` and `intensityScale` (the light source); `extinctionRatio`, `diattenuation` and `axisOffset` (the real linear polarizer); `retardance` and `fastAxisOffset` (the retarder plate); `blackBoxScale`, whose text is `scale` (the black box's scale); `gain` and `darkOffset` (the intensity detector); `rotationUncertainty`, `elementUncertainty` and `throughputUncertainty` (the noise budget); `dialZero` (a dial-mounted item); and `substrateThickness`, whose text is `substrate.thickness`. Static members over positions: `muellerElement (row : int) (column : int)` is `m<row><column>`, rows and columns 0 to 3 as step 208 numbers them; `filmThickness (position : int)` is `film<k>.thickness`; `repeatedLayerThickness (position : int) (layer : int)` is `film<k>.layer<j>.thickness`, both 1-based as step 207 numbers them. `member this.inComponent (position : int) : ParameterName` is the name prefixed `c<k>.` (1-based, light order), so a compound inside a compound prefixes twice. These are members, and a member may speak its type's own primitives (AGENTS.md 'Members may speak their type's own primitives'), so the positions stay `int`. (2) The publishers name the members and change nothing else. `SourcePreset` gains `static member lightSourceAxes : ItemParameterAxis list`, the four light-source axes of step 207 in their order with their kinds and defaults (`azimuth` and `ellipticity` `AngleParameter` 0, `degreeOfPolarization` `FractionParameter` 0, `intensityScale` `ScaleParameter` 1), and step 207's `SourcePreset.parameterAxes` answers it, so a run with no bound source reads the same default parameter set (step 252). `ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes` and `Sample.parameterAxes` (steps 206, 207), and `OpticalForm.parameterAxes` and `ItemModelForm.parameterAxes` (step 208), build every name through these members, a compound's prefix through `inComponent`. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, `ItemDial.parameterAxes` (step 215) names `ParameterName.dialZero`. No publisher writes a published name's text any more, and no other member, type or option is added. Tests, in `ItemModelsTests` (step 205): `every published parameter name is one ParameterName member`: `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` names `ParameterName.azimuth`, `ParameterName.ellipticity`, `ParameterName.degreeOfPolarization` and `ParameterName.intensityScale` in that order and equals `(BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633).parameterAxes`; `ParameterName.degreeOfPolarization.value` is `degreeOfPolarization`; `(ParameterName.muellerElement 2 3).value` is `m23`; `(ParameterName.filmThickness 2).value` is `film2.thickness`; `(ParameterName.repeatedLayerThickness 2 1).value` is `film2.layer1.thickness`; `ParameterName.substrateThickness.value` is `substrate.thickness`; `ParameterName.blackBoxScale.value` is `scale`; `(ParameterName.retardance.inComponent 2).value` is `c2.retardance`; and `((ParameterName.extinctionRatio.inComponent 1).inComponent 2).value` is `c2.c1.extinctionRatio`. Every fact of steps 207, 208 and 215 runs unchanged.","acceptance":"After the names land, every parameter name an item model publishes MUST be one `ParameterName` member that the publishers name, every text, order, kind and default unchanged, and `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` MUST hold the four light-source axes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every published parameter name is one ParameterName member`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.every published parameter name is one ParameterName member","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.azimuth","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.degreeOfPolarization","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.intensityScale","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.dialZero","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.muellerElement","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.filmThickness","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.repeatedLayerThickness","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.substrateThickness","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.ParameterName.inComponent","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-NAMES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number":245,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S81b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[244],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests"],"how_to":"The home of the one item-model evaluator, and the values it reads (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator, ItemModel × parameters × orientation × λ → MuellerMatrix'; 001 §I: `Parameter` = a name plus a `ParameterState`; step 214: 'a kind's range is its model's (S8.1)'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs`: `module ItemEvaluation` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `MuellerInverse.fs`, the last Domain file, because the evaluator calls `MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:retarderMueller`) and `MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward` (`MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward`): one `<Compile Include=\"ItemEvaluation.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the item-model evaluator, model × parameters × orientation × λ (spec 0050 S8.1). It opens `ItemModels` and `Kit`; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (2) `ItemEvaluationError`, an `*Error` union whose cases are `MissingParameterValueErr of reason : string` (the values hold no number for a parameter the model publishes, naming it) and `ParameterOutOfRangeErr of reason : string` (a value outside its kind's range, naming the parameter, the value and the range). `member this.describe : string` renders them `the values hold no number for the parameter: <reason>` and `the parameter value is outside its range: <reason>`. Later steps add their own cases with their renderings. (3) `ParameterValues` = `ParameterValues of Map<ParameterName, ParameterValue>`, the numbers an evaluation reads, by name. `static member ofParameters (parameters : Parameter list) : ParameterValues` takes each parameter's number from its state (step 214): a `KnownParameter` its value, an `UnknownParameter` its `start`, a `CalibratedParameter` its `value`. `static member defaultsOf (axes : ItemParameterAxis list) : ParameterValues` holds each axis's `defaultValue`. `member this.withValue (name : ParameterName) (value : ParameterValue) : ParameterValues` replaces or adds one number. `member this.valueOf (name : ParameterName) : Result<ParameterValue, ItemEvaluationError>` answers it or `MissingParameterValueErr`. `member this.checkedFor (axes : ItemParameterAxis list) : Result<ParameterValues, ItemEvaluationError>` answers the values when every axis has a number within its kind's range and otherwise the first failure in axis order: no number is `MissingParameterValueErr`; a number that is NaN or infinite, a `FractionParameter` outside [0, 1], or a `ScaleParameter` or `ThicknessParameter` below 0 is `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`; an `AngleParameter`, `PhaseParameter`, `MuellerElementParameter` or `ReadingParameter` takes any finite number. Values the axes do not name are kept and ignored. No cache, unit conversion or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs`, `module ItemEvaluationTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation`. `parameter values are read from an item's parameter states`: over parameters `a` `KnownParameter 0.1`, `b` an `UnknownParameter` starting at 0.5 within [0, 1] and `c` a `CalibratedParameter` of 0.25 (sigma 0.01, `FitRunName \"S@20261101T120000Z\"`), `valueOf` answers 0.1, 0.5 and 0.25, and `valueOf` of `d` answers `MissingParameterValueErr` naming `d`. `defaults come from a model's axes and one value can be replaced`: `defaultsOf` of `(OpticalElementModel (RetarderPlateModel ConstantRetardance)).parameterAxes` answers `retardance` π / 2 and `fastAxisOffset` 0, and `withValue ParameterName.retardance` of π / 4 answers π / 4 beside the unchanged offset. `values are checked against a model's axes and their kinds' ranges`: over `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` (step 244), the defaults check; `degreeOfPolarization` 1.5 and −0.1, `intensityScale` −1 and an `azimuth` of NaN answer `ParameterOutOfRangeErr` naming the parameter; an `azimuth` of 7 (radians) checks; values without `ellipticity` answer `MissingParameterValueErr` naming it; and over `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId).parameterAxes` a `substrate.thickness` of −1e-3 answers `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct reason renders its text with the reason.","acceptance":"After `ItemEvaluation.fs` lands, `ParameterValues` MUST read an item's numbers from its parameter states or a model's defaults and `checkedFor` MUST refuse a missing number or one outside its kind's range with a typed `ItemEvaluationError`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `parameter values are read from an item's parameter states`, `defaults come from a model's axes and one value can be replaced`, `values are checked against a model's axes and their kinds' ranges` and `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.parameter values are read from an item's parameter states","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.defaults come from a model's axes and one value can be replaced","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.values are checked against a model's axes and their kinds' ranges","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemEvaluationError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValues","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValues.ofParameters","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValues.defaultsOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValues.checkedFor","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-PARAMETER-VALUES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number":246,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S81c","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[245],"how_to":"The source is real: a light source with a Stokes state and an intensity scale (001 §N 'The source is real: a source item with a Stokes state and an intensity scale'; 001 §I 'Light source | λ or tunable limits (exists) + output polarization (azimuth, ellipticity, degree of polarization) + an intensity scale'; the S8.1 brief: 'The source emits its own Stokes state x intensity scale'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, which opens `ItemModels`, gains before `RunStep`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: `SourceEmission = { azimuth : Angle; ellipticity : Angle; degreeOfPolarization : ParameterValue; intensityScale : ParameterValue }`, the light a source emits. `member this.stokes : StokesVector` is I · [1, p·cos 2χ·cos 2ψ, p·cos 2χ·sin 2ψ, p·sin 2χ] with ψ the azimuth, χ the ellipticity angle, p the degree of polarization and I the intensity scale, written through `StokesVector.create` as `Propagation.inputStokes` writes its vectors (`Propagation.fs:inputStokes`); a positive χ is +S₃, the handedness `inputStokes` calls left, so a fully polarized source at azimuth θ and χ = 0 is `inputStokes IdealLinear θ` and one at χ = 45° is `inputStokes IdealCircularLeft`. The run law is unchanged in this step; step 252 makes it start from the emission. (2) `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: `type ParameterValue with member this.angle : Angle`, the number read as radians (an `AngleParameter`'s unit, step 207). `type SourceEmission with static member ofValues (values : ParameterValues) : Result<SourceEmission, ItemEvaluationError>` checks the values against `SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes` (step 244, `checkedFor`, step 245) and reads the four through the `ParameterName` members, the two angles through `angle`. `ItemEvaluationError` gains `NotALightSourceErr of reason : string`, rendered `the model is not a light source: <reason>`. `type ItemModelChoice with member this.emissionWith (values : ParameterValues) : Result<SourceEmission, ItemEvaluationError>` is `SourceEmission.ofValues values` for a `SourcePresetChoice` (step 216) and `NotALightSourceErr` naming the model's kind for every other choice: the source arm of the one evaluator, which S8.2's source slot and S11.2's forward model call with the source item's values. The wavelength stays the preset's, as today. No other member is added. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`: `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale`: `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)` answers azimuth and ellipticity 0, degree of polarization 0 and scale 1, whose `stokes` is exactly [1, 0, 0, 0] (`Propagation.unpolarizedStokes`). `a source emits its polarization state times its intensity scale`: a degree of polarization 1 at azimuth 30° with scale 2 emits 2 · `inputStokes IdealLinear (30°)`; ellipticity 45° emits `inputStokes IdealCircularLeft (0°)` and −45° `inputStokes IdealCircularRight (0°)`; a degree of polarization 0.5 at azimuth 0 emits [1, 0.5, 0, 0]; each component within 1e-15. `only a light-source model emits, and its values must be in range`: `(PolarizerPresetChoice (the PresetIds.polarizerLp polarizer)).emissionWith` of any values answers `NotALightSourceErr`; `(SourcePresetChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633)).emissionWith` answers the default emission over the defaults, `ParameterOutOfRangeErr` with a degree of polarization of 2, and `MissingParameterValueErr` without `ellipticity`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` (step 245) covers `NotALightSourceErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Verification (claim-check repair, .spec-md §9): ui-tests MUST select OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests (Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:FsxAcceptanceTests) to preserve the constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples. The constructor-unit-tests behavior checks above remain required; this selection neither edits that class nor substitutes for the future kit-acceptance tests.","acceptance":"After the real source lands, `SourceEmission.stokes` MUST be the source's polarization state times its intensity scale, the default parameter set MUST emit unpolarized light of unit S₀, and only a light-source model MUST emit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale`, `a source emits its polarization state times its intensity scale`, `only a light-source model emits, and its values must be in range` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass. ui-tests MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests, preserving its constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples and its test count.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-tests":{"suite":"ui-tests","mode":"selected","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a source emits its polarization state times its intensity scale","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.only a light-source model emits, and its values must be in range","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.SourceEmission","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.SourceEmission.stokes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SourceEmission.ofValues","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemModelChoice.emissionWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValue.angle","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemEvaluationError.NotALightSourceErr","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-SOURCE-EMISSION"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number":247,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S81d","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[246],"how_to":"An optical element with its parameters bound, evaluated at an orientation and a wavelength: the element arm of the one evaluator (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; the S8.1 brief: 'Polarizer presets go through Propagation.behaviorMueller'; 001 §I 'Empty slot (air) | Identity, the calibration reference'). In `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (1) `ElementOrientation = { rotation : Angle; incidence : IncidenceAngle; branch : Propagation.Branch }`: the element's rotation about the beam (its R1, a sample's spin), the incidence the beam meets its drawn face at, and the branch the light leaves it by (`Propagation.fs:Branch`). `static member transmittingAt (rotation : Angle) : ElementOrientation` is that rotation at `IncidenceAngle.normal` on `BranchTransmitted`, an element on the beam that transmits. (2) `BoundOpticalElement` = `BoundPolarizerPreset of PolarizerBehavior` (a preset, which publishes no parameter, step 207) | `BoundEmptySlot`: what an element evaluates from; steps 248, 249 and 250 add the optical forms, the stack samples and the cut plates. (3) `member this.muellerAt (orientation : ElementOrientation) (w : WaveLength) : Result<MuellerMatrix, ItemEvaluationError>`: `BoundPolarizerPreset b` is `Propagation.behaviorMueller b orientation.rotation` (`Propagation.fs:behaviorMueller`), exactly the matrix the run law takes today; `BoundEmptySlot` is `Propagation.identityMueller`. Both act on the light they pass and ignore the incidence: a polarizer is T-only (AGENTS.md 'lenses AND polarizers are T-only'), so `BranchReflected` answers the new `UnmodelledBranchErr of reason : string`, rendered `the element has no such branch: <reason>`, naming the element's kind. No cache, option or other member is added. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`: `a polarizer preset is its behaviour's Mueller matrix at the element's rotation`: for `ComputedIdeal IdealLinear`, `IdealCircularLeft` and `IdealCircularRight`, and for a `ConstantMueller` of two reference ideal LPs at offsets 20° and 65°, at 0°, 30°, 45°, 90°, 135° and 330°, `muellerAt (ElementOrientation.transmittingAt θ)` at 600 nm equals `Propagation.behaviorMueller b θ` element by element exactly (`MuellerMatrix.element`). `an empty slot is the identity, and an element that only transmits has no reflected branch`: `BoundEmptySlot` at 30° and 400 nm is `Propagation.identityMueller`, and both cases on `BranchReflected` answer `UnmodelledBranchErr`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` covers `UnmodelledBranchErr`.","acceptance":"After the bound elements land, a polarizer preset MUST evaluate to `Propagation.behaviorMueller` at its rotation, an empty slot to the identity, and either on a reflected branch to `UnmodelledBranchErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a polarizer preset is its behaviour's Mueller matrix at the element's rotation`, `an empty slot is the identity, and an element that only transmits has no reflected branch` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a polarizer preset is its behaviour's Mueller matrix at the element's rotation","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-BOUND-ELEMENT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.an empty slot is the identity, and an element that only transmits has no reflected branch","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-BOUND-ELEMENT"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","obligations":["S81-BOUND-ELEMENT"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ElementOrientation","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-BOUND-ELEMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.BoundOpticalElement","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-BOUND-ELEMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.BoundOpticalElement.muellerAt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-BOUND-ELEMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemEvaluationError.UnmodelledBranchErr","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-BOUND-ELEMENT"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number":248,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S81e","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[247],"how_to":"The parameterised optical forms of step 208 evaluated through the Stokes–Mueller algebra (001 §N 'black-box and compound items go through the Stokes/Mueller algebra'; 001 §I: real LP, retarder plate, black box 'at reference orientation; rotation as R(−φ) M R(φ)', compound in light order; the S8.1 brief: REUSING `MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller` and the existing rotation helpers). In `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (1) `BoundOpticalElement` gains `BoundOpticalForm of form : OpticalForm * values : ParameterValues`, and `static member ofOpticalForm (values : ParameterValues) (form : OpticalForm) : Result<BoundOpticalElement, ItemEvaluationError>` binds the form after `values.checkedFor form.parameterAxes` (step 245). (2) `type ParameterValues with member this.forComponent (position : int) (axes : ItemParameterAxis list) : Result<ParameterValues, ItemEvaluationError>`: the values of a compound's component, each of `axes` read under its `inComponent position` name (step 244) and held under its own name. `type ParameterValue with member this.retardanceAt (dispersion : RetardanceDispersion) (w : WaveLength) : MuellerReconstruction.Retardance`: the number as radians under `ConstantRetardance`, and scaled by λ_ref / λ under `InverseWaveLengthRetardance λ_ref` (step 208). (3) `muellerAt` on `BoundOpticalForm (form, values)` evaluates the form at `orientation.rotation` (θ) and `w`, its values read through the `ParameterName` members: `RealPolarizerModel leakage` takes the minor transmittance r (`extinctionRatio` under `ExtinctionRatioLeakage`; (1 − D) / (1 + D) of the `diattenuation` D under `DiattenuationLeakage`) and the major transmittance 1, the linear diattenuator ½·[[1 + r, 1 − r, 0, 0], [1 − r, 1 + r, 0, 0], [0, 0, 2√r, 0], [0, 0, 0, 2√r]] written through `RealMatrix4x4.create` as `Propagation.analyzerMueller` writes its matrices, turned by `Propagation.rotateMueller (θ + axisOffset)` (`Propagation.fs:rotateMueller`), so its defaults are the ideal linear polarizer; `RetarderPlateModel dispersion` is `MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller (θ + fastAxisOffset) (retardance.retardanceAt dispersion w)`; `BlackBoxMuellerModel` builds M from `muellerElement row column` (step 244), every element under `SixteenElementMueller` and, under `FifteenElementsAndScale`, `blackBoxScale` times the matrix whose (0, 0) is 1 and whose other fifteen are the values, then turns it by `Propagation.rotateMueller θ` (R(−θ)·M·R(θ)); `CompoundModel components` evaluates component k (1-based, light order) at rotation 0 from `values.forComponent k component.form.parameterAxes`, keeps it as `{ matrix = …; offset = component.offset }` (`ElementId.fs:MuellerComponent`) and answers `Propagation.rotateMueller θ (Propagation.compoundMueller components)` (`Propagation.fs:compoundMueller`), the arm `behaviorMueller` takes for a `ConstantMueller`, so a compound inside a compound recurses. A form passes the light it transmits: `BranchReflected` is `UnmodelledBranchErr` (step 247), and the incidence is ignored. No new 4×4 algebra, cache or option is added. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`, each matrix compared element by element within 1e-12: `a real linear polarizer at its defaults is the ideal one, and its leakage passes crossed light`: a real LP under `ExtinctionRatioLeakage` at its defaults equals `Propagation.analyzerMueller IdealLinear θ` at 0°, 30° and 135°; with `axisOffset` 10° at 30° it equals the ideal LP at 40°; with `extinctionRatio` 0.01 at 0°, unpolarized light through it and an ideal LP at 90° reads S₀ = 0.005; and under `DiattenuationLeakage` a `diattenuation` of 0.98 equals the extinction-ratio form of 0.02 / 1.98. `a retarder plate is the retarder matrix at its fast axis, its retardance dispersed as its model says`: a retarder under `ConstantRetardance` with `retardance` π / 3 and `fastAxisOffset` 5° at 40° equals `MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller (45°) (Retardance (π / 3))` at any λ, and under `InverseWaveLengthRetardance (632.8 nm)` with `retardance` π / 2 evaluated at 316.4 nm equals the half-wave `retarderMueller (θ) (Retardance π)`. `a black-box Mueller matrix is held at reference orientation and turned by the element's rotation`: under `SixteenElementMueller` at its defaults the box is the identity at 30°; holding the sixteen elements of `Propagation.analyzerMueller IdealLinear (0°)` it equals the ideal LP at θ for 0°, 30° and 135°; and under `FifteenElementsAndScale` a `scale` of 0.8 over the fifteen normalised elements of that LP equals 0.8 · 2 · the LP (its m00 is ½). `a compound applies its components in light order, each under its own prefixed parameters`: the compound of a real LP by extinction ratio at offset 0° then a retarder at offset 45°, at its defaults (a quarter wave), equals `retarderMueller (θ + 45°) (π / 2) · analyzerMueller IdealLinear θ` at 0° and 30° and turns unpolarized light circular (|S₃| / S₀ = 1); and that compound as the second component after a black box at its identity defaults, with `c2.c1.extinctionRatio` 0.01, equals at 0° the inner compound alone with `c1.extinctionRatio` 0.01. `a form is bound only with a value for each of its parameters, in range`: binding a real LP without `axisOffset` answers `MissingParameterValueErr`, with `extinctionRatio` 1.2 `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`, and a retarder on `BranchReflected` `UnmodelledBranchErr`.","acceptance":"After the forms land, a real linear polarizer, a retarder plate, a black-box Mueller matrix and a compound MUST evaluate through the Stokes–Mueller algebra at the element's rotation, reusing `retarderMueller`, `rotateMueller` and `compoundMueller`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a real linear polarizer at its defaults is the ideal one, and its leakage passes crossed light`, `a retarder plate is the retarder matrix at its fast axis, its retardance dispersed as its model says`, `a black-box Mueller matrix is held at reference orientation and turned by the element's rotation`, `a compound applies its components in light order, each under its own prefixed parameters` and `a form is bound only with a value for each of its parameters, in range`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a real linear polarizer at its defaults is the ideal one, and its leakage passes crossed light","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a retarder plate is the retarder matrix at its fast axis, its retardance dispersed as its model says","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a black-box Mueller matrix is held at reference orientation and turned by the element's rotation","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a compound applies its components in light order, each under its own prefixed parameters","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a form is bound only with a value for each of its parameters, in range","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.BoundOpticalElement.BoundOpticalForm","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValues.forComponent","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValue.retardanceAt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-OPTICAL-FORMS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number":249,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S81f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[248],"how_to":"A stack sample evaluated through Berreman, as the table solves it (001 §N 'stack samples go through Berreman (Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun for the table …) — REUSED'; 001 §I 'Sample by stack | the existing Sample …; unknowns may be a thickness'). Its thickness parameters (step 207) are applied to the stack and its materials are resolved once, when it is bound, so a sweep re-solves without re-resolving, as the host does today (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`). In `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (1) `type ParameterValue with member this.thickness : Thickness`, the number read as metres, a `ThicknessParameter`'s unit (step 207's `Thickness.parameterValueOpt` is the other way). (2) `type Sample with member this.withThicknessValues (values : ParameterValues) : Result<Sample, ItemEvaluationError>`: after `values.checkedFor this.parameterAxes`, the sample with each finite layer's thickness replaced, every other field kept: the `SingleLayer` at film position k reads `ParameterName.filmThickness k`; layer j of the `Repeated` group at position k reads `repeatedLayerThickness k j`, the cell being stored once and shared by every period; the substrate plate reads `substrateThickness`; a `Thickness.Infinity` layer publishes nothing and is kept. (3) `ItemEvaluationError` gains `SampleMaterialErr of error : MaterialError` (a typed state, the store's own error), rendered `the sample's materials do not resolve: <the material error's reason>`. `BoundOpticalElement` gains `BoundStackSample of Propagation.ResolvedSample`, and `static member ofStackSample (materials : MaterialProxy) (values : ParameterValues) (sample : Sample) : Result<BoundOpticalElement, ItemEvaluationError>` is `withThicknessValues`, then `Propagation.resolveSampleMaterials materials` (`Propagation.fs:resolveSampleMaterials`), its `MaterialError` answered as `SampleMaterialErr`. (4) `muellerAt` on `BoundStackSample resolved` is `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun orientation.branch resolved w orientation.incidence orientation.rotation` (`Propagation.fs:sampleMuellerSpun`), both branches, the rotation being the sample's spin. No cache, catch or option is added; the solve is called as the host calls it today. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`, with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])` (steps 45, 65): `a stack sample at its own thicknesses is solved as the table solves it`: for `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and `SampleIds.glassFilm200Id`, `ofStackSample` over `ParameterValues.defaultsOf sample.parameterAxes` evaluated at spin 20°, incidence 30° and 600 nm equals `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` of `resolveSampleMaterials` of the catalogue sample on both branches, element by element exactly. `a stack sample's thickness parameters change the layers they name`: on a test-local structure of a 5 nm `SingleLayer`, a `Repeated` group of a 10 nm and a 20 nm cell over three periods and a 1 mm substrate plate, `withThicknessValues` with `film1.thickness` 6 nm, `film2.layer2.thickness` 25 nm and `substrate.thickness` 2 mm answers those three thicknesses, the 10 nm cell layer and every material kept, its `expandedFilms` holding 25 nm in each of the three periods; a `film1.thickness` of −1 nm answers `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`; and `glassFilm200` bound with `film1.thickness` 300 nm evaluates, at normal incidence and 600 nm on `BranchTransmitted`, to `sampleMuellerSpun` of the resolved sample whose film is 300 nm, within 1e-12. `a sample whose material does not resolve answers SampleMaterialErr`: `ofStackSample` of `glassPlate1mm` over an empty in-memory material store (`MaterialStore.fs:MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty`) answers `SampleMaterialErr` of an `UnknownMaterialIdErr`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` covers `SampleMaterialErr`.","acceptance":"After the stack samples land, a sample bound at its own thicknesses MUST evaluate exactly as `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` solves it on both branches, its thickness parameters MUST change the layers they name, and an unresolved material MUST be `SampleMaterialErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a stack sample at its own thicknesses is solved as the table solves it`, `a stack sample's thickness parameters change the layers they name`, `a sample whose material does not resolve answers SampleMaterialErr` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a stack sample at its own thicknesses is solved as the table solves it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a stack sample's thickness parameters change the layers they name","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a sample whose material does not resolve answers SampleMaterialErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.Sample.withThicknessValues","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ParameterValue.thickness","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.BoundOpticalElement.BoundStackSample","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemEvaluationError.SampleMaterialErr","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-STACK-SAMPLES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number": 250, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S81g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [249], "how_to": "A crystal plate cut along a crystal axis, evaluated through the spec 0044 Berreman forward (001 §N '`MuellerInverse.orientForCut` + `createBerremanForward` for cut plates — REUSED'; .spec-md §3.16: the study engine evaluates the crystal-parameter records, S11). In `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] CutPlate = { cut : MuellerInverse.SampleCut; thickness : Thickness; predict : MuellerInverse.MeasurementConfiguration -> Result<MuellerMatrix, MuellerInverse.ForwardModelError> }`: a free-standing plate of a crystal whose parameters are already chosen. `static member ofForward (forward : MuellerInverse.ForwardModelProxy<'Parameters>) (parameters : 'Parameters) (cut : MuellerInverse.SampleCut) (thickness : Thickness) : CutPlate` holds `forward.muellerOf` applied to the parameters, so the forward of `MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward` (`MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward`, which orients through `orientForCut`) is called and nothing of it is copied. (2) On `ElementOrientation` (step 247): `member this.sampleAzimuth : MuellerInverse.SampleAzimuth`, the rotation as the plate's azimuth about its normal, and `member this.observable : MuellerInverse.Observable`, `TransmittedMueller` on `BranchTransmitted` and `ReflectedMueller` on `BranchReflected` (`MuellerInverse.fs:Observable`). (3) `BoundOpticalElement` gains `BoundCutPlate of CutPlate`; `muellerAt` predicts `{ cut; thickness; incidenceAngle = orientation.incidence; azimuth = orientation.sampleAzimuth; observable = orientation.observable; waveLength = w }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:MeasurementConfiguration`), and `ForwardSolveFailedErr` answers the new `CutPlateSolveErr of reason : string` carrying its reason, rendered `the cut plate's Berreman solve failed: <reason>`. No crystal-parameter material, builder or option is added here: S10.1 promotes the builders and S11.1 the material form. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`, over `createBerremanForward` of a test-local builder mapping `MuellerInverse.UniaxialParameters` (n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, zero gyration) to `OpticalProperties.fromRefractionIndex (n_o, n_o, n_e)` (`MaterialProperties.fs:OpticalProperties`), with `SolverParameters.defaultValue`: `a cut plate is predicted through the Berreman forward at the element's spin, incidence, branch and wavelength`: an `XCut` 1 mm plate at rotation 30°, incidence 20° and 600 nm equals, element by element exactly, the forward's `muellerOf` of the configuration with `SampleAzimuth.degree 30.0<deg>`, that incidence, that wavelength and `TransmittedMueller`, and on `BranchReflected` the one with `ReflectedMueller`; turning the rotation to 60° changes the transmitted matrix. `a cut plate whose forward fails answers CutPlateSolveErr`: a test-local `ForwardModelProxy` answering `ForwardSolveFailedErr (configuration, \"degenerate\")` makes `muellerAt` answer `CutPlateSolveErr` naming `degenerate`. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` covers `CutPlateSolveErr`.", "acceptance": "After the cut plates land, a `CutPlate` MUST be predicted through the spec 0044 Berreman forward at the element's rotation as the plate's azimuth, its incidence, its branch as the observable and the wavelength, and a failing forward MUST be `CutPlateSolveErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a cut plate is predicted through the Berreman forward at the element's spin, incidence, branch and wavelength`, `a cut plate whose forward fails answers CutPlateSolveErr` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a cut plate is predicted through the Berreman forward at the element's spin, incidence, branch and wavelength", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a cut plate whose forward fails answers CutPlateSolveErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.CutPlate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.CutPlate.ofForward", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.BoundOpticalElement.BoundCutPlate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ElementOrientation.sampleAzimuth", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemEvaluationError.CutPlateSolveErr", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CUT-PLATES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number":251,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S81h","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[250],"how_to":"One entry from an item's model to its bound element, the door S8.2's slots and S11.2's forward model call (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator, ItemModel × parameters × orientation × λ → MuellerMatrix'; .spec-md §3.14: an item instantiates a model, the presets and the stack `Sample` being models themselves). In `ItemEvaluation.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1: `ItemEvaluationError` gains `NotAnOpticalElementErr of reason : string`, rendered `the model is not an optical element: <reason>`. `type ItemModelChoice with member this.boundWith (materials : MaterialProxy) (values : ParameterValues) : Result<BoundOpticalElement, ItemEvaluationError>` over step 216's choices: `PolarizerPresetChoice (polarizerModel, p)` is `BoundPolarizerPreset p.behavior`; `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, _, sample)` is `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample materials values sample` (step 249); `LibraryModelChoice v` matches `v.entry.model` (step 208): `OpticalElementModel form` is `BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm values form` (step 248) and `EmptySlotModel` is `BoundEmptySlot`; `IntensityDetectorModel`, `MuellerPolarimeterModel` and `EllipsometerModel` answer `NotAnOpticalElementErr` naming the model, because a detector reads and its gain, dark offset and noise belong to S11.2's forward model; `SourcePresetChoice` answers `NotAnOpticalElementErr` too, a source emitting through `emissionWith` (step 246). No wildcard arm is written, so a later `ItemModelForm` case is a compile error here. No other member is added. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests`, with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])`: `every item model binds as its kind, and a source or a detector is no optical element`: the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer binds to its `BoundPolarizerPreset`; `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1 evaluates as `ofStackSample` of that sample; the item models of `ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId` and `ItemModelIds.emptySlotModelId` (`BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel`, step 210) over their defaults evaluate as `ofOpticalForm` of their forms and as the identity; and `ItemModelIds.intensityDetectorModelId`, `muellerPolarimeterModelId`, `ellipsometerModelId` and a `SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.heNe633` answer `NotAnOpticalElementErr`. `an item's own parameter values reach its Mueller matrix`: a CPL1 item made by step 216's `ItemDraft` over `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId)` and `FixedMounting`, with `c2.retardance` set by `withParameterState` (step 234) to `KnownParameter` π / 4, bound over `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters`, evaluates at 0° to `retarderMueller (45°) (π / 4) · analyzerMueller IdealLinear (0°)` within 1e-12, and its defaults to the quarter-wave product. `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload` covers `NotAnOpticalElementErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. LibraryModelChoice of SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel or StackSampleItemModel MUST return the typed missing-binding error. Their valid bound choice cases MUST continue calling the same source, polarizer and sample evaluators; no second physics implementation is allowed.","acceptance":"After the entry lands, `ItemModelChoice.boundWith` MUST bind every optical model as its kind and answer `NotAnOpticalElementErr` for a detector or a source, and an item's own parameter values MUST reach its Mueller matrix; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every item model binds as its kind, and a source or a detector is no optical element`, `an item's own parameter values reach its Mueller matrix` and the widened `every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.every item model binds as its kind, and a source or a detector is no optical element","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-MODEL-BINDING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.an item's own parameter values reach its Mueller matrix","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S81-MODEL-BINDING"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.every evaluation error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","obligations":["S81-MODEL-BINDING"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemModelChoice.boundWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-MODEL-BINDING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.ItemEvaluationError.NotAnOpticalElementErr","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S81-MODEL-BINDING"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number": 252, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S81i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [251], "how_to": "The run law walks every element of the light path, in light order, through its Mueller matrix, and starts from a real source whose default parameter set reproduces today's charts (001 §N 'The run law walks any number of objects. ExperimentRun folds slot by slot, in light order, through each item's Mueller matrix'; 'The source is real … \"Unpolarized, unit scale after the first polarizer\" is its default parameter set, so existing charts keep their values'; 001 §R: the 'first polarizer sets unit intensity' special case is removed; the S8.1 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, its module doc rewritten in one to three lines citing spec 0046 and spec 0050 S8.1, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (a) `RunStep` = `ElementStep of mueller : MuellerMatrix` (an element that is not an object, already evaluated at its orientation: a polarizer today, any prep or analyzer item from S8.2) | `ObjectStep of mueller : MuellerMatrix` (an object, already solved for the branch the detector's path leaves it by), with `member this.mueller : MuellerMatrix`. `PolarizerStep` and `SampleStep` are deleted, and a run holds any number of objects. (b) On `SourceEmission` (step 246): `member this.emittedInto (steps : RunStep list) : StokesVector` is `this.stokes` times the path's intensity reference r. For the first `ElementStep` in front of the first `ObjectStep` (the first element of a path with no object), r is the inverse of the S₀ its matrix passes of `Propagation.unpolarizedStokes`, when that S₀ is above zero; otherwise r is 1. So the intensity scale is referenced after the first polarizer, 001 §N's default: unpolarized light of unit scale leaves an ideal polarizer at unit S₀ exactly as `Propagation.inputStokes` gave it (an ideal matrix passes ½, so r is 2 and every product is exact), and a path with no element in front of its first object starts from the source's own state. (c) `detectorStokes (emission : SourceEmission) (steps : RunStep list) : StokesVector` folds `step.mueller * sv` over the steps from `emission.emittedInto steps`, and `read (kind : DetectorKind) (emission : SourceEmission) (steps : RunStep list) : Reading` reads it as today. The fold's `(StokesVector * bool * bool)` state and its first-polarizer arm (`ExperimentRun.fs:detectorStokes`) are deleted. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Propagation.fs`: `behaviorInputStokes` (`Propagation.fs:behaviorInputStokes`) is deleted with its doc, its last consumers going in this step; `inputStokes` and `unpolarizedStokes` stay, because `PropagationTests` builds its inputs from them. `DetectorIntensity`'s doc says the intensity is relative to the source's intensity reference (spec 0050 S8.1). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs` the `PolarizerBehavior` doc says `ComputedIdeal` evaluates through `Propagation.analyzerMueller`, no longer naming `inputStokes`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `model.runInputStokes` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:runInputStokes`), which nothing reads, is deleted. (b) `chartForRun` builds every step through the evaluator (steps 247 and 249). A polarizer element bound to a preset is `BoundPolarizerPreset p.behavior`, evaluated per point at `{ rotation = its R1, or the swept x when its R1 is varied; incidence = IncidenceAngle.normal; branch = the path step's branch }`, as an `ElementStep`. A sample element bound to a library sample is bound once per path step by `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample model.materials (ParameterValues.defaultsOf sample.parameterAxes) sample`, so its materials are resolved once as today, and evaluated per point at `{ rotation = its spin (R1, or the swept x); incidence = its drawn incidence, or the swept x under VaryR2; branch = the path step's branch }` and the point's wavelength, as an `ObjectStep`. Every sample on the detector's `BeamLayout` path is solved, each for its own branch, as today. `StepBuilder`'s swept arm answers `Result<RunStep, ItemEvaluationError>`. (c) Every chart reads with `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)` (step 244), the default parameter set, whatever source preset is bound, because a preset carries no parameter values; S8.2's source slot gives a source item's own values through `emissionWith` (step 246). (d) A `SampleMaterialErr e` keeps today's failure chart, title `Sample materials failed to resolve` and description `e.runFailureCaption` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:runFailureCaption`); any other evaluation error, which the host's own inputs never raise, shows the title `The run cannot be evaluated` and its `describe`. (e) The docs of `chartForRun` and of the run section's header say what the law now is, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (4) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'An experiment runs on the light's real path': its clause 'polarizers before the sample prepare the input (the first sets a unit-intensity state), the sample acts at its drawn incidence and spin (its R1), polarizers after it analyze' becomes: every element on the path acts in light order through its Mueller matrix from `ItemEvaluation` (a polarizer at its R1, every sample at its drawn incidence and spin for the branch the path leaves it by), and the source emits its own Stokes state times its intensity scale, by default unpolarized with the unit scale after the first polarizer. Nothing else in the file changes. Every chart's numbers are unchanged, so `FsxAcceptanceTests` and the chart classes run as they are. Tests. `ExperimentRunTests`: its `lp` helper becomes `ElementStep (Propagation.analyzerMueller IdealLinear θ)`, `clear` becomes `ObjectStep Propagation.identityMueller`, and every fact reads through a file-local default emission (`SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)`). `the source's light is unpolarized; the first polarizer sets a unit-intensity polarized input` becomes `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale, referenced after the first polarizer`, its assertions kept; `a polarizer AFTER the sample analyzes: crossed polarizers around a clear sample pass nothing` and `an ellipsometer reads Psi and Delta of the arriving state` keep their numbers over the new steps. New: `the default source reproduces the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case`: for each ideal kind at 0°, 15°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°, 120°, 135°, 180°, 225°, 270°, 315° and 330°, the paths [prep], [prep; clear], [prep; clear; ideal LP at 60°], [prep; ideal LP at 90°], [clear; ideal LP at 60°] and [] read exactly the old rule's value written through the kept primitives (`inputStokes kind θ` with a prep and `unpolarizedStokes` without, then each later matrix), every component equal, because the products are exact. `objects in series apply their matrices in light order`: with a prep LP at 0°, the objects `MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller (30°) (Retardance (π / 2))` then `retarderMueller (75°) (Retardance (π / 3))` and an analyzer LP at 45°, `detectorStokes` equals A · M₂ · M₁ · `inputStokes IdealLinear (0°)` within 1e-12, and swapping the two objects changes S₀ by more than 1e-3. `a real source emits its own state times its scale`: a source of degree of polarization 1 at azimuth 30° and scale 2 reads 2 · [1, cos 60°, sin 60°, 0] through no element, and S₀ = 4 through an ideal LP at 30°, the reference being that first polarizer's unpolarized throughput (r = 2). `a constant-compound first polarizer passes unit intensity like any other` : `ElementStep (Propagation.behaviorMueller (ConstantMueller [ { matrix = analyzerMueller IdealLinear (0°); offset = 0° } ]) (30°))` with the default source reads [1, cos 60°, sin 60°, 0] within 1e-12. `PolarizerBehaviorTests`: `behaviorInputStokes of a ComputedIdeal equals inputStokes across kinds and orientations` is deleted, its parity being `the default source reproduces the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case`'s, and `behaviorInputStokes applies a constant compound to unpolarized light un-normalized` is deleted, `a constant-compound first polarizer passes unit intensity like any other` pinning the new rule; every other fact is unchanged. `ExperimentControlsTests` (UI): `two bound samples in series are both solved on the detector's path`: over `initMain ()`, two samples added and bound through the file's `bind` helper to `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and `SampleIds.glassFilm200Id`, untilted on the main beam in front of the seeded intensity detector; the film chosen with `VaryR2` over 0 … 60° in 7 points and capture T: the series' value at each x equals the S₀ of the two transmitted `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` matrices (the plate at normal incidence, the film at x, spin 0, 600 nm, each resolved through the model's `materials`) applied to `unpolarizedStokes` in the order the detector's `BeamLayout` path lists them, within 1e-12.", "acceptance": "After the run law lands, `ExperimentRun` MUST fold every step of the path through its Mueller matrix from the source's emission, with no first-polarizer arm, the default source MUST reproduce every existing reading exactly, and the host MUST build its steps through the item evaluator; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale, referenced after the first polarizer`, `the default source reproduces the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case`, `objects in series apply their matrices in light order`, `a real source emits its own state times its scale` and `a constant-compound first polarizer passes unit intensity like any other`, the count rising by 2 (four new facts, two `behaviorInputStokes` facts deleted); ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `two bound samples in series are both solved on the detector's path`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Propagation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.the source's light is unpolarized; the first polarizer sets a unit-intensity polarized input", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.the default source is unpolarized light at unit scale, referenced after the first polarizer", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.a polarizer AFTER the sample analyzes: crossed polarizers around a clear sample pass nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.an ellipsometer reads Psi and Delta of the arriving state", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.the default source reproduces the old unit-intensity rule on every existing case", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.objects in series apply their matrices in light order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.a real source emits its own state times its scale", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.a constant-compound first polarizer passes unit intensity like any other", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PolarizerBehaviorTests.behaviorInputStokes of a ComputedIdeal equals inputStokes across kinds and orientations", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PolarizerBehaviorTests.behaviorInputStokes applies a constant compound to unpolarized light un-normalized", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.two bound samples in series are both solved on the detector's path", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.RunStep", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.detectorStokes", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.read", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.SourceEmission.emittedInto", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Propagation.behaviorInputStokes", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"], "preserves_obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.runInputStokes", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"], "preserves_obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S81-RUN-LAW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number": 253, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S81j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [252], "how_to": "Capture branches are decided per object, as one pure Domain rule over the beam layout (001 §N '`measuredElementOf` (\"the first bound sample\") is deleted, and capture branches are decided per object'; the S8.1 brief: 'Any number of samples (objects) sit in series, and each decides its own capture branch (T / R) for the path the detector is on'; AGENTS.md: logic lives in Domain and is tested there). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs`, after `detectedBranches` (`BeamLayout.fs:detectedBranches`), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (1) `DetectorCapture = { detector : Library.ElementId; branch : BeamTree.BeamBranch }`: one detector an experiment captures, and the branch it captures. (2) `detectorCaptures (scene : SceneLayout) (detectors : Library.ElementId list) (varied : Library.ElementId) (objects : Library.ElementId list) : DetectorCapture list`: in scene order, every LIT detector of `detectors` whose path holds the varied element (the filter `detectedBranches` applies today) captures the branch by which its path leaves the LAST of `objects` on it, the object whose light it receives, each object being solved for its own branch (step 252); a detector whose path holds no object captures `TransmittedBeam` when its path leaves the varied element by the transmitted branch, and nothing otherwise, because a run with nothing to reflect is a pass-through (the no-sample rule of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:availableCaptures`). With one object on every path this is today's rule. `detectedBranches` is unchanged in this step; step 254 re-points it and the host. No other type or function is added. Tests, in `BeamLayoutTests` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs`), over the file's `el`, `tilted`, `transmitting` and `onReflectedOf` builders and `layout`: `each detector captures the branch its light leaves the last object by`: a source, a sample `s1` tilted 30° emitting both branches, a sample `s2` behind it on the main beam tilted 30° emitting both, a detector `dT` behind `s2`, a detector `dR2` on `s2`'s reflected ray and a detector `dR1` on `s1`'s reflected ray: `detectorCaptures` for the varied `src` with objects [`s1`; `s2`] answers `dT` T, `dR2` R and `dR1` R, in scene order; with objects [`s1`] alone, `dR2` captures T, its light leaving `s1` by T. `a detector whose path holds no object captures only light the varied element transmits`: a source, a flat mirror `m` and a detector `d` behind it: with no object, the varied `src` gives `d` T, the varied `m` (which leaves its light by the reflected branch, a mirror's primary branch) gives nothing, and an unlit detector behind `d` is never captured.", "acceptance": "After the rule lands, `BeamLayout.detectorCaptures` MUST give each lit detector that sees the varied element the branch by which its light leaves the last object on its path, and with no object on the path only light the varied element transmits; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each detector captures the branch its light leaves the last object by` and `a detector whose path holds no object captures only light the varied element transmits`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests.each detector captures the branch its light leaves the last object by", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-RULE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests.a detector whose path holds no object captures only light the varied element transmits", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-RULE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.BeamLayout.DetectorCapture", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-RULE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.BeamLayout.detectorCaptures", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-RULE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number": 254, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S81k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [253], "how_to": "The host decides captures per object and `measuredElementOf` goes (001 §N '`measuredElementOf` (\"the first bound sample\") is deleted, and capture branches are decided per object'; 001 §R 'measuredElementOf … replaced by N objects'; the S8.1 brief: 'TableAndElementRotationView.fs measuredElementOf is deleted'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs`: `detectedBranches` takes `objects : Library.ElementId list` in place of `measured` and answers the distinct branches of `detectorCaptures scene detectors varied objects` (step 253), in their order, so one rule decides both; its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `measuredElementOf` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:measuredElementOf`) is deleted. (b) `member private model.objectIds : Library.ElementId list` answers the elements bound to a library sample, in scene order: the one place the host says what an object is, replacing the 'first bound sample' scans of `measuredElementOf` and `availableCaptures`. (c) `captureDetectors varied` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:captureDetectors`) answers, for each `BeamLayout.detectorCaptures model.sceneLayout detectors varied model.objectIds` entry in its order, its branch and the detector's `SceneElementIndex`, the detectors being the scene's `Detector` elements, so `chartForRun` and `captureLabel` read the per-object capture. (d) `availableCaptures model varied` is `BeamLayout.capturesFor (BeamLayout.detectedBranches model.sceneLayout detectors varied model.objectIds)`; its no-sample transmitted-only filter is deleted, being the rule's (step 253). (e) The docs of `captureDetectors` and `availableCaptures` say: a detector captures the branch by which its light leaves the last object on its path, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.1. (3) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'An experiment runs on the light's real path' (step 252): after 'for each captured branch the DETECTOR on it decides the quantity' it adds that a detector captures the branch by which its light leaves the last object on its path. Nothing else changes. After this step `git grep -n -F \"measuredElementOf\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing (S8.2's invariant). Every existing capture is unchanged: with one bound sample the last object on each path is that sample. Tests. `BeamLayoutTests`: `a detector terminates its beam: nothing behind it is lit, drawn to, or captured` and `the captures follow the detectors: T behind the element, R on its reflected ray, both when both` pass `[ Library.ElementId \"s\" ]` as the objects, their assertions unchanged. `ElementMenuTests` (UI): `a detector on the second sample's reflected ray offers R, decided by the last object on its path`: the file's `plateScene ()` with the plate's reflected ray switched off (`ToggleElementRay`), a second sample on the main beam between the plate and the seeded detector, bound through the file's `bind` helper to `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and tilted to R2 = 30° so it opens its own reflected ray, and a detector placed on that ray (`PlaceOnBeam (…, BeamLayout.OnReflectedBeamOf …)`), each by its semantic message: `availableCaptures` for the FIRST plate offers T, R and Both, where the first-bound-sample rule offered T alone; and the experiment varying the first plate's R2 over 0 … 40° in 5 points with capture Both draws `Intensity (T)` and `Intensity (R)`, whose R value at each x is the S₀ of the second plate's reflected `sampleMuellerSpun` at 30° after the first plate's transmitted one at x (spin 0, 600 nm, each resolved through the model's `materials`) applied to `unpolarizedStokes`, within 1e-9.", "acceptance": "After the host captures per object, `measuredElementOf` MUST be gone, `detectedBranches`, `captureDetectors` and `availableCaptures` MUST decide each detector's capture by the last object on its path, and every single-sample capture MUST be unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a detector on the second sample's reflected ray offers R, decided by the last object on its path`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s25 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementMenuTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests.a detector terminates its beam: nothing behind it is lit, drawn to, or captured", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests.the captures follow the detectors: T behind the element, R on its reflected ray, both when both", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests.a detector on the second sample's reflected ray offers R, decided by the last object on its path", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementMenuTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.BeamLayout.detectedBranches", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.measuredElementOf", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"], "preserves_obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.availableCaptures", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.captureDetectors", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S81-CAPTURE-HOST"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.1 -- The run law walks every object; the source is real"}
{"number":255,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S82a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[254],"how_to":"The identities a setup is stored and referenced under, and the one dial rule its slots read, as pure Domain data (001 §J 'Setup = an ordered optical path of slots …; per slot: position on the beam, R1 / R2 / R3, or a dial reading'; 001 §J 'Experiments reference setups (name + revision)'; 001 §I 'Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero and a sign (DialSign exists). Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'; .spec-md §3.11, §5 'Setup, SetupName, slots'). Nothing reads them before step 256. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs`, on `DialSign` (moved there from `MuellerReconstruction.fs` by step 205): `member this.physicalAngleOf (zero : Angle) (reading : Angle) : Angle` is `Angle (this.value * (reading.value - zero.value))`, the rule `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:physicalAngle`) holds today, moved here: `physicalAngle`'s body becomes `analyzer.dialSign.physicalAngleOf analyzer.zeroDial dial`, its signature and doc kept and its doc saying the rule is `DialSign`'s, so the reference pipeline's numbers are unchanged. `member this.readingOf (zero : Angle) (angle : Angle) : Angle` is `Angle (zero.value + this.value * angle.value)`, the reading that gives `angle` (the sign is ±1, so it inverts `physicalAngleOf`). A reading is an `Angle` on the dial's scale, as `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` already takes it; no reading type is added, so no wrap or bijection is introduced (ELEV001, ELEV006). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`. (a) Directly before step 221's `ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong`: `type FileStem with static member firstFreeText (text : string) (taken : FileStem list) : string` answers the first of `<text>`, `<text> (2)`, `<text> (3)`, … whose `FileStem.ofText` (step 24) no stem of `taken` equals ignoring case (`StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`): the suffix sequence step 221 wrote into `ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong`, moved here, and `nextFreeAmong`'s body becomes the `ItemLabel` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` over the taken labels' `fileStem`s, so one sequence serves items and setups (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). A member may speak its type's primitives (AGENTS.md). (b) Appended at the end of the file, in this order, every case name of two words and no `bool`: `SetupError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the setup, the revision, the slot or the item: `InvalidSetupNameErr` (a blank name), `DuplicateSetupNameErr` (another setup of the kit has the name's file stem), `UnknownSetupErr` (the kit holds no setup of that name), `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` (the setup holds no such revision), `UnknownSetupSlotErr` (the table has no slot of that element), `UnknownSlotItemErr` (the kit holds no item of that id, or the library no model of it) and `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` (the item's model does not fit the slot's kind); `member this.describe : string` renders them `the setup name is not valid: <reason>`, `the kit already has a setup of that name: <reason>`, `the kit has no such setup: <reason>`, `the setup has no such revision: <reason>`, `the table has no such slot: <reason>`, `the item is not available: <reason>` and `the item does not fit the slot: <reason>`. `SetupName of string` with `.value`: `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<SetupName, SetupError>` keeps the text as given and refuses an empty or white-space text with `InvalidSetupNameErr`; `member this.fileStem : FileStem` is `FileStem.ofText this.value`, the stem of its `<name>.setup-json` (001 §A), so a name keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md §3.11, step 147's rule); `member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : SetupName list) : SetupName` is the `SetupName` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` over the taken names' `fileStem`s; `static member firstFree (taken : SetupName list) : SetupName` is the first of `Setup 1`, `Setup 2`, … whose `fileStem` no taken name has, ignoring case: the name a table takes when it becomes a setup without one (steps 261 and 264), until S8.3's template names setups from their slots. `SetupRevision of int` with `.value`, `static member first : SetupRevision` (1) and `member this.next : SetupRevision`. `SetupReference = { name : SetupName; revision : SetupRevision }`, one revision of one setup, with `member this.describe : string` = `'<name>' revision <n>`. No other type, member or option is added. Tests. In `KitTests` (step 122): `a setup name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `SetupName.tryCreate \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL\"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL\"`; `\"a: b/c\"` has `FileStem \"a_ b_c\"`, equal to `FileStem.ofText \"a: b/c\"`; `\"\"` and `\"   \"` answer `InvalidSetupNameErr`. `a setup takes the next free suffix of its name, and a table that is no setup yet takes the first free Setup n`: `(SetupName \"Bench\").nextFreeAmong [ SetupName \"bench\"; SetupName \"Bench (2)\" ]` is `SetupName \"Bench (3)\"`, among `[]` it is `SetupName \"Bench\"`, and `(SetupName \"a:b\").nextFreeAmong [ SetupName \"a_b\" ]` is `SetupName \"a:b (2)\"`; `SetupName.firstFree [ SetupName \"Setup 1\"; SetupName \"setup 2\" ]` is `SetupName \"Setup 3\"` and `SetupName.firstFree []` is `SetupName \"Setup 1\"`. `a setup revision starts at one and counts up, and a reference names its setup and revision`: `SetupRevision.first` is 1 and its `next.next` is 3, and `{ name = SetupName \"Bench\"; revision = SetupRevision.first.next }.describe` is `'Bench' revision 2`. `every setup error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. In `ItemModelsTests` (step 205): `a dial maps a raw reading to the physical angle by its sign and zero, and back`: `DialPositive.physicalAngleOf (10°) (40°)` is 30° and `DialNegative.physicalAngleOf (10°) (40°)` is −30°; for both signs and the angles −30°, 0°, 45° and 200°, `readingOf` of `physicalAngleOf` and `physicalAngleOf` of `readingOf` give the angle back within 1e-12; and `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` of an `AnalyzerModel` with `dialSign = DialNegative` and `zeroDial = 10°` at 40° equals `DialNegative.physicalAngleOf (10°) (40°)` exactly. Step 221's `KitItemTests` facts on `ItemLabel.nextFreeAmong` pass unchanged, and `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests` keeps its numbers.","acceptance":"After the setup identities land, `SetupName`, `SetupRevision`, `SetupReference` and `SetupError` MUST exist in `Kit.fs` with the name, suffix and first-free rules, `DialSign.physicalAngleOf` MUST be the one dial rule that `MuellerReconstruction.physicalAngle` calls, and `FileStem.firstFreeText` MUST be the one suffix sequence; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a setup name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `a setup takes the next free suffix of its name, and a table that is no setup yet takes the first free Setup n`, `a setup revision starts at one and counts up, and a reference names its setup and revision`, `every setup error renders its condition and its payload` and `a dial maps a raw reading to the physical angle by its sign and zero, and back`, the count rising by 5; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests` with its numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a setup name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a setup takes the next free suffix of its name, and a table that is no setup yet takes the first free Setup n","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a setup revision starts at one and counts up, and a reference names its setup and revision","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every setup error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.a dial maps a raw reading to the physical angle by its sign and zero, and back","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.SetupError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.SetupName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.SetupRevision","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.SetupReference","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.FileStem.firstFreeText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.DialSign.physicalAngleOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels.DialSign.readingOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-IDENTITIES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number":256,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S82b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[255],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests"],"how_to":"A setup as Domain data: an ordered optical path of slots, each slot one element of the table holding an item or nothing, and the revisions an experiment can reference (001 §J; the S8.2 brief: `Setup { name : SetupName; revision; slots }`, each slot holding an item (`ItemId`) or nothing plus its position on the beam and R1 / R2 / R3, or a dial reading; 'Experiments keep their captured-snapshot meaning through the setup revision: editing a setup that an experiment uses mints the next revision'; .spec-md §5, §6 'Version rule'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`: `module Setups` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `BeamLayout.fs`, because a slot sits on a `BeamLayout.BeamHost`: one `<Compile Include=\"Setups.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the setup, an ordered optical path of slots that the table draws (spec 0050 S8.2). It opens `Placement`, `Kit`, `ItemModels`, `Lifecycle` and `LibraryEntryFiles`; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (2) `SlotTurn` = `PlacementTurn` (the slot's R1 is its placement's own) | `DialTurn of reading : Angle` (the slot's item turns on a dial set to this raw reading, and its R1 is the item's `DialSign.physicalAngleOf` of it, step 255). `SlotContent` = `EmptySlotContent` | `ItemInSlot of item : ItemId * turn : SlotTurn`, with `member this.itemOpt : ItemId option`. (3) `SetupSlot = { id : Library.ElementId; placement : ElementPlacement; zoom : BeamLayout.ElementZoom; beam : BeamLayout.BeamHost; content : SlotContent }`, one slot of a setup and the one table element that draws it: its stable id (an experiment's varied element names it), its placement (the catalogue kind, the position along its beam, R1 / R2 / R3, the locks, the emission and the library entry it is bound to, `Placement.fs:ElementPlacement`), its draw zoom, the beam it sits on and its content. It carries what `Experiments.ElementDescriptor` (`Experiments.fs:ElementDescriptor`) and `Scene.SceneElement` (`Scene.fs:SceneElement`) carry today, which steps 260 and 261 delete. `member this.layoutElement : BeamLayout.LayoutElement` is `{ id = this.id; placement = this.placement; host = this.beam; zoom = this.zoom }` (`BeamLayout.fs:LayoutElement`), what the one ray law lays out (AGENTS.md 'One ray law'). (4) `SetupRevisionRecord = { revision : SetupRevision; slots : SetupSlot list }`, an earlier revision kept for the experiments that reference it. (5) `Setup = { name : SetupName; revision : SetupRevision; slots : SetupSlot list; history : SetupRevisionRecord list }`: the slots in the table's order (the light source, the ray root, first), and the earlier revisions oldest first, as an item file keeps its history (step 215). The brief's three fields gain `history` because an experiment that references an earlier revision must still resolve its slots. Members: `this.reference : SetupReference` (its name and current revision); `this.slotsAt (revision : SetupRevision) : Result<SetupSlot list, SetupError>`, the current slots at the current revision, a history record's at an earlier one, and `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` naming the reference's `describe` otherwise; `this.heldItems : ItemId list`, the items the current slots and then each history record's slots hold, each once, in that order; `static member create (name : SetupName) (slots : SetupSlot list) (held : Setup list) : Result<Setup, SetupError>`, `DuplicateSetupNameErr` naming both names when a held setup's `name.fileStem` equals the name's ignoring case (every `<name>.setup-json` shares the kit root on Windows, step 216's rule for items) and otherwise the setup at `SetupRevision.first` with no history: CreateSetup's pure half (001 §P); and `this.revisedWith (slots : SetupSlot list) (pin : PinState) : Setup`, the setup after the table's slots are written over it, decided by `Lifecycle.decideVersioning` (`Lifecycle.fs:decideVersioning`, the one version rule) over `{ physics = this.slots; metadata = () }` and `{ physics = slots; metadata = () }` with `pin` (step 65's `PinState`): `KeepCurrent` answers the setup unchanged, `MutateInPlace` the setup holding `slots`, and `MintNextVersion` the setup at `revision.next` holding `slots`, its current revision and slots appended to `history`. A setup has no metadata beyond its name, so its slots alone decide. No cache, wire tag or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs`, `module SetupTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its fixture slots are test-local records over `ElementPlacement.create` (`Placement.fs`), zoom `BeamLayout.ElementZoom 5.0` and `BeamLayout.OnMainBeam`: `src` (`LightSource` at `RayModel.defaultSourcePoint`), `lp` (`LinearPolarizer` at x = −0.3 m) and `det` (`Detector` at `RayModel.defaultDetectorPoint`), each `EmptySlotContent`, and a test-local `ItemId`. `a slot lays out as the element it is, on its own beam, and names the item it holds`: `lp.layoutElement` holds `lp`'s id, placement, beam as `host` and zoom; `itemOpt` of `ItemInSlot (item, PlacementTurn)` is `Some item` and of `EmptySlotContent` `None`. `a setup answers its slots at its own revision and at each earlier one, and refuses a revision it never had`: a setup `Bench` at revision 3 with history records r1 and r2 of distinct slot lists answers each list at its revision, and revision 4 answers `UnknownSetupRevisionErr` whose reason names `'Bench' revision 4`. `a setup lists each item its revisions hold once, in order`: a setup whose current slots hold items A then B and whose history holds B then C lists A, B, C. `a setup is created at its first revision, and a name whose file the kit holds is refused`: `create (SetupName \"Bench\")` over no held setup is revision 1 with no history; over a held `bench` it answers `DuplicateSetupNameErr`, and `Bench: A` over a held `Bench_ A` too. `a setup's slots change in place until an experiment pins its revision, which then mints the next`: revising with equal slots answers the setup unchanged, pinned or not; with `lp` turned to R1 30° and `VersionUnpinned` the revision and history are unchanged and the slots are the new ones; with `VersionPinned` the setup is at revision 2 with the new slots and one history record holding revision 1 and the old slots; a second pinned change gives revision 3 with history r1 then r2.","acceptance":"After the setup shape lands, `Setups.fs` MUST hold `SlotTurn`, `SlotContent`, `SetupSlot`, `SetupRevisionRecord` and `Setup`, a setup MUST answer its slots at each revision it holds and refuse others, and `revisedWith` MUST mint the next revision exactly when the revision is pinned and the slots change; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot lays out as the element it is, on its own beam, and names the item it holds`, `a setup answers its slots at its own revision and at each earlier one, and refuses a revision it never had`, `a setup lists each item its revisions hold once, in order`, `a setup is created at its first revision, and a name whose file the kit holds is refused` and `a setup's slots change in place until an experiment pins its revision, which then mints the next`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a slot lays out as the element it is, on its own beam, and names the item it holds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a setup answers its slots at its own revision and at each earlier one, and refuses a revision it never had","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a setup lists each item its revisions hold once, in order","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a setup is created at its first revision, and a name whose file the kit holds is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a setup's slots change in place until an experiment pins its revision, which then mints the next","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SlotTurn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SlotContent","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupRevisionRecord","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.Setup","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.Setup.revisedWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.Setup.create","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-SHAPE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number": 257, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S82c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [256], "how_to": "Each slot's role on the light path, read from the one ray law: Source, Prep 1…k, Object 1…n, Analyzer 1…k and Detector (001 §J 'Source, Prep 1…k, Object 1…n (two or more samples in series), Analyzer 1…k, Detector'; the S8.2 brief's slot roles; AGENTS.md 'One ray law for every element'). The role is derived from the slot's kind and where the light reaches it, never stored, so sliding an element past a sample changes its role with no second source of truth. In `Setups.fs`, after `Setup` (step 256), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) `SlotPosition of int` with `.value`, a slot's 1-based place within its role. (2) `SlotRole` = `SourceSlotRole` | `PrepSlotRole of SlotPosition` | `ObjectSlotRole of SlotPosition` | `AnalyzerSlotRole of SlotPosition` | `DetectorSlotRole of SlotPosition`, with `member this.text : string` = `Source`, `Prep <k>`, `Obj <k>`, `Analyzer <k>` or `Detector <k>` (001 §J's chip names). A role is never stored, so it carries no wire tag. (3) `RoledSlot = { role : SlotRole; slot : SetupSlot }`. (4) `type SetupSlot with static member inLightOrder (slots : SetupSlot list) : RoledSlot list` lays the slots out with `BeamLayout.layout` (`BeamLayout.fs:layout`) over their `layoutElement`s (step 256), the first slot being the ray root, and reads each slot's laid-out `path` (`BeamLayout.fs:PlacedElement`): its light depth is the number of steps of that path. A `LightSource` slot is the source; a `Sample` slot is an object; a `Detector` slot is a detector; any other slot is a prep when no step of its path is a `Sample` slot (the light reaches it before any object) and an analyzer otherwise, an element on an object's reflected ray included. Within each role the slots are ordered by light depth and then by table order, and numbered from 1, so Obj 1 is the sample the light crosses first and a second sample in series is Obj 2. The answer lists the sources, then the preps, the objects, the analyzers and the detectors. A slot the layout does not place (its host's reflected ray is off, say) has an empty path (`BeamLayout.fs:layoutWith`) and keeps its kind's role, ordered after the placed slots of that role. (5) `type Setup with member this.lightOrder : RoledSlot list` is `SetupSlot.inLightOrder this.slots`. No other member is added. Tests, in `SetupTests` (step 256), over test-local slot lists in table order whose x positions lie between `RayModel.defaultSourcePoint` and `RayModel.defaultDetectorPoint`. `a setup's slots take their roles in light order: the source, the preps, the objects in series, the analyzers, the detectors`: the slots `src`, `det`, `lpA` (x −0.3 m), `sampleB` (x 0.1 m), `sampleA` (x −0.1 m) and `lpB` (x 0.3 m), all on the main beam, answer `src` Source, `lpA` Prep 1, `sampleA` Obj 1, `sampleB` Obj 2, `lpB` Analyzer 1 and `det` Detector 1, in that order. `an element behind an object, on its reflected ray included, is an analyzer, and without an object every optical element is a prep`: with `sampleA` emitting both branches (`EmitBoth`), the same slots plus `polR` (a `LinearPolarizer` at x 0.2 m) and `detR` (a `Detector` at x 0.5 m), both on `OnReflectedBeamOf sampleA`, answer `polR` Analyzer 1 (its path src, lpA, sampleA is three steps) before `lpB` Analyzer 2 (four), and `detR` Detector 1 (four) before `det` Detector 2 (five); and the slots `src`, `lp1` (x −0.3 m), `lp2` (x 0.2 m) and `det` with no sample answer Source, Prep 1, Prep 2 and Detector 1. `a role renders its chip name`: `SourceSlotRole`, `PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 2)`, `ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)`, `AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 3)` and `DetectorSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)` render `Source`, `Prep 2`, `Obj 1`, `Analyzer 3` and `Detector 1`.", "acceptance": "After the roles land, `SetupSlot.inLightOrder` and `Setup.lightOrder` MUST give each slot its role from its kind and its laid-out path, objects in series numbered in light order; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a setup's slots take their roles in light order: the source, the preps, the objects in series, the analyzers, the detectors`, `an element behind an object, on its reflected ray included, is an analyzer, and without an object every optical element is a prep` and `a role renders its chip name`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a setup's slots take their roles in light order: the source, the preps, the objects in series, the analyzers, the detectors", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.an element behind an object, on its reflected ray included, is an analyzer, and without an object every optical element is a prep", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a role renders its chip name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SlotPosition", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SlotRole", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.RoledSlot", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.inLightOrder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.Setup.lightOrder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SLOT-ROLES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number":258,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S82d","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[257],"how_to":"The pure halves of AssignSlot and SwapSlot: which items fit a slot, what a slot becomes when it holds one, how a dial reading is drawn and recorded, and which setup a swap lands on (001 §P `AssignSlot`, `SwapSlot`; 001 §J 'Quick swap: … each dropdown lists compatible items only; choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one'; 001 §I 'Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) The number a parameter holds now, moved where a slot can read it. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`: `ParameterState` (step 214) gains `member this.currentValue : ParameterValue`, a `KnownParameter`'s value, an `UnknownParameter`'s `start` and a `CalibratedParameter`'s `value`: the rule step 245 wrote into `ParameterValues.ofParameters`, moved, so `ofParameters` (`ItemEvaluation.fs`) maps each parameter through `state.currentValue` and its answers are unchanged. (b) `ParameterValue.angle` (step 246, an extension in `ItemEvaluation.fs`) moves to `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs` as an intrinsic member of `ParameterValue` (step 207), its body and doc unchanged, deleted from `ItemEvaluation.fs`; its readers there keep calling it. (c) In `Kit.fs`, after `Item` (step 215): `type Item with member this.dialZeroAngle : Angle` is the `currentValue.angle` of the item's `ParameterName.dialZero` parameter (step 244), and `Angle.zero` when it has none (a fixed item). (2) `Setups.fs`, after step 257's members. (a) `type ItemModelChoice with member this.libraryEntryOpt : LibraryEntry option`: `SourcePresetChoice (sourceModel, s)` is `Some (SourceItem s)`, `PolarizerPresetChoice (polarizerModel, p)` `Some (PolarizerItem p)`, `StackSampleChoice (_, s)` `Some (SampleItem s)` and `LibraryModelChoice _` `None`: the library entry a table element is bound to when the item sits on it (`ElementId.fs:LibraryEntry`). `member this.slotKinds : CatalogueKind list` is, for a library entry, its `forKinds` (`ElementId.fs:LibraryEntry`, the rule the table's binding already applies), and for an item model its form's (step 208): `RealPolarizerModel` [`LinearPolarizer`]; `RetarderPlateModel` [`LinearPolarizer`; `CircularPolarizer`; `Sample`]; `BlackBoxMuellerModel` [`Sample`]; `CompoundModel` [`LinearPolarizer`; `CircularPolarizer`], as the compound polarizer presets fit both; `EmptySlotModel` [`LinearPolarizer`; `CircularPolarizer`; `Sample`]; and the three detector models [`Detector`], with no wildcard arm. (b) `type SetupSlot with`: `member this.withItem (item : Item) (model : ItemModelChoice) : Result<SetupSlot, SetupError>` answers `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and the slot's kind when `model.slotKinds` lacks the slot's `placement.catalogueKind`; otherwise the slot holding `ItemInSlot (item.id, turn)`, `turn` being `DialTurn (sign.readingOf item.dialZeroAngle placement.r1)` for `DialMounted sign` (so the drawn angle is kept) and `PlacementTurn` for `FixedMounting`; when `model.libraryEntryOpt` is `Some entry`, the placement's `valueId` becomes `Some entry.entryId` and its emission `Library.placementEmissionForEntry placement.emission entry` (`ElementId.fs:placementEmissionForEntry`), exactly as the table binds an entry (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:withBoundSampleEmission`), so the drawn element and its item agree; an item model leaves the binding as it is. `member this.withoutItem : SetupSlot` holds `EmptySlotContent` and keeps the placement. `member this.drawnWith (items : Item list) : SetupSlot`: a `DialTurn reading` slot whose item is in `items` with `DialMounted sign` has R1 `sign.physicalAngleOf item.dialZeroAngle reading`; every other slot is unchanged. `member this.recordedWith (items : Item list) : SetupSlot` is its inverse: such a slot's reading becomes `sign.readingOf item.dialZeroAngle placement.r1`. The table turns a slot in physical angles, and the setup records the reading. (c) `SetupSwap` = `SwitchToHeldSetup of Setup` | `CreateSwappedSetup of Setup`. `type Setup with static member swapTarget (slots : SetupSlot list) (held : Setup list) (fresh : SetupName) : SetupSwap` answers `SwitchToHeldSetup` of the first held setup whose current slots hold, slot by slot in order, the same `placement.catalogueKind` and `content` as `slots`, and otherwise `CreateSwappedSetup` of `{ name = fresh; revision = SetupRevision.first; slots = slots; history = [] }`. Nothing writes; the host records (steps 263, 264). No other member is added. Tests, in `SetupTests`: `an item fits the slots its model may fill`: the `slotKinds` and `libraryEntryOpt` of `SourcePresetChoice` of `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`, of the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer, of `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, and of `LibraryModelChoice` of each of the eight built-in item models (`BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel`, step 210), as listed above. `an item put in a slot binds the slot to its library entry, and a dial-mounted item keeps the drawn angle as its reading`: into a `LinearPolarizer` slot at R1 30°, a `FixedMounting` item of the LP preset gives `ItemInSlot (id, PlacementTurn)` bound to `PresetIds.polarizerLp`; a `DialMounted DialNegative` item of it whose `dialZero` is known at 10° gives `DialTurn (−20°)`, and that slot `drawnWith [ item ]` keeps R1 30°; a glass-plate item into a `Sample` slot binds the sample's entry id and its `supportedEmission`; a real-LP item-model item keeps the slot's `valueId`; a source item into the polarizer slot answers `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` naming its label; and `withoutItem` holds `EmptySlotContent` with the placement unchanged. `a dial reading is drawn through the item's current zero, and the table's angle is recorded back as a reading`: that dial slot drawn after the item's `dialZero` is set to 20° (`withParameterState`, step 234) has R1 −1 · (−20° − 20°) = 40°; the slot turned to R1 50° and `recordedWith [ item ]` holds `DialTurn (−30°)`; a `PlacementTurn` slot is unchanged by both; all within 1e-12. `a swap switches to the held setup holding that content, and otherwise makes a new setup`: over held setups A and B, `swapTarget` of B's slots answers `SwitchToHeldSetup B`; slots no held setup holds answer `CreateSwappedSetup` named `fresh` at revision 1 with no history; and B's slots with one dial reading changed are not matched. In `KitItemTests` (step 213): `a parameter state answers its current number, and an item its dial zero`: `currentValue` of a known 0.1, an unknown starting at 0.5 within [0, 1] and a calibration of 0.25 answer 0.1, 0.5 and 0.25; an item whose `dialZero` is known at π / 18 answers that angle, and a `FixedMounting` item `Angle.zero`. `ItemEvaluationTests`' facts pass unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the pure slot updates land, `ItemModelChoice.slotKinds` MUST name the slots an item fits, `SetupSlot.withItem` MUST bind the slot to the item's library entry and record a dial-mounted item's reading, `drawnWith` and `recordedWith` MUST map readings through the item's current zero, and `Setup.swapTarget` MUST find the held setup with the swapped content or make a new one; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item fits the slots its model may fill`, `an item put in a slot binds the slot to its library entry, and a dial-mounted item keeps the drawn angle as its reading`, `a dial reading is drawn through the item's current zero, and the table's angle is recorded back as a reading`, `a swap switches to the held setup holding that content, and otherwise makes a new setup` and `a parameter state answers its current number, and an item its dial zero`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.an item fits the slots its model may fill","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.an item put in a slot binds the slot to its library entry, and a dial-mounted item keeps the drawn angle as its reading","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a dial reading is drawn through the item's current zero, and the table's angle is recorded back as a reading","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a swap switches to the held setup holding that content, and otherwise makes a new setup","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests.a parameter state answers its current number, and an item its dial zero","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ParameterState.currentValue","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.Item.dialZeroAngle","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.ItemModelChoice.libraryEntryOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.ItemModelChoice.slotKinds","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.withItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.withoutItem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.drawnWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.recordedWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSwap","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.Setup.swapTarget","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SLOT-ASSIGNMENT"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number": 259, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S82e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.TestWindows", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [258], "how_to": "The table's elements ARE the active setup's slots: one record, not two of the same shape (001 §J 'The table draws the active setup'; the S8.2 brief: 'slots map to table elements … Placing an element binds a slot'; AGENTS.md 'A bijection is collapsed, not bridged … the LOWER type survives'). `TableAndElementRotationView`'s `TestElement` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TestElement`, `{ id; placement; zoom; beam }`) is the shape of `Setups.SetupSlot` (step 256) without its content, and `SetupSlot` is the lower type (Domain), so `TestElement` is deleted. Nothing about what is drawn, laid out or run changes in this step. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (a) `TestElement` is deleted, and `TableAndElementRotationModel.elements` becomes `Setups.SetupSlot list`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2: the table's slots, the light source (the ray root) first. (b) `TestElement`'s members `elementX` and `boxCorners` move unchanged onto a `type Setups.SetupSlot with` extension at the same place in the file, and the `type TestElement with` extension further down (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, the one holding the drawing members) becomes `type Setups.SetupSlot with`. (c) `mkElement`, `mainSeedElements` and `initInverse`'s three seeds (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:mkElement`, `:mainSeedElements`, `:initInverse`), and every other record that built a `TestElement`, build a `SetupSlot` with `content = Setups.EmptySlotContent`: `AddElement`, `AddElementBoundTo` and `PlaceOnBeam` place a slot of the table, empty until step 263 puts an item in it. (d) `model.layoutElements` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:layoutElements`) is `model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.layoutElement)` (step 256), its hand-written record deleted. (e) `captureScene` and `restoreScene` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:captureScene`, `:restoreScene`) map a `SetupSlot` to a `Scene.SceneElement` and back with `EmptySlotContent`, until step 260 deletes all three. (f) Every `TestElement` annotation in the file names `Setups.SetupSlot`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/ElementRotationView.fs`: its `TestElement` annotations name `Setups.SetupSlot` and `initElementRotation`'s `onRay` builds one with `content = Setups.EmptySlotContent`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`: the doc of `SceneElement` that names `TestElement` names `SetupSlot` instead, in no more words. (4) Tests, their assertions unchanged: every `TestElement` annotation or record in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs` and in the UI suite's `ElementMenuTests.fs`, `ElementRotationTests.fs`, `ExperimentControlsTests.fs`, `InverseConstructorTests.fs`, `LayerBandsControlsTests.fs`, `LibraryControlsTests.fs`, `MainSceneMsgTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`, `SourceAndDetectorMoveTests.fs`, `TableAndElementRotationTests.fs` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs` names `Setups.SetupSlot` (or `SetupSlot` under an `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups`), and a record of one gains `content = EmptySlotContent` (`OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`' flagged sample, `SceneRoundTripTests.fs`' three fixture elements). The other readers of the model's elements in the census, `OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs` and the UI suite's `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`, `LibraryWindowTests.fs`, `LightSourceEditorTests.fs` and `ScrollExtentTests.fs`, compile over `SetupSlot` as they are; a record of an element they build gains the content, and nothing else changes in them. `MainSceneMsgTests` gains `the table's elements are slots: each one placed is empty, and each lays out as the table lays it out`: every element of `initMain ()` holds `EmptySlotContent`; after `AddElement LinearPolarizer` and `AddElement Sample` the new elements do too; and `model.layoutElements` equals `model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.layoutElement)`. No other type, member or behaviour changes. After this step `git grep -n -w \"TestElement\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the table's elements become slots, `TestElement` MUST be gone, `TableAndElementRotationModel.elements` MUST be `Setups.SetupSlot list` built with `EmptySlotContent`, and `git grep -n -w \"TestElement\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing, every drawn, laid-out and run value unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the table's elements are slots: each one placed is empty, and each lays out as the table lays it out`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.TestWindows/ElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementMenuTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LayerBandsControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainSceneMsgTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SourceAndDetectorMoveTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests.the table's elements are slots: each one placed is empty, and each lays out as the table lays it out", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainSceneMsgTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-TABLE-SLOTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TestElement", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S82-TABLE-SLOTS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S82-TABLE-SLOTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.elements", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S82-TABLE-SLOTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number":260,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S82f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[259],"actions":["RENAME_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests","RENAME_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests -> OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests","ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests"],"how_to":"`<name>.setup-json` holds a setup, replacing S4.3's scene file, and the constructor's scene save and load become CreateSetup and loading a setup (the S8.2 brief: '<name>.setup-json (schema + version) REPLACES S4.3's scene file shape. Scene.SceneSnapshot, and whatever only it used, is deleted; the constructor's scene save / load becomes setup save / load'; 001 §P `CreateSetup`; 001 §A 'Kit extensions … .setup-json'). The stack is step 146's (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`); no second parser or writer is written. Kit files of the old shape exist only under test output folders, so the schema version stays 1 and no reader of the old shape is kept (.spec-md §7: kit file shapes change in later parts and no migration is needed). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) Domain. (a) `Setups.fs` (step 256): `SetupFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; setup : Setup }`, the `.setup-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1; `type Setup with member this.setupFile : SetupFile` is the setup at the current version, a file being read back as its `setup` field (one direction, ELEV006). `Setup` gains `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list`: the `placement.valueId` of every slot that names a library entry (`ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24) as an `EntryLatestReference`, over the current slots and then each history record's, in slot order, each once: the rule of step 147's `SceneSnapshot.libraryReferences`, moved here, because every revision an experiment may reference needs its entries in the kit. (b) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`: `SceneStoreError`, `SceneName`, `SceneElement`, `SceneSnapshot` and `SceneFile` (`Scene.fs:SceneName`, `:SceneElement`, `:SceneSnapshot`, steps 147 and 151) are deleted with their members. `SnapMode` (`Scene.fs:SnapMode`) stays, because the window's `snapChain` holds it, and the module doc becomes one to three lines: the window's snap mode, which a setup does not carry (spec 0050 S8.2). The comment above `Scene.fs`'s `<Compile>` in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` is cut to the words that stay true, naming no scene file, and nothing is added. A setup is the optical path: the table view, the snap mode and the rotation pivot that step 147's scene file held are the window's, so loading a setup leaves them as they are. (2) Storage. (a) `schema/setup.schema.json` (step 147) describes the setup file. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `setup`, and `setup` holds exactly `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\\S`), `revision` (a positive integer), `slots` (an array) and `history` (an array whose items hold exactly `revision`, a positive integer, and `slots`, an array). A slot's shape is bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one. `SchemaValidation.validateSceneFile` (step 147) is renamed `validateSetupFile`, its schema still loaded once behind a `lazy`. (b) `KitContentFiles.fs`: `SceneFile.fileText` and `KitFileText.parseSceneFile` (step 147) become `SetupFile.fileText` and `KitFileText.parseSetupFile` over the same stack and `SetupKitFile.extension`. On the `KitProxy` extension (step 148), `writeScene`, `readScene` and `readSceneNames` are deleted and replaced by `member this.writeSetup (setup : Setup) : Result<unit, KitError>`, which writes `setup.setupFile.fileText` with `writeKindFile SetupKitFile setup.name.fileStem`, a rendering error being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file, and `member this.readSetups () : Result<Setup list, KitError>`, which parses every stem `listKindFiles SetupKitFile` answers; a refusal, or a file whose setup's `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case, is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and refuses the whole read, so a window never opens a kit with a setup left out; the answer is ordered by name (ordinal). On the `KitLibraryContext` extension (step 149), `recordScene` becomes `member this.recordSetup (setup : Setup) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>`: `snapshotReferences setup.libraryReferences` (step 139), then `writeSetup`, a `KitError` being `KitLibraryKitErr`. Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) `writeSetup` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit.scenes : SceneName list` (step 150) becomes `setups : Setup list`, the kit's setups as read at open, in name order; `openedOver` (step 172) reads `readSetups ()` where it read `readSceneNames ()`, a refusal closing the kit as any failed read does; `withRebindings` keeps it. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) The model: `sceneName` (step 153) becomes `setupName : ControlCaption`, the setup name being typed; `savedScenes` becomes `kitSetups : Setups.Setup list`, the kit's setups in name order as the window last read or wrote them; and the model gains `activeSetupOpt : Setups.Setup option`, the kit setup the table draws as last created or loaded, `None` while the table is not yet a setup of the kit; each with a one-line doc. `initWith` sets them to `ControlCaption \"\"`, `[]` and `None`. The private content function `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` share (step 187 (4)) takes the setups in place of the scene names, sets `kitSetups`, and sets `activeSetupOpt` to the setup among them whose name is the active one's (`None` when there is none): `loadKit` passes `opened.setups`, `ReloadKitChanges` reads `readSetups ()` where it read `readSceneNames ()` (an error keeping the model and the offer with step 187's text), and `CopyChosenExperiments` (step 225) passes `model.kitSetups`. (b) Messages, each with a one-line doc: `SceneSetName` becomes `SetSetupName of ControlCaption`; `SceneSave` becomes `CreateSetup` (the table becomes a new setup of the kit, named by the field); `SceneLoad of SceneName` becomes `ActivateSetup of Kit.SetupName` (the kit's setup of that name is drawn on the table). (c) Arms. `SetSetupName name` sets `setupName`. `CreateSetup` is refused by the read-only guard of step 185 like `SceneSave` was; otherwise `SetupName.tryCreate model.setupName.value` (step 255) and then `Setup.create name (model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.recordedWith model.kitItems)) model.kitSetups` (steps 256, 258), either refusal setting `kitStatus` to `Not created — <e.describe>` and writing nothing; an `Ok setup` is recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordSetup setup`: on `Ok` `kitSetups` holds it in name order, `activeSetupOpt` is `Some setup` and `kitStatus` is `Created setup '<name>'.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `ActivateSetup name`: the setup of that name in `kitSetups` makes `elements` its `slots` drawn through the kit's items (`slot.drawnWith model.kitItems`, step 258), `activeSetupOpt` that setup, `selection` `TableSelected`, `drag` `NotPressed`, `elementMenu` `None` (the resets `restoreScene` made) and `kitStatus` `Loaded setup '<name>'.`; with none, `kitStatus` is `Load failed — <describe>` of `UnknownSetupErr` naming the name and the table is left alone. It writes nothing, so a read-only kit loads setups. `captureScene` and `restoreScene` (step 259) are deleted: the table's elements are the setup's slots (step 259). (d) The view. `collectionBuilderView`'s scene row (step 153) becomes the setup row under the heading `Setup:`: the name `TextBox` carrying `ConstructorUiId.setupNameField`, dispatching `SetSetupName` on Enter and on lost focus, and the `workbenchButton` `Create setup` (`ConstructorUiId.createSetupButton`, dispatching `CreateSetup`, withheld under a read-only kit as Save scene was, step 185); then the `kitStatus` line; then, when `kitSetups` is not empty, `Saved setups:` and a `WrapPanel` named `ConstructorUiId.savedSetups` holding one `workbenchButton` per setup (`ConstructorUiId.savedSetup setup.name`, captioned by the name, dispatching `ActivateSetup`); then the inverse `Data files:` section. (5) Ids. `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: `sceneNameField`, `saveSceneButton` and `savedScenes` (step 153) become `setupNameField` (`\"SetupNameField\"`), `createSetupButton` (`\"CreateSetupButton\"`) and `savedSetups` (`\"SavedSetups\"`) under a doc line naming the setup row. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `savedScene` and the `SceneName.caption` extension (step 153) become `static member savedSetup (name : Kit.SetupName) : ConstructorUiId` (`SavedSetup_<name>`) and `type Kit.SetupName with member this.caption : ControlCaption`. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests. (i) `KitContentFileJsonTests` (steps 146, 147): its fixture becomes a setup `Bench: A` at revision 2 whose slots are a light source bound to the 600 nm source preset (`PresetIds.source600`), a linear polarizer bound to the linear-polarizer preset holding a test-local item with `DialTurn (−20°)` and an unbound detector, with one history record at revision 1 whose polarizer holds nothing. `a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe` becomes `a setup is stored under its name made filesystem-safe` over `SetupName`, the same texts and stems. `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`: the file of that setup round-trips equal through `fileText` and `parseSetupFile`, holds no `\\r`, ends with one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys `schemaVersion` then `setup`, and writes the same text again. `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: `schemaVersion` 2, with the body and alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = SetupKitFile.extension`. `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`: the text without `setup`, with `setup.name` `\"   \"`, with `setup` lacking `history`, with `setup.revision` 0 and with an extra top-level key answer `SchemaValidationErr`, and `{` `MalformedJsonErr`. `a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest` becomes `a setup references the library entries its slots bind in every revision, each once, at their latest`: the fixture's `libraryReferences` are exactly the `EntryLatestReference`s of the source and the linear-polarizer presets, in that order; a revision binding the source preset again references it once; a setup of unbound slots references nothing. (ii) `SceneRoundTripTests.fs` is renamed `SetupRoundTripTests.fs`, `module SetupRoundTripTests`, its `<Compile>` entry and the comment above it naming the setup file, in no more words. It keeps its fixture slots as a setup `Experiment A`. `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state` becomes `a setup round-trips through its kit file, reproducing its slots, their items and its revisions`: `writeSetup` of it, then `readSetups` answers `[ that setup ]`, the folder holds `Experiment A.setup-json`, and a model whose `kitSetups` hold it, after `ActivateSetup`, has `elements` equal to its slots. `writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file` becomes `writing a setup again under its name replaces its kit file`. `reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr` becomes `a kit with no setup files reads no setups`: a fresh kit answers `Ok []`. `a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file` becomes `a setup file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the setup list, naming the file`: `Broken.setup-json` written as `{`, and `B.setup-json` holding `Experiment A`'s text, each make `readSetups` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file. `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a blank name as InvalidScene carrying a reason`, `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a null name as InvalidScene` and `SceneName.tryCreate accepts a non-blank name and round-trips its value` are deleted with `SceneName`; step 255's `a setup name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule` covers the setup name. `SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement` moves with the class unchanged. (iii) `KitLibraryTests` (step 149): `recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind` becomes `recording a setup snapshots the entries its slots bind in every revision, then writes its file`: a setup whose current slots bind the 600 nm source preset and the multilayer sample (`SampleIds.multilayerQwId`) by value id and whose history binds the glass plate (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId`), recorded through `recordSetup`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding the source, both samples at their latest versions, their materials and their categories, and `readSetups` answers the setup. (iv) `KitOpeningTests` (step 150): `opening a kit reads its experiments and scenes` becomes `opening a kit reads its experiments and setups`, a setup `Bench` written through `writeSetup` answering `setups` `[ Bench ]` when the kit is opened again. (v) `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` (step 148): `a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing` becomes `a read-only kit refuses experiment and setup writes and writes nothing`, `writeSetup` answering `KitReadOnlyErr`. (vi) `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 187): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` sends `SetSetupName (ControlCaption \"Bench\")` then `CreateSetup` where it sent the scene messages, with the same assertions over `kitSetups`; `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer` has the other writer write a setup through `writeSetup`, and the reload leaves `kitSetups` holding it. (vii) New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs`, `module SetupModelTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment; its model is `initMain ()` loaded through `loadKit` (step 152) of a kit folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"SetupModelTests\", <a new GUID>)` opened read-write through `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) over the Built-in import context, as `KitWindowModelTests` opens its kits. `CreateSetup records the table as a new kit setup and makes it the active one`: with a linear polarizer added (`AddElement LinearPolarizer`), `SetSetupName (ControlCaption \"Bench\")` then `CreateSetup` leaves `kitSetups` `[ Bench ]` at revision 1 holding the table's slots, `activeSetupOpt` `Some Bench`, `kitStatus` `Created setup 'Bench'.`, the folder holding `Bench.setup-json` and the preset's snapshot under `library/`. `CreateSetup of a blank name, or of a name whose file the kit holds, is told and records nothing`: `\"   \"` and, after `Bench`, `\"bench\"` each set a `kitStatus` starting `Not created` and write no further setup file. `ActivateSetup draws the kit's setup on the table and keeps the window's view, snap mode and pivot`: after `Bench` is created, the polarizer removed (`RemoveSelectedElement`), the view zoomed, `SetRotationPivot PivotAtIncidentFace` sent, `ActivateSetup (SetupName \"Bench\")` puts the polarizer back with `Bench`'s slots, keeps the view, the snap mode and the pivot, and selects the table; `ActivateSetup (SetupName \"nowhere\")` sets a `kitStatus` starting `Load failed` and leaves `elements` as they were. (viii) `SceneSaveLoadTests.fs` is renamed `SetupSaveLoadTests.fs`, `module SetupSaveLoadTests`, its `<Compile>` entry following it. `a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table` becomes `a created setup is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table` over `SetSetupName (ControlCaption \"Bench: A\")`, `CreateSetup`, `Bench_ A.setup-json`, the polarizer removed and `ActivateSetup`, and a model loaded from the same folder opened again lists `Bench: A`. `saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing` becomes `creating a setup with a blank name, or one the kit holds, reports a typed status and writes nothing`: `\"   \"` and a second `Bench: A` each set a `kitStatus` starting `Not created` and write no further setup file. `loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone` becomes `loading a setup the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone`. `the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes` (trait `ui-smoke`) becomes `the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups`, holding `setupNameField`, `createSetupButton`, `savedSetups` and the setup's `savedSetup` button. (ix) `KitWindowTests` (step 185): `a read-only window withholds every write control` looks for `createSetupButton` where it looked for `saveSceneButton`. After this step `git grep -n -E \"SceneSnapshot|SceneName|SceneFile|recordScene|readSceneNames\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.","acceptance":"After the setup file replaces the scene file, `<name>.setup-json` MUST hold a `Setup` read and written by `KitProxy.readSetups` / `writeSetup` and recorded with every revision's library snapshots by `KitLibraryContext.recordSetup`, `Scene.fs` MUST hold `SnapMode` alone, and `CreateSetup` / `ActivateSetup` MUST create the table as a kit setup and load one, `git grep -n -E \"SceneSnapshot|SceneName|SceneFile|recordScene|readSceneNames\" -- Berreman/` finding nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a setup is stored under its name made filesystem-safe`, `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`, `a setup references the library entries its slots bind in every revision, each once, at their latest`, `a setup round-trips through its kit file, reproducing its slots, their items and its revisions`, `writing a setup again under its name replaces its kit file`, `a kit with no setup files reads no setups`, `a setup file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the setup list, naming the file`, `SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement`, `recording a setup snapshots the entries its slots bind in every revision, then writes its file`, `opening a kit reads its experiments and setups`, `a read-only kit refuses experiment and setup writes and writes nothing`, `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`, `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`, `CreateSetup records the table as a new kit setup and makes it the active one`, `CreateSetup of a blank name, or of a name whose file the kit holds, is told and records nothing` and `ActivateSetup draws the kit's setup on the table and keeps the window's view, snap mode and pivot`, the count unchanged (three facts new, three deleted); ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups`, its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a created setup is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table`, `creating a setup with a blank name, or one the kit holds, reports a typed status and writes nothing`, `loading a setup the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMovementTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FacetedTreeControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RayPositionControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererTestTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RotationControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToBeamTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToReflectedTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableRotationTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestLauncherTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/setup.schema.json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupRoundTripTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a setup is stored under its name made filesystem-safe","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a setup file round-trips through its canonical text","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a setup references the library entries its slots bind in every revision, each once, at their latest","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupRoundTripTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests.a setup round-trips through its kit file, reproducing its slots, their items and its revisions","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupRoundTripTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests.writing a setup again under its name replaces its kit file","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupRoundTripTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests.a kit with no setup files reads no setups","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupRoundTripTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests.a setup file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the setup list, naming the file","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"delete","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SceneName.tryCreate rejects a blank name as InvalidScene carrying a reason","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"delete","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SceneName.tryCreate rejects a null name as InvalidScene","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"delete","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SceneName.tryCreate accepts a non-blank name and round-trips its value","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SceneRoundTripTests.SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupRoundTripTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupRoundTripTests.SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording a setup snapshots the entries its slots bind in every revision, then writes its file","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening a kit reads its experiments and scenes","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening a kit reads its experiments and setups","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.a read-only kit refuses experiment and setup writes and writes nothing","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.CreateSetup records the table as a new kit setup and makes it the active one","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.CreateSetup of a blank name, or of a name whose file the kit holds, is told and records nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.ActivateSetup draws the kit's setup on the table and keeps the window's view, snap mode and pivot","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests.a created setup is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests.creating a setup with a blank name, or one the kit holds, reports a typed status and writes nothing","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests.loading a setup the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests.the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests.the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.Setup.libraryReferences","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Scene.SceneFile","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateSceneFile","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateSetupFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeScene","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readScene","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readSceneNames","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeSetup","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readSetups","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordScene","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordSetup","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.OpenedKit","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.captureScene","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.restoreScene","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.sceneName","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.savedScenes","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.setupName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitSetups","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.activeSetupOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SceneSetName","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SceneSave","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SceneLoad","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetSetupName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CreateSetup","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ActivateSetup","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.sceneNameField","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.saveSceneButton","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.savedScenes","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.savedScene","op":"retire","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.setupNameField","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.createSetupButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.savedSetups","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S82-SETUP-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.savedSetup","op":"create","path":"Berreman/Opt