{"number":306,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S92i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[305],"how_to":"Copying experiments brings the kit profiles their data is mapped by, because a profile lives in the kit file, not in the experiment (001 §H 'Between kits'; .spec-md §3.15; step 291: a copy keeps each experiment's profile name and row selection; S6's rule that a clashing name takes the next free suffix). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, at its end: `type ImportProfileName with member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : ImportProfileName list) : ImportProfileName`, the `ImportProfileName` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` (step 255) over the taken names' `FileStem.ofText`, the one suffix sequence items, setups and experiments use. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`: `ExperimentCopyReport` (steps 224, 227) gains, as its last fields, `profiles : ImportProfile list` (each profile the copy added to the kit file, as added) and `kitFile : KitFile` (the kit file as the copy left it). `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` (steps 224, 227, 261, 290, 291) keeps its read-then-write order and its errors: after the kept experiments it takes, in order of first appearance, the distinct profile names of their `dataOpt` that `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName source.kitFile.importProfiles` (step 300) answers as `KitProfileChoice` (a built-in or an unheld name needs nothing). A profile the target holds under that name with equal content is reused; one the target holds under that name with other content is added as the source's profile named `nextFreeAmong` of the target's names and the ones added before it, and the copied experiments mapped by it name the new name; any other is added as it is. When it adds any, it writes `this.saveKitFile { this.kitFile with importProfiles = this.kitFile.importProfiles @ <the added> }` (step 131) after the data files and before any setup or experiment, so a written experiment never names a profile the kit lacks; its `KitError` is `KitLibraryKitErr`. `kitFile` is that saved kit file, else `this.kitFile`. No merge or replace of a held profile is added. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `CopyChosenExperiments` (steps 225, 227, 261) sets the window's content over `{ model.kit with kitFile = report.kitFile }`, so the window holds the profiles the copy added; its texts are unchanged. Tests. `KitTests` gains `a profile name takes the first free suffix among the taken ones`: `(ImportProfileName \"Lab scan\").nextFreeAmong []` is itself, over `[ Lab scan ]` is `Lab scan (2)`, and over `[ Lab scan; LAB SCAN (2) ]` is `Lab scan (3)`. `ExperimentCopyTests` (step 224) gains `a copy brings the kit profiles its experiments use, reusing an equal one and renaming a different one`: the source's kit file also holds a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column) and E1 is mapped by it, E3 by `Intensity series`; copying [E1; E3] into a target whose kit file holds another `Lab scan` (its σ column 5) leaves the target's kit file, read back through `readKitFile`, holding its own `Lab scan` and the source's as `Lab scan (2)`, the copied E1 mapped by `Lab scan (2)` and E3 by `Intensity series`, and the report's `profiles` exactly the one added; copying E1 into a target holding an equal `Lab scan` adds no profile, writes the kit file not at all, and keeps E1's profile name. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 225): `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source` also has the source's kit file hold `Lab scan`, saved through `saveKitFile` before the source is closed, with E2 mapped by it, and asserts that `model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles` and the target's `readKitFile` hold `Lab scan` after the copy. Every other copy fact passes unchanged.","acceptance":"After a copy carries profiles, `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` MUST add each kit profile its copied experiments are mapped by, reusing an equal one and renaming a different one by `ImportProfileName.nextFreeAmong`, before it writes any experiment, and the window MUST take the kit file it left; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a profile name takes the first free suffix among the taken ones` and `a copy brings the kit profiles its experiments use, reusing an equal one and renaming a different one`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a profile name takes the first free suffix among the taken ones","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S92-PROFILES-ON-COPY"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copy brings the kit profiles its experiments use, reusing an equal one and renaming a different one","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S92-PROFILES-ON-COPY"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S92-PROFILES-ON-COPY"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfileName.nextFreeAmong","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S92-PROFILES-ON-COPY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.ExperimentCopyReport","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S92-PROFILES-ON-COPY"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S92-PROFILES-ON-COPY"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 307, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [306], "how_to": "What a picked lab file's bytes suggest, and the preview of its first rows, for the wizard (001 §K 'sniff the delimiter, header and BOM, and show a preview'; 001 §O 'Data dialog: preview, column roles, an import-profile picker'; the S9.2 brief: 'sniffing'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, after `LabFileSource` (step 132): `type FileByteContent with` (`Softellect.Sys.Primitives.FileByteContent`, STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`) `member this.kitFileText : KitFileText`, the bytes decoded as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark (EF BB BF) dropped, and `member this.byteOrderMark : ByteOrderMark`, `ByteOrderMarkPresent` when the bytes start with that mark. Every decode of a kit's bytes with a leading mark dropped calls `kitFileText`: the reads and copy-in of `KitProxy.create` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs`, steps 126-128, 133) and the copy-in of `KitProxy.createInMemory` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`, step 133), their own decode bodies deleted, so one decode remains and every text they answer is unchanged. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `ColumnRoles.tryOfChoices`: `LabFileSniff = { bom : ByteOrderMark; delimiter : DataDelimiter; header : HeaderRowChoice }`, what a file's first lines suggest; `PreviewCell of string` with `.value`; `PreviewRow of PreviewCell list` with `member this.cells : PreviewCell list`; `LabFilePreview = { columnNames : PreviewCell list; rows : PreviewRow list }`, a file's columns and first rows as a layout reads them; and `type LabFileSource with member this.sniffedLayout : LabFileSniff`: the mark is `content.byteOrderMark`; over the first ten non-empty lines of `content.kitFileText` (each trimmed of a `\\r`), the delimiter is the first of `DataDelimiter.all` whose character splits every one of them into the same number of at least two cells, `CommaDelimiter` when none does; the header is `HeaderOnFirstRow` when the first line, split so, has no cell that `Double.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Float` and `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture` reads, or has a cell that does not read where the second line's cell of that position does, and `NoHeaderRow` otherwise. It is a suggestion the wizard shows and the user changes (step 308); it touches no disk. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: `type KitFileText with member this.previewWith (delimiter : DataDelimiter) (header : HeaderRowChoice) : Result<LabFilePreview, ExperimentDataError>`, through step 302's private CSV read, so the preview shows the cells a mapping reads: the column names are the header's trimmed cells, or `Column <n>` for each column of the widest of the first twenty rows when there is no header; the rows are the first twenty data rows' cells; an empty text is `EmptyDataFileErr`, and the read's error passes through. No cache, encoding guess or other member is added. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` (step 300) gains `sniffing suggests the delimiter, the header and the byte-order mark of a lab file`: a `LabFileSource` of the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\\n` sniffs `ByteOrderMarkPresent`, `CommaDelimiter` and `HeaderOnFirstRow`, and its `content.kitFileText` starts `experiment,` with no mark; `0;1.5\\n20;1.25\\n` sniffs `ByteOrderMarkAbsent`, `SemicolonDelimiter` and `NoHeaderRow`; `phi\\tI\\n0\\t0.5\\n` sniffs `TabDelimiter` and `HeaderOnFirstRow`; and `one column\\n` sniffs `CommaDelimiter` and `HeaderOnFirstRow`. `LabFileImportTests` (step 301) gains `the preview shows a lab file's columns and first rows as the mapping reads them`: the Phone ROI text of step 303 previewed by comma with a header shows the five column names and its two rows; with `NoHeaderRow` it shows `Column 1` to `Column 5` and three rows, the header among them; a text of thirty data rows shows twenty. `KitProxyTests`' byte-order-mark facts (steps 128, 133, 204) pass unchanged. Verification (claim-check repair, .spec-md §9): ui-tests MUST select OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests (Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:FsxAcceptanceTests) to preserve the constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples. The constructor-unit-tests behavior checks above remain required; this selection neither edits that class nor substitutes for the future kit-acceptance tests.", "acceptance": "After sniffing and the preview land, `LabFileSource.sniffedLayout` MUST suggest a picked file's byte-order mark, delimiter and header, `KitFileText.previewWith` MUST show its columns and first twenty rows through the reader the mappings use, and `FileByteContent.kitFileText` MUST be the kit's one decode; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `sniffing suggests the delimiter, the header and the byte-order mark of a lab file` and `the preview shows a lab file's columns and first rows as the mapping reads them`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass. ui-tests MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests, preserving its constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples and its test count.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"suite": "ui-tests", "mode": "selected", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.sniffing suggests the delimiter, the header and the byte-order mark of a lab file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.the preview shows a lab file's columns and first rows as the mapping reads them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.FileByteContent.kitFileText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.FileByteContent.byteOrderMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.LabFileSniff", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.PreviewCell", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.PreviewRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.LabFilePreview", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.LabFileSource.sniffedLayout", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LabFileImport.KitFileText.previewWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "obligations": ["S92-SNIFF-PREVIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 308, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [307], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests"], "how_to": "The column-mapping wizard's pure MVU: it opens on a picked file, shows how its layout reads, takes a built-in or kit profile or a new column mapping, and on Attach hands the kit window the profile to attach by and the new profile to save (001 §K 'Column-mapping import wizard'; 001 §O 'Data dialog: preview, column roles, an import-profile picker'; the S9.2 brief: its own view and window; .spec-md §10.3 identify → confirm: nothing is attached or saved until Attach; the shape of step 107's import dialog). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView`, compiled directly after `SetupGridView.fs` (step 283), before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, one `<Compile>` line and no comment; the module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §K and spec 0050 S9.2, and every type, case and field has a one-line doc. (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ImportWizardRequest = { experimentId : Experiments.ExperimentId; file : FileName; readPickedFile : FileName -> Result<LabFileSource, KitError>; kitProfiles : ImportProfile list; defaultProfile : ImportProfileName }`: what the kit window hands the wizard (step 310). (2) `ImportWizardApplied = { experimentId : Experiments.ExperimentId; file : FileName; profile : ImportProfileName; savedOpt : ImportProfile option }`: what Attach chose, the profile to attach the file by and the new profile to save first. (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ImportWizardContext = { request : ImportWizardRequest; onApplied : ImportWizardApplied -> unit; requestClose : unit -> unit }`, in the shape of `ImportDialogContext` (step 107). (4) `WizardProfileChoice` = `PickedImportProfile of ImportProfileName` | `NewColumnMapping`. (5) `ImportWizardModel = { context : ImportWizardContext; source : Result<LabFileSource, KitError>; delimiter : DataDelimiter; header : HeaderRowChoice; bom : ByteOrderMark; choice : WizardProfileChoice; columns : ColumnChoice list; profileName : ControlCaption; lastError : ImportProfileError option }`, with `member this.preview : Result<LabFilePreview, ExperimentDataError>`: the source's `content.kitFileText.previewWith delimiter header` (step 307), or `MalformedDataFileErr` of the read's `describe`. (6) `initImportWizard (context : ImportWizardContext) : ImportWizardModel` reads `context.request.readPickedFile context.request.file`, its one read; an `Ok` source takes its `sniffedLayout` (step 307), any error the comma, a header row and no mark; the choice is `PickedImportProfile context.request.defaultProfile`; `columns` is one `UnmappedColumnRole` choice per column of the preview, numbered from 1 (none when the preview failed); the name is empty and there is no error. (7) `ImportWizardMsg`, each case documented: `SetImportDelimiter of DataDelimiter`, `SetImportHeader of HeaderRowChoice`, `PickImportProfile of ImportProfileName`, `StartColumnMapping`, `SetColumnRole of DataColumnNumber * ColumnRoleChoice`, `SetImportProfileName of ControlCaption`, `ApplyImportWizard` and `CancelImportWizard`. (8) `updateImportWizard (msg : ImportWizardMsg) (m : ImportWizardModel) : ImportWizardModel`. `SetImportDelimiter` and `SetImportHeader` set the layout and remake `columns` over the new preview, each column number that remains keeping its role and a new one `UnmappedColumnRole`. `PickImportProfile name` takes the choice `PickedImportProfile name` when `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName request.kitProfiles name` (step 300) resolves it, a kit profile also setting the layout to its delimiter, header and mark, and is inert otherwise. `StartColumnMapping` takes `NewColumnMapping`. `SetColumnRole (column, role)` replaces that column's role and takes `NewColumnMapping`, and is inert for a column the model lacks. `SetImportProfileName` sets the name. Each of these clears `lastError`. `ApplyImportWizard` is the only message that reaches the context, and is inert while the source is an error: under `PickedImportProfile name` it calls `onApplied { experimentId; file; profile = name; savedOpt = None }` and then `requestClose ()`; under `NewColumnMapping` it takes `ImportProfileName.tryCreate profileName.value` (step 291; `None` is `BlankProfileNameErr` `the profile name is empty`), its `availableAmong request.kitProfiles` (step 299) and `ColumnRoles.tryOfChoices columns` (step 300), and the first error sets `lastError` and applies nothing, while success calls `onApplied` with the profile's name and `savedOpt = Some { name; delimiter; header; bom; roles }`, then `requestClose ()`. `CancelImportWizard` calls `requestClose ()` and nothing else. No other message, option or seam is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs`, `module ImportWizardTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended to the compile list after `ImportDialogTests.fs` with no comment, over a recording context: its request's `experimentId` is `ExperimentId 1`, its `file` a test-local name, its `readPickedFile` answers the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\\n`, its `kitProfiles` hold `Lab scan` (step 299's fixture, written test-locally) and its `defaultProfile` is `Intensity series`; `onApplied` and `requestClose` are recorded. `the wizard opens on the picked file with its sniffed layout and the detector's profile chosen`: `initImportWizard` holds `CommaDelimiter`, `HeaderOnFirstRow`, `ByteOrderMarkPresent`, `PickedImportProfile` of `Intensity series` and five `UnmappedColumnRole` columns numbered 1 to 5. `picking a profile, changing the layout or mapping a column changes nothing outside the wizard`: `PickImportProfile` of `Phone ROI CSV` takes it, of `Lab scan` also sets the layout to `Lab scan`'s, and of `Nope` is inert; `SetImportDelimiter SemicolonDelimiter` leaves one column; and no `onApplied` or close is recorded. `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes`: `PickImportProfile` of `Phone ROI CSV` then `ApplyImportWizard` records one `onApplied` of `ExperimentId 1`, the file, `Phone ROI CSV` and `None`, then one close. `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it`: `SetColumnRole` of column 1 `KeyColumnRole`, 2 `CaptureIndexColumnRole`, 3 `TimestampColumnRole`, 4 `ScanColumnRole (DegreeColumnUnit, RawDialReading)` and 5 `SignalColumnRole`, `SetImportProfileName (ControlCaption \"Phone ROI by columns\")` and `ApplyImportWizard` record one `onApplied` whose `profile` is `Phone ROI by columns` and whose `savedOpt` holds a profile of comma, a header row, the mark, scan column 4 in degrees as a raw dial reading, `SignalColumns (5, None)`, timestamp 3, capture index 2 and key 1, then one close. `a mapping that cannot be a profile is told and nothing is applied`: Attach with an empty name sets `BlankProfileNameErr`, with the name `Intensity series` `BuiltInProfileNameErr`, with `Lab scan` `DuplicateProfileNameErr` and with two signal columns `SignalColumnCountErr`, each recording no `onApplied` and no close. `a picked file that cannot be read offers only Cancel, and Cancel applies nothing`: over a `readPickedFile` answering `KitIoErr`, the source is that error, the model has no column, `ApplyImportWizard` records nothing, and `CancelImportWizard` records one close and no `onApplied`.", "acceptance": "After the wizard's MVU lands, `ImportWizardView` MUST open on a picked file's sniffed layout with the detector's profile chosen and reach its context only on `ApplyImportWizard`, handing the kit window the chosen profile and any new mapping as a profile to save, with a refused mapping told; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the wizard opens on the picked file with its sniffed layout and the detector's profile chosen`, `picking a profile, changing the layout or mapping a column changes nothing outside the wizard`, `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes`, `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it`, `a mapping that cannot be a profile is told and nothing is applied` and `a picked file that cannot be read offers only Cancel, and Cancel applies nothing`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.the wizard opens on the picked file with its sniffed layout and the detector's profile chosen", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.picking a profile, changing the layout or mapping a column changes nothing outside the wizard", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.a mapping that cannot be a profile is told and nothing is applied", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.a picked file that cannot be read offers only Cancel, and Cancel applies nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardRequest", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardApplied", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.WizardProfileChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardMsg", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.initImportWizard", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.updateImportWizard", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-MVU"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 309, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [308], "how_to": "The wizard's view, under stable ids (001 §K: preview, column roles, the profile picker; 001 §O 'Automation: every new control gets a stable id'; .spec-md §10.5: Attach and Cancel share a row with a gap and distinct colours; AGENTS.md: a WrapPanel never sits in a horizontal StackPanel). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs` (step 308): `importWizardView (m : ImportWizardModel) (dispatch : ImportWizardMsg -> unit) : IView` is a `DockPanel`. Docked at the bottom is one horizontal row of `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton ConstructorUiId.importWizardAttachButton (ControlCaption \"Attach\") positiveBackground`, present only while the source read, and `actionButton ConstructorUiId.importWizardCancelButton (ControlCaption \"Cancel\") negativeBackground` (step 107's look), sending `ApplyImportWizard` and `CancelImportWizard`. Above it a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importWizardMessage` shows `lastError`'s caption, or `The file could not be read — <e.describe>` while the source is an error, in `messageColor`, and is absent otherwise. Docked at the top, in a vertical `StackPanel`: a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `importWizardHeading` with `Import <the file's leaf name>` and the line `Nothing is attached until you press Attach.`; a `Layout:` block whose `WrapPanel` holds one box per `DataDelimiter.all` (`importWizardDelimiterChoice delimiter.uiKey`, sending `SetImportDelimiter`) and one per header choice (`importWizardHeaderChoice header.uiKey`, sending `SetImportHeader`), the chosen ones `actionButton`s on `positiveBackground` and the others `verbButton`s, and a `TextBlock` carrying `importWizardBomText` with the mark's caption; a `Profile:` block whose `WrapPanel` holds one box per built-in, in `BuiltInImportProfile.all` order, and per kit profile, in the kit's order, each carrying `importWizardProfileChoice name.uiKey` with the name as its label and sending `PickImportProfile`, then `New column mapping` carrying `importWizardNewMappingButton` and sending `StartColumnMapping`, the chosen one on `positiveBackground`; and, under `NewColumnMapping`, a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Profile name:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `importWizardProfileNameField` that shows `profileName` and sends `SetImportProfileName` at every change. A `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways fills the rest and holds a `Grid` carrying `importWizardPreviewGrid`, one column per preview column: its first row the column's name; under `NewColumnMapping` a second row holding, per column, a `ComboBox` carrying `importWizardColumnRoleChoice column.uiPosition` whose items are the roles' captions (`UnmappedColumnRole`, `ScanColumnRole (DegreeColumnUnit, PhysicalScanValue)`, `SignalColumnRole`, `SigmaColumnRole`, `TimestampColumnRole`, `CaptureIndexColumnRole`, `ObservableColumnRole`, `KeyColumnRole`, `ThroughputColumnRole` and `MuellerElementRole` of each `MuellerElementIndex.all`), the column's role selected (any scan role at the scan item), sending `SetColumnRole`; and, for a column whose role is a scan role, two more `ComboBox`es carrying `importWizardColumnUnitChoice` (`ScanColumnUnit.all`) and `importWizardColumnReadingChoice` (`ScanReading.all`) that send `SetColumnRole` with the new unit or reading; then one row per preview row, a `TextBlock` per cell. A preview error shows its caption in place of the grid. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type DataDelimiter with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`comma`, `semicolon`, `tab`); `type HeaderRowChoice with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`first-row`, `no-header`) and `member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`First row is a header`, `No header row`); `type DataDelimiter with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Comma`, `Semicolon`, `Tab`); `type ByteOrderMark with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Byte-order mark: yes`, `Byte-order mark: no`); `type ImportProfileName with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` and `member this.caption : ControlCaption`, both its text; `type DataColumnNumber with member this.uiPosition : ConstructorUiPosition`, its value; `type ImportProfileError with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its `describe`; `type ColumnRoleChoice with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its `text` (`scan variable` for every scan role); `type ScanColumnUnit with member this.caption : ControlCaption` and `type ScanReading with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, their texts. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a group after the import dialog's (step 107), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S9.2, each with a one-line doc: `importWizardWindow` (`\"ImportWizardWindow\"`), `importWizardHeading` (`\"ImportWizardHeading\"`), `importWizardDelimiterChoice (delimiter : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportWizardDelimiter_{delimiter.value}\"`), `importWizardHeaderChoice (header : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportWizardHeader_{header.value}\"`), `importWizardBomText` (`\"ImportWizardBomText\"`), `importWizardProfileChoice (profile : ConstructorUiKey)` (`$\"ImportWizardProfile_{profile.value}\"`), `importWizardNewMappingButton` (`\"ImportWizardNewMappingButton\"`), `importWizardProfileNameField` (`\"ImportWizardProfileNameField\"`), `importWizardPreviewGrid` (`\"ImportWizardPreviewGrid\"`), `importWizardColumnRoleChoice (column : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$\"ImportWizardColumnRole_{column.value}\"`), `importWizardColumnUnitChoice (column : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$\"ImportWizardColumnUnit_{column.value}\"`), `importWizardColumnReadingChoice (column : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$\"ImportWizardColumnReading_{column.value}\"`), `importWizardMessage` (`\"ImportWizardMessage\"`), `importWizardAttachButton` (`\"ImportWizardAttachButton\"`), `importWizardCancelButton` (`\"ImportWizardCancelButton\"`). No other id is added. Tests, in `ImportWizardTests` (step 308): `the import wizard UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the fifteen ids' texts, the parameterised ones over `comma`, `Phone ROI CSV` and position 4. `the wizard shows the sniffed layout, every profile and the preview, with Attach and Cancel in one row`: `importWizardView` over the class's opened model, mounted headless as `ImportDialogTests` mounts the import dialog's view (step 107), shows the heading naming the file, the comma choice on the positive background, the byte-order-mark caption, profile choices for the four built-ins and `Lab scan` and `importWizardNewMappingButton`, and the preview grid holding the five column names and both rows' cells; `importWizardAttachButton` and `importWizardCancelButton` have equal tops, Cancel to the right of Attach with a gap between them. `a new column mapping shows a role per column, and a scan role its unit and reading`: after `StartColumnMapping` and `SetColumnRole` of column 4 to a scan role, the grid holds a role choice for each of the five columns and a unit and a reading choice for column 4 alone, and `importWizardProfileNameField` is present; before it, neither is. `a refused Attach shows its reason in the wizard`: after Attach with an empty name, `importWizardMessage` shows `the import profile name is blank`.", "acceptance": "After the view lands, `importWizardView` MUST show the heading, the layout choices and the mark, every profile, the preview grid with a role per column under a new mapping, and Attach and Cancel in one row, under the fifteen stable `ConstructorUiId` members; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import wizard UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the wizard shows the sniffed layout, every profile and the preview, with Attach and Cancel in one row`, `a new column mapping shows a role per column, and a scan role its unit and reading` and `a refused Attach shows its reason in the wizard`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.the import wizard UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.the wizard shows the sniffed layout, every profile and the preview, with Attach and Cancel in one row", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.a new column mapping shows a role per column, and a scan role its unit and reading", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.a refused Attach shows its reason in the wizard", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.importWizardView", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardHeading", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardDelimiterChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardHeaderChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardBomText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardProfileChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardNewMappingButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardProfileNameField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardPreviewGrid", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardColumnRoleChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardColumnUnitChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardColumnReadingChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardMessage", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardAttachButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.importWizardCancelButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.DataDelimiter.uiKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.HeaderRowChoice.uiKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ImportProfileName.uiKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ColumnRoleChoice.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ImportProfileError.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number":310,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S92m","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[309],"how_to":"The kit window attaches a file through the wizard, by semantic messages (001 §P `AttachDataFile`; 001 §K: a named profile is saved in `.kit-json`; the S9.2 brief: AttachDataFile takes the file, copies it in or records it in place (S4.2), applies a profile and gives mapped points; .spec-md §4 'UI': the button and the test send the same message, and the window hosts a new surface through messages). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2: (1) `KitWindowShell` (steps 186, 201, 225) gains `openImportWizard : ImportWizardRequest -> unit` (opens the wizard over a request, step 311), documented in one line; `inert` holds `ignore`, and every shell built as an update of `inert` (step 201) is unchanged. (2) `AttachDataFileTo` (steps 135, 291, 295) is renamed `AttachDataFile of Experiments.ExperimentId * FileName * ImportProfileName` (attach the picked file and map it by that profile), its doc saying so: its arm records `profile` from the message where it recorded the detector's `builtInProfile`, with `rows = AllDataRows`, and everything else in it — the read-only guard (step 185), the attach, the record, the badge and the refusal's `kitStatus` (step 295) — is unchanged. (3) New messages, each documented in one line and behind the read-only guard of step 185 (`The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.`, nothing opened or written): `OpenImportWizard of Experiments.ExperimentId * FileName`, the Attach data file… button's message after its file dialog: for an experiment the collection holds, it calls `model.kitShell.openImportWizard { experimentId; file; readPickedFile = model.experimentData.readPickedFile; kitProfiles = model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles; defaultProfile = (detectorKindOf model.library <the experiment's slots>).builtInProfile }` (steps 291, 305) and answers the model unchanged; an experiment it lacks changes nothing. `SaveImportProfile of ImportProfile`, the wizard's new mapping: `model.kit.kitFile.withImportProfile` (step 299), whose `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved — <e.describe>` and writes nothing, and whose `Ok kitFile` is written by `model.kit.saveKitFile kitFile` (step 131): `Ok kit` makes `model.kit` that context and `kitStatus` `Saved the import profile '<name>'.`, and `Error e` keeps the model and sets `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`, as `SaveNamingTemplate` does (step 273). The window's own write is not a change offered for reload (step 130). (4) `type ImportWizardApplied with member this.messages : TableAndElementRotationMsg list`, the wizard's Attach as the window's messages: `SaveImportProfile p` when `savedOpt` is `Some p`, then `AttachDataFile (experimentId, file, profile)`, so a new profile is in the kit before a file is mapped by it. (5) `attachDataFileButton` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton`, steps 135, 241) sends `OpenImportWizard (experiment.id, file)` on a confirmed pick where it sent `AttachDataFileTo`; the picker and its folder memory are unchanged. No other message, field or option is added. Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184), over a folder kit holding an experiment `E1` (a one-axis R1 scan over 0…360°, as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:filledExperiments` builds one) loaded into `initInverse` with a recording shell: `Save import profile writes the wizard's new mapping into the kit file and refuses a name the kit holds`: `SaveImportProfile` of a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column) leaves `model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles` and `readKitFile ()` holding it and `kitStatus` `Saved the import profile 'Lab scan'.`, and a second send sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not saved —` and holding `already holds`, the `.kit-json` bytes unchanged. `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default`: after `SaveImportProfile` of `Lab scan`, `OpenImportWizard (ExperimentId 1, <a test-local file>)` records one request with that id and file, `kitProfiles` holding `Lab scan` and `defaultProfile` `Intensity series`, and leaves the model unchanged. `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it`: `messages` of an applied `{ ExperimentId 1; <a Phone ROI file written outside the kit as the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\\n`>; Phone ROI by columns; Some <a test-local profile `Phone ROI by columns`: comma, a header row, the mark, scan column 4 in degrees as a physical value, `SignalColumns (5, None)`, timestamp 3, capture index 2, key 1> }` are `[ SaveImportProfile <it>; AttachDataFile (ExperimentId 1, <the file>, Phone ROI by columns) ]`; passed through the update in order, they leave the kit file holding the profile, E1's `dataOpt` holding an attachment at `data/<the file's leaf>` mapped by `Phone ROI by columns` over every row, its file read back through `readExperiments` holding the same, and `model.dataBadgeOf E1` `ValidatedDataBadge` of 2 points. `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` (step 185) also sends `OpenImportWizard`, `SaveImportProfile` and `AttachDataFile`, with its assertions and an empty shell recorder. `InverseConstructorTests`: every `AttachDataFileTo` it dispatches becomes `AttachDataFile` with `ImportProfileName.intensitySeries`, or `ellipsometricSeries` for the ellipsometric fixture, every assertion kept (`attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why`); `the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path` is renamed `the profile the wizard chose selects the ellipsometric read`, dispatching `ellipsometricSeries`, its assertions kept. `DataFilePickerFolderTests` passes as written. After this step `git grep -n -F \"AttachDataFileTo\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.","acceptance":"After the kit window attaches through the wizard, `OpenImportWizard` MUST hand the shell a request with the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default, `SaveImportProfile` MUST write a new profile into the kit file and refuse a held or built-in name, `AttachDataFile` MUST attach the file by the profile it names, `ImportWizardApplied.messages` MUST save before it attaches, a read-only kit MUST refuse all three, and `git grep -n -F \"AttachDataFileTo\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Save import profile writes the wizard's new mapping into the kit file and refuses a name the kit holds`, `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default` and `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including the renamed `the profile the wizard chose selects the ellipsometric read` and the changed `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why`, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Save import profile writes the wizard's new mapping into the kit file and refuses a name the kit holds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.the profile the wizard chose selects the ellipsometric read","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.AttachDataFileTo","op":"retire","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"],"preserves_obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.AttachDataFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.OpenImportWizard","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SaveImportProfile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ImportWizardApplied.messages","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S92-ATTACH-WITH-PROFILE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 311, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92n", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [310], "how_to": "The wizard's own window, and the shell that opens it over the kit window's dispatch (the S9.2 brief: its own view and window, `keepOnScreen`, `ScrollExtentTests`; .spec-md §4 'UI': every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `KitWindowView.fs` (step 188), one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §K and spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `type ImportWizardWindow(request : ImportWizardRequest, onApplied : ImportWizardApplied -> unit)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `ImportDialogWindow` does (step 108). Its title is `Import data file`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.importWizardWindow`; it asks for 1000 × 700 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`). It runs `Program.mkProgram` over `initImportWizard`, `updateImportWizard` and `importWizardView` (steps 308, 309) with the context `{ request = request; onApplied = onApplied; requestClose = this.Close }`. Closing it any other way than Attach applies nothing. (2) After it, `module ImportWizardOpening` holds `type KitWindowShell with member this.withImportWizard (owner : Window) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : KitWindowShell`, with a one-line doc: the shell whose `openImportWizard` shows an `ImportWizardWindow` over the request, owned by `owner` (`Show owner`), whose `onApplied` dispatches `applied.messages` (step 310) in order. No other member is added. Tests. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the import wizard leaves everything reachable`: over a request reading a test-local lab file of twelve comma columns and forty rows, with `onApplied` `ignore`, `assertReachable \"ImportWizard\"` over an `ImportWizardWindow` of it, and `assertReachable \"ImportWizard (mapping)\"` over a `HostWindow` running `Program.mkSimple` of the model `initImportWizard` opens on it taken by `StartColumnMapping` and `SetColumnRole` of column 12 to a scan role, with `updateImportWizard` and `importWizardView`, as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` hosts a model, so the grid of role, unit and reading choices is wider and taller than the screen. `ImportWizardTests` (step 308) gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: the import wizard window maps a picked file and its Attach reaches the kit window as messages`: over a shown headless owner `Window`, `KitWindowShell.inert.withImportWizard owner <a recording dispatch>`'s `openImportWizard` of the class's request shows a window carrying `importWizardWindow` that holds `importWizardHeading`, `importWizardPreviewGrid`, and `importWizardAttachButton` and `importWizardCancelButton` with equal tops, Cancel right of Attach with a gap; pressing the centre of `importWizardProfileChoice` of `Phone ROI CSV`, then of Attach, as `ImportDialogTests` presses a box, records exactly `[ AttachDataFile (ExperimentId 1, <the file>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv) ]` and closes the window.", "acceptance": "After the window lands, `ImportWizardWindow` MUST call `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and leave everything reachable, and `KitWindowShell.withImportWizard` MUST open it and dispatch its Attach as the kit window's messages; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the import wizard window maps a picked file and its Attach reaches the kit window as messages`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the import wizard leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the import wizard leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-WINDOW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.acceptance: the import wizard window maps a picked file and its Attach reaches the kit window as messages", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-WINDOW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardWindow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-WINDOW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardOpening.KitWindowShell.withImportWizard", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardWindow.fs", "obligations": ["S92-WIZARD-WINDOW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number":312,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-S92o","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[311],"how_to":"The constructor windows compose the wizard, and the section is proved end to end through the kit window and a real folder (the S9.2 brief; .spec-md §3.13: AT-2 writes its observation files through the Mueller-matrix profile; AGENTS.md: wait for deterministic conditions, drive by id). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (steps 189, 233): the shell it builds is followed by `.withImportWizard window dispatch` (step 311), over the dispatch it captures from its init command, and the file opens `OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardOpening`, so a constructor window's Attach data file… opens the real wizard over itself. Its doc says so in no more words; nothing else in it changes. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs` (steps 184, 297) gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: Attach data file maps a picked lab file through the wizard into the kit and validates it`: over a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write through `openKitAt`, holding experiment `E1` (a one-axis R1 scan over 0…360°, as step 310's facts record it) and loaded into `initInverse`, the fact keeps the model and dispatches through `updateTableAndElementRotation`, its shell being `KitWindowShell.inert.withImportWizard <a shown headless host Window> <that dispatch>`, as `mount` composes it. `OpenImportWizard (ExperimentId 1, <a Phone ROI file written outside the kit as the bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5\\nCPL-(AIR#0)-CPL,1,2026-07-15T12:05:00+00:00,45,912.25\\n`>)` shows a window carrying `importWizardWindow`; pressing `importWizardProfileChoice` of `Phone ROI CSV` and then `importWizardAttachButton` at their centres closes it and leaves E1's `dataOpt` an attachment at `data/<the file's leaf>` mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` over every row, the kit folder holding that file with exactly the picked bytes, E1's file read back through `readExperiments` holding the same mapped attachment, and `model.dataBadgeOf E1`'s text `validated (2 points)`. (3) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'An experiment is a scan over a setup revision' (step 297), one bullet of at most six lines: **Lab files are read through import profiles** (`ImportProfiles.fs`, `LabFileImport.fs`, spec 0050 S9.2): an experiment's data is a kit file, a profile name and a row selection; a profile is a built-in (`Intensity series`, `Ellipsometric series`, `Phone ROI CSV`, `Mueller-matrix observations`, each calling its parser) or a named column mapping in `.kit-json`, never replaced once saved; `ChosenImportProfile.mapText` is the one read and `MappedPoints.validatedFor` the one validation; the app writes only observation files (`KeyedObservation.observationFileText`); Attach data file… opens the wizard, whose Attach sends `SaveImportProfile` then `AttachDataFile`. Nothing else in the file changes.","acceptance":"After the wizard is wired, the constructor windows' shell MUST open the real wizard over the window's dispatch, a picked lab file MUST be mapped through the wizard into the kit, attached and validated end to end, and AGENTS.md MUST carry the gotcha 'Lab files are read through import profiles'; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: Attach data file maps a picked lab file through the wizard into the kit and validates it`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","AGENTS.md"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: Attach data file maps a picked lab file through the wizard into the kit and validates it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S92-WIZARD-WIRED"]}],"contracts":[],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number":313,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S93a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[312],"how_to":"The experiment file records the exclusions of its data's points and the corrections of its setup, each with its reason or audit note (001 §K 'Raw data is immutable; exclusions carry a reason and stay visible in plots, marked'; 001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact (e.g. \"LR was at −45\"), with a mandatory audit note'; 001 §E 'Lab files are read-only for the app. Exclusions, corrections and mappings live in the experiment file'; the S9.3 brief; the S9.2 mapper's request: `MappedRow` carries no row number, so an exclusion numbers its point). This is one step because the two records' new fields change every consumer at once (the step 261 precedent); the messages that set them are steps 315 and 316. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, directly before `MappedAttachment` (step 291): (a) `MappedPointNumber of int` with `.value`, a point's 1-based place among the points its attachment's row selection keeps, in file order (the answer of `ExperimentDataProxy.readMapped`, step 305): `static member tryCreate (number : int) : MappedPointNumber option` answers `None` below 1. (b) `ExclusionReason of string` with `.value`: `static member tryCreate (text : string) : ExclusionReason option` keeps the text as given and answers `None` for an empty or white-space text. (c) `PointExclusion = { point : MappedPointNumber; reason : ExclusionReason }`. No int tag is added: none of them is a closed set. (2) `MappedAttachment` gains `exclusions : PointExclusion list` after `rows`: its exclusions in point order, at most one per point. An exclusion belongs to the mapped attachment because it numbers that attachment's points: attaching a file anew builds a new mapped attachment, which starts with none. On `MappedAttachment`: `member this.withExclusion (exclusion : PointExclusion) : MappedAttachment` (that point's exclusion replaced, or the new one inserted in point order), `member this.withoutExclusion (point : MappedPointNumber) : MappedAttachment` (that point's exclusion removed; the attachment unchanged when it has none) and `member this.tryFindExclusion (point : MappedPointNumber) : PointExclusion option`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, after `ExperimentNotes` (step 285): `CorrectionNote of string` with `.value` and `static member tryCreate (text : string) : CorrectionNote option` (`None` for an empty or white-space text); `SetupCorrection = { previous : SetupReference; corrected : SetupReference; note : CorrectionNote }`, one re-pointing of the experiment's setup and why it was made. `Experiment` gains `corrections : SetupCorrection list` after `dataOpt`, oldest first. `commit` (step 290) gives an appended experiment `[]` and keeps an edited one's, so an edit never loses its audit trail. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json` (steps 288, 290, 291), schema version 1 kept (no kit of the old shape exists outside test output, .spec-md §7): a non-null `dataOpt` holds exactly `attachment`, `profile`, `rows` and `exclusions`, an array of objects holding exactly `point` (an integer from 1) and `reason` (a string holding a non-white-space character); `experiment` also holds `corrections`, an array of objects holding exactly `previous` and `corrected` (each the object `experiment.setup` is, step 261) and `note` (a string holding a non-white-space character). `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`: `copyExperimentsFrom` (steps 224, 261, 291, 306) keeps each copied experiment's exclusions and corrections as written; only its id, its name and its attachment's path are given anew, as before. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the `AttachDataFile` arm (step 310) builds its mapped attachment with `exclusions = []`; nothing else in the window changes. (6) Every fixture that builds a `MappedAttachment` sets `exclusions = []`, and every fixture that builds an `Experiment` sets `corrections = []`, every fact keeping its assertions: in `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`, `KitContentFileJsonTests`, `KitLibraryTests`, `ExperimentCopyTests`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`, `SetupTests`, `SetupModelTests`, `KitWindowModelTests`, `ExperimentDataProxyTests`, `ExperimentDataStoreTests`, `ExperimentModelTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `InverseConstructorTests` and `KitWindowTests`, whichever of them build one. No other field, member or option is added. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `a point exclusion needs a point from 1 and a reason, and an attachment keeps one exclusion per point in point order`: `MappedPointNumber.tryCreate` of 1 and 7 keeps them and of 0 and −1 answers `None`; `ExclusionReason.tryCreate \"cosmic ray\"` keeps the text and `\"\"` and `\"  \"` answer `None`; a test-local mapped attachment with no exclusion, `withExclusion` of point 3 (`cosmic ray`) then of point 1 (`shutter`) holds points 1 and 3 in that order; `withExclusion` of point 3 with `stray light` replaces its reason and keeps two exclusions; `tryFindExclusion` of 3 answers it and of 2 `None`; `withoutExclusion` of 1 leaves point 3 alone, and of 2 the attachment unchanged. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `a correction note refuses a blank text, and a committed experiment starts with no correction and keeps its corrections through an edit`: `CorrectionNote.tryCreate \"LR was at -45\"` keeps the text and `\"  \"` answers `None`; `commit` of a target over `Bench` revision 1 appends an experiment with `corrections = []`; that experiment given one test-local correction (`Bench` revision 1 → `Plate` revision 1, `LR was at -45`) through a `with` copy and stored back (`withStoredExperiment`, step 294), then `edit` and `commit` of a target over `Bench` revision 1 keep the correction. `KitContentFileJsonTests` (steps 146, 261, 288, 291): `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text` also round-trips E1 whose data excludes point 3 for `cosmic ray` and whose corrections hold `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL` revision 1 → `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` revision 1 with the note `LR was at -45`; `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` also refuses an exclusion of point 0, an exclusion whose reason is `\"  \"`, a `dataOpt` without `exclusions`, an experiment without `corrections` and a correction without `note`. `ExperimentCopyTests` (step 291): `a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection` also finds the copied experiment's exclusion of point 2 (`saturated`) and its one correction as written.","acceptance":"After the two records gain their fields, a mapped attachment MUST hold its point exclusions (a point from 1 and a non-blank reason, one per point, in point order) and an experiment its setup corrections (previous, corrected and a non-blank note, oldest first), the experiment file MUST round-trip both and refuse a malformed one, a commit MUST start an experiment with no correction and an edit keep them, and a copy MUST keep both; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a point exclusion needs a point from 1 and a reason, and an attachment keeps one exclusion per point in point order` and `a correction note refuses a blank text, and a committed experiment starts with no correction and keeps its corrections through an edit`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` and `a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a point exclusion needs a point from 1 and a reason, and an attachment keeps one exclusion per point in point order","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a correction note refuses a blank text, and a committed experiment starts with no correction and keeps its corrections through an edit","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.MappedPointNumber","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ExclusionReason","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.PointExclusion","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.MappedAttachment.withExclusion","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.MappedAttachment.withoutExclusion","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.MappedAttachment.tryFindExclusion","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.MappedAttachment","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.CorrectionNote","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.SetupCorrection","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs","obligations":["S93-EXCLUSION-CORRECTION-SHAPES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 314, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [313], "how_to": "An excluded point stays in the data and leaves what is validated, and the badge says how many are excluded (001 §K 'Raw data is immutable; exclusions carry a reason …'; 001 §K 'Status badges: no data / mapped / validated (points) / excluded points / data changed / out of range'; the S9.1 mapper's request: the excluded-points badge joins `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck`). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `selectedBy` (step 305): `type MappedPoints with member this.keptBy (exclusions : PointExclusion list) : MappedPoints`, the points in order without those whose `MappedPointNumber` (step 313) an exclusion names, the case kept: `SeriesPoints` keeps its series' kind (`IntensityData` or `EllipsometricData`, `MeasuredData.fs:MeasuredSeries`) over the kept points, and each list case its kept items; an exclusion naming no point changes nothing. It is the one rule from an attachment's exclusions to the points a validation reads, and the one a study's residual reads in S11. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` (steps 291, 304, 305) is `dataProxy.readMapped data`, then `keptBy data.exclusions`, then `validatedFor` as before, so an excluded point is never out of range and never counted as validated. `ExperimentDataBadge` (step 295) gains `ExcludedPointsBadge of kept : MeasuredPointCount * excluded : MeasuredPointCount` after `ValidatedDataBadge`, its `text` `excluded points (<k> excluded, <n> validated)`; `ofCheck` answers it, in place of `ValidatedDataBadge`, for an `Ok points` outcome of a mapped attachment whose `exclusions` are not empty, `kept` being the points' `pointCount` and `excluded` the number of exclusions; every other branch, and its order, is unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `ExperimentDataBadge.caption` (step 295) answers `Loaded — <n> point(s) kept, <k> excluded` for it, every other caption unchanged. The two callers of `loadAndValidate` are authorized and nothing in them changes: `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, whose `model.dataBadgeOf` and one private validation function (steps 295, 304) already pass the experiment's mapped attachment to `ofCheck`, and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`), which counts the validated points it answers. No other member, case or option is added. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` (step 300) gains `kept points leave out the excluded ones and keep the rest in order`: over a two-point intensity series, three Phone ROI rows and three `Lab scan` rows (step 300's test-local fixtures), excluding point 2 keeps points 1 and 3 of each list in order and the series' first point as an `IntensityData` series; no exclusion keeps each whole; and an exclusion of point 9 changes nothing. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation` (steps 295, 304) also answers `ExcludedPointsBadge (MeasuredPointCount 2, MeasuredPointCount 1)` for an attachment excluding one point whose outcome is `Ok` of two points, whose `text` is `excluded points (1 excluded, 2 validated)`, and keeps `DataChangedBadge` ahead of it for a changed file; and it gains `loading data validates the kept points, so an excluded point outside the range does not refuse the data`: over its mock (step 305), answering for a test-local attachment the canned three-point intensity series `0 → 1.0`, `45 → 0.5`, `90 → 0.0`, step 288's one-axis experiment over R1 0…45° answers `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming `90` with no exclusion, and `Ok (SeriesPoints _)` of two points when the attachment excludes point 3 (`beam blocked`).", "acceptance": "After kept points land, `MappedPoints.keptBy` MUST leave out exactly the excluded points, `loadAndValidate` MUST validate only the kept points, and `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` MUST answer `ExcludedPointsBadge` (kept and excluded counts) for validated data with exclusions, its caption `Loaded — <n> point(s) kept, <k> excluded`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `kept points leave out the excluded ones and keep the rest in order` and `loading data validates the kept points, so an excluded point outside the range does not refuse the data`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.kept points leave out the excluded ones and keep the rest in order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-KEPT-POINTS-BADGE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.loading data validates the kept points, so an excluded point outside the range does not refuse the data", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-KEPT-POINTS-BADGE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-KEPT-POINTS-BADGE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MappedPoints.keptBy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S93-KEPT-POINTS-BADGE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-KEPT-POINTS-BADGE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.ExperimentDataBadge", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S93-KEPT-POINTS-BADGE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 315, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [314], "how_to": "The Data step reviews one experiment's points, and a point is excluded with a reason, or taken back, by semantic messages that write the experiment file (001 §P `ExcludePoint`; 001 §O 'Data dialog: … per-point exclusion with a reason'; 001 §K 'Raw data is immutable'; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message; .spec-md §10.5: an exclusion is taken back by `IncludePoint`, its undo). The views that send them are step 325's. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3: (1) Before the model: `ReviewedData = { experimentId : Experiments.ExperimentId; points : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError> }`, the experiment the Data step reviews and every point of its data as read, the excluded ones included, so that they stay visible; and `DataStepDraft = { exclusionReason : ControlCaption; correctionNote : ControlCaption }`, the texts of the Data step's two fields, with `static member empty : DataStepDraft` (both blank). `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `reviewedDataOpt : ReviewedData option` and `dataDraft : DataStepDraft`, each with a one-line doc; `initWith` sets `None` and `DataStepDraft.empty`. (2) Messages, each documented in one line: `ReviewExperimentData of Experiments.ExperimentId` (review an experiment's data): for an experiment the collection holds, `reviewedDataOpt` becomes `Some { experimentId; points }` with `points` = `model.experimentData.readMapped data` (step 305) for its `dataOpt = Some data`, and `Error (EmptyDataFileErr \"<name> has no data file\")` for `None`; an experiment the collection lacks changes nothing. It reads and writes nothing else, so a read-only kit reviews too. `SetExclusionReason of ControlCaption` sets `dataDraft.exclusionReason`, writing nothing. `ExcludePoint of Experiments.ExperimentId * MappedPointNumber * ControlCaption` (exclude that point of the experiment's data for that reason) and `IncludePoint of Experiments.ExperimentId * MappedPointNumber` (take the point's exclusion back) are each refused by the read-only guard of step 185, which every write message calls. (3) `ExcludePoint (id, point, reason)`: an experiment the collection lacks changes nothing; a reason `ExclusionReason.tryCreate` refuses sets `kitStatus` to `Not excluded — an exclusion needs a reason.`; an experiment with no data `Not excluded — <name> has no data file.`; a `readMapped data` error `Not excluded — <e.caption>`; a point above the read points' `pointCount` `Not excluded — <name> has <n> point(s).`; each of these writes nothing. Otherwise the experiment whose `dataOpt` is `Some (data.withExclusion { point; reason })` (step 313) is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (step 261): on `Ok` the collection takes it (`withStoredExperiment`, step 294), its badge is computed again by the one private validation function (steps 136, 295), `reviewedDataOpt` is read again when it reviews this experiment, and `kitStatus` is `Excluded point <n> of <name>: <reason>.`; on `Error e` the model is kept with `kitStatus` `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `IncludePoint (id, point)`: an experiment the collection lacks, or whose data holds no exclusion of that point, changes nothing and writes nothing; otherwise `data.withoutExclusion point` is recorded and taken the same way, with `kitStatus` `Included point <n> of <name> again.`. Neither message changes the lab file, the attachment, the profile or the row selection. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `ExperimentModelTests` (step 292), over its folder kit with `E1` committed over the polarizer's R1 with the draft's range 0…90° and a test-local intensity file `angle_deg,intensity\\n0,1.0\\n45,0.5\\n90,0.0\\n` written outside the kit attached by `AttachDataFile (ExperimentId 1, <it>, ImportProfileName.intensitySeries)`: `reviewing an experiment's data reads every point, the excluded ones included, and writes nothing`: `ReviewExperimentData (ExperimentId 1)` leaves `reviewedDataOpt` holding E1 and `Ok (SeriesPoints _)` of three points, and every file's bytes unchanged; after `ExcludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 2, ControlCaption \"beam blocked\")` it still holds three points; `ReviewExperimentData (ExperimentId 9)` changes nothing. `ExcludePoint records a point's exclusion and its reason in the experiment file, and IncludePoint takes it back`: that `ExcludePoint` leaves E1's data excluding point 2 for `beam blocked`, the `E1.experiment-json` read back through `readExperiments` holding the same, the attached file's bytes unchanged, `model.dataBadgeOf E1` `ExcludedPointsBadge (2, 1)` and `kitStatus` `Excluded point 2 of E1: beam blocked.`; then `IncludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 2)` leaves no exclusion in the model and the file, the badge `ValidatedDataBadge` of 3 points, and a second `IncludePoint` writes nothing. `an exclusion without a reason, of a point the data lacks, or of an experiment without data writes nothing`: `ExcludePoint` with the reason `\"  \"`, of point 4, and of `E2` (committed with no data) each set the `kitStatus` above and leave every file's bytes unchanged. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 294, 310): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `ExcludePoint` and `IncludePoint`, with its assertions.", "acceptance": "After the review and exclusion messages land, `ReviewExperimentData` MUST read every point of an experiment's data and write nothing, `ExcludePoint` MUST record a point's exclusion with its non-blank reason in the experiment file and `IncludePoint` take it back, each refused typed for a blank reason, a point the data lacks, an experiment without data and a read-only kit, the lab file never changing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `reviewing an experiment's data reads every point, the excluded ones included, and writes nothing`, `ExcludePoint records a point's exclusion and its reason in the experiment file, and IncludePoint takes it back` and `an exclusion without a reason, of a point the data lacks, or of an experiment without data writes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.reviewing an experiment's data reads every point, the excluded ones included, and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.ExcludePoint records a point's exclusion and its reason in the experiment file, and IncludePoint takes it back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.an exclusion without a reason, of a point the data lacks, or of an experiment without data writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ReviewedData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.DataStepDraft", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.reviewedDataOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.dataDraft", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ReviewExperimentData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetExclusionReason", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ExcludePoint", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.IncludePoint", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-POINT-EXCLUSION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 316, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [315], "how_to": "Correcting an experiment's setup after the fact, with a mandatory audit note, as a semantic message (001 §P `CorrectSetup`; 001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact (e.g. \"LR was at −45\"), with a mandatory audit note'; the S9.3 brief: the lab file is untouched; the S9.1 mapper's request: CorrectSetup re-points `Experiment.setup`, an edit keeping the name). The view that sends it is step 326's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, beside `withRole` (step 294): `type Experiment with member this.correctedTo (setup : SetupReference) (note : CorrectionNote) : Experiment`, the experiment over `setup` whose `corrections` end with `{ previous = this.setup; corrected = setup; note }` (step 313); its name, scan, role, session, notes and data are unchanged, so a lab file keyed by its name still matches it. Pinning follows: the corrected setup's revision is pinned by `Setup.pinFor` (step 261) because the experiment now references it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `SetCorrectionNote of ControlCaption` sets `dataDraft.correctionNote` (step 315), writing nothing; `CorrectSetup of Experiments.ExperimentId * SetupReference * ControlCaption` (re-point the experiment to that setup revision, for that note), each with a one-line doc, refused by the read-only guard of step 185. Its arm: an experiment the collection lacks changes nothing; a note `CorrectionNote.tryCreate` refuses sets `kitStatus` to `Not corrected — a correction needs an audit note.`; a reference no setup of `model.kitSetups` answers at its revision (`slotsAt`, step 256) `Not corrected — the kit holds no setup <reference.describe>.`; the experiment's own reference `Not corrected — <name> already references <reference.describe>.`; each writes nothing. Otherwise `experiment.correctedTo reference note` is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (step 261): on `Ok` the collection takes it (`withStoredExperiment`), its badge is computed again by the one private validation function (the detector may differ in the corrected slots), `reviewedDataOpt` is read again when it reviews this experiment, and `kitStatus` is `Corrected <name>: <previous.describe> → <reference.describe> (<note>).`; on `Error e` the model is kept with `kitStatus` `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. Nothing reads or writes the lab file, and the experiment keeps its name and its file. No other message, field or option is added. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `a correction re-points the experiment's setup and appends the audit entry, its name and data unchanged`: a test-local experiment named `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL` over `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL` revision 1 with a mapped attachment, `correctedTo` `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` revision 1 with the note `LR was at -45` is over that reference, its corrections holding exactly that entry, and its name, scan, role and data equal to before; a second correction back appends a second entry after it. `ExperimentModelTests` (step 292), over its folder kit with `E1` committed over `Setup 1` and the polarizer then turned to R1 30° and recorded by `CreateSetup` as `Bench B` (step 260), E1's data attached as step 315 attaches it: `CorrectSetup re-points the experiment to a setup of the kit with its audit note, and the lab file and the experiment's name are untouched`: `CorrectSetup (ExperimentId 1, <Bench B revision 1>, ControlCaption \"LP1 was at 30\")` leaves E1 over `Bench B` revision 1 with one correction from `Setup 1` revision 1 and that note, `E1.experiment-json` read back holding the same, the name `E1`, the attached file's bytes unchanged and `kitStatus` `Corrected E1: 'Setup 1' revision 1 → 'Bench B' revision 1 (LP1 was at 30).`. `a correction without a note, to a setup the kit lacks, or to the setup it already references writes nothing`: `CorrectSetup` with the note `\"  \"`, to `Gone` revision 1, and to `Setup 1` revision 1 while E1 is over it each set the `kitStatus` above and leave every file's bytes unchanged. `KitWindowModelTests`: `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `CorrectSetup`, with its assertions.", "acceptance": "After `CorrectSetup` lands, it MUST re-point an experiment to a setup revision the kit holds and append the audit entry (previous, corrected, non-blank note) to its file, its name, scan and data unchanged and the lab file untouched, refused typed for a blank note, an unknown or unchanged setup and a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a correction re-points the experiment's setup and appends the audit entry, its name and data unchanged`, `CorrectSetup re-points the experiment to a setup of the kit with its audit note, and the lab file and the experiment's name are untouched` and `a correction without a note, to a setup the kit lacks, or to the setup it already references writes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a correction re-points the experiment's setup and appends the audit entry, its name and data unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SETUP-CORRECTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.CorrectSetup re-points the experiment to a setup of the kit with its audit note, and the lab file and the experiment's name are untouched", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SETUP-CORRECTION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.a correction without a note, to a setup the kit lacks, or to the setup it already references writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SETUP-CORRECTION"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SETUP-CORRECTION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.correctedTo", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SETUP-CORRECTION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetCorrectionNote", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SETUP-CORRECTION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CorrectSetup", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SETUP-CORRECTION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 317, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [316], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests"], "how_to": "One file splits into groups by its key column, as pure Domain (001 §K 'One file → many experiments: split by a key column'; 001 §P `SplitByColumn`; the S9.2 mapper's request: a split group is a `KeyedDataRows` of one `MappedAttachment`, and `MappedPoints.selectedBy` is the selection). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, before `selectedBy` (step 305): `type MuellerExperimentLabel with member this.rowKey : DataRowKey`, a Phone ROI row's experiment label as the key it is selected by (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerExperimentLabel`; `MuellerReconstruction.fs` itself is not edited); and `type MappedPoints with member this.pointKeys : DataRowKey option list`, each point's key in point order: `None` for every point of a `SeriesPoints`, the label's `rowKey` for a capture row, the observation's `key`, and a mapped row's `keyOpt`. `selectedBy` keeps its contract and its texts and finds the points of `KeyedDataRows key` as those whose `pointKeys` entry is `Some key`, so one reading of a point's key remains. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs`: `module DataSplits` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ExperimentDataLoad.fs` (step 304), the last Domain file, because it reads mapped points, experiments, setups and the naming template: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §K and spec 0050 S9.3. In this order: (a) `SplitKeyColumn of string` with `.value`, the column a file is split by, as the split names it. (b) `type ChosenImportProfile with member this.splitKeyOpt : SplitKeyColumn option` (step 300): `experiment` for `PhoneRoiCsvProfile` (the label column `parseMuellerCsv` reads), `sample` for `MuellerObservationProfile` (the key column of the observation file, step 301), `column <n>` for a kit profile whose roles map the key to column n (`roles.keyOpt`, step 299), and `None` for the two X,Y built-ins and a kit profile with no key column. (c) `KeyedGroup = { key : DataRowKey; points : MeasuredPointCount }`, one group of a split file. (d) `type MappedPoints with member this.splitGroups : Result<KeyedGroup list, ExperimentDataError>`: the distinct `Some` keys of `pointKeys` in order of first appearance, each with the number of points holding it; a point without a key belongs to no group. A `SeriesPoints` answers `MalformedDataFileErr` `an X,Y data file has no key column to split by`, and `ColumnPoints` none of whose rows holds a key `MalformedDataFileErr` `the import profile maps no key column to split by`. A group's points are exactly what `selectedBy (KeyedDataRows key)` keeps. No other type, member, cache or option is added. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` (step 300) gains `a point's key is the one selection reads, and a selection keeps the points of its key`: over Phone ROI rows labelled `K1`, `K2`, `K1`, the observations keyed `K1` and `K2`, `Lab scan` rows keyed `K1`, none and `K2` (test-local), and a two-point intensity series, `pointKeys` answers `[Some K1; Some K2; Some K1]`, `[Some K1; Some K2]`, `[Some K1; None; Some K2]` and `[None; None]`, and `selectedBy (KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey \"K1\"))` keeps the two, one and one points `pointKeys` names `K1`, as step 305's fact keeps them; step 305's `a row selection keeps every row or the rows of one key` passes as written. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs`, `module DataSplitTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment: `a file splits into one group per key in first-appearance order, each counting its points`: Phone ROI rows labelled `B`, `A`, `B`, `C`, `A`, `B` split into `B` (3), `A` (2) and `C` (1), in that order; observations keyed `Z-cut`, `Z-cut`, `X-cut` into `Z-cut` (2) and `X-cut` (1); `Lab scan` rows keyed `K1`, none, `K1` into `K1` (2); and an empty `CapturePoints` into no group. `a file without a key column does not split, and a profile names the key column it splits by`: a series answers `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `no key column to split by`, `Lab scan` rows none of which holds a key answer `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `maps no key column`; `splitKeyOpt` of `Phone ROI CSV` is `experiment`, of `Mueller-matrix observations` `sample`, of `Lab scan` `column 4`, of `Intensity series` and `Ellipsometric series` `None`, and of a kit profile with no key column `None`.", "acceptance": "After the split's groups land, `MappedPoints.pointKeys` MUST be the one reading of a point's key that `selectedBy` and `splitGroups` share, `splitGroups` MUST answer one group per key in first-appearance order with its point count and refuse a file without a key column typed, and `ChosenImportProfile.splitKeyOpt` MUST name the key column each profile splits by; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a point's key is the one selection reads, and a selection keeps the points of its key`, `a file splits into one group per key in first-appearance order, each counting its points` and `a file without a key column does not split, and a profile names the key column it splits by`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.a point's key is the one selection reads, and a selection keeps the points of its key", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.a file splits into one group per key in first-appearance order, each counting its points", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.a file without a key column does not split, and a profile names the key column it splits by", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MuellerExperimentLabel.rowKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MappedPoints.pointKeys", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.SplitKeyColumn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.ChosenImportProfile.splitKeyOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.KeyedGroup", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.MappedPoints.splitGroups", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-GROUPS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number":318,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S93f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[317],"how_to":"Each group of a split file is matched to an experiment by the naming template, and an unmatched group the template can read is offered the setup and the experiment its name describes (001 §K 'match each group by the naming template, list the unmatched groups and offer to create setups for them (the template parse supplies slots and angles)'; 001 §P `MatchByTemplate`; the S9.1 mapper's request: an experiment made from a group is named by `experimentNameAmong` with the read name's note, or the key). Nothing is written here: the window applies a split in step 320. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs` (step 317), after `splitGroups`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `type DataRowKey with member this.nameText : NameText`, a key as a name the template reads (step 269), as `MuellerExperimentLabel.nameText` is (step 270); no member converts back (ELEV006). (2) `DataSplitError`, an `*Error` union whose cases carry the error that stopped the group: `SplitKeyTextErr of ExperimentError` (the key is no experiment name, step 286), `SplitKeyNameErr of NamingTemplateError` (the template does not read the key, or the key names no item, steps 268-271), `SplitKeySetupErr of SetupError` (the table cannot hold the key's items and angles, steps 255, 274) and `SplitKeyTwiceErr of reason : string` (an earlier group matched the same experiment), with `member this.describe : string` rendering `the key is no experiment name: <e.describe>`, `the key does not read through the naming template: <e.describe>`, `the table cannot hold the key's setup: <e.describe>` and `two groups match one experiment: <reason>`. (3) `SplitSetupOffer = { setup : Setup; experiment : ExperimentName }`, a setup (held, or new) and the new experiment the group would be attached to; `SplitGroupMatch` = `ExperimentForGroup of experiment : ExperimentName` (the kit's experiment of that name) | `SetupOfferForGroup of offer : SplitSetupOffer` | `GroupWithoutMatch of problem : DataSplitError`; `SplitGroup = { key : DataRowKey; points : MeasuredPointCount; matching : SplitGroupMatch }`; and `DataSplit = { groups : SplitGroup list }`. A split is never stored, so no wire tag is added. (4) `[<ReferenceEquality>] DataSplitParam = { template : NamingTemplate; experiments : Experiment list; setups : Setup list; table : SetupSlot list; items : Item list; choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option }`, the kit's template, experiments, setups and items, the table, and how an item resolves to its model (the window's `tryItemModelChoice`, step 263). (5) `static member DataSplit.ofGroups (param : DataSplitParam) (groups : KeyedGroup list) : DataSplit`, the one matching rule, group by group in order. (a) The key's name: `key.nameText.toExperimentName` (step 286); an error is `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyTextErr e)`. (b) An experiment of `param.experiments` whose `name.fileStem` equals that name's ignoring case (the kit's name identity, step 286) matches: `ExperimentForGroup` of its name, the first in list order. (c) Otherwise `param.template.readName key.nameText` (step 269), an error being `SplitKeyNameErr`; its `writeName` made an `ExperimentName` (the name the template would give, `-(QZ#45.0)-` read back as `-(QZ#45)-`) matches an experiment of that file stem the same way. (d) Otherwise the group is offered: the reading's items are `param.template.itemsOf reading param.items` (step 271), an error being `SplitKeyNameErr`. Over `SetupSlot.inLightOrder param.table` (step 257), every slot whose role a `SlotPlaceholder` of the template's `pieces` names takes a `SlotChoice` (step 274): the item the reading names in that role, or nothing when it names none, turned for an `ObjectSlotRole k` with a read angle to that angle for a `FixedMounting` item and to `sign.physicalAngleOf item.dialZeroAngle angle` for a `DialMounted sign` item (steps 255, 258), so the recorded reading is the name's, and otherwise keeping the slot's `placement.r1`; every other slot is left as the table holds it. A role the reading names and the table has no slot of is `SplitKeySetupErr (UnknownSetupSlotErr <the key and the role's text>)`. The setup is `generate` (step 274) of the grid of those one-choice axes over `param.table`, `param.items`, `param.choiceOf` and `param.template`, held being `param.setups` followed by the setups offered to earlier groups, so two groups whose keys describe one setup are offered the same one; its error is `SplitKeySetupErr`. The experiment is `param.template.experimentNameAmong setup.slots param.items reading.noteOpt taken <the key's name>` (step 286), `taken` being the names of `param.experiments` and of the experiments offered to earlier groups. (e) A group whose matched experiment an earlier group matched is `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyTwiceErr <both keys and the name>)`. Members of `DataSplit`, each a filter of `groups` in order: `this.matched`, `this.offered` and `this.unmatched`. No cache, sort, fuzzy match or other member is added. Tests, in `DataSplitTests` (step 317), over test-local copies of step 271's slots (`src`, `lpA`, `sampleA`, `sampleB`, `lpB`, `det`), items (`Laser`, `CPL1`, `CPL2`, `QZ`, `LR`, `QZd` dial-mounted with its zero at 10°) and template `lab`, with a `choiceOf` answering each item's choice: `a group matches the experiment its key names, as written or as the template writes it back`: with the experiments `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` and `E2`, `ofGroups` of the group `cpl-(qz#45-lr#45)-cpl` alone matches the first by its name, of `CPL-(QZ#45.0-LR#45)-CPL` alone matches it by its written name, and of `e2` matches `E2`. `an unmatched group the template reads is offered its setup and experiment over the table's slots`: with no experiment and no held setup, `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-2` is offered a new setup whose `lpA` holds `CPL1`, `sampleA` `QZ` at R1 90°, `sampleB` nothing and `lpB` `CPL2`, named `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL`, and the experiment `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-2`; a later group `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-BR` is offered that same setup and `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-BR`; with that setup held, the offer is the held setup itself; `CPL-(QZd#-20)-CPL` places `QZd` at R1 30° recorded as the reading −20°. `an unmatched group the template cannot place is listed with its reason, and two groups never share an experiment`: `Darkness` and `CPL-(XX#0)-CPL` are `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyNameErr _)`; over a table without `sampleB`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-CPL` is `SplitKeySetupErr` naming `Obj 2`; the groups `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` and `CPL-(QZ#45.0-LR#45)-CPL` with that experiment held match it once and refuse the second with `SplitKeyTwiceErr` naming both keys; `matched`, `offered` and `unmatched` list the groups in order. `every split error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local payload renders a distinct text holding it. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After matching lands, `DataSplit.ofGroups` MUST match each group to the kit's experiment its key names, as written or as the template writes it back, offer an unmatched group the template can read the setup (held or new) and experiment its name describes over the table's slots and angles, and list every other group with its typed reason, two groups never matching one experiment; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a group matches the experiment its key names, as written or as the template writes it back`, `an unmatched group the template reads is offered its setup and experiment over the table's slots`, `an unmatched group the template cannot place is listed with its reason, and two groups never share an experiment` and `every split error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.a group matches the experiment its key names, as written or as the template writes it back","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.an unmatched group the template reads is offered its setup and experiment over the table's slots","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.an unmatched group the template cannot place is listed with its reason, and two groups never share an experiment","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.every split error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.DataRowKey.nameText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.DataSplitError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.SplitSetupOffer","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.SplitGroupMatch","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.SplitGroup","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.DataSplit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.DataSplitParam","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MATCHING"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number":319,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S93g","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[318],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests"],"how_to":"Splitting a picked file by its key column is a semantic message that shows the matched, offered and unmatched groups and writes nothing (001 §P `SplitByColumn`; 001 §K 'One file → many experiments'; .spec-md §10.3 identify → confirm: nothing is attached or created until `MatchByTemplate`, step 320). The panel that shows it is step 324's. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3: (1) Before the model: `DataSplitState = { file : FileName; profile : ImportProfileName; key : SplitKeyColumn; split : DataSplit; creating : DataRowKey list }`, the file being split, the profile and key column it is split by, its groups as matched (step 318), and the offered groups ticked for creation. `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `dataSplitOpt : DataSplitState option`, `None` in `initWith`, with a one-line doc. (2) Messages, each documented in one line: `SplitByColumn of FileName * ImportProfileName` (split the picked file by that profile's key column), refused by the read-only guard of step 185 as `OpenImportWizard` is (step 310); `ToggleSplitOffer of DataRowKey` (tick or untick creating an offered group's setup and experiment) and `CancelDataSplit` (forget the split), which write nothing. (3) `SplitByColumn (file, name)`: `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles name` (step 300); `None` sets `kitStatus` to `Not split — the import profile '<name>' is not available.`, and a profile whose `splitKeyOpt` (step 317) is `None` `Not split — the import profile '<name>' maps no key column.`. Otherwise `model.experimentData.readPickedFile file` (step 305), its `content.kitFileText` (step 307) mapped by the profile's `mapText` (step 303) and its `splitGroups` (step 317): an error of any of them sets `kitStatus` `Not split — <the error's caption or describe>`. With the groups, `dataSplitOpt` becomes `Some { file; profile = name; key; split = DataSplit.ofGroups <param> groups; creating = [] }`, `<param>` being `{ template = model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate; experiments = model.experimentCollection.experiments; setups = model.kitSetups; table = model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.recordedWith model.kitItems); items = model.kitItems; choiceOf = model.tryItemModelChoice }` (steps 258, 263), and `kitStatus` is `Split <the file's leaf> by '<key>': <m> matched, <o> offered, <u> unmatched.`. Every refusal leaves `dataSplitOpt` as it was. Nothing is read from or written to the kit. (4) `ToggleSplitOffer key`: with a split whose group of that key is a `SetupOfferForGroup`, `creating` gains the key, or loses it when it holds it; any other key, or no split, changes nothing. `CancelDataSplit` sets `dataSplitOpt` to `None` and nothing else. No other message, field or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs`, `module DataSplitModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended to `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write, as `SetupModelTests`' is (steps 260, 263, 272): its items `LP1`, `QZ`, `QZ2`, `Laser` and `LPd`, its kit file holding `NamingTemplate.standard`, its table a linear polarizer holding `LP1`, a sample holding `QZ` turned to R1 45° and a second linear polarizer holding `LPd` before the seeded detector (each by `AssignSlot`), and, after the first polarizer is chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and `ExpCommit`, the setup `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` and its experiment `E1`, which the template names `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`, and a test-local Phone ROI file written outside the kit, the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total` and the rows `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5`, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd,1,2026-07-15T12:01:00+00:00,45,912.25`, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd-2,0,2026-07-15T12:02:00+00:00,0,870`, `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd,0,2026-07-15T12:03:00+00:00,0,801.5` and `Darkness,0,2026-07-15T12:04:00+00:00,0,12.5`, each ending in `\\n`. `splitting a picked file lists its groups matched, offered and unmatched, and writes nothing`: `SplitByColumn (<the file>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv)` leaves `dataSplitOpt` holding the key `experiment` and five groups in file order: `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` (2 points) matched to `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`; `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd-2` (1) offered the held setup `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` and the experiment `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd-2`; `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` (1) offered a new setup of that name and the experiment `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd`; and `Darkness` (1) unmatched with `SplitKeyNameErr`; `creating` empty; `kitStatus` `Split <leaf> by 'experiment': 1 matched, 2 offered, 1 unmatched.`; and every file of the folder unchanged. `a split offer is ticked and unticked, and cancelling the split forgets it`: `ToggleSplitOffer` of `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` ticks it, a second untick it, and of `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` and `Darkness` changes nothing; `CancelDataSplit` leaves `dataSplitOpt` `None`. `a file the profile cannot split, or a profile the kit lacks, is told and nothing is split`: `SplitByColumn` with `Intensity series` sets `kitStatus` holding `maps no key column`, with `Nope` holding `not available`, and of a file that does not exist holding the read's reason, each leaving `dataSplitOpt` `None`. `KitWindowModelTests`: `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `SplitByColumn`, with its assertions. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the split messages land, `SplitByColumn` MUST read a picked file through the chosen profile, split it by its key column and hold every group matched, offered or unmatched, writing nothing and refusing typed a profile the kit lacks, a profile without a key column, an unreadable file and a read-only kit, `ToggleSplitOffer` MUST tick only offered groups and `CancelDataSplit` forget the split; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `splitting a picked file lists its groups matched, offered and unmatched, and writes nothing`, `a split offer is ticked and unticked, and cancelling the split forgets it` and `a file the profile cannot split, or a profile the kit lacks, is told and nothing is split`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.splitting a picked file lists its groups matched, offered and unmatched, and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.a split offer is ticked and unticked, and cancelling the split forgets it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.a file the profile cannot split, or a profile the kit lacks, is told and nothing is split","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.DataSplitState","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.dataSplitOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SplitByColumn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ToggleSplitOffer","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CancelDataSplit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-MESSAGES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 320, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [319], "how_to": "Applying a split attaches the file once and maps each group to its experiment by the key's rows, creating the ticked offers' setups and experiments (001 §P `MatchByTemplate`; 001 §K 'match each group by the naming template, list the unmatched groups and offer to create setups for them'; 001 §E 'Attaching a file from outside the kit copies it into `data/`'; the S9.2 mapper's request: a split group is a `KeyedDataRows` of one `MappedAttachment`; the precedent of `GenerateSetupGrid`, step 276: setups and experiments written in order, the first failure stopping the run). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3: (1) `MatchByTemplate` (apply the split: attach the file once, map each matched group, create each ticked offer), documented in one line and refused by the read-only guard of step 185. With no split (`dataSplitOpt = None`) it changes nothing. With `dataSplitOpt = Some s`, `s.creating` not empty and a draft that cannot record an experiment (no chosen axis or no capture the detectors allow, as `RecordExperiment` requires, step 278), it sets `kitStatus` to `Not split — a new experiment records the Experiments draft's scan: choose a variable there, or tick no offer.` and writes nothing. (2) Otherwise `model.experimentData.attachDataFile s.file` (step 305) attaches the file once, copied into `data/` from outside the kit or recorded in place (steps 133, 134); an error sets `kitStatus` `Not attached — <e.describe>` and writes nothing else. With the attachment, each group of `s.split.groups` in order: an `ExperimentForGroup name` group's experiment (the collection's of that name) takes `attachDataFile` of `{ attachment; profile = s.profile; rows = KeyedDataRows key; exclusions = [] }` (steps 291, 313) and is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment`; a `SetupOfferForGroup offer` group whose key `s.creating` holds records `offer.setup` through `recordSetup` (step 260) when `kitSetups` lacks it (by equality), then appends a new experiment of the draft's scan over `offer.setup.reference` named `offer.experiment`, as `RecordExperiment` appends one (step 278, never editing the draft's own), which takes the same keyed attachment before it is recorded, so each experiment file is written once; an unticked offer and a `GroupWithoutMatch` group write nothing. The first write that fails stops the run: the collection and `kitSetups` hold what was written, and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. (3) On success `dataSplitOpt` is `None`, `kitSetups` holds the new setups in name order, each experiment given data has its badge computed by the one private validation function (steps 136, 295), and `kitStatus` is `Attached <the file's leaf> to <a> experiment(s): <m> matched, <c> created with <s> new setup(s); <u> group(s) left unattached.`, `u` counting the unticked offers and the unmatched groups. The table, `activeSetupOpt`, the draft and `reviewedDataOpt` are unchanged. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `DataSplitModelTests` (step 319), over its fixture after `SplitByColumn (<the file>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv)`: `applying a split attaches the file once and gives each matched experiment the rows of its key, and an unticked offer creates nothing`: `MatchByTemplate` leaves `data/<the file's leaf>` holding the file's exact bytes once, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`'s data that attachment mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey \"LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd\")` with no exclusion, its file read back through `readExperiments` holding the same, `model.dataBadgeOf` of it `ValidatedDataBadge` of 2 points, no setup or experiment file added, `dataSplitOpt` `None` and `kitStatus` `Attached <leaf> to 1 experiment(s): 1 matched, 0 created with 0 new setup(s); 3 group(s) left unattached.`. `a ticked offer records its setup when the kit lacks it and a new experiment of the draft's scan with its rows`: with both offers ticked (`ToggleSplitOffer`), `MatchByTemplate` writes `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd.setup-json` and no second `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json`, the experiments `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd-2` over `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` revision 1 and `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` over `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` revision 1, each of the draft's scan and mapped to the rows of its key, and `kitStatus` naming 3 experiments, 2 created and 1 new setup; E1's draft still edits what it edited. `a split with a ticked offer and no draft scan, or with no split, writes nothing`: after `ExpNew` (no axis) with an offer ticked, `MatchByTemplate` sets the `Not split —` status and every file's bytes are unchanged, and `MatchByTemplate` after `CancelDataSplit` changes nothing. `KitWindowModelTests`: `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `MatchByTemplate`, with its assertions.", "acceptance": "After `MatchByTemplate` lands, applying a split MUST attach the file once and give each matched experiment the keyed rows of its group through the chosen profile, record each ticked offer's setup when the kit lacks it and a new experiment of the draft's scan with its keyed rows, leave unticked and unmatched groups unattached, and write nothing for a ticked offer without a draft scan or a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `applying a split attaches the file once and gives each matched experiment the rows of its key, and an unticked offer creates nothing`, `a ticked offer records its setup when the kit lacks it and a new experiment of the draft's scan with its rows` and `a split with a ticked offer and no draft scan, or with no split, writes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.applying a split attaches the file once and gives each matched experiment the rows of its key, and an unticked offer creates nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-MATCH-BY-TEMPLATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.a ticked offer records its setup when the kit lacks it and a new experiment of the draft's scan with its rows", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-MATCH-BY-TEMPLATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.a split with a ticked offer and no draft scan, or with no split, writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-MATCH-BY-TEMPLATE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATCH-BY-TEMPLATE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.MatchByTemplate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATCH-BY-TEMPLATE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 321, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [320], "how_to": "The column-mapping wizard also opens on a file to split across the kit's experiments, so the data dialog's preview, column roles and profile picker serve the split too (001 §O 'Data dialog: preview, column roles, an import-profile picker, the key split with a matched / unmatched table'; the S9.3 brief: the profile picker (S9.2); .spec-md §6 'Reuse before invention': one wizard). The Data step's button that opens it is step 323's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs` (step 308): before `ImportWizardRequest`, `ImportWizardTarget` = `AttachWizardTarget of Experiments.ExperimentId` (attach the file to that experiment) | `SplitWizardTarget` (split the file across the kit's experiments by its key column), each case documented in one line. `ImportWizardRequest` and `ImportWizardApplied` replace `experimentId` with `target : ImportWizardTarget`, and `ApplyImportWizard` hands the request's target on unchanged; nothing else in the model or the update changes. `importWizardView` (step 309) reads the target in two places only: the heading is `Import <the file's leaf name>` for `AttachWizardTarget` and `Split <the file's leaf name> by its key column` for `SplitWizardTarget`, and `importWizardAttachButton` is captioned `Attach` or `Split`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ImportWizardApplied.messages` (step 310) answers, after `SaveImportProfile p` when `savedOpt` is `Some p`, `AttachDataFile (id, file, profile)` for `AttachWizardTarget id` and `SplitByColumn (file, profile)` (step 319) for `SplitWizardTarget`, so a new profile is in the kit before a file is mapped or split by it. `OpenImportWizard` (step 310) builds its request with `target = AttachWizardTarget experimentId`. New `OpenSplitWizard of FileName` (the Data step's Split a file by key… after its file dialog), documented in one line and refused by the read-only guard of step 185: it calls `model.kitShell.openImportWizard { target = SplitWizardTarget; file; readPickedFile = model.experimentData.readPickedFile; kitProfiles = model.kit.kitFile.importProfiles; defaultProfile = ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv }` (the built-in that carries a key column, step 298) and answers the model unchanged. `ImportWizardWindow` and `withImportWizard` (step 311) are unchanged: the shell opens one wizard for either target. No other message, field or option is added. Tests. `ImportWizardTests` (steps 308, 309, 311): the class's request takes `target = AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`; `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes` and `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it` record an `onApplied` whose `target` is `AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`, their other assertions kept; every other fact passes with that request; new `a split wizard says it splits and hands the kit window the file and the profile to split by`: over the class's request with `target = SplitWizardTarget`, `importWizardView` mounted as the class mounts it shows the heading `Split <leaf> by its key column` and the button `Split`, and `PickImportProfile` of `Phone ROI CSV` then `ApplyImportWizard` record one `onApplied` of `SplitWizardTarget`, the file, `Phone ROI CSV` and `None`, then one close. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 310): `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default` records a request whose `target` is `AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`; `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it` builds its applied value with that target, its assertions kept; new `opening the split wizard hands it the picked file with Phone ROI CSV chosen, and its Apply splits by the chosen profile`: `OpenSplitWizard <a test-local file>` records one request of `SplitWizardTarget`, that file, the kit's profiles and `defaultProfile` `Phone ROI CSV`, the model unchanged; `messages` of an applied `{ SplitWizardTarget; <the file>; Lab scan; Some <step 310's test-local Lab scan> }` are `[ SaveImportProfile <it>; SplitByColumn (<the file>, Lab scan) ]`. `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `OpenSplitWizard`, recording no request. `ScrollExtentTests`' `the import wizard leaves everything reachable` (step 311) builds its request with `target = AttachWizardTarget (ExperimentId 1)`, its assertions kept.", "acceptance": "After the wizard gains its target, the same wizard MUST open on a file to attach to one experiment or to split across the kit's experiments, say which, and hand the kit window `AttachDataFile` or `SplitByColumn` after any new profile is saved, and `OpenSplitWizard` MUST open it with Phone ROI CSV chosen, refused under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening the split wizard hands it the picked file with Phone ROI CSV chosen, and its Apply splits by the chosen profile`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default`, `the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it` and `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a split wizard says it splits and hands the kit window the file and the profile to split by`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes` and `Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.Attach with a picked profile hands it to the kit window once and closes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.Attach with a new mapping hands the kit window the profile to save and attaches by it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests.a split wizard says it splits and hands the kit window the file and the profile to split by", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ImportWizardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportWizardTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.opening the import wizard hands it the picked file, the kit's profiles and the detector's default", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the wizard's Attach saves its new mapping first and attaches the file by it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.opening the split wizard hands it the picked file with Phone ROI CSV chosen, and its Apply splits by the chosen profile", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardTarget", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportWizardView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardRequest", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ImportWizardView.ImportWizardApplied", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ImportWizardApplied.messages", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.OpenSplitWizard", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-WIZARD"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 322, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [321], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentMatrixTests"], "how_to": "The experiment matrix as pure Domain: rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer, each cell the experiments measured there (001 §O 'Experiment matrix view: rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer, with a data badge per cell'; the S9.3 brief; step 268's reading of 001's words: the source is the polarization source, the Prep slots). The view and its badges are step 327's. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs`: `module ExperimentMatrices` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `DataSplits.fs` (step 317): one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §O and spec 0050 S9.3, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. In this order: (1) `MatrixObject = { item : ItemLabel; angle : Angle }`, an object slot's item and its angle (`SetupSlot.turnAngle`, step 277: a dial reading, else R1). (2) `MatrixRowKey = { sources : ItemLabel list; objects : MatrixObject list }` and `MatrixColumnKey = { analyzers : ItemLabel list }`. (3) `MatrixCell = { row : MatrixRowKey; column : MatrixColumnKey; experiments : Experiments.ExperimentId list }`. (4) `ExperimentMatrix = { rows : MatrixRowKey list; columns : MatrixColumnKey list; cells : MatrixCell list; unplaced : Experiments.ExperimentId list }`, with `member this.tryFindCell (row : MatrixRowKey) (column : MatrixColumnKey) : MatrixCell option` and `static member ofExperiments (experiments : Experiment list) (setups : Setup list) (items : Item list) : ExperimentMatrix`, the one rule: for each experiment in order, `experiment.slotsIn setups` (step 261); an error puts its id in `unplaced`. Its slots in light order (`SetupSlot.inLightOrder`, step 257) give: `sources`, the labels of the items the `PrepSlotRole` slots hold; `objects`, for each `ObjectSlotRole` slot holding an item, its label and the slot's `turnAngle`; and the column's `analyzers`, the labels of the items the `AnalyzerSlotRole` slots hold, each list in light order. A slot holding nothing, or an item `items` lacks, adds nothing; the source and detector slots do not enter. Rows and columns are listed in the order they first appear, and a cell holds the ids of its experiments in the collection's order, cells listed in the order their first experiment appears. No sort, cache, text or other member is added: captions are the view's (step 327). Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentMatrixTests.fs`, `module ExperimentMatrixTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local copies of step 271's slots and items (`Laser`, `CPL1`, `CPL2`, `QZ`, `LR`, `QZd` dial-mounted with its zero at 10°): `the matrix puts each experiment in the row of its sources and objects at their angles and the column of its analyzers`: setups `A` (`lpA` `CPL1`, `sampleA` `QZ` at R1 45°, `lpB` `CPL2`), `B` (the same with `QZ` at 90°) and `C` (as `A` with `lpB` empty), and experiments E1 over A, E2 over B, E3 over A and E4 over C, give the rows `CPL1 · QZ@45` and `CPL1 · QZ@90` and the columns `[CPL2]` and `[]`, in that order, and the cells (row 1, `[CPL2]`) = [E1; E3], (row 2, `[CPL2]`) = [E2] and (row 1, `[]`) = [E4]; `tryFindCell` of row 2 and `[]` answers `None`. `two objects in series make one row, a dial-mounted object sits at its reading, and an experiment whose setup the kit lacks is unplaced`: a setup with `QZ` at 45° in `sampleA` and `LR` at 45° in `sampleB` gives one row whose objects are `QZ@45` then `LR@45`; `QZd` in `sampleA` at R1 30° sits at −20°; and an experiment over `Gone` revision 1 is in `unplaced` and in no cell.", "acceptance": "After the matrix lands, `ExperimentMatrix.ofExperiments` MUST place each experiment in the row of its Prep items and its objects at their angles and the column of its analyzers, in first-appearance order, and list every experiment whose setup the kit lacks as unplaced; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the matrix puts each experiment in the row of its sources and objects at their angles and the column of its analyzers` and `two objects in series make one row, a dial-mounted object sits at its reading, and an experiment whose setup the kit lacks is unplaced`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentMatrixTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentMatrixTests.the matrix puts each experiment in the row of its sources and objects at their angles and the column of its analyzers", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentMatrixTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentMatrixTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-EXPERIMENT-MATRIX"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentMatrixTests.two objects in series make one row, a dial-mounted object sits at its reading, and an experiment whose setup the kit lacks is unplaced", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentMatrixTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentMatrixTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S93-EXPERIMENT-MATRIX"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentMatrices.MatrixObject", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs", "obligations": ["S93-EXPERIMENT-MATRIX"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentMatrices.MatrixRowKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs", "obligations": ["S93-EXPERIMENT-MATRIX"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentMatrices.MatrixColumnKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs", "obligations": ["S93-EXPERIMENT-MATRIX"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentMatrices.MatrixCell", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs", "obligations": ["S93-EXPERIMENT-MATRIX"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentMatrices.ExperimentMatrix", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs", "obligations": ["S93-EXPERIMENT-MATRIX"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number":323,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S93k","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[322],"how_to":"The Data step of the flow strip, and the Experiments bay's Data files section moved into it (001 §O 'a left flow strip: Items → Setups → Experiments → Data → …, each step reachable directly'; 001 §O 'the Experiments bay's \"Data files\" section moves into Data'; .spec-md §3.22: a step appears when it works; spec 0046's rule, kept: measured data belong to the Inverse constructor, `ScrollExtentTests.fs`'s `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window alone`). The step's panels arrive in steps 324-327. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` (steps 238, 242) gains `DataFlowStep` after `ExperimentsFlowStep`: `all` lists Items, Setups, Experiments and Data; its `caption` is `Data` and its `flowUiId` `flowDataStep`. `static member stepsOf (mode : ConstructorMode) : ConstructorFlowStep list` answers `all` for `InverseConstructor` and `all` without `DataFlowStep` for `ForwardConstructor`. `ShowFlowStep DataFlowStep` sets `flowStep` alone, the open bay kept, and changes nothing under `ForwardConstructor`. `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` (step 186) from `DataFlowStep` also sets `flowStep` to `ExperimentsFlowStep` and `ribbon` to `BayNames.experiments`; every other switch is unchanged. The private `pickDataFile`, `attachDataFileButton` and `dataFileRow` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`, `:attachDataFileButton`, `:dataFileRow`) MOVE to the new view below and are deleted here; `collectionBuilderView` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:collectionBuilderView`) loses its `Data files:` section and its mode match, and its doc and the section comment above it say that the data files are the Data step's; `buildDataFilePickerOptions` stays where it is (`DataFilePickerFolderTests` pins it). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView`, compiled directly after `FlowStripView.fs` (step 242) and before `KitWindowView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §O and spec 0050 S9.3. It holds the three moved functions, their bodies unchanged but for colours, which they take from the `MaterialsWindowView` buttons the import wizard's view uses (step 309), never a copied helper, and `dataStepView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`, documented in one to three lines: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `dataStepPanel`, margin 8, holding the heading `Data files:` and the `StackPanel` named `experimentDataFiles` with one `dataFileRow` per experiment (or the hint `(add experiments in the Experiments step, then attach one data file to each)` when there is none), then one row holding the verb `Split a file by key…` carrying `dataSplitFileButton`, which opens the picker through `pickDataFile` and sends `OpenSplitWizard file` (step 321) on a confirmed pick, and is disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld` (step 185) as the attach verb is. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs` (steps 188, 242): `DataFlowStep` shows `DataStepView.dataStepView model dispatch` keyed `data`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui/FlowStripView.fs` (step 242) shows one box per step of `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf model.constructorMode`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the flow strip's (step 242) under one comment line citing spec 0050 S9.3, each with a one-line doc: `flowDataStep` (`\"FlowDataStep\"`), `dataStepPanel` (`\"DataStepPanel\"`) and `dataSplitFileButton` (`\"DataSplitFileButton\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: the doc of `attachDataFile` and `dataFileStatus` names the Data step. No other control, message or option is added. Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 238): `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` lists Items, Setups, Experiments and Data with their captions, its other assertions kept; new `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`: `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` is Items, Setups and Experiments and `stepsOf InverseConstructor` adds Data; over `initInverse`, `ShowFlowStep DataFlowStep` sets `DataFlowStep` with the bay kept, and `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` then answers `ExperimentsFlowStep` with `BayNames.experiments`; over `initMain ()` `ShowFlowStep DataFlowStep` changes nothing. `KitWindowTests` (steps 185, 242): `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowDataStep`, `DataStepPanel` and `DataSplitFileButton`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds, in the inverse window, the Data box below Experiments and, on `DataFlowStep`, `dataStepPanel` present and `tableElementCanvas` absent, and in the Main window no Data box; `a read-only window withholds every write control` looks for the `attachDataFile` of `E1` and `dataSplitFileButton` in `dataStepView` mounted over the same models (disabled read-only, enabled read-write) and finds no `attachDataFile` in the Experiments bay; with trait `ui-smoke`, new `pressing the Data step shows the data files and the Split a file by key button`: pressing `flowDataStep` in the inverse kit window shows `dataStepPanel`, the `attachDataFile` of E1 and `dataSplitFileButton`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable` is renamed `Inverse: the Experiments bay leaves everything reachable`, its assertion kept; `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window alone` is renamed `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window's Data step alone`: the forward and the inverse `mainView` texts hold neither `Data files:` nor `Attach data file…`, `dataStepView` over the inverse model with those experiments holds both, and `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` lacks `DataFlowStep`; new `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"KitWindowData\"` over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over the inverse model on `DataFlowStep` with `filledExperiments ()`'s experiments. `DataFilePickerFolderTests` and `InverseConstructorTests` pass as written.","acceptance":"After the Data step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST show Data after Experiments and the Main constructor's none, the Data step MUST hold every experiment's data-file row and the Split a file by key verb, the Experiments bay MUST hold no data-file section, and leaving the Inverse constructor MUST leave the Data step; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing the Data step shows the data files and the Split a file by key button`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable`, the renamed `Inverse: the Experiments bay leaves everything reachable` and `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window's Data step alone`, and the changed `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/FlowStripView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.pressing the Data step shows the data files and the Split a file by key button","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.Inverse: the Experiments bay leaves everything reachable","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"rename","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window alone","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","successor":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window's Data step alone","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ConstructorFlowStep","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.flowDataStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataStepPanel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitFileButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView.kitWindowView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.FlowStripView.flowStripView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S93-DATA-STEP"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number":324,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S93l","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[323],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"],"how_to":"The key split's matched / unmatched table in the Data step, with Apply and Cancel (001 §O 'Data dialog: … the key split with a matched / unmatched table'; 001 §O 'Automation': `DataSplitKeyColumn`; .spec-md §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 Apply / Cancel share a row with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; the S9.3 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs` (step 323): when `model.dataSplitOpt` is `Some s` (step 319), under the Split verb, a bordered vertical panel holding: a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `dataSplitKeyColumn` with `Split <the file's leaf> by '<s.key>' through '<s.profile>'`; one row per group of `s.split.groups`, in order, carrying `dataSplitGroupRow group.key` and reading `<key> — <n> point(s) — ` then, for `ExperimentForGroup name`, `→ <name>`; for `SetupOfferForGroup offer`, a box carrying `dataSplitOfferToggle group.key` labelled `Create <offer.experiment> over '<offer.setup.name>'`, followed by ` (new setup)` when `model.kitSetups` lacks the setup, on the positive background when `s.creating` holds the key and in the verb look otherwise, sending `ToggleSplitOffer group.key`; and for `GroupWithoutMatch problem`, `unmatched — <problem.describe>` in the message colour; then one horizontal row of `Apply split` (`dataSplitApplyButton`, the positive action look, sending `MatchByTemplate`, step 320, disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`) and, after a gap, `Cancel` (`dataSplitCancelButton`, the negative action look, sending `CancelDataSplit`), the `MaterialsWindowView` action buttons step 309 uses. A label never sits in a horizontal `StackPanel` beside a wrapping one (AGENTS.md: dock it in a `DockPanel`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group (step 323), each with a one-line doc: `dataSplitKeyColumn` (`\"DataSplitKeyColumn\"`), `dataSplitApplyButton` (`\"DataSplitApplyButton\"`) and `dataSplitCancelButton` (`\"DataSplitCancelButton\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type DataRowKey with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (its text); on `ConstructorUiId`, `static member dataSplitGroupRow (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataSplitGroup_<key>`) and `static member dataSplitOfferToggle (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataSplitOffer_<key>`), as `attachDataFile` is keyed by its experiment; and `type DataSplitError with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its `describe`. No other control or message is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs`, `module DataStepTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended to the compile list after `KitWindowTests.fs` with no comment; its views are mounted over the inverse model (`initInverse`, as `KitWindowTests` builds it, step 184) loaded from a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write, with `E1` committed, as `KitWindowTests` mounts the kit window (step 242), and a test-local `DataSplitState` over `phone.csv` by `experiment` through `Phone ROI CSV` whose groups are `K1` (2 points) matched to `E1`, `K2` (1) offered the new setup `Bench B` and the experiment `K2`, and `K3` (1) unmatched with `SplitKeyNameErr`. `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the Data step's ids so far (`FlowDataStep`, `DataStepPanel`, `DataSplitFileButton`, `DataSplitKeyColumn`, `DataSplitApplyButton`, `DataSplitCancelButton`, `DataSplitGroup_K1`, `DataSplitOffer_K2`). `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row`: `dataSplitKeyColumn` reads `Split phone.csv by 'experiment' through 'Phone ROI CSV'`; the three group rows read `→ E1`, `Create K2 over 'Bench B' (new setup)` and a text starting `unmatched —`; only `K2` has a toggle; `dataSplitApplyButton` and `dataSplitCancelButton` have equal tops, Cancel right of Apply with a gap between. `pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split`: over a `HostWindow` running `Program.mkSimple` of the model with `updateTableAndElementRotation` and `dataStepView`, pressing the toggle's centre leaves `creating` [`K2`] and the toggle on the positive background, and pressing Cancel's centre leaves `dataSplitOpt` `None` and no split panel. With trait `ui-smoke`, `the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group`: over a folder kit holding `E1` and its split by `SplitByColumn` of a test-local Phone ROI file whose rows all carry `E1`'s name, the rendered Data step shows the panel, and pressing `dataSplitApplyButton` leaves E1 mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to the rows of its key and the panel gone.","acceptance":"After the split panel lands, the Data step MUST show a pending split's key column and each group matched, offered (with its toggle) or unmatched (with its reason), with Apply split and Cancel in one row, sending `ToggleSplitOffer`, `MatchByTemplate` and `CancelDataSplit` under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row` and `pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitKeyColumn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitApplyButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitCancelButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.DataRowKey.uiKey","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitGroupRow","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitOfferToggle","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.DataSplitError.caption","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 325, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [324], "how_to": "The reviewed experiment's points in the Data step, each with Exclude or Include, and a chart in which an excluded point stays, marked (001 §O 'Data dialog: … per-point exclusion with a reason'; 001 §K 'exclusions carry a reason and stay visible in plots, marked'; the S9.3 brief; .spec-md §4 'UI'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`, after the inline chart: `PointMark` = `KeptPointMark` | `ExcludedPointMark`; `PlottedPoint = { position : ConstructorUiPosition; point : ChartPoint; mark : PointMark }`; and `pointsChartView (id : ConstructorUiId) (points : PlottedPoint list) (xLabel : ControlCaption) (yLabel : ControlCaption) : IView`, documented in one to three lines: a `Canvas` carrying `id`, of the inline chart's size, drawn with the private `PlotWindow.over`, `gridLines`, `axisLines` and `axisLabels` the bay's chart is drawn with (called, not copied; `PlotWindow.over` takes the points as one series); each kept point a filled 5 × 5 `Ellipse` in the first series colour carrying `dataPointDot position`, and each excluded point an unfilled 9 × 9 `Ellipse` ring with a red stroke of 1.5 carrying `dataExcludedPointMark position`, each centred on its point. No line joins the points. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type MappedPointNumber with member this.uiPosition : ConstructorUiPosition` (its value); `type MappedPoints with member this.pointCaptions : ControlCaption list`, one per point in order, numbers by `%g`: an intensity point `x = <x>, I = <intensity>`, an ellipsometric point `λ = <nm> nm, Ψ = <ψ>°, Δ = <δ>°`, a capture row `<label> #<capture index>: <description>° → <avg_total>`, an observation `<key> <T or R>: θ = <incidence>°, φ = <azimuth>°, m00 = <m00>` and a mapped row `<its scan cells' display values joined by \", \">: <signal, or m00>`; and `member this.chartPoints : ExperimentControls.ChartPoint list`, one per point, x its 1-based number and y its reading's first value (the intensity, Ψ in degrees, `avg_total`, the observation's m00, or the mapped signal or m00). On `ConstructorUiId`: `static member dataReviewButton (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataReview_<id>`), `static member dataPointRow (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataPoint_<n>`), `static member dataExcludePointButton (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataExcludePoint_<n>`) and `static member dataIncludePointButton (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataIncludePoint_<n>`). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group, each with a one-line doc: `dataReviewPanel` (`\"DataReviewPanel\"`), `dataExclusionReasonField` (`\"DataExclusionReasonField\"`), `dataPointsChart` (`\"DataPointsChart\"`), `dataPointDot (point : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$\"DataPointDot_{point.value}\"`) and `dataExcludedPointMark (point : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$\"DataPointExcluded_{point.value}\"`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: each `dataFileRow` gains, after its attach verb, the verb `Review` carrying `dataReviewButton experiment.id` and sending `ReviewExperimentData experiment.id` (step 315), offered read-only too. When `model.reviewedDataOpt` is `Some r`, after the split panel, a bordered panel carrying `dataReviewPanel`: the heading `Points of <name> — <its badge text>` (`model.dataBadgeOf`, step 295); a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Reason:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `dataExclusionReasonField` that shows `model.dataDraft.exclusionReason` and sends `SetExclusionReason` on Enter and on losing focus; for `r.points = Ok points`, `ExperimentControls.pointsChartView ConstructorUiId.dataPointsChart` of the `chartPoints` marked `ExcludedPointMark` where the experiment's data excludes the point (`tryFindExclusion`, step 313), with the labels `point` and `reading`, and then one row per point carrying `dataPointRow n`: `#<n>  <its caption>` and, for an excluded point, `excluded — <reason>` in the message colour and the verb `Include` (`dataIncludePointButton n`, sending `IncludePoint`), otherwise the verb `Exclude` (`dataExcludePointButton n`, sending `ExcludePoint (id, n, model.dataDraft.exclusionReason)`), both disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`; for `Error e`, `e`'s caption. No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests` (step 324): `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `DataReviewPanel`, `DataExclusionReasonField`, `DataPointsChart`, `DataPointDot_2`, `DataPointExcluded_2`, `DataReview_1`, `DataPoint_2`, `DataExcludePoint_2` and `DataIncludePoint_2`. New `each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number`: the captions and chart points of a two-point intensity series, two Phone ROI rows and one observation (test-local) are as listed above, each x its number. `the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings`: over the class's model whose data proxy is a mock answering E1's attachment with the series `0 → 1.0`, `45 → 0.5`, `90 → 0.0` and whose E1 data excludes point 2 for `beam blocked`, after `ReviewExperimentData (ExperimentId 1)`, the panel shows three point rows, row 2 reading `excluded — beam blocked` with `Include` and rows 1 and 3 `Exclude`, and the chart holds `DataPointDot_1`, `DataPointDot_3` and `DataPointExcluded_2` and no `DataPointDot_2`. `pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back`: over a recording dispatch with the reason field holding `stray light`, pressing `Exclude` of point 3 records `ExcludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 3, ControlCaption \"stray light\")` and pressing `Include` of point 2 records `IncludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 2)`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart`: in the rendered Data step over that model, pressing `dataReviewButton` of E1 shows `dataReviewPanel` and `dataPointsChart`.", "acceptance": "After the review panel lands, the Data step MUST review an experiment's points with each point's caption, an excluded point listed with its reason and drawn as a ring on the chart beside the kept dots, Exclude sending the typed reason and Include taking an exclusion back, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number`, `the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings` and `pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.PointMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/Exper