", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataReviewPanel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataExclusionReasonField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataPointsChart", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataPointDot", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataExcludedPointMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 326, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93n", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [325], "how_to": "Correcting the reviewed experiment's setup from the Data step, with its audit note and trail (001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact (e.g. \"LR was at −45\"), with a mandatory audit note'; 001 §P `CorrectSetup`; the S9.3 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: the review panel (step 325) ends with a `Setup:` block: the line `Setup: <the experiment's setup.describe>`; a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Audit note:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `dataCorrectionNoteField` that shows `model.dataDraft.correctionNote` and sends `SetCorrectionNote` (step 316) on Enter and on losing focus; a `WrapPanel` holding, for each setup of `model.kitSetups` in order whose `reference` is not the experiment's own, the verb `Re-point to <reference.describe>` carrying `dataCorrectSetupChoice setup.name` and sending `CorrectSetup (id, setup.reference, model.dataDraft.correctionNote)`, disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`; and, when the experiment's `corrections` are not empty, a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `dataCorrectionTrail` with one wrapping line per correction, oldest first: `<previous.describe> → <corrected.describe>: <note>`. The lab file is never shown as changed, because it is not. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group, each with a one-line doc: `dataCorrectionNoteField` (`\"DataCorrectionNoteField\"`) and `dataCorrectionTrail` (`\"DataCorrectionTrail\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, on `ConstructorUiId` beside `savedSetup` (step 260), with a one-line doc: `static member dataCorrectSetupChoice (name : SetupName) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataCorrectSetup_<name>`). No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests`: `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `DataCorrectionNoteField`, `DataCorrectionTrail` and `DataCorrectSetup_Bench B`. New `the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail`: over the class's model whose kit holds the setups `Setup 1` (E1's) and `Bench B`, and whose E1 holds one correction `'Setup 0' revision 1 → 'Setup 1' revision 1: LP1 was at 30`, the reviewed E1 shows `Setup: 'Setup 1' revision 1`, one choice `Re-point to 'Bench B' revision 1` and no choice for `Setup 1`, and the trail's one line. `pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note`: over a recording dispatch with the note field holding `LR was at -45`, pressing the choice of `Bench B` records `CorrectSetup (ExperimentId 1, <Bench B revision 1>, ControlCaption \"LR was at -45\")`.", "acceptance": "After the correction panel lands, the reviewed experiment MUST show its setup, every other setup of the kit as a re-point choice sending `CorrectSetup` with the typed audit note, and its audit trail, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail` and `pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataCorrectionNoteField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataCorrectionTrail", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.dataCorrectSetupChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 327, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93o", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [326], "how_to": "The experiment matrix at the top of the Data step, a data badge per experiment in each cell (001 §O 'Experiment matrix view: rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer, with a data badge per cell'; the S9.3 brief; S9.1's badges). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type MatrixRowKey with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its sources' labels joined by ` + ` (or `—`), ` · `, then its objects as `<label>@<angle.degreeCaption>` (step 280) joined by ` → ` (or `—`); `type MatrixColumnKey with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its analyzers' labels joined by ` + ` (or `—`); and on `ConstructorUiId` `static member experimentMatrixEntry (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` (`ExperimentMatrixEntry_<id>`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group: `experimentMatrix` (`\"ExperimentMatrix\"`), with a one-line doc. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: first in the panel, the heading `Experiment matrix:` and a `Grid` carrying `experimentMatrix` over `ExperimentMatrix.ofExperiments model.experimentCollection.experiments model.kitSetups model.kitItems` (step 322): its first row the columns' captions, then one row per matrix row, its caption first and then, per column, a vertical `StackPanel` holding, for each experiment of that cell, a verb carrying `experimentMatrixEntry id` that reads `<name> · <model.dataBadgeOf experiment's text>` and sends `ReviewExperimentData id` (step 315), the reviewed experiment's on the positive background; an empty cell holds nothing. When `unplaced` is not empty, a wrapping line `Not in the matrix (setup missing): <their names joined by \", \">`. With no experiment, the line `(no experiments yet)`. No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests`: `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `ExperimentMatrix` and `ExperimentMatrixEntry_1`. New `the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones`: over the class's model holding E1 over `Setup 1`, E2 over `Bench B` (its polarizer turned) and E3 over `Gone` revision 1, the grid holds the row captions of `Setup 1` and `Bench B`, E1's entry reading `E1 · no data` and E2's `E2 · no data`, and the line naming `E3`; after E1's data is attached through the class's mock, E1's entry reads `E1 · validated (3 points)`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment`: pressing E2's entry in the rendered Data step reviews E2 and shows `dataReviewPanel`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable` (step 323) also holds a pending split of three groups, a reviewed experiment of three points, one excluded, with one correction, and the matrix of three experiments, its assertion kept.", "acceptance": "After the matrix view lands, the Data step MUST open on the experiment matrix, each experiment in the row of its sources and objects with their angles and the column of its analyzers, showing its data badge and reviewing it when pressed, the experiments whose setup the kit lacks listed apart; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.MatrixRowKey.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.MatrixColumnKey.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.experimentMatrixEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentMatrix", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 328, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93p", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [327], "how_to": "The section proved end to end through the kit window and a real folder, and `AGENTS.md` told where data live (the S9.3 brief: update the AGENTS.md 'Main ribbon' gotcha to match; 001 §E 'Exclusions, corrections and mappings live in the experiment file'; AGENTS.md: drive by id and wait for deterministic conditions). Nothing in `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs` changes: the split wizard is the import wizard `ConstructorScene.mount` composes (steps 312, 321), and the Data step is part of `kitWindowView`. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs` (steps 184, 312, 323) gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: the Data step splits a lab file across the kit's experiments, excludes a point and corrects a setup, all kept in the kit`: over a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write, as `SetupModelTests`' is (steps 260, 263, 272): its items `LP1`, `QZ`, `QZ2`, `Laser` and `LPd`, its kit file holding `NamingTemplate.standard`, its table a linear polarizer holding `LP1`, a sample holding `QZ` turned to R1 45° and a second linear polarizer holding `LPd` before the seeded detector (each by `AssignSlot`), and, after the first polarizer is chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and `ExpCommit`, the setup `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` and its experiment `E1`, which the template names `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`, loaded into `initInverse` and mounted as step 312 mounts it (`kitWindowView` over the model, dispatching through `updateTableAndElementRotation`, its shell `KitWindowShell.inert`), and a test-local Phone ROI file written outside the kit, the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total` and the rows `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5`, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd,1,2026-07-15T12:01:00+00:00,45,912.25`, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd-2,0,2026-07-15T12:02:00+00:00,0,870`, `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd,0,2026-07-15T12:03:00+00:00,0,801.5` and `Darkness,0,2026-07-15T12:04:00+00:00,0,12.5`, each ending in `\\n`: pressing `flowDataStep` shows `dataStepPanel`; dispatching `SplitByColumn (<the file>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv)`, as the split wizard's Split would, shows `dataSplitKeyColumn`; pressing the centres of `dataSplitOfferToggle` of `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` and then `dataSplitApplyButton` leaves `data/<the file's leaf>` holding the file's bytes, `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd.setup-json` and `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd.experiment-json` written, and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`'s file mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to the rows of its key; pressing its `experimentMatrixEntry` shows `dataReviewPanel` with two point rows; dispatching `SetExclusionReason (ControlCaption \"saturated\")` and pressing `dataExcludePointButton` of point 2 leaves its file, read back through `readExperiments`, excluding point 2 for `saturated` and its entry reading `excluded points (1 excluded, 1 validated)`; dispatching `SetCorrectionNote (ControlCaption \"QZ was at 0\")` and pressing `dataCorrectSetupChoice` of `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` leaves that experiment over `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` revision 1: `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`'s file holds one correction with that note, its name and its data unchanged; and the lab file's bytes in `data/` are unchanged throughout. Each press waits for its control as step 312's fact does. (2) `AGENTS.md`: in the gotcha **Main ribbon**, the sentence naming the Experiments bay's \"Data files\" section becomes: Attach data file… lives in the Inverse constructor's Data step (DataStepView.fs), not in the Experiments bay; the rest of the bullet is unchanged. After the gotcha 'Lab files are read through import profiles' (step 312), one bullet of at most six lines: **The Data step never edits a lab file** (`DataSplits.fs`, `ExperimentMatrices.fs`, `DataStepView.fs`, spec 0050 S9.3): an exclusion numbers a point of its mapped attachment (`MappedPointNumber`, one per point, with its reason) and a new attachment starts with none; `MappedPoints.keptBy` is the one rule from exclusions to the points validated and fitted; a correction re-points `Experiment.setup` and appends its audit note, the name kept; a split groups a file by its profile's key column (`splitGroups`) and `DataSplit.ofGroups` matches by name, then by the template, else offers the setup the name describes; `MatchByTemplate` attaches the file once, each group as `KeyedDataRows`. Nothing else in the file changes.", "acceptance": "After the end-to-end proof lands, the kit window's Data step MUST split a lab file across a folder kit's experiments (matched and created), review an experiment from the matrix, exclude a point and correct a setup with the experiment files holding each and the lab file unchanged, and AGENTS.md MUST say where Attach data file… lives and carry the gotcha 'The Data step never edits a lab file'; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Data step splits a lab file across the kit's experiments, excludes a point and corrects a setup, all kept in the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: the Data step splits a lab file across the kit's experiments, excludes a point and corrects a setup, all kept in the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S93-DATA-STEP-END-TO-END"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 329, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S94a", "touches": ["BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [328], "how_to": "The reference half of `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` moves into the optics-mueller kit (001 §Q AT-1 'Data: … the reference pipeline's scripts, `README.md` and `reference_step1_summary.json` / `reference_step2_linear_summary.json` into `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/`'; 001 §S9 'MOVE `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` into the AT-1 kit folder'; .spec-md §3.20 'The optics-mueller archive moves whole'; the S9.4 brief). `data.zip`, the measured data, moves in step 330, which deletes the folder. This step changes no code and no behaviour, and `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. (1) `git mv` each of these seven files from `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` to `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` under the same name: `README.md`, `cpl_cpl_analyzer.py`, `matrix_glue.py`, `matrix_step1_air_fit.py`, `matrix_fit_linear.py`, `reference_step1_summary.json` and `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`. The four scripts and the two summaries keep their bytes; they hold no carriage return, so the `*.py` and `*.json` rules of `.gitattributes` (`.gitattributes:25`, `:35`) change nothing in them. No `.kit-json` or other kit file is written: S12.1 builds the kit around these files. Under `data/`, `.gitignore` ignores only `/data/chroma/` and `/data/*/.oc/` (`.gitignore:333-334`), so `git check-ignore` matches none of the new paths. (2) In the moved `README.md` only what the move makes untrue changes, in the README's own voice: (a) its opening paragraph says that this folder, the optics-mueller kit's `data/reference/`, holds the reference implementation and the reference numerical results that `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` was written against, and that the measured data it inventories is `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip`; (b) every other place that says `data.zip` is here (the paragraph after the provenance table, the `Measured data` table and the inventory sentence under it) names it by that repository path; (c) `Further reading` gains one bullet: `specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md` §Q AT-1 and §S9, which move this folder into the optics-mueller kit. Every other line keeps its text. (3) In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`, the comments that give the summaries' provenance name them at `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/`, and the README beside them as `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md`: the class doc's spec 0044 §8.5 bullet ('`reference_step*_summary.json` in that same folder'), the acceptance-band comment above `stage1Tol` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:stage1Tol`), the comment of `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` that names the README's inventory, the provenance comment of `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values`, and the two of `section 7.2 end-to-end: …` (in its spec 0044 §8.5 paragraph and above `expectedQz`). No code line changes. The other `Data/MuellerMatrix` texts under `Berreman/` change with what they describe: the class doc's bullet on `data.zip` and `loadDataSet`'s doc with the data (step 330), and the doc of `archiveEntryName` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName`) with that member (step 331).", "acceptance": "After the reference files move, `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` MUST hold `README.md`, the four scripts and the two summaries, the scripts and summaries byte for byte, `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` MUST hold only `data.zip`, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST name the summaries at their kit path; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/README.md", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/cpl_cpl_analyzer.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_glue.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_step1_air_fit.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/reference_step1_summary.json", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/reference_step2_linear_summary.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/cpl_cpl_analyzer.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_glue.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_step1_air_fit.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_fit_linear.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/reference_step1_summary.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/reference_step2_linear_summary.json", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.4 -- The optics-mueller lab files move into the kit folder"}
{"number": 330, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S94b", "touches": ["BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [329], "how_to": "The measured data moves out of `data.zip` into the optics-mueller kit byte for byte, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` reads it there, read-only, through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (001 §Q AT-1 'the CSV entries of `data.zip` into `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` … `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` is then deleted, with its `Content` link in `BerremanTests.fsproj` … There is no second copy of the data' and 'The CSVs are read through the existing `MuellerDataStore` parser (`parseMuellerCsv`, the \"Phone ROI CSV\" import profile)'; 001 §K 'Raw data is immutable'; 001 §G 'The two committed reference kits … are read-only to tests'; .spec-md §3.12, §3.20, §3.21 and §7 'moved byte-for-byte … There is no second copy'; the S9.4 brief). After this step nothing reads `data.zip`; the archive-keyed seam the tests stop using is retired in step 331. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. (1) Byte for byte. The lab CSVs are CRLF text, all but `cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv` with a UTF-8 byte-order mark, and the catch-all `* text=auto eol=lf` (`.gitattributes:9`) would store them as LF, so a clone would hold other bytes than the archive and than the SHA-256 a kit records at attach (001 §E). `.gitattributes` therefore gains, after its last rule, a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S9.4 (lab files are kept exactly as recorded) and the rule `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/** -text !eol`, the form of its `*.nb` rule (`.gitattributes:58`). `AGENTS.md`'s 'Line endings: LF' gotcha (`AGENTS.md:513-516`) gains one sentence: the lab files under `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` are the exception, kept byte for byte by that rule (spec 0050 S9.4), and are never converted. (2) The move. Each entry of `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip` is written with the bytes the archive holds: each CSV to `data/optics-mueller/` joined with its archive path, so `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` becomes `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` and the eight exploratory CSVs land in `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/`; and each of the three `data/shapes/*.json` to `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/` under its own name. Before the archive is deleted, each written file's SHA-256 is checked against its entry's (the values in (4)). Then `data.zip` is deleted, with the folders `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` and `Berreman/Data/` it leaves empty. `BerremanTests.fsproj` loses the `ItemGroup` holding the `data.zip` `Content` link and its comment (`BerremanTests.fsproj:52-62`), and the comment above the `OpticalConstructor.Storage` `ProjectReference` (`BerremanTests.fsproj:88-90`), which names `createFileBacked`, gone since spec 0044, and the contract that step 331 retires; the reference stays, because the tests read the parser, the folder `KitProxy` and the Phone ROI CSV profile from Storage. The README (`data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md`, step 329) describes the data where it now is, in its own voice: the opening paragraph says the measured data is this kit's lab files under `data/raw/`; the paragraph after the provenance table says the lab files live in this kit, that `MuellerReconstructionTests` reads them read-only through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (`MuellerDataStore.parseMuellerCsv`), and that no code path references the external checkout; the provenance sentence on line endings says the scripts and summaries were converted to LF while the lab CSVs keep their recorded bytes; the `Measured data` table's row is `data/raw/`, the lab files moved byte for byte out of the former `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip` by spec 0050 S9.4; and the inventory says the folder holds 15 CSVs, seven of them the science data under `data/raw/final/` (the table's entries, now kit paths, keep their texts), the other eight earlier exploratory work under `data/raw/`, and that the archive's three beam-shape descriptions are in `data/reference/shapes/`. Every other line keeps its text. (3) The locator (.spec-md §3.21). New `Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs` in `namespace BerremanTests`, compiled directly before `MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` (one `<Compile>` line in `BerremanTests.fsproj`, no comment): `type CommittedKit = | OpticsMuellerKit`, the committed reference kits under the repository's `data/` folder, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.4 and saying that S10.2 moves it to `BerremanTestSupport`; and `member this.tryFindFolder : KitFolder option`: from `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, each folder upward in turn until one holds `Berreman/Berreman.slnx`, which is the repository root; the answer is `KitFolder (FolderName <root>/data/optics-mueller)` (`KitFolder`, step 122) when that folder exists, and `None` when no folder upward holds the solution or the kit folder is absent. It writes nothing and reads no environment variable. No other case, member or file is added; AT-2's kit adds its case when S12.2 commits that kit. (4) The reads, in `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`. `loadDataSet` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:loadDataSet`) becomes `loadDataSet (file : KitRelativePath) : MuellerRawRow list`: `OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, then `(KitProxy.create folder).readOnlyView.readDataFile file` (steps 126, 128 and 131: a read-only view writes nothing, not even `.oc/`), then `(BuiltInProfileChoice PhoneRoiCsvProfile).mapText` (step 303) of the file's `text`, answering its `CapturePoints` rows; no kit folder, a `KitError`, an `ExperimentDataError` or another `MappedPoints` case fails the test with what it says, as the helper fails today. Its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.4. The seven data sets become test-local `KitRelativePath` values bound ahead of the members, each born by `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123) of its kit path, an `Error` failing the test: `lpLpFile` `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv`, `lpCplFile` `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv`, `cplLpFile` `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv`, `cplCplDay1File` `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv`, `cplCplDay2File` `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv`, `darknessChecksFile` `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv`, `bullshitChecksFile` `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv`, the mapping `MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName` holds. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` and `section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly` drop `MuellerDataStore.createArchiveBacked ()`, bind `load` to `loadDataSet` and load each data set's file in place of its case (`load LpLpFamily` becomes `load lpLpFile`, …); every comment of theirs that names the archive store names the kit's lab files, and their bodies and assertions are otherwise unchanged. `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` becomes `the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts`: through `loadDataSet`, `lpLpFile` 209, `lpCplFile` 209, `cplLpFile` 209, `cplCplDay1File` 170, `cplCplDay2File` 57, `darknessChecksFile` 6, `bullshitChecksFile` 2 rows, its comment naming the inventory of `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md` (spec 0042 §6). New fact `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte`: through `(KitProxy.create folder).readOnlyView` over `OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, `readDataFile` of each of these kit paths answers a file whose `contentHash` is the `ContentHash` (step 24) of its former archive entry's hex SHA-256: `data/raw/cpl_cpl.csv` `c1cbbde1c7b77acf6d23f972bb85f679e0072779d396a49aaf02b1d92e447eb5`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_big_center.csv` `515d16bb7a375b734038a8dbc6730bb6e726d99bfd11d954b986adf81d47b7b8`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_center.csv` `f2d97088f562cb5e8097b827b6774d1ba88baefd25b15f312515ad77b958d703`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_small_center.csv` `aa18398266782f7cedf15008a8e66beff28f89c81304d68e062d6f8f8216c78b`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_standard_ellipse.csv` `94b8ef01770a12617f55e1b329d1513670044cee3c0c5e340e9c5826588372e5`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_095.csv` `59a7b7d7f223bf28c4623299df6a530f63787570eb346935b76d468228fbd3bc`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_105.csv` `4fd5b0b5fc09cd291d57732edfd1f582c37119c230c7550d100ebd4a94493336`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv` `53de707ce70b9792d024db41ae39eac8506656916c97b0db1ef9f1512ef50813`; `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv` `f2f7d28d881b57f5760562d030c12d1e554c7c8cc82d6657e9e4fb5c281c2c9e`; `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv` `9920ae4768558bd865c0190878adf97dde9901e9436a299a0c49e7d48ed39664`; `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv` `fcace7c401940d6b4a84347acd2b2afb925f5ea9c2c57e64fcc6d88e4ad26b2e`; `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv` `9737ebe6534446ce3d4e1bcbcda222b88fae2d3c58de0cc8db1d322a5c002f39`; `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv` `3b11f42dd67f29a09275b13442849415c82d7a967f5d5933713abb06dfb43cc2`; `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv` `d014c90144a98eb1949d30716be1f01049ec9763e0e3b94ceb68d2e43c4b1ba8`; `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` `0fc29a63fd7de90b85842af5020cd79fb1e74ac2d24b49f7c7673cbead82cd81`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_095.json` `f8b15f8069d4986c6a68924349c66b0455b7a976da441adfdf5620af3d9e9425`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_105.json` `e254c679a2861bf5f625a03b5d62c2e6a6f3aac38f29afdfba632521370bedeb`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_v1.json` `76bb56c20c63356640ad286f1f1b109eaa9714f7ea16c2606086705d88854f2d`. The class doc's first sentence names the Phone ROI CSV parser in place of 'the archive-backed `MuellerDataStore`', and its spec 0044 §8 bullet on `data.zip` says the measured data is the optics-mueller kit's lab files, found from the repository root and read read-only through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (spec 0050 S9.4); its other bullets keep their text. The trailing comments of the two `open OpticalConstructor.Storage…` lines are deleted. `muellerCsvFixture`, `malformedMuellerCsv`, `the real parseMuellerCsv parses a committed multi-column CSV fixture into MuellerRawRows (description elevated to Angle)` and `the real parseMuellerCsv maps a malformed file to a typed MuellerDataError, never a throw` are unchanged; the mock data proxy, its three facts and the two `tryLoadFromArchive` facts, which read no archive file, go with the seam in step 331.", "acceptance": "After the lab files move, `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` MUST hold the fifteen CSVs and `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/` the three shape files, each byte for byte its former `data.zip` entry under the `-text !eol` rule, `Berreman/Data/` and the `data.zip` `Content` link MUST be gone, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read the kit's lab files read-only through the Phone ROI CSV profile from the repository root; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers unchanged, `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` renamed `the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts` and `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte` added, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": [".gitattributes", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_big_center.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_center.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_small_center.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_standard_ellipse.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_095.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_105.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_095.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_105.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_v1.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md", "Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "successor": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts", "obligations": ["S94-LAB-FILES-IN-KIT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S94-LAB-FILES-IN-KIT"]}], "