{"number":331,"anchor":"RETIRE_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-S94c","id":"STORE_XDUO_0009","name":"MuellerDataProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","BerremanTests"],"depends_on":[330],"how_to":"The archive-keyed load seam goes, with the data-set identity it was keyed by, the archive path, the two archive error cases and the archive store (001 §R '`MuellerDataSet` (a hard-coded DU of data sets), the archive-keyed `MuellerDataProxy` and `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/`. `parseMuellerCsv` is reused as an import profile'; 001 §S9 'DELETE the `MuellerDataSet` DU and the archive-keyed `MuellerDataProxy`'; 001 §T 'From section 9' (both greps), which this step makes true; .spec-md §0.1, rows `MuellerDataStore.fs` and `MuellerReconstruction.fs`; the S9.4 brief). After step 330 nothing reads them but the facts that test them. This step only deletes: no replacement seam, wrapper, path-keyed variant or compatibility alias is added. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: delete `MuellerDataSet` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerDataSet`), `MuellerArchivePath` (`:MuellerArchivePath`) and `MuellerDataProxy` (`:MuellerDataProxy`) with their docs, and the cases `ArchiveUnreadableErr` and `DataSetMissingErr` of `MuellerDataError` (`:MuellerDataError`). `MuellerDataError` keeps `MalformedRowErr` and `EmptyFileErr`; its doc becomes one to three lines: a typed failure of parsing a Phone ROI CSV text, never a throw (spec 0050 S9.4 removed the archive cases). The comment block that opens the seam ('Spec 0042 (005, ADD_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0009) — the Mueller measured-data LOAD seam …', `MuellerReconstruction.fs:293-320`, which also tells spec 0044 §8.3's re-key from `Experiments.DataFilePath`) becomes one to three lines: the capture rows of a Phone ROI CSV file, read through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (spec 0042; spec 0050 S9.4 deleted the archive-keyed seam). `MuellerExperimentLabel`, `CaptureIndex` and `MuellerRawRow` are unchanged. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs`: delete the `type MuellerDataSet with` extension holding `archiveEntryName` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName`, its doc naming `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/README.md`), `committedArchive`, `tryLoadFromArchive` and `createArchiveBacked` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:createArchiveBacked`) with their docs, and `open System.IO` and `open System.IO.Compression`, which nothing left reads; the `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction` line loses its trailing comment. The module doc becomes one to three lines: the Phone ROI CSV parser, the body of the `Phone ROI CSV` import profile (spec 0042 step 6; spec 0050 S9.2), whose archive store spec 0050 S9.4 deleted. `CaptureCsvRow` and `DataFileText.parseMuellerCsv` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv`) are unchanged, their rules and diagnostics included. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: in `ChosenImportProfile.mapText` (step 303) the `PhoneRoiCsvProfile` arm loses its two arms for `ArchiveUnreadableErr` and `DataSetMissingErr`, and its doc the words about them; `MalformedRowErr r` stays `MalformedDataFileErr r` and `EmptyFileErr r` `EmptyDataFileErr r`. (4) In `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` the comment above `MuellerDataStore.fs`'s `<Compile>` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:46-49`, naming the step-005 `MuellerDataProxy` and `createFileBacked`) is deleted and nothing is added. (5) Tests. In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` delete the seam's five facts, `a mock MuellerDataProxy loads canned capture rows through its exact tryLoadDataSet signature`, `an unseeded data set yields a typed MuellerDataError from tryLoadDataSet, never a throw`, `a MuellerDataProxy compares by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)`, `tryLoadFromArchive maps an absent archive to a typed ArchiveUnreadable, never a throw` and `tryLoadFromArchive maps an archive without the requested entry to a typed DataSetMissing, never a throw`, with `cannedRows`, `makeMockData`, `seededDataMock` and the comment block above them (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:79-105`), and `open System.IO.Compression` and `open System.IO`, which nothing left reads (the `DataSetMissing` fact wrote its throw-away archive under `%TEMP%`). Nothing replaces the five facts: the parser facts (`the real parseMuellerCsv parses a committed multi-column CSV fixture into MuellerRawRows (description elevated to Angle)`, `the real parseMuellerCsv maps a malformed file to a typed MuellerDataError, never a throw`) and step 330's kit facts cover what remains. In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`, the comment in `both proxies compare by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)` names the `ExperimentDataProxy / MuellerSolverProxy` convention, dropping the retired proxy; no code changes there. After this step `git grep -n -E \"MuellerDataProxy|MuellerDataSet|MuellerArchivePath|ArchiveUnreadableErr|DataSetMissingErr|createArchiveBacked|tryLoadFromArchive|committedArchive|archiveEntryName|tryLoadDataSet\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -w -E \"LpLpFamily|LpCplFamily|CplLpFamily|CplCplDay1|CplCplDay2|DarknessChecks|BullshitChecks\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -F \"Data/MuellerMatrix\" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -w \"DataFilePath\" -- Berreman/` find nothing.","acceptance":"After the retirement, `MuellerDataSet`, `MuellerArchivePath`, `MuellerDataProxy`, `ArchiveUnreadableErr`, `DataSetMissingErr`, `archiveEntryName`, `committedArchive`, `tryLoadFromArchive` and `createArchiveBacked` MUST be gone, with the five facts that test them, `parseMuellerCsv` MUST stay as the Phone ROI CSV profile's body, and `git grep -n -E \"MuellerDataProxy|MuellerDataSet|MuellerArchivePath|ArchiveUnreadableErr|DataSetMissingErr|createArchiveBacked|tryLoadFromArchive|committedArchive|archiveEntryName|tryLoadDataSet\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -w -E \"LpLpFamily|LpCplFamily|CplLpFamily|CplCplDay1|CplCplDay2|DarknessChecks|BullshitChecks\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -F \"Data/MuellerMatrix\" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -w \"DataFilePath\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers unchanged and the count falling by 5; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj","Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"delete","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.a mock MuellerDataProxy loads canned capture rows through its exact tryLoadDataSet signature","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"op":"delete","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.an unseeded data set yields a typed MuellerDataError from tryLoadDataSet, never a throw","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"op":"delete","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.a MuellerDataProxy compares by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"op":"delete","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.tryLoadFromArchive maps an absent archive to a typed ArchiveUnreadable, never a throw","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"op":"delete","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.tryLoadFromArchive maps an archive without the requested entry to a typed DataSetMissing, never a throw","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerDataSet","op":"retire","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"],"preserves_obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerArchivePath","op":"retire","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"],"preserves_obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerDataProxy","op":"retire","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"],"preserves_obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerDataError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.archiveEntryName","op":"retire","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"],"preserves_obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.tryLoadFromArchive","op":"retire","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"],"preserves_obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.createArchiveBacked","op":"retire","obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"],"preserves_obligations":["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S9.4 -- The optics-mueller lab files move into the kit folder"}
{"number": 332, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [331], "how_to": "The uniaxial crystal builder becomes product physics on its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16: reusable tensor construction lives on product parameter records while the required ground-truth/design builders retain their test-support home; the S10.1 brief 'UniaxialParameters gets the uniaxial builder MuellerInverseTests uses'). Two copies exist today, `buildUniaxialGyrotropic` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:buildUniaxialGyrotropic`) and its body-for-body duplicates `buildLangasite` (`LangasiteInverseTests.fs:buildLangasite`) and the fact-local `buildUniaxial` of `BiaxialInverseTests`' `the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one` (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:433`); all three go (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs`, `UniaxialParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:UniaxialParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is the deleted builder's: `OpticalProperties.type_3_4_6_Crystal (EpsValue.fromRefractionIndex this.ordinaryIndex) (EpsValue.fromRefractionIndex this.extraordinaryIndex) this.g11 this.g33`, so diag(n_o², n_o², n_e²) and diag(g₁₁, g₁₁, g₃₃) stay the engine's own (`OpticalProperties/Active.fs:type_3_4_6_Crystal`). Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of a uniaxial gyrotropic crystal (classes 3/32/4/422/6/622) with these four constants, through the engine's class 3/4/6 builder (spec 0050 §3.16). `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalProperties.Active`, which Domain already reaches through its `Analytics` reference (`MaterialLibrary.fs:12` opens it). The module doc's sentence that `OpticalConstructor.Domain` does not reference `OpticalProperties`, so that nothing here names a crystal class (`MuellerInverse.fs:15-20`), becomes: the forward proxy takes a caller-supplied `'Parameters -> OpticalProperties` builder, each parameter record carries its crystal class's builder as `opticalProperties` (spec 0050 §3.16), and no named material lives here. No other line of the file changes. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`: delete `buildUniaxialGyrotropic` with its doc; `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`; in `orientForCut carries the optic axis from the surface normal into the surface plane` `props` is `quartz.opticalProperties`. (3) `Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs`: delete `buildLangasite` with its doc; `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs`: in `the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one`, delete the local `buildUniaxial`; `uniaxialForward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member evaluates the same expression the three builders did. No test is added or removed. `LangasiteInverseTests`, whose facts drive the uniaxial member through `forward`, is the cheapest class that exercises it.", "acceptance": "After the promotion, `UniaxialParameters.opticalProperties` MUST be the one uniaxial builder, `buildUniaxialGyrotropic`, `buildLangasite` and `BiaxialInverseTests`' local `buildUniaxial` MUST be gone, and the three uniaxial forward models MUST read the member; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.a positive g11 moves the transmission maximum toward smaller analyzer angles", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.n_e and g33 are structurally invisible at z-cut normal incidence", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.the langasite plate measurement determines g11", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.the recovered parameters reproduce all six measured intensities within the noise the data carries", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.the residual Jacobian shows n_o is unobservable against the data's noise floor", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.orientForCut carries the optic axis from the surface normal into the surface plane", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.UniaxialParameters.opticalProperties", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.buildUniaxialGyrotropic", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.buildLangasite", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 333, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [332], "how_to": "The triclinic crystal builder moves onto its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16; the S10.1 brief 'TriclinicParameters gets BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `MuellerInverse.fs`, `TriclinicParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:TriclinicParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is `buildTriclinic`'s (`BiaxialSample.fs:buildTriclinic`): `{ eps = Eps.fromRefractionIndex (this.index1, this.index2, this.index3); mu = Mu.vacuum; rho = Rho.type_1_Crystal this.g11 this.g22 this.g33 this.g23 this.g13 this.g12 }`, the engine's own biaxial permittivity and full symmetric gyration tensor (`OpticalProperties/Active.fs:type_1_Crystal`). Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of a triclinic (class 1) gyrotropic crystal with these nine constants (spec 0050 §3.16). (2) Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs MUST retain buildTriclinic with its concrete parameter and return signature; its body MUST become a call to p.opticalProperties. Only the tensor-construction expression moves to the product member; the ground-truth/design builder itself MUST remain in this module and move with it to BerremanTestSupport in step 345, as 001 §Q requires. The old tensor body MUST be deleted in this step, leaving one implementation of the arithmetic. Its short contract comment MUST describe the builder without claiming a product destination. (3) BiaxialInverseTests and FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests MUST continue calling buildTriclinic for their forward models and direct tensor assertions; no test is deleted, no expected value or tolerance changes, and no product project references test support.  BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member evaluates the same record expression. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s, 5 facts) is the cheapest class whose facts drive the member through `forward`; `BiaxialInverseTests` (997 s) is not selected, as the S10.1 brief directs.", "acceptance": "After extracting shared tensor construction, TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties MUST hold the single kernel and BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic MUST remain a test-side caller of that kernel, preserving every forward-model result and its required move to BerremanTestSupport; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.a plate cut perpendicular to an optic axis is a pure circular retarder, and that is what buys the signal", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the order ambiguity is real on the principal cuts and is broken by the optic-axis cuts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 334, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [333], "how_to": "The absorbing triclinic builder moves onto its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16; the S10.1 brief 'AbsorbingTriclinicParameters gets AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `MuellerInverse.fs`, `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is `buildAbsorbing`'s (`AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:buildAbsorbing`) with `p` read as `this`: ε is the complex symmetric matrix with diagonal (n₁², n₂², n₃²) + i(ε″₁₁, ε″₂₂, ε″₃₃) and off-diagonal i·ε″₁₂, i·ε″₁₃, i·ε″₂₃ through `Eps.create`, μ is `Mu.vacuum`, and ρ is the purely imaginary symmetric matrix of the six gyration components through `Rho.create`, the same entries in the same order. Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of an absorbing triclinic gyrotropic crystal; ε″ is general in the ε′ frame and ρ stays imaginary (spec 0050 §3.16; specs/0044/.manual/018-absorbing-biaxial-inverse.md). (2) Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs MUST retain buildAbsorbing with its concrete parameter and return signature; its body MUST become a call to p.opticalProperties. Only the tensor-construction expression moves to the product member; the ground-truth/design builder itself MUST remain in this module and move with it to BerremanTestSupport in step 346, as 001 §Q requires. The old tensor body MUST be deleted in this step, leaving one implementation of the arithmetic. Its short contract comment MUST describe the builder without claiming a product destination. (3) AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests and AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests MUST continue calling buildAbsorbing for their forward models and direct tensor assertions; no test is deleted, no expected value or tolerance changes, and no product project references test support.  BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member builds the same complex entries by the same operations. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s, 7 facts) is the cheapest class whose facts drive the member; `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` (946 s) is not selected.", "acceptance": "After extracting shared tensor construction, AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties MUST hold the single kernel and AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing MUST remain a test-side caller of that kernel, preserving every forward-model result and its required move to BerremanTestSupport; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing sample attenuates, and every configuration stays physically realizable", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.all fifteen parameters are observable and the problem is conditioned well enough to solve", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 335, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [334], "how_to": "The fit machinery gets its product home, and the configuration builder and the observation generator move first (001 §Q AT-2 'Promoted to product (`OpticalConstructor.Optimization`) … `observeWith`'; 001 §S10 first bullet; the S10.1 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs`, `module MuellerFitting` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `MuellerInverseSolver.fs`: one `<Compile Include=\"MuellerFitting.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`, no comment. Its module doc, one to three lines: the Mueller-matrix fit machinery the inverse-problem suites, the study engine and the Planner share, moved from `BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` by spec 0050 S10.1 (spec 0044 manual tasks 010-016). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) `type MuellerFitError = | ObservationForwardErr of ForwardModelError`, doc one line: a typed failure of generating observations or fitting them, never a throw. Steps 337, 339, 341 and 342 add one case each, in their own words; no other case is added here. (3) `configurationOf` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:configurationOf`) moves with its incidence and azimuth as `float<deg>` (`Berreman.Constants.deg`), because a bare `double` beside our types is ELEV003 / ELEV010 and a measured `float<deg>` is the form `SampleAzimuth.degree` and `Angle.degree` already take (`MuellerInverse.fs:SampleAzimuth`; specs/0048/.manual/002-elevation-ledger.jsonl): `configurationOf (cut : SampleCut) (thickness : Thickness) (incidence : float<deg>) (azimuth : float<deg>) (observable : Observable) (waveLength : WaveLength) : MeasurementConfiguration`, with `incidenceAngle = Angle.degree incidence |> IncidenceAngle.create` and `azimuth = SampleAzimuth.degree azimuth`, the other fields as today. (4) `observeWith` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:observeWith`) moves as `observeWith (forward : ForwardModelProxy<'Parameters>) (truth : 'Parameters) (configurations : MeasurementConfiguration list) : Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`: each configuration in order through `forward.muellerOf c truth`, in the fold `MuellerInverse.forwardModels` uses (`MuellerInverse.fs:forwardModels`); the first `Error e` answers `Error (ObservationForwardErr e)` and evaluates nothing after it; otherwise `Ok` of `{ configuration = c; measured = m }` in configuration order. (5) `Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs`: delete `configurationOf` and `observeWith`, and add to the module `let expectOk (result : Result<'Value, MuellerFitError>) : 'Value` answering the `Ok` value and failing the test with `failwith $\"%A{e}\"` on `Error e`; its doc, one line: a moved product call's value, or the test fails with its typed error (spec 0050 S10.1). It is the one test-side assertion every later move uses. (6) Callers. The local `configuration` helpers of `MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` keep their `double` parameters and pass `(incidenceDeg * 1.0<deg>) (azimuthDeg * 1.0<deg>)` to `configurationOf`. The `observe` helpers of `MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs` become `observeWith forward <truth> configurations |> expectOk`, so their signatures and every fact using them are unchanged. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): a multiplication by `1.0<deg>` is exact, so `Angle.degree` receives the same double, and the forward calls run in the same order. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` is the cheapest class that builds configurations through `configurationOf` and observes them through `observeWith`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `MuellerFitError`, `configurationOf` (incidence and azimuth in `float<deg>`) and `observeWith` (a `Result` whose first forward failure is `ObservationForwardErr`), compiled directly after `MuellerInverseSolver.fs`, `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare neither function and MUST declare `expectOk`, and every suite MUST build its configurations and observations through the product; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.every plate in this design is one a vendor will actually sell", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.a plate cut perpendicular to an optic axis is a pure circular retarder, and that is what buys the signal", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the order ambiguity is real on the principal cuts and is broken by the optic-axis cuts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.configurationOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.observeWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.expectOk", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.configurationOf", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.observeWith", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 336, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [335], "how_to": "The residual closures, the Jacobian adapter and the generic scaling move into `MuellerFitting` (001 §Q AT-2 '`observeWith`, `residualFor`, `throughputResidualFor`; `scalingAround`'; the S10.1 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) Into `MuellerFitting.fs` (step 335), after `observeWith`, with their signatures and bodies unchanged: `residualFor` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:residualFor`), the total, fixed-length 15-per-observation closure with its 1.0e3 penalty; `throughputResidualFor` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:throughputResidualFor`), 16 per observation, the 16th the log-throughput difference; `residualJacobianAt` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:residualJacobianAt`), the `FitQuality.residualJacobian` adapter over `ScaledVector`; and `scalingAround` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:scalingAround`). Every signature already speaks `ForwardModelProxy`, `MuellerObservation`, `ParameterScaling`, `ScaledVector`, `ResidualVector` and `ResidualJacobian`, the last three `[<NumericCarrier>]` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualVector`, `:ScaledVector`, `:ResidualJacobian`), so no shape changes. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. The throughput closure keeps one line saying the log term restores the isotropic absorption that normalization discards (specs/0044/.manual/018-absorbing-biaxial-inverse.md). (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the four; its `fitWithResidual`, `fitObservations` and `fitAbsorbingObservations`, which step 337 moves, call the product closures. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. The generic `scalingAround` has no caller in BerremanTests today: `BiaxialSample.scalingAround`, `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbingScalingAround` and `MuellerInverseTests.scalingAround` build their own one-argument specialisations and shadow it. It moves because 001 §Q AT-2 lists it for the study engine (S11). The shadowing comment above `MuellerInverseTests.scalingAround` ('It deliberately shadows the harness's general `scalingAround`') names `MuellerFitting.scalingAround`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the bodies are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` reaches `residualFor` and `residualJacobianAt`, and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` reaches `throughputResidualFor`, the two cheapest classes that do.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `residualFor`, `throughputResidualFor`, `residualJacobianAt` and `scalingAround` with unchanged signatures and bodies, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.all fifteen parameters are observable and the problem is conditioned well enough to solve", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.residualFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.residualJacobianAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.scalingAround", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.residualFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.throughputResidualFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.residualJacobianAt", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.scalingAround", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 337, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [336], "how_to": "The search box, the fit record and the three fit runners move into `MuellerFitting` (001 §Q AT-2 '`scalingAround`, `fitWithResidual`, `fitObservations`, `fitAbsorbingObservations`'; the S10.1 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) Into `MuellerFitting.fs`, after `scalingAround`: `SearchBox` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:SearchBox`) with `halfWidth`, unchanged; and the harness's `InverseFit<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:InverseFit`) RENAMED `MuellerFitData<'Parameters>`, because `InverseFit` is already the module `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.InverseFit` (`InverseFit.fs:InverseFit`) and names are unique, not qualified (ELEV014 / ELEV015; the S10.1 brief): the same `[<ReferenceEquality>]` record `{ recovered; solution : NonlinearSolution; scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>; residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector }` with the members `chiSquared` and `rmsResidual`, bodies unchanged. (2) `MuellerFitError` gains `NonlinearFitErr of NonlinearSolverError` (the solve failed). (3) `fitWithResidual (box : SearchBox) (residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector) (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) : Result<MuellerFitData<'Parameters>, MuellerFitError>`: the request is today's (`InverseFitHarness.fs:fitWithResidual`: start at the zero vector, bounds ±`box.halfWidth`, `IterationCount 400`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-12`, through `MuellerInverseSolver.createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt ()`), `Ok` carries the same record, and a solver `Error e` answers `Error (NonlinearFitErr e)`. `fitObservations` and `fitAbsorbingObservations` keep their parameters and answer `fitWithResidual`'s `Result` over `residualFor` and `throughputResidualFor`. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (4) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes `SearchBox`, `InverseFit` and the three runners. `NoisyExperiment.fit`, `fitReportOf` and `predictedRelativeErrors`, which steps 341 and 342 move, take `MuellerFitData<'Parameters>`. (5) Callers unwrap with `expectOk`: `fitObservations … |> expectOk` in `BiaxialInverseTests` (`recoverFromNoisy` and its two fit facts) and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`; `fitAbsorbingObservations … |> expectOk` in `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` and in `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.recoverFromNoisy`; `MuellerInverseTests`' own `fitObservations` wrapper calls `MuellerFitting.fitObservations forward box observations (scalingAround start) |> expectOk` and keeps its tuple, and its `recoverFromNoisy` record literal is the renamed record. The `MuellerInverseTests` comments that place the fit driver in the harness say where it now is: the class doc's 'The fit driver both suites use lives in `InverseFitHarness`' names `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting`, the wrapper's doc 'the shared harness runner' names `MuellerFitting.fitObservations`, and the trailing comment of `open BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness` is deleted. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the request, the solver and the record are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` runs `fitObservations` and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` runs `fitAbsorbingObservations`, both through `fitWithResidual`, the two cheapest classes that fit.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `SearchBox`, `MuellerFitData<'Parameters>` and the three fit runners answering `Result<MuellerFitData<'Parameters>, MuellerFitError>` (a solver failure being `NonlinearFitErr`), `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them and no type named `InverseFit`, and every suite MUST fit through the product; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.SearchBox", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.fitWithResidual", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.fitObservations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.fitAbsorbingObservations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.SearchBox", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFit", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitWithResidual", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitObservations", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitAbsorbingObservations", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 338, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [337], "how_to": "The relative error and the per-parameter recovery errors move into `MuellerFitting` (the S10.1 brief 'RelativeError … recoveryErrors'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) New in `MuellerFitting.fs`, after `fitAbsorbingObservations`: `type QuantityValue = | QuantityValue of double` with `member this.value`, doc one line: a recovered quantity's value in its own physical units (an index, a gyration or ε″ component, a birefringence). It exists because `RelativeError.between` took two bare `double`s beside our type (ELEV010), and steps 341 and 342 read every recovered value through it. (2) `RelativeError` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RelativeError`) moves with `value`, and `between` becomes `static member between (actual : QuantityValue) (expected : QuantityValue) : RelativeError`, the same `|actual − expected| / |expected|` on the two values. `recoveryErrors` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:recoveryErrors`) moves after it with its signature, each axis's error being `RelativeError.between` of `QuantityValue (a.read recovered)` and `QuantityValue (a.read truth)`. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (3) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes `RelativeError` and `recoveryErrors`. Until step 341 moves them, `statisticsFor`'s `bias` and `worst` call `RelativeError.between` over `QuantityValue` of the same doubles, and `describeErrors` reads the product type. `MuellerInverseTests.relativeError` becomes `RelativeError.between (QuantityValue actual) (QuantityValue expected)`. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the division runs on the same doubles. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` asserts on `recoveryErrors`, the cheapest class that does.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `QuantityValue`, `RelativeError` (whose `between` takes two `QuantityValue`s) and `recoveryErrors`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare neither `RelativeError` nor `recoveryErrors`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.QuantityValue", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.RelativeError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.recoveryErrors", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.RelativeError", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.recoveryErrors", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number":339,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S101h","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","BerremanTests"],"depends_on":[338],"how_to":"The complete bench-noise data and the transparent functions MUST move from Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs to OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs, as 001 §Q and §S10 specify. Domain retains only detector parameter axes (.spec-md §3.23). This step moves the transparent path; step 340 moves the absorbing one. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs`, `module BenchNoise` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `MuellerFitting.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment), opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels` for the parameter-axis projection. Its module doc, one to three lines: the bench measurement-error model, angle errors filed against the nominal configuration and detector errors on the normalized elements, uniform max errors drawn from a seeded provider; the magnitudes and their sources are specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md and, for the throughput, 019-absorbing-biaxial-noisy-tests.md (moved by spec 0050 S10.1). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) Before NoiseSeed, MOVE AngleUncertainty (angle, value, degrees, degree), ElementUncertainty, ThroughputUncertainty and NoiseParam (rotation, element, throughput, decentLab, noiseless) from InverseFitHarness.fs, with their bodies and numerical constants unchanged, deleting all four source declarations in this step. The four types MUST have their only product declarations in Optimization/BenchNoise.fs. Add their source-type parameterValue members, and NoiseParam.parameterAxes MUST call ItemParameterAxis.detectorNoiseAxes over those converted values; names and ordering are shared with Domain, with no duplicated axis construction. The harness and every resolved consumer MUST open BenchNoise, retaining their behavior. `NoiseSeed` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:NoiseSeed`) with `value`, unchanged. New `type UniformDeviate = | UniformDeviate of double` with `member this.value`, doc one line: one draw, uniform on [−1, +1]; it exists because the provider's field `unit -> double` is ELEV008. `UniformDeviateProvider` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:UniformDeviateProvider`) keeps `[<ReferenceEquality>]` and becomes `{ nextDeviate : unit -> UniformDeviate }`; `fromSeed (seed : NoiseSeed)` keeps `System.Random(seed.value)` and answers `2.0 * rng.NextDouble() - 1.0 |> UniformDeviate` per draw. `disturb` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:disturb`) keeps its signature and its signed `IncidenceAngle + Angle` excursion, its wobble `noise.rotation.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value |> Angle`. `misread` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:misread`) answers `Result<MuellerMatrix, MuellerFitError>`: the same element loop over `m.normalized` (row by row, m₀₀ left at 1, each other element plus `noise.element.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value`), and a normalization `Error e` is `Error (MuellerNormalizationErr e)`. `noisyObserveWith` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:noisyObserveWith`) keeps its five parameters and answers `Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`: one provider from the seed, each nominal configuration in order disturbed, sent through `forward.muellerOf` (an `Error e` is `ObservationForwardErr e`), misread, and filed against the NOMINAL configuration; the first `Error` stops the walk. The draws are taken in exactly today's order, two for `disturb` then fifteen for `misread` per configuration, so a seed gives the same stream bit for bit. (3) `MuellerFitError` gains `MuellerNormalizationErr of InversionError` (a generated matrix could not be normalized). (4) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes `NoiseSeed`, `UniformDeviateProvider`, `disturb`, `misread` and `noisyObserveWith`, and the measurement-error banner above `NoiseSeed` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:59-110`), whose narrative and sources specs/0044/.manual/011 already records (AGENTS.md 'Document a decision once'). Until step 340, its `misreadAbsolute` reads `(draws.nextDeviate ()).value` and its `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` calls the product `disturb`; `ensembleSeeds` maps the product `NoiseSeed`. (5) Callers. `MuellerInverseTests`: `firstTen` reads `(d.nextDeviate ()).value`, the direct `misread` read pipes `|> expectOk`, and `noisyObserve` is `noisyObserveWith forward quartz noise seed configurations |> expectOk`; the comments that send the reader to 'the commentary above `NoiseParam.decentLab`' or say the model 'lives in `InverseFitHarness`' (the class doc, the banner above `blindStart`, the one above the noisy facts) name `BenchNoise` and specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md. `BiaxialInverseTests.recoverFromNoisy` pipes `noisyObserveWith … |> expectOk`, and its two comments that place the measurement-error model or its commentary in `InverseFitHarness` (the noisy-section banner, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs:233-234`, and the ensemble fact's 'see the commentary in `InverseFitHarness`', `:829-830`) name `BenchNoise` and specs/0044/.manual/011 likewise. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the generator, the draw order and every arithmetic expression are unchanged. No BerremanTests fact is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests` (about 456 s) is the one class below `BiaxialInverseTests` that reaches `disturb`, `misread`, `noisyObserveWith` and the provider: `the measurement-error model is reproducible, bounded, and files data against the NOMINAL angles` drives each directly and the ensemble fact drives `noisyObserveWith`. In OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs add `the promoted bench budgets equal the detector catalogue defaults`: NoiseParam.decentLab MUST retain rotation 0.2 degrees, element 0.005 and throughput 0.01, NoiseParam.noiseless MUST retain zero in all three, and each shipped detector's noise axes MUST equal NoiseParam.decentLab.parameterAxes. Use the repository tolerance helpers for floating-point conversions. This fact MUST also verify that the four types' declaring assembly is Softellect.Berreman.OpticalConstructor.Optimization; numerical behavior is separately exercised by the seeded-noise facts.","acceptance":"After the move, `BenchNoise.fs` MUST declare `NoiseSeed`, `UniformDeviate`, `UniformDeviateProvider`, `disturb`, `misread` and `noisyObserveWith` (the last two answering `Result`s with `MuellerNormalizationErr` and `ObservationForwardErr`), compiled directly after `MuellerFitting.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them and no measurement-error banner; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass. The four noise data types MUST be declared only in Optimization/BenchNoise.fs; `the promoted bench budgets equal the detector catalogue defaults` MUST pass, adding one constructor test, with unchanged seeded observations.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.the measurement-error model is reproducible, bounded, and files data against the NOMINAL angles","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers every constant, and its scatter IS what one fit's own covariance predicts","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests.the promoted bench budgets equal the detector catalogue defaults","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemModelsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemModelsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.NoiseSeed","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.UniformDeviate","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.UniformDeviateProvider","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.disturb","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.misread","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.noisyObserveWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.NoiseSeed","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.UniformDeviateProvider","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.disturb","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.misread","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.noisyObserveWith","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.AngleUncertainty","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.AngleUncertainty","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.ElementUncertainty","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.ElementUncertainty","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.ThroughputUncertainty","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.ThroughputUncertainty","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"},{"symbol":"BerremanTests.NoiseParam","op":"retire","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"preserves_obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.NoiseParam","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.AngleUncertainty.parameterValue","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.ElementUncertainty.parameterValue","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.ThroughputUncertainty.parameterValue","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.NoiseParam.parameterAxes","op":"create","obligations":["S101-NOISE-MOVE"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs"}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 340, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [339], "how_to": "The absorbing half of the noise model moves into `BenchNoise` (001 §Q AT-2; .spec-md §3.23), which makes 001 §T 'From section 10' true: `git grep -n -F \"let noisyObserveAbsoluteWith\" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/` finds nothing, as every section from S10.2 on asserts. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) Into `BenchNoise.fs`, after `misread`: `misreadAbsolute` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:misreadAbsolute`) answering `Result<MuellerMatrix, MuellerFitError>`: the throughput draw FIRST (`trueThroughput * (1.0 + noise.throughput.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value)`), then the fifteen element draws in `misread`'s order, each reported element `reportedThroughput * (n.element i j + noise.element.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value)` and m₀₀ the reported throughput; a normalization `Error e` is `Error (MuellerNormalizationErr e)`. After `noisyObserveWith`: `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:noisyObserveAbsoluteWith`), the same walk as `noisyObserveWith` with `misreadAbsolute`, answering `Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. `misreadAbsolute` keeps one line saying the throughput draw comes first so a seed reproduces the experiment (specs/0044/.manual/019-absorbing-biaxial-noisy-tests.md). (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes both. `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.recoverFromNoisy` pipes `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith forward absorbing noise seed fullConfigurations |> expectOk`. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the draws are taken in the same order by the same arithmetic. No test is added or removed. The absorbing path is reached by `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` alone (946 s, its one ensemble fact), so that class is selected here and nowhere else in S10.1, as the S10.1 brief allows for a function reached nowhere else.", "acceptance": "After the move, `BenchNoise.fs` MUST declare `misreadAbsolute` and `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` answering `Result`s, `git grep -n -F \"let noisyObserveAbsoluteWith\" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST find nothing (001 §T 'From section 10'), and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` MUST draw its observations through the product; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers the absorption far better than the optical activity", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.misreadAbsolute", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.noisyObserveAbsoluteWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.misreadAbsolute", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.noisyObserveAbsoluteWith", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 341, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [340], "how_to": "The ensemble statistics move into Optimization (001 §Q AT-2 '`RecoveredQuantity`, `RecoveryStatistics`, `statisticsFor`'; the S10.1 brief 'RecoveredQuantity, RecoveryStatistics, NoisyExperiment, statisticsFor, standardErrorOfMean, rowFor'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Names are `ParameterName`s and values `QuantityValue`s (step 338), because a bare `string` or `double` in a record field or beside our types is ELEV008 / ELEV010. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs`, `module RecoveryEnsembles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `BenchNoise.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment). Its module doc, one to three lines: what an ensemble of noisy experiments says about each recovered quantity, moved by spec 0050 S10.1 (specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) In it: `RecoveredQuantity<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RecoveredQuantity`) becomes `{ name : ParameterName; valueIn : 'Parameters -> QuantityValue }`, `ofAxis axis` reading `QuantityValue (axis.read p)` and `derived (name : ParameterName) (valueIn : 'Parameters -> QuantityValue)`. `RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RecoveryStatistics`) keeps its fields with `mean` and `absoluteScatter` as `QuantityValue`; `describe` renders the same text from their values. `NoisyExperiment<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:NoisyExperiment`) is `{ seed : NoiseSeed; fit : MuellerFitData<'Parameters> }`. New `type EnsembleSize = | EnsembleSize of int` with `value`, doc one line: how many experiments an ensemble holds. `statisticsFor` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:statisticsFor`) keeps its signature and runs today's arithmetic on the same doubles in the same order (the mean by `List.average`, the Bessel-corrected variance, `bias` as `RelativeError.between` of the mean and the truth, `scatter` as `sqrt variance / abs truth`, `worst` the `List.max` of the per-experiment `RelativeError`s), its `mean` and `absoluteScatter` born as `QuantityValue`s. `standardErrorOfMean (size : EnsembleSize) (row : RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>) : RelativeError` is `row.scatter.value / sqrt (float size.value) |> RelativeError`. `rowFor (table : RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters> list) (name : ParameterName) : Result<RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>, MuellerFitError>` answers the row whose `quantity.name` is `name`, and `Error (UnknownQuantityErr name)` when none is. (3) `MuellerFitError` gains `UnknownQuantityErr of ParameterName` (no ensemble row of that name). (4) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the three types and the three functions. (5) Callers, test code only. `BiaxialSample.recoveredQuantities`, `MuellerInverseTests.recoveredQuantities` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.reportedQuantities` pass `RecoveredQuantity.derived (ParameterName \"<name>\") (fun p -> QuantityValue (<today's expression>))`. In `MuellerInverseTests`, `BiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` every `rowFor table <name>` becomes `(rowFor table (ParameterName <name>) |> expectOk)`, and `rowFor table name.value` (`observedScatter`, whose `name` is already a `ParameterName`) becomes `(rowFor table name |> expectOk)`; every `absoluteScatter` compared as a number reads `.value`, and `standardErrorOfMean (List.length <seeds>) row` becomes `standardErrorOfMean (EnsembleSize (List.length <seeds>)) row`. Every band, message and assertion keeps its text. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the statistics are the same operations on the same doubles. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact is the cheapest that drives all six (`BiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests`, at about 1000 s each, are not selected).", "acceptance": "After the move, `RecoveryEnsembles.fs` MUST declare `RecoveredQuantity` (named by `ParameterName`, valued in `QuantityValue`), `RecoveryStatistics`, `NoisyExperiment`, `EnsembleSize`, `statisticsFor`, `standardErrorOfMean` and `rowFor` (an unknown name being `UnknownQuantityErr`), compiled directly after `BenchNoise.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers every constant, and its scatter IS what one fit's own covariance predicts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.RecoveredQuantity", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.RecoveryStatistics", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.NoisyExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.EnsembleSize", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.statisticsFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.standardErrorOfMean", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.rowFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.RecoveredQuantity", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.RecoveryStatistics", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.NoisyExperiment", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.statisticsFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.standardErrorOfMean", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.rowFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 342, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [341], "how_to": "A fit's own account of its uncertainty moves into Optimization, for the Planner's layer 2 (001 §Q AT-2 '`predictedRelativeErrors`, `combinationVariance` (the Planner's layer 2 reuses them, §M)'; the S10.1 brief 'fitReportOf … predictedRelativeErrors, combinationVariance, differenceWeights'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) `fitReportOf` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:fitReportOf`), a function of one of our types, becomes the member `member this.report : FitQuality.FitReport` of `MuellerFitData` in `MuellerFitting.fs` (ELEV013), with its body: `FitQuality.reportFrom` over the residual and the solution as a `DesignVector`, with the final residuals. (2) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs`, `module FitUncertainty` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `RecoveryEnsembles.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment). Its module doc, one to three lines: what a fit's covariance and Jacobian say about the uncertainty of its parameters and of their combinations, moved by spec 0050 S10.1 for the Planner (001 §M). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (3) In it: `type ParameterWeights = | ParameterWeights of float[]` with `value`, marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"a weight vector over a fit's parameters in its scaling's axis order (R3): read whole against the covariance and the residual Jacobian\")>]` (the S10.1 brief: float[] weight vectors are carriers). `type PredictedVariance = | PredictedVariance of double` with `value`, doc one line: the variance a fit's covariance predicts for a linear combination of its parameters, in scaled units. `predictedRelativeErrors` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:predictedRelativeErrors`) moves with its signature over `MuellerFitData` and body. `combinationVariance (quality : FitQuality.FitReport) (weights : ParameterWeights) : PredictedVariance` is today's `wᵀCw` double sum (`InverseFitHarness.fs:combinationVariance`) on the carrier's array. `differenceWeights (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) (plus : ParameterName) (minus : ParameterName) : Result<ParameterWeights, MuellerFitError>` answers, built without mutation, the vector holding 1.0 at `plus`'s axis, −1.0 at `minus`'s (−1.0 when they coincide, as today) and 0.0 elsewhere; an axis name that is not in `scaling.axes` is `Error (UnknownAxisErr <name>)`. (4) `MuellerFitError` gains `UnknownAxisErr of ParameterName` (no fitted parameter of that name). (5) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the four. Callers: `fitReportOf first.fit` becomes `first.fit.report` in `MuellerInverseTests` and `BiaxialInverseTests`; in `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact `pairVariance` is `combinationVariance quality (differenceWeights first.fit.scaling (ParameterName \"n_e\") (ParameterName \"n_o\") |> expectOk)`, read as `pairVariance.value` in `pairPrediction` and in the message. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the report, the conversion out of the scaled space and the quadratic form are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact drives all four; `BiaxialInverseTests` (997 s) is not selected.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitData.report` MUST replace `fitReportOf`, `FitUncertainty.fs` MUST declare `ParameterWeights` (a `[<NumericCarrier>]`), `PredictedVariance`, `predictedRelativeErrors`, `combinationVariance` and `differenceWeights` (an unknown axis being `UnknownAxisErr`), compiled directly after `RecoveryEnsembles.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers every constant, and its scatter IS what one fit's own covariance predicts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitData.report", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.ParameterWeights", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.PredictedVariance", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.predictedRelativeErrors", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.combinationVariance", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.differenceWeights", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitReportOf", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.predictedRelativeErrors", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.combinationVariance", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.differenceWeights", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 343, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [342], "how_to": "The last two harness functions move, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` is left holding only test assertions and formatting (001 §Q AT-2 '`BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` keeps only test assertions (`assertMuellerEqual`, the error formatting) and opens the product modules'; the S10.1 brief 'sumWeights, directionalSensitivity'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) Into `FitUncertainty.fs`, after `differenceWeights`: `sumWeights (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) (names : ParameterName list) : Result<ParameterWeights, MuellerFitError>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:sumWeights`), built without mutation, 1.0 at each named axis and 0.0 elsewhere, the first name not in `scaling.axes` being `Error (UnknownAxisErr name)`; new `type DirectionalSensitivity = | DirectionalSensitivity of double` with `value`, doc one line: how hard the residual pushes back along one direction of parameter space, ‖J·v‖ for a unit v; and `directionalSensitivity (jacobian : ResidualJacobian) (direction : ParameterWeights) : DirectionalSensitivity` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:directionalSensitivity`), today's normalization and row sums on the carrier's array. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes both and is left with five module bindings and no type, each doc one to three lines: `expectOk` (step 335), `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:describeErrors`, `:describeColumnNorms`, `:assertMuellerEqual`, `:ensembleSeeds`), their bodies unchanged. Its module doc becomes one to three lines: the test-side assertions and formatting the inverse-problem suites share; the machinery they drive is `OpticalConstructor.Optimization`'s `MuellerFitting`, `BenchNoise`, `RecoveryEnsembles` and `FitUncertainty` (spec 0050 S10.1). An `open` nothing in the file reads any more is deleted. (3) `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`: `isotropicAbsorption` answers `ParameterWeights` as `sumWeights scaling [ ParameterName \"e11\"; ParameterName \"e22\"; ParameterName \"e33\" ] |> expectOk`; `anisotropicAbsorption` answers `ParameterWeights`, its array built as today and wrapped where it is born; in `normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it` the three sensitivities are compared and reported through `.value`, every band and message text unchanged. (4) `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`' class doc sentence 'The fit driver, the residual, the scaling, the measurement-error model and the acceptance arithmetic are all shared with `MuellerInverseTests` through `InverseFitHarness`' (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:94-95`) names the four product modules instead; the rest of that doc keeps its text. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the weights hold the same 1.0 / 0.0 entries and the norm is the same sum. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` is the one class that reaches `sumWeights` and `directionalSensitivity`. After this step `git grep -n -E \"^    let |^type \" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` lists exactly `expectOk`, `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `FitUncertainty.fs` MUST declare `sumWeights` (a `Result` over `ParameterName`s), `DirectionalSensitivity` and `directionalSensitivity`, and `git grep -n -E \"^    let |^type \" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST list exactly `expectOk`, `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.sumWeights", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.DirectionalSensitivity", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.directionalSensitivity", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.sumWeights", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.directionalSensitivity", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 344, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102a", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [343], "how_to": "The shared test-support project is born, and S9.4's repository-root kit locator is its first source (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs … move into a shared test-support project, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/`, one `.fsproj` in its own folder. Both `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` reference it, so one compiled copy serves both test suites'; 001 §S10 'create `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/` (own folder, own `.fsproj`, a plain library)'; .spec-md §3.21 'The helper lives in `BerremanTests` until S10 moves it to `BerremanTestSupport`'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `CommittedKit` exists. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, the only project file in its folder (AGENTS.md 'One `.fsproj` per folder'). It is a plain library, not a test project: no `OutputType`, `IsTestProject` or `UseMicrosoftTestingPlatformRunner` property and no test package. Its two property groups are those of `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj` (`OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj:3-14`) without the `AssemblyName` line: `TargetFramework` `net10.0`, `Platforms` `x64` and `IsPackable` `false`; and, for `Release|x64`, `OtherFlags` `--warnaserror+:25 --platform:x64`, `PlatformTarget` `x64` and `NoWarn` `NU5100;NU5110;NU5111;NU1903`. It keeps the SDK's default assembly name, `BerremanTestSupport`. One `ItemGroup` holds `<Compile Include=\"CommittedKits.fs\" />`, and one holds the project reference to `..\\OpticalConstructor\\OpticalConstructor.Domain\\OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` (`KitFolder` is Domain's, step 122). It has no package reference and no comment (AGENTS.md 'No new comments in `.fsproj`'), and like every file this section writes it has LF line endings (AGENTS.md 'Line endings: LF'). (2) `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` gains the entry `<Project Path=\"BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj\">` holding `<Platform Project=\"x64\" />`, in the shape of its neighbours, directly after the `BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj` entry (`Berreman.slnx:17-19`). (3) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs` (the file step 330 creates), and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Its opens, its one case `OpticsMuellerKit` and the body of `tryFindFolder` are unchanged. The locator therefore still walks up from `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, the folder of the running test assembly, and writes nothing. The type's doc says, in one to three lines, that these are the committed reference kits under the repository's `data/` folder, found from the folder holding `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` (spec 0050 §3.21, S9.4), and that both test suites share them through `BerremanTestSupport` (S10.2). The sentence saying that S10.2 moves it is deleted. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include=\"CommittedKits.fs\" />`. It gains the project reference to `..\\BerremanTestSupport\\BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` after its last `ProjectReference`, with no comment. (5) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` gains `open BerremanTestSupport` after its last `open` line, and nothing else in it changes. (6) Elevation. Nothing under `Elevation/` and nothing in `.elevation-analyzers.json` changes. The gate driver scopes every solution `.fsproj` whose name does not end in `Tests.fsproj` (`Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1:151`), so it analyzes `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` too. The analyzers apply no rule to that assembly and report zero findings: its name matches neither `inScopePatterns` (`Softellect.Berreman.*`) nor `ownAssemblyPatterns` (`Softellect.*`) (`.elevation-analyzers.json:13-21`), and the same holds for the test projects. No `[<ElevationBoundary>]` or `[<NumericCarrier>]` mark is added to it. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the locator's body is unchanged. No test is added or removed. `MuellerReconstructionTests` is the one class that reaches the locator, through `loadDataSet` and through `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte`.", "acceptance": "After the project is created, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` MUST be a plain net10.0 x64 library with the assembly name `BerremanTestSupport`, listed in `Berreman.slnx`. It MUST compile `CommittedKits.fs` (namespace `BerremanTestSupport`) and be referenced by `BerremanTests`, and `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST hold no `CommittedKits.fs`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/Berreman.slnx", "Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.CommittedKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.CommittedKit", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 345, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102b", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [344], "how_to": "The transparent triclinic ground truth moves into `BerremanTestSupport` whole (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs (`BiaxialSample.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`: constants, …) move into a shared test-support project'; 001 §S10 'holding `BiaxialSample` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample`'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `BiaxialSample` module exists. (1) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs`, and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Every declaration moves with its body unchanged, as S10.1 leaves it: `referenceWaveLength`, the three indices and the six gyration components, `triclinic`, `solverParameters`, `scalingAround`, `opticAxisFromLargest`, `opticAxisWaveNormal`, `epsDiagonal`, `rhoImaginary` and `recoveredQuantities`. The retained `BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic` MUST move with the module and MUST call `TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties`, whose tensor kernel was extracted in step 333, and `recoveredQuantities` has named `ParameterName`s and read `QuantityValue`s since step 341. Its opens are unchanged. It reads no name of the `BerremanTests` namespace, and `BerremanTestSupport` references no test project. In the module doc, only what the move makes untrue changes. The first sentence's 'every biaxial suite in this assembly shares' (`BiaxialSample.fs:13`) becomes 'every biaxial suite shares', and that paragraph gains one sentence citing spec 0050 S10.2 (001 §Q AT-2): the sample lives in `BerremanTestSupport`, so one compiled copy serves `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`. In the spec R3 sentence, 'in the TEST assembly' (`BiaxialSample.fs:23`) becomes 'in test code'. Every other doc line keeps its text. (2) `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` gains `<Compile Include=\"BiaxialSample.fs\" />` after `CommittedKits.fs`. It also gains the project reference to `..\\OpticalConstructor\\OpticalConstructor.Optimization\\OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj` after the Domain one, because `RecoveredQuantity` and `QuantityValue` are `OpticalConstructor.Optimization`'s (steps 341 and 338). No comment is added. (3) `BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include=\"BiaxialSample.fs\" />` with the comment above it (`BerremanTests.fsproj:40-41`). It also deletes the comment above `<Compile Include=\"InverseFitHarness.fs\" />` (`BerremanTests.fsproj:36-38`), which S10.1 made untrue: after step 343 the harness declares no type and drives no fit. The `InverseFitHarness.fs` line keeps its place. (4) The consumers read the moved module. `open BerremanTests.BiaxialSample` becomes `open BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample`, keeping its trailing comment, in `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` (which step 346 moves). Nothing else in them changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every expression is unchanged, and only its namespace moves. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s) drives `triclinic`, `scalingAround`, `opticAxisWaveNormal`, `solverParameters` and `referenceWaveLength`. `BiaxialInverseTests` (about 997 s) is selected too, because it alone reaches `epsDiagonal`, `rhoImaginary`, `opticAxisFromLargest` and `recoveredQuantities`; the S10.2 brief names both classes. The moved test-support module MUST still declare buildTriclinic; every direct test caller MUST use the new namespace, and the old BerremanTests source MUST be deleted. Product code MUST use the parameter-record member and MUST NOT reference BerremanTestSupport. This preserves 001 §Q's named builder destination without copying physics.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs` MUST declare the module `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample` with every declaration and number unchanged. `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST neither hold nor compile `BiaxialSample.fs`, and every consumer MUST open `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass. BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic MUST exist and call the shared product kernel; the former BerremanTests source MUST be absent.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.every plate in this design is one a vendor will actually sell", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.a plate cut perpendicular to an optic axis is a pure circular retarder, and that is what buys the signal", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the order ambiguity is real on the principal cuts and is broken by the optic-axis cuts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.the triclinic builder produces a biaxial permittivity and a FULL symmetric gyration tensor", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.orientForCut carries each of the three principal axes onto the surface normal, gyration tensor and all", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.an optic axis is reachable from the x-cut and unreachable from the z-cut, which is what the steep configurations are for", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers all nine constants, and the birefringences survive far better", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests|T:BerremanTests.BiaxialSample", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 346, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102c", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [345], "how_to": "The absorbing ground truth and its measurement design move into `BerremanTestSupport` whole, beside their transparent twin (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs (… `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`: constants, `buildAbsorbing`, the cuts, `a1` / `a2` / `a3`, `perturbedStart`, `searchBox`) move into a shared test-support project'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `AbsorbingBiaxialSample` module exists. (1) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Every declaration moves with its body unchanged, as S10.1 leaves it: the six ε″ components, `absorbing`, `absorbingScalingAround`, `plate`, `waveLength`, `opticAxisCut`, `otherOpticAxisCut`, `configuration`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `fullConfigurations`, `perturbedStart` and `searchBox`. The retained `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing` MUST move with the module and MUST call `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties`, whose tensor kernel was extracted in step 334, `configuration` has passed `float<deg>` angles to `MuellerFitting.configurationOf` since step 335, and `SearchBox` has been `MuellerFitting`'s since step 337. The file keeps `open BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample` (step 345). No `open` of a `BerremanTests` module remains in it: `open BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness` is deleted, because after S10.1 nothing in the file reads the harness and `BerremanTestSupport` references no test project. In the module doc, the first paragraph gains one sentence citing spec 0050 S10.2 (001 §Q AT-2): the sample and its design live in `BerremanTestSupport`, so one compiled copy serves `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`. Every other doc line keeps its text. (2) `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` gains `<Compile Include=\"AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs\" />` after `BiaxialSample.fs`. No reference and no comment is added. (3) `BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include=\"AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs\" />`, so its compile list holds no ground-truth file. (4) In `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs`, `open BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample` becomes `open BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample`, keeping its trailing comment. Nothing else in them changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every expression is unchanged, and `fullConfigurations` holds the same 44 configurations in the same order. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s) reads every moved declaration that `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` (946 s, not selected) reads, and it reaches the rest through `configuration` and `fullConfigurations`. The moved test-support module MUST still declare buildAbsorbing; every direct test caller MUST use the new namespace, and the old BerremanTests source MUST be deleted. Product code MUST use the parameter-record member and MUST NOT reference BerremanTestSupport. This preserves 001 §Q's named builder destination without copying physics.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` MUST declare the module `BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample` with every declaration and number unchanged and no `open` of a `BerremanTests` module. `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST neither hold nor compile `BiaxialSample.fs` or `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, and both absorbing suites MUST open `BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass. BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing MUST exist and call the shared product kernel; the former BerremanTests source MUST be absent.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the scaled parameter space round-trips all fifteen coordinates and a unit step moves exactly one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.absorption and refraction do NOT share principal axes, which is what makes this crystal triclinic-absorbing", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the REAL part of rho has no first-order effect, so circular dichroism is not expressible through it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing sample attenuates, and every configuration stays physically realizable", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.all fifteen parameters are observable and the problem is conditioned well enough to solve", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests|T:BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 347, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [346], "how_to": "`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` references the shared test-support project, so one compiled copy of the ground truth, the designs and the kit locator serves both test suites (001 §Q AT-2 'Both `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` reference it, so one compiled copy serves both test suites'; 001 §S10 'referenced by `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`'; the S10.2 brief). `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` gains the project reference to `..\\..\\BerremanTestSupport\\BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` after its last `ProjectReference`, the `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.App` one (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj:268`), with no comment (AGENTS.md 'No new comments in `.fsproj`'). This step adds the reference 001 §Q AT-2 requires and changes no source file of the suite, so no `ui-tests` class holds a changed fact and that gate is not selected; what the reference can affect, the suite's build and load, is what `build` and `ui-smoke` prove. The reference brings no assembly besides `BerremanTestSupport` itself, because `OpticalConstructor.Domain` and `OpticalConstructor.Optimization` already reach the suite through `OpticalConstructor.Ui` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:176-178`). The test projects stay outside the elevation gate's scope (`Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1:151`), so the gate analyzes nothing new here. No test and no package is added. `ui-smoke` runs whole (`whole_suite: light`, about 27 s) and shows that the headless host still loads, discovers and runs the suite with the new reference.", "acceptance": "After the reference is added, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` MUST reference `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, so that `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` build against one `BerremanTestSupport` assembly. ui-smoke MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 348, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103a", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [347], "how_to": "The reference pipeline's transcribed expectations get ONE home in test support, which `MuellerReconstructionTests` and AT-1 (S12.1) share (001 §Q AT-1 'the transcribed expected literals move from the §7.2 test body into one shared reference module, which both tests open. The test reads no file for its expectations (spec 0044 §8.5)'; 001 §S10 third bullet 'move its expected literals into one shared reference module'; the S10.3 brief 'dataMatrixTol moves with them'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step every expected literal of the Stage-1 and section 7.2 facts exists once, in `MuellerReference`. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs`: `module MuellerReference` in `namespace BerremanTestSupport`, the shape of `BiaxialSample.fs` (step 345), compiled after `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` through one `<Compile Include=\"MuellerReference.fs\" />` line in `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, with no comment and no reference added (Domain since step 344, Optimization since step 345). The module opens only what its values need. Its doc, one to three lines: the optics-mueller reference pipeline's full-precision results, transcribed from `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/reference_step1_summary.json` and `reference_step2_linear_summary.json` (step 329), which `MuellerReconstructionTests` and AT-1 assert against, so no test reads a file for its expectations (spec 0044 §8.5; spec 0050 S10.3). Each value is born elevated (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin … This holds for test fixtures too'), and each value's doc, one line, names its summary key. In this order: (a) The two bands, moved from the class bindings `stage1Tol` and `dataMatrixTol` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:stage1Tol`, `:dataMatrixTol`) with their values `1.0e-12` and `1.0e-9` and their docs, and the comment block above `stage1Tol` (the spec 0044 §8.5 / §9 bands and their observed figures) with its text as step 329 leaves it. (b) The Stage-1 constants of `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values`, from `reference_step1_summary.json`: `darkMean` = `DarkMean 869.666` (`dark_mean_avg_total`); `lpAnalyzerZero` = `Angle.degree 155.44011830109392<deg>` (`lp_lp_anchor.zero_angle_deg`); `cplAnalyzerZero` = `Angle.degree 96.99613336321012<deg>` (`cpl_analyzer_from_lp_cpl.zero_angle_deg`); `cplAnalyzerRetardance` = `Retardance.degree 83.66804489441891<deg>` (`cpl_analyzer_from_lp_cpl.retardance_raw_deg`, the magnitude stage 1 derives); `cplSourceAxisOffset` = `Angle.degree 39.31100224361002<deg>` and `cplSourceRetardance` = `Retardance.degree 82.55344158462403<deg>` (`cpl_source_from_cpl_lp.source_theta_relaxed_model.theta_rel_deg` and `.retardance_deg`). Each of these degree literals comes back bit for bit from `.degrees` (checked when this spec was authored), so every comparison stays exact. (c) The section 7.2 values, from `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`: `qzMatrix`, `lrMatrix` and `combinedMatrix`, the `MuellerMatrix`es of `qz_matrix`, `lr_matrix` and `combined_matrix`, built from the literals the fact's `expectedQz`, `expectedLr` and `expectedComb` hold today (`RealMatrix4x4.create … |> MuellerMatrix`); `cascadeFrobenius`, `cascadeMeanAbs` and `cascadeMaxAbs`, the `MatrixDeviation`s 0.5714178795538456, 0.11328628636347338 and 0.26806464658062423 (`combined_vs_product_matrix.frobenius_norm`, `.mean_abs_entry_diff`, `.max_abs_entry_diff`); and `cascadeLargestDeltaPositions : Set<MuellerRowIndex * MuellerColumnIndex>`, the 0-indexed positions (3, 3) and (3, 1) of the two largest `delta_matrix` magnitudes, with the fact's spec 0044 note on them cut to one to three lines. (d) `excludedPoints : ExcludedPoint list`, the one point of the reference's `EXCLUDED_POINTS` (`Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_glue.py:22`, in `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` from step 329): experiment `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`, description 140°, capture index 17. It is the caller's data to the reconstruction (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:ExcludedPoint`, spec 0042 §0). (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` reads each of them as `MuellerReference.<name>` (`BerremanTestSupport` is open since step 344). It deletes `stage1Tol`, `dataMatrixTol` and the comment block above them. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` compares `darkMean` with `MuellerReference.darkMean.value` and each angle or retardance through `.degrees` of its `MuellerReference` value, in the same order and at `MuellerReference.stage1Tol`; its provenance comment says, in one to three lines, that the expected values are `MuellerReference`'s (spec 0050 S10.3). The section 7.2 fact deletes `expectedQz`, `expectedLr`, `expectedComb`, its local `excluded` and its three metric literals, and reads their `MuellerReference` values. It compares at `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` and checks its two largest-delta positions, now enumerated as `(MuellerRowIndex i, MuellerColumnIndex j)`, against `MuellerReference.cascadeLargestDeltaPositions`; its comments that name the summary say the values are `MuellerReference`'s. `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)` reads `MuellerReference.excludedPoints` in place of its local copy of the same point (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a re-transcribed constant is a defect). The class doc's spec 0044 §8.5 bullet adds that the expectations live in `BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference` (spec 0050 S10.3); no other comment changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every computed value and every expected value is the same double, so each assertion compares the same numbers. No test is added or removed. The test support project is outside the ELEV analyzers' scope (`.elevation-analyzers.json:13-21`, as step 344 records), so nothing under `Elevation/` changes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` MUST declare `BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference` holding the two bands, the six Stage-1 constants, the three section 7.2 matrices, the three cascade metrics, the two largest-delta positions and the excluded point, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST hold none of these literals and read them from the module; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number":349,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S103b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","BerremanTests","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[348],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests"],"how_to":"Stage 1 of the reference pipeline, which `MuellerReconstructionTests` composes by hand, becomes the first half of the study's staged Mueller path in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization` (001 §Q AT-1 'the stage pipeline that §7.2 composes by hand (`loadDataSet`, `reduceAirTraces`, `unwrapFit`, stage-1 constants, …) is promoted into product code as the study's staged Mueller path, and §7.2 is re-pointed to call it'; 001 §S10 third bullet; the S10.3 brief 'the stage-1 constants (freeCosineFit, sourceCplFromLpFrame, the analyzer zeros and retardances)' and 'The test-only failure helpers (unwrapFit throws) become typed errors'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step `reduceAirTraces`, `lpFrameCoeffs` and `unwrapFit` exist nowhere in the test. Errors are values (AGENTS.md 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the test `failwith`s becomes a typed error. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs`, `module StagedMuellerPath` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `FitUncertainty.fs` (step 342): one `<Compile Include=\"StagedMuellerPath.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`, no comment. It opens what it needs (`OpticalConstructor.Domain` for `Library.PolarizerKind`, `ItemModels` for `DialSign` since step 205, `MuellerReconstruction`). Module doc, one to three lines: the optics-mueller reference pipeline (spec 0042 §7.2) as the study's staged Mueller path, a pure function of the lab files' capture rows and a `MuellerSolverProxy`, promoted from `MuellerReconstructionTests` by spec 0050 S10.3. Each declaration's doc is one to three lines naming the reference script function it mirrors. In this order: (a) `StagedMuellerCaptureData`, the capture rows of the seven lab files as the Phone ROI CSV profile reads them (step 303): `lpLpRows`, `lpCplRows`, `cplLpRows`, `cplCplDay1Rows`, `cplCplDay2Rows`, `darknessRows` and `bullshitCheckRows`, each a `MuellerRawRow list`. (b) `StagedMuellerError`, doc one line (a typed failure of the staged path, never a throw): `EmptyCaptureSetErr of reason : string` (a set of capture rows the path needs holds none; the reason names it) and `AirCalibrationFitErr of family : Family * error : SolverError` (the stage-1 AIR cosine fit of that family failed; `MuellerReconstruction.fs:Family`, `:SolverError`). Steps 351 and 352 add their own cases; no other case is added here. (c) `StageOneCalibrationData = { darkMean : DarkMean; lpZero : Angle; cplZero : Angle; cplAnalyzerRetardance : Retardance; cplSourceModel : SourceCplModel }`, the stage-1 constants (`matrix_step1_air_fit.py`), with the stage-2 models built from them (`matrix_glue.py` `load_step1_models`) as members, moved from the section 7.2 fact's `analyzerLp`, `analyzerCpl` and `sourceCpl` with their values: `member this.lpAnalyzer : AnalyzerModel` (`Library.IdealLinear`, `zeroDial = this.lpZero`, `DialNegative`, no retarder); `member this.cplAnalyzer : AnalyzerModel` (`Library.IdealCircularLeft`, `zeroDial = this.cplZero`, `DialPositive`, `thetaRelOpt = Some (Angle.degree 45.0<deg>)`, `retardanceOpt = Some (Retardance.degree (- this.cplAnalyzerRetardance.degrees * 1.0<deg>))`, the fact's expression, so the same double); and `member this.cplSource : SourceModel` (`CplSource (this.cplSourceModel.thetaRel, this.cplSourceModel.retardance)`). (d) Private, moved from the test: `reduceAirTraces` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:reduceAirTraces`, the reference `load_air_traces` + `prepare_normalized_traces`) with its dark mean as `DarkMean` (ELEV003P, ELEV010P), read through `.value` where it subtracts, its body otherwise unchanged; and the LP-frame fit (`:lpFrameCoeffs`, the reference `fit_lp_frame_coeffs`), whose `CosineCoefficient * CosineCoefficient` answer is ELEV011, as a helper answering `Result<SourceCplModel, SolverError>`: the same phased 2-column solve through the proxy, each coefficient bound as a `CosineCoefficient` where it is read from the solution (ELEV001), then `sourceCplFromLpFrame` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:sourceCplFromLpFrame`). (e) `calibrateStageOne (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (captures : StagedMuellerCaptureData) : Result<StageOneCalibrationData, StagedMuellerError>`, the stage-1 part of today's section 7.2 body in its order: no darkness row answers `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the darkness checks; the dark mean is the mean `avgTotal` of `darknessRows`; `freeCosineFit` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:freeCosineFit`) of `reduceAirTraces` over `lpLpRows` gives `lpZero`, and over `lpCplRows` gives `cplZero` and `cplAnalyzerRetardance` (its `visibility.retardance`); the LP-frame fit over `cplLpRows`, phased on `lpZero`, gives `cplSourceModel`. A failed solve answers `AirCalibrationFitErr` of `LpLp`, `LpCpl` or `CplLp` with its `SolverError`, and nothing after it runs. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath` and deletes `reduceAirTraces`, `lpFrameCoeffs` and `unwrapFit`. After the seven kit file values (step 330) it binds `let opticsMuellerCaptures () : StagedMuellerCaptureData`, each field `loadDataSet` of its file, its doc one line. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` calls `calibrateStageOne (createMathNetSvd ()) (opticsMuellerCaptures ())`, an `Error` failing the fact with its `%A`, and compares `stageOne.darkMean.value` and, through `.degrees`, `lpZero`, `cplZero`, `cplAnalyzerRetardance`, `cplSourceModel.thetaRel` and `cplSourceModel.retardance` with the `MuellerReference` values as step 348 left the comparison. The section 7.2 fact makes the same call and takes `darkMean`, `lpAnalyzer`, `cplAnalyzer` and `cplSource` from it, with `LpSource`, in place of its hand-written Stage 1 and Stage 2 blocks; it binds one `opticsMuellerCaptures ()` and reads every lab file's rows from it, the call included. Its Stage 3 and its assertions are unchanged in this step. `loadDataSet` stays: it is the test's read of the committed kit (IO), and the promoted path is pure over the rows it reads (the S10.3 brief 'a pure function over the parsed capture rows'). `degree` stays, for `freeCosineFit recovers a synthetic cosine zero and visibility within tolerance (always-run)`. (3) Tests. New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs`, `module StagedMuellerPathTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests` (the shape of `MeasuredDataTests.fs`), appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction`, `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath` and what its facts need, each fact over the real `createMathNetSvd ()` and fixed-literal rows: `stage one answers a typed error naming the empty darkness checks, never a throw`: all seven row lists empty answer `EmptyCaptureSetErr` whose reason names the darkness checks; `stage one answers a typed error naming the family whose AIR cosine fit fails`: one darkness row and no other row answer `AirCalibrationFitErr (LpLp, SingularDesignErr _)`, the empty LP-LP AIR trace being an empty design. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every number is computed by the same float operations in the same order. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged.","acceptance":"After stage one is promoted, `StagedMuellerPath.fs`, compiled directly after `FitUncertainty.fs`, MUST declare `StagedMuellerCaptureData`, `StagedMuellerError` (`EmptyCaptureSetErr`, `AirCalibrationFitErr`), `StageOneCalibrationData` with its `lpAnalyzer`, `cplAnalyzer` and `cplSource` members, and `calibrateStageOne`, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST declare none of `reduceAirTraces`, `lpFrameCoeffs` and `unwrapFit` and take its stage-1 constants from `calibrateStageOne`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `stage one answers a typed error naming the empty darkness checks, never a throw` and `stage one answers a typed error naming the family whose AIR cosine fit fails`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj","Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"unit-tests","id":"BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly","path":"Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.stage one answers a typed error naming the empty darkness checks, never a throw","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.stage one answers a typed error naming the family whose AIR cosine fit fails","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerCaptureData","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StageOneCalibrationData","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.calibrateStageOne","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs","obligations":["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 350, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [349], "how_to": "`buildDesign` hands each kept row's label reading to its per-row projection, so no projection reads a label again and the staged path (step 351) is total without an arm for an `Error` that cannot occur (AGENTS.md 'Errors are values'; the S10.3 brief 'The test-only failure helpers … become typed errors'). Since step 270, `buildDesign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign`) keeps a row only when `NamingTemplate.standard.readName r.experiment.nameText` reads it, and the section 7.2 fact's `prepareRow` reads the same label again and fails the fact on an `Error` that no kept row can give. (1) In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`, `buildDesign`'s first parameter becomes `prepareRow : MuellerRawRow -> NameReading -> StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity`. Each row's label is read once. A row is kept, in row order and with its reading, when the reading's `matrixKind` equals `kind`, the label is no AIR#0 label and the row is no excluded point, as today; each kept row is projected by `prepareRow row reading`. The rows kept, their order and the system are unchanged. Its doc says so in one to three lines (spec 0050 S10.3). No other declaration changes. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's `prepareRow` takes `(reading : NameReading)` after its row and its φ is `reading.objectPhi`; its own read of the label and the failure on that read's `Error` (step 270) are deleted. `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)`'s stub projection takes an ignored `NameReading` after its row; its rows, its assertions and its numbers are unchanged. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the reading `buildDesign` hands over is the reading the fact made itself, so every row has the same φ and every design row the same entries. No test is added or removed. No other consumer of `buildDesign` exists: the S10.3 path adopts this form in step 351.", "acceptance": "After the change, `buildDesign`'s projection MUST have the type `MuellerRawRow -> NameReading -> StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity` and receive each kept row's reading, and no projection in `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read a label; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-DESIGN-READING"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-DESIGN-READING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-DESIGN-READING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 351, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [350], "how_to": "Stages 2 and 3 of the reference pipeline join stage 1 in `StagedMuellerPath`, and the section 7.2 fact keeps only its assertions (001 §Q AT-1 '… `familyGain`, `correctSignal`, `buildDesign`, `reconstruct`) is promoted into product code as the study's staged Mueller path, and §7.2 is re-pointed to call it'; 001 §S10 third bullet; the S10.3 brief 'It returns typed stage-1 constants, the reconstructed matrices with rank and residual' and 'sec 7.2 calls the promoted path, and its body keeps only assertions'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step the hand-composed Stage 3 exists once, in product code. (1) In `StagedMuellerPath.fs` (step 349): (a) `StagedMuellerError` gains `ObjectReconstructionErr of kind : MatrixKind * error : SolverError` (the stage-3 solve of that object failed; `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixKind`). (b) After `calibrateStageOne`, `StagedMuellerData = { stageOne : StageOneCalibrationData; gains : GainCalibration; cplCplDay1Gain : InterpolatedGain; qz : ReconstructedMatrix; lr : ReconstructedMatrix; qzLr : ReconstructedMatrix }`, doc one to three lines: the stage-1 constants, the AIR gain rules (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:GainCalibration`, whose `cplCpl` is the day-2 `Day2Single`), the day-1 CPL-CPL interpolation (`:InterpolatedGain`), and M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} with their rank and residual (`:ReconstructedMatrix`). (c) `reconstructStaged (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (excluded : ExcludedPoint list) (captures : StagedMuellerCaptureData) : Result<StagedMuellerData, StagedMuellerError>`, the rest of today's section 7.2 body moved with its rules and values, in this order: `calibrateStageOne`, its error passing through; the CPL-LP split time, the earliest `capturedAt` of `bullshitCheckRows` (the reference `assign_gain_model` reads the first check), no row answering `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the bullshit checks; the nine AIR blocks, each the rows of its file whose `experiment` equals its label, in this order: `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2` and `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R` of `lpLpRows`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` and `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R` of `lpCplRows`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R` of `cplLpRows`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR` of `cplCplDay1Rows` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` of `cplCplDay2Rows` (the labels `assign_gain_model` selects, `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py:94-144`), the first block with no row answering `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming its label, where the fact divides 0 by 0 or throws today; each block's gain by the fact's `fitAirGain` and the day-1 block times by its `meanTime`, with the sources (`LpSource`, `stageOne.cplSource`) and analyzers (`stageOne.lpAnalyzer`, `stageOne.cplAnalyzer`) its `calibration` and `day1Cal` use; the five families' projections as its `prepareRow` and `families` build them, in step 350's form; and, for `Qz`, `Lr` and `QzLrProduct` in that order, the five families' `buildDesign` systems over `excluded`, concatenated in family order and solved by `reconstruct`, the first failure answering `ObjectReconstructionErr` with the kind and the `SolverError`. The nine labels are literals of the path, born as `MuellerExperimentLabel`s: they are the reference procedure's gain rules, which S11.1 turns into session data (001 §L 'familyGain becomes their first implementation'). The excluded points are the caller's data (spec 0042 §0; 001 §Q AT-1 'the excluded frame [is] applied as data'). Helpers are private or local and meet ELEV003P, ELEV010P and ELEV013. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` gains, after the cascade values, the nine AIR gains of `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`'s `gain_summary`, each an `AirGain` with a one-line doc naming its key: `lpLpGainA` 45028.89958338373 (`lp_lp.gain_air2`), `lpLpGainB` 44514.55313613668 (`lp_lp.gain_air2r`), `lpCplGainA` 64241.39738340334 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2`), `lpCplGainB` 63009.84001492676 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2r`), `cplLpGainPre` 36886.57620207925 (`cpl_lp.gain_pre_air2`), `cplLpGainPost` 40015.20947516168 (`cpl_lp.gain_post_air2r`), `cplCplDay1GainStart` 34623.69085844701 and `cplCplDay1GainEnd` 37056.15607055087 (`cpl_cpl_day1.gain_start`, `.gain_end`) and `cplCplDay2Gain` 36225.080943100205 (`cpl_cpl_day2.gain`). `dataMatrixTol`'s doc gains one line: it also bands the AIR gains, whose worst observed deviation was 2.9e-11 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2`) when spec 0050 was authored, 2026-11-04, so the band is about 34 times looser (spec 0044 §9). (3) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact calls `reconstructStaged (createMathNetSvd ()) MuellerReference.excludedPoints (opticsMuellerCaptures ())`, an `Error` failing the fact with its `%A`, and deletes every binding of its body that is neither an assertion nor its formatting (the stage-1 call of step 349, `airRowsOf`, `fitAirGain`, `meanTime`, `splitTime`, `day1Start`, `day1End`, `calibration`, `day1Cal`, `prepareRow`, `families` and `reconstructKind`); `worstElementDeviation` and `describeDeviation` stay. Its assertions read `staged.qz`, `staged.lr` and `staged.qzLr` (rank 16 each; the matrices within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol`), and its cascade check reads `cascadeProduct staged.lr.matrix staged.qz.matrix` until step 352. It gains one assertion that reports all nine deviations, as the matrix assertion does: each AIR gain of `staged.gains` (`lpLp.gainA`, `lpLp.gainB`, `lpCpl.gainA`, `lpCpl.gainB`, `cplLp.gainPre`, `cplLp.gainPost` and the `Day2Single` gain of `cplCpl`, a `Day1Interp` failing the fact) and of `staged.cplCplDay1Gain` (`gainStart`, `gainEnd`) is within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of its `MuellerReference` value. Its leading comment says, in one to three lines, that it runs the promoted staged path (spec 0050 S10.3) over the kit's lab files; its spec 0044 §8.4 and §8.5 paragraphs keep their text, and the comments of the moved code go with it. (4) Tests, in `StagedMuellerPathTests` (step 349), over test-local synthetic captures whose AIR rows are, per label, nine readings at 0°, 20°, …, 160° with `avgTotal` 2 + cos 2α at fixed literal times, one darkness row and one bullshit-check row, so stage 1 solves: `the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row`: the LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP files hold only their first block (`LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2`) and the day files nothing, so `reconstructStaged` answers `EmptyCaptureSetErr` whose reason holds `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`; `the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails`: all nine blocks and no science row answer `ObjectReconstructionErr (Qz, SingularDesignErr _)`, the empty QZ design reaching the real `createMathNetSvd ()`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the path computes every gain, projection and solve by the same float operations in the same order; a probe this spec ran at authoring through the same functions reproduced the summary's nine gains within 2.9e-11 and its row counts (QZ 228, LR 227, QZ+LR 228). The gain assertion compares values the fact already computes, and `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged (001 §W: no new inverse-physics test).", "acceptance": "After the staged path is promoted, `StagedMuellerPath.reconstructStaged` MUST answer the stage-1 constants, the nine AIR gains and M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} with their rank and residual, or a typed `StagedMuellerError`, and the section 7.2 fact MUST call it, hold only assertions and their formatting, and find every gain within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference`'s; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row` and `the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.reconstructStaged", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"], "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs"}, {"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"], "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs"}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 352, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [351], "how_to": "The product check, the combined QZ+LR matrix against the cascade M_LR · M_QZ, becomes part of the staged path's answer, with the product-check RMSE ratio the reference reports (001 §L 'the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ)'; 001 §Q AT-1 'Assertions: … the product-check RMSE ratio'; the S10.3 brief 'the cascade comparison' and 'It returns … the product check'; S11.4 reuses it). The reference computes `fit_rmse`, the combined matrix's own RMSE over its rows, and `product_rmse`, the cascade's prediction RMSE over the same rows (`Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py:372-373`, in `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` from step 329), and its report prints `product / fit` (`:334`). (0) The residual RMSE of a solution over a least-squares system gets one implementation, which the SVD proxy and the product check share (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy … A duplicated function body … is a defect'): `createMathNetSvd` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:createMathNetSvd`) computes `‖A·x − b‖ / √m` inline today, in its `residual`, `rows` and `rmse` bindings. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs` the record `LeastSquaresSystem` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`) gains `member this.residualRmseAt (solution : RealVector) : ResidualRmse`: `RealMatrix.create` of its design rows' values times `solution`, minus `RealVector.create` of `rhs`, the difference's `norm` divided by `sqrt` of the row count, the expression `createMathNetSvd` evaluates, in its order (`ResidualRmse` is declared above the record, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:ResidualRmse`). Its doc, one to three lines: the residual RMSE of a solution over this system's rows, the one the solver reports and the product check reuses (spec 0050 S10.3). In `createMathNetSvd` those three bindings become `system.residualRmseAt (RealVector x)`; its checks, its errors and the rest of its body are unchanged, so every solver RMSE is the same double, as `the real createMathNetSvd proxy solves a known over-determined full-rank system`, `reconstruct recovers a seeded MuellerMatrix from a synthetic full-rank design at rank 16 (always-run)`, `freeCosineFit recovers a synthetic cosine zero and visibility within tolerance (always-run)` and the section 7.2 fact, which read it through the proxy, show. No other declaration of the file changes. (1) In `StagedMuellerPath.fs`, before `StagedMuellerData`: (a) `ProductRmseRatio of float` with `member this.value`, doc one line, and `static member between (productRmse : ResidualRmse) (fitRmse : ResidualRmse) : ProductRmseRatio` (`productRmse.value / fitRmse.value`), the one place the ratio is formed, as `RelativeError.between` is (step 338). (b) `ProductCheckData = { cascade : MuellerMatrix; difference : MatrixDiff; fitRmse : ResidualRmse; productRmse : ResidualRmse }` with `member this.rmseRatio : ProductRmseRatio` (`ProductRmseRatio.between this.productRmse this.fitRmse`). (c) `productCheckOf (lr : MuellerMatrix) (qz : MuellerMatrix) (combined : ReconstructedMatrix) (combinedSystem : LeastSquaresSystem) : ProductCheckData`: `cascade` is `cascadeProduct lr qz` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:cascadeProduct`, in its operand order), `difference` is `frobeniusDiff combined.matrix cascade` (`:frobeniusDiff`), `fitRmse` is `combined.rmse` and `productRmse` is `combinedSystem.residualRmseAt cascade.vecColumnMajor` (part 0). (2) `StagedMuellerData` gains `productCheck : ProductCheckData` after `qzLr`; `reconstructStaged` keeps the `QzLrProduct` system it solves and fills the field with `productCheckOf lr.matrix qz.matrix qzLr` of that system, after the three solves. (3) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath` and gains, after the gains, `combinedFitRmse` = `ResidualRmse 0.10162659513724465` (`combined_check.fit_rmse`), `productRmse` = `ResidualRmse 0.12833930975940816` (`combined_check.product_rmse`) and `productCheckRmseRatio` = `ProductRmseRatio.between productRmse combinedFitRmse`. `dataMatrixTol`'s doc gains one line: it also bands the ratio, whose observed deviation was 5.7e-13 when spec 0050 was authored, 2026-11-04. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's cascade check reads `staged.productCheck` and its own `cascadeProduct` and `frobeniusDiff` calls go: the three metrics are `staged.productCheck.difference`'s, compared with `MuellerReference`'s at `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` as before, and the two largest-delta positions compare `staged.qzLr.matrix` with `staged.productCheck.cascade`. It gains one assertion: `staged.productCheck.rmseRatio` is within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.productCheckRmseRatio`, its message naming the two RMSEs and the two ratios. (5) Test, in `StagedMuellerPathTests`: `the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows`: with `lr` = `Propagation.identityMueller`, `qz` = the diagonal Mueller matrix diag(1, 0.5, 0.5, 1), `combined` = `{ matrix = Propagation.identityMueller; rank = MatrixRank 16; rmse = ResidualRmse 0.1 }` and the system of the two design rows `kron4 (StokesVector.create [ 1.0; 0.0; 0.0; 0.0 ]) (RealVector4.create [ 1.0; 0.0; 0.0; 0.0 ])` and the same two constructors over [ 0.0; 1.0; 0.0; 0.0 ] (they read M₀₀ and M₁₁, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:kron4`) with the right-hand side 1.0 and 0.8, `productCheckOf` answers a `cascade` equal to `qz` element by element, a `difference` whose `maxAbs` is 0.5 and whose `frobenius` is √0.5, `fitRmse` 0.1, `productRmse` √0.045 and a `rmseRatio` of √0.045 / 0.1, each within 1e-12. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the three metrics and the two positions are computed from the same matrices by the same calls, and every solver RMSE by the same operations. A probe this spec ran at authoring reproduced the summary's `fit_rmse`, `product_rmse` and their ratio within 2.3e-14, 2.9e-14 and 5.7e-13, so the new assertion holds at `dataMatrixTol`. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the product check lands, `LeastSquaresSystem.residualRmseAt` MUST compute `‖A·x − b‖ / √m` and `createMathNetSvd` MUST report its RMSE through it, `productCheckOf` MUST answer the cascade M_LR · M_QZ, its difference from M_{QZ+LR}, the combined fit's RMSE and the cascade's RMSE over the combined rows, and their ratio, `reconstructStaged` MUST carry it, and the section 7.2 fact MUST read it, finding the ratio within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.productCheckRmseRatio`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows`, the count rising by 1; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.LeastSquaresSystem.residualRmseAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.ProductRmseRatio", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.ProductCheckData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.productCheckOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerData", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"], "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs"}, {"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"], "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs"}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number":353,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S111a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","BerremanTestSupport","BerremanTests"],"depends_on":[352],"how_to":"The three crystal-parameter records move ahead of the material library, so that a material version can hold one of them as its physics (.spec-md §3.16 'A material version can hold one of the three parameter records as its physics (S11)'; the S11.1 brief 'Material physics form'). `MaterialEntry` is declared in `MaterialLibrary.fs`, which `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` compiles long before `MuellerInverse.fs`, where the records live today (`MuellerInverse.fs:UniaxialParameters`, `:TriclinicParameters`, `:AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`), so the records and the builders S10.1 put on them (steps 332-334, `opticalProperties`) move. This departs from .spec-md §3.16's location for the builders ('promoted into `MuellerInverse.fs` as members of their parameter records'), and the departure is recorded here: §3.16's own next bullet needs the records before `MaterialLibrary.fs`, and ONE implementation of each builder still exists. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'): after the step each record and each builder is declared once. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs`, `module CrystalPhysics` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `DispersionModels.fs` and before `MaterialLibrary.fs`: one `<Compile Include=\"CrystalPhysics.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the crystal-parameter records a material version can hold as its physics, each with its engine builder (spec 0050 S11.1, .spec-md §3.16). It opens what the moved bodies read (the engine's `Fields`, `MaterialProperties` and `OpticalProperties.Active`, as `MuellerInverse.fs` opens them). It holds `UniaxialParameters`, `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` in that order, each with its doc, its fields and its `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` exactly as steps 332-334 leave them. `MuellerObservation`, declared between two of them today, stays in `MuellerInverse.fs`. (2) Each record's `axes` stays in `MuellerInverse.fs`, because `ParameterAxis` is declared there and `ParameterName` in `ItemModels.fs` (step 205), both after `MaterialLibrary.fs`: directly after `ParameterAxis`, three type extensions `type UniaxialParameters with static member axes : ParameterAxis<UniaxialParameters> list = …`, the same for `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`, each with the doc and the body it has today. Every `UniaxialParameters.axes` call therefore reads as today wherever `MuellerInverse` is open. `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics`, and its module doc's sentence that each parameter record carries its crystal class's builder (step 332) adds that the records live in `CrystalPhysics` (spec 0050 S11.1). No other line of the file changes. (3) The files that name a record open `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics` where the compiler asks and change nothing else: `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `LangasiteInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs` and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, and `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` (steps 345-346). The Optimization fit wrappers are generic in `'Parameters` (`MuellerFitting.fs`, step 337) and name no record. No alias, re-export or second declaration remains (ELEV014), so `git grep -n -E \"type (UniaxialParameters|TriclinicParameters|AbsorbingTriclinicParameters) =\" -- Berreman/` finds only `CrystalPhysics.fs`. The edits also name `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, the paths the repository census still gives the two files steps 345-346 moved; nothing is written there. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the builders and the axes are the same expressions, and no BerremanTests fact is added or removed. `LangasiteInverseTests` (the uniaxial builder and axes), `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s, the triclinic ones) and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s, the absorbing ones) are the cheapest classes that drive each moved record. (4) Test, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs`, which reaches the records from the module ahead of the material library: `{F_BUILDERS}`: over test-local records written as literals, the uniaxial record's `opticalProperties.eps` is diagonal (n_o², n_o², n_e²), the triclinic record's is diagonal (n₁², n₂², n₃²), and the absorbing record's has ε₁₁ = n₁² + i·ε″₁₁ and ε₁₂ = i·ε″₁₂ (steps 332-334's builders), each within 1e-15.","acceptance":"After the move, `UniaxialParameters`, `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` with their `opticalProperties` MUST be declared only in `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs`, compiled directly after `DispersionModels.fs`, and their `axes` MUST stay static members declared in `MuellerInverse.fs`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests`, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each crystal record's builder composes its permittivity from its own fields`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests","BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests","BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs","Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs","Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs","Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.each crystal record's builder composes its permittivity from its own fields","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.UniaxialParameters","op":"retire","obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"],"preserves_obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.TriclinicParameters","op":"retire","obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"],"preserves_obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.AbsorbingTriclinicParameters","op":"retire","obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"],"preserves_obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.UniaxialParameters","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs","obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.TriclinicParameters","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs","obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.AbsorbingTriclinicParameters","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs","obligations":["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 354, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [353], "how_to": "A material's physics becomes a union that can hold more than the complexity tree, with one case for now, so that the next step adds the crystal case without touching every reader again (the S11.1 brief 'a new case beside the existing complexity tree'; .spec-md §3.2 'A material's physics is its complexity', which this widens). This is one step because the record field's type changes every consumer at once (the step 13 precedent). No behaviour changes. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: directly after `MaterialComplexity` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialComplexity`), `MaterialPhysics` = `ComplexityPhysics of complexity : MaterialComplexity`, with `member this.toProperties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp` answering the complexity's `toProperties`. `MaterialEntry` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`) replaces `complexity : MaterialComplexity` (step 13) with `physics : MaterialPhysics`, and its `properties` member is `this.physics.toProperties`; its doc says the physics is the entry's data and `properties` its engine composition. (2) The members the readers share, each with one arm here: in `LibraryFacets.fs`, beside `MaterialComplexity.anisotropy` (`LibraryFacets.fs:anisotropy`), `type MaterialPhysics with member this.anisotropy : Anisotropy`; in `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs`, beside `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:isEditable`), `type MaterialPhysics with member this.editableComplexityOpt : MaterialComplexity option`, `Some` of the complexity when its `isEditable` holds and `None` otherwise (an option rather than a flag, ELEV012); in `OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs`, beside `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` (`NkDispersionChart.fs:gyrationComponentsOfComplexity`) and `MaterialComplexity.muKind`, `type MaterialPhysics with member this.gyrationComponents : GyrationComponent list` (the complexity's `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity`) and `member this.muKind : MuKind` (the complexity's `muKind`). (3) Readers. `MaterialStore.fs`: `MaterialEntry.versionPayload` (step 68) becomes `VersionPayload<MaterialPhysics, MaterialMetadata>` with `physics = this.physics`, so the version rule compares the physics structurally as it compared the complexity. `LibraryFacets.fs`: the private `constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt` and `magneticOpt` match `entry.physics` (`ComplexityPhysics complexity` → today's body), the anisotropy facet extracts `entry.physics.anisotropy`, and the transparency facet matches `ComplexityPhysics _` around today's rule. `OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `ReachableMaterial.ofEntry` (`OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:ofEntry`) matches the physics, `ComplexityPhysics complexity` → `ReachableMaterial.definedSegmentsOf complexity`. `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (step 25): `ofMaterialEntry` writes `MaterialPayload` of the physics' complexity and `toMaterialEntry` reads it back as `ComplexityPhysics`, so every entry file, catalogue file, snapshot and stored payload keeps its bytes and its hash (`BuiltInCatalogueParityTests` and `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests` stay green unchanged). `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs` (`entryFromTabulated`, `entryOfAxis`) and `Report.fs` (`dtoToEntry`) build `physics = ComplexityPhysics …`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs`: `ViewOnlyMaterial of reason : ControlCaption * shown : MaterialComplexity` (step 13) carries `shown : MaterialPhysics`; `previewProperties`, `previewGyrationComponents` and `previewMuKind` read `shown.toProperties`, `shown.gyrationComponents` and `shown.muKind`; `initMaterialEditor` seeds through `entry.physics.editableComplexityOpt`: `Some complexity` → `ofComplexity` as today, its `Error e` giving `ViewOnlyMaterial (e.caption, entry.physics)`, and `None` → `ViewOnlyMaterial (ControlCaption \"this entry's physics is not editable term data — view-only\", entry.physics)`; `entryUnder` builds `physics = ComplexityPhysics complexity`. `MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `editableSelection` and the view panel's editability read `entry.physics.editableComplexityOpt` (`Some _` is editable), and both chart call sites read `shownEntry.physics.anisotropy`. `MaterialEditorWindow.fs`: its module doc names the physics. (4) Every test fixture that builds a `MaterialEntry` writes `physics = ComplexityPhysics c` for `complexity = c`, and every test read of `.complexity` reads the physics' complexity through a match; no assertion changes: in `OpticalConstructor.Tests` `MaterialProxyTests.fs`, `SampleProxyTests.fs`, `MaterialComplexityTests.fs`, `MaterialImportTests.fs`, `LibraryFacetsTests.fs`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`, `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `ExportImportTests.fs`, `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs`, `EntryFileJsonTests.fs`, `CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs`, `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` and `BuiltinCatalogue.fs`; in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `MaterialsWindowTests.fs`, `NkDispersionChartTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` and `MaterialsControlsTests.fs`, whichever of them build or read one. A comment or message in an edited file that names the entry's `complexity` field names its physics. No other type, member or option is added. (5) Tests. `MaterialComplexityTests`: `a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does`: for a constant isotropic complexity and a uniaxial dispersive one, `ComplexityPhysics` of each answers `toProperties.getProperties` at 600 nm equal to the complexity's, `anisotropy` equal to the complexity's, and `editableComplexityOpt` `Some` of it; a complexity whose active aspect is `PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw` (step 10) answers `None`. `NkDispersionChartTests`: `a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity`: for a uniaxial-active complexity the physics answers `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` of it and its `muKind`. `MaterialEditorWindowTests`' `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry` reads the view-only case's shown physics where it read its complexity, its assertions otherwise unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the physics union lands, `MaterialEntry` MUST hold `physics : MaterialPhysics` with `properties` its `toProperties`, `MaterialPhysics` MUST hold the one case `ComplexityPhysics`, and every entry file MUST keep its bytes and hash; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity` and the changed `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialPhysics", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialEntry.complexity", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialEntry.physics", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.MaterialPhysics.anisotropy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialComplexityEditor.MaterialPhysics.editableComplexityOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.NkDispersionChart.MaterialPhysics.gyrationComponents", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.NkDispersionChart.MaterialPhysics.muKind", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialEditorView.EditorMode", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 355, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [354], "how_to": "A material version holds one of the three crystal-parameter records as its physics, beside the complexity tree, and composes its engine properties through the S10.1 builders; the editor, the facets and the entry-file schema follow (the S11.1 brief 'Material physics form'; .spec-md §3.16). The editor follows as it followed the published gyration law (step 10): the ladder edits complexity trees, so a crystal entry opens view-only; a crystal material reaches the library through its entry file (import and drop, S3.1-S3.2) and through Promote to library (S11.5). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `CrystalPhysics.fs` (step 353), after the three records: `CrystalParameters` = `UniaxialCrystal of UniaxialParameters` | `TriclinicCrystal of TriclinicParameters` | `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal of AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`, with `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` (each case its record's `opticalProperties`) and `member this.toProperties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp`, `this.opticalProperties.dispersive` (`Dispersion.fs`, `OpticalProperties.dispersive`): the same tensors at every wavelength. It is stored in the serializer's case form, as `SlotTurn` is (step 256), so no int tag is added. (2) `MaterialLibrary.fs`: `MaterialPhysics` (step 354) gains `CrystalParameterPhysics of crystal : CrystalParameters`, and `toProperties` answers `crystal.toProperties` for it. (3) Each shared member gains its arm. `LibraryFacets.fs`: `type CrystalParameters with member this.anisotropy : Anisotropy` (`Uniaxial` for `UniaxialCrystal`, `Biaxial` for the two triclinic cases) and `member this.transparency : Transparency` (`Transparent` for the uniaxial and the triclinic crystal, `Absorbing` for the absorbing one), and `MaterialPhysics.anisotropy` answers the crystal's. `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs`: `editableComplexityOpt` answers `None`. `NkDispersionChart.fs`: `gyrationComponents` answers `allGyrationComponents` and `muKind` `ScalarMuKind`, μ being the vacuum's in every builder. So `initMaterialEditor` opens a crystal entry as `ViewOnlyMaterial` with step 354's caption, its preview charting `shown.toProperties`, and the Materials window offers no Edit for it, with no change to either view. (4) `LibraryFacets.fs`: the private `constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt` and `magneticOpt` answer `None` for a crystal, and the transparency facet extracts `crystal.transparency` for it; the dispersion facet already reads `MaterialEntry.dispersion`, which is `ConstantMaterial` for a crystal; the dispersion-model, gyration-class, handedness and magnetic facets do not apply, because they classify the ladder's value trees and a crystal's gyration is parameters. `OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `ofEntry` answers no defined segment for a crystal, so it never flags, as a constant complexity does not. (5) Entry files. `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `LibraryEntryPayload` (step 25) gains `CrystalMaterialPayload of CrystalParameters`, whose `kind` is `MaterialEntryKind`; `ofMaterialEntry` writes it for a crystal and `MaterialPayload` for a complexity; `toMaterialEntry` reads either; every other decoder answers `EntryKindMismatchErr` for it as for `MaterialPayload`, and every other complete match over the payload gains the case. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-material.schema.json` (step 30): under version 1 the payload's case tag is `MaterialPayload` or `CrystalMaterialPayload`, written as the schema writes the existing tag, the crystal inside it bound by the serializer (`MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one). The schema version stays 1: no stored file changes, because every existing material keeps `MaterialPayload` (.spec-md §7: no migration, no stored data predates the case). The database stores the canonical payload (step 69), so nothing else in Storage changes. No editor for crystal parameters, no wire tag and no other member is added. (6) Tests, over test-local records written as literals (a uniaxial crystal n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, g11 3.0e-5, g33 −1.0e-5; a triclinic one; an absorbing triclinic one with fifteen distinct values). `MaterialComplexityTests`: `a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength`: for each case an entry of `CrystalParameterPhysics` answers, at 400, 600 and 800 nm, `properties.getProperties` equal to its record's `opticalProperties` (ε, μ and ρ through the file's tolerance helpers, 1e-15) and `dispersion` `ConstantMaterial`; `a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only`: a crystal answers `editableComplexityOpt = None` and a constant isotropic complexity `Some` of itself. `LibraryFacetsTests`: `a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply`, over entries built as `materialEntryWith` builds them, with a crystal physics:anisotropy `Uniaxial` / `Biaxial` / `Biaxial`, transparency `Transparent` / `Transparent` / `Absorbing`, dispersion `Constant`, and the dispersion-model, gyration-class, handedness and magnetic facets not applicable. `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`: `a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band`: a wavelength sweep over 300-900 nm flags nothing for a crystal entry. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`: `a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse`: `ofMaterialEntry` then `toMaterialEntry` answers each crystal entry, its content's payload being `CrystalMaterialPayload`, and `toSample` of it `EntryKindMismatchErr`. `EntryFileJsonTests`: `a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record`: each crystal content goes `sealed`, `fileText`, `parseEntry MaterialEntryKind` and answers an equal envelope whose decoder answers the entry, the text naming `CrystalMaterialPayload`. `MaterialProxyTests` (`MaterialProxyContract`, steps 66, 69, so both stores run it): `a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics`: a minted absorbing crystal material saved through `saveMaterial` resolves at version 1 to an equal entry and is listed by `listMaterials ActiveOnly`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`: `a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties`: `initMaterialEditor` over a uniaxial crystal entry gives `ViewOnlyMaterial`, its `previewProperties.getProperties` at 600 nm equal to the crystal's `opticalProperties`, and its `previewGyrationComponents` equal to `allGyrationComponents`.", "acceptance": "After the crystal case lands, an entry of `CrystalParameterPhysics` MUST compose its record's builder at every wavelength, classify by its crystal's anisotropy and transparency, never flag out of band, open view-only, and round-trip its entry file as `CrystalMaterialPayload` while every existing file keeps its bytes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength`, `a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only`, `a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply`, `a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band`, `a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse`, `a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record` and `a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics` under `MaterialProxyTests` and `MaterialProxySqliteTests`, the count rising by 8; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-material.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests.a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OutOfBandDiagnosticTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.CrystalParameters", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialPhysics", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.CrystalParameters.anisotropy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.CrystalParameters.transparency", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.LibraryEntryPayload.CrystalMaterialPayload", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 356, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [355], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests"], "how_to": "Sessions' gain models become data, and `MuellerReconstruction.familyGain` with its `GainCalibration` cases becomes their first implementation (001 §L 'Sessions and gain models as data: … per session the gain is free, anchored to its AIR runs, or interpolated between two AIR repeats … These rules replace the hand-written family rules: `MuellerReconstruction.familyGain` becomes their first implementation'; the S11.1 brief 'moved, not copied'; .spec-md §6 row 'Gain rules'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'): after the step `familyGain`, `GainCalibration`, `RepeatPairGain`, `SplitGain`, `CplCplGain` and `InterpolatedGain` exist nowhere, and each of their rules exists once, in the gain model. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs`, `module Studies` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ImportProfiles.fs` (step 300), the last Domain file, because a study names experiments, items, materials, the crystal axes and AIR gains declared before it: one `<Compile Include=\"Studies.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: a study, a named set of one kit's experiments fitted together, with its unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials (spec 0050 S11.1). In this order: (a) `StudyError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `EmptyGainAnchorsErr` (an anchored gain model names no AIR run), `MissingAnchorGainErr` (a gain model names an AIR run whose gain is not given) and `FreeSessionGainErr` (a free session gain is fitted, so no AIR rule derives it), with `member this.describe : string` in step 39's form: `the gain model names no AIR run: <reason>`, `the AIR run's gain is not known: <reason>` and `the session gain is fitted, not derived from AIR runs: <reason>`. Later S11.1 steps add cases, each with its line. (b) `AirRepeatPair = { opening : ExperimentName; closing : ExperimentName }`, the AIR runs that open and close a drifting session. (c) `SessionGainModel` = `FreeSessionGain` | `AnchoredSessionGain of anchors : ExperimentName list` | `InterpolatedSessionGain of repeats : AirRepeatPair`, stored in the serializer's case form (step 256's `SlotTurn` precedent), no int tag. (d) `AirAnchorGain = { run : ExperimentName; gain : AirGain; capturedAt : System.DateTimeOffset }`, one AIR run's fitted gain and the mean capture time of its rows (the reference `fit_air_gain`). (e) `GainInterpolation = { gainStart : AirGain; timeStart : System.DateTimeOffset; gainEnd : AirGain; timeEnd : System.DateTimeOffset }`, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:InterpolatedGain` moved and renamed, its fields unchanged. (f) `SessionGainRule` = `SteadyGainRule of gain : AirGain` | `InterpolatedGainRule of interpolation : GainInterpolation`, with `member this.gainAt (t : System.DateTimeOffset) : AirGain`: the steady gain, or `familyGain`'s `Day1Interp` arm moved verbatim (the span in `TotalSeconds`, weight 0 for a span ≤ 0 and otherwise `(t − timeStart) / span` clamped to [0, 1], then `AirGain ((1.0 - weight) * gainStart.value + weight * gainEnd.value)`). (g) `type SessionGainModel with member this.ruleWith (anchors : AirAnchorGain list) : Result<SessionGainRule, StudyError>`, each anchor found by its `run`: `FreeSessionGain` → `FreeSessionGainErr`; an anchored model with no run → `EmptyGainAnchorsErr`; a run `anchors` lacks → `MissingAnchorGainErr` naming it (the first, in model order); one run → `SteadyGainRule` of its gain (`familyGain`'s `Day2Single`, and each side of its `SplitGain`); two → `SteadyGainRule (AirGain (0.5 * (a.value + b.value)))` (`familyGain`'s `meanPair`, moved); more → `SteadyGainRule` of their sum over their count; `InterpolatedSessionGain` → `InterpolatedGainRule` of the opening run's gain and time and the closing run's. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: delete `RepeatPairGain`, `InterpolatedGain`, `CplCplGain` (`Day1Interp`, `Day2Single`), `SplitGain`, `GainCalibration` and `familyGain` with their docs (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:familyGain`). The Stage-3 section comment and `correctSignal`'s doc name the session's gain rule (`SessionGainRule.gainAt`, spec 0050 S11.1) where they name `familyGain`. `AirGain`, `scalarGain`, `darkSubtract`, `DarkMean`, `airIdentityPred` and `correctSignal` stay. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs` (steps 349-352) opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies`. (a) The nine AIR block literals become `ExperimentName`s, born as names because in a kit the AIR runs are experiments of those names and a gain model anchors to experiments by name (001 §L); a block's rows are those whose `experiment.nameText.toExperimentName` (steps 270, 286) answers `Ok` of its name. (b) Each block's `AirAnchorGain` is its name, the gain `fitAirGain` fits over it and the time `meanTime` computes over it, for all nine. (c) The five families' gain rules become six gain models resolved through `ruleWith` over the nine anchors: LP-LP `AnchoredSessionGain [ LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2; LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R ]`, LP-CPL `[ LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2; LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R ]`, CPL-LP before the split `[ CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2 ]` and from the split on `[ CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R ]`, CPL-CPL day 1 `InterpolatedSessionGain { opening = CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL; closing = CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR }` and CPL-CPL day 2 `AnchoredSessionGain [ CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2 ]`; a refusal is the new `StagedMuellerError` case `SessionGainErr of error : StudyError`, which no committed data reaches. (d) Each science row's signal is `correctSignal darkMean r.avgTotal (rule.gainAt r.capturedAt)` with its family's rule, a CPL-LP row captured strictly before the split time taking the pre rule and every other CPL-LP row the post rule, as `SplitGain` did. (e) `StagedMuellerData` replaces `gains : GainCalibration` and `cplCplDay1Gain : InterpolatedGain` with `airGains : AirAnchorGain list`, the nine in the reference order (LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP each `-2` then `-2R`, then `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`), and its doc says so. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's gain assertion reads each gain from `staged.airGains` by run name against its `MuellerReference` value (`lpLpGainA` for `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `lpLpGainB` for `-2R`, …, `cplCplDay1GainStart` for `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `cplCplDay1GainEnd` for `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR`, `cplCplDay2Gain` for `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`), a run missing from the list failing the fact; its band, its numbers and the rest of the fact are unchanged. The fact `Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred, correctSignal and every per-family familyGain rule (always-run)` keeps its `scalarGain`, `darkSubtract`, `correctSignal` and `airIdentityPred` pins, loses its `familyGain` block, whose rules moved, and is renamed `Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred and correctSignal (always-run)`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4): every row divides by the gain the same operations compute (one run's gain itself, two runs' `0.5 * (a + b)`, the interpolation's same expression). `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged. (5) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs`, `module StudySessionTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, carrying the moved block's literals at fixed literal times: `a session anchored to one AIR run takes its gain, and to more the mean of their gains`: anchors of 10 and 20 answer a steady 15 equal by `=` to `AirGain (0.5 * (10.0 + 20.0))`, 4 and 6 answer 5, one anchor of 42 answers 42, three anchors of 1, 2 and 6 answer 3, and the CPL-LP split as two one-run sessions of 100 and 200 answers 100 and 200 at any time; `a session interpolated between two AIR repeats weighs their gains by time and clamps outside them`: opening 30 at 10:00 and closing 50 at 14:00 answer 40 at 12:00, 30 at 10:00, 50 at 14:00, 30 at 09:00 and 50 at 15:00, within 1e-12; `a free gain has no AIR rule, and an anchored model with no run or a missing run is refused`: `FreeSessionGain` answers `FreeSessionGainErr`, `AnchoredSessionGain []` `EmptyGainAnchorsErr`, and an anchored or interpolated model naming a run the anchors lack `MissingAnchorGainErr` whose reason holds that name; `every study error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it.", "acceptance": "After the gain models land, `SessionGainModel.ruleWith` MUST resolve a free, anchored or interpolated model by `familyGain`'s moved rules, `familyGain`, `GainCalibration`, `RepeatPairGain`, `SplitGain`, `CplCplGain` and `InterpolatedGain` MUST be gone, and `StagedMuellerPath` MUST divide each row by its session's rule and answer the nine AIR gains as `airGains`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a session anchored to one AIR run takes its gain, and to more the mean of their gains`, `a session interpolated between two AIR repeats weighs their gains by time and clamps outside them`, `a free gain has no AIR rule, and an anchored model with no run or a missing run is refused` and `every study error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, with `Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred and correctSignal (always-run)` in place of the familyGain fact, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred, correctSignal and every per-family familyGain rule (always-run)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "successor": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred and correctSignal (always-run)", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a session anchored to one AIR run takes its gain, and to more the mean of their gains", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a session interpolated between two AIR repeats weighs their gains by time and clamps outside them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a free gain has no AIR rule, and an anchored model with no run or a missing run is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.familyGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.GainCalibration", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.RepeatPairGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.SplitGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.CplCplGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.InterpolatedGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.AirRepeatPair", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.AirAnchorGain", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.GainInterpolation", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainRule", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainModel.ruleWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerData", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 357, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [356], "how_to": "A study's experiments fall into session blocks, split automatically at the Diagnostic runs or set by hand, and a session's dark comes from the Dark runs (001 §L 'Sessions and gain models as data: auto-split at Diagnostic experiments, or by hand; … dark from the Dark runs'; the S11.1 brief 'Sessions, auto-split at DiagnosticRun experiments or set by hand'; step 285: a hand-set `SessionName` is the session a run belongs to, the rest split at the Diagnostic runs). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after `SessionGainModel.ruleWith` (step 356): (1) `StudySession = { name : SessionName; experiments : ExperimentName list }`, one session block. (2) `static member splitAll (experiments : Experiment list) : StudySession list`, over the experiments in the order given: an experiment whose `sessionOpt` is `Some s` (`SetExperimentSession`, step 294) joins the session named `s`; a `DiagnosticRun` (step 285) with no hand-set session belongs to no session and closes the current automatic block; every other experiment joins the current automatic block. Each non-empty automatic block is a session named `Session <k>`, `k` the smallest positive integer whose `SessionName` neither a hand-set session of the list nor an earlier block holds, so two Diagnostic runs in a row, or one at either end, make no empty session. The sessions are ordered by the position of their first experiment, each holding its experiments in list order. (3) `member this.darkRunsIn (experiments : Experiment list) : ExperimentName list`: the session's `DarkRun` experiments in its order, or, when it holds none, every `DarkRun` experiment of `experiments` in their order, because one darkness file can serve every session (the optics-mueller kit's `darkness_checks.csv`, step 330). Reading the dark level from those runs' data is the forward model's (S11.2). No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `StudySessionTests` (step 356), over test-local experiments built as `ExperimentProxyTests`' fixtures build them, differing only in name, role and session: `experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own`: E1 (Science), E2 (Calibration), D1 (Diagnostic), E3 (Science), E4 (Science, hand-set `Day 2`), E5 (Dark) and D2 (Diagnostic) split into `Session 1` [E1; E2], `Session 2` [E3; E5] and `Day 2` [E4], in that order; the same list with E1 hand-set to `Session 1` gives `Session 1` [E1], `Session 2` [E2] and `Session 3` [E3; E5] and `Day 2` [E4], ordered by first experiment; and a list of only Diagnostic runs gives no session. `a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study`: in the first split, `Session 2`'s dark runs are [E5], and `Session 1`'s and `Day 2`'s are every Dark run of the list, [E5]; a session holding two Dark runs answers its own two.", "acceptance": "After sessions land, `StudySession.splitAll` MUST gather hand-set sessions, split the rest at each Diagnostic run into `Session <k>` blocks ordered by their first experiment, and `darkRunsIn` MUST answer a session's own Dark runs or else every Dark run; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own` and `a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudySession", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudySession.splitAll", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudySession.darkRunsIn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number":358,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S111f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[357],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests"],"how_to":"The study as Domain data, and CreateStudy's pure half (001 §L '`Study` grows from the experiment collection: a named set of experiments inside ONE kit, plus: the unknowns (owner + scope); sessions; fit settings; its append-only fit runs', the scope table, 'Weights and ablation: a weight per experiment or per detector; enable / disable per experiment'; 001 §E 'notes on … studies … live in their files'; 001 §P `CreateStudy`; the S11.1 brief). Fit runs are their own files (S11.3). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. Every case name has two words and no `bool` appears. In `Studies.fs`, after `StudySession` (step 357), in this order: (1) `StudyName of string` with `.value`, `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<StudyName, StudyError>` keeping the text and refusing an empty or white-space one with `InvalidStudyNameErr`, and `member this.fileStem : FileStem` = `FileStem.ofText this.value` (step 24), the stem of its `<name>.study-json` (001 §A). (2) `StudyNotes of string` with `.value` and `static member none`. (3) `ParameterScope` = `ItemScope` | `MaterialScope` | `SessionBlockScope` | `ExperimentScope` (001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'): `member this.value : int` 1 to 4 in that order, `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : ParameterScope option`, `member this.text : string` (`Item`, `Material`, `Session`, `Experiment`) and `static member all`. The session case is `SessionBlockScope`, after 001's 'one value per session block', because STL declares a `SessionScope` case and DU case names are unique among ours (AGENTS.md, ELEV016; the lower assembly keeps its name). (4) `StudyParameterRef` = `ItemParameterRef of item : ItemId * name : ParameterName` | `MaterialParameterRef of material : MaterialVersionId * name : ParameterName`, with `member this.name : ParameterName` and `member this.describe : string` (`item <GUID> <name>` or `material <GUID> v<n> <name>`). (5) `ScopedParameter = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; scope : ParameterScope }`, a scope the study sets. (6) `ParameterLink = { follower : StudyParameterRef; leader : StudyParameterRef }`, 'CPL2.δ = CPL1.δ': the follower takes the leader's value (001 §L 'Explicit links … are constraints'). (7) `SessionGainSetting = { session : SessionName; model : SessionGainModel }`. (8) `FitMode` = `JointFit` | `StagedFit` (001 §L 'Fit modes'; S11.3 runs them), with `value` 1-2, `tryOfWire`, `text` (`Joint`, `Staged`) and `all`. (9) `ResidualWeight of float` with `.value`, `static member tryCreate (value : float) : Result<ResidualWeight, StudyError>` refusing a NaN, infinite, zero or negative value with `InvalidResidualWeightErr`, and `static member unit` (1.0). (10) `ExperimentWeightSetting = { experiment : ExperimentName; weight : ResidualWeight }` and `DetectorWeightSetting = { detector : ItemId; weight : ResidualWeight }`. (11) `StudyFitSettings = { mode : FitMode; experimentWeights : ExperimentWeightSetting list; detectorWeights : DetectorWeightSetting list; disabled : ExperimentName list }`, with `static member initial` (`JointFit`, no weight, nothing disabled). (12) `OpenedMaterial = { version : MaterialVersionId; name : EntryName; crystal : CrystalParameters; parameters : Parameter list }`, the study-local working copy of an opened material version (001 §I 'a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file'), which step 361 fills. (13) `Study = { name : StudyName; experiments : ExperimentName list; materials : OpenedMaterial list; scopes : ScopedParameter list; links : ParameterLink list; sessionGains : SessionGainSetting list; settings : StudyFitSettings; notes : StudyNotes }`. Experiments are named by `ExperimentName`, because a kit stores each under its name (step 290). (14) `static member create (name : StudyName) (experiments : ExperimentName list) (held : Study list) (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`: `DuplicateStudyNameErr` naming both when a held study's `name.fileStem` equals the name's ignoring case (every `<name>.study-json` shares the kit root, step 216's rule for items); `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming the first name no kit experiment has; otherwise the study holding the names in order, each once, with nothing opened, scoped or linked, no gain setting, `StudyFitSettings.initial` and `StudyNotes.none`. (15) `member this.sessionsIn (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : StudySession list`: `StudySession.splitAll` of the study's experiments as `kitExperiments` holds them, in study order. (16) `member this.gainModelOf (session : SessionName) : SessionGainModel`: the setting's model, or `FreeSessionGain`. `StudyError` gains `InvalidStudyNameErr` (`the study name is not valid: <reason>`), `DuplicateStudyNameErr` (`the kit already has a study of that name: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` (`the kit has no such experiment: <reason>`) and `InvalidResidualWeightErr` (`the residual weight is not valid: <reason>`). No wire converter is added here: the study file (step 359) adds the two. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs`, `module StudyTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local experiments built as in `StudySessionTests`: `a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `StudyName.tryCreate \"QZ:LR\"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem \"QZ_LR\"`, and `\"\"` and `\"  \"` answer `InvalidStudyNameErr`; `a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text`: the tags 1-4 and 1-2 in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 5 (and 3), the texts as above and `all` in tag order; `a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value`: 0.5 and 2 are kept, and NaN, +∞, 0 and −1 answer `InvalidResidualWeightErr`; `a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks`: over E1, E2 and E3, `create` of `QZ-LR` with [E2; E1; E2] answers [E2; E1] with the initial settings; with a held study `qz-lr` it answers `DuplicateStudyNameErr`; with [E1; E9] `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming E9; `a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain`: a study of [E3; D1; E1] (D1 Diagnostic) answers `Session 1` [E3] and `Session 2` [E1], and `gainModelOf` of each is `FreeSessionGain`. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the four new cases.","acceptance":"After the study's shape lands, `Studies.fs` MUST declare `StudyName`, `StudyNotes`, `ParameterScope` (with `SessionBlockScope`), `StudyParameterRef`, `ScopedParameter`, `ParameterLink`, `SessionGainSetting`, `FitMode`, `ResidualWeight`, the weight settings, `StudyFitSettings`, `OpenedMaterial` and `Study`, and `Study.create` MUST refuse a held name and an unknown experiment; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text`, `a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value`, `a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks` and `a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyNotes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterScope","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyParameterRef","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ScopedParameter","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterLink","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainSetting","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.FitMode","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ResidualWeight","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ExperimentWeightSetting","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.DetectorWeightSetting","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyFitSettings","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.create","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.sessionsIn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.gainModelOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError","op":"change_shape","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number":359,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S111g","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[358],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests"],"how_to":"A study persists as its own kit file, `<name>.study-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema, and recording it snapshots and pins the material versions it opens (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .study-json'; 001 §E 'Library closure snapshot', 'Writes are atomic'; 001 §P '`KitProxy` … studies'; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 146's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`) and step 217's shape for items; no second parser or writer is written. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `Studies.fs`, after `Study` (step 358): `StudyFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; study : Study }`, the `.study-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1; `type Study with member this.studyFile : StudyFile` (one direction, ELEV006); and `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list`, each opened material's `EntryVersionReference { entryId = version.materialId.toLibraryEntryId; version = version.version }` in study order (steps 24, 137): what the kit snapshots and pins. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/item.schema.json` (step 217), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/study.json`: `schemaVersion` a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 (`then`), the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `study`, and `study` holds exactly `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\\S`), `experiments` (an array of non-empty strings), `materials`, `scopes`, `links` and `sessionGains` (arrays), `settings` (an object holding exactly `mode`, an integer from 1 to 2, `experimentWeights` and `detectorWeights`, arrays, and `disabled`, an array of non-empty strings) and `notes` (a string). The inner shapes are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/item.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateStudyFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateItemFile` (step 217) does. (3) `CanonicalJson.options` (`CanonicalJson.fs`) gains two converters, for `ParameterScope` and `FitMode`, written as step 285's `ExperimentRole` converter is and registered beside it before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: each writes the case's `value` and reads through `tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. `SessionGainModel`, `StudyParameterRef` and `CrystalParameters` keep the serializer's case form, and nothing else in the options changes. (4) `KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146, 217-219): `type StudyFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText`); `type KitFileText with member this.parseStudyFile : Result<StudyFile, StorageError>` (`parseVersionedText validateStudyFile StudyKitFile.extension StudyFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value`, steps 123-124); on the `KitProxy` extension `member this.writeStudy (study : Study) : Result<unit, KitError>`, which writes `study.studyFile.fileText` with `writeKindFile StudyKitFile study.name.fileStem`, a rendering error being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file, and `member this.readStudies () : Result<Study list, KitError>`, which parses every stem `listKindFiles StudyKitFile` answers, a refusal or a file whose study's `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason and refusing the whole read, ordered by the name's text (ordinal); and on the `KitLibraryContext` extension `member this.recordStudy (study : Study) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>`: `this.snapshotReferences study.libraryReferences` (step 139), then `this.kit.proxy.writeStudy study`, a `KitError` wrapped as `KitLibraryKitErr`. Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) `writeStudy` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. No delete, rename, cache or other member is added. There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. (5) Tests. Their study is test-local: `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2, with an opened absorbing crystal material written as an `OpenedMaterial` record literal over a test-local probe whose one parameter, `n3`, is an `UnknownParameter` with a prior, one `ScopedParameter` (`ExperimentScope`), one `ParameterLink`, one gain setting of each `SessionGainModel` case, both weights, E2 disabled and two lines of notes. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `a study is stored under its name`: `StudyKitFile.fileNameOf (StudyName \"QZ-LR\").fileStem` is `FileName \"QZ-LR.study-json\"`; `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`: `studyFile`, `fileText`, `parseStudyFile` answer an equal file; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys as `schemaVersion` then `study` in ordinal order, writes the fit mode and the scope as their tags, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text; `a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` 2, with its body and alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = StudyKitFile.extension`, found 2 and expected 1; `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds`: without `study`, with an extra top-level key, with `study.name` `\"  \"` and with `study.settings.mode` 3 each answer `SchemaValidationErr`, and `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`. `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 166, 285): `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes each `ParameterScope` and `FitMode` as its tag (`SessionBlockScope` as `3`) and reads it back, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the scope tag 5 and the mode tag 3 with `MalformedJsonErr`. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs`, `module KitStudyFileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, whose facts each make a folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitStudyFileTests\", <a new GUID>)` and a `KitProxy.create` over it with `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (step 218's precedent): `a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name`: `QZ-LR` and `LR` written answer `LR.study-json` and `QZ-LR.study-json` in the folder and `readStudies` answers `LR` then `QZ-LR`; `a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file`: `Broken.study-json` holding `{` and `Other.study-json` holding `QZ-LR`'s text each make `readStudies` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file; `a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView` `writeStudy` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and the folder's bytes are unchanged. `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), over its built-in library, its recorder of pins and its in-memory kit opened read-write: `recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file`: a user absorbing crystal material saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial` and held by `QZ-LR` as an `OpenedMaterial` record literal of its version, recorded through `recordStudy`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding that material's version 1 and its category, `paths` holding `library/<its GUID>@v1.material-json` and `QZ-LR.study-json`, the recorder holding that version, and `kit.proxy.readStudies ()` answering the study; `a read-only kit records no study`: under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` `recordStudy` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged.","acceptance":"After the study file lands, `StudyFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseStudyFile` reads back equal against `schema/study.schema.json`, `KitProxy.writeStudy` / `readStudies` MUST store each study under its name and refuse a bad file whole, and `KitLibraryContext.recordStudy` MUST snapshot and pin the opened material versions before it writes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study is stored under its name`, `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds`, `a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name`, `a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file`, `a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing`, `recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file` and `a read-only kit records no study`, the count rising by 9, and the widened `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study is stored under its name","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study file round-trips through its canonical text","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests.a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests.a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests.a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a read-only kit records no study","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.studyFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.libraryReferences","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateStudyFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.StudyFile.fileText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitFileText.parseStudyFile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeStudy","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readStudies","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordStudy","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 360, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [359], "how_to": "AddExperimentsToStudy's pure half (001 §P `AddExperimentsToStudy`; 001 §L 'a named set of experiments inside ONE kit'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. On `Study` in `Studies.fs`: `member this.withExperiments (names : ExperimentName list) (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`. It answers `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming the first name no kit experiment has, and changes nothing then; otherwise the study whose experiments are its own, in place, followed by each given name it does not hold yet, in the given order and each once. Every other field is unchanged: a study's scopes, links and gain settings name parameters and sessions, not the experiment list. No removal member is added; disabling an experiment is step 365's. Tests, in `StudyTests` (step 358): `adding experiments appends the new ones in order and keeps those the study holds`: a study of [E2] given [E3; E2; E1; E3] answers [E2; E3; E1], its other fields equal; `adding an experiment the kit lacks changes nothing`: given [E1; E9] it answers `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming E9.", "acceptance": "After AddExperimentsToStudy's pure half lands, `Study.withExperiments` MUST append the names the study lacks in order, each once, and refuse a name the kit lacks with nothing changed; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `adding experiments appends the new ones in order and keeps those the study holds` and `adding an experiment the kit lacks changes nothing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.adding experiments appends the new ones in order and keeps those the study holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-ADD-EXPERIMENTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.adding an experiment the kit lacks changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-ADD-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withExperiments", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-ADD-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number":361,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S111i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[360],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests"],"how_to":"A study opens a material version into a working copy whose every component is a parameter, generated from the material's crystal record, shared by every sample made of it (001 §I 'Material parameters as unknowns: a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file, with `Unknown` components; every sample made of it shares them (`MaterialScope`)'; 001 §N 'Parameter-axis generation: … publishes its `ParameterAxis` list. Case 1b's generated axes equal `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` — an exact test'; 001 §P `OpenMaterial`; the S11.1 brief 'Generated axes', 'the EXACT test'; .spec-md §3.16 'its generated axes are that record's `axes`'). A complexity tree publishes no parameter axis in this spec: its eps is formula, table or constant data the ladder edits, so a material is fitted through its crystal-parameter form (step 355). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after step 360's member: (1) `type ParameterAxis<'Parameters> with member this.parameterValueOf (p : 'Parameters) : ParameterValue` (`this.read p` as a `ParameterValue`, the one conversion from an axis read to a parameter's number) and `member this.writeValue (value : ParameterValue) (p : 'Parameters) : 'Parameters` (`this.write value.value p`, the one conversion back). (2) `type CrystalParameters with member this.parameterAxes : ParameterAxis<CrystalParameters> list`: the axes of its record (`UniaxialParameters.axes`, `TriclinicParameters.axes` or `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes`, step 353) in their order, each lifted onto the crystal by a private helper per case: the same `name` and the same field case (`RefractionIndexField`, `RhoValueField`, `EpsValueField`), its access reading the record of a crystal of the same case and writing back a crystal of that case; a crystal of another case reads as `this` reads and is written back unchanged, because the axes are generated from `this` and a study applies them to its own working copy only. The list is generated, never hand-written. (3) On `OpenedMaterial` (step 358): `static member openFrom (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<OpenedMaterial, StudyError>`, for a `CrystalParameterPhysics crystal` the working copy `{ version; name = entry.name; crystal; parameters }` whose parameters are, per generated axis in order, `{ name = axis.name; state = KnownParameter (axis.parameterValueOf crystal) }`, and for a `ComplexityPhysics` `MaterialWithoutParametersErr` naming the entry; `member this.withParameterState (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<OpenedMaterial, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyParameterErr` naming the material and the name when no component has it, `InvalidStudyParameterErr` carrying the `ItemError.describe` of `{ name = name; state = state }.validate` (step 214) when the state breaks its rules, and otherwise that component's state replaced in place (freeing a component is its `UnknownParameter` state, 001 §I); and `member this.currentCrystal : CrystalParameters`, the crystal with each component written through its generated axis at its parameter's current number (a known or calibrated value, an unknown's start), in order. (4) On `Study`: `member this.openMaterial (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr` naming the version when `materials` holds it, `openFrom`'s error passing through, and otherwise the study with the working copy appended; `member this.withMaterialParameterState (version : MaterialVersionId) (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyMaterialErr` naming the version when it is not opened, and otherwise its copy's `withParameterState` in place. (5) `type Sample with member this.openedMaterialsIn (study : Study) : OpenedMaterial list`: the study's working copies whose version the sample's `structure.referencedMaterialVersions` (step 61) holds, in study order, so every sample made of an opened material reads the same copy (`MaterialScope`); the forward model reads it (S11.2). `StudyError` gains `MaterialWithoutParametersErr` (`the material publishes no parameter to fit: <reason>`), `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr` (`the study already opens that material version: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyMaterialErr` (`the study opens no such material version: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyParameterErr` (`the study has no such parameter: <reason>`) and `InvalidStudyParameterErr` (`the parameter state is not valid: <reason>`). No cache, conversion or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs`, `module StudyMaterialTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over test-local entries of each crystal case (fifteen distinct literal values for the absorbing probe) and a test-local `MaterialVersionId`: `the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` (the exact test): the opened copy's `crystal.parameterAxes` has the fifteen names of `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` in its order and the same field case at each position; at each position the generated read of `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal probe` equals the record axis's read of `probe` exactly, and the generated write of 2.5 times that value answers `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal` of the record axis's write of it; and the copy's parameters are those fifteen names, each `KnownParameter` at the probe's value; `an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way`: the same over a uniaxial (4 axes) and a triclinic (9) entry; `a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused`: a constant isotropic complexity entry answers `MaterialWithoutParametersErr`, and opening the absorbing version twice `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr`; `freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value`: setting `n3` to an `UnknownParameter` starting at 1.70 within [1.60, 1.80] changes that parameter in place, the copy's `currentCrystal` reading index3 1.70 and every other field the probe's; a name the copy lacks answers `UnknownStudyParameterErr` and reversed bounds `InvalidStudyParameterErr`, the study unchanged; `every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy`: a plate sample whose substrate is the opened version and a film sample whose `Repeated` cell names it each answer [the copy], and a sample of another version answers []. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the five new cases.","acceptance":"After OpenMaterial's pure half lands, `OpenedMaterial.openFrom` MUST turn a crystal-parameter version into a working copy whose parameters follow the record's generated axes, refusing a complexity tree, and the generated axes of an opened `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` material MUST equal `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` in names, order, field kinds and read / write on a probe; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes`, `an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way`, `a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused`, `freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value` and `every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterAxis.parameterValueOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterAxis.writeValue","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.CrystalParameters.parameterAxes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial.openFrom","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial.withParameterState","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial.currentCrystal","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.openMaterial","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withMaterialParameterState","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Sample.openedMaterialsIn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError","op":"change_shape","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number":362,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S111j","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[361],"how_to":"The study's unknowns, each with its scope, and the owners each scope gives it (001 §L 'the unknowns (owner + scope)' and the scope table: ItemScope 'One value for every experiment using the item', MaterialScope 'One value for every sample of an opened material', SessionScope 'One value per session block (gain)', ExperimentScope 'One value per run'; 001 §I 'Intensity detector | Gain (session-scoped)'; the S11.1 brief 'each with an owner (item / material / session / experiment) and a scope'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after step 361's members: (1) `UnknownOwner` = `ItemOwner of ItemId` | `MaterialOwner of MaterialVersionId` | `SessionOwner of SessionName` | `ExperimentOwner of ExperimentName`: what holds one value of an unknown; it is derived and never stored, so it carries no tag. (2) `StudyUnknown = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; scope : ParameterScope; unknown : UnknownParameterData }` (step 214's start, bounds and prior). (3) `type Study with member this.scopeOf (parameter : StudyParameterRef) : ParameterScope`: the study's `ScopedParameter` for it, or the default: `MaterialScope` for a material component, `SessionBlockScope` for an item parameter named `gain` (the one `IntensityDetectorModel` publishes, step 208), `ItemScope` for every other item parameter. (4) `member this.unknownsWith (used : Item list) : StudyUnknown list`: for each item of `used` in order, each of its parameters whose state is `UnknownParameter`, then for each opened material in order each component whose state is `UnknownParameter`, each with `scopeOf`; a parameter that is a link's follower is left out, because it takes its leader's value (001 §L). `used` is the items the study's experiments use (`Experiment.itemsUsedBy`, step 261), which the caller passes. (5) `type StudyUnknown with member this.owners (sessions : StudySession list) (users : ExperimentName list) : UnknownOwner list`: under `ItemScope` or `MaterialScope` its one owner, the `ItemOwner` of its item or the `MaterialOwner` of its material; under `SessionBlockScope` one `SessionOwner` per session holding a user, in session order; under `ExperimentScope` one `ExperimentOwner` per user, in order. `users` is the enabled experiments of the study whose setups use the unknown's item or a sample made of its material, which the forward model knows (S11.2). The fitter's vector holds one value per owner of each unknown (S11.2-S11.3). No other type or member is added. Tests, in `StudyTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216) over the built-in circular-polarizer and intensity-detector models: CPL1 with `c2.retardance` unknown, CPL2 with `c2.retardance` and `c2.fastAxisOffset` unknown, a Phone with `gain` unknown, and an opened absorbing material with `n1` and `e11` unknown: `the study's unknowns are its items' and opened materials' unknown parameters, with their scopes, leaving out link followers`: `unknownsWith [ CPL1; CPL2; Phone ]` answers CPL1 `c2.retardance` (ItemScope), CPL2's two (ItemScope), Phone `gain` (SessionBlockScope), `n1` and `e11` (MaterialScope), in that order; with a `ScopedParameter` making CPL1's `ExperimentScope` it answers that scope; with a link (a record literal) whose follower is CPL2's `c2.retardance` that parameter is left out. `an unknown's owners are its item or material, one per session holding a user, or one per user`: over sessions `Session 1` [E1; E2] and `Session 2` [E3], CPL1's unknown has the one `ItemOwner`, `n1` the one `MaterialOwner`, Phone's `gain` with users [E1; E3] `SessionOwner` of both sessions and with users [E2] only `Session 1`, and an `ExperimentScope` unknown with users [E3; E1] the owners E3 then E1.","acceptance":"After the unknowns land, `Study.unknownsWith` MUST list the used items' and opened materials' unknown parameters with their scopes (a detector's `gain` session-scoped by default) and leave out link followers, and `StudyUnknown.owners` MUST give one owner per item or material, per session holding a user, or per user; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the study's unknowns are its items' and opened materials' unknown parameters, with their scopes, leaving out link followers` and `an unknown's owners are its item or material, one per session holding a user, or one per user`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.the study's unknowns are its items' and opened materials' unknown parameters, with their scopes, leaving out link followers","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-UNKNOWNS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.an unknown's owners are its item or material, one per session holding a user, or one per user","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.UnknownOwner","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-UNKNOWNS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyUnknown","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-UNKNOWNS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.scopeOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-UNKNOWNS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.unknownsWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-UNKNOWNS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyUnknown.owners","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number":363,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S111k","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[362],"how_to":"SetParameterScope's pure half (001 §P `SetParameterScope`; 001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. On `Study` in `Studies.fs`: `member this.withParameterScope (scoped : ScopedParameter) (used : Item list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`. It refuses, changing nothing: a parameter the study does not have, an item parameter of no item of `used` holding that name (`Item.tryFindParameter`, step 215) or a material component of no opened copy, with `UnknownStudyParameterErr` naming its `describe`; a scope its kind does not take, with `ScopeNotAllowedErr` naming the parameter and the scope's `text`: an item parameter takes `ItemScope`, `SessionBlockScope` or `ExperimentScope`, and a material component `MaterialScope` only, because 'One value for every sample of an opened material' is a material's sharing rule; and a parameter that is a link's follower or leader, with `ScopeNotAllowedErr` naming the link, so a link always joins parameters of one scope (step 364). Otherwise it answers the study whose `scopes` hold the given entry in place of that parameter's earlier one, or appended. Every other field is unchanged. `StudyError` gains `ScopeNotAllowedErr` (`the parameter cannot take that scope: <reason>`). Tests, in `StudyTests`, over step 362's items and opened material: `setting a parameter's scope replaces its entry in place or adds it, and the default applies until then`: Phone `gain` set to `ExperimentScope` appends its entry and `scopeOf` answers it; set again to `ItemScope` it replaces the entry in place, the list still one long; CPL1's `c2.retardance` answers `ItemScope` before any entry. `a scope is refused for a parameter the study does not use, for a linked parameter, and MaterialScope fits a material component only`: a parameter of an item outside `used`, a name CPL1 lacks, CPL1's `c2.retardance` under `MaterialScope`, `n1` under `ItemScope` and, in a study holding a test-local link (a record literal) whose follower is CPL2's `c2.retardance`, that parameter under `ExperimentScope` each answer their error, the study unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.","acceptance":"After SetParameterScope's pure half lands, `Study.withParameterScope` MUST replace or add a parameter's scope entry, and MUST refuse a parameter the study does not use, a linked parameter and a scope the parameter's kind does not take; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `setting a parameter's scope replaces its entry in place or adds it, and the default applies until then` and `a scope is refused for a parameter the study does not use, for a linked parameter, and MaterialScope fits a material component only`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.setting a parameter's scope replaces its entry in place or adds it, and the default applies until then","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-SET-SCOPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a scope is refused for a parameter the study does not use, for a linked parameter, and MaterialScope fits a material component only","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-SET-SCOPE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs","obligations":["S111-SET-SCOPE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withParameterScope","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-SET-SCOPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError","op":"change_shape","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-SET-SCOPE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 364, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [363], "how_to": "LinkParameters' pure half (001 §L 'Explicit links (\"CPL2.δ = CPL1.δ\") are constraints'; 001 §P `LinkParameters`). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. On `Study` in `Studies.fs`: `member this.withLink (link : ParameterLink) (used : Item list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`. It refuses, changing nothing: either parameter the study does not have (step 363's rule), with `UnknownStudyParameterErr` naming it; and, with `InvalidParameterLinkErr` naming both `describe`s and the broken rule, a follower equal to its leader, a follower that already follows or leads a link, a leader that follows a link (no chain, so every follower reads its leader directly), and two parameters whose `scopeOf` (step 362) differ, because a link equates one value per owner. Otherwise it answers the study with the link appended; nothing else changes. No unlink member is added. `StudyError` gains `InvalidParameterLinkErr` (`the link is not valid: <reason>`). Tests, in `StudyTests`, over step 362's items: `linking CPL2's retardance to CPL1's makes it follow and leaves it out of the unknowns`: linking CPL2's `c2.retardance` (follower) to CPL1's (leader) appends the link, and `unknownsWith` then lists CPL1's retardance and leaves CPL2's out. `a link to itself, a chain, a second link of one follower, a missing parameter or differing scopes is refused`: CPL1's retardance linked to itself; then, with that first link held, CPL1's `c2.retardance` following CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` (a leader made a follower), CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` following CPL2's `c2.retardance` (a chain through a follower), CPL2's retardance following CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` (a second link of one follower), a name CPL1 lacks, and CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` following Phone's `gain` (`ItemScope` against `SessionBlockScope`) each answer their error, the study unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.", "acceptance": "After LinkParameters' pure half lands, `Study.withLink` MUST append a link between two parameters of one scope and MUST refuse a self link, a chain, a second link of a follower, a missing parameter and differing scopes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `linking CPL2's retardance to CPL1's makes it follow and leaves it out of the unknowns` and `a link to itself, a chain, a second link of one follower, a missing parameter or differing scopes is refused`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.linking CPL2's retardance to CPL1's makes it follow and leaves it out of the unknowns", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a link to itself, a chain, a second link of one follower, a missing parameter or differing scopes is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withLink", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 365, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [364], "how_to": "A study's per-session gain models, fit settings, weights, enablement and notes, as pure updates (the S11.1 brief 'Per session a gain model …', 'Fit settings (joint / staged, S11.3), weights per experiment or per detector, enable / disable per experiment, and notes'; 001 §L 'Weights and ablation'; 001 §E notes). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`: (1) `ExperimentEnablement` = `EnabledInStudy` | `DisabledInStudy`, a two-case union in place of a flag; it is not stored, the study keeps its `disabled` list. (2) On `Study`, each refusal changing nothing: `member this.withSessionGainModel (session : SessionName) (model : SessionGainModel) (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`: `UnknownStudySessionErr` naming the session when `sessionsIn kitExperiments` (step 358) holds none of that name, `GainAnchorOutsideSessionErr` naming the run when an anchor or a repeat is no experiment of that session, and otherwise the setting replaced in place or appended; `member this.withFitMode (mode : FitMode) : Study`; `member this.withExperimentWeight (experiment : ExperimentName) (weight : ResidualWeight) : Result<Study, StudyError>` and `member this.withExperimentEnablement (experiment : ExperimentName) (enablement : ExperimentEnablement) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, each `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` for an experiment the study does not hold; the weight replaced in place or appended; `DisabledInStudy` adding the name to `disabled` once and `EnabledInStudy` removing it; `member this.withDetectorWeight (detector : ItemId) (weight : ResidualWeight) (used : Item list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyItemErr` for an item outside `used`, else replaced or appended; `member this.withNotes (notes : StudyNotes) : Study`. (3) `member this.enabledExperiments : ExperimentName list`, the study's experiments without the disabled ones, in order; and `member this.residualWeightOf (experiment : ExperimentName) (detector : ItemId) : ResidualWeight`, the experiment's weight times the detector's, each `ResidualWeight.unit` when unset, the weight the residual rows of that experiment take (S11.2). `StudyError` gains `UnknownStudySessionErr` (`the study has no such session: <reason>`), `GainAnchorOutsideSessionErr` (`the AIR run is not in that session: <reason>`) and `UnknownStudyItemErr` (`the study uses no such item: <reason>`). No threshold or other setting is added. Tests, in `StudyTests`, over a study of E1, E2, D1 (Diagnostic) and E3 and step 362's items: `a session's gain model is set for a session of the study, anchored within it`: `Session 1`'s model set to `AnchoredSessionGain [ E2 ]`, then to `InterpolatedSessionGain { opening = E1; closing = E2 }`, leaves one setting holding the second, and `gainModelOf` answers it while `Session 2`'s stays `FreeSessionGain`; `fit mode, weights, enablement and notes are set in place, and an unset weight reads one`: `StagedFit`, an experiment weight of 2 on E1 set twice (the second 4), a detector weight of 0.5 on the Phone, E2 disabled twice then enabled, E3 disabled, and notes give one weight entry of 4, `residualWeightOf E1 Phone` 2, `residualWeightOf E3 CPL1` 1, `enabledExperiments` [E1; E2; D1] and the notes; `a setting naming an experiment, item or session the study lacks is refused`: a session `Day 9`, an anchor E3 for `Session 1`, a weight or enablement for E9 and a detector weight for an item outside `used` each answer their error, the study unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases.", "acceptance": "After the settings land, a study MUST set a session's gain model only for a session it has with anchors inside it, set its fit mode, weights, enablement and notes in place, and answer `enabledExperiments` and `residualWeightOf`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a session's gain model is set for a session of the study, anchored within it`, `fit mode, weights, enablement and notes are set in place, and an unset weight reads one` and `a setting naming an experiment, item or session the study lacks is refused`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a session's gain model is set for a session of the study, anchored within it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.fit mode, weights, enablement and notes are set in place, and an unset weight reads one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a setting naming an experiment, item or session the study lacks is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ExperimentEnablement", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withSessionGainModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withFitMode", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withExperimentWeight", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withExperimentEnablement", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withDetectorWeight", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withNotes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.enabledExperiments", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.residualWeightOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number":366,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S111n","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[365],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests"],"how_to":"The five study messages as one semantic union with a pure update over what logic receives, tested over in-memory kits (001 §P 'Every user step is a semantic message: … `CreateStudy`, `AddExperimentsToStudy`, `OpenMaterial`, `SetParameterScope`, `LinkParameters` … The same messages back the buttons, so tests drive by meaning'; 001 §P 'Logic receives a `KitContext`'; the S11.1 brief 'The messages are pure updates, with tests over in-memory kits'; .spec-md §4 'Every user step is a semantic Elmish message. The button and the test send the same message'). The study view that sends them is S11.5's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, last: (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyContext = { studies : Study list; experiments : Experiment list; setups : Setup list; items : Item list; resolveMaterial : MaterialVersionId -> Result<MaterialEntry, StudyError> }`, the kit's studies, experiments, setups and items as the window last read them and the library's resolution of a material version (the `*Context` convention; the composer maps its store's failure to `MaterialUnavailableErr`), with `member this.itemsUsedBy (study : Study) : Item list`, `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` (step 261) of the study's experiments as `experiments` holds them, over `setups` and `items`. (2) `StudyMsg` = `CreateStudy of name : StudyName * experiments : ExperimentName list` | `AddExperimentsToStudy of study : StudyName * experiments : ExperimentName list` | `OpenMaterial of study : StudyName * material : MaterialVersionId` | `SetParameterScope of study : StudyName * scoped : ScopedParameter` | `LinkParameters of study : StudyName * link : ParameterLink`, each case documented. (3) `member this.applyTo (context : StudyContext) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, the study the message creates or changes: `CreateStudy` is `Study.create` over `context.studies` and `context.experiments` (step 358); every other case finds its study in `context.studies` by name, `UnknownStudyErr` naming it when none has it, then answers `withExperiments` (step 360), `openMaterial` of `context.resolveMaterial`'s entry (step 361), `withParameterScope` or `withLink` over `context.itemsUsedBy` of the study (steps 363, 364). A refusal answers its error and changes nothing. The caller records the answered study through `KitLibraryContext.recordStudy` (step 359) and replaces it in its list. `StudyError` gains `UnknownStudyErr` (`the kit has no such study: <reason>`) and `MaterialUnavailableErr` (`the material version could not be read: <reason>`). No other message, field or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs`, `module StudyMessageTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Each fact builds an in-memory kit as `KitLibraryTests` does (step 139): `KitProxy.createInMemory`, `KitContext.openKit` read-write with a stepping clock and a `KitLibraryContext` over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`'s import seam; it records step 362's CPL1, CPL2 and Phone through `recordItem` (step 219), one setup holding them through `recordSetup` (step 260) and E1, E2 and E3 over it through `recordExperiment`, and saves a user absorbing crystal material through the set's `materials.saveMaterial`; the context's lists are what the kit reads back, and `resolveMaterial` reads `materials.resolveVersion`, `Ok None` and `Error _` answering `MaterialUnavailableErr`. Each answered study is recorded through `recordStudy`. `CreateStudy and AddExperimentsToStudy write the study file over the kit's experiments`: `CreateStudy (QZ-LR, [ E1 ])`, then `AddExperimentsToStudy (QZ-LR, [ E2; E1 ])` over the refreshed list, leave `readStudies` answering `QZ-LR` over [E1; E2]. `OpenMaterial snapshots the material version into the kit and stores its working copy in the study file`: `OpenMaterial (QZ-LR, <its version>)` leaves `paths` holding `library/<its GUID>@v1.material-json` and `readStudies`' study holding the working copy with its fifteen known parameters. `SetParameterScope and LinkParameters change the stored study`: `SetParameterScope (QZ-LR, Phone gain → ExperimentScope)` and `LinkParameters (QZ-LR, CPL2 c2.retardance → CPL1 c2.retardance)` leave the read-back study holding that scope entry and that link. `a refused study message records nothing`: `AddExperimentsToStudy (LR, [ E1 ])` with no study `LR` answers `UnknownStudyErr`, `OpenMaterial` of a version the library lacks `MaterialUnavailableErr`, and `paths` and every file's bytes are unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.","acceptance":"After the study messages land, `StudyMsg` MUST hold `CreateStudy`, `AddExperimentsToStudy`, `OpenMaterial`, `SetParameterScope` and `LinkParameters`, and `StudyMsg.applyTo` MUST answer the created or changed study through the pure updates, or a typed refusal that changes nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `CreateStudy and AddExperimentsToStudy write the study file over the kit's experiments`, `OpenMaterial snapshots the material version into the kit and stores its working copy in the study file`, `SetParameterScope and LinkParameters change the stored study` and `a refused study message records nothing`, the count rising by 4, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.CreateStudy and AddExperimentsToStudy write the study file over the kit's experiments","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.OpenMaterial snapshots the material version into the kit and stores its working copy in the study file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.SetParameterScope and LinkParameters change the stored study","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.a refused study message records nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyContext","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyContext.itemsUsedBy","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg.applyTo","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError","op":"change_shape","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","obligations":["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 367, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [366], "how_to": "The forward model of an experiment (001 §N 'The forward model of an experiment = slots + scan point + parameters → predicted reading') evaluates a RECORDED setup in Domain, and three rules it needs live today inside the table's run in the UI, so they MOVE into Domain and the table calls them (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). Nothing the table draws, lays out or runs changes. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs`, after `layout` (`BeamLayout.fs:layout`): `type PlacedElement with member this.incidenceOn (placement : ElementPlacement) : IncidenceAngle`, the body of the private extension `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:incidenceOn` moved verbatim (the angle between the element's drawn face normal, `r1Axis (RayModel.orientedToBeam d placement)`, and its arriving beam `d`, capped at `Propagation.r2SweepMaxDegrees`, and 0° for the root, which has no arriving beam), its doc kept with spec 0046 and spec 0050 S11.2 cited; and `type BeamTree.BeamBranch with member this.propagationBranch : Propagation.Branch`: `TransmittedBeam` is `BranchTransmitted` and `ReflectedBeam` `BranchReflected` (`Propagation.fs:Branch`), the mapping `chartForRun` writes inline today. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`, after `SetupSlot.inLightOrder` (step 257): `type SetupSlot with static member boundSourceIn (slots : SetupSlot list) (library : LibraryProxy) : SourcePreset option`, the body of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:boundSource` moved: in slot order, the first `LightSource` slot whose `placement.valueId` `library.tryGetEntry` answers as a `SourceItem`, that preset; `None` when no slot does. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, after `read`: `type Library.SourcePreset with static member operatingWaveLengthOf (sourceOpt : SourcePreset option) (requested : WaveLength option) : WaveLength`, the body of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:operatingWaveLength` moved: a `TunableBetween` source's `requested` wavelength clamped to its limits, or its own wavelength when nothing is requested; a `FixedLine` source's own wavelength whatever is requested; 600 nm without a source. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the private `incidenceOn` extension is deleted and `chartForRun` calls the Domain member on the same placed element; `chartForRun`'s inline branch match becomes `step.branch.propagationBranch`; `model.boundSource` is `SetupSlot.boundSourceIn model.elements model.library`; and `operatingWaveLength model requested` is `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf model.boundSource requested`. Their docs say in one line that the rule is Domain's. No other UI line changes, so every chart, caption and status is as it was. Tests. In `BeamLayoutTests`, `the drawn incidence is the angle between an element's drawn face normal and its arriving beam`: over elements laid out by `BeamLayout.layout` from the file's own placement helper on the main beam, a sample at R2 30° meets its beam at 30°, an untilted one at 0°, the root answers 0°, and a sample at R2 89.5° is capped at 89°, each within 1e-9; and `TransmittedBeam.propagationBranch` is `BranchTransmitted` and `ReflectedBeam.propagationBranch` `BranchReflected`. In `SetupTests` (step 256), `the bound source is the first light-source slot bound to a source preset`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()` and the file's slot fixtures, the slots [an unbound source; a source bound to the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` preset; a source bound to `PresetIds.heNe633`] answer the HeNe preset, and slots with no bound source answer `None`. In `ExperimentRunTests`, `the run's wavelength is a tunable source's clamped request, a fixed line's own, or 600 nm without a source`: the HeNe preset with its tuning set to `TunableBetween` limits of 400 nm and 700 nm (a record copy) answers 500 nm for a request of 500 nm, 700 nm for 900 nm, 400 nm for 300 nm and its own wavelength for `None`; the HeNe preset as it is answers 632.8 nm whatever is requested; `None` answers 600 nm.", "acceptance": "After the move, `PlacedElement.incidenceOn`, `BeamBranch.propagationBranch`, `SetupSlot.boundSourceIn` and `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf` MUST be declared in Domain, and `chartForRun`, `boundSource` and `operatingWaveLength` MUST call them with no copy left in the UI; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the drawn incidence is the angle between an element's drawn face normal and its arriving beam`, `the bound source is the first light-source slot bound to a source preset` and `the run's wavelength is a tunable source's clamped request, a fixed line's own, or 600 nm without a source`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, every chart unchanged and the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests.the drawn incidence is the angle between an element's drawn face normal and its arriving beam", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.the bound source is the first light-source slot bound to a source preset", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.the run's wavelength is a tunable source's clamped request, a fixed line's own, or 600 nm without a source", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.BeamLayout.PlacedElement.incidenceOn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.BeamLayout.BeamBranch.propagationBranch", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.boundSourceIn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.incidenceOn", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.boundSource", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.operatingWaveLength", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number":368,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S112b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[367],"how_to":"The second half of the run rules the forward model needs: how a slot binds for a run and what the source emits, written today inside `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun` (steps 252 and 265) and `model.runEmission` (step 266), MOVE into Domain and the table calls them (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move'; step 251: `boundWith` is 'the door S8.2's slots and S11.2's forward model call'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs`, which opens `Setups`, after `ItemModelChoice.boundWith` (step 251): (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] SlotRunParam = { library : LibraryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; items : Item list; choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option; valuesOf : Item -> ParameterValues }`: the library a bare slot is bound in, the material store a stack sample resolves through (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialProxy`), the kit's items, an item's model as the window's stores resolve it (`model.tryItemModelChoice`, step 263) and the numbers an item is evaluated with. (2) `SlotRunError`, an `*Error` union: `SlotItemErr of error : SetupError` | `SlotEvaluationErr of error : ItemEvaluationError`, with `member this.describe : string` answering the inner error's `describe` unchanged. (3) `type SetupSlot with member this.runElementWith (param : SlotRunParam) : Result<BoundOpticalElement option, SlotRunError>`, the binding `chartForRun` does once per path step today, by the slot's `placement.catalogueKind`: a `LightSource`, `Detector`, `Lens`, `FlatMirror` or `CurvedMirror` slot answers `Ok None` (a source emits, a detector reads, and a mirror or a lens only steers the ray, as the run law has always treated them); a `LinearPolarizer`, `CircularPolarizer` or `Sample` slot holding `ItemInSlot (id, _)` takes the item of that id in `param.items`, else `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the id, then its `param.choiceOf`, else `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and that its model is not in the library, then `choice.boundWith param.materials (param.valuesOf item)` (step 251), its error as `SlotEvaluationErr`; such a slot of `EmptySlotContent` is its library binding: a polarizer slot bound to a `PolarizerItem p` is `BoundPolarizerPreset p.behavior`, a sample slot bound to a `SampleItem s` is `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample param.materials (ParameterValues.defaultsOf s.parameterAxes) s` (step 252), and an unbound slot, any other entry or a binding `library.tryGetEntry` does not answer (`Ok None` or `Error`) is `Ok None`, as today. The reasons are the ones `chartForRun` gives today (steps 263, 265). `member this.runStepOf (mueller : MuellerMatrix) : ExperimentRun.RunStep`: an `ObjectStep` for a `Sample` slot and an `ElementStep` for any other (step 265). `static member runEmissionOf (slots : SetupSlot list) (param : SlotRunParam) : Result<SourceEmission, SlotRunError>`, `model.runEmission`'s rule (step 266): the first `LightSource` slot holding an item emits `choice.emissionWith (param.valuesOf item)` (step 246), the item and its model found as above and an evaluation error answered as `SlotEvaluationErr`; without such a slot, `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)` (step 252's default). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `chartForRun` binds each path step's slot through `slot.runElementWith` over `{ library = model.library; materials = model.materials; items = model.kitItems; choiceOf = model.tryItemModelChoice; valuesOf = fun item -> ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters }` and makes each evaluated matrix its step through `slot.runStepOf`; `model.runEmission` is `SetupSlot.runEmissionOf model.elements` over the same param, its error's `describe` as its `ControlCaption`. The failure charts keep their texts: `SlotEvaluationErr (SampleMaterialErr e)` shows `Sample materials failed to resolve` with `e.runFailureCaption`, every other error `The run cannot be evaluated` with its `describe`. The inline bindings are deleted, so one rule binds a slot, and every chart's numbers and texts are unchanged. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests` (step 245), with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])` and `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, over slots built as `SetupTests`' fixtures build them (step 256) and items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216): `a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element`: a linear-polarizer slot bound to `PresetIds.polarizerLp` with no item binds its `BoundPolarizerPreset`; the same slot holding a real-LP item (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`) whose `valuesOf` answers an `extinctionRatio` of 0.01 evaluates at 0° and 600 nm to `BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm` of those values, within 1e-12; a sample slot bound to `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` evaluates as `ofStackSample` at its defaults; a source, a detector and a flat-mirror slot answer `Ok None`; and `runStepOf` makes an `ObjectStep` of the sample slot and an `ElementStep` of the polarizer. `a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr`: a polarizer slot holding an item id outside `items`, and one holding an item whose `choiceOf` answers `None`, each answer `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr`. `the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item`: a source slot holding a HeNe item (`BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`) whose `valuesOf` answers a degree of polarization 1 at azimuth 30° emits that `SourceEmission`; slots with no source item emit the default emission; and a `degreeOfPolarization` of 1.5 answers `SlotEvaluationErr` of `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the move, `SetupSlot.runElementWith`, `runStepOf` and `runEmissionOf` MUST bind a slot and emit the source in Domain, and `chartForRun` and `model.runEmission` MUST call them with no inline binding left; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element`, `a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr` and `the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, every chart unchanged and the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SlotRunParam","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SlotRunError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SetupSlot.runElementWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SetupSlot.runStepOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SetupSlot.runEmissionOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.runEmission","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 369, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [368], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests"], "how_to": "The study's pre-fit checks are `SolverHandoffView`'s three checks, moved into Domain (001 §R '`SolverHandoffView`'s stub screen, replaced by the study view. Its three validation checks are reused as the study's pre-fit checks'; .spec-md §6 row 'Pre-fit checks'; the S11.2 brief 'SolverHandoffView calls the moved checks until S11.5 deletes it'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs`, `module PrefitChecks` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ExperimentMatrices.fs` (step 322), the last Domain file, because the checks read setups, experiments and the data seam: one `<Compile Include=\"PrefitChecks.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: an experiment's checks before a fit (spec 0050 S11.2; spec 0038 Part L). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In order: (a) `SlotSpecification` = `SpecifiedSlot` | `UnspecifiedSlot`, and `type SetupSlot with member this.specification : SlotSpecification`: specified when it holds an item or its placement is bound (`valueId`), the rule `SolverHandoffView.fs:unspecifiedElements` reads (step 261). (b) `PrefitError`, an `*Error` union: `UnspecifiedSlotsErr of reason : string` (a slot other than a sample's is unspecified, or the experiment's setup does not resolve), `MissingDataErr of reason : string` (no data is attached), `UnreadableDataErr of error : ExperimentDataError` (the attached file does not read through its profile: a `MalformedDataFileErr` or an `EmptyDataFileErr`, `MeasuredData.fs:ExperimentDataError`) and `InconsistentDataErr of error : ExperimentDataError` (its points do not fit the scan: a `DataRangeMismatchErr` or a `DataUnitsMismatchErr`), with `member this.describe : string`: `a slot is not specified: <reason>`, `no data is attached: <reason>`, `the data file does not read: <the error's reason>` and `the data does not fit the scan: <the error's reason>`. (c) `type Experiment with member this.prefitCheckWith (library : LibraryProxy) (dataProxy : ExperimentDataProxy) (setups : Setup list) : Result<MappedPoints, PrefitError>`, the three checks of `SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment` in order, each with the reason text the view gives today (steps 261, 291, 304): (1) `this.slotsIn setups` (step 261), a `SetupError` answering `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` of its `describe`, then the slots of `SetupSlot.inLightOrder` (step 257) that are not `Sample` slots and are `UnspecifiedSlot`, answering `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` naming their roles' `text`; (2) `this.dataOpt` of `None` answers `MissingDataErr`; (3) `ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate library dataProxy slots this data` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`: read through the profile, the exclusions removed by `keptBy`, then `validatedFor`, steps 304 and 314), whose `Ok points` is answered as it is, the kept and validated points a fit reads, a `MalformedDataFileErr` or `EmptyDataFileErr` as `UnreadableDataErr` and a `DataRangeMismatchErr` or `DataUnitsMismatchErr` as `InconsistentDataErr`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`: `validateExperiment` answers `experiment.prefitCheckWith library dataProxy setups` mapped onto the screen's `ExperimentHandoffStatus` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:ExperimentHandoffStatus`): `Ok points` is `HandoffReady points.pointCount`, `UnspecifiedSlotsErr r` `UnspecifiedElements` and `MissingDataErr r` `MissingDataFile`, each of its reason as a `ControlCaption`, `UnreadableDataErr e` `DataFileParseError e.caption` and `InconsistentDataErr e` `DataFileValidationError e.caption`; the private `unspecifiedElements` member is deleted and `handoffSetupCaption` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:handoffSetupCaption`) tags a slot through its `specification`. The status union stays the screen's display until S11.5 deletes the view. Every caption the screen shows is unchanged, so `SolverHandoffWindowTests` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`), which calls `validateExperiment`, runs with every fact and fixture as it is. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs`, `module PrefitCheckTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, setups made by `Setup.create` (step 256) of slots built as `SetupTests` builds them (a source bound to `PresetIds.heNe633`, a linear polarizer, a sample and a detector holding an intensity-detector item, `ItemModelIds.intensityDetectorModelId`), test-local experiments built as `StudySessionTests` builds them (step 357) with a `oneAxis` `VaryR1` scan of the polarizer over 0…90° in 4 points, and a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy` record whose `readMapped` answers by attachment path and whose other fields answer errors: `a slot other than a sample's must hold an item or a binding, and a setup the kit lacks is named`: with the polarizer slot empty, `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` whose reason names `Prep 1` and not `Obj 1`; with it holding a linear-polarizer item, the slot check passes although the sample is empty; an experiment whose setup is `'Missing' revision 1` answers `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` naming it. `an experiment without data fails the data check`: `dataOpt = None` answers `MissingDataErr`. `a data file that does not read is unreadable, and points outside the scan are inconsistent`: `readMapped` answering a `MalformedDataFileErr` or an `EmptyDataFileErr` answers `UnreadableDataErr` carrying it, and an intensity series holding x = 120 answers `InconsistentDataErr` of a `DataRangeMismatchErr`. `a ready experiment answers its kept, validated points`: a series at 0, 30, 60 and 90 with point 2 excluded (`PointExclusion`, step 313) answers `Ok` of the three points 0, 60 and 90. `every pre-fit error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct payload renders its text with it.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Experiment.prefitCheckWith` MUST run the three checks in Domain and answer the kept, validated points or a typed `PrefitError`, and `SolverHandoffView.validateExperiment` MUST call it with every caption unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot other than a sample's must hold an item or a binding, and a setup the kit lacks is named`, `an experiment without data fails the data check`, `a data file that does not read is unreadable, and points outside the scan are inconsistent`, `a ready experiment answers its kept, validated points` and `every pre-fit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a slot other than a sample's must hold an item or a binding, and a setup the kit lacks is named", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.an experiment without data fails the data check", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a data file that does not read is unreadable, and points outside the scan are inconsistent", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a ready experiment answers its kept, validated points", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.every pre-fit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.SlotSpecification", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.SetupSlot.specification", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.PrefitError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.Experiment.prefitCheckWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SolverHandoffView.validateExperiment", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SolverHandoffView.unspecifiedElements", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 370, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [369], "how_to": "Before a fit, an experiment's data is flagged when it changed since it was attached or since the last fit run read it (001 §E 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open and before each fit (\"data changed since attach / since the last fit run\")'; the S11.2 brief 'Add S4.2's \"data changed since attach / since the last fit run\" flag'). The since-attach half is S4.2's check (`DataAttachment.statusAgainst`, step 132; `KitProxy.attachmentStatus`, step 134); the since-fit half compares the attachment with the attachments a fit run read, which S11.3's fit runs record. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `PrefitChecks.fs`, after `prefitCheckWith` (step 369): (1) `DataChangeFlag` = `DataUnchangedFlag` | `ChangedSinceAttachFlag of current : ContentHash` | `ChangedSinceFitFlag of current : ContentHash` | `MissingDataFileFlag`, with `member this.text : string`: `data unchanged`, `data changed since attach`, `data changed since the last fit run` and `data file missing`. It is derived, never stored, so it carries no tag. (2) `type MappedAttachment with member this.changeWith (status : DataAttachmentStatus) (fitted : DataAttachment list) : DataChangeFlag`, over the status S4.2's check answers for this attachment: `AttachedDataMissing` is `MissingDataFileFlag`; `AttachedDataChanged current` is `ChangedSinceAttachFlag current`; `AttachedDataUnchanged` is `ChangedSinceFitFlag` of `this.attachment.contentHash` when `fitted` holds an attachment of the same `path` whose `contentHash` differs, and `DataUnchangedFlag` otherwise. `fitted` is the attachments the study's last fit run read, empty before its first. No other member or option is added. Tests, in `PrefitCheckTests` (step 369), over test-local attachments and hashes: `a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it`: `AttachedDataMissing` answers `MissingDataFileFlag`; `AttachedDataChanged h2` answers `ChangedSinceAttachFlag h2`, also when `fitted` holds the path at another hash; `AttachedDataUnchanged` with `fitted` empty, holding the path at the same hash or holding only other paths answers `DataUnchangedFlag`, and with `fitted` holding the path at another hash `ChangedSinceFitFlag` of the attachment's hash; and the four `text`s are as above.", "acceptance": "After the flag lands, `MappedAttachment.changeWith` MUST flag a missing file, a change since attach and a change since the last fit run, in that precedence; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-DATA-CHANGE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.DataChangeFlag", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-DATA-CHANGE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.MappedAttachment.changeWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-DATA-CHANGE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 371, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [370], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests"], "how_to": "What a detector records, and each measured point paired with what fixes its prediction (001 §K 'Observables: intensity, Ψ / Δ, full Mueller matrices (the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, normalized + absolute throughput). A study mixes them'; step 304: '`ObservationPoints` pass as read, each observation carrying its own configuration, which the study pairs with the experiment (S11.2)'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs`, `module StudyForward` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `PrefitChecks.fs` (step 369), the last Domain file, because the forward model reads studies, setups, items, the evaluator and the data seam: one `<Compile Include=\"StudyForward.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the forward model of an experiment and the study residual (spec 0050 S11.2). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In order: (a) `StudyForwardError`, an `*Error` union, its first case `UnpairedPointsErr of reason : string` (a mapped point the experiment's scan cannot place), with `member this.describe : string`: `the data cannot be placed on the scan: <reason>`. Later steps add their cases, each with its line. (b) `RecordedReading` = `RecordedSignal of MeasuredIntensity` (an intensity detector's signal) | `RecordedPsiDelta of PsiDelta` (an ellipsometer's Ψ and Δ, `AnalysisFunctions.fs:PsiDelta`) | `RecordedMueller of MuellerMatrix` (a polarimeter's ABSOLUTE Mueller matrix, its m₀₀ the throughput, as S9.2's Mueller readings hold it, steps 301-302): what a detector records, predicted or measured. (c) `MeasuredRow` = `SettingsRow of settings : ScanSetting list * waveLengthOpt : WaveLength option * measured : RecordedReading` (a point taken at those scan settings, step 287, at its own wavelength when it carries one) | `ObservationRow of observation : MuellerObservation` (a point carrying its own configuration, `MuellerInverse.fs:MuellerObservation`). (d) `type MappedPoints with member this.measuredRowsFor (scan : ExperimentScan) : Result<MeasuredRow list, StudyForwardError>`: the points in their order, each placed by the rules `validatedFor` checks (step 304) over `scan.quantities` (step 304), a quantity set as `{ elementId; variable; value }` with the value `validatedFor` admits for the point, through the same conversion: a `SeriesPoints (IntensityData s)` point is `SettingsRow` of the one quantity at its x, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of its intensity; a `SeriesPoints (EllipsometricData s)` point is `SettingsRow` of the scan's `VaryR2` quantity at its angle of incidence when it carries one and the scan has that quantity (else no setting), `Some` of its wavelength, and `RecordedPsiDelta` of its Ψ and Δ; a `CapturePoints` row is `SettingsRow` of the one quantity at its `description` in degrees, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of its `avgTotal`; a `ColumnPoints` row is `SettingsRow` of the quantities, cell i the i-th quantity at the cell's `displayValue`, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of a `SignalReading`'s signal (its σ is not read: a study weighs runs and detectors, 001 §L) or `RecordedMueller` of a `MuellerReading`; an `ObservationPoints` observation is `ObservationRow` of it. Under a scan of no quantity (a dark line, step 287) a series point, capture row or column row has no setting. A series point or capture row under more than one quantity, and a column row whose cells do not number the quantities, answer `UnpairedPointsErr` naming the point's number and the counts. No cache or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs`, `module StudyForwardTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local scans of `ScanAxis` records on test-local element ids: `each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over`: under a one-axis `VaryR1` scan of a polarizer, an intensity series at x 0 and 30 gives two `SettingsRow`s setting the polarizer's `VaryR1` to 0 and 30, no wavelength, their intensities; under a one-axis `VaryDialReading` scan, a capture row of description 20° sets the dial reading to 20 with its `avgTotal`; under a two-axis scan (the polarizer's `VaryR1` outer, a sample's `VaryR2` inner), a column row of cells 10 and 45 sets both in that order, and its `MuellerReading` is `RecordedMueller`; an ellipsometric point at 500 nm with an angle of incidence of 60° under that scan sets the sample's `VaryR2` to 60 with `Some` 500 nm and its Ψ and Δ; observations give one `ObservationRow` each, in order; under a dark-line scan a series point has no setting. `a point the scan cannot place is refused`: under the two-axis scan an intensity series point, a capture row and a column row of one cell each answer `UnpairedPointsErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct payload renders its text with it.", "acceptance": "After the readings land, `MappedPoints.measuredRowsFor` MUST place every kind of mapped point on its experiment's scan or refuse it with `UnpairedPointsErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over`, `a point the scan cannot place is refused` and `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a point the scan cannot place is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.RecordedReading", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.MeasuredRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.MappedPoints.measuredRowsFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number":372,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S112f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[371],"how_to":"The parameter vector a fit searches, laid out by the generated axes: one value per owner of each unknown (step 362: 'The fitter's vector holds one value per owner of each unknown (S11.2-S11.3)'; 001 §N 'Parameter-axis generation'; 001 §L scopes; the S11.2 brief 'a parameter vector laid out by the generated axes'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `measuredRowsFor` (step 371): (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyForwardContext = { kit : StudyContext; library : LibraryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; experimentData : ExperimentDataProxy; choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option; solverParameters : SolverParameters }`: what a study's forward model reads, the kit as the study messages see it (step 366), the library and material stores, the data seam (step 305), an item's model as the window's stores resolve it (step 263) and the solver parameters a cut plate is solved with, passed rather than defaulted as `MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward` asks. (2) `StudyRunUse` = `ResidualRunUse` | `DarkLevelRunUse` | `UnreadRunUse`, and `type ExperimentRole with member this.studyUse : StudyRunUse` (step 285's roles, no wildcard arm): `ScienceRun`, `CalibrationRun` and `DriftCheckRun` give residual rows, `DarkRun` gives its session's dark level (001 §L 'dark from the Dark runs'), and `DiagnosticRun`, `IgnoredRun` and `PlannedRun` are not read. It is derived, never stored, so it carries no tag. (3) `type Study with member this.fittedRunsIn (experiments : Experiment list) : Experiment list`: the study's `enabledExperiments` (step 365) whose role's use is `ResidualRunUse`, as `experiments` holds them, in study order. (4) `StudyVectorEntry = { unknown : StudyUnknown; owner : UnknownOwner }` (step 362), one value of the vector. (5) `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"the study's parameter vector: built whole for every residual evaluation and handed whole to the fit\")>] StudyParameterVector = StudyParameterVector of float[]` with `.value`, `static member ofParameterValues (values : ParameterValue list) : StudyParameterVector` and `member this.valueAt (index : int) : ParameterValue`. (6) `StudyParameterLayout = { entries : StudyVectorEntry list; sessions : StudySession list }` with `member this.startVector : StudyParameterVector`, each entry's `unknown.unknown.start` (step 214) in order. (7) `type Study with member this.parameterLayoutWith (context : StudyForwardContext) : StudyParameterLayout`: `sessions` is `this.sessionsIn context.kit.experiments` (step 358); for each of `this.unknownsWith (context.kit.itemsUsedBy this)` (steps 362, 366) in order, one entry per owner of `unknown.owners sessions users` (step 362), in its order, `users` being the names of `this.fittedRunsIn context.kit.experiments` whose slots (`slotsIn context.kit.setups`, step 261; a run whose setup does not resolve uses nothing) hold the unknown's item for an `ItemParameterRef`, or, for a `MaterialParameterRef`, an item whose `context.choiceOf` is `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, _, sample)` with `sample.openedMaterialsIn this` (step 361) holding a copy of that version. No bound, scaling or option is added: the fit's are S11.3's. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216): CPL1 (`ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId`, `c2.retardance` unknown from π / 2 within [1, 2]), a Phone (`ItemModelIds.intensityDetectorModelId`, `gain` unknown from 1 within [0.1, 10]) and QZ (a `StackSampleChoice` of a test-local plate sample whose substrate is a test-local uniaxial crystal version), a study opening that version with `n_o` unknown from 1.54 within [1.5, 1.6] (step 361), setups made by `Setup.create` of slots built as `SetupTests` builds them holding CPL1, QZ and the Phone, test-local experiments E1 and E2 (Science, `Session 1`), D1 (Diagnostic) and E3 (Science), a `StudyContext` record of them and a `choiceOf` answering each item's choice: `the vector holds one value per owner of each unknown, in the unknowns' order, and starts at each unknown's start`: the layout's entries are CPL1 `c2.retardance` with its `ItemOwner`, the Phone `gain` with `SessionOwner` `Session 1` then `Session 2`, and `n_o` with its `MaterialOwner`, in that order, and `startVector` is [π / 2; 1; 1; 1.54]; with a scope making CPL1's retardance `ExperimentScope` its owners are E1, E2 and E3 in that order. `a disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a run whose setup does not use an unknown own none of its values`: with E2 disabled (`withExperimentEnablement`, step 365) the experiment-scoped retardance has the owners E1 and E3; E1 made a Dark run owns none of them; and a run over a setup holding no QZ is no user of `n_o`, which keeps its one `MaterialOwner` through the others. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the layout lands, `Study.parameterLayoutWith` MUST hold one entry per owner of each of the study's unknowns, in the unknowns' order, owned only through enabled fitted runs that use them, and `startVector` MUST be their starts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the vector holds one value per owner of each unknown, in the unknowns' order, and starts at each unknown's start` and `a disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a run whose setup does not use an unknown own none of its values`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.the vector holds one value per owner of each unknown, in the unknowns' order, and starts at each unknown's start","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a run whose setup does not use an unknown own none of its values","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardContext","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyRunUse","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ExperimentRole.studyUse","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.fittedRunsIn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyVectorEntry","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyParameterVector","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyParameterLayout","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.parameterLayoutWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 373, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [372], "how_to": "The numbers one experiment is evaluated with at one parameter vector: each item's values and each opened material's crystal (001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'; 001 §I 'every sample made of it shares them (`MaterialScope`)'; step 361: `Sample.openedMaterialsIn` — 'the forward model reads it (S11.2)'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `parameterLayoutWith` (step 372): (1) `ExperimentAssignment = { itemValues : Map<ItemId, ParameterValues>; crystals : Map<MaterialVersionId, CrystalParameters> }`, with `member this.valuesOf (item : Item) : ParameterValues`, its entry or `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` (step 245) for an item the map lacks; `member this.crystalOf (material : OpenedMaterial) : CrystalParameters`, its entry or the copy's `currentCrystal` (step 361); and `member this.materialProxyOver (materials : MaterialProxy) : MaterialProxy`, `materials` with `resolveVersion` answering, for a version `crystals` holds, the entry the store answers with its `physics` replaced by `CrystalParameterPhysics` of the assignment's crystal (step 355), every other version and field passing through, so a stack sample made of an opened material is solved with the study's working copy. (2) `type StudyParameterLayout with member this.assignmentFor (study : Study) (items : Item list) (experiment : ExperimentName) (vector : StudyParameterVector) : Result<ExperimentAssignment, StudyForwardError>`: `VectorLengthErr` naming both lengths when the vector does not hold one value per entry; otherwise an entry's owner holds the experiment when it is an `ItemOwner` or a `MaterialOwner`, a `SessionOwner s` whose session of `this.sessions` lists it, or the `ExperimentOwner` of it, and (a) each of `items` takes `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` with each entry k on one of its parameters whose owner holds the experiment set by `withValue name (vector.valueAt k)` (step 245); (b) each of `study.materials` takes its `currentCrystal` with each such entry on one of its components written through the generated axis of that name (`crystal.parameterAxes`, `writeValue`, step 361); (c) then each of `study.links` (step 364) sets its follower to its leader's value in this assignment: an item parameter's `valueOf`, or a component read through its generated axis's `parameterValueOf`, written as in (a) or (b). `StudyForwardError` gains `VectorLengthErr of reason : string`, rendered `the parameter vector does not fit the study: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 372's fixture and its layout: `an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own`: at [0.7; 2; 3; 1.6], E1's assignment gives CPL1 `c2.retardance` 0.7 and the Phone `gain` 2 and `darkOffset` its own 0, E3's gives `gain` 3, and every other parameter of each item is its own value. `an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value`: E1's crystal of the opened version is the uniaxial copy with `n_o` 1.6 and its other three components the copy's; with CPL2 added (`c2.retardance` known at 1.2) and linked to follow CPL1's (step 364), CPL2's value is 0.7 at E1 and its known 1.2 in an assignment taken before the link. `a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy`: `materialProxyOver`'s `resolveVersion` of the opened version answers the entry whose physics is `CrystalParameterPhysics` of E1's crystal, and of another version the store's entry unchanged. `a vector of another length is refused`: a vector of three values answers `VectorLengthErr` naming 3 and 4. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers `VectorLengthErr`.", "acceptance": "After the assignment lands, `StudyParameterLayout.assignmentFor` MUST give each item the vector's value for the owner holding the experiment and its own value otherwise, each opened material its crystal from the vector, each link's follower its leader's value, and `materialProxyOver` MUST resolve an opened version to the working copy; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own`, `an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value`, `a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy` and `a vector of another length is refused`, the count rising by 4, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a vector of another length is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ExperimentAssignment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyParameterLayout.assignmentFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number":374,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S112h","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[373],"how_to":"The forward model of an experiment at a scan point: its setup's slots, the point's settings and the study's numbers give the predicted reading, through S8.1's evaluator (001 §N 'The forward model of an experiment = slots + scan point + parameters → predicted reading: intensity → S₀ · gain + dark; polarimeter → Mueller elements + throughput; ellipsometer → Ψ / Δ'; step 251: a detector's 'gain, dark offset and noise belong to S11.2's forward model'). The noise budget a detector publishes is not read: nothing is simulated here. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, after `read`: `type RunStep with static member productOf (steps : RunStep list) : MuellerMatrix`, the steps' matrices multiplied in light order from `Propagation.identityMueller` (each `step.mueller * product`). (2) In `StudyForward.fs`, after `assignmentFor` (step 373): (a) `type ParameterValue with member this.darkMean : DarkMean`, the number as a dark level in the detector's own units (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:DarkMean`; a `ReadingParameter`, step 207). (b) `DetectorReadout` = `IntensityDetectorReadout of gain : ParameterValue * dark : DarkMean` | `PolarimeterDetectorReadout` | `EllipsometerDetectorReadout`. (c) `BoundPathStep = { slot : SetupSlot; element : BoundOpticalElement; branch : Propagation.Branch; drawnIncidence : IncidenceAngle; dial : ItemDial; dialZero : Angle }`. (d) `BoundExperiment = { experiment : Experiment; emission : SourceEmission; operatingWaveLength : WaveLength; path : BoundPathStep list; detectorItem : ItemId; readout : DetectorReadout }`. (e) `type Experiment with member this.boundWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (assignment : ExperimentAssignment) (darkOpt : DarkMean option) : Result<BoundExperiment, StudyForwardError>`: the slots are `this.slotsIn context.kit.setups` (step 261; a `SetupError` answers `ForwardSetupErr`), each `drawnWith context.kit.items` (step 258), laid out by `BeamLayout.layout` of their `layoutElement`s; `param` is `{ library = context.library; materials = assignment.materialProxyOver context.materials; items = context.kit.items; choiceOf = context.choiceOf; valuesOf = assignment.valuesOf }` (steps 368, 373); the emission is `SetupSlot.runEmissionOf slots param`; the operating wavelength `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf (SetupSlot.boundSourceIn slots context.library) this.scan.sourceWaveLengthOpt` (step 367); the detector is the first `DetectorSlotRole` slot of `SetupSlot.inLightOrder slots` (step 257) holding an item whose `context.choiceOf` is a `LibraryModelChoice` of a detector form (step 208), else `StudyDetectorErr` naming the setup reference, and its readout is, for `IntensityDetectorModel`, `IntensityDetectorReadout` of the item's `ParameterName.gain` value and `darkOpt`, or else the item's `ParameterName.darkOffset` value's `darkMean`; for `MuellerPolarimeterModel`, `PolarimeterDetectorReadout`; for `EllipsometerModel`, `EllipsometerDetectorReadout`; the path is the detector's placed `path` (`BeamLayout.fs:PathStep`), each step's slot bound by `runElementWith param` (step 368) and kept when it answers `Some element`, with `step.branch.propagationBranch`, its placed element's `incidenceOn slot.placement` (step 367), and its item's `dial` and `dialZero` value's `angle` (`FixedMounting` and `Angle.zero` for a slot without an item). Every `SlotRunError` answers `ForwardSlotErr`. (f) `type BoundExperiment with member this.readingAt (settings : ScanSetting list) (waveLengthOpt : WaveLength option) : Result<RecordedReading, StudyForwardError>`: the wavelength is `waveLengthOpt`, else a `VaryWaveLength` setting's value in nanometres, else `operatingWaveLength`; each path step is evaluated by `element.muellerAt` (step 247) at `{ rotation; incidence; branch }` and made its run step by `slot.runStepOf` (step 368), its rotation a `VaryR1` setting on its slot in degrees, else a `VaryDialReading` setting's reading in degrees through its dial, else its slot's `DialTurn reading` through its dial, else `slot.placement.r1` (a reading through a `DialMounted sign` dial being `sign.physicalAngleOf dialZero reading`, step 255, and through `FixedMounting` the reading itself), and its incidence a `VaryR2` setting on its slot in degrees, else `drawnIncidence`; then `IntensityDetectorReadout (gain, dark)` reads `RecordedSignal` of S₀ · gain + dark, S₀ being the intensity `ExperimentRun.read Intensity this.emission steps` gives (step 252); `EllipsometerDetectorReadout` reads `RecordedPsiDelta` of the Ψ and Δ `ExperimentRun.read Ellipsometer` gives; `PolarimeterDetectorReadout` reads `RecordedMueller (RunStep.productOf steps)`. An `ItemEvaluationError` answers `ForwardSlotErr (SlotEvaluationErr e)`. `StudyForwardError` gains `ForwardSetupErr of error : SetupError`, `ForwardSlotErr of error : SlotRunError` and `StudyDetectorErr of reason : string`, rendered `the experiment's setup does not resolve: <describe>`, `a slot cannot be evaluated: <describe>` and `the setup has no detector item: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests. In `ExperimentRunTests`, `a path's Mueller matrix is the product of its steps in light order`: [`ElementStep A`; `ObjectStep B`; `ElementStep C`] of three distinct test-local matrices is C · B · A, and [] is the identity. In `StudyForwardTests`, with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])` and `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, over setups of slots built as `SetupTests` builds them: a HeNe source item, a linear-polarizer item at R1 0° (prep), a real-LP item (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`, analyzer) and a detector item, each assignment from `assignmentFor` or a test-local `ExperimentAssignment`: `an intensity detector reads S0 times its gain plus its dark level along the setup's path`: with an intensity detector item at `gain` 2 and `darkOffset` 0.1, a `VaryR1` setting of the analyzer at 60° reads S₀ · 2 + 0.1 within 1e-12, S₀ being `ExperimentRun.read Intensity` over the default emission and the two polarizers' matrices from `runElementWith` and `muellerAt` at 0° and 60°; with `darkOpt = Some (DarkMean 0.3)` the dark is 0.3. `a scan setting turns, tilts or retunes the path, and a dial reading turns its slot through the vector's zero`: the analyzer as a `DialMounted DialNegative` item whose `dialZero` is 10° in the assignment reads a `VaryDialReading` setting of −20° as the analyzer at 30°, and its recorded `DialTurn` of −20° without a setting likewise; a sample slot holding a glass-plate item (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1) between the polarizers, under a `VaryR2` setting of 40°, is evaluated at incidence 40°; a `VaryWaveLength` setting of 500 reads as evaluated at 500 nm, and `waveLengthOpt` of 450 nm wins over it. `a polarimeter reads its path's Mueller matrix, and an ellipsometer Psi and Delta of the arriving state`: a polarimeter detector item (`ItemModelIds.muellerPolarimeterModelId`) reads `RecordedMueller` of the analyzer's matrix times the prep's within 1e-12, and an ellipsometer item (`ItemModelIds.ellipsometerModelId`) the Ψ and Δ of `ExperimentRun.read Ellipsometer` over the same steps. `a setup without a detector item, or whose setup or slot item does not resolve, is refused`: a detector slot holding no item answers `StudyDetectorErr`; an experiment over `'Missing' revision 1` answers `ForwardSetupErr`; an analyzer slot holding an item the kit lacks answers `ForwardSlotErr` of `SlotItemErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases. Verification (claim-check repair, .spec-md §9): ui-tests MUST select OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests (Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:FsxAcceptanceTests) to preserve the constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples. The constructor-unit-tests behavior checks above remain required; this selection neither edits that class nor substitutes for the future kit-acceptance tests.","acceptance":"After the forward model lands, `Experiment.boundWith` and `BoundExperiment.readingAt` MUST predict an intensity detector's S₀ · gain + dark, a polarimeter's path Mueller matrix and an ellipsometer's Ψ and Δ at each scan setting through S8.1's evaluator, and refuse a setup without a detector item or with an unresolved setup or slot item; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a path's Mueller matrix is the product of its steps in light order`, `an intensity detector reads S0 times its gain plus its dark level along the setup's path`, `a scan setting turns, tilts or retunes the path, and a dial reading turns its slot through the vector's zero`, `a polarimeter reads its path's Mueller matrix, and an ellipsometer Psi and Delta of the arriving state` and `a setup without a detector item, or whose setup or slot item does not resolve, is refused`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass. ui-tests MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests, preserving its constructor/export numerical parity with the Analytics examples and its test count.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-tests":{"suite":"ui-tests","mode":"selected","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.a path's Mueller matrix is the product of its steps in light order","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an intensity detector reads S0 times its gain plus its dark level along the setup's path","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a scan setting turns, tilts or retunes the path, and a dial reading turns its slot through the vector's zero","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a polarimeter reads its path's Mueller matrix, and an ellipsometer Psi and Delta of the arriving state","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a setup without a detector item, or whose setup or slot item does not resolve, is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.RunStep.productOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ParameterValue.darkMean","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.DetectorReadout","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundPathStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Experiment.boundWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment.readingAt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number":375,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S112i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[374],"how_to":"A Mueller observation carries its own configuration, and the study pairs it with the experiment (step 304): its object is a plate of an opened crystal, solved through the spec 0044 Berreman forward at that configuration (001 §K 'the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape'; 001 §N '`MuellerInverse.orientForCut` + `createBerremanForward` for cut plates — REUSED'; .spec-md §3.16: the study engine evaluates the crystal-parameter records). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`: (1) After `readingAt` (step 374), `type MeasurementConfiguration with member this.elementOrientation : ElementOrientation`: `{ rotation = this.azimuth.angle; incidence = this.incidenceAngle; branch }`, `BranchTransmitted` for `TransmittedMueller` and `BranchReflected` for `ReflectedMueller` (`MuellerInverse.fs:MeasurementConfiguration`), so that `ElementOrientation.sampleAzimuth` and `observable` (step 250) give the configuration's back. (2) `BoundExperiment` (step 374) gains `observedCrystalOpt : CrystalParameters option` and `solverParameters : SolverParameters`, and `Experiment.boundWith` takes the study as its second parameter, `(context : StudyForwardContext) (study : Study) (assignment : ExperimentAssignment) (darkOpt : DarkMean option)`, to fill them: `solverParameters` is `context.solverParameters`; `observedCrystalOpt` is `assignment.crystalOf` (step 373) of the one copy `sample.openedMaterialsIn study` (step 361) answers when the setup's `ObjectSlotRole` slots (step 257) hold exactly one item, whose `context.choiceOf` is a `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, _, sample)` made of exactly one opened material, and `None` otherwise. Step 374's facts pass the study. (3) `type BoundExperiment with member this.predictedReadingOf (row : MeasuredRow) : Result<RecordedReading, StudyForwardError>`: a `SettingsRow (settings, waveLengthOpt, _)` reads `readingAt settings waveLengthOpt`; an `ObservationRow o` under `PolarimeterDetectorReadout` with `Some crystal` reads `RecordedMueller` of `BoundCutPlate (CutPlate.ofForward (MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (c : CrystalParameters) -> c.opticalProperties) this.solverParameters) crystal o.configuration.cut o.configuration.thickness)` (steps 250, 355; `MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward`) evaluated by `muellerAt o.configuration.elementOrientation o.configuration.waveLength`, its `ItemEvaluationError` answering `ForwardSlotErr (SlotEvaluationErr e)`; with `None` it answers `ObservationPlateErr` naming the experiment, and under another readout `ReadingMismatchErr` naming the readout. `StudyForwardError` gains `ObservationPlateErr of reason : string` and `ReadingMismatchErr of reason : string`, rendered `the observation has no single plate of one opened crystal: <reason>` and `the reading is not what the detector records: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 374's setups with a polarimeter detector item and an object item made of a test-local plate sample of an opened uniaxial version (n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, zero gyration in the assignment), with `SolverParameters.defaultValue`: `an observation is predicted as a cut plate of its object's opened crystal at its own configuration`: an `XCut` 1 mm observation at incidence 20°, azimuth 30° and 600 nm, transmitted, reads `RecordedMueller` equal element by element exactly to `(MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) SolverParameters.defaultValue).muellerOf` of its configuration and those parameters, and the reflected one likewise; `elementOrientation`'s `sampleAzimuth` and `observable` give the configuration's back; and a `SettingsRow` reads as `readingAt` does. `an observation without one opened plate, or under a detector that is no polarimeter, is refused`: an object made of no opened material, and a setup holding two object items, answer `ObservationPlateErr`; an observation under an intensity detector answers `ReadingMismatchErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the observations land, `BoundExperiment.predictedReadingOf` MUST predict an observation as the cut plate of its experiment's one opened crystal through `createBerremanForward` at the observation's configuration, exactly as the spec 0044 forward does, and read a settings row as `readingAt`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an observation is predicted as a cut plate of its object's opened crystal at its own configuration` and `an observation without one opened plate, or under a detector that is no polarimeter, is refused`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an observation is predicted as a cut plate of its object's opened crystal at its own configuration","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an observation without one opened plate, or under a detector that is no polarimeter, is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.MeasurementConfiguration.elementOrientation","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment.predictedReadingOf","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Experiment.boundWith","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 376, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [375], "how_to": "The residual entries of one measured row, per kind, REUSING the semantics of `MuellerInverse.observationResidual` / `residualVector` for Mueller matrices (the S11.2 brief; 001 §K 'the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, normalized + absolute throughput'). The log-throughput term the study needs lives inside `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor` (step 336), which Domain cannot reference, so it MOVES into `MuellerInverse.fs` beside `observationResidual` and the fit calls it (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs`, after `residualVector` (`MuellerInverse.fs:residualVector`): `throughputResidual (measured : MuellerMatrix) (model : MuellerMatrix) : Result<ResidualVector, InversionError>`, the one entry ln m₀₀(model) − ln m₀₀(measured), and `NonPositiveIntensityErr` of the measured, then the model's, m₀₀ when it is not above zero or not finite (the refusal `normalized` makes, `MuellerInverse.fs:InversionError`); its doc says it is the term that keeps isotropic absorption in the data and points at `throughputResidualFor`'s doc for why. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs`: `throughputResidualFor` takes each observation's term from `throughputResidual o.measured model`, an `Error` giving `1.0e3` where its local `logThroughput` gave `None`; the local helper is deleted. The same `log` and the same subtraction run, so every BerremanTests number is bit-identical. (3) In `StudyForward.fs`, after `predictedReadingOf` (step 375): `RowResidual = { elements : ResidualVector; throughputOpt : ResidualVector option }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualVector`), and `type RecordedReading with member this.residualAgainst (measured : RecordedReading) : Result<RowResidual, StudyForwardError>`, `this` being the prediction: two signals give the one element `predicted − measured`; two Ψ / Δ readings give the elements Ψ_p − Ψ_m and `Math.IEEERemainder (Δ_p − Δ_m, 2π)`, in radians, so a Δ near ±180° is not a 2π jump; two Mueller matrices give the elements `observationResidual measured predicted` (`MuellerInverse.fs:observationResidual`, the 15 normalized differences) and the throughput `throughputResidual measured predicted`; an `InversionError` answers the new `RowResidualErr of error : InversionError`, and readings of different kinds `ReadingMismatchErr` (step 375) naming both. `RowResidualErr` renders `the residual cannot be formed: <the error>` (each `InversionError` case's payload). No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`: `a signal row's entry is the predicted signal less the measured`: a predicted 2.5 against a measured 2 gives [0.5]. `a Psi and Delta row's entries are their differences, Delta's taken on the circle`: Ψ 30° against 28° and Δ 179° against −179° give 2° and −2°, in radians, within 1e-12. `a Mueller row's entries are the normalized element differences and the log-throughput ratio`: a predicted ideal-LP matrix scaled by 0.8 against a measured one scaled by 0.5 gives the elements `observationResidual` gives (15 zeros here) and the throughput [ln 0.8 − ln 0.5] within 1e-15, and a measured retarder (`MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller`) against it the 15 entries `observationResidual` gives. `a reading of another kind than the row's, or a Mueller matrix without positive throughput, is refused`: a signal against a Mueller matrix answers `ReadingMismatchErr`, and a measured matrix of m₀₀ 0 answers `RowResidualErr` of `NonPositiveIntensityErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers `RowResidualErr`. BerremanTests' `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, the cheapest class running `throughputResidualFor`, runs unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the row residual lands, `MuellerInverse.throughputResidual` MUST be the one log-throughput term, called by `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor` with its numbers bit-identical, and `RecordedReading.residualAgainst` MUST give a signal's difference, Ψ and the wrapped Δ, and a Mueller matrix's 15 normalized differences with its log-throughput ratio; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a signal row's entry is the predicted signal less the measured`, `a Psi and Delta row's entries are their differences, Delta's taken on the circle`, `a Mueller row's entries are the normalized element differences and the log-throughput ratio` and `a reading of another kind than the row's, or a Mueller matrix without positive throughput, is refused`, the count rising by 4, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a signal row's entry is the predicted signal less the measured", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a Psi and Delta row's entries are their differences, Delta's taken on the circle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a Mueller row's entries are the normalized element differences and the log-throughput ratio", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a reading of another kind than the row's, or a Mueller matrix without positive throughput, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.throughputResidual", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.RowResidual", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.RecordedReading.residualAgainst", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 377, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [376], "how_to": "The study's pre-fit validation: every run a fit reads checked by the moved checks and flagged by the data-change check (001 §R 'Its three validation checks are reused as the study's pre-fit checks'; 001 §E 'flagged … before each fit'; steps 369 and 370). A failed check is reported, not raised: the study view (S11.5) lists each. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `residualAgainst` (step 376): (1) `ExperimentPrefit = { experiment : Experiment; check : Result<MappedPoints, PrefitError>; changeOpt : DataChangeFlag option }`: one run's checked points or its typed failure, and its data's change flag (`None` without data, whose check already answers `MissingDataErr`). (2) `type Study with member this.prefitWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (fitted : DataAttachment list) : Result<ExperimentPrefit list, StudyForwardError>`: the study's `enabledExperiments` (step 365) whose role's `studyUse` (step 372) is `ResidualRunUse` or `DarkLevelRunUse`, in study order, each found by name in `context.kit.experiments` (else `MissingStudyRunErr` naming it), its `check` `prefitCheckWith context.library context.experimentData context.kit.setups` (step 369), and its `changeOpt` for an attached run `data.changeWith` (step 370) of `context.experimentData.attachmentStatus data.attachment` (step 305), a `KitError` answering `StudyRunKitErr`. `fitted` is the attachments the study's last fit run read, empty before its first. `StudyForwardError` gains `MissingStudyRunErr of reason : string` and `StudyRunKitErr of error : KitError`, rendered `the kit has no such experiment: <reason>` and `the kit cannot report the data's status: <describe>`. No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 374's setups, a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy` record answering `readMapped` and `attachmentStatus` by attachment path, and a study of E1 (Science, attached, unchanged), K1 (Dark, attached, changed since attach), X1 (Diagnostic, attached), E2 (Calibration, no data), E3 (Science, attached, disabled) and P1 (Planned): `a study's pre-fit checks every run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag`: with `fitted` holding E1's path at another hash, `prefitWith` answers E1 (`Ok` of its points, `ChangedSinceFitFlag`), K1 (`Ok`, `ChangedSinceAttachFlag`) and E2 (`MissingDataErr`, `None`), in that order, and nothing for X1, E3 or P1. `a study naming an experiment the kit lacks, or a data status the kit cannot read, is refused`: a study naming E9, which the kit lacks, answers `MissingStudyRunErr` naming it, and an `attachmentStatus` answering a `KitIoErr` answers `StudyRunKitErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After the study's pre-fit lands, `Study.prefitWith` MUST check every enabled run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag, and leave out diagnostic, ignored, planned and disabled runs; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study's pre-fit checks every run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag` and `a study naming an experiment the kit lacks, or a data status the kit cannot read, is refused`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a study's pre-fit checks every run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a study naming an experiment the kit lacks, or a data status the kit cannot read, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ExperimentPrefit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.prefitWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 378, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [377], "how_to": "What a study's residual reads, gathered once from its pre-fit: each fitted run's measured rows and each session's dark level from its Dark runs (001 §L 'dark from the Dark runs'; step 357: 'Reading the dark level from those runs' data is the forward model's (S11.2)'; step 314: `keptBy` is 'the one a study's residual reads in S11'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `prefitWith` (step 377): (1) `StudyRun = { experiment : Experiment; rows : MeasuredRow list }`; `SessionDark = { session : SessionName; dark : DarkMean }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:DarkMean`); `StudyData = { runs : StudyRun list; darks : SessionDark list }` with `member this.darkOf (session : SessionName) : DarkMean option`. (2) `type Study with member this.dataWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) : Result<StudyData, StudyForwardError>`: the first prefit whose `check` is an `Error` answers `PrefitFailedErr` naming its experiment; `runs` are the prefits whose role's use is `ResidualRunUse`, in order, each its checked points' `measuredRowsFor experiment.scan` (step 371); `darks` hold, for each session of `this.sessionsIn context.kit.experiments` (step 358) listing a run, the mean of the signals of every row of `session.darkRunsIn` over the prefits' experiments (step 357: its own Dark runs, else every Dark run the fit reads), each row a `RecordedSignal` (else `DarkReadingErr` naming the run), as a `DarkMean`; a session with no Dark run has none, and its intensity runs take their detector's `darkOffset` (step 374). `StudyForwardError` gains `PrefitFailedErr of experiment : ExperimentName * error : PrefitError` and `DarkReadingErr of reason : string`, rendered `the experiment is not ready for a fit: <name>: <the error's describe>` and `a dark run does not record a signal: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 377's fixture with every check passing: `a study's data holds each fitted run's kept rows in study order`: E1's rows and E2's are in `runs` in that order, E1's three intensity points with point 2 excluded giving two rows, and K1 is not a run. `a session's dark level is the mean signal of its own dark runs, else of every dark run, and none without a dark run`: with K1 in `Session 1` holding signals 0.2 and 0.4, `Session 1`'s dark is 0.3; with a second session E4 holding no Dark run of its own, its dark is the mean over every Dark run the fit reads; with K1 disabled no session has a dark. `a failed pre-fit check or a dark run that records no signal is refused`: a prefit whose check is `MissingDataErr` answers `PrefitFailedErr` naming E2, and a Dark run whose rows are `RecordedPsiDelta` answers `DarkReadingErr` naming it. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After the study's data lands, `Study.dataWith` MUST hold each fitted run's kept rows in study order and each session's dark level as the mean signal of its Dark runs, else of every Dark run, and refuse a failed check or a Dark run without signals; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study's data holds each fitted run's kept rows in study order`, `a session's dark level is the mean signal of its own dark runs, else of every dark run, and none without a dark run` and `a failed pre-fit check or a dark run that records no signal is refused`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a study's data holds each fitted run's kept rows in study order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a session's dark level is the mean signal of its own dark runs, else of every dark run, and none without a dark run", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a failed pre-fit check or a dark run that records no signal is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyRun", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.SessionDark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.dataWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 379, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [378], "how_to": "The study residual: one weighted vector over every enabled fitted run of the study, against its data, at a parameter vector laid out by the generated axes (the S11.2 brief; 001 §L 'Weights and ablation: a weight per experiment or per detector; enable / disable per experiment'; 001 §K 'A study mixes them'; step 365: `residualWeightOf` is 'the weight the residual rows of that experiment take (S11.2)'). The engines that minimise it are S11.3's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, last: `type Study with member this.residualWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (layout : StudyParameterLayout) (data : StudyData) (vector : StudyParameterVector) : Result<ResidualVector, StudyForwardError>`: for each run of `data.runs` in order, its assignment `layout.assignmentFor this context.kit.items run.experiment.name vector` (step 373), the dark `data.darkOf` gives the session of `layout.sessions` listing it (step 378), `run.experiment.boundWith context this assignment darkOpt` (step 375), its weight `this.residualWeightOf run.experiment.name bound.detectorItem` (step 365), and for each row `bound.predictedReadingOf row` (step 375) `residualAgainst` the row's measured reading (step 376), every entry multiplied by the weight. The vector is every run's element entries, run after run and row after row, followed by every Mueller row's throughput entry in the same order: the layout of `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor` (step 336), so a study of polarimeter observations at unit weight is that harness vector, which S12.2 asserts on AT-2 (001 §Q AT-2 'Model identity'). The first error stops the walk. A disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a Dark run add no entry, because `data.runs` holds none of them (steps 377, 378). No cache, scaling or penalty is added: S11.3's engines decide what an error costs. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, each study's data made by `prefitWith` and `dataWith` over a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy`: `a mixed study's residual holds every run's entries in study order, the Mueller throughputs last`: a study of an intensity run (two rows, its session holding a Dark run of signal 0.25), an ellipsometer run (one row) and a polarimeter observation run (one row of an opened uniaxial plate) gives 20 entries: the two signal differences with the dark 0.25, Ψ and Δ, the 15 normalized differences, then the one throughput entry, each equal to `residualAgainst` of `predictedReadingOf` the row within 1e-12. `a run's weight multiplies its entries, and a disabled run adds none`: the intensity run at an experiment weight of 3 (`withExperimentWeight`) and its detector at 0.5 (`withDetectorWeight`) has its two entries times 1.5 and the others unchanged; with the ellipsometer run disabled the residual holds 18 entries, the same others. `a polarimeter study's residual is the throughput residual of its observations`: a study opening a uniaxial version with its four components unknown, its one plate run holding three observations (`XCut` 1 mm transmitted at incidence 0°, the same reflected at 20°, a `ZCut` 0.5 mm transmitted at 10°) at a vector of the crystal's values, equals entry by entry, within 1e-12 relative, `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor (MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) SolverParameters.defaultValue)` of those observations over `scalingAround UniaxialParameters.axes` of any scale centred on the same parameters, at the zero scaled vector.", "acceptance": "After the residual lands, `Study.residualWith` MUST give one vector over every enabled fitted run, run after run, each entry times the run's weight, the Mueller throughputs last, equal for a polarimeter study to `throughputResidualFor`'s; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a mixed study's residual holds every run's entries in study order, the Mueller throughputs last`, `a run's weight multiplies its entries, and a disabled run adds none` and `a polarimeter study's residual is the throughput residual of its observations`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a mixed study's residual holds every run's entries in study order, the Mueller throughputs last", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a run's weight multiplies its entries, and a disabled run adds none", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a polarimeter study's residual is the throughput residual of its observations", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.residualWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 380, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S113a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [379], "how_to": "A long fit runs on `JobRunner` with per-iteration progress and Cancel (001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`, with progress and cancel'; the S11.3 brief 'per-iteration progress and Cancel'; .spec-md §10.2, §10.3). The Levenberg–Marquardt solve runs whole inside one ALGLIB call (`AlglibAdapter.fs:runLm`), so the adapter, the one file allowed to name ALGLIB, reports each iteration and honours a stop request; nothing else learns of ALGLIB. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OptimizationInterface.fs`, after `OptimizationRequest` (`OptimizationInterface.fs:OptimizationRequest`): `[<ReferenceEquality>] OptimizerIterationObserver = { reportIteration : IterationCount -> unit; cancellation : CancellationToken }`, told after each iteration of a watched solve how many it has made (1, 2, …), and read after each whether to stop (the observer shape of step 197's `KitArchiveObserver`); and `IterationWatch` = `UnwatchedIterations` | `WatchedIterations of OptimizerIterationObserver`, whether a solve is watched (a union, no flag). `TerminationReason.SearchCancelled`'s doc (`OptimizationInterface.fs:TerminationReason`) gains 'or a watched Levenberg–Marquardt solve was asked to stop (spec 0050 S11.3)', and the module doc's 'No caching, retry, or progress-callback registry lives here — progress reporting is wired separately in G.10 (slice 011).' becomes 'No caching or retry lives here; a watched solve reports its iterations through `IterationWatch` (spec 0050 S11.3).' (2) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/AlglibAdapter.fs`: `CompletionCode.terminationReason` (`AlglibAdapter.fs:CompletionCode`) gains `| CompletionCode 8 -> SearchCancelled` before its `c > 0` arm, ALGLIB's stop on a termination request; no caller requests one today, so no existing result changes. `runLm` takes `(watch : IterationWatch)`: under `UnwatchedIterations` it makes exactly today's calls (no `minlmsetxrep`, `minlmoptimize` with a null report callback), so every existing solve is bit-identical; under `WatchedIterations observer` it calls `alglib.minlmsetxrep(state, true)` and passes `minlmoptimize` an `alglib.ndimensional_rep` callback that numbers its calls k = 1, 2, …, calls `observer.reportIteration (IterationCount k)` and then, when `observer.cancellation.IsCancellationRequested`, `alglib.minlmrequesttermination(state)`; the counter is a local mutable inside `runLm`, the interop boundary. `member this.optimizeWatched (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<OptimizationResult, OptimizationError>` holds the body of `optimize ()` (`AlglibAdapter.fs:optimize`), its `LevenbergMarquardt` arm calling `this.runLm watch` and every other method running as today, unwatched (the study fit needs the LM solve only; its doc says so in one line); `optimize ()` becomes `this.optimizeWatched UnwatchedIterations`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerInverseSolver.fs`: `type IterationWatch with member this.levenbergMarquardtSolver : NonlinearSolverProxy` holds the body of `createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt ()` (`MuellerInverseSolver.fs:createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt`) with `optimizationRequest.optimizeWatched this` in place of `optimize ()`, a member because a free function of one of our types belongs on it (ELEV013); `createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt ()` becomes `UnwatchedIterations.levenbergMarquardtSolver`, its doc kept. A cancelled solve ends `OptimizationFailed`, so the proxy answers `DidNotConvergeErr` as for any failed run; the caller tells a cancel by its own token. No other member, retry or option is added. Tests, in `OptimizationInterfaceTests`: `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve reports each iteration and answers what the unwatched solve answers`: the AC-G1 request (r = [x0 − 3; x1 + 1] from [0; 0], `IterationCount 100`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-9`) through `optimizeWatched (WatchedIterations o)`, `o` recording each count over `CancellationToken.None`, answers the solution, iteration count and termination reason `optimize ()` answers (each coordinate within 1e-12), and the recorded counts are 1, 2, … without a gap, at least one; `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve stops when its cancellation is requested`: a Rosenbrock request (r = [10 · (x1 − x0²); 1 − x0] from [−1.2; 1], `IterationCount 400`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-12`, unbounded) whose observer cancels its own `CancellationTokenSource` at its first report answers `SearchCancelled` and `OptimizationFailed` after at most two reports, and the same request through `(WatchedIterations o).levenbergMarquardtSolver` as a `NonlinearRequest` with bounds ±10 answers `Error (DidNotConvergeErr _)`. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, the cheapest class whose fits run `createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt` (step 337), shows every number unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the watch lands, a watched Levenberg–Marquardt solve MUST report each iteration and stop on a requested cancellation as `SearchCancelled`, and an unwatched solve MUST make exactly today's ALGLIB calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve reports each iteration and answers what the unwatched solve answers` and `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve stops when its cancellation is requested`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` with its numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OptimizationInterface.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/AlglibAdapter.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerInverseSolver.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OptimizationInterfaceTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OptimizationInterfaceTests.a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve reports each iteration and answers what the unwatched solve answers", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OptimizationInterfaceTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OptimizationInterfaceTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-WATCHED-SOLVE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OptimizationInterfaceTests.a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve stops when its cancellation is requested", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OptimizationInterfaceTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OptimizationInterfaceTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-WATCHED-SOLVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.OptimizationInterface.OptimizerIterationObserver", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OptimizationInterface.fs", "obligations": ["S113-WATCHED-SOLVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.OptimizationInterface.IterationWatch", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OptimizationInterface.fs", "obligations": ["S113-WATCHED-SOLVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.AlglibAdapter.OptimizationRequest.optimizeWatched", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/AlglibAdapter.fs", "obligations": ["S113-WATCHED-SOLVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerInverseSolver.IterationWatch.levenbergMarquardtSolver", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerInverseSolver.fs", "obligations": ["S113-WATCHED-SOLVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.AlglibAdapter.terminationReason", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S113-WATCHED-SOLVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number": 381, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S113b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [380], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests"], "how_to": "The study engine solves from the parameters' own starts within their own bounds (the S11.3 brief 'The start is the parameters' start values, the bounds come from their states'), while the S10.1 fit wrapper `MuellerFitting.fitWithResidual` (step 337) always starts at the zero scaled vector inside a symmetric box. The solve request moves into one member both call (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'), so one request (`IterationCount 400`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-12`, the ALGLIB Levenberg–Marquardt proxy) exists. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs`, after `SearchBox` (step 337): (1) `ScaledSearch = { start : ScaledVector; lowerBounds : ScaledVector; upperBounds : ScaledVector }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ScaledVector`, a `NumericCarrier`), where a scaled solve starts and the box it keeps to. (2) `type ScaledSearch with member this.solveWith (watch : IterationWatch) (residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector) : Result<NonlinearSolution, NonlinearSolverError>`: the `NonlinearRequest` (`MuellerInverse.fs:NonlinearRequest`) `{ residual; initial = this.start; lowerBounds = this.lowerBounds; upperBounds = this.upperBounds; maxIterations = IterationCount 400; epsX = StepTolerance 1.0e-12 }` through `watch.levenbergMarquardtSolver` (step 380). (3) On `SearchBox`, `member this.centredSearch (dimension : int) : ScaledSearch`: the zero start and bounds of minus and plus `halfWidth` in every coordinate, `fitWithResidual`'s box today. (4) `fitWithResidual` becomes `(box.centredSearch scaling.dimension).solveWith UnwatchedIterations residual`, its `Ok` mapped to the same `MuellerFitData` record and its `Error e` to `NonlinearFitErr e` as today; the request and its numbers are unchanged, so every BerremanTests number is bit-identical. No other member, scaling or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs`, `module StudyEngineTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, the home of the study engine's facts: `a scaled search starts where it is told and keeps to its own box`: the residual r(v) = [v0 − 5] from start [0.5] within [−1; 2] answers a solution of 2 (pinned at its upper bound) and within [−10; 10] a solution of 5, each within 1e-9, through `UnwatchedIterations`; `a search box's centred search starts at zero within plus or minus its half-width`: `(SearchBox 50.0).centredSearch 3` holds the start [0; 0; 0], the lower bounds [−50; −50; −50] and the upper [50; 50; 50]. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (`fitObservations`) and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (`fitAbsorbingObservations`), the cheapest classes running `fitWithResidual` (step 337), show their numbers unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the scaled search lands, `ScaledSearch.solveWith` MUST hold the one bounded Levenberg–Marquardt request and `fitWithResidual` MUST call it over `SearchBox.centredSearch` with its numbers unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scaled search starts where it is told and keeps to its own box` and `a search box's centred search starts at zero within plus or minus its half-width`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` with their numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a scaled search starts where it is told and keeps to its own box", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-SCALED-SEARCH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a search box's centred search starts at zero within plus or minus its half-width", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-SCALED-SEARCH"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.ScaledSearch", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S113-SCALED-SEARCH"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.ScaledSearch.solveWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S113-SCALED-SEARCH"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.SearchBox.centredSearch", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S113-SCALED-SEARCH"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number": 382, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S113c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [381], "how_to": "The nonlinear engine is multi-start (001 §L 'the nonlinear path is `InverseFit` / `MuellerInverseSolver` (Alglib, multi-start)'; the S11.3 brief), and how many starts a study's fit makes is one of its fit settings, stored in the study file beside the mode (001 §L 'fit settings'). One start, the parameters' own, is the default, so a study fits as the inverse suites do (the reference kits' studies keep it, S12). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `Studies.fs`, before `StudyFitSettings` (step 358): `FitStartCount of int` with `.value`, `static member tryCreate (count : int) : Result<FitStartCount, StudyError>` refusing a count below 1 with `InvalidFitStartCountErr` naming it, and `static member single : FitStartCount` (1). `StudyFitSettings` gains `starts : FitStartCount` as its last field, `StudyFitSettings.initial` holding `FitStartCount.single`; `type Study with member this.withFitStarts (starts : FitStartCount) : Study` sets it in place, beside `withFitMode` (step 365). `StudyError` gains `InvalidFitStartCountErr of reason : string`, rendered `the fit start count is not valid: <reason>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json` (step 359): under version 1, `settings` holds exactly `mode`, `experimentWeights`, `detectorWeights`, `disabled` and `starts`, an integer of at least 1. The serializer writes the count as its number; no converter is added. There are no up-converters: a study file without `starts` is refused by its schema (.spec-md §4 'Stored formats'), and the kits that exist are written after this step (S12). (3) Every record expression that spells out a `StudyFitSettings` in the tests gains `starts = FitStartCount.single`, and nothing else changes. Tests: in `StudyTests`, `a fit start count refuses fewer than one start, and a study's starts are set in place`: `FitStartCount.tryCreate` keeps 1 and 5 and answers `InvalidFitStartCountErr` for 0 and −2; `withFitStarts` of 4 leaves the other settings as they were and `StudyFitSettings.initial.starts` is 1. In `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 359), `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`'s study holds 3 starts and reads them back, and `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds` also refuses `study.settings.starts` 0 and a `settings` without `starts` with `SchemaValidationErr`. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.", "acceptance": "After the start count lands, `StudyFitSettings.starts` MUST hold a `FitStartCount` of at least one, written and read in the study file under its schema; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fit start count refuses fewer than one start, and a study's starts are set in place`, the count rising by 1, and the widened `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds` and `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a fit start count refuses fewer than one start, and a study's starts are set in place", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.FitStartCount", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withFitStarts", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyFitSettings", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-STARTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number":383,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S113d","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[382],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests"],"how_to":"A fit run is the append-only record of one fit, `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json` (001 §A; 001 §E 'Fit runs are append-only and store the full parameter vector they used and produced'; 001 §I 'Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'; the S11.3 brief 'A run holds the full parameter vector used and produced, the mode and stage, the data hashes it read, and notes. S11.4 fills in the results'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3, every case name has two words and no `bool` appears. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs`, `module FitRuns` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `StudyForward.fs` (step 371), the last Domain file, because a fit run names studies, items, materials, owners and attachments: one `<Compile Include=\"FitRuns.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the record of one study fit and the stage it fits (spec 0050 S11.3). In this order: (1) `FitStage` = `JointStage` (every unknown at once) | `CalibrationStage` (stage 1: the instruments on the Calibration runs) | `ObjectStage` (stage 2: the objects behind the published calibration) (001 §L 'Fit modes'), with `member this.value : int` 1 to 3 in that order, `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : FitStage option`, `member this.text : string` (`Joint`, `Stage 1 (calibration)`, `Stage 2 (objects)`) and `static member all`. (2) `CalibrationUse` = `CalibrationHeldFixed` | `CalibrationAsPrior`: whether a `CalibratedParameter` is held at its value or freed with a prior of its value and sigma (001 §L 'stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with σ'), `value` 1-2, `tryOfWire`, `text` (`fixed`, `as priors`) and `all`. (3) `StudyEngineKind` = `LinearStudyEngine` | `NonlinearStudyEngine`, the engine the automatic choice took (001 §L 'The choice is automatic'), `value` 1-2, `tryOfWire`, `text` (`linear`, `nonlinear`) and `all`. (4) `FitRunNotes of string` with `.value` and `static member none`; `FitChiSquared of float` with `.value`, the sum of a solution's squared residual entries; `FitMemberFailure of string` with `.value`, why a multi-start member failed, as rendered. (5) `FitMemberOutcome` = `MemberConverged of fitted : ParameterValue list * chiSquaredOpt : FitChiSquared option` | `MemberFailed of failure : FitMemberFailure`, stored in the serializer's case form (step 356's `SessionGainModel` precedent), no int tag; `FitRunMember = { start : ParameterValue list; outcome : FitMemberOutcome }`, one multi-start member: the vector it started from and where it ended. (6) `FitRunEntry = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; owner : UnknownOwner; start : ParameterValue; fitted : ParameterValue }` (steps 358, 362), one value of the fitted vector, in the layout's order (step 372); `FitRunParameter = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; state : ParameterState }` (step 214), one parameter as the fit read it. `UnknownOwner` is stored in the serializer's case form, as `StudyParameterRef` is (step 359). (7) `ObjectMatrixFit = { items : ItemId list; elements : ParameterValue list; rank : MatrixRank; rmse : ResidualRmse }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:ReconstructedMatrix`'s readouts): one linear object solve, the black-box items it reconstructs in light order (one item, or a series whose combined matrix S11.4's product check reads), its sixteen elements m00 … m33 row-major, the solver's rank and RMSE. (8) `FitRun = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; name : FitRunName; study : StudyName; stamp : ClockTime; mode : FitMode; stage : FitStage; calibrationUse : CalibrationUse; engine : StudyEngineKind; runs : ExperimentName list; dataRead : DataAttachment list; parameters : FitRunParameter list; entries : FitRunEntry list; members : FitRunMember list; objectMatrices : ObjectMatrixFit list; notes : FitRunNotes }`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1: the runs it fitted, every data file it read at the hash it read (step 132's `DataAttachment`, which step 377's `prefitWith` takes back as `fitted`), every parameter it read with its state (the full vector used), the fitted vector with each entry's start and fitted value (used and produced), every multi-start member and every linear object solve. S11.4 adds the results. (9) `type StudyName with member this.fitRunNameAt (at : ClockTime) : FitRunName` (`FitRunName`, step 214): `<the study name's fileStem>@<at as yyyyMMdd'T'HHmmss'Z', invariant culture, UTC>`, the form steps 235, 241 and 245 write (`QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z`); and `type FitRunName with member this.fileStem : FileStem`, `FileStem.ofText` of its text (step 24), the stem of its `.fitrun-json` (`FitRunKitFile`, step 123). (10) `type NonlinearSolverError with member this.failureText : FitMemberFailure` (`MuellerInverse.fs:NonlinearSolverError`): `the solver did not converge: <reason>` for `DidNotConvergeErr` and `the solve request is not valid: <reason>` for `InvalidNonlinearRequestErr`. No other type or member is added: the stage is step 385's, the file step 384's. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs`, `module FitRunTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment: `a fit run is named by its study's file stem and the clock's instant`: `(StudyName \"QZ:LR\").fitRunNameAt` of `ClockTime` of `DateTime(2026, 11, 1, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)` is `FitRunName \"QZ_LR@20261101T120000Z\"`, its `fileStem` is `FileStem \"QZ_LR@20261101T120000Z\"` and `FitRunKitFile.fileNameOf` of it is `FileName \"QZ_LR@20261101T120000Z.fitrun-json\"`; `a fit stage, a calibration use and an engine round-trip their wire tags and render their text`: the tags 1-3, 1-2 and 1-2 in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and one past the last, the texts as above and `all` in tag order; `a solver failure renders the reason a multi-start member failed`: `DidNotConvergeErr \"step too small\"` and `InvalidNonlinearRequestErr \"empty\"` render their two texts, each holding its reason.","acceptance":"After the fit run's shape lands, `FitRuns.fs` MUST declare `FitStage`, `CalibrationUse`, `StudyEngineKind`, the member, entry, parameter and object-solve records and `FitRun`, and a fit run MUST be named `<study stem>@<UTC stamp>`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fit run is named by its study's file stem and the clock's instant`, `a fit stage, a calibration use and an engine round-trip their wire tags and render their text` and `a solver failure renders the reason a multi-start member failed`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.a fit run is named by its study's file stem and the clock's instant","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.a fit stage, a calibration use and an engine round-trip their wire tags and render their text","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.a solver failure renders the reason a multi-start member failed","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitStage","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.CalibrationUse","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.StudyEngineKind","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRunNotes","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitChiSquared","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitMemberFailure","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitMemberOutcome","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRunMember","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRunEntry","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRunParameter","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.ObjectMatrixFit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRun","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.StudyName.fitRunNameAt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRunName.fileStem","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.NonlinearSolverError.failureText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN-SHAPE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number": 384, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S113e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [383], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests"], "how_to": "A fit run persists as its own kit file, `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema, written once and never rewritten (001 §E 'Fit runs are append-only'; 001 §A; 001 §P '`KitProxy` … studies and fit runs'; the S11.3 brief 'Fit runs are append-only and never rewritten'; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 146's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`) and step 359's shape for studies; no second parser or writer is written, and no proxy verb is added: append-only is a check over `listKindFiles` before `writeKindFile` (step 127). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `Kit.fs`: `KitError` (step 122) gains `FitRunExistsErr of reason : string` (the kit already holds a fit run of that name), rendered `the kit already holds that fit run: <reason>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/fitrun.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/study.schema.json` (step 359), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/fitrun.json`: `schemaVersion` a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 (`then`), the root holds exactly the fifteen fields of `FitRun` (step 383): `name` and `study` (strings holding a non-white-space character, `\\S`), `stamp` (a string), `mode` (an integer from 1 to 2), `stage` (1 to 3), `calibrationUse` (1 to 2), `engine` (1 to 2), `runs` (an array of non-empty strings), `dataRead`, `parameters`, `entries`, `members` and `objectMatrices` (arrays) and `notes` (a string). The inner shapes are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/study.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateFitRunFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateStudyFile` (step 359) does. (3) `CanonicalJson.options` (`CanonicalJson.fs`) gains three converters, for `FitStage`, `CalibrationUse` and `StudyEngineKind`, written as step 359's `ParameterScope` and `FitMode` converters are and registered beside them: each writes the case's `value` and reads through `tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. `FitMemberOutcome` and `UnknownOwner` keep the serializer's case form; nothing else in the options changes. (4) `KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146, 359): `type FitRun with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText`); `type KitFileText with member this.parseFitRun : Result<FitRun, StorageError>` (`parseVersionedText validateFitRunFile FitRunKitFile.extension FitRun.currentSchemaVersion this.value`); on the `KitProxy` extension `member this.writeFitRun (run : FitRun) : Result<unit, KitError>`: when `listKindFiles FitRunKitFile` holds `run.name.fileStem` (step 383) ignoring case, `FitRunExistsErr` naming the file, writing nothing; otherwise `writeKindFile FitRunKitFile run.name.fileStem` of `run.fileText`, a rendering error being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file; and `member this.readFitRuns (study : StudyName) : Result<FitRun list, KitError>`, which parses every stem `listKindFiles FitRunKitFile` answers, a refusal or a run whose `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason and refusing the whole read, and answers the runs whose `study` is the given one, ordered by `stamp` then by name (ordinal). Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) `writeFitRun` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. No delete, rename, replace, cache or other member is added: a fit run is written once. Tests. Their fit run is test-local: `QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z` of study `QZ-LR` at that instant, `JointFit`, `ObjectStage`, `CalibrationHeldFixed`, `LinearStudyEngine`, runs [E1], one `DataAttachment` (`data/raw/e1.csv`, a test-local hash), one `FitRunParameter` (CPL1 `c2.retardance`, a `CalibratedParameter`), one `FitRunEntry` (QZ `m00`, its `ItemOwner`, start 1, fitted 0.98), one member (start [1], `MemberConverged ([0.98], Some (FitChiSquared 0.5))`), one `ObjectMatrixFit` (QZ, sixteen elements, rank 16, RMSE 0.01) and two lines of notes. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `a fit run is stored under its name`: `FitRunKitFile.fileNameOf` of its name's `fileStem` is `FileName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z.fitrun-json\"`; `a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text`: `fileText` then `parseFitRun` answers an equal run; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys in ordinal order, writes the mode, stage, calibration use and engine as their tags, and writing the parsed run again gives the same text; `a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused`: the text with `schemaVersion` 2 answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` (found 2, expected 1, `fileExtension = FitRunKitFile.extension`), without `entries`, with an extra top-level key or with `stage` 4 `SchemaValidationErr`, and `{` `MalformedJsonErr`. `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 359): `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes each `FitStage`, `CalibrationUse` and `StudyEngineKind` as its tag and reads it back, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the stage tag 4, the use tag 3 and the engine tag 3. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFitRunFileTests.fs`, `module KitFitRunFileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, whose facts each make a folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitFitRunFileTests\", <a new GUID>)` and a `KitProxy.create` over it with `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (step 359's precedent): `a kit's fit runs round-trip, each under its name, read per study in stamp order`: the run above, a second of `QZ-LR` an hour later and one of study `LR` written answer three `.fitrun-json` files named by their stems, `readFitRuns (StudyName \"QZ-LR\")` the two in stamp order and `readFitRuns (StudyName \"LR\")` the one; `a fit run is never rewritten: writing its name again is FitRunExistsErr and leaves the file's bytes`: writing the run again, and a run of the same name with other entries, each answer `FitRunExistsErr` naming the file, and the file's bytes are unchanged; `a read-only kit refuses a fit run write and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView` `writeFitRun` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and the folder's bytes are unchanged. `KitTests`' `every kit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.", "acceptance": "After the fit-run file lands, `KitProxy.writeFitRun` MUST write a fit run once as `<name>.fitrun-json` in canonical JSON and refuse an existing name with `FitRunExistsErr`, writing nothing, and `readFitRuns` MUST read a study's runs in stamp order; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fit run is stored under its name`, `a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused`, `a kit's fit runs round-trip, each under its name, read per study in stamp order`, `a fit run is never rewritten: writing its name again is FitRunExistsErr and leaves the file's bytes` and `a read-only kit refuses a fit run write and writes nothing`, the count rising by 6, and the widened `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back`, `an unknown disk tag is refused` and `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/fitrun.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFitRunFileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a fit run is stored under its name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests.a kit's fit runs round-trip, each under its name, read per study in stamp order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFitRunFileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests.a fit run is never rewritten: writing its name again is FitRunExistsErr and leaves the file's bytes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFitRunFileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests.a read-only kit refuses a fit run write and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFitRunFileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every kit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateFitRunFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.FitRun.fileText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitFileText.parseFitRun", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeFitRun", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readFitRuns", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-RUN-FILES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number":385,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S113f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[384],"how_to":"What one fit fits: the runs and the unknowns of its stage (001 §L 'Fit modes: joint; staged: stage 1 calibrates items on Calibration runs (the Eigenvalue Calibration Method); Publish calibration; stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with σ'; the S11.3 brief 'Joint: every unknown at once'). The stage is expressed through the study's own levers, so S11.2's layout, prefit, data and residual (steps 372-379) serve every stage unchanged: runs outside the stage are disabled (`withExperimentEnablement`, step 365) and unknowns outside it are held at their start. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `FitRuns.fs`, after step 383's members: (1) `FitRunError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr` (stage 2 meets an instrument parameter that stage 1 has not published), `NoStageRunErr` (the stage has no run to fit) and `NoStageUnknownErr` (the stage has nothing to fit), with `member this.describe : string`: `an instrument parameter is not calibrated yet: <reason>`, `the stage has no run to fit: <reason>` and `the stage has nothing to fit: <reason>`. (2) `StagedStudy = { study : Study; items : Item list; stage : FitStage; calibrationUse : CalibrationUse; fittedRuns : ExperimentName list }`: the study as the stage reads it, the items as the stage holds them, and the runs whose residual rows it fits. (3) `type Study with member this.stageWith (context : StudyContext) (stage : FitStage) (calibrationUse : CalibrationUse) : Result<StagedStudy, FitRunError>` (`StudyContext`, step 366). The instruments are the items `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` (step 261) of the study's `enabledExperiments` (step 365) whose role is `CalibrationRun`, over `context.setups` and `context.items`. The fitted runs are, of the study's enabled experiments in study order: under `CalibrationStage` the `CalibrationRun` ones; under `ObjectStage` the `ScienceRun` and `DriftCheckRun` ones; under `JointStage` every one whose role's `studyUse` is `ResidualRunUse` (step 372). The runs the stage reads are the fitted runs, the AIR runs the gain models (`gainModelOf`, step 358) of the sessions holding a fitted run name (`AnchoredSessionGain` anchors, `InterpolatedSessionGain` repeats) and every Dark run; every other enabled experiment whose use is `ResidualRunUse` is disabled in the staged study, so step 377's pre-fit reads only what the stage reads. The items are `context.items` with, in order: under `CalibrationStage`, every `UnknownParameter` of an item that is not an instrument held as `KnownParameter` of its start, and every opened material's unknown component held likewise (`withMaterialParameterState`, step 361); under `ObjectStage`, an instrument's `UnknownParameter` whose `scopeOf` (step 362) is `ItemScope` answering `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr` naming the item's label and the parameter, because stage 1 publishes it first (001 §L), its session- or experiment-scoped unknowns staying free (this check reads the states as given, before any calibration is freed below); under `CalibrationAsPrior`, every `CalibratedParameter` of an item the fitted runs use becoming `UnknownParameter { start = c.value; bounds = { lower = c.value − 50 · σ; upper = c.value + 50 · σ }; priorOpt = Some { centre = c.value; sigma = c.sigma } }`, fifty sigma being the box every inverse suite searches in scaled units (`AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:searchBox`, `SearchBox 50.0`), so its scaled unit in step 387 is its sigma. `NoStageRunErr` names the study and the stage's `text` when no run is fitted, and `NoStageUnknownErr` likewise when the staged study's `unknownsWith` the items its experiments use (step 362) is empty. Nothing is written: a staged study is never stored, the fit run records the stage (step 383). No other member or option is added. Tests, in `FitRunTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216): LP1 (`PolarizerPresetChoice` of the ideal LP), CPL1 (circular polarizer, `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2]), QZ (black-box Mueller, `m00` unknown from 1 within [0, 2]) and a Phone (intensity detector, `gain` known 1000); setups made as `SetupTests` makes them: A (CPL1 prep, empty object, LP1 analyzer, the Phone) and Q (the same with QZ in its object slot); experiments A1, A2 (Calibration, over A), E1 (Science, over Q) and K1 (Dark); a `StudyContext` record of them: `stage one fits the calibration runs and frees only the instruments' unknowns`: `CalibrationStage` fits [A1; A2], disables E1 and keeps K1, and its items hold QZ's `m00` as `KnownParameter 1` and CPL1's retardance unknown; `stage two refuses an uncalibrated instrument and holds a calibrated one`: `ObjectStage` answers `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr` naming CPL1 and `c2.retardance`; after CPL1's `publishRevision` of it as `CalibratedParameter { value = 1.55; sigma = 0.002; fitRun = FitRunName \"S@20261101T120000Z\" }` (step 235) it fits [E1], disables A1 and A2, holds CPL1's calibration and frees QZ's `m00`; `as priors, a calibrated parameter is freed with its value as start and prior, within fifty sigma`: the same under `CalibrationAsPrior` frees CPL1's retardance as an unknown starting at 1.55 within [1.45, 1.65] with the prior 1.55 ± 0.002, within 1e-12; `a stage with no run to fit or nothing to fit is refused`: `ObjectStage` over a study holding no Science run answers `NoStageRunErr`, and `JointStage` over a study whose every parameter is known `NoStageUnknownErr`; `every fit-run error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the stage lands, `Study.stageWith` MUST fit the Calibration runs with only the instruments free under stage 1, refuse an uncalibrated instrument under stage 2 and free a calibration with its prior within fifty sigma under `CalibrationAsPrior`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `stage one fits the calibration runs and frees only the instruments' unknowns`, `stage two refuses an uncalibrated instrument and holds a calibrated one`, `as priors, a calibrated parameter is freed with its value as start and prior, within fifty sigma`, `a stage with no run to fit or nothing to fit is refused` and `every fit-run error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.stage one fits the calibration runs and frees only the instruments' unknowns","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.stage two refuses an uncalibrated instrument and holds a calibrated one","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.as priors, a calibrated parameter is freed with its value as start and prior, within fifty sigma","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.a stage with no run to fit or nothing to fit is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests.every fit-run error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitRunTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitRunTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRunError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.StagedStudy","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.Study.stageWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-STAGE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number":386,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S113g","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[385],"how_to":"The study engine chooses its engine automatically: linear when the unknowns enter linearly, nonlinear otherwise (001 §L 'Engines — the existing ones, reused: the linear path is `MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign` + `reconstruct` (SVD, rank, condition); the nonlinear path is `InverseFit` / `MuellerInverseSolver` (Alglib, multi-start) over `MuellerInverse.forwardModels`, driven by the generated parameter axes. The choice is automatic: linear when the unknowns enter linearly'; the S11.3 brief 'LINEAR when the unknowns enter linearly, e.g. black-box Mueller objects with calibrated instruments: S10.3's staged path'). The linear engine is the staged Mueller path (S10.3), whose solves are all linear least squares through `MuellerSolverProxy`: its stage 1 (the AIR cosine fits, steps 349, 389) and its stage 3 (`buildDesign` + `reconstruct`, steps 351, 390). The rule is structural and pure. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. New `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs`, `module StudyEngine` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `StagedMuellerPath.fs` (step 349): one `<Compile Include=\"StudyEngine.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the study engine, its automatic choice, its linear and nonlinear paths and the fit (spec 0050 S11.3). In this order: (1) `StudyFitError`, an `*Error` union, first cases `StudyForwardFitErr of error : StudyForwardError` (the forward model, the pre-fit or the data refused, step 371) and `FitStageErr of error : FitRunError` (step 385), with `member this.describe : string`: `the study's model or data refused the fit: <the error's describe>` and `the stage refused the fit: <the error's describe>`. Later steps add cases, each with its line. (2) `CalibrationPolarizer` = `LinearCalibrationPolarizer` | `CircularCalibrationPolarizer` (derived, never stored, no tag), the reference families' two polarizers (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:Family`), and `type ItemModelChoice with member this.calibrationPolarizerOpt : CalibrationPolarizer option` (step 216): `PolarizerPresetChoice` of a preset whose `behavior` is `ComputedIdeal IdealLinear` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerBehavior`) and `LibraryModelChoice` of a form `OpticalElementModel (RealPolarizerModel _)` are linear; `LibraryModelChoice` of `OpticalElementModel (CompoundModel [ { form = RealPolarizerModel _; offset = 0° }; { form = RetarderPlateModel _; offset = 45° } ])`, the built-in circular polarizer's form (step 210), is circular; everything else is `None`. `member this.familyWith (analyzer : CalibrationPolarizer) : Family` on `CalibrationPolarizer` (the prep's) answers `LpLp`, `LpCpl`, `CplLp` or `CplCpl`. (3) `type StagedStudy with member this.engineWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) : StudyEngineKind` (steps 372, 377, 385). Over the forward context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items` (a record copy), its layout `this.study.parameterLayoutWith` (step 372), and each fitted run's slots `slotsIn` (step 261) in `SetupSlot.inLightOrder` (step 257) with their items' `context.choiceOf`, the answer is `LinearStudyEngine` when the stage's shape is one of these two, and `NonlinearStudyEngine` otherwise: (a) the calibration shape, under `CalibrationStage`: every fitted run holds no item in an `ObjectSlotRole` slot other than an `EmptySlotModel` item, exactly one item in a `PrepSlotRole` slot and one in an `AnalyzerSlotRole` slot, each with a `calibrationPolarizerOpt`, and a `DetectorSlotRole` item of an `IntensityDetectorModel` form; its prefit `check` is `Ok (CapturePoints _)` (step 300's Phone ROI CSV rows); the runs hold the families `LpLp`, `LpCpl` and `CplLp` each at least once; and every layout entry is an item parameter with an `ItemOwner` and is one of: the `dialZero` of an `LpLp` run's analyzer, the `dialZero` or `c2.retardance` of an `LpCpl` run's analyzer, or the `c2.fastAxisOffset` or `c2.retardance` of a `CplLp` run's prep (the reference stage-1 constants, step 349); (b) the black-box shape, under `ObjectStage` or `JointStage`: every layout entry is an item parameter `m<row><column>` with an `ItemOwner`, of an item whose choice is a `LibraryModelChoice` of form `OpticalElementModel (BlackBoxMuellerModel SixteenElementMueller)` (step 208), each such item having a non-empty subset of its sixteen coefficients as entries after resolving study links (step 364) to their independent layout leaders; equality-linked coefficients MUST share the leader's column; coefficients absent from the layout MUST retain their staged KnownParameter or held CalibratedParameter values. Fixing any subset, including only m33 or all but one coefficient, MUST preserve linear classification when the preparation, analyzer and gains remain fixed; every fitted run has the affine shape just defined, permitting fixed object matrices around its unknown-bearing matrix, all source, preparation, analyzer, orientation and surrounding-element parameters are fixed and evaluated through ItemModelChoice.boundWith and BoundOpticalElement, including either ideal-CP handedness, constant-Mueller presets and fixed compounds; calibrationPolarizerOpt MUST NOT gate object or joint linear classification, its detector item is of an `IntensityDetectorModel` form whose `gain` is no entry, and its prefit `check` is `Ok (CapturePoints _)`; and each independent matrix coefficient has the corresponding linear design columns; rank deficiency MUST reach the SVD solver, not change engine classification (step 390). No score, threshold or option is added; the choice is recorded in the fit run (step 383). Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216) as `FitRunTests` makes them (step 385), prefits made as `StudyForwardTests` makes them (step 377) over a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy` answering `CapturePoints` rows: `a polarizer item is classified linear or circular by its model`: the ideal-LP preset and the real linear polarizer model are linear, the circular polarizer model circular, the retarder plate, the black-box model and the ideal CP preset `None`, and the four families come out of `familyWith`; `the calibration stage of LP and CPL AIR runs over capture rows is linear`: AIR Calibration runs over LP1→LP2, LP1→CPL2 and CPL1→LP2 with LP2's `dialZero`, CPL2's `dialZero` and `c2.retardance` and CPL1's `c2.fastAxisOffset` and `c2.retardance` unknown are `LinearStudyEngine` under `CalibrationStage`; without the CPL→LP run, or with the Phone's `gain` unknown, `NonlinearStudyEngine`; `fully or partly unknown black-box matrices behind fixed instruments are linear, while a free gain or an unresolved series is nonlinear`: Science runs of QZ behind the published instruments MUST be `LinearStudyEngine` under both `ObjectStage` and `JointStage` with all sixteen unknown, with only `m33` held KnownParameter, with `m23` known and `m32` held CalibratedParameter, and with only `m00` unknown; each fixed value MUST be taken from the same synthetic truth used for its observations. With the Phone's `gain` unknown, or with QZ only ever behind an unknown LR in series, the answer MUST remain `NonlinearStudyEngine`. These cases MUST call `engineWith` on valid prefits and a non-empty layout, rather than failing earlier validation. Step 390 MUST prove the corresponding reduced solve numerically and step 391 MUST prove automatic dispatch through `runFit`; `a study fitting an opened material's components is nonlinear`: a polarimeter study of an opened uniaxial material (step 379's shape) is `NonlinearStudyEngine` under `JointStage`; `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local payload renders a distinct text holding it. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Equality links among matrix coefficients MUST remain linear, including links across independently observed objects; links to a fixed leader MUST become fixed contributions. A path with one unknown-bearing matrix and any number of fixed optical matrices MUST remain linear. Products of two independently unknown matrices on the same fitted path remain nonlinear; a separately reconstructed series matrix is a diagnostic, not a claim that their product is affine in both sets of coefficients. The calibration-family recognizer in (2) is only for calibration and MUST keep its specialized meaning. Extend the black-box classification fact with valid prefits and nonempty layouts: only m00 unknown with fixed ideal-circular preparation (both handednesses), fixed linear analyzer and fixed gain; a fixed constant-Mueller or compound preparation; one unknown matrix surrounded by fixed optics; and equality-linked Mueller coefficients. Each MUST be LinearStudyEngine in ObjectStage and JointStage. An unknown gain multiplying an unknown coefficient, or two unknown matrices coupled in the fitted objective, MUST be NonlinearStudyEngine.","acceptance":"After the choice lands, `StagedStudy.engineWith` MUST answer `LinearStudyEngine` for the calibration shape under stage 1 and the black-box shape under stage 2 or joint, including any non-empty subset of unknown matrix coefficients with the others held fixed, and `NonlinearStudyEngine` otherwise; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the calibration stage of LP and CPL AIR runs over capture rows is linear`, `fully or partly unknown black-box matrices behind fixed instruments are linear, while a free gain or an unresolved series is nonlinear`, `a study fitting an opened material's components is nonlinear`, `a polarizer item is classified linear or circular by its model` and `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass. Both ideal-CP handednesses, fixed constant or compound optics, fixed surrounding objects and equality links MUST preserve linear classification; calibrationPolarizerOpt MUST restrict only calibration-family recognition.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests","BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.the calibration stage of LP and CPL AIR runs over capture rows is linear","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.fully or partly unknown black-box matrices behind fixed instruments are linear, while a free gain or an unresolved series is nonlinear","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a study fitting an opened material's components is nonlinear","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a polarizer item is classified linear or circular by its model","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.CalibrationPolarizer","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.ItemModelChoice.calibrationPolarizerOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.CalibrationPolarizer.familyWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.engineWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number": 387, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S113h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [386], "how_to": "The nonlinear engine: the study residual (step 379) minimised by the ALGLIB Levenberg–Marquardt solve over the generated axes, multi-start (001 §L 'the nonlinear path is `InverseFit` / `MuellerInverseSolver` (Alglib, multi-start) over `MuellerInverse.forwardModels`, driven by the generated parameter axes'; the S11.3 brief 'The start is the parameters' start values, the bounds come from their states, and priors are residual rows with sigma'). It reuses the scaled search (step 381), the watched solve (step 380) and the deviate provider (step 339); the forward models are the residual's (steps 374-376). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `engineWith` (step 386): (1) `StudyFitSolution = { engine : StudyEngineKind; layout : StudyParameterLayout; members : FitRunMember list; fitted : StudyParameterVector; objectMatrices : ObjectMatrixFit list }` (steps 372, 383): what every engine answers and the fit run records (step 391). (2) `studySearchBox : SearchBox` = `SearchBox 50.0` (step 337): an entry's scaled unit is its bounds' span over twice this half-width, so ±50 scaled units span its bounds — the box every inverse suite searches (`AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:searchBox`) and fifty sigma for a calibration freed as a prior (step 385) — and ALGLIB's fixed 1e-6 differentiation step stays a small, linear perturbation (`MuellerInverseSolver.fs:createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt`'s doc). (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] ScaledStudyProblem = { layout : StudyParameterLayout; centre : StudyParameterVector; unit : StudyParameterVector; search : ScaledSearch; residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector }`, with `member this.physicalOf (scaled : ScaledVector) : StudyParameterVector`, entry k `centre_k + unit_k · scaled_k`. (4) `type StagedStudy with member this.scaledProblemWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (data : StudyData) : Result<ScaledStudyProblem, StudyFitError>`, over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items`: the layout `this.study.parameterLayoutWith` (step 372); for each entry, its unknown's start as the centre and `(upper − lower) / (2 · studySearchBox.halfWidth)` as the unit, the search starting at the zero vector within `(lower − start) / unit` and `(upper − start) / unit`; the data's runs kept to `this.fittedRuns`; and the residual of a scaled vector: `this.study.residualWith` (step 379) at its `physicalOf`, followed by one row per entry whose unknown has a prior, in entry order, `(x_k − prior.centre) / prior.sigma`. A vector the forward model refuses gives every entry of a residual of that length the 1.0e3 penalty `MuellerFitting.residualFor` uses (step 336), so the closure is total; the residual at the start is taken first, and its error answers `StudyForwardFitErr`. A fitted run whose session (`layout.sessions`) has an `AnchoredSessionGain` or `InterpolatedSessionGain` model (`gainModelOf`, step 358) answers `SessionGainNeedsLinearEngineErr` naming the session: this engine fits a detector's gain as its parameter (step 374), and a gain derived from AIR runs is the linear engine's (step 390). (5) `type StagedStudy with member this.fitNonlinear (context : StudyForwardContext) (data : StudyData) (deviates : UniformDeviateProvider) (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<StudyFitSolution, StudyFitError>`: the problem of (4), then `this.study.settings.starts` members (step 382): the first starts at the zero scaled vector (the parameters' own starts); each further one at `lower'_k + (d + 1) / 2 · (upper'_k − lower'_k)` in every coordinate, `d` the provider's `nextDeviate ()` (uniform on [−1, 1], step 339), drawn entry after entry, member after member. Each member is `{ problem.search with start = <its start> }.solveWith` its watch `problem.residual` (step 381): under `WatchedIterations o` a watch reporting `o.reportIteration` of the earlier members' iterations plus its own count, over `o.cancellation`, so the progress counts every iteration of the fit; `UnwatchedIterations` stays unwatched. A requested cancellation, read before each member and after it, answers `FitCancelledErr` naming how many members ran, the running member's result dropped. A member's `Ok solution` is `MemberConverged` of `physicalOf solution.solution` as values and `Some` of its `finalResiduals.sumOfSquares` (`OptimizationInterface.fs`) as a `FitChiSquared`; its `Error e` is `MemberFailed e.failureText` (step 383). Every member's start is recorded as values. No converged member answers `NoConvergedMemberErr` naming each member's failure; otherwise `fitted` is the converged member of least chi-squared, the earliest on a tie, and the answer `{ engine = NonlinearStudyEngine; layout; members; fitted; objectMatrices = [] }`. `StudyFitError` gains `SessionGainNeedsLinearEngineErr`, `NoConvergedMemberErr` and `FitCancelledErr`, each `of reason : string`, rendered `the nonlinear engine fits a session's gain as its detector's parameter: <reason>`, `no start of the fit converged: <reason>` and `the fit was cancelled: <reason>`. No retry, cache, threshold or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over a study opening a test-local uniaxial version (n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, g11 and g33 known at 0) with n_o and n_e unknown from 1.0002 and 1.0001 times the truth (a retardance error well inside half a fringe), each within its start ± 0.05 (a scaled unit of 1e-3, the harness's), staged by `JointStage` and `CalibrationHeldFixed` (step 385), its one plate run over a polarimeter detector holding four observations at the truth through `MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) SolverParameters.defaultValue` (an `XCut` 100 µm plate at azimuth 30° and 600 nm, transmitted at incidence 0° and 30°, reflected at 30° and 50°) and read as `ObservationPoints` through a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy`, its pre-fit and data made as `StudyForwardTests` makes them (step 379): `a polarimeter study recovers an opened uniaxial material's two indices from a perturbed start`: `fitNonlinear` unwatched recovers each index within 1e-9 of its truth from one converged member; `the first member starts at the parameters' starts and each further member where the deviates place it within the bounds`: with `withFitStarts` of 3 and a stub provider answering −1, 1, 0 and 0.5 in turn, the second member starts at n_o's lower and n_e's upper bound and the third at n_o's start and n_e's start plus 0.025, each within 1e-12, and `fitted` is the values of the converged member of least chi-squared; `a prior adds one residual row, its scaled offset from its centre over its sigma`: with n_o given the prior 1.545 ± 0.001, `scaledProblemWith`'s residual at the zero vector is the data entries followed by one more, (1.0002 · 1.544 − 1.545) / 0.001, within 1e-12, and without the prior no extra row; `a session whose gain is anchored or interpolated is refused by the nonlinear engine`: an intensity study whose session's model is `AnchoredSessionGain` of an AIR run answers `SessionGainNeedsLinearEngineErr` naming the session; `a cancelled fit stops before its next member and answers FitCancelledErr`: with 3 starts and a watch whose `CancellationTokenSource` is cancelled at its first report, `fitNonlinear` answers `FitCancelledErr` and the provider was asked for no deviate. `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases.", "acceptance": "After the nonlinear engine lands, `StagedStudy.fitNonlinear` MUST minimise the study residual plus one row per prior over each entry's own bounds, from the parameters' starts and then from deviate-placed starts, keep the converged member of least chi-squared, count every iteration through its watch and stop on Cancel; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a polarimeter study recovers an opened uniaxial material's two indices from a perturbed start`, `the first member starts at the parameters' starts and each further member where the deviates place it within the bounds`, `a prior adds one residual row, its scaled offset from its centre over its sigma`, `a session whose gain is anchored or interpolated is refused by the nonlinear engine` and `a cancelled fit stops before its next member and answers FitCancelledErr`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a polarimeter study recovers an opened uniaxial material's two indices from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.the first member starts at the parameters' starts and each further member where the deviates place it within the bounds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a prior adds one residual row, its scaled offset from its centre over its sigma", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a session whose gain is anchored or interpolated is refused by the nonlinear engine", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a cancelled fit stops before its next member and answers FitCancelledErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitSolution", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.studySearchBox", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.ScaledStudyProblem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.scaledProblemWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.fitNonlinear", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S113-NONLINEAR"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number": 388, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S113i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [387], "how_to": "The linear engine is the staged Mueller path driven by a study (001 §L 'the linear path is `MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign` + `reconstruct`'; the S11.3 brief 'S10.3's staged path'), so the pieces of that path the study needs become callable, each MOVED out of a private helper and called back by the reference path, not copied (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). Every number of the reference path is computed by the same operations in the same order, so `MuellerReconstructionTests` is bit-identical. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: `Family` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:Family`) gains `member this.text : string` (`LP-LP`, `LP-CPL`, `CPL-LP`, `CPL-CPL`) and `MatrixKind` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixKind`) `member this.text : string` (`AIR`, `QZ`, `LR`, `QZ+LR`); `SolverError` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:SolverError`) gains `member this.describe : string` (`the design is singular: <reason>`, `the design is rank-deficient: rank <n>`); `AnalyzerModel` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:AnalyzerModel`) gains `static member linearAt (zero : Angle) (sign : DialSign) : AnalyzerModel` (`IdealLinear`, no retarder) and `static member circularAt (zero : Angle) (sign : DialSign) (retardance : Retardance) : AnalyzerModel` (`IdealCircularLeft`, `thetaRelOpt = Some (Angle.degree 45.0<deg>)`, `retardanceOpt = Some (Retardance.degree (- retardance.degrees * 1.0<deg>))`, the stage-one expression of step 349, so the same double); and `LeastSquaresSystem` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`) gains `static member ofProjections (projections : (StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity) list) : LeastSquaresSystem` (each `designRow s a` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:designRow`) and its signal, in order), the assembly `buildDesign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign`) ends with today, which it now calls, and `static member concat (systems : LeastSquaresSystem list) : LeastSquaresSystem` (design rows and right-hand sides in list order), the concatenation `reconstructStaged` makes (step 351), which it now calls. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs` (steps 349-356): (a) `StageOneAirRows = { darknessRows : MuellerRawRow list; lpLpAirRows : MuellerRawRow list; lpCplAirRows : MuellerRawRow list; cplLpAirRows : MuellerRawRow list }` and `calibrateFromAirRows (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (rows : StageOneAirRows) : Result<StageOneCalibrationData, StagedMuellerError>`, the body of `calibrateStageOne` moved over AIR rows the caller selected: the private `reduceAirTraces` loses its AIR-label filter, and `calibrateStageOne solver captures` becomes `calibrateFromAirRows` of the darkness rows and of each family file's rows whose label holds `(AIR#0)`, the filter it applied, so the same rows reach the same traces. (b) `airAnchorGainOf (source : SourceModel) (analyzer : AnalyzerModel) (dark : DarkMean) (run : ExperimentName) (rows : MuellerRawRow list) : Result<AirAnchorGain, StagedMuellerError>` (`AirAnchorGain`, step 356), the private `fitAirGain` and `meanTime` of step 351 moved: `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the run for no row; else `scalarGain` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:scalarGain`) of the rows' `darkSubtract` signals against `airIdentityPred` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:airIdentityPred`) of `source.baseStokes` and `analyzerBaseRow analyzer r.description`, at the rows' mean capture time; `reconstructStaged` calls it for its nine anchors. (c) `projectCaptureRow (source : SourceModel) (analyzer : AnalyzerModel) (phi : Angle) (dark : DarkMean) (gain : AirGain) (row : MuellerRawRow) : StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity`, the private `prepareRow` of step 351 moved: `effectiveSource phi source.baseStokes`, `effectiveAnalyzer phi (analyzerBaseRow analyzer row.description)` and `correctSignal dark row.avgTotal gain` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:effectiveSource`, `:effectiveAnalyzer`, `:correctSignal`); `reconstructStaged`'s projections call it with the reading's `objectPhi` and the session rule's `gainAt row.capturedAt`. (d) `StageOneCalibrationData.lpAnalyzer` and `cplAnalyzer` (step 349) are `AnalyzerModel.linearAt this.lpZero DialNegative` and `AnalyzerModel.circularAt this.cplZero DialPositive this.cplAnalyzerRetardance`. (e) `StagedMuellerError` gains `member this.describe : string`, each case's condition and payload: `a set of capture rows the staged path needs is empty: <reason>`, `the AIR cosine fit of <family text> failed: <the solver error's describe>`, `the reconstruction of <kind text> failed: <the solver error's describe>` and `a session gain model was refused: <the study error's describe>`. No other declaration of either file changes, and no BerremanTests file is edited. Tests, in `StagedMuellerPathTests` (step 349), over its synthetic captures (step 351): `stage one over AIR rows given directly equals stage one over the files that hold them`: `calibrateStageOne` over the files equals, field by field and exactly, `calibrateFromAirRows` over their darkness rows and their `(AIR#0)` rows; `an AIR anchor's gain scales its ideal prediction onto its dark-subtracted signal, at its rows' mean time`: two LP-LP AIR rows at dials 0° and 40°, captured at 10:00 and 10:02, whose `avgTotal` is 3 · `airIdentityPred` of `LpSource.baseStokes` and `analyzerBaseRow (AnalyzerModel.linearAt Angle.zero DialPositive)` at the dial, plus 5, give `airAnchorGainOf` a gain of 3 within 1e-12 at 10:01 for `DarkMean 5`, and no row `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the run; `a capture row is projected into its object frame and its signal corrected by the dark and the gain`: `projectCaptureRow` of a CPL source, a circular analyzer, φ 30°, dark 5 and gain 2 equals the three expressions above exactly, and `LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections` of two projections holds their two `designRow`s and signals, `concat` of two systems their rows in order; `the stage-one analyzer and source models are the shared calibrated models of its constants`: a stage-one constant set's `lpAnalyzer` and `cplAnalyzer` equal `linearAt` and `circularAt` of its zeros and retardance, field by field; `every staged path error renders its condition and its payload`: each `StagedMuellerError` case over a distinct test-local payload renders a distinct text holding its payload's text (`LP-CPL` for `AirCalibrationFitErr (LpCpl, SingularDesignErr \"x\")`), each `Family` and `MatrixKind` its text and each `SolverError` its describe. `MuellerReconstructionTests` runs unchanged, every number bit-identical.", "acceptance": "After the moves, `calibrateFromAirRows`, `airAnchorGainOf`, `projectCaptureRow`, `LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections` / `concat` and `AnalyzerModel.linearAt` / `circularAt` MUST be public with the reference path calling them and keeping no private copy, and every staged path error MUST render through `describe`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `stage one over AIR rows given directly equals stage one over the files that hold them`, `an AIR anchor's gain scales its ideal prediction onto its dark-subtracted signal, at its rows' mean time`, `a capture row is projected into its object frame and its signal corrected by the dark and the gain`, `the stage-one analyzer and source models are the shared calibrated models of its constants` and `every staged path error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; unit-tests MUST pass over `MuellerReconstructionTests` with every number unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.stage one over AIR rows given directly equals stage one over the files that hold them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.an AIR anchor's gain scales its ideal prediction onto its dark-subtracted signal, at its rows' mean time", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.a capture row is projected into its object frame and its signal corrected by the dark and the gain", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the stage-one analyzer and source models are the shared calibrated models of its constants", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.every staged path error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.Family.text", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MatrixKind.text", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.SolverError.describe", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.AnalyzerModel.linearAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.AnalyzerModel.circularAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.LeastSquaresSystem.concat", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StageOneAirRows", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.calibrateFromAirRows", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.airAnchorGainOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.projectCaptureRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerError.describe", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S113-STAGED-REUSE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number":389,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S113j","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[388],"how_to":"Stage 1 of a staged fit calibrates the instruments on the Calibration runs by the reference AIR calibration (001 §L 'stage 1 calibrates items on Calibration runs (the Eigenvalue Calibration Method)'; the S11.3 brief 'the Eigenvalue Calibration Method path over the AIR runs'): the study's AIR runs are handed, family by family, to S10.3's stage one (`calibrateFromAirRows`, step 388), and its constants become the instruments' parameter values. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `fitNonlinear` (step 387): (1) `type Angle with member this.parameterValue : ParameterValue`, the angle in radians (`ParameterValue.angle`, step 246, is the reading the other way), and `type Retardance with member this.parameterValue : ParameterValue` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:Retardance`), in radians. (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.calibrateLinear (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) : Result<StudyFitSolution, StudyFitError>`, taken only where `engineWith` (step 386) found the calibration shape: over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items`, its layout (step 372) and each fitted run's family, its prep item's `calibrationPolarizerOpt` `familyWith` its analyzer item's (step 386); `StageOneAirRows` (step 388) of the capture rows (its prefit's `Ok (CapturePoints rows)`, exclusions applied by `keptBy`, step 314) of every Dark run among the prefits, in prefit order, and of the `LpLp`, `LpCpl` and `CplLp` runs, each in study order; then `StagedMuellerPath.calibrateFromAirRows solver` of them, an error answering the new `StagedPathFitErr of error : StagedMuellerError`, rendered `the staged Mueller path refused the fit: <the error's describe>` (step 388). Each layout entry takes its constant: an `LpLp` run's analyzer's `dialZero` the `lpZero`; an `LpCpl` run's analyzer's `dialZero` the `cplZero` and its `c2.retardance` the `cplAnalyzerRetardance`; a `CplLp` run's prep's `c2.fastAxisOffset` the source model's `thetaRel` less 45° (the built-in circular polarizer's retarder sits at 45° plus its offset, step 210) and its `c2.retardance` the source model's `retardance`, each through `parameterValue`. The answer is `{ engine = LinearStudyEngine; layout; members = [ { start = <the start vector's values>; outcome = MemberConverged (<those values>, None) } ]; fitted = <those values>; objectMatrices = [] }`: the cosine fits report no common chi-squared. The dark mean is the stage one's own, over every Dark run, as the reference reads it (step 349). No other mapping, constant or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over a test-local truth `StageOneCalibrationData` (dark 5, `lpZero` 3°, `cplZero` −2°, `cplAnalyzerRetardance` 88°, source `thetaRel` 46° and `retardance` 91°), items made by `ItemDraft`: LP1 (`PolarizerPresetChoice` of the ideal LP, prep), LP2 (the real linear polarizer model, `DialMounted DialNegative`, its `dialZero` unknown, analyzer), CPL1 (the circular polarizer model, its `c2.fastAxisOffset` and `c2.retardance` unknown, prep), CPL2 (the circular polarizer model, `DialMounted DialPositive`, its `dialZero` and `c2.retardance` unknown, analyzer) and a Phone (the intensity detector model, `gain` known 1000); AIR setups LP1→LP2, LP1→CPL2 and CPL1→LP2 with empty object slots, a Calibration experiment over each scanning `VaryDialReading` 0° to 160° by 20°, and a Dark experiment, whose data a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy` answers as `CapturePoints` rows: each AIR row's `avgTotal` is 1000 · `airIdentityPred` of the truth's source model (`LpSource` behind LP1, `cplSource` behind CPL1) and its `lpAnalyzer` or `cplAnalyzer` (`analyzerBaseRow` at the dial) plus 5, each dark row 5: `the calibration stage recovers the instruments' zeros, retardances and offset through the reference stage one`: `calibrateLinear` with `createMathNetSvd ()` answers `LinearStudyEngine`, LP2's and CPL2's `dialZero` equal to 3° and −2° within 1e-9, and each of the five fitted values equal exactly to the constant `calibrateFromAirRows` answers over the same rows; `a calibration stage without a dark run is refused with the staged path's error`: without the Dark experiment it answers `StagedPathFitErr (EmptyCaptureSetErr _)` naming the darkness rows. `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After stage 1 lands, `StagedStudy.calibrateLinear` MUST hand the study's AIR runs by family and its Dark runs to `calibrateFromAirRows` and give each instrument entry its reference constant; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the calibration stage recovers the instruments' zeros, retardances and offset through the reference stage one` and `a calibration stage without a dark run is refused with the staged path's error`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.the calibration stage recovers the instruments' zeros, retardances and offset through the reference stage one","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-CALIBRATION"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a calibration stage without a dark run is refused with the staged path's error","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-CALIBRATION"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-CALIBRATION"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.Angle.parameterValue","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-CALIBRATION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.Retardance.parameterValue","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-CALIBRATION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.calibrateLinear","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-CALIBRATION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-CALIBRATION"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number":390,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S113k","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[389],"how_to":"Stage 2 (and a joint fit of the same shape) reconstructs each black-box object by the reference linear path, its sessions' gains derived from their AIR runs (001 §L 'per session the gain is free, anchored to its AIR runs, or interpolated between two AIR repeats; dark from the Dark runs'; 001 §L 'the linear path is `MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign` + `reconstruct` (SVD, rank, condition)'; the S11.3 brief 'black-box Mueller objects with calibrated instruments: S10.3's staged path / MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign + reconstruct through MuellerSolverProxy'; step 378's record: 'Deriving an anchored or interpolated session gain from its AIR runs is the staged engine's'). The models are built from the instruments' own (calibrated) values with step 388's constructors, and every row is projected by `projectCaptureRow`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `calibrateLinear` (step 389): (1) `type ParameterValue with member this.airGain : AirGain` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:AirGain`), the number as a detector's gain; `type MuellerMatrix with member this.rowMajorValues : ParameterValue list`, its sixteen elements m00 … m33 row-major (`MuellerMatrix.element`). (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.reconstructLinear (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) : Result<StudyFitSolution, StudyFitError>`, taken only where `engineWith` (step 386) found the black-box shape, over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items` and its layout (step 372). For each fitted run, in study order, over its slots in light order and each item's values `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` (step 245): the source Stokes state and fixed optical matrices MUST come from the same SourceEmission, ItemModelChoice.boundWith, BoundOpticalElement evaluation and per-row dial/orientation/wavelength rules used by the run law (steps 246-252, 258, 367, 374). The incident Stokes vector s MUST fold every fixed matrix before the unknown object; the analyzer row a MUST fold every fixed matrix after it into the detector's S0 row. The object's reference-orientation transforms MUST use effectiveSource and effectiveAnalyzer, with source intensity normalization identical to SourceEmission.emittedInto. This projection MUST work for ideal CP of either handedness, constant-Mueller presets, fixed compounds and fixed surrounding objects without constructing an LP/CPL SourceModel or requiring calibrationPolarizerOpt. its session is the session of `layout.sessions` listing it, its dark `data.darkOf` that session (step 378) or else the detector's `darkOffset` value's `darkMean` (step 374); and its gain MUST follow the session rule at the row's capture time. FreeSessionGain uses the held detector gain; anchored and interpolated rules MUST use each AIR row's actual fixed Stokes/analyzer projection and dark correction with the same gain-ratio arithmetic as airAnchorGainOf from step 388. Factor and call that scalar gain calculation; MUST NOT substitute an LP family for an unsupported fixed optic. Each row MUST produce (s, a, dark-and-gain-corrected intensity) and use LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections, whose designRow is shared with buildDesign (step 388).  The affine runs MUST group by their unknown-bearing object, preserving first-run order; fixed surrounding objects are part of the row projection and MUST NOT become fitted coefficients. Each group's full system MUST reuse LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections. Groups sharing equality-linked leaders MUST be assembled into one reduced system in layout order. An independently reconstructed combined matrix of a series remains a separate diagnostic over that series' rows, never a substitute for either constituent's coefficients. For a single item with all sixteen coefficients free, and for the independently reconstructed combined matrix of a series group, the solve MUST remain `reconstruct solver` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:reconstruct`). For a partly fixed or equality-linked system, resolve each full coefficient to its independent layout leader or a fixed value. Build m = k + P*x, where k holds fixed contributions and P maps independent parameters to their matrix positions. The reduced solve MUST be A*P*x = b - A*k through the injected MuellerSolverProxy.solveLinearLeastSquares. For unlinked unknowns P selects columns, preserving the partial-matrix formula A_U*m_U = b - A_K*m_K. Equality-linked columns MUST be summed, never discarded or solved independently then overwritten. Links across separately observed objects MUST stack their rows into one system using the shared leader column. A link to a fixed leader contributes to k. P and k MUST follow the study's actual link and owner rules; no second parameter-layout implementation is permitted. This MUST reuse `LeastSquaresSystem`, `DesignRow` and the SVD proxy, with no second solver or change to the public `reconstruct` contract. Column selection and reconstruction MUST respect `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerMatrix.vecColumnMajor` (m[row,column] occupies 4*column+row), while fitted entries MUST follow the study layout's order. The solved free values and unchanged fixed values MUST be assembled into a complete sixteen-value vector before `RealVector.columnMajorMueller` is called; a reduced solution MUST NOT be passed directly to that sixteen-value conversion. Fixed KnownParameter and held CalibratedParameter coefficients MUST retain their values exactly and MUST NOT become fitted entries. The returned rank MUST describe the reduced system (15 when only m33 is fixed, 1 when only m00 is free), and rmse MUST describe its corrected measurement residual; rank deficiency MUST be judged against the free-column count by the same solver. Any solver error MUST answer the new `ObjectSolveFitErr of items : ItemId list * error : SolverError`. A group of one item MUST fill only that item's free layout entries from the fitted matrix; every group MUST give one `ObjectMatrixFit { items; elements = matrix.rowMajorValues; rank; rmse }` (step 383) with all sixteen elements, a series group's being the combined matrix S11.4's product check compares with the cascade (001 §L 'the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ)'). The answer is `{ engine = LinearStudyEngine; layout; members = [ { start = <the start values>; outcome = MemberConverged (<the fitted values>, Some <the sum over the groups of rmse² times the group's row count>) } ]; fitted; objectMatrices }`. `SessionGainFitErr` renders `a session gain model was refused: <the error's describe>` and `ObjectSolveFitErr` `the objects could not be reconstructed: <each item id> — <the solver error's describe>`. No weighting, threshold or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over step 389's items with their five instrument parameters published at the truth's constants as `CalibratedParameter`s (step 235), QZ and LR (the black-box model, all sixteen unknown from the identity within [−2, 2]) and the truths M_QZ = `retarderMueller (Angle.degree 30.0<deg>) (Retardance.degree 40.0<deg>)` and M_LR = `retarderMueller (Angle.degree 10.0<deg>) (Retardance.degree 25.0<deg>)` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:retarderMueller`); Science runs of the four families at φ 0°, 30°, 60° and 90° scanning the analyzer dial 0° to 160° by 20°, each row's `avgTotal` g · (`designRow s a` · `M.vecColumnMajor`) + 5 for the projection's s and a; a Dark run of 5; and two hand-set sessions (step 294): `Day 1` anchored to an LP-LP AIR run of gain 1000 (`AnchoredSessionGain`), `Day 2` interpolated between AIR runs of gain 1000 at 10:00 and 1200 at 12:00 (`InterpolatedSessionGain`), its rows generated at the gain the interpolation gives at each row's time: `the object stage reconstructs a black-box matrix behind calibrated instruments, each row divided by its session's gain at its time`: `reconstructLinear` with `createMathNetSvd ()` MUST give QZ's sixteen entries within 1e-9 of M_QZ and one `ObjectMatrixFit` for QZ of rank 16. The same fact MUST also solve three partial variants over those same observations: only m33 held known (15 free), m23 known and m32 held calibrated (14 free, using their distinct signed truth values to expose row/column transposition), and only m00 unknown (1 free). A recording solver proxy MUST delegate to the real `createMathNetSvd ()` and assert the actual reduced column count, column order and right-hand side `b - A_K * m_K` for each variant; this MUST detect a full sixteen-column solve followed by overwriting fixed values. Each result MUST recover the free coefficients within 1e-9, preserve all fixed coefficients exactly, keep fixed coefficients out of fitted entries, return the complete matrix within 1e-9 and report rank equal to the free-column count. All comparisons MUST use the project's tolerance helpers; `a series of two black-box objects is reconstructed as one combined matrix`: with LR's runs and runs of QZ then LR at a shared φ added, LR's entries are within 1e-9 of M_LR and the series' `ObjectMatrixFit` [QZ; LR] holds `cascadeProduct M_LR M_QZ`'s elements within 1e-9; `an object stage whose design is rank-deficient is refused naming its objects`: QZ's runs in the LP-LP family at φ 0° alone MUST answer `ObjectSolveFitErr ([ QZ's id ], RankDeficientErr _)` for both the full matrix and the partial variant with only m33 fixed, after reaching the solver; the partial variant MUST compare rank against its 15 free columns. `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases. Extend the reconstruction fact with (a) only m00 free behind fixed ideal CP of each handedness and a fixed linear analyzer, (b) fixed constant/compound preparation, (c) an unknown matrix between fixed objects, and (d) equality-linked coefficients with observations generated from truth satisfying the links. The recording SVD proxy MUST delegate to createMathNetSvd and assert one column for the m00 case, linked-column sums A*P and target b-A*k, including a fixed leader. The linked fixture MUST include two independently observed objects sharing a leader, so independent per-object solves cannot pass. Recovered independent values MUST meet 1e-9, known values MUST be preserved exactly, linked followers MUST equal their leaders, and rank MUST equal the independent-column count. Source/analyzer projections MUST equal the ordinary run law at each row; no case may pass through an unrelated pre-fit error.","acceptance":"After stage 2 lands, `StagedStudy.reconstructLinear` MUST project every capture row of the fitted runs through the fixed instruments' actual item-model matrices, the object angle and the session's dark and gain at the row's time, and solve full object groups by `reconstruct` or a partly fixed single object through the same SVD proxy on `A_U * m_U = b - A_K * m_K`; the partial variants with 15, 14 and 1 free coefficients MUST recover their synthetic truth within 1e-9, preserve every fixed coefficient exactly, report the reduced rank and keep fixed coefficients out of fitted entries, and the reduced rank-deficient case MUST reach the solver and return `ObjectSolveFitErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the object stage reconstructs a black-box matrix behind calibrated instruments, each row divided by its session's gain at its time`, `a series of two black-box objects is reconstructed as one combined matrix` and `an object stage whose design is rank-deficient is refused naming its objects`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass. Fixed ideal-CP, constant/compound optics and fixed surrounding objects MUST reach the real SVD solve. Equality-linked coefficients MUST use combined columns, recover one value per independent leader within 1e-9 and report the independent rank, including cross-object links and fixed leaders.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.the object stage reconstructs a black-box matrix behind calibrated instruments, each row divided by its session's gain at its time","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS","S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a series of two black-box objects is reconstructed as one combined matrix","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.an object stage whose design is rank-deficient is refused naming its objects","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.ParameterValue.airGain","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.MuellerMatrix.rowMajorValues","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.reconstructLinear","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S113-LINEAR-OBJECTS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number":391,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S113l","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[390],"how_to":"One fit: a study, a stage and a calibration use in; one fit run out, stamped by the clock (001 §P `RunFit`; 001 §E 'Fit runs are append-only and store the full parameter vector they used and produced'; the S11.3 brief 'The stamp comes from ClockProvider', 'A run holds the full parameter vector used and produced, the mode and stage, the data hashes it read, and notes'). The fit computes; writing is the job's, on completion only (step 393). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `StudyEngine.fs`, last: (1) `StudyFitRequest = { study : StudyName; stage : FitStage; calibrationUse : CalibrationUse }`, what `RunFit` asks (Run joint is `JointStage`, Run stage `CalibrationStage` or `ObjectStage`, S11.5). (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitParam = { forward : StudyForwardContext; clock : ClockProvider; linearSolver : MuellerSolverProxy; deviates : UniformDeviateProvider; fitRuns : FitRun list }` (the `*Param` convention): the kit as the study sees it (step 372), the clock (step 122), the SVD proxy, the deviates (step 339) and the study's fit runs as the kit last read them (step 384). (3) `type StudyFitParam with member this.runFit (request : StudyFitRequest) (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>`: the study of `this.forward.kit.studies` named by the request (else the new `UnknownFitStudyErr of reason : string`, rendered `the kit has no such study: <reason>`); its `stageWith this.forward.kit request.stage request.calibrationUse` (step 385, an error `FitStageErr`); over the context with `kit.items` replaced by the staged items, the staged study's `prefitWith` (step 377) of `fitted`, the `dataRead` of the latest of `this.fitRuns` of that study by stamp (empty before its first), and its `dataWith` (step 378), an error `StudyForwardFitErr`; the engine `engineWith` chooses (step 386), `calibrateLinear` for a linear `CalibrationStage`, `reconstructLinear` for any other linear stage, and `fitNonlinear` (with the watch) otherwise (steps 387-390); then `this.clock.now ()`, read once, and the `FitRun` (step 383): `schemaVersion` current; `name` the study name's `fitRunNameAt` that instant and `stamp` the instant; `mode` the study's `settings.mode`; the request's stage and calibration use; the solution's engine; `runs` the staged study's `fittedRuns`; `dataRead`, for each prefit whose experiment carries data, in order, its attachment's path at the hash the fit read: `current` of a `ChangedSinceAttachFlag` or `ChangedSinceFitFlag` and the attachment's own hash for `DataUnchangedFlag` (step 370); `parameters`, every parameter of every staged item `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` the fitted runs (step 261), item by item in their order, as `ItemParameterRef` with its state, then every component of every opened material of the staged study as `MaterialParameterRef` with its state; `entries`, the layout's entries with the start vector's and the solution's fitted values; the solution's members and object matrices; and `FitRunNotes.none`. Nothing is written here. No other member or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`: `a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced`: step 387's polarimeter study through a `StudyFitParam` whose clock answers 2026-11-04 09:30:00 UTC and whose `fitRuns` are empty, `runFit` of `JointStage` and `CalibrationHeldFixed` unwatched, answers the run named `<the study's stem>@20261104T093000Z` at that stamp, `JointFit`, `JointStage`, `CalibrationHeldFixed`, `NonlinearStudyEngine`, its plate run as the one fitted run, its attachment's path at its hash as the one `dataRead`, the opened material's four components with their states among its parameters, n_o's and n_e's entries with their starts and fitted values equal to `fitNonlinear`'s, and one member. The same fact MUST additionally drive the valid partial-matrix fixture from step 390 (only m33 fixed, all instruments and gains fixed) through `runFit` under both `ObjectStage` and `JointStage` with `CalibrationHeldFixed`. Each request MUST complete a real SVD solve and return a `LinearStudyEngine` FitRun, fifteen fitted entries recovering the synthetic truth within 1e-9, m33 unchanged with its known state in `parameters` and absent from `entries`, and a complete `ObjectMatrixFit` with rank 15. This MUST exercise automatic dispatch rather than calling `reconstructLinear` directly or accepting a pre-fit error; `a fit naming no study of the kit, or refused by its stage, records nothing`: a request naming `LR`, which the kit lacks, answers `UnknownFitStudyErr`, and `ObjectStage` over step 385's study with CPL1 uncalibrated `FitStageErr (InstrumentNotCalibratedErr _)`. `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case. Extend the existing fit-run fact to drive every new step 390 case through runFit under both ObjectStage and JointStage. The ideal-CP m00 cases MUST produce LinearStudyEngine runs of rank 1 and one fitted entry. Equality-linked cases MUST produce one fitted entry per independent leader, preserve full parameter snapshots with followers resolved consistently, and produce complete matrices satisfying the links. Use a recording linear proxy that delegates to the real SVD; an unexpected nonlinear solve or an earlier error MUST fail the fact.","acceptance":"After the fit lands, `StudyFitParam.runFit` MUST stage the study, check and read its data, choose and run the engine and answer a `FitRun` stamped by the clock holding the runs, the data hashes, every parameter read and the vector used and produced, writing nothing; with only m33 fixed and the instruments and gains fixed, both object-stage and joint requests MUST automatically run the linear solver, recover the fifteen free coefficients within 1e-9, preserve m33 exactly and record reduced rank 15; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced` and `a fit naming no study of the kit, or refused by its stage, records nothing`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass. Automatic dispatch MUST also complete the ideal-CP m00 and equality-linked fixtures in both requested stages using the real linear solver, recording independent fitted entries, resolved followers and the reduced rank.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests","BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN","S113-ENGINE-CHOICE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a fit naming no study of the kit, or refused by its stage, records nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitRequest","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitParam","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitParam.runFit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S113-FIT-RUN"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number":392,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S113m","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[391],"how_to":"The staged hand-off, end to end over the engines (001 §L 'staged: stage 1 calibrates items on Calibration runs …; Publish calibration; stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with σ'; the S11.3 brief 'Publish calibration (S11.5's revision write) then feeds stage 2' and its test 'the staged hand-off fixes the stage-1 values'). The publish is the item revision write `Item.publishRevision` (step 235), which S11.5's `PublishCalibration` performs with each value's sigma from S11.4's results; these facts publish with a test-local sigma. No product code changes. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over steps 389 and 390's fixture with the five instrument parameters unknown, the AIR Calibration runs, the Dark run and QZ's Science runs in one study, each fit through `runFit` (step 391) with `createMathNetSvd ()`: `publishing stage one fixes the instruments' values for stage two`: `ObjectStage` first answers `FitStageErr (InstrumentNotCalibratedErr _)`; `CalibrationStage` answers a `LinearStudyEngine` run s1 whose five entries hold the instruments' values; each instrument's `publishRevision` of its s1 entries as `CalibratedParameter { value = <the fitted value>; sigma = ParameterSigma 1.0e-6; fitRun = s1.name }`, recorded into the context's items, then `ObjectStage` with `CalibrationHeldFixed` answers a `LinearStudyEngine` run s2 whose `parameters` hold each instrument parameter as exactly that calibration, whose entries are QZ's sixteen alone, and whose fitted values are within 1e-9 of M_QZ; `as priors, stage two frees the published calibration with its priors for the nonlinear engine`: over the published items, the staged study of `ObjectStage` with `CalibrationAsPrior` (step 385) is `NonlinearStudyEngine` by `engineWith` (step 386), and its layout (step 372) holds, beside QZ's sixteen, each published instrument parameter as an entry starting at its s1 value within ± 5.0e-5 with the prior of that value and sigma 1.0e-6.","acceptance":"After the hand-off facts land, a published stage-1 run MUST fix the instruments' values in stage 2 and free them with their priors under `CalibrationAsPrior`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `publishing stage one fixes the instruments' values for stage two` and `as priors, stage two frees the published calibration with its priors for the nonlinear engine`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.publishing stage one fixes the instruments' values for stage two","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-HAND-OFF"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.as priors, stage two frees the published calibration with its priors for the nonlinear engine","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S113-HAND-OFF"]}],"contracts":[],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number": 393, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S113n", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [392], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests"], "how_to": "A fit runs off the UI thread on `JobRunner` with per-iteration progress and Cancel, and its fit run is written on completion only (001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`, with progress and cancel; the fit run is written on completion'; 001 §P `RunFit`; the S11.3 brief; .spec-md §10.2 'one fit iteration … Each shows a progress bar with Cancel, through JobRunner', §10.3 'Fits … are one click with Cancel', §10.4 'The job's completion message updates the Elmish model, so the fit-run history … re-render[s] without a manual reload'). It hosts the fit as step 200 hosts an archive job, over `JobRunner.fs:startBackground`, `:updateJob` and `:JobModel`; the study view that sends `RunFit` and binds this state is S11.5's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `StudyEngine.fs`: `StudyFitError` gains `FitRunKitErr of error : KitError` (`the kit refused the fit run: <the error's describe>`) and `FitRunRaisedErr of reason : string` (`the fit raised: <reason>`). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob`, compiled directly after `KitArchiveJob.fs` (step 200), before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`, no comment. In order: (a) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitJobHandle = { cancelStudyFit : unit -> unit }`. (b) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitJobHost = { startStudyFit : (IterationWatch -> Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>) -> StudyFitJobHandle }`, with `static member posting (post : (unit -> unit) -> unit) (progressed : JobProgress -> unit) (ended : Result<FitRun, StudyFitError> -> unit) : StudyFitJobHost`: a `CancellationTokenSource` and a `Stopwatch` per job; the fit runs through `JobRunner.startBackground` as `RanToCompletion [ fit (WatchedIterations o) ]`, `o` reporting each iteration count k as `post (fun () -> progressed { completed = JobStepCount k.value; total = None; elapsed = JobElapsed <the stopwatch's elapsed> })` (an iteration count with no known total, `JobRunner.fs:JobProgress`, which `progressText` shows as `<k> iterations (<t> s)…`) over the source's token; its `onDone` posts `ended` of the fit's result, a raise (`Error (JobRunExn e)`) ending as `Error (FitRunRaisedErr e.Message)` and an outcome holding no result as `Error (FitRunRaisedErr <a reason naming it>)`; the handle cancels the source. `static member onUiThread (progressed) (ended) : StudyFitJobHost` is `posting` through Avalonia's `Dispatcher.UIThread.Post`, the host a window composes. (c) `StudyFitJobState = { job : JobModel<FitRunName>; handleOpt : StudyFitJobHandle option; errorOpt : StudyFitError option }` with `static member idle` (`initModel`, no handle, no error): the one fit a surface runs, whose committed result is the last fit run written. (d) `StudyFitMsg` = `RunFit of request : StudyFitRequest` (the semantic message the Run joint / Run stage buttons and the tests send, 001 §P) | `CancelStudyFit` | `StudyFitProgressed of progress : JobProgress` | `StudyFitEnded of result : Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>`, each case documented. (e) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyFitEnvironment = { host : StudyFitJobHost; fitWith : StudyFitRequest -> IterationWatch -> Result<FitRun, StudyFitError>; kit : KitProxy }`, with `static member create (host : StudyFitJobHost) (kit : KitProxy) (forward : StudyForwardContext) (clock : ClockProvider) : StudyFitEnvironment`, whose `fitWith request watch` reads `kit.readFitRuns request.study` (step 384, an error `FitRunKitErr`) and answers `{ forward; clock; linearSolver = createMathNetSvd (); deviates = UniformDeviateProvider.fromSeed (NoiseSeed 1); fitRuns }.runFit request watch` (step 391): one fixed seed, so a study refits reproducibly and every run records its starts (step 383). (f) `type StudyFitMsg with member this.updateWith (environment : StudyFitEnvironment) (state : StudyFitJobState) : StudyFitJobState`: `RunFit r` while `state.job.isRunning` changes nothing (one fit at a time), and otherwise starts `environment.fitWith r` through `environment.host.startStudyFit`, the job through `updateJob StartRequested`, holding the handle and clearing the error; `CancelStudyFit` calls the handle's `cancelStudyFit` while the job runs and changes nothing else; `StudyFitProgressed p` is `updateJob (ProgressReported p)`; `StudyFitEnded (Ok run)` writes `environment.kit.writeFitRun run` (step 384), then `updateJob (RunCompleted run.name)` with no handle and no error, or, when the kit refuses (an existing name is `FitRunExistsErr`, a read-only kit `KitReadOnlyErr`), returns the job to `Idle` with its committed result kept and holds `FitRunKitErr`; `StudyFitEnded (Error (FitCancelledErr _))` is `updateJob RunCancelled` with no handle, nothing written; any other error returns the job to `Idle`, its committed result kept, and holds the error. This is the only place a fit run is written. No queue, retry, second job or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs`, `module StudyFitJobTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over `KitProxy.createInMemory` of an initialised `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 125), a host `posting` whose `post` calls at once and whose `progressed` and `ended` feed `StudyFitProgressed` and `StudyFitEnded` back through `updateWith`, test-local `fitWith` stubs answering step 384's test-local fit run, and waits on a `ManualResetEventSlim` with a ten-second limit, never a sleep: `RunFit reports each iteration, then writes the fit run once the fit completes`: a stub reporting iterations 1, 2 and 3 through its watch then answering the run leaves the state `Completed` with that name committed, its last progress `completed` 3 with no total and a progress text starting `3 iterations`, and `readFitRuns` answering the run; `a cancelled fit writes nothing and keeps the last committed fit run`: after a completed first run, a stub that waits until its watch's cancellation is requested and answers `FitCancelledErr`, sent `CancelStudyFit`, leaves the state `Cancelled` with the first name still committed and one fit-run file; `a fit run that would overwrite an existing one is refused and nothing is written`: with the run's name already written, the end holds `FitRunKitErr (FitRunExistsErr _)`, the job `Idle`, and the file's bytes are unchanged; `a fit that raises ends with FitRunRaisedErr carrying its message`: a stub raising `InvalidOperationException \"solver gone\"` ends with `FitRunRaisedErr` whose reason holds `solver gone`; `RunFit while a fit runs starts nothing`: a second `RunFit` while the first stub waits starts no second fit (the stub is called once). `StudyEngineTests`' `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After the job lands, `RunFit` MUST run the fit off the UI thread through `JobRunner.startBackground` with per-iteration progress and Cancel, and `StudyFitEnded` MUST write the fit run once on completion and nothing on cancel or error; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RunFit reports each iteration, then writes the fit run once the fit completes`, `a cancelled fit writes nothing and keeps the last committed fit run`, `a fit run that would overwrite an existing one is refused and nothing is written`, `a fit that raises ends with FitRunRaisedErr carrying its message` and `RunFit while a fit runs starts nothing`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests.RunFit reports each iteration, then writes the fit run once the fit completes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests.a cancelled fit writes nothing and keeps the last committed fit run", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests.a fit run that would overwrite an existing one is refused and nothing is written", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests.a fit that raises ends with FitRunRaisedErr carrying its message", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests.RunFit while a fit runs starts nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyFitJobTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob.StudyFitJobHandle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob.StudyFitJobHost", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob.StudyFitJobState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob.StudyFitMsg", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob.StudyFitEnvironment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob.StudyFitMsg.updateWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs", "obligations": ["S113-FIT-JOB"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.3 -- Engines, staged and joint fits, and append-only fit runs"}
{"number": 394, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [393], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests"], "how_to": "A fit's results report the rank of each solve's residual Jacobian, and the linear solves' results read the residual of their solution row by row (001 §L 'Results, stored in the fit run: … correlation matrix, rank, condition; per-experiment residuals and RMSE'; the S11.4 brief 'the correlation matrix, the rank and the condition, through the MuellerInverse.ResidualJacobian carrier'). The carrier has the condition, the column norms and the correlation, but no rank. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs`: `ResidualJacobian` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualJacobian`) gains, after `conditionNumber` (`MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber`), `member this.rank : MatrixRank` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixRank`): the count of its singular values above 1.0e-6 times the largest, taken through the same `RealMatrix.create` seam and `Svd(false)` `conditionNumber` uses; `MatrixRank 0` for an empty Jacobian or one whose largest singular value is not above zero. Its doc says why the floor is relative and where it sits: two orders above the noise of a forward-difference Jacobian taken at ALGLIB's own step (about 1e-8 of a column), so two columns that agree only to that noise, an exactly confounded pair, count once, while a direction ten thousand times weaker than the strongest still counts. No other member of the carrier changes. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: `LeastSquaresSystem` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`) gains, before `residualRmseAt` (step 352), `member this.residualsAt (solution : RealVector) : RealVector`: `RealMatrix.create` of its design rows' values times `solution`, less `RealVector.create` of `rhs`, the difference `residualRmseAt` takes the norm of; `residualRmseAt` becomes `(this.residualsAt solution).norm` over `sqrt` of the row count, the same operations in the same order, so the RMSE `createMathNetSvd` reports through it (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:createMathNetSvd`) and the product check's (step 352) are the same doubles. No other declaration of either file changes. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs`, `module FitResultsTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, the home of S11.4's facts over the result shapes and synthetic least-squares problems: `a Jacobian's rank counts the directions its data constrains, above forward-difference noise`: the rank of `ResidualJacobian` of the rows [1; 0], [0; 1], [1; 1] is 2; of [1; 1], [2; 2], [3; 3] is 1; of [1; 1 + 1e-9], [2; 2 − 1e-9], [3; 3 + 2e-9] (columns proportional to a part in 1e9) is 1; of [1; 0], [0; 1e-4] is 2; and of no row is 0. `the residuals of a solution over a least-squares system are its design times the solution less its right-hand side`: the system of design rows [1; 0], [0; 1], [1; 1] and right-hand side [0.1; 2.1; 1.9] at the solution [0; 2] has `residualsAt` [−0.1; −0.1; 0.1] and `residualRmseAt` 0.1, each within 1e-15. `MuellerReconstructionTests` (the RMSE `createMathNetSvd` and the product check report) and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (the cheapest class reading a `ResidualJacobian`, through `residualJacobianAt`, step 336) run unchanged, their numbers bit-identical.", "acceptance": "After the rank and the residuals land, `ResidualJacobian.rank` MUST count the singular values above 1.0e-6 of the largest and `LeastSquaresSystem.residualsAt` MUST answer A·x − b, the difference `residualRmseAt` reads; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a Jacobian's rank counts the directions its data constrains, above forward-difference noise` and `the residuals of a solution over a least-squares system are its design times the solution less its right-hand side`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over `MuellerReconstructionTests` and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` with their numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.a Jacobian's rank counts the directions its data constrains, above forward-difference noise", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-JACOBIAN-RANK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.the residuals of a solution over a least-squares system are its design times the solution less its right-hand side", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-JACOBIAN-RANK"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.ResidualJacobian.rank", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S114-JACOBIAN-RANK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.LeastSquaresSystem.residualsAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S114-JACOBIAN-RANK"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number": 395, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [394], "how_to": "Which fitted parameters are suspect, and so are profiled, is decided by two thresholds stated in the study's fit settings (the S11.4 brief 'post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood, for parameters flagged suspect (correlation or sigma above thresholds stated in the fit settings)'; 001 §L 'fit settings'). They are study data, stored in the study file beside the mode and the start count (step 382), not an application setting (.spec-md §8 'configuration knobs'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. (1) `Studies.fs`, before `StudyFitSettings` (steps 358, 382): `FitCorrelation of float` with `.value`, a correlation coefficient between two fitted parameters, which the results read both as a measured correlation and as its threshold; `SigmaFraction of float` with `.value`, a parameter's standard deviation over the span of its bounds; and `SuspectThresholds = { correlation : FitCorrelation; sigmaFraction : SigmaFraction }`, a fitted parameter being suspect when its correlation with another exceeds `correlation` in magnitude or its sigma exceeds `sigmaFraction` of its bounds' span, with `static member initial` holding 0.95 and 0.1 and `static member tryCreate (correlation : float) (sigmaFraction : float) : Result<SuspectThresholds, StudyError>`, which keeps a correlation in (0, 1] and a finite fraction above 0 and refuses anything else, NaN included, with the new `InvalidSuspectThresholdErr` naming the value. `StudyFitSettings` gains `suspect : SuspectThresholds` as its last field, after `starts`, and `StudyFitSettings.initial` holds `SuspectThresholds.initial`; `type Study with member this.withSuspectThresholds (thresholds : SuspectThresholds) : Study` sets it in place, beside `withFitStarts` (step 382). `StudyError` gains `InvalidSuspectThresholdErr of reason : string`, rendered `the suspect thresholds are not valid: <reason>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json` (steps 359, 382): under version 1, `settings` holds exactly `mode`, `experimentWeights`, `detectorWeights`, `disabled`, `starts` and `suspect`, an object holding exactly `correlation`, a number above 0 and at most 1, and `sigmaFraction`, a number above 0. The serializer writes both as numbers; no converter is added. There are no up-converters: a study file without `suspect` is refused by its schema (.spec-md §4 'Stored formats'), and the kits that exist are written after this step (S12). (3) Every record expression that spells out a `StudyFitSettings` in the tests gains `suspect = SuspectThresholds.initial`, and nothing else changes. Tests: in `StudyTests`, `suspect thresholds keep a correlation in zero to one and a positive sigma fraction, and a study's are set in place`: `tryCreate 0.9 0.2` keeps both; a correlation of 0, −0.5, 1.5 or NaN and a fraction of 0, −0.1, NaN or infinity each answer `InvalidSuspectThresholdErr`; `StudyFitSettings.initial.suspect` holds 0.95 and 0.1; and `withSuspectThresholds` of 0.9 and 0.2 leaves the mode, the weights, the disabled runs and the starts as they were. In `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 359), `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`'s study holds the thresholds 0.9 and 0.2 and reads them back, and `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds` also refuses a `settings` without `suspect`, a `suspect.correlation` of 1.5 and a `suspect.sigmaFraction` of 0 with `SchemaValidationErr`. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.", "acceptance": "After the thresholds land, `StudyFitSettings.suspect` MUST hold a correlation in (0, 1] and a positive sigma fraction, 0.95 and 0.1 initially, written and read in the study file under its schema; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `suspect thresholds keep a correlation in zero to one and a positive sigma fraction, and a study's are set in place`, the count rising by 1, and the widened `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds` and `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.suspect thresholds keep a correlation in zero to one and a positive sigma fraction, and a study's are set in place", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.FitCorrelation", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SigmaFraction", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SuspectThresholds", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withSuspectThresholds", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyFitSettings", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S114-SUSPECT-THRESHOLDS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number":396,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S114c","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[395],"how_to":"What a fit run records as its results (001 §L 'Results, stored in the fit run: value ± σ (Jacobian covariance; FitQuality REUSED); correlation matrix, rank, condition; per-experiment residuals and RMSE; Mueller realizability (coherency eigenvalues ≥ 0); the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ); post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood for suspect parameters'; step 383: 'S11.4 adds the results'). The shapes come first; steps 397-403 fill them and step 404 stores them in the fit run. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4, every case name has two words and no `bool` appears. In `FitRuns.fs` (step 383), after `ObjectMatrixFit` and before `FitRun`, in this order: (1) `FitEntryRef = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; owner : UnknownOwner }` (steps 358, 362), one entry of the fitted vector as `FitRunEntry` names it. (2) `FitCoordinate` = `EntryCoordinate of entries : FitEntryRef list` (the entries one coordinate of a solve is the value of: one in the nonlinear and object solves, every entry taking that stage-one constant in a calibration fit) | `ElementCoordinate of row : MuellerRowIndex * column : MuellerColumnIndex` (an element of a series' combined matrix, which no entry holds; `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerRowIndex`, `:MuellerColumnIndex`) | `FringeVisibilityCoordinate` (the free visibility of the LP-LP AIR fringe, which stage one fits and no entry holds). (3) `FitProblemSubject` = `StudyEntriesProblem` (the nonlinear fit of the study residual and its priors) | `ObjectSolveProblem of items : ItemId list` (one linear object solve, a series' combined matrix when it names more than one item) | `AirFringeProblem of runs : ExperimentName list` (one stage-one AIR fringe fit of those runs). (4) Two `NumericCarrier`s, each a single-case union with `.value`: `JacobianColumnNorms of float[]` (a solve's Jacobian column norms, read whole from the `ResidualJacobian` carrier) and `CorrelationMatrix of float[][]` (a solve's parameter correlation matrix, read whole from the same carrier). (5) `FitProblemQuality = { subject : FitProblemSubject; coordinates : FitCoordinate list; rank : MatrixRank; conditionOpt : ConditionNumber option; columnNorms : JacobianColumnNorms; correlationOpt : CorrelationMatrix option; chiSquared : FitChiSquared; rmse : ResidualRmse }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixRank`, `:ResidualRmse`; `MuellerInverse.fs:ConditionNumber`): one solve's identifiability in its own coordinates (the nonlinear fit's scaled ones), the condition and the correlation present only where its Jacobian has full rank. (6) `FitEntrySigma = { entry : FitEntryRef; sigmaOpt : ParameterSigma option }` (step 214), one value's ± σ, `None` where its solve leaves it undetermined. (7) `RunResidual = { run : ExperimentName; residuals : ResidualVector; rmse : ResidualRmse }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualVector`), one fitted run's residual entries in the units of the solve that fitted it, and their root mean square. (8) `MuellerRealizability` = `RealizableMueller` | `UnrealizableMueller` (derived, never stored, so it carries no tag) and `ObjectRealizability = { item : ItemId; eigenvalues : CoherencyEigenvalue list }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:CoherencyEigenvalue`), one black-box object's four Cloude coherency eigenvalues at its fitted values, with `member this.realizability : MuellerRealizability`: `RealizableMueller` when every eigenvalue is at least −1.0e-12 times their sum (the coherency matrix's trace, its m₀₀), a round-off allowance on the positive semi-definite test `MuellerInverse.fs:cloudeEigenvalues` documents (a matrix is physically realizable if and only if no eigenvalue is negative), else `UnrealizableMueller`. (9) `SeriesProductCheck = { items : ItemId list; cascade : ParameterValue list; difference : MatrixDiff; fitRmse : ResidualRmse; productRmse : ResidualRmse }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixDiff`): a series' combined matrix against the cascade of its objects' own matrices, the cascade's sixteen elements row-major, step 352's readouts. (10) `SuspectReason` = `UndeterminedSigmaReason` (its solve leaves its σ undetermined) | `WideSigmaReason of fraction : SigmaFraction` (its σ over its bounds' span, past the threshold) | `CorrelatedEntryReason of partner : FitEntryRef * correlation : FitCorrelation` (its correlation with that entry, past the threshold) (step 395). (11) `ProfileOutcome` = `ProfileConverged of chiSquared : FitChiSquared` | `ProfileFailed of failure : FitMemberFailure` (step 383); `ProfilePoint = { value : ParameterValue; outcome : ProfileOutcome }`, one re-fit with the parameter held at `value`; and `ParameterProfile = { entry : FitEntryRef; reasons : SuspectReason list; points : ProfilePoint list }`, a suspect entry's χ² profile. (12) `FitRunResults = { sigmas : FitEntrySigma list; problems : FitProblemQuality list; runResiduals : RunResidual list; realizability : ObjectRealizability list; productChecks : SeriesProductCheck list; profiles : ParameterProfile list }`, a fit's results. The unions carrying payloads are stored in the serializer's case form, as `FitMemberOutcome` is (step 383); none carries a wire tag. No other type or member is added: the file form is step 404's. Tests, in `FitResultsTests`: `a fitted Mueller matrix is realizable when no coherency eigenvalue is negative beyond round-off`: an `ObjectRealizability` of `Propagation.identityMueller`'s `cloudeEigenvalues` and of `(MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller (Angle.degree 30.0<deg>) (Retardance.degree 40.0<deg>)).cloudeEigenvalues` is `RealizableMueller`; of the diagonal Mueller matrix diag(1, 1.5, 0, 0), whose eigenvalues are 0.625, 0.625, −0.125 and −0.125, `UnrealizableMueller`; and of the literal eigenvalues 1, 0, 0 and −1e-14 `RealizableMueller`, of 1, 0, 0 and −1e-6 `UnrealizableMueller`.","acceptance":"After the shapes land, `FitRuns.fs` MUST declare the coordinate, subject, solve-quality, sigma, run-residual, realizability, product-check, suspect-reason and profile shapes and `FitRunResults`, and `ObjectRealizability.realizability` MUST flag a coherency eigenvalue negative beyond round-off; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fitted Mueller matrix is realizable when no coherency eigenvalue is negative beyond round-off`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.a fitted Mueller matrix is realizable when no coherency eigenvalue is negative beyond round-off","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitEntryRef","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitCoordinate","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitProblemSubject","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.JacobianColumnNorms","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.CorrelationMatrix","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitProblemQuality","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitEntrySigma","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.RunResidual","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.MuellerRealizability","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.ObjectRealizability","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.ObjectRealizability.realizability","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.SeriesProductCheck","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.SuspectReason","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.ProfileOutcome","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.ProfilePoint","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.ParameterProfile","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRunResults","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs","obligations":["S114-RESULT-SHAPES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number": 397, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [396], "how_to": "Every engine's results are read the same way off each least-squares solve it made: its residual Jacobian and covariance through `FitQuality` (REUSED; the S11.4 brief 'value +/- sigma from the Jacobian covariance (REUSE FitQuality.FitReport / standardErrors)'), its rank, condition, column norms and correlation through the `ResidualJacobian` carrier (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualJacobian`, step 394), and a suspect coordinate's χ² profile by re-fitting the solve with that coordinate held (the brief 're-fit with the parameter stepped across its sigma range, and record the chi-squared profile'). One record serves the nonlinear fit (step 399), the object solves (step 400) and the calibration fits (step 401). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. New `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs`, `module FittedProblems` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `StagedMuellerPath.fs` and before `StudyEngine.fs` (steps 349, 386): one `<Compile Include=\"FittedProblems.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one line: the least-squares solves a fit's results are read from, and their profiles (spec 0050 S11.4). In this order: (1) `type IterationWatch with member this.after (earlier : IterationCount) : IterationWatch` (step 380): `UnwatchedIterations` stays unwatched, and `WatchedIterations o` becomes a watch telling `o.reportIteration` of `earlier` plus each count it is told, over `o.cancellation`. It is the rule `fitNonlinear` applies to each multi-start member (step 387), MOVED here: `fitNonlinear`'s members call `watch.after` of the earlier members' iterations in its place, so every count it reports is unchanged. (2) `FitCoordinateIndex of int` with `.value`, the position of one coordinate in a solve. (3) `FitProfileError`, an `*Error` union: `ProfileCancelledErr of reason : string`, with `member this.describe : string` rendering `the profile re-fits were cancelled: <reason>`. (4) `ProfileRun = { points : ProfilePoint list; iterations : IterationCount }` (step 396): one coordinate's profile and the iterations its re-fits took. (5) `[<ReferenceEquality>] FittedProblem = { subject : FitProblemSubject; coordinates : FitCoordinate list; residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector; search : ScaledSearch; centre : StudyParameterVector; unit : StudyParameterVector }` (steps 381, 372, 396): one solve, `search.start` the solution it reached and its bounds the box it kept to, coordinate k standing for the physical value centreₖ + unitₖ · sₖ (the nonlinear fit's scaling, step 387; a zero centre and a unit scale for the linear and calibration solves). Its members: (a) `member this.jacobian : ResidualJacobian`: `FitQuality.residualJacobian` (`FitQuality.fs:residualJacobian`) of the offset residual y ↦ residual (start + y − 100) at the vector of hundreds, so FitQuality's relative step, √ε · max(|x|, 1e-12), is about 1.5e-6 in the solve's own coordinates, the order of the 1e-6 step ALGLIB's own solve differentiates with (`AlglibAdapter.fs:runLm`, its `minlmcreatev`), and a coordinate at zero is still perturbed; the doc says so in one line. (b) `member this.report : FitQuality.FitReport`: `FitQuality.reportFrom` (`FitQuality.fs:reportFrom`) of the same offset residual at the vector of hundreds with `residual start` as its final residuals, read for its standard errors only (its parameters are the offset frame's). (c) `member this.quality : FitProblemQuality`: the subject and the coordinates; `jacobian.rank` (step 394); `jacobian.conditionNumber` and `jacobian.correlation` (`MuellerInverse.fs:conditionNumber`, `:correlation`), each `Some` only when the rank equals the coordinate count and the condition is finite; `jacobian.columnNorms` as `JacobianColumnNorms`; `FitChiSquared` of `(residual start).sumOfSquares` (`OptimizationInterface.fs:sumOfSquares`); and the RMSE √(χ² / rows), zero for no row. (d) `member this.sigmaAt (coordinate : FitCoordinateIndex) : ParameterSigma option`: unitₖ times the report's standard error k when the rank equals the coordinate count and the product is finite, else `None`. (e) `member this.entrySigmas : FitEntrySigma list`: for each `EntryCoordinate` in order, each of its entries with that coordinate's `sigmaAt`. (f) `member this.profileAt (coordinate : FitCoordinateIndex) (earlier : IterationCount) (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<ProfileRun, FitProfileError>`: with `sigmaAt` `Some σ`, the seven physical values x̂ + j · σ for j = −3 … 3, x̂ the coordinate's physical value at `start`, each whose scaled value lies outside the coordinate's bounds left out, and the point at j = 0 `ProfileConverged` of the solve's own χ² with no re-fit; with `None`, seven values evenly spaced across the coordinate's bounds, lower to upper, and none when a bound is infinite. Every other point is a re-fit: the coordinate held at the point's scaled value and the others searched from their `start` within their bounds by `ScaledSearch.solveWith` (step 381) under `watch.after` of `earlier` plus the iterations of the re-fits before it, `Ok s` being `ProfileConverged` of `s.finalResiduals.sumOfSquares` and `Error e` `ProfileFailed e.failureText` (step 383); a solve with no other coordinate has nothing to re-fit, and its point is the residual at the held vector. A requested cancellation, read before each re-fit and after it as `fitNonlinear` reads it (step 387), answers `ProfileCancelledErr` naming the coordinate and the points done. `iterations` counts every re-fit's. No cache, retry, threshold or option is added: which coordinates are profiled is step 402's. Tests, in `FitResultsTests`, over test-local `FittedProblem`s whose residual is `ResidualVector` of `system.residualsAt` (step 394) of a test-local least-squares system, centre zero, unit one and unbounded (`infinity`, `OptimizationInterface.fs:ParameterBounds`) unless stated: `a fitted problem's Jacobian, sigmas, correlation, rank and condition are those of its least-squares design`: the system of design rows [1; 0], [0; 1], [1; 1] and right-hand side [0.1; 2.1; 1.9], solved at [0; 2], has a Jacobian of columns [1; 0; 1] and [0; 1; 1] within 1e-6, both `sigmaAt` √0.02 within 1e-6 relative (√(χ² / (m − n) · (AᵀA)⁻¹ₖₖ) with χ² 0.03), a correlation of −0.5 and a condition of √3, each within 1e-6, rank 2, χ² 0.03 and RMSE 0.1 within 1e-12, and with unit 2 at coordinate 0 a `sigmaAt` there of 2√0.02; `a problem whose Jacobian is rank-deficient has no sigma, correlation or condition`: the rows [1; 1], [2; 2], [3; 3] with right-hand side [1; 2; 3.1], solved at its least-squares point x₀ = x₁ = 14.3 / 28, have rank 1, no σ, no correlation and no condition; `a linear problem's profile rises by the reduced chi-squared times the step squared, within the coordinate's bounds`: `profileAt` coordinate 0 of the first system answers seven points at j · √0.02 whose χ² is 0.03 · (1 + j²) within 1e-9 relative, the middle one without a re-fit, and with coordinate 0's lower bound at −0.3 the point at −3√0.02 is left out; `a sigma-less profile steps across the coordinate's bounds and is flat along a confounded direction`: `profileAt` coordinate 0 of the second system, coordinate 0 within [−1, 1] and coordinate 1 within [−2, 3], answers seven points at −1, −2/3, …, 1, each χ² equal to the solve's within 1e-9 relative; `a cancelled profile answers ProfileCancelledErr, and a watch after earlier iterations counts on from them`: under a watch whose `CancellationTokenSource` is already cancelled, `profileAt` answers `ProfileCancelledErr`; `(WatchedIterations o).after (IterationCount 5)` tells `o` 6 and 7 when told 1 and 2; and `UnwatchedIterations.after (IterationCount 5)` matches `UnwatchedIterations`. `StudyEngineTests`' facts over `fitNonlinear` (step 387) run unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the fitted problem lands, `FittedProblem` MUST give a solve's Jacobian and FitQuality report about a frame offset by one hundred, its rank, condition, column norms and correlation, its σ in physical units, and its profiles by held re-fits under the fit's watch, and `fitNonlinear` MUST count its members' iterations through `IterationWatch.after`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fitted problem's Jacobian, sigmas, correlation, rank and condition are those of its least-squares design`, `a problem whose Jacobian is rank-deficient has no sigma, correlation or condition`, `a linear problem's profile rises by the reduced chi-squared times the step squared, within the coordinate's bounds`, `a sigma-less profile steps across the coordinate's bounds and is flat along a confounded direction` and `a cancelled profile answers ProfileCancelledErr, and a watch after earlier iterations counts on from them`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.a fitted problem's Jacobian, sigmas, correlation, rank and condition are those of its least-squares design", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.a problem whose Jacobian is rank-deficient has no sigma, correlation or condition", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.a linear problem's profile rises by the reduced chi-squared times the step squared, within the coordinate's bounds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.a sigma-less profile steps across the coordinate's bounds and is flat along a confounded direction", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests.a cancelled profile answers ProfileCancelledErr, and a watch after earlier iterations counts on from them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/FitResultsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.FitResultsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.IterationWatch.after", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FitCoordinateIndex", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FitProfileError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.ProfileRun", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FittedProblem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FittedProblem.jacobian", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FittedProblem.report", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FittedProblem.quality", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FittedProblem.sigmaAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FittedProblem.entrySigmas", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FittedProblems.FittedProblem.profileAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FittedProblems.fs", "obligations": ["S114-FITTED-PROBLEMS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number": 398, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [397], "how_to": "Stage one fits each AIR trace by two cosine coefficients (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:freeCosineFit`; the LP-frame fit of step 349 read through `MuellerReconstruction.fs:sourceCplFromLpFrame`), but a calibration's results are wanted in the instruments' own constants, the values step 389 writes, so that each gets its σ, correlation and profile like any other fitted parameter (001 §L 'value ± σ'; S11.5 publishes each calibrated value with its σ, 001 §I). The same two cosine models are written here in those constants: a reparameterisation that is one-to-one on the physical branch, so each fit's minimum and residual are unchanged and FitQuality's covariance in the constants is the propagated one, with no second formula for it. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs` (steps 349, 388): (1) `reduceAirTraces` (step 349; its AIR-label filter gone since step 388) becomes public, its body unchanged: the AIR trace of capture rows, averaged per dial reading, dark-subtracted and normalised per experiment label, which stage one fits and S11.4's per-run residuals read. (2) After it, `type AirTrace with member this.fringeResidualAt (zero : Angle) (visibility : FringeVisibility) : ResidualVector` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:AirTrace`, `:FringeVisibility`): entry i is V · cos 2(αᵢ − z) − (normᵢ − 1), αᵢ the trace's dial angle read in degrees as `freeCosineFit` reads it. This is `freeCosineFit`'s model p · cos 2α + q · sin 2α − (norm − 1) at the zero and visibility it reports, p = V cos 2z and q = V sin 2z. (3) `type SourceCplModel with member this.lpFrameResidualOn (trace : AirTrace) (lpZero : Angle) : ResidualVector` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:SourceCplModel`): entry i is q_LP · cos 2(αᵢ − z_LP) + u_LP · sin 2(αᵢ − z_LP) − (normᵢ − 1), the LP-frame fit's model phased on `lpZero`, with 1 − q_LP = (1 − cos δ) · sin² 2θ and u_LP = (1 − cos δ) · sin 2θ · cos 2θ for θ its `thetaRel` and δ its `retardance`. These are the coefficients `sourceCplFromLpFrame` reads back as this model wherever 0° < θ < 90°, its physical branch (its doc: '2θ = atan2(1 − qLp, uLp)', 'cosδ = 1 − (1 − qLp) / sin²2θ'); the doc names the branch. No other declaration changes. Tests, in `StagedMuellerPathTests` (step 349), over test-local `AirTrace`s at the dial angles 0° to 160° by 20°: `an AIR trace's fringe residual at its cosine fit's zero and visibility is that fit's residual`: with normᵢ − 1 = 0.54 · cos 2αᵢ − 0.62 · sin 2αᵢ + 0.01 · (−1)ⁱ, `freeCosineFit (createMathNetSvd ())` answers a zero and a visibility whose `fringeResidualAt` equals, entry by entry within 1e-12, the fit's design times its coefficients less (norm − 1), the coefficients recomputed in the test as V cos 2z and V sin 2z, and whose root mean square is the fit's `rmse` within 1e-12; `an LP-frame residual vanishes on the trace of the source model sourceCplFromLpFrame reads`: with normᵢ − 1 = 0.16 · cos 2(αᵢ − 155°) + 0.17 · sin 2(αᵢ − 155°), `(sourceCplFromLpFrame (CosineCoefficient 0.16) (CosineCoefficient 0.17)).lpFrameResidualOn trace (Angle.degree 155.0<deg>)` is zero within 1e-12 in every entry; `the AIR trace of two experiments' rows is each experiment's trace in turn`: `reduceAirTraces` of two experiments' AIR rows is the trace of the first experiment's rows followed by the second's, angle for angle and value for value. `MuellerReconstructionTests` runs unchanged, every number bit-identical.", "acceptance": "After the fringes land, `reduceAirTraces` MUST be public and unchanged, `AirTrace.fringeResidualAt` MUST be the free cosine fit's residual in the zero and visibility it reports, and `SourceCplModel.lpFrameResidualOn` the LP-frame fit's residual in the source model it reads back; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an AIR trace's fringe residual at its cosine fit's zero and visibility is that fit's residual`, `an LP-frame residual vanishes on the trace of the source model sourceCplFromLpFrame reads` and `the AIR trace of two experiments' rows is each experiment's trace in turn`, the count rising by 3; unit-tests MUST pass over `MuellerReconstructionTests` with every number unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.an AIR trace's fringe residual at its cosine fit's zero and visibility is that fit's residual", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-AIR-FRINGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.an LP-frame residual vanishes on the trace of the source model sourceCplFromLpFrame reads", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-AIR-FRINGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the AIR trace of two experiments' rows is each experiment's trace in turn", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-AIR-FRINGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.reduceAirTraces", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S114-AIR-FRINGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.AirTrace.fringeResidualAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S114-AIR-FRINGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.SourceCplModel.lpFrameResidualOn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S114-AIR-FRINGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number": 399, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [398], "how_to": "The nonlinear fit's results are read off the study residual it minimised (step 387), over the scaled coordinates it searched, and each fitted run's residual is the study residual over that run alone (001 §L 'per-experiment residuals and RMSE'; the S11.4 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `reconstructLinear` (step 390) and before `StudyFitRequest` (step 391): (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] EngineProblems = { problems : FittedProblem list; runResiduals : RunResidual list; productChecks : SeriesProductCheck list }` (steps 396, 397): what a fit's results are read from, each engine giving its own. (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.nonlinearProblemsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (data : StudyData) (solution : StudyFitSolution) : Result<EngineProblems, StudyFitError>`, for a solution `fitNonlinear` answered (steps 385, 387). Over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items`, the problem `this.scaledProblemWith context data` (step 387, its error as there) gives one `FittedProblem`: `StudyEntriesProblem`; one `EntryCoordinate [ { parameter = e.unknown.parameter; owner = e.owner } ]` per entry `e` of `problem.layout.entries`, in order (step 372); the problem's `residual` (the study residual and one row per prior); its `search` with `start` at entry k (fittedₖ − centreₖ) / unitₖ, `fitted` being `solution.fitted`; and its `centre` and `unit`. `runResiduals` hold, for each run of `data.runs` whose name `this.fittedRuns` holds, in order, `this.study.residualWith context problem.layout { data with runs = [ run ] } solution.fitted` (step 379), that run's weighted entries, with their root mean square (zero for no entry); an error answers `StudyForwardFitErr`. `productChecks` is empty: the nonlinear engine solves no series. No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over step 387's polarimeter study of the opened uniaxial version, fitted by `fitNonlinear` unwatched: `the nonlinear fit's problem is the study residual over its scaled coordinates at the fitted vector`: `nonlinearProblemsWith` answers one `StudyEntriesProblem` whose coordinates are n_o's then n_e's entry, whose residual at its start equals `scaledProblemWith`'s residual at (fitted − centre) / unit within 1e-12, whose quality has rank 2 and a χ² within 1e-12 of the converged member's (step 387), and whose `sigmaAt` k is unitₖ times its report's standard error k; `each run of a nonlinear fit has the study residual over that run alone`: its one `RunResidual` is the plate run's, equal entry by entry within 1e-12 to `residualWith` over a `StudyData` holding that run alone at `solution.fitted`, with the root mean square of those entries.", "acceptance": "After the nonlinear problem lands, `StagedStudy.nonlinearProblemsWith` MUST answer the study residual and its priors over the fit's scaled coordinates at the fitted vector, and each fitted run's residual over that run alone; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the nonlinear fit's problem is the study residual over its scaled coordinates at the fitted vector` and `each run of a nonlinear fit has the study residual over that run alone`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.the nonlinear fit's problem is the study residual over its scaled coordinates at the fitted vector", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-NONLINEAR-PROBLEM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.each run of a nonlinear fit has the study residual over that run alone", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-NONLINEAR-PROBLEM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.EngineProblems", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-NONLINEAR-PROBLEM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.nonlinearProblemsWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-NONLINEAR-PROBLEM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number": 400, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [399], "how_to": "The object stage's results are read off each linear solve it made (step 390): its design over the matrix's sixteen elements, each run's rows within it, and for a series the product check against the cascade of its objects' own solves (001 §L 'the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ)'; the S11.4 brief 'REUSE MuellerReconstruction.cascadeProduct and the RMSE ratio S10.3 computes'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `nonlinearProblemsWith` (step 399): (1) `ObjectRunSystem = { run : ExperimentName; system : LeastSquaresSystem }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`), one run's projected rows, and `ObjectGroupSystem = { items : ItemId list; runs : ObjectRunSystem list }` with `member this.system : LeastSquaresSystem`, `LeastSquaresSystem.concat` of its runs' systems in order (step 388). (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.objectSystemsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) : Result<ObjectGroupSystem list, StudyFitError>`: the projection and grouping of `reconstructLinear` (step 390) MOVED, each run's system `LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections` of its own capture rows' projections (step 388), the groups in the order of their first run, the errors as there. `reconstructLinear` becomes `objectSystemsWith` followed, for each group, by `reconstruct solver group.system` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:reconstruct`) and what it did with each solve. The runs' rows concatenated in run order are the system it solved, row for row, so every number it answers is unchanged. (3) `type ProductCheckData with member this.storedFor (items : ItemId list) : SeriesProductCheck` (step 352): its cascade's `rowMajorValues` (step 390), its difference and its two RMSEs; and `type SeriesProductCheck with member this.rmseRatio : ProductRmseRatio`, `ProductRmseRatio.between this.productRmse this.fitRmse` (step 352), the one place the stored check's ratio is formed. (4) `type StagedStudy with member this.objectProblemsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) : Result<EngineProblems, StudyFitError>`, for a solution `reconstructLinear` answered. Over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items` and its layout (step 372), `objectSystemsWith`, then each group's `reconstruct solver group.system` (an error `ObjectSolveFitErr` as in step 390) gives one `FittedProblem` (step 397): `ObjectSolveProblem group.items`; sixteen coordinates in the solve's own order, k = 4c + r for the element (r, c) (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:vecColumnMajor`), each, for a group of one item, `EntryCoordinate [ <the layout entry of that item's m<r><c>, with its ItemOwner> ]` and, for a series, `ElementCoordinate (MuellerRowIndex r, MuellerColumnIndex c)`; the residual s ↦ `ResidualVector` of `group.system.residualsAt` s (step 394); a `search` starting at the solved matrix's `vecColumnMajor`, within each entry's unknown bounds for one item and unbounded (`infinity`, `OptimizationInterface.fs:ParameterBounds`) for a series; centre zero and unit one. `runResiduals` hold, run by run in study order, each run's own `system.residualsAt` its group's solution, with their root mean square. `productChecks` hold, for each group of two or more items, in order, whose every item has a group of its own, `productCheckOf later first series group.system` (step 352) stored for `group.items`: `first` the first item's own matrix, `later` the cascade of the others' own matrices in light order (for [i₁; i₂; …; iₖ], `cascadeProduct` of each next one onto the product so far, so that `productCheckOf`'s `cascadeProduct later first` is Mₖ ⋯ M₂ · M₁, for [QZ; LR] exactly M_LR · M_QZ, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:cascadeProduct`), and `series` the group's own solve. No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over step 390's fixture: `an object solve's problem is its design over the matrix's elements, each coordinate an entry of the object`: QZ's problem is `ObjectSolveProblem [ QZ ]`, its coordinate 4c + r QZ's `m<r><c>` entry, its start equal to QZ's fitted entries in that order exactly, and its quality of rank 16 with a condition within 1e-6 relative of `(ResidualJacobian <its design rows>).conditionNumber`; with every row's `avgTotal` moved by 0.01 · (−1)ⁱ, each of its sixteen `sigmaAt` is `Some` and above zero, and the one of `m00` is √(χ² / (m − 16) · (AᵀA)⁻¹₀₀) within 1e-6 relative, computed in the test through `RealMatrix`; `each run of an object stage has its own rows' residual at its object's solve`: each Science run's `RunResidual` holds its own rows' A · x − b at QZ's solve, with their root mean square, run by run; `a series is checked against the cascade of its objects' own solves`: with the series runs of QZ then LR added (step 390), one `SeriesProductCheck` for [QZ; LR] whose cascade is `cascadeProduct` of LR's and QZ's own solved matrices element by element within 1e-12, whose difference's `maxAbs` is below 1e-9 and whose `fitRmse` is the series' `ObjectMatrixFit` RMSE, and the series' problem has sixteen `ElementCoordinate`s. Step 390's facts over `reconstructLinear` run unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the object problems land, `StagedStudy.objectProblemsWith` MUST answer each object solve's design over its sixteen elements, each run's own residual and each series' product check against the cascade of its objects' own solves, and `reconstructLinear` MUST answer what it answered before; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an object solve's problem is its design over the matrix's elements, each coordinate an entry of the object`, `each run of an object stage has its own rows' residual at its object's solve` and `a series is checked against the cascade of its objects' own solves`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.an object solve's problem is its design over the matrix's elements, each coordinate an entry of the object", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.each run of an object stage has its own rows' residual at its object's solve", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a series is checked against the cascade of its objects' own solves", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.ObjectRunSystem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.ObjectGroupSystem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.ObjectGroupSystem.system", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.objectSystemsWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.ProductCheckData.storedFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.SeriesProductCheck.rmseRatio", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.objectProblemsWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-OBJECT-PROBLEMS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number": 401, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [400], "how_to": "The calibration stage's results are read off its three AIR fits (step 389), written in the instruments' own constants by step 398's fringe residuals, and each AIR run's residual is its own trace's (001 §L 'value ± σ', 'per-experiment residuals and RMSE'; S11.5 publishes each calibrated value with its σ). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `objectProblemsWith` (step 400): (1) `AirRunRows = { run : ExperimentName; rows : MuellerRawRow list }`, one AIR run's kept capture rows, and `AirFamilyRuns = { darkRows : MuellerRawRow list; lpLpRuns : AirRunRows list; lpCplRuns : AirRunRows list; cplLpRuns : AirRunRows list }` with `member this.stageOneRows : StageOneAirRows` (step 388), each family's rows run after run. (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.airRunsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) : Result<AirFamilyRuns, StudyFitError>`: the selection of `calibrateLinear` (step 389) MOVED: the Dark runs' rows in prefit order and each family's runs in study order, the family given by the run's prep and analyzer (step 386's `familyWith`), each run's rows its prefit's `Ok (CapturePoints rows)` with exclusions applied (`keptBy`, step 314). `calibrateLinear` becomes `calibrateFromAirRows solver` of `stageOneRows` of `airRunsWith` (step 388) and what it did with the constants: the same rows in the same order, so every number it answers is unchanged. (3) `type StagedStudy with member this.calibrationProblemsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) : Result<EngineProblems, StudyFitError>`, for a solution `calibrateLinear` answered. Over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items` and its layout, `airRunsWith`, then `calibrateFromAirRows solver runs.stageOneRows` (an error `StagedPathFitErr`), whose constants are c; each family's trace is `reduceAirTraces c.darkMean` of its rows (step 398); the entries of a constant are those step 389 gives it (an `LpLp` run's analyzer `dialZero` the `lpZero`; an `LpCpl` run's analyzer `dialZero` and `c2.retardance` the `cplZero` and `cplAnalyzerRetardance`; a `CplLp` run's prep `c2.fastAxisOffset` and `c2.retardance` the source model's θ − 45° and δ), each `EntryCoordinate` holding every entry of its constant. Three `FittedProblem`s (step 397), centre zero and unit one, each within its entries' unknown bounds: (a) `AirFringeProblem <the LP-LP runs>`: coordinates [the `lpZero` entries; `FringeVisibilityCoordinate`, unbounded], the residual s ↦ the trace's `fringeResidualAt` of s₀ in radians and `FringeVisibility s₁`, starting at the zero and the visibility `freeCosineFit solver` answers for that trace (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:freeCosineFit`, the fit stage one made, whose zero is the `lpZero`), an error answering `StagedPathFitErr (AirCalibrationFitErr (LpLp, e))`; (b) `AirFringeProblem <the LP-CPL runs>`: coordinates [the `cplZero` entries; the `cplAnalyzerRetardance` entries], the residual s ↦ `fringeResidualAt` of s₀ and `FringeVisibility (cos s₁)` (the visibility a retardance gives, the inverse of `FringeVisibility.retardance` on 0 ≤ δ ≤ 90°, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:FringeVisibility`), starting at [`cplZero`; `cplAnalyzerRetardance`]; (c) `AirFringeProblem <the CPL-LP runs>`: coordinates [the offset entries; the source retardance entries], the residual s ↦ `{ thetaRel = s₀ + 45°; retardance = s₁ }.lpFrameResidualOn trace c.lpZero` (step 398), starting at θ − 45° and δ of `c.cplSourceModel`. `runResiduals` hold, for each AIR run of the three families in that order, its own trace (`reduceAirTraces c.darkMean run.rows`) under its family's residual at its problem's start, with their root mean square; a Dark run has none. `productChecks` is empty. No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over step 389's fixture: `the calibration fit's problems are the three AIR fringes in the instruments' own constants`: three problems naming the LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP runs, whose coordinates hold LP2's `dialZero` and the visibility, CPL2's `dialZero` and `c2.retardance`, and CPL1's `c2.fastAxisOffset` and `c2.retardance`; each entry coordinate starts exactly at the value `calibrateLinear` gives its entry, and the LP-LP and LP-CPL problems' residuals at their starts have the root mean square `freeCosineFit` reports as `rmse` over their traces, within 1e-12; `each instrument constant of a calibration fit gets its sigma from its fringe`: with every AIR row's `avgTotal` moved by 2 · (−1)ⁱ, each of the five entries' σ is `Some` and above zero, and LP2's `dialZero` σ is below 1°; `each AIR run of a calibration fit has its own trace's residual`: one `RunResidual` per AIR Calibration run, each with as many entries as its trace has dial readings, and none for the Dark run. Step 389's facts over `calibrateLinear` run unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the calibration problems land, `StagedStudy.calibrationProblemsWith` MUST answer the LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP AIR fringes over the instruments' entries starting at the constants stage one wrote, and each AIR run's own residual, and `calibrateLinear` MUST answer what it answered before; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the calibration fit's problems are the three AIR fringes in the instruments' own constants`, `each instrument constant of a calibration fit gets its sigma from its fringe` and `each AIR run of a calibration fit has its own trace's residual`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.the calibration fit's problems are the three AIR fringes in the instruments' own constants", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.each instrument constant of a calibration fit gets its sigma from its fringe", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.each AIR run of a calibration fit has its own trace's residual", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.AirRunRows", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.AirFamilyRuns", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.AirFamilyRuns.stageOneRows", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.airRunsWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.calibrationProblemsWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "obligations": ["S114-CALIBRATION-PROBLEMS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number":402,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S114i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[401],"how_to":"The engines' problems become each entry's σ, each black-box object is checked for realizability, and the suspect entries are named (001 §L 'value ± σ', 'Mueller realizability (coherency eigenvalues ≥ 0)', 'post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood for suspect parameters'; the S11.4 brief 'Mueller realizability for every black-box object: coherency eigenvalues >= 0 (REUSE MuellerInverse.CoherencyEigenvalue and the coherency members beside it)' and 'parameters flagged suspect (correlation or sigma above thresholds stated in the fit settings)'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `calibrationProblemsWith` (step 401): (1) `type StagedStudy with member this.engineProblemsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (solution : StudyFitSolution) : Result<EngineProblems, StudyFitError>`: `nonlinearProblemsWith` for a `NonlinearStudyEngine` solution, `calibrationProblemsWith` for a `LinearStudyEngine` one under `CalibrationStage`, and `objectProblemsWith` for any other `LinearStudyEngine` one: the engine `runFit` took (step 391). (2) `type EngineProblems with member this.sigmasFor (layout : StudyParameterLayout) : FitEntrySigma list`: one per entry of `layout.entries`, in order, with the σ of the first problem's `entrySigmas` (step 397) naming it, else `None`. (3) `[<ReferenceEquality>] SuspectCoordinate = { problem : FittedProblem; coordinate : FitCoordinateIndex; entry : FitEntryRef; reasons : SuspectReason list }` (steps 396, 397), and `type EngineProblems with member this.suspectsWith (thresholds : SuspectThresholds) (layout : StudyParameterLayout) : SuspectCoordinate list` (step 395): for each problem in order, each `EntryCoordinate` k in order and each of its entries, whose bounds are its layout entry's `unknown.unknown.bounds` (step 214), the reasons are `UndeterminedSigmaReason` when `sigmaAt k` is `None`; `WideSigmaReason` of σ / (upper − lower) when that exceeds `thresholds.sigmaFraction`; and, when the problem's quality holds a correlation matrix, `CorrelatedEntryReason` of the first entry of each other `EntryCoordinate` l whose |ρₖₗ| exceeds `thresholds.correlation`, with ρₖₗ, in coordinate order. An entry with a reason is suspect. (4) `type StagedStudy with member this.realizabilityWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (layout : StudyParameterLayout) (fitted : StudyParameterVector) : Result<ObjectRealizability list, StudyFitError>`: over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items`, for each item `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` the fitted runs (step 261), in order, whose `context.choiceOf` is a `LibraryModelChoice` of form `OpticalElementModel (BlackBoxMuellerModel _)` (step 208): its values at the first fitted run that uses it (`layout.assignmentFor this.study this.items run fitted` and its `valuesOf`, step 373); its matrix, `BoundOpticalForm (form, values)` (step 248) evaluated by `muellerAt` at rotation zero, normal incidence and the transmitted branch, its reference orientation (step 248), at that run's operating wavelength (step 367); and the `ObjectRealizability` of the item and that matrix's `cloudeEigenvalues` (`MuellerInverse.fs:cloudeEigenvalues`). A forward or evaluation error answers `StudyForwardFitErr`. No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`: `an entry is suspect when its sigma is undetermined, wide against its bounds, or correlated past the threshold`: over an `EngineProblems` holding step 397's two test-local problems, each of whose coordinates is an `EntryCoordinate` of a test-local entry, and a test-local layout giving those entries the bounds [−2, 2]: under `SuspectThresholds.initial` the full-rank problem's entries are not suspect; under thresholds of 0.4 and 0.1 each is suspect with `CorrelatedEntryReason` naming the other at −0.5 within 1e-6; with bounds [−0.5, 0.5] each also has `WideSigmaReason` of √0.02 within 1e-6; and the rank-deficient problem's entries are each suspect with `UndeterminedSigmaReason`. `every entry takes the sigma of the coordinate that holds it`: over step 400's noisy fixture, `sigmasFor` gives QZ's sixteen entries in layout order each the σ of its coordinate, and an entry no problem holds `None`. `every black-box object of a fit is checked for realizability at its fitted values`: over step 390's fixture, QZ's realizability holds `(retarderMueller (Angle.degree 30.0<deg>) (Retardance.degree 40.0<deg>)).cloudeEigenvalues` within 1e-9 and is `RealizableMueller`; with QZ's rows generated from diag(1, 1.5, 0, 0), it is `UnrealizableMueller`. `each engine's results are read off the solves it made`: `engineProblemsWith` answers three `AirFringeProblem`s over step 389's calibration solution, one `ObjectSolveProblem` per group over step 390's object solution, and one `StudyEntriesProblem` over step 387's nonlinear solution.","acceptance":"After the sigmas, realizability and suspects land, each entry MUST take its σ from the coordinate holding it, each black-box object the fitted runs use MUST be checked by its coherency eigenvalues at its fitted values, and an entry MUST be suspect exactly when its σ is undetermined, wide past the sigma fraction of its bounds, or correlated past the threshold; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an entry is suspect when its sigma is undetermined, wide against its bounds, or correlated past the threshold`, `every entry takes the sigma of the coordinate that holds it`, `every black-box object of a fit is checked for realizability at its fitted values` and `each engine's results are read off the solves it made`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests","BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.an entry is suspect when its sigma is undetermined, wide against its bounds, or correlated past the threshold","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every entry takes the sigma of the coordinate that holds it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.every black-box object of a fit is checked for realizability at its fitted values","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.each engine's results are read off the solves it made","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.engineProblemsWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.EngineProblems.sigmasFor","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.SuspectCoordinate","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.EngineProblems.suspectsWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.realizabilityWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S114-SIGMAS-SUSPECTS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number":403,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S114j","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Optimization","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[402],"how_to":"A fit's results, gathered, with each suspect entry's χ² profile (001 §L 'post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood for suspect parameters'; 001 §M workflow '6. post-fit identifiability'; the S11.4 brief 're-fit with the parameter stepped across its sigma range, and record the chi-squared profile' and 'Tests on synthetic studies: an identifiable pair against a confounded pair'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `realizabilityWith` (step 402): `type StagedStudy with member this.resultsWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (data : StudyData) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (solution : StudyFitSolution) (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<FitRunResults, StudyFitError>`: the problems `engineProblemsWith` answers (step 402); `sigmas` their `sigmasFor solution.layout`; `problems` each one's `quality` (step 397), in order; their `runResiduals` and `productChecks`; `realizability` `realizabilityWith context solution.layout solution.fitted`; and `profiles`, for each of `suspectsWith this.study.settings.suspect solution.layout` in order, `{ entry; reasons; points }` of its problem's `profileAt coordinate earlier watch` (step 397), `earlier` the iterations of the profiles before it, so the profile pass counts its re-fits on from one through the fit's own watch. A `ProfileCancelledErr` answers `FitCancelledErr` (step 387) with its reason. A study whose thresholds flag nothing re-fits nothing, and nothing is written. No cache, retry or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over test-local intensity studies made as step 387 makes its studies: items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216): a HeNe source item (`intensityScale`, step 207), a prep item of the ideal-LP preset at R1 0°, an analyzer item of the ideal-LP preset and an intensity-detector item (`gain`, `darkOffset`, step 208); one setup of the four, its slots built as `SetupTests` builds them; one Science run in one session, its gain model free, scanning the analyzer's `VaryR1` over nine readings; its points `IntensityData` answered by a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy`, point i being 2 · S₀ + 0.1 + 0.002 · (−1)ⁱ, S₀ the unit-scale intensity `ExperimentRun.read Intensity` gives at that reading (step 252); each study staged `JointStage` / `CalibrationHeldFixed` (step 385), fitted by `fitNonlinear` and its results taken by `resultsWith`, unwatched. `an identifiable pair is determined, with no suspect and no profile`: with `gain` unknown from 1.8 within [1, 4] and `darkOffset` unknown from 0 within [−1, 1], over the readings 0° to 160° by 20°: one problem of rank 2, both σ `Some` and below a tenth of their spans, their correlation −√(2/3) within 1e-6 (−Σuᵢ / √(n Σuᵢ²) for uᵢ = ½ cos² θᵢ), no suspect and no profile. `an exactly confounded pair has no sigma, and its profile is flat along the confounded direction`: with `gain` unknown from 1.8 within [1, 4], the source's `intensityScale` unknown from 1 within [0.25, 4] and `darkOffset` known at 0.1, over the same readings: rank 1, both σ `None`, no correlation, both entries suspect with `UndeterminedSigmaReason`; the gain's profile is seven points at 1, 1.5, …, 4, each `ProfileConverged` at the fit's χ² within 1e-9 relative (holding the gain, the scale takes up their product, which is all the data sees), and the scale's is seven points across [0.25, 4], each `ProfileConverged`. `a nearly confounded pair is suspect by its correlation and profiled across three sigmas`: with `gain` and `darkOffset` unknown as in `an identifiable pair is determined, with no suspect and no profile` over the readings 0° to 20° by 2.5°: rank 2 with a correlation beyond −0.95, each entry suspect with `CorrelatedEntryReason` naming the other, each profile seven points at x̂ + j · σ whose middle is the fit's χ² and whose χ² is χ²_min · (1 + j² / 7) within 1e-6 relative (a model linear in both, nine points and two parameters). `a profile pass under a cancelled watch answers FitCancelledErr`: `an exactly confounded pair has no sigma, and its profile is flat along the confounded direction`'s solution with `resultsWith` under a watch whose `CancellationTokenSource` is already cancelled answers `FitCancelledErr`. `a fit's results gather its sigmas, solves, run residuals, realizability and product checks`: over step 390's series fixture, under the thresholds `tryCreate 1.0 1.0e9`, the results hold one σ per entry, one problem per object solve, one run residual per fitted run, QZ's and LR's realizability, the [QZ; LR] product check and no profile.","acceptance":"After the profiles land, `StagedStudy.resultsWith` MUST gather the entries' σ, every solve's quality, every fitted run's residual, every black-box object's realizability, every series' product check and a χ² profile of every suspect entry by re-fits under the fit's watch, an identifiable pair yielding no profile and a confounded one flat profiles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an identifiable pair is determined, with no suspect and no profile`, `an exactly confounded pair has no sigma, and its profile is flat along the confounded direction`, `a nearly confounded pair is suspect by its correlation and profiled across three sigmas`, `a profile pass under a cancelled watch answers FitCancelledErr` and `a fit's results gather its sigmas, solves, run residuals, realizability and product checks`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"unit-tests","values":["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests","BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.an identifiable pair is determined, with no suspect and no profile","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-PROFILES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.an exactly confounded pair has no sigma, and its profile is flat along the confounded direction","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-PROFILES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a nearly confounded pair is suspect by its correlation and profiled across three sigmas","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-PROFILES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a profile pass under a cancelled watch answers FitCancelledErr","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-PROFILES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a fit's results gather its sigmas, solves, run residuals, realizability and product checks","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S114-PROFILES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StagedStudy.resultsWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs","obligations":["S114-PROFILES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number": 404, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S114k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [403], "how_to": "The fit run stores its results (001 §L 'Results, stored in the fit run'; step 383 'S11.4 adds the results'; the S11.4 brief 'The fit run records: …'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. (1) `FitRuns.fs`: `FitRun` (step 383) gains `results : FitRunResults` (step 396) after `objectMatrices`. `FitRun.currentSchemaVersion` stays 1: no fit-run file exists before the committed kits are written in S12 (.spec-md §7 'Kit file shapes change in later parts; no migration is needed'). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/fitrun.schema.json` (step 384): under version 1 the root holds exactly sixteen fields, `results` added, an object holding exactly `sigmas`, `problems`, `runResiduals`, `realizability`, `productChecks` and `profiles`, each an array; the inner shapes stay the serializer's to bind (`MalformedJsonErr`). No converter is added: every union in the results is stored in the serializer's case form (step 396), and every number in them is finite (a condition, a correlation matrix or a σ that is not is `None`, step 397). (3) `StudyEngine.fs`: `runFit` (step 391), after the engine's solution and before it reads the clock, takes `resultsWith` of its staged study over the staged context, its prefits, its data, `this.linearSolver`, the solution and its watch (step 403), its error answered as it stands (a cancelled profile pass is `FitCancelledErr`, so the job writes nothing, step 393), and the fit run's `results` is it. Nothing else in `runFit` changes. (4) Every record expression that spells out a `FitRun` in the tests gains `results`, a record of six empty lists unless stated here. Tests. In `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 384), `a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text`'s fit run holds results with one of each: QZ `m00`'s σ `Some (ParameterSigma 0.002)` and CPL1 `c2.retardance`'s `None`; a problem of each subject and each coordinate case, one with a condition and a correlation matrix and one with neither; a run residual of two entries; a realizability of four eigenvalues; a product check; and a profile holding all three reasons and both outcomes; it reads back equal, and writing the parsed run again gives the same text. `a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused` also refuses a run without `results` and a `results` without `profiles` with `SchemaValidationErr`. In `StudyEngineTests` (step 391), `a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced` also finds in its run the results `resultsWith` gives that fit: n_o's and n_e's σ, one `StudyEntriesProblem` and the plate run's residual; and `a fit run stores its results, profiles included`: step 403's exactly confounded intensity study through `runFit` records the gain's and the scale's profiles in its run's results, each of seven points.", "acceptance": "After the results are stored, every fit run `runFit` answers MUST hold the `FitRunResults` `resultsWith` gives its fit, written and read in its `.fitrun-json` under its schema; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fit run stores its results, profiles included`, the count rising by 1, and the widened `a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused` and `a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced`; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/FitRuns.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/fitrun.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StudyEngine.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFitRunFileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyFitJobTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a fit run stores its results, profiles included", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S114-STORED-RESULTS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S114-STORED-RESULTS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S114-STORED-RESULTS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests.a fit run records its name, stamp, stage, engine, fitted runs, the data it read and the vector it used and produced", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs", "obligations": ["S114-STORED-RESULTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.FitRuns.FitRun", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S114-STORED-RESULTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StudyEngine.StudyFitParam.runFit", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S114-STORED-RESULTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.4 -- Fit results: uncertainty, correlation, realizability, product check, profile likelihood"}
{"number":405,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[404],"how_to":"A promoted library entry says where it was fitted (001 §I 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database, with provenance \"fitted in kit K, study S, run R\"'; 001 §L 'Publishing: … material or black-box object → Promote to library'; the S11.5 brief 'add an EntryProvenance case here if none fits'). None fits: `UserProvenance` carries nothing and `KitImportProvenance` names the kit alone (`LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, steps 24, 91). The study and the fit run are named by the file stems the kit stores them under (001 §A), because `StudyName` and `FitRunName` are declared after this file (steps 214, 358) and their `fileStem` members (steps 358, 383) are how a kit names them; nothing is moved. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `EntryProvenance` (steps 24, 91) gains a sixth case, `FitProvenance of EntryFitInfo`, declared together with `and EntryFitInfo = { kit : KitId; studyStem : FileStem; fitRunStem : FileStem }`: the kit the fit ran in (step 24's `KitId`) and the stems of the study's `<study>.study-json` and of the fit run's `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json`, the files that reproduce the fitted values (001 §I 'Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'). A fitted entry belongs to the user: `protection` answers `UserManaged`, `categoryOrigin` answers `UserCategory`, and `attributionOpt` (step 113) answers `None`, because a fit carries no licence. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (steps 63, 91): `kindValue` answers 6 for a fit and `catalogueIdOpt` answers `None`, because a fitted entry ships in no catalogue. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json` (steps 30, 91): the provenance definition gains a sixth shape, exactly what the serializer writes for `FitProvenance`: `kit` a GUID, and `studyStem` and `fitRunStem` non-empty strings. The entry schemas keep version 1, because no entry file has been released (.spec-md §7). Any other complete match on `EntryProvenance` that FS0025 reports answers a fit as it answers `UserProvenance`. No other case, member, converter or schema changes; the promotion builds the case (step 407). (4) Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` also covers a `FitProvenance` of a test-local `KitId` with `FileStem \"QZ-LR\"` and `FileStem \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\"`: it is `UserManaged` and `UserCategory`; its `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none` (step 113) also answers `None` for it. `EntryFileJsonTests`' `every provenance round-trips through an entry file` gains a material under that `FitProvenance`; it round-trips through its entry file, and its decoder answers the material.","acceptance":"After the provenance lands, `EntryProvenance` MUST hold `FitProvenance of EntryFitInfo` (the kit, the study's file stem and the fit run's file stem), user-managed with no attribution, stored with provenance kind 6 and no catalogue, and written and read back in an entry file under `library-common.schema.json`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the widened `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed`, `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none` and `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs","obligations":["S115-FIT-PROVENANCE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs","obligations":["S115-FIT-PROVENANCE"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.every provenance round-trips through an entry file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs","obligations":["S115-FIT-PROVENANCE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryFitInfo","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S115-FIT-PROVENANCE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.EntryProvenance.FitProvenance","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs","obligations":["S115-FIT-PROVENANCE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":406,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[405],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests"],"how_to":"Publish calibration, as a pure update of the kit's items: a fit run's item-owned values become the items' next revisions, each value a `CalibratedParameter` with its σ and its fit run (001 §I 'Revisions: an item file carries a revision number and a short value history; \"Publish calibration\" writes the next revision. Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'; 001 §L 'Publishing: item → next revision (`Calibrated`)', 'staged: stage 1 calibrates items …; Publish calibration; stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with σ', 'Explicit links (\"CPL2.δ = CPL1.δ\") are constraints'; 001 §P `PublishCalibration`; the S11.5 brief). It REUSES `Item.publishRevision` (step 235), the one revision write, and reads the σ S11.4 stores (`FitRunResults.sigmas`, steps 396, 404); recording the items is the window's (step 413). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5, and every case name has two words. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs`, `module StudyPublishing` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `FitRuns.fs` (step 383), the last Domain file, because publishing reads studies, items, fit runs and the kit's library: one `<Compile Include=\"StudyPublishing.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: what a fit run publishes back into the kit and the library (spec 0050 S11.5). In order: (1) `PublishError`, an `*Error` union: `ForeignFitRunErr of reason : string` (the fit run is another study's), `UnknownPublishedItemErr of reason : string` (the run fitted an item the kit no longer holds), `UndeterminedSigmaErr of reason : string` (a fitted value whose σ the run leaves undetermined, step 396's `sigmaOpt = None`), `NoCalibrationErr of reason : string` (the run fitted no item-owned value), `CalibrationAlreadyPublishedErr of reason : string` (every item already holds the run's calibration) and `PublishItemErr of error : ItemError` (step 213), with `member this.describe : string`: `the fit run belongs to another study: <reason>`, `the kit has no such item: <reason>`, `the fit leaves a sigma undetermined: <reason>`, `the fit run calibrates no item: <reason>`, `the calibration is already published: <reason>` and `the item refused the calibration: <the error's describe>`. (2) `type Study with member this.calibratedItemsWith (run : FitRun) (items : Item list) : Result<Item list, PublishError>`, over the kit's items, in this order. `run.study` other than `this.name` is `ForeignFitRunErr` naming both. The item-owned entries are the `run.entries` (step 383) whose `parameter` is `ItemParameterRef (id, name)` and whose `owner` is `ItemOwner id`, in entry order; one whose item `items` lacks is `UnknownPublishedItemErr` naming its GUID and the run. Each one's σ is the `sigmaOpt` of the `run.results.sigmas` element whose `entry` is `{ parameter = e.parameter; owner = e.owner }` (`FitEntryRef`, step 396); `None`, or no element, is `UndeterminedSigmaErr` naming the item's label, the parameter and the run. No item-owned entry is `NoCalibrationErr` naming the run. An entry owned by a session or an experiment (`SessionOwner`, `ExperimentOwner`, step 362) holds one value per session block or run and is no item's calibration, so it is left out and stays in the fit run (001 §L scope table). Each item-owned entry publishes `{ name = name; state = CalibratedParameter { value = e.fitted; sigma = <its σ>; fitRun = run.name } }` (step 214). Each `this.links` link (step 364) whose leader is a published `ItemParameterRef` and whose follower is an `ItemParameterRef` of an item of `items` publishes the leader's state under the follower's name, so stage 2 finds the follower calibrated as `stageWith` requires (step 385, `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr`). Per item of `items`, in order, its published parameters are its own entries in entry order, then its followers in link order; one whose state the item already holds is dropped, and an item with none left is not published, so publishing one run twice writes no second revision. None left at all is `CalibrationAlreadyPublishedErr` naming the run. Each remaining item is `item.publishRevision <its published parameters>` (step 235), an `ItemError` answering `PublishItemErr`. The answer is the published items, in `items` order. Nothing is written and no clock is read. No other type or member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs`, `module StudyPublishingTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216) as `StudyTests` makes them (step 362): CPL1 and CPL2 over the built-in circular-polarizer model, each with `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2], and a Phone over the intensity-detector model with `gain` unknown from 1000 within [100, 10000]; a test-local study record `QZ-LR` whose one link makes CPL2's `c2.retardance` follow CPL1's; and a test-local `FitRun` record (steps 383, 404) of `QZ-LR` named `FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\"`, whose entries are CPL1's `c2.retardance` (`ItemOwner`) fitted at 1.55 and the Phone's `gain` (`SessionOwner (SessionName \"Session 1\")`) fitted at 900, and whose results hold CPL1's σ `Some (ParameterSigma 0.002)`, the gain's `None` and five empty lists. `publishing a calibration writes each item-owned fitted value with its sigma and fit run into the item's next revision, and a linked follower takes its leader's`: `calibratedItemsWith run [ CPL1; CPL2; Phone ]` answers CPL1 then CPL2, each at revision 2 whose history is the one record of revision 1's values and whose `c2.retardance` is `CalibratedParameter { value = 1.55; sigma = ParameterSigma 0.002; fitRun = FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\" }`, every other parameter unchanged; the Phone is not answered. `a session-owned value is no item calibration, and a run that calibrates nothing or only what is published is refused`: a run whose only entry is the session-owned gain answers `NoCalibrationErr`, and the first run over CPL1 and CPL2 as the first fact answers them answers `CalibrationAlreadyPublishedErr`. `a value without a sigma, a run of another study or an item the kit lacks publishes nothing`: with CPL1's σ `None` it answers `UndeterminedSigmaErr` naming `CPL1` and `c2.retardance`; a run of the study `LR` answers `ForeignFitRunErr`; and the items without CPL1 answer `UnknownPublishedItemErr`. `every publish error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local payload renders a distinct text holding it.","acceptance":"After the calibration lands, `Study.calibratedItemsWith` MUST answer each item a fit run calibrates at its next revision, every item-owned fitted value a `CalibratedParameter` of its value, its σ and the run, a link's follower taking its leader's, session- and run-owned values left out, and MUST refuse a run of another study, an undetermined σ, an unknown item and a run with nothing new to publish; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `publishing a calibration writes each item-owned fitted value with its sigma and fit run into the item's next revision, and a linked follower takes its leader's`, `a session-owned value is no item calibration, and a run that calibrates nothing or only what is published is refused`, `a value without a sigma, a run of another study or an item the kit lacks publishes nothing` and `every publish error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.publishing a calibration writes each item-owned fitted value with its sigma and fit run into the item's next revision, and a linked follower takes its leader's","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-CALIBRATION"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a session-owned value is no item calibration, and a run that calibrates nothing or only what is published is refused","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-CALIBRATION"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a value without a sigma, a run of another study or an item the kit lacks publishes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-CALIBRATION"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.every publish error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-CALIBRATION"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.PublishError","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-CALIBRATION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.PublishError.describe","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-CALIBRATION"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.Study.calibratedItemsWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-CALIBRATION"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":407,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115c","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[406],"how_to":"What a fit run promotes to the library, as pure values: a fitted material is its opened version's entry holding the fitted crystal, and a fitted black-box object is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix (001 §I 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database, with provenance \"fitted in kit K, study S, run R\"'; 001 §L 'material or black-box object → Promote to library'; 001 §I table 'Sample as black-box Mueller matrix: 16 parameters (or 15 + scale) at reference orientation'; the S11.5 brief). A black-box object's library form is the polarizer preset, because the preset is the one library kind that holds a fixed Mueller matrix (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerBehavior`'s `ConstantMueller`, `ElementId.fs:PolarizerCategory`'s `CustomMueller`, 'a custom Mueller stack'), while an item-model form holds no values (step 208) and a stack sample holds layers. Its entry takes the item's GUID, so promoting the same item again finds the entry and mints its next version (step 408). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5, and every case name has two words. In `StudyPublishing.fs`, after `calibratedItemsWith` (step 406): (1) `type ItemId with member this.toLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId` (the GUID kept, as `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId` keeps it, step 24) and `member this.toElementValueId : ElementValueId` (the GUID's canonical text, as `SampleId.toElementValueId` writes it); `type ItemLabel with member this.entryName : EntryName`, the label's text. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006). (2) `type FitRun with member this.provenanceIn (kit : KitId) : EntryProvenance`: `FitProvenance { kit = kit; studyStem = this.study.fileStem; fitRunStem = this.name.fileStem }` (steps 358, 383, 405). (3) `PromotionSubject` = `MaterialPromotion of MaterialVersionId` (an opened material version, step 361) | `BlackBoxPromotion of ItemId` (a black-box item): what `PromoteToLibrary` names (001 §P). It is derived, never stored, so it carries no tag. (4) `PublishError` (step 406) gains `UnfittedPromotionErr of reason : string` (`the fit run fitted none of its values: <reason>`), `ScopedPromotionErr of reason : string` (`the fit gives it no single value: <reason>`, a value fitted per session block or per run), `NotBlackBoxErr of reason : string` (`the item is not a black-box Mueller matrix: <reason>`), `PromotionStudyErr of error : StudyError` (`the study refused the promoted value: <the error's describe>`) and `PromotionEvaluationErr of error : ItemEvaluationError` (`the fitted matrix could not be evaluated: <the error's describe>`, step 247). (5) `type Study with member this.promotedMaterialWith (run : FitRun) (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<MaterialEntry, PublishError>`, over the entry the caller resolved for `version`: `ForeignFitRunErr` as in step 406; the opened copy is the one of `this.materials` of that version (else `UnfittedPromotionErr` naming it); the run's entries of `MaterialParameterRef (version, name)` (step 358) are its fitted components, one owned by anything but `MaterialOwner version` answering `ScopedPromotionErr` naming the component, and none answering `UnfittedPromotionErr` naming the material and the run. Each component of the copy is set through `withParameterState` (step 361, its error `PromotionStudyErr`) to `KnownParameter` of its fitted value when the run fitted it, and otherwise to the state `run.parameters` (step 383) records for it, the state the fit read. The answer is `{ entry with physics = CrystalParameterPhysics <that copy's currentCrystal> }` (steps 355, 361): every other field of the entry is kept, its id is the material's, and so the library mints that material's next version (step 408). (6) `type FitRun with member this.promotedBlackBoxWith (item : Item) (choice : ItemModelChoice) : Result<PolarizerPreset, PublishError>`: `choice` a `LibraryModelChoice` whose form is `OpticalElementModel (BlackBoxMuellerModel normalisation)` (steps 208, 216), else `NotBlackBoxErr` naming the item's label; the run's entries of `ItemParameterRef (item.id, name)` are its fitted elements, one owned by anything but `ItemOwner item.id` answering `ScopedPromotionErr` and none answering `UnfittedPromotionErr`. Its values are `ParameterValues.ofParameters` (step 245) of the item's parameters, each fitted one as `KnownParameter` of its fitted value and each other in the state `run.parameters` records for it. Its matrix is the bound form `BoundOpticalForm (BlackBoxMuellerModel normalisation, values)` (`BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm`, step 248) evaluated by `muellerAt` at rotation zero, normal incidence and the transmitted branch, its reference orientation, as `realizabilityWith` evaluates a black box (step 402), at the 600 nm `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf` answers without a source (step 367), which a black-box form does not read (step 248); an evaluation error answers `PromotionEvaluationErr`. The answer is `{ id = item.id.toElementValueId; name = item.label.entryName; behavior = ConstantMueller [ { matrix = <the matrix>; offset = Angle 0.0 } ]; category = CustomMueller; protection = UserManaged }` (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerPreset`, `ElementId.fs:MuellerComponent`): one component at reference orientation, turned at run time as any element is (001 §I 'rotation as R(−φ) M R(φ)'). (7) `type FitRun with member this.promotionSubjectsWith (study : Study) (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : PromotionSubject list`: the study's opened materials, in study order, of which the run has a `MaterialParameterRef` entry, each as `MaterialPromotion`, then the items of `items`, in order, whose `choiceOf` answers a black-box `LibraryModelChoice` and of which the run has an `ItemParameterRef` entry, each as `BlackBoxPromotion`; the Publish step lists them (step 418). Nothing is written. No other type or member is added. Tests, in `StudyPublishingTests` (step 406). `a promoted material is its opened version's entry with the crystal its fit run produced`: over a test-local absorbing crystal entry of fifteen distinct literal values (as `StudyMaterialTests` builds its probe, step 361) opened by the study, with `n1` and `e11` unknown, and a run of the study fitting `n1` at 1.7 and `e11` at 0.02 (`MaterialOwner`) whose `parameters` record every other component at the probe's value: `promotedMaterialWith` answers the entry under `CrystalParameterPhysics` whose generated axes read 1.7 for `n1`, 0.02 for `e11` and the probe's value for every other component, its id and name unchanged. `a material component fitted per run, or a material the study did not open or the run did not fit, is not promoted`: `n1` owned by an `ExperimentOwner` answers `ScopedPromotionErr` naming `n1`; a version the study did not open, and a run with no entry of the material, each answer `UnfittedPromotionErr`. `a promoted black box is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix under the item's GUID and label`: QZ over the built-in black-box model (`ItemModelIds.blackBoxMuellerModelId`, sixteen elements at the identity, step 208), with `m00` fitted at 0.9 and `m01` at 0.25 (`ItemOwner`), answers the preset whose id is QZ's GUID text, named `QZ`, `CustomMueller` and `UserManaged`, with one `ConstantMueller` component at offset zero whose matrix holds 0.9 at (0, 0), 0.25 at (0, 1) and the identity elsewhere, within 1e-15; CPL1 over the circular-polarizer model answers `NotBlackBoxErr` naming `CPL1`; and QZ's `m01` owned by an `ExperimentOwner` answers `ScopedPromotionErr`. `a fit run's provenance names its kit, its study's file and its own file`: `provenanceIn` of a test-local `KitId` is `FitProvenance { kit = <it>; studyStem = FileStem \"QZ-LR\"; fitRunStem = FileStem \"QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z\" }`. `a fit run offers each opened material and black box it fitted for promotion`: over CPL1, QZ and the opened material, `promotionSubjectsWith` of a run fitting `n1`, CPL1's `c2.retardance` and QZ's `m00` answers `MaterialPromotion` of the opened version, then `BlackBoxPromotion` of QZ; of a run fitting CPL1 alone, `[]`. `every publish error renders its condition and its payload` covers the five new cases. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the promoted values land, `Study.promotedMaterialWith` MUST answer the opened version's entry holding the crystal its fit run produced, `FitRun.promotedBlackBoxWith` MUST answer a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of the item's fitted matrix under its GUID and label, `FitRun.provenanceIn` MUST answer the fitted provenance and `promotionSubjectsWith` MUST list what the run can promote, values fitted per session or run refused; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a promoted material is its opened version's entry with the crystal its fit run produced`, `a material component fitted per run, or a material the study did not open or the run did not fit, is not promoted`, `a promoted black box is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix under the item's GUID and label`, `a fit run's provenance names its kit, its study's file and its own file` and `a fit run offers each opened material and black box it fitted for promotion`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every publish error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a promoted material is its opened version's entry with the crystal its fit run produced","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a material component fitted per run, or a material the study did not open or the run did not fit, is not promoted","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a promoted black box is a custom-Mueller polarizer preset of its fitted matrix under the item's GUID and label","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a fit run's provenance names its kit, its study's file and its own file","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a fit run offers each opened material and black box it fitted for promotion","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.every publish error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.ItemId.toLibraryEntryId","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.ItemId.toElementValueId","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.ItemLabel.entryName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.FitRun.provenanceIn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.PromotionSubject","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.Study.promotedMaterialWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.FitRun.promotedBlackBoxWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.FitRun.promotionSubjectsWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.PublishError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S115-PROMOTED-VALUES"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs"}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":408,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115d","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[407],"how_to":"Promote to library writes the promoted value as the entry's next version in the library database and snapshots that version into the kit (001 §I 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database'; 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'; 001 §E 'a snapshot of every library version it uses'; the S11.5 brief 'It is then snapshotted into the kit (S4.2)'). It REUSES the import seam's write (`CatalogueImportProxy.putEntryVersion` and `CatalogueImportContext.sealEntry`, step 94), the one path that stores a whole entry version with its own provenance and hash, and the kit's snapshot (`KitLibraryContext.snapshotReferences`, step 139, which pins the version before it writes `library/<GUID>@v<n><kind extension>`), so no library or kit verb is added. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. In `StudyPublishing.fs`, after `promotionSubjectsWith` (step 407): (1) `PublishError` gains `PromotionImportErr of error : CatalogueImportError` (`the library refused the promoted version: <the error's describe>`), `PromotionEntryErr of error : LibraryEntryError` (`the promoted entry could not be built: <the error's describe>`) and `PromotionKitErr of error : KitLibraryError` (`the kit could not snapshot the promoted version: <the error's describe>`). (2) On a `type KitLibraryContext with` extension (step 139): `member this.promoteMaterial (study : Study) (run : FitRun) (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<LibraryVersionRef, PublishError>` and `member this.promoteBlackBox (run : FitRun) (item : Item) (choice : ItemModelChoice) : Result<LibraryVersionRef, PublishError>`, each in this order. Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` it answers `PromotionKitErr (KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr \"promoteToLibrary\"))`, reading and writing nothing, because the put comes before the snapshot that would refuse. Then the promoted value: `study.promotedMaterialWith run version entry` or `run.promotedBlackBoxWith item choice` (step 407). Its entry id: `version.materialId.toLibraryEntryId` (step 24) or `item.id.toLibraryEntryId` (step 407). Its version: `VersionNumber.first` when `this.imports.proxy.tryHeldEntry` of the id (step 94) answers `None`, a black box promoted for the first time being a new entry, and `held.latest.next` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:VersionNumber.next`) otherwise; a read error is `PromotionImportErr`. Its content: `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry <the version> (run.provenanceIn this.kit.kitFile.id) <the promoted entry>` (steps 25, 355: a crystal writes `CrystalMaterialPayload`) or `LibraryEntryContent.ofPolarizerPreset <the version> <that provenance> <the preset>` (step 25), its error `PromotionEntryErr`. `this.imports.sealEntry` of it and `this.imports.proxy.putEntryVersion { envelope = <the sealed envelope>; latest = MoveLatestVersion }` (step 94), either error `PromotionImportErr`. Then `this.snapshotReferences [ EntryVersionReference { entryId = <the id>; version = <the version> } ]` (steps 137, 139), its error `PromotionKitErr`. The answer is that `LibraryVersionRef`. The version the study opened stays as it was and pinned (step 359), so the study and every sample that names it are unchanged, while the library database answers the promoted version as the entry's latest (001 §C). Nothing is replaced or deleted, so no undo is needed. No other member, retry or option is added. Tests, in `StudyPublishingTests`, each fact over a fresh `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67), disposed at its end: a `KitLibraryContext` whose kit is `KitProxy.createInMemory` of an initialised `InMemoryKitFolder` opened read-write through `KitContext.openKit` with a stepping clock, as `StudyMessageTests` opens its kits (step 366), and whose imports are `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase <the database>)` (step 95); a user absorbing crystal material saved through `(MaterialProxy.createInDatabase <the database>).saveMaterial` (step 69) at version 1, opened by the study and recorded through `recordStudy` (steps 359, 361), which pins it; and step 407's runs. `promoting a fitted material mints its next library version under the fit's provenance and snapshots it into the kit`: `promoteMaterial` answers version 2 of the material; `MaterialProxy.createInDatabase`'s `resolveVersion` answers the promoted entry for version 2 and the saved one for version 1; `imports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope` of version 2 (step 105) holds `FitProvenance` of the kit file's id, `FileStem \"QZ-LR\"` and the run's stem; and the kit's `paths` hold `library/<the GUID>@v2.material-json` beside `library/<the GUID>@v1.material-json`. `promoting a black box adds a custom-Mueller preset at version 1, and promoting it again mints version 2`: `promoteBlackBox` of QZ (step 407's black box, its choice `LibraryModelChoice (BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel ItemModelIds.blackBoxMuellerModelId)`) answers version 1 under QZ's GUID, the kit holding `library/<QZ's GUID>@v1.polarizer-json`; promoting it again from a second run of the study answers version 2, and the kit holds both snapshots. `a read-only kit promotes nothing`: over a context whose kit is opened `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, both members answer `PromotionKitErr` of `KitReadOnlyErr`, `tryHeldEntry` answers what it answered before, and `paths` and every file's bytes are unchanged. `every publish error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the mint lands, `KitLibraryContext.promoteMaterial` and `promoteBlackBox` MUST write the promoted value as its entry's next version (version 1 for a new black-box entry) through the import seam under `FitProvenance`, MUST snapshot and pin that version into the kit, and MUST write nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `promoting a fitted material mints its next library version under the fit's provenance and snapshots it into the kit`, `promoting a black box adds a custom-Mueller preset at version 1, and promoting it again mints version 2` and `a read-only kit promotes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every publish error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.promoting a fitted material mints its next library version under the fit's provenance and snapshots it into the kit","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTE-MINT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.promoting a black box adds a custom-Mueller preset at version 1, and promoting it again mints version 2","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTE-MINT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.a read-only kit promotes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PROMOTE-MINT"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyPublishingTests.every publish error renders its condition and its payload","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyPublishingTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTE-MINT"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.KitLibraryContext.promoteMaterial","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTE-MINT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.KitLibraryContext.promoteBlackBox","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs","obligations":["S115-PROMOTE-MINT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyPublishing.PublishError","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S115-PROMOTE-MINT"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyPublishing.fs"}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":409,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115e","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[408],"how_to":"Fixing or freeing a component of an opened material is a study message, as an item parameter's state is `SetParameterState` (001 §P 'Every user step is a semantic message: … `SetParameterState`; `CreateStudy`, `AddExperimentsToStudy`, `OpenMaterial`, `SetParameterScope`, `LinkParameters`'; 001 §I 'a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file, with `Unknown` components'; 001 §O 'the unknowns table (owner, scope, fix / free, bounds, priors, links)'). The pure half exists (`Study.withMaterialParameterState`, step 361); the unknowns table's Set needs the message that reaches it (step 414). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `Studies.fs`: `StudyMsg` (step 366) gains, last and documented, `SetOpenedMaterialParameter of study : StudyName * material : MaterialVersionId * parameter : Parameter`: set one component of an opened material's working copy, its name and state being the `Parameter` (step 214). `applyTo` answers it as it answers the other study cases: the study of `context.studies` by name (else `UnknownStudyErr`), then `withMaterialParameterState material parameter.name parameter.state` (step 361), whose refusals (`UnknownStudyMaterialErr`, `UnknownStudyParameterErr`, `InvalidStudyParameterErr`) pass through. The caller records the answered study through `recordStudy` (step 359), as for every study message. No other case, field or option is added. Tests, in `StudyMessageTests` (step 366), over its in-memory kit and its opened absorbing material: `SetOpenedMaterialParameter frees an opened component in the stored study, and a refused one records nothing`: after `OpenMaterial`, `SetOpenedMaterialParameter (QZ-LR, <its version>, n1 as UnknownParameter from 1.70 within [1.60, 1.80])` recorded through `recordStudy` leaves `readStudies`' study holding that state for `n1` and every other component known; the same message over a version the study did not open answers `UnknownStudyMaterialErr`, and with reversed bounds `InvalidStudyParameterErr`, and `paths` and every file's bytes are unchanged after either.","acceptance":"After the message lands, `StudyMsg.SetOpenedMaterialParameter` MUST set one component of an opened material's working copy through `withMaterialParameterState` and MUST refuse an unopened version and a state that breaks its rules; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SetOpenedMaterialParameter frees an opened component in the stored study, and a refused one records nothing`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.SetOpenedMaterialParameter frees an opened component in the stored study, and a refused one records nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-MATERIAL-PARAMETER-MSG"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S115-MATERIAL-PARAMETER-MSG"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg.applyTo","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S115-MATERIAL-PARAMETER-MSG"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs"}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":410,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115f","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[409],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests"],"how_to":"The constructor window holds its kit's studies and fit runs, read when the kit opens and when it reloads, and the five study messages of S11.1 become window messages that record what they answer (001 §P 'CreateStudy, AddExperimentsToStudy, OpenMaterial, SetParameterScope, LinkParameters … The same messages back the buttons'; 001 §O 'Study view'; the S11.1 mapper's note 'The study view that sends them is S11.5's'; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic Elmish message). It follows the items' precedent (step 223). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit` (steps 150, 223) gains `studies : Study list` and `fitRuns : FitRun list` after `items`, each documented in one line: the kit's studies as `readStudies ()` (step 359) orders them, and every study's fit runs, study by study in that order and each in stamp order (`readFitRuns`, step 384). The private `openedOver` reads them after the items; a refusal closes the kit and is the answer, as any failed read is (step 150). `withRebindings` keeps them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) Before the model: `StudySurfaceState = { studyOpt : StudyName option; fitRunOpt : FitRunName option; newStudyName : ControlCaption; newStudyExperiments : ExperimentName list }` with `static member initial` (nothing chosen, an empty name, no experiment): which study and fit run the study surfaces show, and the New study form's typed name and chosen experiments; window state, never stored. (b) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `kitStudies : Study list`, `kitFitRuns : FitRun list` and `studySurface : StudySurfaceState` after `flowStep` (step 238), each documented in one line; `initWith` sets `[]`, `[]` and `StudySurfaceState.initial`. (c) The private function of a kit's content that `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` share (steps 187, 223) takes the studies and fit runs after the items and sets `kitStudies` and `kitFitRuns`; it keeps `studySurface.studyOpt` when the kit still holds that study and otherwise chooses its first study, or none, and keeps `fitRunOpt` only when the kit holds that run. `loadKit` passes `opened.studies` and `opened.fitRuns`; `ReloadKitChanges` reads `readStudies ()` and each study's `readFitRuns` after `readItems ()`, an `Error e` keeping the model and the offer with step 187's text; `CopyChosenExperiments` (step 225) passes the model's own. A changed `.study-json` or `.fitrun-json` is offered for reload by step 130's check, because both are kinds of `KitFileKind.all` (step 123). (d) On the model extension holding `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263), each documented in one line: `member model.studyContext : StudyContext` (step 366) = `{ studies = model.kitStudies; experiments = model.experimentCollection.experiments; setups = model.kitSetups; items = model.kitItems; resolveMaterial = <…> }`, whose `resolveMaterial version` answers `model.materials.resolveVersion version`'s `Ok (Some entry)` as `Ok entry`, `Ok None` as `MaterialUnavailableErr` naming the version's GUID and number, and `Error e` as `MaterialUnavailableErr` of `e.caption`'s text (`ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:MaterialError.caption`); `member model.selectedStudyOpt : Study option`, the study of `kitStudies` that `studySurface.studyOpt` names; and `member model.studyFitRuns : FitRun list`, the `kitFitRuns` of that study, oldest first, `[]` without one. (e) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `StudyCommand of StudyMsg` (the study verbs' message and how a test sends one, 001 §P), `SelectStudy of StudyName`, `SetNewStudyName of ControlCaption` and `ToggleNewStudyExperiment of ExperimentName`. (f) Arms. `StudyCommand msg` goes through step 185's read-only guard first; then `msg.applyTo model.studyContext` (step 366): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `The study was not changed — <e.describe>` and records nothing; `Ok study` is recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordStudy study` (step 359), whose `Ok ()` replaces the study of that name in `kitStudies` or adds it, in `readStudies`' order, sets `studySurface.studyOpt` to it, clears the New study form after a `CreateStudy` and sets `kitStatus` to `None`, and whose `Error e` keeps `kitStudies` and sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `SelectStudy name` sets `studyOpt` when `kitStudies` holds the name, and `fitRunOpt` to the last of its fit runs or `None`; otherwise it changes nothing. `SetNewStudyName` sets the form's name; `ToggleNewStudyExperiment` removes the name when the form holds it and appends it otherwise. These three write nothing. No other field, message or option is added; the surfaces that send them are steps 414-418. Tests. `KitOpeningTests` (step 150) gains `opening a kit reads its studies and their fit runs, and a study file that does not read refuses the open`: a kit holding the studies `QZ-LR` and `LR`, written through `recordStudy`, and two fit runs of `QZ-LR` written through `writeFitRun` (step 384), closed, answers `studies` `LR` then `QZ-LR` and `fitRuns` the two in stamp order when opened again read-write and read-only; a kit whose `Broken.study-json` the test writes as `{` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitFileRejectedErr _)` naming it, and its folder holds no `.oc/lock`. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs`, `module StudyWindowModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, the home of the window's study arms. Its kit is a folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"StudyWindowModelTests\", <a new GUID>)` opened read-write through `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) over the Built-in import context, as `KitWindowModelTests` opens its kits (step 184), holding CPL1, CPL2 and the Phone recorded through `recordItem` (step 219) over `ItemDraft`s of the built-in circular-polarizer and intensity-detector models (CPL1's and CPL2's `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2], the Phone's `gain` unknown from 1000 within [100, 10000]), one setup `Bench` holding them through `recordSetup` (step 260) and E1 and E2 (Science) and E3 (Calibration) over it through `recordExperiment` (step 149), closed, opened again and loaded into `initInverse` through `loadKit` (step 152), the window's stores and its `catalogueImports` being one `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` set, as `StudyMessageTests`' are (step 366). `a loaded kit's studies and fit runs are the window's, and Reload reads a study another writer wrote`: with `QZ-LR` and one test-local fit run of it written before the load, `kitStudies` is `[ QZ-LR ]`, `kitFitRuns` the run and `studySurface.studyOpt` `Some QZ-LR`; after another writer (step 187's `KitProxy.create` over the folder) records the study `LR`, `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnActivation` offers `LR.study-json` and `ReloadKitChanges` leaves `kitStudies` `LR` then `QZ-LR` with `QZ-LR` still chosen. `CreateStudy from the window records the study, selects it and clears the New study form`: `SetNewStudyName (ControlCaption \"QZ-LR\")`, `ToggleNewStudyExperiment` of E1, of E2 and of E3, then of E3 again, and `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (QZ-LR, [ E1; E2 ]))` leave `kitStudies` holding `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2, `readStudies ()` answering it, `studyOpt` `Some QZ-LR` and the form `StudySurfaceState.initial`'s. `a refused study message is told and records nothing, and a read-only kit takes none`: `StudyCommand (AddExperimentsToStudy (LR, [ E1 ]))` with no study `LR` sets `kitStatus` containing `the kit has no such study`; over the kit opened read-only, `StudyCommand (CreateStudy …)` is refused by the guard; in both, `kitStudies` and the folder's files are unchanged. `selecting a study shows its own fit runs, oldest first`: with `QZ-LR` and `LR` and two fit runs of each written before the load, `SelectStudy LR` gives `studyFitRuns` `LR`'s two, oldest first, and `fitRunOpt` the later; `SelectStudy` of an unknown name changes nothing. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the window holds studies, `OpenedKit` MUST carry the kit's studies and fit runs read at open, `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` MUST set `kitStudies` and `kitFitRuns`, and `StudyCommand` MUST apply a study message over `model.studyContext` and record the answered study through `recordStudy`, telling a refusal and writing nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `opening a kit reads its studies and their fit runs, and a study file that does not read refuses the open`, `a loaded kit's studies and fit runs are the window's, and Reload reads a study another writer wrote`, `CreateStudy from the window records the study, selects it and clears the New study form`, `a refused study message is told and records nothing, and a read-only kit takes none` and `selecting a study shows its own fit runs, oldest first`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests.opening a kit reads its studies and their fit runs, and a study file that does not read refuses the open","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitOpeningTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitOpeningTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.a loaded kit's studies and fit runs are the window's, and Reload reads a study another writer wrote","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.CreateStudy from the window records the study, selects it and clears the New study form","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.a refused study message is told and records nothing, and a read-only kit takes none","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.selecting a study shows its own fit runs, oldest first","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.OpenedKit.studies","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.OpenedKit.fitRuns","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.StudySurfaceState","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitStudies","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.kitFitRuns","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.studySurface","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.studyContext","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.selectedStudyOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.studyFitRuns","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.StudyCommand","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SelectStudy","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetNewStudyName","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ToggleNewStudyExperiment","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-STUDIES"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":411,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115g","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[410],"how_to":"The unknowns table fixes and frees a parameter, and sets its bounds and prior, through the Items panel's parameter editor, so one editor serves an item's parameter and an opened material's component (001 §O 'the unknowns table (owner, scope, fix / free, bounds, priors, links)'; 001 §O 'Items panel: … a parameter grid (state, value, bounds, σ, provenance)'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). The draft is keyed by the study's parameter reference (`StudyParameterRef`, step 358) in place of an item id and a name, and the editor's view becomes a function both surfaces call; a new function rather than a flag on the old one (the S11.5 brief's study view). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ParameterEditDraft` (step 240) holds `parameter : StudyParameterRef` in place of `itemId : ItemId` and `name : ParameterName`; `ofParameter` takes `(parameter : StudyParameterRef) (current : Parameter)`, and `tryState` names `this.parameter.name` where it named the name; every other field and rule is unchanged. `EditItemParameter name` opens `ParameterEditDraft.ofParameter (ItemParameterRef (<the selected item's id>, name))` of the selected item's parameter, as before. `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `EditStudyParameter of StudyParameterRef`, documented in one line: a press of a parameter row of the study's unknowns table; its arm opens the draft of an `ItemParameterRef (id, name)` of `kitItems` or of a `MaterialParameterRef (version, name)` of the chosen study's opened material of that version (`model.selectedStudyOpt`, step 410), and changes nothing when neither holds it. It writes nothing, so it is behind no guard. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ItemsPanelView.fs` (step 241): the editor block becomes `parameterEditorView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (draft : ParameterEditDraft) (setWith : ParameterState -> TableAndElementRotationMsg) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`, public and documented in one to three lines: the block moved whole, its ids, texts, colours and rules unchanged, its `Set` sending `setWith state`. The Items panel shows it when `parameterEditOpt` holds an `ItemParameterRef` of the selected item, with `setWith` `fun state -> SetParameterState (item.id, name, state)` (step 240), so the panel's behaviour is unchanged. The study's unknowns table calls it (step 414). No other view changes. Tests. `ItemsPanelModelTests` (step 240): `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets` keeps its assertions over the draft's `parameter`, `ItemParameterRef (CPL1's id, c2.retardance)`, where it read the item id and the name. `StudyWindowModelTests` (step 410) gains `the study's parameter editor opens on an item parameter or an opened material component, and a parameter it lacks opens nothing`: `EditStudyParameter (ItemParameterRef (CPL1's id, c2.retardance))` opens a draft of `UnknownStateChoice` starting at 1.5 within [1, 2]; with an absorbing crystal material opened by `QZ-LR` (`StudyCommand (OpenMaterial …)` over a user material saved through the window's `materials`, as `StudyMessageTests` saves its own, step 366), `EditStudyParameter (MaterialParameterRef (<its version>, n1))` opens a draft of `KnownStateChoice` at the material's `n1`; and a reference to a parameter neither holds leaves `parameterEditOpt` `None`. `ItemsPanelTests`' `the parameter editor offers Known and Unknown, and Set and Cancel on one row` (step 241) runs as written over the moved block.","acceptance":"After the editor is shared, `ParameterEditDraft` MUST be keyed by a `StudyParameterRef`, `EditStudyParameter` MUST open it on an item parameter or an opened material component, and `ItemsPanelView.parameterEditorView` MUST be the one editor view, the Items panel unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the study's parameter editor opens on an item parameter or an opened material component, and a parameter it lacks opens nothing`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ItemsPanelView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests.the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PARAMETER-EDITOR"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.the study's parameter editor opens on an item parameter or an opened material component, and a parameter it lacks opens nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-PARAMETER-EDITOR"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ParameterEditDraft","op":"change_shape","obligations":["S115-PARAMETER-EDITOR"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs"},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.EditStudyParameter","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-PARAMETER-EDITOR"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ItemsPanelView.parameterEditorView","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ItemsPanelView.fs","obligations":["S115-PARAMETER-EDITOR"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":412,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115h","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[411],"how_to":"The constructor window runs a study's fit off the UI thread through a job host its shell carries, and a completed fit's run joins the window's history at once (001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`, with progress and cancel; the fit run is written on completion'; 001 §P `RunFit`; .spec-md §10.2 'one fit iteration … a progress bar with Cancel, through `JobRunner`', §10.3 'Fits … are one click with Cancel', §10.4 'The job's completion message updates the Elmish model, so the fit-run history, the results tabs … re-render without a manual reload'). It hosts S11.3's fit job (`StudyFitJob.fs`, step 393) as Send kit hosts its archive job (steps 200, 201): the host in the shell, the state in the model, the message wrapping `StudyFitMsg`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs`: `StudyFitJobHost` (step 393) gains `static member inert : StudyFitJobHost`, which runs nothing and answers a handle that does nothing, `KitArchiveJobHost.inert`'s shape (step 200): the default of a scene that runs no fit. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `KitWindowShell` (steps 186, 201) gains `studyFits : StudyFitJobHost`, documented in one line; `KitWindowShell.inert` holds `StudyFitJobHost.inert`, so every shell built as an update of `inert` keeps its behaviour until the windows compose the real host (step 419). (b) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `studyFit : StudyFitJobState` (step 393) after `studySurface` (step 410), documented in one line; `initWith` sets `StudyFitJobState.idle`. (c) On the model extension holding `studyContext` (step 410): `member model.studyForwardContext : StudyForwardContext` (step 372) = `{ kit = model.studyContext; library = model.library; materials = model.materials; experimentData = model.experimentData; choiceOf = model.tryItemModelChoice; solverParameters = SolverParameters.defaultValue }` (`Berreman/Berreman/Solvers.fs:SolverParameters.defaultValue`), documented in one line. (d) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `StudyFit of StudyFitMsg`, documented in one line: the Fit step's verbs and the fit job's own progress and end. (e) The arm. `StudyFit (RunFit _)` goes through step 185's read-only guard first, because a fit writes its fit run (step 384). Every `StudyFit msg` is then `msg.updateWith (StudyFitEnvironment.create model.kitShell.studyFits model.kit.proxy model.studyForwardContext model.kit.clock) model.studyFit` (step 393), the model taking the answered state: one fit at a time, the run written on completion only, nothing on cancel or error. After `StudyFitEnded (Ok run)`, when the answered state's job is `Completed` with `committedResults = Some run.name` (`JobRunner.fs:JobModel`) and its `errorOpt` is `None`, `kitFitRuns` gains `run` at its end and `studySurface.fitRunOpt` becomes `Some run.name`, so the history and the results show it with no reload; when the kit refused it (`FitRunKitErr`), the error stays in the state for the Fit step to show (step 415) and `kitFitRuns` is unchanged. No queue, retry, second job or option is added. Tests, in `StudyWindowModelTests` (step 410), the shell's `studyFits` being either `StudyFitJobHost.posting` whose `post` calls at once and whose `progressed` and `ended` record `StudyFit (StudyFitProgressed _)` and `StudyFit (StudyFitEnded _)`, which the fact passes back through `updateTableAndElementRotation` in order after waiting on a `ManualResetEventSlim` with a ten-second limit, never a sleep (`StudyFitJobTests`' host, step 393), or a test-local host record whose `startStudyFit` records the job and answers a handle that records its cancel. `RunFit starts one fit through the shell's host, Cancel cancels it, and a read-only kit starts none`: with `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2, `StudyFit (RunFit { study = QZ-LR; stage = JointStage; calibrationUse = CalibrationHeldFixed })` over the recording host leaves `studyFit.job.isRunning` and one recorded job; a second `RunFit` records none; `StudyFit CancelStudyFit` records the cancel; over the kit opened read-only the guard refuses `RunFit` and no job is recorded. `a fit's end writes its fit run into the kit and shows it in the history at once`: after a recorded start, `StudyFit (StudyFitEnded (Ok <a test-local fit run of QZ-LR>))` leaves `readFitRuns QZ-LR` answering the run, `kitFitRuns` ending with it and `studySurface.fitRunOpt` naming it; the same end when the kit already holds that run leaves `kitFitRuns` unchanged and `studyFit.errorOpt` holding `FitRunKitErr (FitRunExistsErr _)`. `a fit that cannot run tells why and writes nothing`: over the posting host, after `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (Empty, []))`, `RunFit` of `Empty`, a study of no experiment, ends with `studyFit.errorOpt` holding `FitStageErr (NoStageRunErr _)` (step 385), the job not running and the kit holding no `.fitrun-json`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the fit is hosted, `StudyFit` MUST run a study's fit through the shell's `StudyFitJobHost` over `model.studyForwardContext`, refused under a read-only kit, and a completed fit's run MUST join `kitFitRuns` and be chosen with no reload while an error stays in `studyFit`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RunFit starts one fit through the shell's host, Cancel cancels it, and a read-only kit starts none`, `a fit's end writes its fit run into the kit and shows it in the history at once` and `a fit that cannot run tells why and writes nothing`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.RunFit starts one fit through the shell's host, Cancel cancels it, and a read-only kit starts none","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.a fit's end writes its fit run into the kit and shows it in the history at once","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.a fit that cannot run tells why and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitJob.StudyFitJobHost.inert","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.KitWindowShell.studyFits","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.studyFit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.studyForwardContext","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.StudyFit","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-FIT"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":413,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[412],"how_to":"Publish calibration and Promote to library as semantic messages of the constructor window (001 §P `PublishCalibration`, `PromoteToLibrary`; 001 §I 'Revisions … \"Publish calibration\" writes the next revision', 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database'; .spec-md §4 'UI'). The arms call the Domain members (steps 406, 408) and record items through the kit as the Items panel does (step 240); the Publish step's buttons send them (step 418). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `PublishCalibration of FitRunName` (publish the run's item calibrations as the items' next revisions) and `PromoteToLibrary of FitRunName * PromotionSubject` (step 407). (2) Arms. Both go through step 185's read-only guard first. The run is the one of `kitFitRuns` of that name and its study the one of `kitStudies` the run names; a miss sets `kitStatus` to `The kit holds no fit run <name>.` and changes nothing. `PublishCalibration`: `study.calibratedItemsWith run model.kitItems` (step 406); `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Nothing was published — <e.describe>`; `Ok items` records each item, in order, through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordItem` (step 219), which snapshots its model and writes `<label>.item-json`, each recorded item replacing its old self in `kitItems`; all recorded, `kitStatus` is `Published the calibration of <the labels, comma-separated> from <the run's name>.`; the first write error stops it, the items recorded before it staying recorded (each item file is written whole, step 218), and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `PromoteToLibrary (name, subject)`: for `MaterialPromotion version`, the entry `model.materials.resolveVersion version` answers (`Ok None` or `Error _` setting `kitStatus` to `The material version could not be read.`) and then `promoteMaterial study run version entry` (step 408); for `BlackBoxPromotion id`, the item of `kitItems` with that id and its `model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 263; a miss setting `kitStatus` to `The item or its model is not in the kit.`) and then `promoteBlackBox run item choice`; `Ok version` sets `kitStatus` to `Promoted to the library as <version.describe>.` and `Error e` to `Not promoted — <e.describe>`. Nothing else in the model changes: the library windows read the stores, and the member writes the kit's snapshot. No undo is added: publishing keeps every replaced value in the item's history (step 235), and promoting replaces nothing (step 408). No other message or option is added. Tests, in `StudyWindowModelTests`, over its kit with the study `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2 whose link makes CPL2's `c2.retardance` follow CPL1's (`StudyCommand (LinkParameters …)`), and a test-local fit run of it written through `writeFitRun` before the load, fitting CPL1's `c2.retardance` (`ItemOwner`) at 1.55 with σ 0.002, named `QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z`. `PublishCalibration records each calibrated item's next revision in the kit and tells which`: `PublishCalibration` of the run leaves `kitItems`' CPL1 and CPL2 at revision 2 holding that calibration, `readItems ()` answering them, and `kitStatus` `Published the calibration of CPL1, CPL2 from QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z.`. `a publish the run refuses, or of a fit run the kit lacks, is told and records nothing`: `PublishCalibration` of the same run again sets `kitStatus` containing `the calibration is already published`, and of a name the kit lacks `The kit holds no fit run`; `kitItems` and the item files are unchanged by either. `PromoteToLibrary of a fitted material mints its next library version and snapshots it into the kit`: with a user absorbing crystal material saved through the window's `materials` (as `StudyMessageTests` saves its own, step 366), opened by `QZ-LR` and fitted by a second run (`n1` at 1.7, `MaterialOwner`), `PromoteToLibrary (<that run>, MaterialPromotion <its version>)` sets `kitStatus` to `Promoted to the library as <the material's GUID> v2.`, `model.catalogueImports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope` of version 2 holds `FitProvenance`, and the kit's `paths` hold `library/<the GUID>@v2.material-json`. `a read-only kit publishes and promotes nothing`: over the kit opened read-only, both messages are refused by the guard, and the folder's files and `tryHeldEntry` of the material are unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the publishing messages land, `PublishCalibration` MUST record every item a fit run calibrates at its next revision through `recordItem`, and `PromoteToLibrary` MUST promote a material or black box through `promoteMaterial` / `promoteBlackBox`, each telling its outcome in `kitStatus` and writing nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `PublishCalibration records each calibrated item's next revision in the kit and tells which`, `a publish the run refuses, or of a fit run the kit lacks, is told and records nothing`, `PromoteToLibrary of a fitted material mints its next library version and snapshots it into the kit` and `a read-only kit publishes and promotes nothing`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.PublishCalibration records each calibrated item's next revision in the kit and tells which","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-PUBLISH"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.a publish the run refuses, or of a fit run the kit lacks, is told and records nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-PUBLISH"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.PromoteToLibrary of a fitted material mints its next library version and snapshots it into the kit","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-PUBLISH"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.a read-only kit publishes and promotes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-PUBLISH"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.PublishCalibration","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-PUBLISH"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.PromoteToLibrary","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-WINDOW-PUBLISH"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":414,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115j","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[413],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"],"how_to":"The study view's first flow step, Unknowns: the kit's studies, a New study form, the study's experiments and opened materials, and the unknowns table (001 §O 'Study view: the unknowns table (owner, scope, fix / free, bounds, priors, links)'; 001 §O 'a left flow strip: Items → Setups → Experiments → Data → Unknowns → Plan → Fit → Results → Publish, each step reachable directly'; 001 §P `CreateStudy`, `AddExperimentsToStudy`, `OpenMaterial`, `SetParameterScope`, `LinkParameters`; the S11.5 brief; .spec-md §3.22: a step appears when it works). The study's steps are the Inverse constructor's alone, as Data is (step 323), because studies fit measured data. The surface is a step of the kit window, not a window, so no `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` call is added; it joins `ScrollExtentTests` (.spec-md §4 'UI'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the Data step's (step 323) under `// --- The study's Unknowns step (StudyUnknownsView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `flowUnknownsStep` (`\"FlowUnknownsStep\"`), `studyUnknownsPanel` (`\"StudyUnknownsPanel\"`), `studyList` (`\"StudyList\"`), `studyStatusLine` (`\"StudyStatusLine\"`), `newStudyNameField` (`\"NewStudyNameField\"`), `createStudyButton` (`\"CreateStudyButton\"`), `studyExperimentsText` (`\"StudyExperimentsText\"`) and `studyUnknownsGrid` (`\"StudyUnknownsGrid\"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S11.5: `studyChoice (name : StudyName)` is `StudyChoice_<the name's file stem>`; `newStudyExperimentToggle (name : ExperimentName)` is `NewStudyExperiment_<its file stem>`; `addExperimentToStudyButton (name : ExperimentName)` is `AddExperimentToStudy_<its file stem>`; `openMaterialButton (version : MaterialVersionId)` is `OpenMaterial_<the GUID>_v<n>`; and `studyParameterRow`, `studyParameterScopeChoice` and `studyParameterLinkChoice (parameter : StudyParameterRef)` are `StudyParameterRow_`, `StudyParameterScope_` and `StudyParameterLink_` followed by `<the item's GUID>_<name>` or `<the material's GUID>_v<n>_<name>`, one private helper writing that key. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` (steps 238, 242, 323) gains `UnknownsFlowStep` after `DataFlowStep`, its `caption` `Unknowns` and its `flowUiId` `flowUnknownsStep`; `all` lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data and Unknowns, and `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` answers `all` without Data and the study's steps. `ShowFlowStep` of a step `stepsOf model.constructorMode` lacks changes nothing, and `ShowFlowStep UnknownsFlowStep` otherwise sets `flowStep` alone, the open bay kept; `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` from a step `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` lacks lands on `ExperimentsFlowStep` with `BayNames.experiments`, as from Data (step 323). On the model extension holding `studyContext` (step 410): `member model.studyParameterCaption (parameter : StudyParameterRef) : ControlCaption`, `<the item's label> <name>` or `<the material's name> v<n> <name>` (a material named through `model.materials.resolveVersion`, its GUID when that answers nothing), documented in one line. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyUnknownsView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyUnknownsView`, compiled directly after `DataStepView.fs` (step 323) and before `KitWindowView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment; its module doc one to three lines citing 001 §O and spec 0050 S11.5. (a) `studyBarView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`, the head every study surface shows (steps 415, 417, 418): the semi-bold `Study:`, a `WrapPanel` carrying `studyList` with one box per study of `kitStudies` carrying `studyChoice` and the name, sending `SelectStudy`, the chosen one an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the others `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton`s (step 241's chosen-option look), or the line `This kit holds no study yet.`; then, when `kitStatus` is `Some`, its text in a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `studyStatusLine`. (b) `studyUnknownsView (model) (dispatch) : IView`: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `studyUnknownsPanel`, margin 8, holding in order: the study bar; while `model.kitWrites` (step 185) offers writes, the New study form: a `DockPanel` of `New study:` and a `TextBox` carrying `newStudyNameField` whose every change sends `SetNewStudyName`, a `WrapPanel` of one box per kit experiment carrying `newStudyExperimentToggle` and its name, sending `ToggleNewStudyExperiment`, a chosen one on `positiveBackground`, and `Create study` (`createStudyButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, present only when `StudyName.tryCreate` of the typed text answers `Ok name`, sending `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (name, <the chosen experiments>))`); then, for `model.selectedStudyOpt`: `Experiments: <its experiments' names, comma-separated>` (`studyExperimentsText`), and while writes are offered, one verb per kit experiment the study lacks, `Add <name>` (`addExperimentToStudyButton`, sending `StudyCommand (AddExperimentsToStudy (study.name, [ name ]))`), and one verb per material version that a sample of the study's items references (`model.tryItemModelChoice` answering `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, _, sample)`, its `structure.referencedMaterialVersions`, step 61) and the study has not opened, `Open <its caption>` (`openMaterialButton`, sending `StudyCommand (OpenMaterial (study.name, version))`); then a `Grid` carrying `studyUnknownsGrid`, eight `Auto` columns `Owner`, `Parameter`, `State`, `Value`, `Bounds`, `σ`, `Scope` and `Link`, a semi-bold header row and one row per parameter of `model.studyContext.itemsUsedBy study` (step 366) in order as `ItemParameterRef`s, then per component of each opened material in study order as `MaterialParameterRef`s: the owner (the item's label, or `<the material's name> v<n>`); a box carrying `studyParameterRow` with the name, sending `EditStudyParameter` (step 411); the parameter's `gridCells` (step 241) for state, value, bounds and σ; for an unknown, a `ComboBox` carrying `studyParameterScopeChoice` over `ParameterScope.all`'s `text`s, `study.scopeOf` (step 362) selected, enabled by writes, whose change sends `StudyCommand (SetParameterScope (study.name, { parameter = <it>; scope = <the chosen> }))`, and `—` otherwise; for a link's follower, `= <its leader's studyParameterCaption>`, and for any other unknown a `ComboBox` carrying `studyParameterLinkChoice` over `(no link)` and every other unknown's caption, enabled by writes, whose choice of an unknown sends `StudyCommand (LinkParameters (study.name, { follower = <it>; leader = <the chosen> }))`. Fix and free are the editor's Known and Unknown, bounds and prior its fields: with `parameterEditOpt` open on a row the grid lists, `ItemsPanelView.parameterEditorView model draft setWith dispatch` (step 411) follows the grid, `setWith` being `fun state -> SetParameterState (id, name, state)` for an `ItemParameterRef (id, name)` and `fun state -> StudyCommand (SetOpenedMaterialParameter (study.name, version, { name = name; state = state }))` (step 409) for a `MaterialParameterRef (version, name)`. Without a chosen study the panel ends with `No study is chosen: create one above.`. No unlink verb is added: 001 §P names `LinkParameters` alone, and the follower keeps its own state. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs` (steps 242, 323): `UnknownsFlowStep` shows `StudyUnknownsView.studyUnknownsView model dispatch` keyed `unknowns`. No other surface changes. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs` (step 83) gains `studyKitIn (owner : FolderName) : TableAndElementRotationModel`, with a one-line doc citing spec 0050 S11.5, the one study fixture of the UI suite: over `freshAppContext owner` and a kit from `openedKitIn owner` (step 152), it records through the kit's library (`recordItem`, `recordSetup`, `recordExperiment`, steps 219, 260, 149) CPL1 and CPL2 over the built-in circular-polarizer model, each `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2], and a Phone over the intensity-detector model, `gain` unknown from 1000 within [100, 10000], one setup `Bench` holding them, and E1, E2 and E3, Science runs scanning the analyzer's R1 over 0…90° in 4 points (as step 310's facts record a one-axis scan), E1 and E3 attached at `data/e1.csv` and `data/e3.csv` (`Intensity series`, every row) and E2 without data; closes the kit, opens it again through `KitOpening.openKitAt`, loads it into an Inverse model over the context's stores as `InverseConstructorTests.inverse` builds its model (step 152), and sends `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (QZ-LR, [ E1; E2; E3 ]))`. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs`, `module StudyViewTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, its screens mounted as `KitWindowTests` mounts `kitWindowView` (step 242). Without a trait: `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the eight fixed ids' texts and the derived ids of `QZ-LR`, `E1`, CPL1's `c2.retardance` and a test-local material version's `n1`; `the Unknowns step lists the study's item parameters and opened material components with their owner, state, bounds, sigma, scope and link`: over `studyKitIn` with a user absorbing crystal material saved through the context's material store and opened (`StudyCommand (OpenMaterial …)`) and CPL2's `c2.retardance` linked to CPL1's, on `UnknownsFlowStep`, the grid holds the rows of CPL1, CPL2 and the Phone in that order and then the material's fifteen components, the Phone's `gain` row reading `Unknown` and `Session`, CPL2's `c2.retardance` reading `= CPL1 c2.retardance`, and a known parameter's scope cell `—`. With trait `ui-smoke`: `typing a study name and pressing Create study records the study in the kit`: pressing `flowUnknownsStep`, typing `LR` into `newStudyNameField`, pressing E1's `newStudyExperimentToggle` and `createStudyButton` leaves the kit's folder holding `LR.study-json` over E1 and `studyChoice` of `LR` shown; `pressing a study parameter's row, Unknown and Set frees it in the kit`: pressing the Phone's `darkOffset` row, `parameterEditUnknownChoice`, typing `-1` and `1` into `parameterEditLowerField` and `parameterEditUpperField` and pressing `parameterEditSetButton` leaves `Phone.item-json` holding `darkOffset` unknown within [−1, 1] and its row reading `Unknown`. `KitWindowTests` (steps 242, 323): `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowUnknownsStep`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds, in the inverse window, the Unknowns box below Data and, on `UnknownsFlowStep`, `studyUnknownsPanel` present and `tableElementCanvas` absent, and in the Main window no Unknowns box; `a read-only window withholds every write control` finds in `studyUnknownsView` over the read-only model no `createStudyButton`, no `addExperimentToStudyButton` and every `studyParameterScopeChoice` disabled. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 238, 323): `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data and Unknowns with their captions; `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it` also finds `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` without Unknowns, `ShowFlowStep UnknownsFlowStep` over `initMain ()` changing nothing, and `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` from `UnknownsFlowStep` answering `ExperimentsFlowStep`. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"KitWindowUnknowns\"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over `studyKitIn`'s model on `UnknownsFlowStep`, its material opened, the editor open on CPL1's `c2.retardance`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the Unknowns step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST show Unknowns after Data and the Main constructor's none, and `studyUnknownsView` MUST show the kit's studies, the New study form, the chosen study's experiments, material offers and unknowns table (owner, state, value, bounds, σ, scope, link) under their `ConstructorUiId`s, sending the study messages and opening the shared parameter editor, every write control withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` and `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `typing a study name and pressing Create study records the study in the kit` and `pressing a study parameter's row, Unknown and Set frees it in the kit`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the Unknowns step lists the study's item parameters and opened material components with their owner, state, bounds, sigma, scope and link` and `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyUnknownsView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S115-UNKNOWNS-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalCo