{"number": 416, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S115l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [415], "actions": ["DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests -> OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"], "how_to": "The solver hand-off stub goes: the Inverse flow ends at the study view, whose Fit step lists the moved pre-fit checks (001 §R '`SolverHandoffView`'s stub screen, replaced by the study view. Its three validation checks are reused as the study's pre-fit checks'; 001 §S11 'DELETE the `SolverHandoffView` stub, reusing its checks as pre-fit validation'; .spec-md §0.1 'Deleted. Their three checks become the study's pre-fit validation'; the S11.5 brief; AGENTS.md 'No legacy': superseded code is deleted in the change that replaces it). The checks moved in step 369 (`Experiment.prefitCheckWith`) and are listed by step 415, so nothing they do is lost. No product code opens the window: only the tests' root factory keys it (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:rootWindowFactory`). Each doc touched keeps one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) Deleted: `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs` and `SolverHandoffWindow.fs`, with their two `<Compile>` lines and the comment above them in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:106-113`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs`: the `SolverHandoffWindowKey` case (`WindowLauncher.fs:37`) goes, and the docs that name the solver hand-off (`WindowLauncher.fs:4`, the `WindowKey` doc) name the single-instance windows that remain, in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: the five `solverHandoff…` members and their group comment (`UiIds.fs:274-279`) go; `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `solverHandoffRow` and `solverHandoffStatus` with their doc (`ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:58-61`) go. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line and the comment above it in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`: `CollectionName` and `ExperimentCollectionSnapshot` were kept for the hand-off alone (step 152), and the kit's experiments are what a study reads. Any remaining `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentCollectionStore` goes with it. (5) Docs and comments: `ExperimentDataLoad.fs`' module doc (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:8-10`) and its `<Compile>` comment in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` drop 'the future `SolverHandoffWindow`', naming the study's pre-fit (step 369) in no more words; `PrefitChecks.fs` keeps no doc naming the deleted view; the `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` comment above `WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs` drops 'the SolverHandoff'; and any comment in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj` or `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs` that still names `CollectionName` or `ExperimentCollectionSnapshot` names the kit's experiment files. Each is cut to the words that stay true; no comment is added to a project file. (6) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line and comment. Its eight validation facts test the checks step 369 moved, which `PrefitCheckTests` proves (`a slot other than a sample's must hold an item or a binding, and a setup the kit lacks is named`, `an experiment without data fails the data check`, `a data file that does not read is unreadable, and points outside the scan are inconsistent`, `a ready experiment answers its kept, validated points`) and `InverseConstructorTests`' `the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path` covers, so they are deleted. Its three view facts move to `StudyViewTests` over step 414's `studyKitIn`, its model's `experimentData` a test-local proxy answering `readMapped` by attachment path (E1's a 3-point series inside the scan, E3's a series holding x = 120) and `attachmentStatus` with `AttachedDataUnchanged`, as the deleted facts' mocks did: without a trait, `the Fit step checks every run the fit reads, in study order, under the chosen study`: `model.studyPrefitsOpt` answers E1 `Ok` of 3 points, E2 `MissingDataErr` and E3 `InconsistentDataErr`, in that order, under `QZ-LR`; with trait `ui-smoke`, `the Fit step mounts its pre-fit list with one row per run the fit reads`: on `FitFlowStep` the mounted window carries `studyFitPanel` and `studyPrefitList` with one `studyPrefitRow` per run; and `a ready run shows its point count, and a run without data or out of range shows its typed message`: E1's row reads `E1: ready, 3 point(s)`, E2's holds `no data is attached` and E3's `the data does not fit the scan`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `the chart and solver-handoff windows leave everything reachable` becomes `the chart window leaves everything reachable`, its handoff `assertReachable` and the `noData` proxy it alone used (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:169-174`) going. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`: `handoffSnapshot` and the factory's `SolverHandoffWindowKey` arm (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:32-38`, `:50-51`) go, and `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff` becomes `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors and Data locations`, opening every key it opened but the hand-off's. `WindowLauncherTests`' `acceptance: a second open of the same WindowKey activates the live window instead of creating` drops `SolverHandoffWindowKey` from its keys (`WindowLauncherTests.fs:133`), its assertion kept. After this step `git grep -n -E \"SolverHandoff|solverHandoff|solver-handoff|HandoffReady|ExperimentHandoffStatus|ExperimentCollectionStore|ExperimentCollectionSnapshot\" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -w CollectionName -- Berreman/` find nothing.", "acceptance": "After the hand-off goes, `SolverHandoffView.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindow.fs`, `ExperimentCollectionStore.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindowKey`, the hand-off ids and `SolverHandoffWindowTests` MUST be gone, with nothing under `Berreman/` naming them, and the study view's Fit step MUST carry the moved view facts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, the count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass, including the moved `the Fit step mounts its pre-fit list with one row per run the fit reads` and `a ready run shows its point count, and a run without data or out of range shows its typed message`, the renamed `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors and Data locations` and the changed `acceptance: a second open of the same WindowKey activates the live window instead of creating`, the count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including the moved `the Fit step checks every run the fit reads, in study order, under the chosen study` and the renamed `the chart window leaves everything reachable`, the count falling by 8 as the eight deleted validation facts leave; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/WindowLauncher.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "