{"number":417,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115m","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[416],"how_to":"The study view's Results step: the chosen fit run's results in six tabs (001 §O 'results tabs: values, correlation, residuals, realizability, product check, profile likelihood'; 001 §L 'Results, stored in the fit run: value ± σ …; correlation matrix, rank, condition; per-experiment residuals and RMSE; Mueller realizability …; the product check …; post-fit identifiability by profile likelihood'). It shows what the fit run stores (`FitRun.results`, steps 396, 404) and computes nothing. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` gains `ResultsFlowStep` after `FitFlowStep`, its `caption` `Results` and its `flowUiId` `flowResultsStep`, one of the study's steps (step 414). Before `StudySurfaceState`: `FitResultsTab` = `ValuesResultsTab` | `CorrelationResultsTab` | `ResidualsResultsTab` | `RealizabilityResultsTab` | `ProductCheckResultsTab` | `ProfileResultsTab`, in 001 §O's order, with `static member all`, `member this.caption : ControlCaption` (`Values`, `Correlation`, `Residuals`, `Realizability`, `Product check`, `Profile likelihood`) and `member this.tabUiId : ConstructorUiId` (its box's id, below); window state, never stored, so no tag. `StudySurfaceState` gains `resultsTab : FitResultsTab`, `ValuesResultsTab` initially; `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ShowResultsTab of FitResultsTab`, which sets it and writes nothing. On the model extension holding `studyPrefitsOpt` (step 415), each documented in one line: `member model.selectedFitRunOpt : FitRun option`, the run of `model.studyFitRuns` that `fitRunOpt` names, else the latest of them, else `None`; `member model.ownerCaption (owner : UnknownOwner) : ControlCaption`, the item's label, `<the material's name> v<n>`, `session <name>` or `run <name>` (step 362); and `member model.fitEntryCaption (entry : FitEntryRef) : ControlCaption`, `<its owner's caption> <the parameter's name>` (step 396). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the Fit step's under `// --- The study's Results step (StudyResultsView). ---`, each with a one-line doc: `flowResultsStep` (`\"FlowResultsStep\"`), `studyResultsPanel` (`\"StudyResultsPanel\"`), `fitResultsRunText` (`\"FitResultsRunText\"`), `fitResultsTabStrip` (`\"FitResultsTabStrip\"`), `fitResultsValuesTab` (`\"FitResultsValuesTab\"`), `fitResultsCorrelationTab` (`\"FitResultsCorrelationTab\"`), `fitResultsResidualsTab` (`\"FitResultsResidualsTab\"`), `fitResultsRealizabilityTab` (`\"FitResultsRealizabilityTab\"`), `fitResultsProductCheckTab` (`\"FitResultsProductCheckTab\"`), `fitResultsProfileTab` (`\"FitResultsProfileTab\"`) and `fitResultsTable` (`\"FitResultsTable\"`, the shown tab's table). (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyResultsView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyResultsView`, compiled directly after `StudyFitView.fs` (step 415): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `studyResultsView (model) (dispatch) : IView`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `studyResultsPanel`, margin 8, holding `StudyUnknownsView.studyBarView` and, for `model.selectedFitRunOpt`: `Fit run <name> — <stage.text>, <engine.text>` (`fitResultsRunText`); a `WrapPanel` carrying `fitResultsTabStrip` of one box per `FitResultsTab.all` carrying its `tabUiId` with its `caption`, sending `ShowResultsTab`, the chosen one on `positiveBackground`; and the chosen tab's table carrying `fitResultsTable`, every number `ToString(\"G6\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)` as the parameter grid writes them (step 241). Values: a `Grid` of `Parameter`, `Start`, `Fitted` and `σ`, one row per `run.entries` entry (step 383) by `model.fitEntryCaption`, its σ that of `results.sigmas` or `undetermined`. Correlation: per `results.problems` element, the line `<subject>: rank <r>, condition <c or —>, χ² <x>, RMSE <rmse>` (`StudyEntriesProblem` written `Study residual`, `ObjectSolveProblem items` `Object <the items' labels>`, `AirFringeProblem runs` `AIR fringe <the runs>`), then, with a correlation matrix, a `Grid` whose header row and column are its coordinates (an `EntryCoordinate`'s entries' captions joined by `, `, `ElementCoordinate (r, c)` written `m<r><c>`, `FringeVisibilityCoordinate` written `fringe visibility`) and whose cells are ρ written `F3`, and without one the line `no correlation: the Jacobian is rank-deficient`. Residuals: per `results.runResiduals`, `<run>: RMSE <rmse> over <n> residual(s)`. Realizability: per `results.realizability`, `<the item's label>: realizable` or `not realizable` (`ObjectRealizability.realizability`, step 396), `; eigenvalues <the four>`. Product check: per `results.productChecks`, `<the items' labels joined by → >: product RMSE <p>, fit RMSE <f>, ratio <rmseRatio>, max |ΔM| <difference.maxAbs>` (steps 352, 400). Profile likelihood: per `results.profiles`, `<the entry's caption> (<its reasons>)`, each reason `σ undetermined`, `σ is <fraction> of its bounds` or `correlated with <the partner's caption> (ρ = <ρ>)`, then one line per point, `<value>: χ² <x>` or `<value>: <the failure's text>`. A tab with nothing reads `Nothing to show for this fit run.`; without a fit run the panel ends with `No fit run yet: run the fit in the Fit step.`. (4) `KitWindowView.fs`: `ResultsFlowStep` shows `StudyResultsView.studyResultsView model dispatch` keyed `results`. Tests. `StudyWindowModelTests` gains `a results tab and a fit run choose what the Results step shows, the study's latest run by default`: with two fit runs of `QZ-LR` loaded and `fitRunOpt` `None`, `selectedFitRunOpt` is the later; after `SelectFitRun` of the earlier it is the earlier; `ShowResultsTab CorrelationResultsTab` sets the surface's tab; `FitResultsTab.all` is the six in 001 §O's order with their captions. `StudyViewTests`: `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins the Results step's ids and each tab's `tabUiId`; without a trait, `the Results step shows the chosen fit run's six tabs and each tab's table`: over `studyKitIn` with a test-local fit run of `QZ-LR` written through `writeFitRun` whose results hold one value of each list (its correlation matrix 2 × 2 and its profile of seven points), as step 404's round-trip run holds them, on `ResultsFlowStep` with each tab chosen in turn through `ShowResultsTab`, `fitResultsTable` holds CPL1's `c2.retardance` with its σ, the study residual's rank and a 2 × 2 correlation grid, the run's RMSE, the realizable object's eigenvalues, the series' ratio and the profile's seven points; with trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing each results tab shows its table`: pressing each `tabUiId` in turn shows that tab's `fitResultsTable`. `KitWindowTests`: `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowResultsStep`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds the Results box below Fit and, on `ResultsFlowStep`, `studyResultsPanel`. `KitWindowModelTests`: `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` adds Results; `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it` also finds `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` without Results. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the kit window's Results step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"KitWindowResults\"` over `kitWindowView` on `ResultsFlowStep` with the correlation tab of a run whose problem holds a 16 × 16 correlation matrix.","acceptance":"After the Results step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST show Results after Fit, and `studyResultsView` MUST show the chosen fit run, the study's latest by default, in six tabs (values, correlation, residuals, realizability, product check, profile likelihood) of what its results store; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a results tab and a fit run choose what the Results step shows, the study's latest run by default`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` and `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing each results tab shows its table`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Results step shows the chosen fit run's six tabs and each tab's table` and `the kit window's Results step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyResultsView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests.a results tab and a fit run choose what the Results step shows, the study's latest run by default","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyWindowModelTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyWindowModelTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.the Results step shows the chosen fit run's six tabs and each tab's table","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.pressing each results tab shows its table","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Results step leaves everything reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.flowResultsStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.studyResultsPanel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsRunText","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsTabStrip","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsValuesTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsCorrelationTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsResidualsTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsRealizabilityTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsProductCheckTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsProfileTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.fitResultsTable","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ConstructorFlowStep.ResultsFlowStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.FitResultsTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.StudySurfaceState.resultsTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ShowResultsTab","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.selectedFitRunOpt","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.ownerCaption","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.fitEntryCaption","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyResultsView.studyResultsView","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyResultsView.fs","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView.kitWindowView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S115-RESULTS-STEP"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs"}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":418,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S115n","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[417],"how_to":"The study view's last flow step, Publish: the chosen fit run's calibration previewed and published, and its fitted materials and black boxes promoted to the library (001 §L 'Publishing: item → next revision (`Calibrated`); material or black-box object → Promote to library'; 001 §O 'a left flow strip: … → Results → Publish'; 001 §P `PublishCalibration`, `PromoteToLibrary`; .spec-md §10.5: an action that changes user-visible state names its undo or why it has none). The buttons send the window's messages (step 413), and the preview is the pure `calibratedItemsWith` (step 406), so what is shown is what is published. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` gains `PublishFlowStep` after `ResultsFlowStep`, its `caption` `Publish` and its `flowUiId` `flowPublishStep`, one of the study's steps (step 414); `all` now lists Items, Setups, Experiments, Data, Unknowns, Fit, Results and Publish, where S14.2 inserts Plan between Unknowns and Fit. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the Results step's under `// --- The study's Publish step (StudyPublishView). ---`, each with a one-line doc: `flowPublishStep` (`\"FlowPublishStep\"`), `studyPublishPanel` (`\"StudyPublishPanel\"`), `publishCalibrationPreview` (`\"PublishCalibrationPreview\"`), `publishCalibrationButton` (`\"PublishCalibrationButton\"`) and `promotionList` (`\"PromotionList\"`). `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `promoteButton (subject : PromotionSubject)` (step 407) is `Promote_<the material's GUID>_v<n>` or `Promote_<the item's GUID>`. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyPublishView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyPublishView`, compiled directly after `StudyResultsView.fs` (step 417): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `studyPublishView (model) (dispatch) : IView`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `studyPublishPanel`, margin 8, holding `StudyUnknownsView.studyBarView` and, for `model.selectedFitRunOpt` (step 417) of the chosen study: `Fit run <name>`; the semi-bold `Publish calibration`; a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `publishCalibrationPreview` showing `study.calibratedItemsWith run model.kitItems`: for `Ok items` one line per item, `<label> → revision <n>: <name> = <value> ± <σ>, …` of its published parameters, and for `Error e` its `describe` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`; `Publish calibration` (`publishCalibrationButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`), present only when the preview is `Ok` and writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185), sending `PublishCalibration run.name`; and the line `Publishing writes each item's next revision; the values it replaces stay in the item's revision history.` (no undo is needed: the history keeps them, step 235). Then the semi-bold `Promote to library` and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `promotionList`, one row per `run.promotionSubjectsWith study model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 407): `<the material's name> v<n> → its next library version` or `<the item's label> (black box) → a custom-Mueller polarizer`, with, while writes are offered, `Promote` (`promoteButton` of the subject, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`) sending `PromoteToLibrary (run.name, subject)`; or the line `This fit run fitted no material or black box.`; and the line `Promoting mints a new library version under the fit's provenance; the version the study opened stays as it is.` (nothing is replaced, step 408). `kitStatus` tells each outcome through the study bar (step 414). Without a fit run the panel ends with `No fit run yet: run the fit in the Fit step.`. (4) `KitWindowView.fs`: `PublishFlowStep` shows `StudyPublishView.studyPublishView model dispatch` keyed `publish`. Tests. `StudyViewTests`: `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins the Publish step's ids and `promoteButton` of each subject case; without a trait, `the Publish step previews the chosen run's calibration and lists what it can promote`: over `studyKitIn` with a test-local fit run of `QZ-LR` named `QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z`, written through `writeFitRun`, fitting CPL1's `c2.retardance` at 1.55 with σ 0.002 (`ItemOwner`), on `PublishFlowStep` the preview reads `CPL1 → revision 2: c2.retardance = 1.55 ± 0.002`, `publishCalibrationButton` is present, and `promotionList` reads `This fit run fitted no material or black box.`; with a QZ black-box item fitted by a second run and chosen through `SelectFitRun`, the list holds QZ's `promoteButton`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing Publish calibration writes the calibrated items' next revisions into the kit`: pressing `flowPublishStep` and `publishCalibrationButton` leaves `CPL1.item-json` at revision 2 holding the calibration and `studyStatusLine` reading `Published the calibration of CPL1 from QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z.`. `KitWindowTests`: `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowPublishStep`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds the Publish box below Results and, on `PublishFlowStep`, `studyPublishPanel`; `a read-only window withholds every write control` finds in `studyPublishView` over the read-only model neither `publishCalibrationButton` nor any `promoteButton`. `KitWindowModelTests`: `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` lists the eight steps with their captions; `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it` also finds `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` without Publish. `ScrollExtentTests` gains `the kit window's Publish step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"KitWindowPublish\"` over `kitWindowView` on `PublishFlowStep` over a run calibrating three items and promoting a material and a black box. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.","acceptance":"After the Publish step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST end with Publish after Results, and `studyPublishView` MUST preview the chosen fit run's calibration through `calibratedItemsWith`, offer Publish calibration and one Promote per subject `promotionSubjectsWith` lists, sending `PublishCalibration` and `PromoteToLibrary`, withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` and `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Publish calibration writes the calibrated items' next revisions into the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Publish step previews the chosen run's calibration and lists what it can promote` and `the kit window's Publish step leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyPublishView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.the Publish step previews the chosen run's calibration and lists what it can promote","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.pressing Publish calibration writes the calibrated items' next revisions into the kit","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Publish step leaves everything reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.flowPublishStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.studyPublishPanel","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.publishCalibrationPreview","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.publishCalibrationButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.promotionList","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.promoteButton","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ConstructorFlowStep.PublishFlowStep","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyPublishView.studyPublishView","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyPublishView.fs","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView.kitWindowView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S115-PUBLISH-STEP"],"path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs"}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":419,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-S115o","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[418],"how_to":"The constructor windows compose the real study-fit host, and the Inverse flow is proved end to end through a shown window and a real kit folder: it ends at the study view (the S11.5 brief 'The Inverse flow ends at the study view'; 001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`'; .spec-md §0.1 `Program.fs`; AGENTS.md: wait for deterministic conditions, drive by id). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (steps 189, 233, 312): the shell it builds gains `studyFits = StudyFitJobHost.onUiThread (fun p -> dispatch (StudyFit (StudyFitProgressed p))) (fun r -> dispatch (StudyFit (StudyFitEnded r)))` (steps 393, 412), over the dispatch the mount captures from its init command, so a fit runs on a thread-pool worker and its progress and end arrive on the window's own thread. The docs of `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` say, in no more words, that the Inverse window's study runs its fits off the UI thread. No other seam changes. (2) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'Lab files are read through import profiles' (step 312), one bullet of at most six lines: **The Inverse flow ends at the study** (`Studies.fs`, `StudyEngine.fs`, `StudyPublishing.fs`, spec 0050 S11): the Inverse constructor's flow strip adds Unknowns → Fit → Results → Publish after Data (S14 inserts Plan before Fit); a study fits experiments of one kit; its fit runs on `JobRunner` through the shell's `StudyFitJobHost` and writes one append-only `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json` on completion; Publish calibration writes each item's next revision (`CalibratedParameter`), and Promote to library mints the entry's next library version under `FitProvenance` and snapshots it into the kit. There is no hand-off window. Nothing else in the file changes. (3) Tests. `KitWindowTests` gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: the Inverse constructor creates a study in its kit and runs its fit off the UI thread, telling why it ended`: a shown `InverseConstructorWindow` over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitWindowTests\")` and a kit from `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` (step 152), driven by id at the controls' centres: pressing `flowUnknownsStep`, setting `newStudyNameField`'s text to `Empty` and pressing `createStudyButton`, then `flowFitStep` and `studyRunFitButton`, and waiting through `Dispatcher.UIThread.RunJobs` until `studyFitErrorText` shows text, within ten seconds and never by a sleep, leaves the kit's folder holding `Empty.study-json` and no `.fitrun-json`, and `studyFitErrorText` holding `the stage has no run to fit` (step 385's `NoStageRunErr` through `FitStageErr`, step 386): the fit ran through the real host on a worker and its end was posted back to the window. The windows' other consumers keep their assertions.","acceptance":"After the windows are wired, a constructor window's shell MUST hold `StudyFitJobHost.onUiThread` over the window's dispatch, a study created in a real Inverse window MUST be written to its kit and its fit MUST run off the UI thread and report its end in the Fit step, and AGENTS.md MUST carry the gotcha 'The Inverse flow ends at the study'; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Inverse constructor creates a study in its kit and runs its fit off the UI thread, telling why it ended`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","AGENTS.md","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppContextTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LauncherTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: the Inverse constructor creates a study in its kit and runs its fit off the UI thread, telling why it ended","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S115-WIRE"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.App.MainConstructorWindow","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S115-WIRE"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.App.InverseConstructorWindow","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S115-WIRE"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S11.5 -- Publishing, the study view; the solver hand-off stub goes"}
{"number":420,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S121a","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[419],"how_to":"A new kit's identity is injected, as an item's is, so a kit built twice by the same messages is the same kit file (001 §Q 'It asserts that the built kit equals the committed kit, file by file'; AGENTS.md 'Inject ambient effects (time, randomness) as provider records'; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO'). Today the one mint is `KitId (Guid.NewGuid ())` inside `KitOpening.openKitAt`'s read-write path (step 150), and no start-screen seam reaches it (steps 176, 177). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, directly after `ItemIdProvider` (step 236): `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitIdProvider = { mintKitId : unit -> KitId }`, the provider that mints a new kit's identity (step 24's `KitId`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, beside `ItemIdProvider.system` (step 239): `type KitIdProvider with static member system : KitIdProvider` mints `KitId (Guid.NewGuid ())` at each call. `openKitAt`'s body moves into `openKitWith (kitIds : KitIdProvider) (folder : KitFolder) (access : KitAccess) (clock : ClockProvider) (author : KitAuthor) (imports : CatalogueImportContext) : Result<OpenedKit, KitLibraryError>`, whose read-write path initialises an empty folder with `folder.namedKitFile (kitIds.mintKitId ()) author` (step 145) and calls `mintKitId` only when it initialises; `openKitAt` keeps its signature and is `openKitWith KitIdProvider.system`, so none of its callers changes. A read-only open never initialises and never calls the provider (step 150). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs`: `KitStartContext` (steps 176, 190, 230) gains `kitIds : KitIdProvider` directly after `clock`, and `CreateKit` (step 177) opens through `openKitWith m.context.kitIds` where it called `openKitAt`; `OpenKit`, `OpenKitReadOnly` and `OpenKitZip` are unchanged. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs` (steps 179, 230, 232) composes `kitIds = KitIdProvider.system`. Every other literal of `KitStartContext` (`KitStartTests.fs`; `KitStartWindowTests.fs` where it builds one) composes `KitIdProvider.system`, its assertions unchanged. No other field, message or option is added; `scratchKit` (step 150) keeps its mint, because a scratch kit is never written. (4) Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs`: `a new kit takes its id from the start screen's kit-id provider`: over a context whose `kitIds` answers `KitId (Guid.Parse \"e63c9d6e-7961-4d9f-9c8d-e5a151414e0e\")`, `CreateKit` of a fresh folder under the test output hands over a kit whose kit file holds that id, and `(KitProxy.create folder).readKitFile ()` reads the same id from `.kit-json`; `opening an existing kit, read-write or read-only, mints no kit id`: over a context whose `kitIds` counts its calls, `OpenKit` and `OpenKitReadOnly` of that kit (the second after the first is closed) hand it over with its stored id and the count stays 0.","acceptance":"After the provider lands, `CreateKit` MUST initialise a kit whose id the start screen's `KitIdProvider` mints, `openKitAt` MUST keep its signature over `KitIdProvider.system`, and opening an existing kit MUST mint no id; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a new kit takes its id from the start screen's kit-id provider` and `opening an existing kit, read-write or read-only, mints no kit id`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected class, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitStartWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.a new kit takes its id from the start screen's kit-id provider","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S121-KIT-IDS"]},{"op":"create","suite":"constructor-unit-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests.opening an existing kit, read-write or read-only, mints no kit id","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests","discovery_gate":"constructor-unit-tests","obligations":["S121-KIT-IDS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitIdProvider","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs","obligations":["S121-KIT-IDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.KitIdProvider.system","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","obligations":["S121-KIT-IDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitOpening.openKitWith","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs","obligations":["S121-KIT-IDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.KitStartContext.kitIds","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs","obligations":["S121-KIT-IDS"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView.updateKitStart","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S121-KIT-IDS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number":421,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S121b","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[420],"actions":["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"],"how_to":"AT-1 builds the optics-mueller kit (001 §1a; 001 §Q 'Common rules' 'Build: each test builds its kit ONLY through the semantic messages (§P), against a SQLite `:memory:` library, and writes it through the REAL folder `KitProxy` into a throw-away folder under the test run's output directory'; .spec-md §3.13). The class is the kit-acceptance gate's (001 §U; `.gates/OpticalConstructor/kit-acceptance.gates`, which runs `--filter-trait \"Category=kit-acceptance\"` in this project and which `ui-tests` excludes); from this step on it runs on every step that touches the study, the run law, the import code, this file or the kits. It follows `FsxAcceptanceTests`' pattern (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:runOnTable`): the app's own update functions (`updateKitStart`, step 176; `updateTableAndElementRotation`) fold the same semantic messages the controls send, and nothing is clicked. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs` (steps 83, 152, 154, 414): `inverseModelOver (context : AppContext) (opened : OpenedKit) : TableAndElementRotationModel`, with a one-line doc, is the Inverse model `studyKitIn` builds today (step 414: `initInverse` over the context's stores overlaid with `opened.overlay`, `loadKit opened`, and the item models and catalogue imports the window's seed threads, steps 154, 243); `studyKitIn` calls it in place of its own body, so one composition exists (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy') and `StudyViewTests` keeps its assertions. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs`, `module KitAcceptanceTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment (the project references `BerremanTestSupport` since step 347). Its module doc, one to three lines: AT-1 and AT-2 build the two reference kits through the app's messages and prove them against the committed kits (001 §Q; spec 0050 S12). Every fact carries `[<Trait(\"Category\", \"kit-acceptance\")>]`. (3) The build, a private function of the module that later steps extend and every AT-1 fact calls: `buildOpticsMuellerKit (run : FolderName)` answers the built folder, the app context, the window model and the test clock, in this order. (a) The folder is `<System.AppContext.BaseDirectory>/KitAcceptanceTests/<run>/optics-mueller`, created fresh, its leaf naming the kit (step 145's `namedKitFile`); the committed kit's `data/` tree (`CommittedKit.OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, `BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs`, steps 330, 344; .spec-md §3.21) is copied into it byte for byte, and nothing else. (b) The context is `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitAcceptanceTests\")`, a SQLite `:memory:` library filled from `Catalogue/Builtin` (steps 83, 100). (c) The clock is a test-local `ClockProvider` over a mutable cell holding `ClockTime` of 2026-05-31T12:00:00Z (UTC), which only the build advances (step 427), so every stamp the kit stores is fixed. (d) New kit: a `KitStartModel` from `initKitStart` over a `KitStartContext` of `KitHistoryProxy.createInMemory ()`, `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, the test clock, `kitIds` answering `KitId (Guid.Parse \"e63c9d6e-7961-4d9f-9c8d-e5a151414e0e\")` (step 420), `KitAuthor \"optics-mueller lab\"`, `context.catalogueImports`, `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf` the folder, a `showKit` that keeps the opened kit, `activateKitWindow` answering `NoKitWindowOpen`, `KitZipPicker.none`, `KitArchiveProxy.create ()` and `KitArchiveJobHost.inert`; `CreateKit` of the folder initialises it around its lab files (001 §F 'a folder that already has files keeps them'). The window model is `TestAppScope.inverseModelOver context <the opened kit>`, whose `itemIds` is replaced by a test-local `ItemIdProvider` answering, call by call, Laser `d4d8dfc0-3d43-4a24-853c-369479de4f5d`, LP1 `375bde88-fe45-4bd7-ad77-f13708076224`, LP2 `72d0505d-8685-4884-89ad-ea13694c8693`, CPL1 `0d2c2b6e-c91f-486b-b80b-a1b815c03aac`, CPL2 `b9f73589-6cfe-46d2-a5eb-2b11d6d6cd5f`, AIR `dc89cf47-6d94-4887-a0fb-49e3a8ca1cb4`, QZ `436f47ea-a1c4-47ed-8c5c-f09eae8098b1`, LR `69c2edf9-3a4d-4b23-bea2-94ba305ca507`, Phone `93fae6cc-d838-45b7-b5f0-949f7a759e91`. (e) The lab naming template: `SetNamingTemplateText (ControlCaption \"{source:LP1=LP,CPL1=CPL}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer:LP2=LP,CPL2=CPL}-{note}\")` and `SaveNamingTemplate` (step 273): `NamingTemplate.standard`'s placeholders (step 267) with the aliases that write the lab's parts `LP` and `CPL` for the items labelled `LP1`, `CPL1`, `LP2` and `CPL2` (step 268), because item labels are unique (001 §I) while the lab's names are not. (f) The nine items, each through `OpenAddItemForm`, `ChooseNewItemModel` of the form's offer, `SetNewItemLabel`, `SetNewItemDial` and `AddItem` of the form's draft (step 239), in this order: `Laser`, the `PresetIds.heNe633` source preset (the bench's red laser; a black-box reconstruction does not read the wavelength); `LP1` and `LP2`, the real linear polarizer (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`); `CPL1` and `CPL2`, the circular polarizer (`circularPolarizerModelId`, a linear polarizer then a retarder at 45° plus its offset, step 210); `AIR`, the empty slot (`emptySlotModelId`); `QZ` and `LR`, the black-box Mueller model (`blackBoxMuellerModelId`); `Phone`, the intensity detector (`intensityDetectorModelId`). `LP2` is `DialMounted DialNegative` and `CPL2` `DialMounted DialPositive` (the reference's analyzer conventions, `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_glue.py:185-189`); every other item is `FixedMounting`. Then `SetParameterState` (step 240) sets the unknowns, each an `UnknownParameter` with no prior and its start and bounds in the parameter's own unit (`Angle.parameterValue`, step 389): `LP2`'s `dialZero` from 152° within [0°, 360°] and `CPL2`'s from 80° within [0°, 360°] (the lab's mounting readings, optics-mueller `AGENTS.md`); `CPL2`'s and `CPL1`'s `c2.retardance` from 90° within [0°, 180°]; `CPL1`'s `c2.fastAxisOffset` from 0° within [−45°, 45°]; and each of `QZ`'s and `LR`'s sixteen `m<r><c>` (`ParameterName.muellerElement`, step 244) from its default within [−2, 2]. Every other parameter keeps its known default (the `Phone`'s `gain` 1 and `darkOffset` 0). (g) The table: the Inverse table's `src`, `sample` and `det` slots plus, through the table's own messages (`AddElement`, then the Move bay's along-beam messages where a slot's default place is not its light-order place), a polarizer slot before `sample`, a second sample slot after it and a polarizer slot after that, so `Setup.lightOrder` (step 257) reads Source, Prep 1, Obj 1, Obj 2, Analyzer 1, Detector 1; `AssignSlot` (step 263) puts `Laser` in Source and `Phone` in Detector 1. (h) The setups, by the grid generator (steps 274, 281, 282; 001 §J), the Experiments draft holding no capture so the grids record setups alone (step 276): grid one toggles `LP1` and `CPL1` on Prep 1, `AIR`, `QZ` and `LR` on Obj 1 with the angles 0°, 45° and 90° (`AddSetupGridAngle`), and `LP2` and `CPL2` on Analyzer 1, unticks the combinations of `AIR` at 45° and 90° (`ToggleSetupGridCombination`) and sends `GenerateSetupGrid model.setupGrid`; grid two (after `CloseSetupGrid` and `OpenSetupGrid`) toggles `LP1` and `CPL1`, `QZ` on Obj 1 and `LR` on Obj 2, each object at 0°, 45° and 90°, and both analyzers, unticks every combination whose two object angles differ, and generates. The template names them (001 §J 'two-sample setups put QZ in Object 1 and LR in Object 2'), forty in all: `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#0)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#45)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#90)-LP`, `LP-(LR#0)-LP`, `LP-(LR#45)-LP`, `LP-(LR#90)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#0-LR#0)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#45-LR#45)-LP`, `LP-(QZ#90-LR#90)-LP`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#0)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#45)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#90)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#45)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#90)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#0-LR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`, `LP-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#0)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#45)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#90)-LP`, `CPL-(LR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(LR#45)-LP`, `CPL-(LR#90)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-LP`, `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-LP`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(LR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL`, `CPL-(LR#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL`. Then the two setups the LR correction re-points to (001 §1a 'LR was labelled +45/+90 but physically sat at −45/−90'; step 424): `ActivateSetup` of `CPL-(LR#90)-CPL`, its Obj 1 slot's R1 set to −90° through the Rotate bay's messages, `SetSetupName (ControlCaption \"CPL-(LR#-90)-CPL\")` and `CreateSetup` (step 260); and the same from `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` with Obj 2 at −90° as `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#-90)-CPL`. Every write goes through the window's kit, which is `KitProxy.create` of the folder (step 126). (4) The fact `AT-1 builds the optics-mueller kit's items and setups through the app's messages`: after the build, a second `KitProxy.create` of the built folder reads `.kit-json` holding the id `e63c9d6e-7961-4d9f-9c8d-e5a151414e0e`, the name `optics-mueller`, the author `optics-mueller lab`, created and modified at 2026-05-31T12:00:00Z, the lab template, no import profile and no send exclusion; `readItems` the nine items with their ids, labels, models, dials, revision 1 and the unknowns above; `readSetups` exactly the forty-two setups named above, each in light order Source `Laser`, Prep 1 `LP1` or `CPL1` as its name's source part says, its objects and angles as its name says (the two corrected ones with LR at −90°), Analyzer 1 `LP2` or `CPL2`, Detector 1 `Phone`; every file under `library/` byte-identical to the built-in entry file of its id and version (`Catalogue/Builtin/`), the six entries the items instantiate among them; and every file under `data/` byte-identical to the committed kit's. Each assertion's message names the file and both values.","acceptance":"After AT-1's first part lands, `KitAcceptanceTests` MUST build the optics-mueller kit around a copy of the committed lab files through the start screen's and the kit window's messages alone, its kit file, nine items and forty-two setups as specified, and `studyKitIn` MUST build its model through `TestAppScope.inverseModelOver`; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `AT-1 builds the optics-mueller kit's items and setups through the app's messages`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected class, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","kit-acceptance","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"]},"kit-acceptance":{"mode":"selected","suite":"kit-acceptance","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"kit-acceptance","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests.AT-1 builds the optics-mueller kit's items and setups through the app's messages","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests","discovery_gate":"kit-acceptance","obligations":["S121-AT1-ITEMS-SETUPS"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestAppScope.inverseModelOver","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs","obligations":["S121-AT1-ITEMS-SETUPS"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number": 422, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S121c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [421], "how_to": "A lab group whose key the naming template cannot read reaches an experiment of its own name (001 §K 'One file → many experiments: split by a key column, match each group by the naming template, list the unmatched groups and offer to create setups for them'; 001 §Q AT-1 'Roles for Darkness, BullshitCheck and the AIR repeats'). Today such a group is `GroupWithoutMatch` (step 318) and no message gives it an experiment: `AttachDataFile` attaches every row (step 310), `MatchByTemplate` reaches an experiment only by its name or the template's (step 320), and no message names an experiment (steps 286, 290). The optics-mueller darkness and diagnostic captures (`Darkness`, `LP-(Darkness)-CPL2`, `BullshitCheck-2`, … in `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv` and `bullshit_checks.csv`) are such groups (step 269 refuses them by name). The user names the setup the capture was taken over; the experiment takes the key's name. The offer reuses step 320's ticked-offer path whole, so nothing is attached twice. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs` (steps 317, 318): `DataSplitError` gains `SplitKeyUnknownErr of reason : string` (`no group of the split has the key: <reason>`) and `SplitKeyReadableErr of reason : string` (`the group's setup comes from its key or its experiment: <reason>`). `type DataSplit with member this.withGroupOver (key : DataRowKey) (setup : Setup) (taken : ExperimentName list) : Result<DataSplit, DataSplitError>`: the group of that key whose matching is `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyNameErr _)` or `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeySetupErr _)` becomes `SetupOfferForGroup { setup = setup; experiment = <the key's name, key.nameText.toExperimentName (step 318's rule (a)), made free among taken by nextFreeAmong (step 286)> }`, every other group unchanged; no group of that key is `SplitKeyUnknownErr` naming the key; a group matched, offered, or unmatched for `SplitKeyTextErr` or `SplitKeyTwiceErr` is `SplitKeyReadableErr` naming the key. Every complete match on `DataSplitError` that FS0025 reports (`DataSplitError.caption` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, step 324) renders the two cases as it renders the others. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `OfferSplitGroupOver of DataRowKey * Kit.SetupName`, documented in one line. With `dataSplitOpt = Some s` (step 319) and a kit setup of that name in `model.kitSetups` (step 260) it sets `s.split` to `s.split.withGroupOver key setup <the kit experiments' names and every other offer's experiment>` and ticks the key in `s.creating`, as `ToggleSplitOffer` ticks an offer; it writes nothing, so it needs no read-only guard. No split is `kitStatus` `Not offered — no file is being split.`, an unknown setup `Not offered — the kit holds no setup <name>.`, and a refusal `Not offered — <e.describe>`. `MatchByTemplate` (step 320) is unchanged: it records a ticked offer's setup when the kit lacks it and appends a new experiment of the draft's scan, named by the offer, with the key's rows. (3) Tests. `DataSplitTests` (steps 317, 318), over its test-local kit: `a group the template cannot read is offered over the setup the user names, its experiment named by its key`: in a split of a Phone ROI CSV whose groups are `Darkness` and `CPL-(QZ#0)-CPL`, `withGroupOver (DataRowKey \"Darkness\") <a kit setup> []` answers `Darkness` offered over that setup with the experiment `Darkness`, and the other group unchanged; with `Darkness` taken, the experiment is `Darkness (2)`. `only a group without a readable setup is offered by hand, and an unknown key is refused`: the offered and the matched groups answer `SplitKeyReadableErr` and `Nothing` answers `SplitKeyUnknownErr`, each naming the key. `every split error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases. `DataSplitModelTests` (steps 319, 320): `offering an unreadable group over a kit setup ticks it, and applying the split records its experiment under the key's name with the key's rows`: over a folder kit holding a setup `Bench` and a draft with a scan and a capture, `SplitByColumn` of a file whose groups are `Darkness` and `BullshitCheck`, then `OfferSplitGroupOver (DataRowKey \"Darkness\", SetupName \"Bench\")` and `MatchByTemplate`, leave the kit holding the experiment `Darkness` over `Bench` with `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey \"Darkness\")` of the file and no experiment for `BullshitCheck`; `OfferSplitGroupOver` with no split or of an unknown setup writes nothing and tells why.", "acceptance": "After the offer lands, `DataSplit.withGroupOver` MUST offer a group the template cannot read over the setup the user names, its experiment named by its key, and refuse any other group or an unknown key, and `OfferSplitGroupOver` MUST tick that offer so `MatchByTemplate` records the experiment with the key's rows; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a group the template cannot read is offered over the setup the user names, its experiment named by its key`, `only a group without a readable setup is offered by hand, and an unknown key is refused`, the widened `every split error renders its condition and its payload` and `offering an unreadable group over a kit setup ticks it, and applying the split records its experiment under the key's name with the key's rows`, the count rising by 3; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "kit-acceptance", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "kit-acceptance": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "kit-acceptance", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.a group the template cannot read is offered over the setup the user names, its experiment named by its key", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.only a group without a readable setup is offered by hand, and an unknown key is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitTests.every split error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitTests.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests.offering an unreadable group over a kit setup ticks it, and applying the split records its experiment under the key's name with the key's rows", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DataSplitModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DataSplitModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.DataSplitError.SplitKeyUnknownErr", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.DataSplitError.SplitKeyReadableErr", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.DataSplits.DataSplit.withGroupOver", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.OfferSplitGroupOver", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.DataSplitError.caption", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-OVER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number": 423, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S121d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [422], "how_to": "The button for step 422's message: the user chooses, on an unmatched group's row of the split panel, the setup the capture was taken over (AGENTS.md 'Every user action is a semantic Elmish message. The button and the test send the same message'; 001 §O 'Data dialog: … the key split with a matched / unmatched table'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `dataSplitGroupRow` and `dataSplitOfferToggle` (step 324): `static member dataSplitGroupSetupChoice (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId`, `DataSplitGroupSetup_<the key's file stem>`, documented in one line. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`, the split panel (step 324): the row of a group whose matching is `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyNameErr _)` or `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeySetupErr _)` keeps its `unmatched — <describe>` text and gains, on the same row, `Record over:` and a `ComboBox` carrying `dataSplitGroupSetupChoice key`, listing `model.kitSetups`' names in kit order with nothing selected, whose choice sends `OfferSplitGroupOver (key, <the chosen name>)`; a kit holding no setup shows no box. An offered group keeps its toggle (`dataSplitOfferToggle`), so a group offered this way is ticked and untickable like any offer. No other control or text changes. (3) Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs` (step 324), mounted as its facts mount the Data step: `an unreadable group's row offers the kit's setups, and choosing one sends OfferSplitGroupOver`: over a model whose split lists `Darkness` unmatched for `SplitKeyNameErr` and a kit holding `Bench` and `Bench (2)`, the row of `Darkness` carries `DataSplitGroupSetup_Darkness` listing both names, choosing `Bench (2)` dispatches `OfferSplitGroupOver (DataRowKey \"Darkness\", SetupName \"Bench (2)\")`, and a matched or offered row carries no such box; `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also checks `dataSplitGroupSetupChoice (DataRowKey \"Darkness\")`'s text; `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row` also finds the box on the unmatched row of its fixture.", "acceptance": "After the panel lands, an unmatched group's row MUST offer the kit's setups through `dataSplitGroupSetupChoice` and send `OfferSplitGroupOver` on a choice; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected class, including `an unreadable group's row offers the kit's setups, and choosing one sends OfferSplitGroupOver` and the widened `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row`, its count rising by 1; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests", "kit-acceptance"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}, "kit-acceptance": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "kit-acceptance", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.an unreadable group's row offers the kit's setups, and choosing one sends OfferSplitGroupOver", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitGroupSetupChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S121-SPLIT-GROUP-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number": 424, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S121e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [423], "how_to": "AT-1's build gains the experiments and their data (001 §Q AT-1 'Attach, split by `experiment`, match by the lab template. Roles for Darkness, BullshitCheck and the AIR repeats. The LR correction and the excluded frame are applied as data'; 001 §K; 001 §1a). `buildOpticsMuellerKit` (step 421) continues, through the window's messages alone. (1) The draft: `ActivateSetup` of `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, `ExpChooseElement` of the Analyzer 1 slot, `ExpChooseVariable VaryDialReading` (0…360° over 19 points, offered because `LP2` is dial-mounted, step 289) and `ExpChooseMeasurement` of the capture the `Phone`'s slot offers: one experiment is one analyzer-dial sweep recorded as raw dial readings (001 §1a), every lab capture's description among those readings. (2) The data, file by file in this order: `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv`, `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv`, `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv`, `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv`, `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv`, `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv`, `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv`. For each, `SplitByColumn (FileName <its absolute name inside the built folder>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv)` (step 319: the Phone ROI CSV profile, `parseMuellerCsv`, split by `experiment`); `ToggleSplitOffer` of every group offered its setup and experiment by the template (step 318's rule (d): the forty grid setups hold every readable key); for the groups the template cannot read, `OfferSplitGroupOver` (step 422) over their family's AIR setup: `Darkness` over `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(Darkness)-CPL2` over `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(Darkness)-LP-2` and `-2R` over `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(Darkness)-LP-2` and `-2R` and both `BullshitCheck` captures over `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP` (the family each was taken in, by its name or its time); then `MatchByTemplate`. Each file is attached in place (step 134: a file inside the kit is recorded, never copied), so the kit's 53 experiments are the 53 groups, named by their keys, each with `KeyedDataRows` of its key. (3) Roles (`SetExperimentRole`, step 294): `CalibrationRun` for the nine AIR runs `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` (stage 1 calibrates on them and every session's gain anchors to them, 001 §L; a `DriftCheckRun` would be fitted as an object run by stage 2, step 385, which an AIR run cannot be), `DarkRun` for the six darkness captures, `DiagnosticRun` for `BullshitCheck` and `BullshitCheck-2`; every other experiment stays `ScienceRun`. (4) Sessions (`SetExperimentSession`, step 294; 001 §L 'Sessions and gain models as data … by hand'), the reference's six gain blocks (step 356): `LP-LP` for the eleven `lp_lp.csv` experiments, `LP-CPL` for the eleven `lp_cpl.csv` ones, `CPL-LP before the restart` for the `cpl_lp.csv` experiments whose captures all precede the earliest `BullshitCheck` capture (the laser restart that splits the CPL-LP gain block, 001 §1a; read from the data, not transcribed) and `CPL-LP after the restart` for the rest, `CPL-CPL day 1` and `CPL-CPL day 2` for the two `cpl_cpl` files' experiments; the darkness and diagnostic captures hold no session. (5) The LR correction, as data (001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact … with a mandatory audit note'): `CorrectSetup` (step 316) re-points `CPL-(LR#90)-CPL` to `CPL-(LR#-90)-CPL` and `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` to `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#-90)-CPL` (step 421), each with the note `LR was labelled +90 but physically sat at -90 (optics-mueller AGENTS.md, Current Known Caveats).`. The lab's caveat is the day-1 CPL-CPL dataset's; its `LR#45` runs were re-measured at +45 on day 2 (`CPL-(LR#45)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`; optics-mueller `notes/images_final_export_task.md:39-46`), so no `+45` run of the final data is re-pointed. The reference used +90 for these two runs; a Mueller rotation repeats every 180°, so −90° gives the same rotation and the reference values stay reproducible within `dataMatrixTol`. (6) The excluded frame, as data (001 §K 'exclusions carry a reason'): `ReviewExperimentData`, then `ExcludePoint` (step 315) of `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` at the `MappedPointNumber` of the point whose capture index is `MuellerReference.excludedPoints`' (17, at 140°; `BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs`, step 348), its place among the key's points in file order, with the reason `Likely contaminated frame; keep visible in plots but exclude from harmonic fits.` (`data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_glue.py:27`). (7) The fact `AT-1 attaches every lab group of the final data files through the Phone ROI CSV profile, with its role, session, correction and exclusion`: after the build, a second `KitProxy.create` of the built folder reads exactly the 53 experiments, in the files' group order, each over the setup its key reads to (the darkness and diagnostic captures over the setups named in (2), the two corrected ones over their −90° setups with one `SetupCorrection` from their labelled setup carrying the note), with the dial-sweep scan, the role and session above, and `dataOpt` the attachment of its lab file at `data/raw/final/<file>` (the committed file's SHA-256), profile `Phone ROI CSV`, `KeyedDataRows` of its key and no exclusion but the one point of `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`; each reads through the window's `experimentData` (`readMapped`, step 305) to its group's points, and `MappedPoints.keptBy` (step 314) of `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`'s keeps every point but the excluded one; and no file under `data/` is changed or added. The step-421 fact keeps its assertions.", "acceptance": "After AT-1's second part lands, the build MUST attach every group of the seven final lab files in place through the Phone ROI CSV profile to an experiment named by its key, with the specified roles, sessions, LR correction and excluded frame, touching no lab file; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `AT-1 attaches every lab group of the final data files through the Phone ROI CSV profile, with its role, session, correction and exclusion`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "kit-acceptance", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"kit-acceptance": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "kit-acceptance", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "kit-acceptance", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests.AT-1 attaches every lab group of the final data files through the Phone ROI CSV profile, with its role, session, correction and exclusion", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests", "discovery_gate": "kit-acceptance", "obligations": ["S121-AT1-DATA"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number": 425, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S121f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [424], "how_to": "A study's per-session gain models and its fit mode become semantic messages (001 §L 'per session the gain is free, anchored to its AIR runs, or interpolated between two AIR repeats'; 001 §L 'Fit modes: joint; staged'; 001 §P 'Every user step is a semantic message'). Today they are reachable only through `Study.withSessionGainModel` and `withFitMode` (step 365): no `StudyMsg` case (steps 366, 409) and no window message calls them, so a study cannot anchor its gains from the app, and the linear engine's anchored and interpolated gains (step 390) are out of the user's reach. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs`: (1) `StudyMsg` (steps 366, 409) gains `SetSessionGainModel of study : StudyName * setting : SessionGainSetting` and `SetFitMode of study : StudyName * mode : FitMode`, each documented in one line. `applyTo` finds the study by name as for its other cases (`UnknownStudyErr` naming it when the context lacks it) and answers `study.withSessionGainModel setting.session setting.model context.experiments` (its `UnknownStudySessionErr` and `GainAnchorOutsideSessionErr` refusals unchanged) or `study.withFitMode mode`. The window sends both through its existing `StudyCommand` (step 410), whose read-only guard and `recordStudy` apply unchanged, so no window case is added. (2) `type StudySession with member this.gainModelOffers (experiments : Experiment list) : SessionGainModel list`: the models the study view offers a session (step 426), over the kit's experiments: `FreeSessionGain`; `AnchoredSessionGain` of the session's `CalibrationRun` experiments in its order, when it holds one or more; and `InterpolatedSessionGain { opening = <the first of them>; closing = <the last> }`, when it holds two or more. The AIR runs of a session are its Calibration runs (001 §L 'anchored to its AIR runs'), so each offer satisfies `withSessionGainModel`'s session rule. No other type, member or setting is added; weights and enablement keep their members (step 365). (3) Tests. `StudyMessageTests` (steps 366, 409), over its folder kit: `setting a session's gain model and the study's fit mode are study messages, and a refused one records nothing`: `StudyCommand`'s Domain half, `SetSessionGainModel (S, { session = SessionName \"Day 1\"; model = AnchoredSessionGain [ E1 ] })` over a study whose `Day 1` holds E1 and E2, recorded through `recordStudy`, leaves the stored study's `gainModelOf (SessionName \"Day 1\")` that model, and `SetFitMode (S, StagedFit)` its `settings.mode` `StagedFit`; an unknown study, an unknown session and an anchor outside the session answer `UnknownStudyErr`, `UnknownStudySessionErr` and `GainAnchorOutsideSessionErr` and leave the stored study unchanged. `StudySessionTests` (steps 356, 357): `a session offers a free gain, a gain anchored to its AIR runs, and one interpolated between its first and last`: a session of E1 (Calibration), E2 (Science) and E3 (Calibration) offers `FreeSessionGain`, `AnchoredSessionGain [ E1; E3 ]` and `InterpolatedSessionGain { opening = E1; closing = E3 }`; one of E1 (Calibration) and E2 offers the first two; one without a Calibration run offers `FreeSessionGain` alone.", "acceptance": "After the messages land, `StudyMsg` MUST hold `SetSessionGainModel` and `SetFitMode`, applied through `withSessionGainModel` and `withFitMode` with their refusals, and `StudySession.gainModelOffers` MUST offer the free, anchored and interpolated models a session's Calibration runs allow; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `setting a session's gain model and the study's fit mode are study messages, and a refused one records nothing` and `a session offers a free gain, a gain anchored to its AIR runs, and one interpolated between its first and last`, the count rising by 2; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "kit-acceptance"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "kit-acceptance": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "kit-acceptance", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.setting a session's gain model and the study's fit mode are study messages, and a refused one records nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S121-STUDY-GAIN-MSG"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a session offers a free gain, a gain anchored to its AIR runs, and one interpolated between its first and last", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S121-STUDY-GAIN-MSG"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S121-STUDY-GAIN-MSG"], "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs"}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg.SetSessionGainModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S121-STUDY-GAIN-MSG"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg.SetFitMode", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S121-STUDY-GAIN-MSG"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg.applyTo", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S121-STUDY-GAIN-MSG"], "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs"}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudySession.gainModelOffers", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S121-STUDY-GAIN-MSG"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number":426,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S121g","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[425],"how_to":"The buttons for step 425's messages, in the study view's own files (001 §O 'Study view'; .spec-md §4 'New surfaces live in their own files'; AGENTS.md 'The button and the test send the same message'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) Ids: `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, beside the study view's fixed ids (step 414): `static member studySessionGrid : ConstructorUiId = ConstructorUiId \"StudySessionGrid\"`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, beside `studyParameterRow` (step 414): `studySessionGainChoice (session : SessionName)`, `StudySessionGain_<FileStem.ofText of the session's text>` (step 24's file-stem rule, as the other derived ids), and `studyFitModeChoice (mode : FitMode)`, `StudyFitMode_<mode.value>`, each documented in one line; and `type SessionGainModel with member this.caption : ControlCaption`: `Free`, `Anchored to <the anchors' names, comma-separated>` and `Interpolated from <opening> to <closing>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyUnknownsView.fs`, `studyUnknownsView` (step 414): after the unknowns grid, for the chosen study, the semi-bold `Sessions and gains:` and a `Grid` carrying `studySessionGrid`, three `Auto` columns `Session`, `Experiments` and `Gain`, a semi-bold header row and one row per `study.sessionsIn model.kitExperiments` (step 358): its name, its experiments' names comma-separated, and a `ComboBox` carrying `studySessionGainChoice session.name` over `session.gainModelOffers model.kitExperiments` (step 425) by `caption`, `study.gainModelOf session.name` selected, enabled while `model.kitWrites` offers writes (step 185), whose choice sends `StudyCommand (SetSessionGainModel (study.name, { session = session.name; model = <the chosen> }))`. A study of no session shows `This study's experiments form no session.`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitView.fs`, `studyFitView` (step 415): directly before the Run row, `Fit mode:` and one box per `FitMode.all` carrying `studyFitModeChoice mode` with `mode.text`, the study's `settings.mode` an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` and the other a `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (step 241's chosen-option look), each sending `StudyCommand (SetFitMode (study.name, mode))`, shown only while writes are offered; under a read-only kit the line `Fit mode: <its text>`. The Run buttons are unchanged: the stage they send decides what a run fits, and the mode is what the study and its fit runs record (step 391). No other control changes. (4) Tests, mounted as `StudyViewTests` mounts its screens (step 414) over `TestAppScope.studyKitIn` with E1 and E3 set to `CalibrationRun` by `SetExperimentRole`: `each session of the study offers its gain models, and choosing one sends SetSessionGainModel`: the Unknowns step's `StudySessionGrid` holds `Session 1` with `E1, E2, E3` and a `StudySessionGain_Session 1` box offering `Free`, `Anchored to E1, E3` and `Interpolated from E1 to E3`, `Free` selected; choosing the anchored one dispatches `StudyCommand (SetSessionGainModel (QZ-LR, { session = SessionName \"Session 1\"; model = AnchoredSessionGain [ E1; E3 ] }))`; `the Fit step's mode choice sends SetFitMode`: the Fit step shows `StudyFitMode_1` chosen and pressing `StudyFitMode_2` dispatches `StudyCommand (SetFitMode (QZ-LR, StagedFit))`; `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also checks `studySessionGrid`, `studySessionGainChoice (SessionName \"Session 1\")` and `studyFitModeChoice StagedFit`; `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable` also reaches the sessions grid; and `KitWindowTests`' `a read-only window withholds every write control` also finds the gain box disabled and no `StudyFitMode_<n>` box.","acceptance":"After the view lands, the Unknowns step MUST list the study's sessions with a gain choice sending `SetSessionGainModel`, and the Fit step MUST offer the fit mode sending `SetFitMode`, both withheld from a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `each session of the study offers its gain models, and choosing one sends SetSessionGainModel`, `the Fit step's mode choice sends SetFitMode` and the widened `the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 2; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests","kit-acceptance"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"]},"kit-acceptance":{"mode":"selected","suite":"kit-acceptance","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyUnknownsView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitView.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.each session of the study offers its gain models, and choosing one sends SetSessionGainModel","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.the Fit step's mode choice sends SetFitMode","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","discovery_gate":"ui-tests","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests.the study view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/StudyViewTests.fs","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Unknowns step leaves everything reachable","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"op":"change_expectation","suite":"ui-tests","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]}],"contracts":[{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.studySessionGrid","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.studySessionGainChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.studyFitModeChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.SessionGainModel.caption","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyUnknownsView.studyUnknownsView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.StudyFitView.studyFitView","op":"change_behavior","obligations":["S121-STUDY-GAIN-VIEW"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number":427,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S121h","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[426],"how_to":"AT-1's build ends with its staged study (001 §Q AT-1 'Study: staged (stage 1 AIR calibration → publish → stage 2 objects)'; 001 §L). The engines are the existing ones: stage 1 is the linear calibration over the LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP AIR runs and the dark runs (steps 386, 389), stage 2 the linear object reconstruction behind the published instruments (step 390), so the numbers are the reference pipeline's (steps 349-352). `buildOpticsMuellerKit` continues, through the window's messages alone. (1) `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (StudyName \"QZ-LR\", <the kit's 53 experiments in kit order>))` (steps 366, 410), then `StudyCommand (SetFitMode (QZ-LR, StagedFit))` and, per session, `StudyCommand (SetSessionGainModel (QZ-LR, ...))` (step 425): `LP-LP` `AnchoredSessionGain [ LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2; LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R ]`, `LP-CPL` `[ LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2; LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R ]`, `CPL-LP before the restart` `[ CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2 ]`, `CPL-LP after the restart` `[ CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R ]`, `CPL-CPL day 1` `InterpolatedSessionGain { opening = CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL; closing = CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR }` and `CPL-CPL day 2` `AnchoredSessionGain [ CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2 ]`: the reference's six gain rules (step 356), each one of its session's `gainModelOffers`. A session uses every dark run, because none holds its own (step 357). (2) The fits run through the window's own host contract: the model's `kitShell.studyFits` (step 412) is `StudyFitJobHost.posting` whose `post` runs its job at once, recording `StudyFit (StudyFitProgressed _)` and `StudyFit (StudyFitEnded _)`, as `StudyWindowModelTests` drives a fit (step 412); the build waits for the end on a `ManualResetEventSlim` within sixty seconds, never by a sleep, then passes the recorded messages through the update in order, so `StudyFitEnded (Ok run)` writes the fit run. The test clock moves to 2026-05-31T12:01:00Z, then `StudyFit (RunFit { study = QZ-LR; stage = CalibrationStage; calibrationUse = CalibrationHeldFixed })` writes `QZ-LR@20260531T120100Z.fitrun-json`; `PublishCalibration (FitRunName \"QZ-LR@20260531T120100Z\")` (step 413) writes `LP2`, `CPL1` and `CPL2` at revision 2; the clock moves to 2026-05-31T12:02:00Z, then `RunFit` of `ObjectStage` with `CalibrationHeldFixed` writes `QZ-LR@20260531T120200Z.fitrun-json`. (3) The reference comparison, two private functions of the module that step 429 calls too, each assertion's message naming the quantity and both values: `assertReferenceInstruments (items : Item list)`: the `CalibratedParameter` values (step 214) of `LP2`'s `dialZero`, `CPL2`'s `dialZero` and `c2.retardance`, and `CPL1`'s `c2.retardance` and `c2.fastAxisOffset`, each read as an angle in degrees (`ParameterValue.angle`, step 258), are within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` (`BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs`, step 348) of `lpAnalyzerZero`, `cplAnalyzerZero`, `cplAnalyzerRetardance`, `cplSourceRetardance` and `cplSourceAxisOffset` less 45° (the stage-1 hand-off, step 389), each in degrees. `assertReferenceObjects (run : FitRun)`: its `objectMatrices` (step 383) hold the groups `[ QZ ]`, `[ LR ]` and `[ QZ; LR ]`, whose sixteen elements (m00…m33, row-major) are each within `dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.qzMatrix`, `lrMatrix` and `combinedMatrix`, and its one product check's `rmseRatio` (`results.productChecks`, steps 396, 400) is within `dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.productCheckRmseRatio`. The expectations are the shared module's literals, so the test reads no file for them (spec 0044 §8.5). (4) The fact `AT-1's staged study calibrates the instruments on the AIR runs, publishes them and reconstructs QZ, LR and QZ then LR as the reference does`: after the build, a second `KitProxy.create` of the built folder reads `QZ-LR.study-json` holding the 53 experiments, `StagedFit` and the six gain settings; `readFitRuns` (step 384) the two runs in stamp order, the first `CalibrationStage` of `LinearStudyEngine` whose five entries are the five instrument unknowns, the second `ObjectStage` of `LinearStudyEngine` with `CalibrationHeldFixed`; `readItems` `LP2`, `CPL1` and `CPL2` at revision 2, each of the five values the first run's fitted one with its σ and that run's name, and every other item at revision 1; and `assertReferenceInstruments` of the read items and `assertReferenceObjects` of the second run hold. The step-421 and step-424 facts keep their assertions.","acceptance":"After AT-1's third part lands, the build MUST create the staged study through the window's messages, run stage 1, publish it and run stage 2 into two append-only fit runs, and the published instruments and the stage-2 matrices and product check MUST be within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of the reference; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `AT-1's staged study calibrates the instruments on the AIR runs, publishes them and reconstructs QZ, LR and QZ then LR as the reference does`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","kit-acceptance","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"kit-acceptance":{"mode":"selected","suite":"kit-acceptance","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"kit-acceptance","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests.AT-1's staged study calibrates the instruments on the AIR runs, publishes them and reconstructs QZ, LR and QZ then LR as the reference does","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests","discovery_gate":"kit-acceptance","obligations":["S121-AT1-STUDY"]}],"contracts":[],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S12.1 -- AT-1 and the optics-mueller reference kit"}
{"number":428,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-S121i","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[427],"how_to":"The reference kit is committed as AT-1's build writes it, once, and never by hand (001 §Q 'Section 12 creates them by running the build below once, through the app's own folder `KitProxy`, and commits the result. They are never hand-written'; 001 §1 'complete kit folders … `library/` and the raw lab files under `data/`'; .spec-md §3.13). (1) The fact `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file` in `KitAcceptanceTests`: it builds the kit (`buildOpticsMuellerKit`, steps 421-427) into a fresh run folder and compares it with the committed kit (`CommittedKit.OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, .spec-md §3.21): the two folders' relative file paths, `.oc/` left out of both, are the same set, and each file's bytes are equal: every kit file at the root, every file under `library/` and every file under `data/` (001 §Q 'every kit file and every file under `data/` and `library/`; `.oc/` excluded'). A difference fails naming the built folder's absolute path, the first differing relative path and why (missing, extra or different bytes). It reads the committed kit and writes nothing there (.spec-md §4 'Tests' data'). (2) The committed kit, created by this step once: run the fact (`kit-acceptance`, filtered to it); it fails, because `data/optics-mueller/` holds the lab files alone (step 330), and names its built folder; copy every file of that folder except those under `data/` (the committed lab files, equal by the step-421 fact) and under `.oc/` into `data/optics-mueller/`, keeping their relative paths and bytes; run the fact again, and it passes. The files are the kit file, the nine `<label>.item-json`, the forty-two `<setup>.setup-json`, the fifty-three `<experiment>.experiment-json`, `QZ-LR.study-json`, the two `QZ-LR@<stamp>.fitrun-json` and `library/`'s snapshots of the built-in entries the kit references, each `library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json` named by a GUID the built-in catalogue froze (steps 20, 35, 209), all canonical JSON with LF line endings, which `.gitattributes`' `* text=auto eol=lf` keeps byte-identical; `git check-ignore` matches none of them, and `/data/*/.oc/` stays ignored (.spec-md §10.6). Nothing under `data/optics-mueller/data/` changes. (3) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha on `data/` (the last bullet of 'Gotchas'), one bullet of at most four lines: **The reference kits are AT-1's and AT-2's output, never hand-edited** (`KitAcceptanceTests.fs`, spec 0050 S12): `data/optics-mueller/` is exactly what the AT-1 build writes, `.oc/` aside; a change to what the build writes (a kit-file shape, a snapshotted catalogue entry, the build's messages) re-runs `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file` and re-commits the kit files it names in the same step. Nothing else in the file changes.","acceptance":"After the kit is committed, `data/optics-mueller/` MUST hold, beside its unchanged lab files, exactly the kit files and library snapshots AT-1's build writes, and `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file` MUST pass; AGENTS.md MUST carry the reference-kit gotcha; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `the built optics-mueller kit equals the committed kit file by file`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","kit-acceptance","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"kit-acceptance":{"mode":"selected","suite":"kit-acceptance","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs","AGENTS.md","data/opti