":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.planBoundsGrid","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.planInstrumentList","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs","obligations":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.planMaterialChoice","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs","obligations":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.PlanView.planView","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/PlanView.fs","obligations":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView.kitWindowView","op":"change_behavior","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs","obligations":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestAppScope.planKitOver","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs","obligations":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]},{"symbol":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestAppScope.planKitIn","op":"create","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs","obligations":["S142-PLAN-VIEW"]}],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S14.2 -- The Planner's numerical layer, the plan, the cache and the Plan view"}
{"number": 491, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S142p", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [490], "how_to": "The Plan view's ranked candidates, each with 'Add to kit' (001 §O 'Plan view: … and the ranked candidates, with \"Add to kit\"'; the S14.2 brief). The view shows what the report holds and computes nothing but each candidate's place in the kit now, so a candidate added since the plan ran shows as added with no new run (.spec-md §10.4). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Plan step's group: `planCandidateList` (`\"PlanCandidateList\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `planCandidateRow (candidate : PlanCandidate)` and `addPlanCandidateButton (candidate : PlanCandidate)` are `PlanCandidate_` and `AddPlanCandidate_` followed by `<the plate item's GUID>_<t or r>_<the wavelength in nm, one decimal, invariant culture>`, one private helper writing that key. (2) `PlanView.fs` (step 490): after the report's instrument lines, `Next experiments, in the order the plan adds them:` and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `planCandidateList`: per ranked step, in order, a row carrying `planCandidateRow` reading `<k>. <the candidate's caption> — rank <r>`, then under `DeterminantPlanCriterion` `, log det <the information's logDeterminant, three decimals>` and under `TargetTracePlanCriterion` `, Σσ² <traceOpt, G4>` when it has one, then `; σ: <each bound as name value, G3, joined by \", \">` when its bounds exist; and, at its end, while writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185) and its `coverageIn model.kitSetups model.experimentCollection.experiments` (step 482) is `CandidateNotInKit`, `Add to kit` (`addPlanCandidateButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, sending `AddPlannedExperiment candidate`, step 489), or, when it is `CandidateInKit name`, the text `In the kit as <name>.`; before them, one line per report `inKit` candidate, `Already in the kit: <its caption>.`; with no ranked step, `No candidate is open: every candidate is in the kit, or the kit has no Mueller polarimeter or placed plate.`. Tests, in `PlanViewTests` (step 490), over `planKitIn` with a plan run through the posting host: without a trait, `the Plan step ranks the candidates and offers Add to kit for each the kit does not hold`: `planCandidateList` holds QZ-Z's two candidates' `planCandidateRow`s, the first reading `1. QZ-Z (z-cut plate), ` and `rank`, each with its `addPlanCandidateButton`, and over the kit opened read-only no `addPlanCandidateButton`; `the plan view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `PlanCandidateList` and the two derived ids of a test-local candidate. With trait `ui-smoke`: `pressing Add to kit records a planned experiment of the candidate in the kit`: pressing the transmitted candidate's `addPlanCandidateButton` leaves the kit's folder holding one more `.setup-json` and one `.experiment-json` whose role is `PlannedRun`, and that row then reading `In the kit as ` with no `addPlanCandidateButton`. `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit window's Plan step leaves everything reachable` (step 490) now reaches the candidate rows too. `KitWindowTests`' `a read-only window withholds every write control` finds no `addPlanCandidateButton` over the read-only model.", "acceptance": "After the candidates show, `planView` MUST list the report's ranked candidates in order with their rank, criterion measure and bounds, offer Add to kit for each the kit does not hold while writes are offered, and show an added one as in the kit; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Add to kit records a planned experiment of the candidate in the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Plan step ranks the candidates and offers Add to kit for each the kit does not hold`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the plan view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the kit window's Plan step leaves everything reachable` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/PlanView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/PlanViewTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests.the Plan step ranks the candidates and offers Add to kit for each the kit does not hold", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/PlanViewTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests.pressing Add to kit records a planned experiment of the candidate in the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/PlanViewTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests.the plan view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/PlanViewTests.fs", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Plan step leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.planCandidateList", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.planCandidateRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.addPlanCandidateButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.PlanView.planView", "op": "change_behavior", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/PlanView.fs", "obligations": ["S142-PLAN-CANDIDATES-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S14.2 -- The Planner's numerical layer, the plan, the cache and the Plan view"}
{"number":492,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-S142q","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[491],"how_to":"The constructor windows compose the real plan host, and the Plan step is proved end to end through a shown window and a real kit folder (001 §M 'Workflow: kit; planner report and plan; measure; attach; fit'; 001 §P `RunPlan`; .spec-md §0.1 `Program.fs`; AGENTS.md: wait for deterministic conditions, drive by id). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`, `ConstructorScene.mount` (steps 189, 233, 312, 419): the shell it builds gains `planRuns = PlanJobHost.onUiThread (fun p -> dispatch (StudyPlan (PlanProgressed p))) (fun r -> dispatch (StudyPlan (PlanEnded r)))` (steps 487, 488), over the dispatch the mount captures from its init command, so a plan runs on a thread-pool worker and its progress and end arrive on the window's own thread. The docs of `MainConstructorWindow` and `InverseConstructorWindow` say, in no more words, that the Inverse window's Plan step runs off the UI thread too. No other seam changes. (2) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha **The Inverse flow ends at the study** (step 419): `Unknowns → Fit → Results → Publish after Data (S14 inserts Plan before Fit)` becomes `Unknowns → Plan → Fit → Results → Publish after Data`, and it gains one sentence, the bullet staying within six lines: Plan runs the Measurement Planner (`MeasurementPlanner.fs`, `PlannerInformation.fs`, `PlannerRuns.fs`, spec 0050 S14) on `JobRunner`, caches each candidate's Jacobian under `.oc/planner/` (derived, safe to delete, never sent, never written by a read-only open), and Add to kit writes `PlannedRun` experiments. Nothing else in the file changes. (3) Tests. `KitWindowTests` gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: the Inverse constructor plans a kit's next experiments off the UI thread and caches them under .oc/planner`: a shown `InverseConstructorWindow`, composed as step 419's acceptance fact composes it, over the app context `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName \"KitWindowTests\")` and the kit `TestAppScope.planKitOver` builds with that context (step 490): its model's kit closed (`close`, step 131) and its folder (`kitFolderOpt`, step 184) opened again through `KitOpening.openKitAt` over that context, so the library holds every snapshot and no import dialog opens; driven by id at the controls' centres, pressing `studyChoice` of `QZ`, `flowPlanStep` and `planRunButton`, and waiting through `Dispatcher.UIThread.RunJobs` until `planRankText` shows text, within thirty seconds and never by a sleep, leaves the kit's folder holding exactly two `.oc/planner/*.candidate-json` files and `planCandidateList` holding QZ-Z's two `planCandidateRow`s: the plan ran through the real host on a worker, its candidates went through the kit's cache, and its end was posted back to the window. The windows' other consumers keep their assertions.","acceptance":"After the windows are wired, a constructor window's shell MUST hold `PlanJobHost.onUiThread` over the window's dispatch, a plan run in a real Inverse window MUST run off the UI thread, cache its candidates under `.oc/planner/` and show its report and ranked candidates in the Plan step, and AGENTS.md's gotcha 'The Inverse flow ends at the study' MUST list Plan before Fit and name the Planner's cache; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Inverse constructor plans a kit's next experiments off the UI thread and caches them under .oc/planner`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"selected","suite":"ui-tests","values":["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","AGENTS.md","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: the Inverse constructor plans a kit's next experiments off the UI thread and caches them under .oc/planner","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["S142-WIRE"]}],"contracts":[],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"S14.2 -- The Planner's numerical layer, the plan, the cache and the Plan view"}
{"number": 493, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-Ca", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [439, 492], "how_to": "The committed kits open read-only through one shared fixture, so the closing composition test (step 494) opens them through the code AT-1 and AT-2 already use (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a reuse is a move, the old body deleted in the same step; .spec-md §3.12 'A read-only open writes nothing', §3.21; 001 §V 'open in the app from the start screen'). `KitAcceptanceTests.fs` (appended by step 421) compiles after `WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj:233`), so the composition test cannot call a function of it. (1) `openCommittedReadOnly` and `assertCommittedUnchanged` (step 439) MOVE from `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs` into `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs` (steps 83, 152, 154, 421, 429), after `inverseModelOver`, public, together with the recording's type and every private helper that only they call. Their bodies are unchanged but for one parameter: `openCommittedReadOnly (owner : FolderName) (kit : CommittedKit)` composes over `emptyLibraryAppContext owner` in place of the literal `FolderName \"KitAcceptanceTests\"`, because every `TestAppScope` helper takes the calling class's folder (step 83). A private helper that the AT-1 or AT-2 build also calls moves with them, and the builds call it from `TestAppScope`, so the start screen is composed in one place. `TestAppScope` opens `BerremanTestSupport` for `CommittedKit` (`BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs`, steps 330, 344, 431). Each moved declaration's doc is one line citing spec 0050 Close. (2) `KitAcceptanceTests`: the facts of steps 429 and 439 call `TestAppScope.openCommittedReadOnly (FolderName \"KitAcceptanceTests\")` and `TestAppScope.assertCommittedUnchanged`, every assertion kept, and the module declares neither function any more. No product file, other test class or fact changes, and no fact, retry or cache is added.", "acceptance": "After the read-only open moves, `TestAppScope` MUST declare the one `openCommittedReadOnly` (taking the calling class's folder) and `assertCommittedUnchanged`, and `KitAcceptanceTests` MUST call them and declare neither; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only against an empty library, writes nothing, and its study reproduces the reference reconstruction` and `the committed absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit opens read-only against an empty library, writes nothing, and reproduces AT-2's data, model and fit`, the count unchanged; ui-smoke MUST pass, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s47 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "kit-acceptance", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "kit-acceptance": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "kit-acceptance", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitStartWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.StudyViewTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitAcceptanceTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "Close -- the composition root and the whole-tree proof"}
{"number":494,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-Cb","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[493],"how_to":"The composition root is closed and the whole tree proves 001 §V (001 §V 'Done when'; 001 §R; 001 §F, §G, §O; the Close brief; .spec-md §0, §3.9, §3.10, §3.12, §9 'Done when'; AGENTS.md: a comment says why in one to three lines; drive by id and wait for deterministic conditions). When this step starts, `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs` and `AppContext.create` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`) already compose everything 001 asks of the root, each wired by the step that introduced it: the SQLite library over the configured `DataLocations` (`Program.fs:Startup`, `AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings`, steps 83, 88, 89), the catalogue import on every start (step 100), the start screen behind Main and Inverse (steps 180, 191, 232), the kit window with the flow-strip steps of its mode (steps 189, 242, 323, 414-419, 490-492) and the Data locations window behind the Launcher's footer link (step 195). This step changes no code in those two files: it rewrites their stale docs, updates AGENTS.md, and proves the composition end to end. (1) Docs, each citing spec 0050 Close. `Program.fs`: the first paragraph of the file doc (`Program.fs:1-6`, spec 0038's launcher narrative) becomes at most four lines: the root reads the settings and the locations once (`Startup`), composes `AppContext.create` over them, and shows `LauncherWindow`, whose Main and Inverse open `KitStartWindow` and whose footer opens `DataLocationsWindow`; a chosen kit opens the constructor window of its mode (`KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn`), which runs the kit window. The file doc's second paragraph (`Program.fs:8-12`, the FuncUI clone) is unchanged. The docs of `Startup.workbenchSettings` and `Startup.context` (`Program.fs:37-47` and `:50-58` today, edited by steps 83 and 88) become one to three lines each: the settings and `DataLocations` that `appsettings.json` gives, read once; and the one app scope `AppContext.create` answers over them, an open failure shown by the launcher (step 88). `AppContext.fs`: its file doc (`AppContext.fs:1-9`, spec 0038's in-memory narrative) becomes one to three lines: the one app scope, composed at the root over the configured locations (the SQLite library stores and the catalogue import of every start) and injected into the launcher, the start screen and every window. Any other doc in the two files that still says in-memory store, re-seed, experiment collection, scene store or a `STORE_XDUO_*` seam this spec deleted is cut to the words that stay true. (2) `AGENTS.md`, wherever this spec changed a fact it states; nothing else in the file changes. (a) `## Build & test`: the sentence `No test, fixture or kit lives under Documents; test kits and databases go under the test run's output directory.` (`AGENTS.md:60-61`) becomes: no test, fixture, kit or database lives under `Documents`, `%APPDATA%` or `%LOCALAPPDATA%`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`' own `appsettings.json` (step 82) and `TestAppScope` (`testLocations`, `fileLocations`) put every location, the SQLite library (`:memory:` or a file) included, under the test run's output directory, and the committed kits under `data/` are opened read-only (spec 0050 §3.9, §3.12). (b) `## Project layout` (`AGENTS.md:142-159`), in the block's column layout: `OpticalConstructor.Domain`'s note `project model` becomes `library entries, kits, setups, experiments, studies, planner`; `OpticalConstructor.Storage`'s note `project files, JSON (de)serialization, schema validation, export` becomes `kit folders, entry and catalogue files, canonical JSON, schema validation, SQLite library proxies, export`; and four lines are added: `BerremanTestSupport/` after `BerremanTests/` (shared test ground truth: crystal samples, designs, the committed-kit locator), `Catalogue/Builtin/` first under `OpticalConstructor/` (the shipped built-in library catalogue, as entry files), `OpticalConstructor.Database` after `OpticalConstructor.Storage` (the C# EF Core library model: SQLite, `EnsureCreated` plus a schema stamp) and `data/` after `Elevation/` (the committed reference experiment kits, read-only to tests). (c) `## Gotchas`, directly after 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE' (as steps 58 and 100 left it), three bullets of at most six lines each. **The library is data, not code** (spec 0050 S1-S3): every material, sample, source, polarizer, detector, item model and category is a versioned entry file (`<name>.material-json` and so on: canonical JSON with its SHA-256, `LibraryEntryEnvelope`) held in the SQLite library database (`library.db`, the `OpticalConstructorSqlite` connection string; EF Core `EnsureCreated` plus a schema stamp, never a migration); the built-ins ship as `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/`, imported with every registered catalogue folder on every start by manifest hash (`CatalogueImportContext.importOnStart`); code names a built-in only by its frozen GUID (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`, `ItemModelIds`) and holds no seed value; a library of another schema is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr`, which the Launcher remedies with Recreate library from catalogues. **Everything else lives in a kit folder** (`Kit.fs`, `KitOpening.fs`, spec 0050 S4-S12): a folder holding `.kit-json`, its root flat (`<label>.item-json`, `<name>.setup-json`, `<name>.experiment-json`, `<study>.study-json`, append-only `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json`) with three subfolders: `library/` (a snapshot of every library version the kit uses, so it opens on any machine), `data/` (lab files the app only reads, referenced by relative path and SHA-256) and `.oc/` (the lock and the Planner's derived cache, never sent); logic reaches it only through `KitProxy` (`KitProxy.create (folder : KitFolder)`) in a `KitContext`; every write is atomic (`*.tmp`, then replace), a read-only open writes nothing, and a file of another schema version is `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`. **Main and Inverse open the kit start screen** (`KitStartView.fs`, `KitStartWindow.fs`, spec 0050 S5-S6): New kit… (an empty folder is initialised, a folder with files keeps them), Open kit…, Open kit from zip… and the history (`KitHistoryProxy` in the per-user preferences, at most `KitHistoryLimit`, starred first); a chosen kit opens the constructor of that mode, one window per kit, titled by the kit and its folder; Materials and Library need no kit; the Launcher's footer link opens Data locations, every `DataLocations` path, each overridable in `appsettings.json`. (d) 'Main ribbon' (as step 328 left it) gains one sentence: the kit window's left flow strip (`FlowStripView.fs`, `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf`) reaches Items, Setups and Experiments, the last being this bay, in both constructors, and Data, Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results and Publish in the Inverse one alone. (3) Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`, whose module doc gains one to three lines citing spec 0050 Close naming the two proofs below. Each new fact runs on `HeadlessSession.run`, finds a control by its `Name` or `AutomationId`, presses a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:69` (`clickOn`) does, observes the windows a click opens through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent` as `LauncherTests.fs:58` (`clickAndObserve`) does, waits only through `Dispatcher.UIThread.RunJobs`, never a sleep, and closes every window it opened, so no `WindowRegistry` key outlives it. With trait `ui-smoke`: (a) `acceptance: the composed app goes from the Launcher through the start screen to a kit under the test output and shows every flow-strip step of its mode`: over `locations = TestAppScope.fileLocations (FolderName \"WireUiFinalCompositionTests\")` (step 88: a SQLite library file under the test output, the build-copied `Catalogue/Builtin` as the shipped catalogue), `AppContext.create locations WorkbenchSettings.defaults` answers `Ok ctx`, composed as `Program.fs:Startup` composes the app, an `Error` failing the fact with its `describe`; the file `LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf locations.libraryConnection` names exists and `ctx.materials.tryGetMaterial MaterialIds.silicon` answers Silicon, so the start-up import ran into the database. With `kit = TestAppScope.freshKitFolder (FolderName \"WireUiFinalCompositionTests\")` (step 152), a shown `LauncherWindow(locations, WorkbenchSettings.defaults, Ok ctx, fun _ -> TestAppScope.kitPickerOf kit)` (steps 89, 154): raising `Click` on `openInverseButton` opens exactly one `KitStartWindow`, titled `Open a kit — Inverse`; pressing its `newKitButton` opens exactly one `InverseConstructorWindow`, closes the start screen, leaves `.kit-json` and `.oc/lock` in `kit` and makes `kit` the first entry of `ctx.kitHistory.readHistory ()`; the window's title ends with ` — Optical Constructor — Inverse`; its flow strip holds one box per step of `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf InverseConstructor`, and pressing each, in order, shows its surface: `itemsPanel` (Items), `tableElementCanvas` (Setups), the Experiments bay's pane `ConstructorUiId.ribbonPane` of its key (Experiments), `dataStepPanel` (Data), `studyUnknownsPanel` (Unknowns), `planPanel` (Plan), `studyFitPanel` (Fit), `studyResultsPanel` (Results) and `studyPublishPanel` (Publish) (steps 242, 323, 414-418, 490); pressing `kitCloseButton` closes the window and leaves no `.oc/lock` in `kit`. Raising `Click` on `openMainButton` then opens exactly one `KitStartWindow` titled `Open a kit — Main`; pressing its `openKitButton` opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow` over the same kit, whose flow strip holds `flowItemsStep`, `flowSetupsStep` and `flowExperimentsStep` and none of `flowDataStep`, `flowUnknownsStep`, `flowPlanStep`, `flowFitStep`, `flowResultsStep` and `flowPublishStep` (`stepsOf ForwardConstructor`), each of the three showing its surface when pressed; `kitCloseButton` closes it and leaves no `.oc/lock`. Raising `Click` on `launcherDataLocationsLink` opens exactly one `DataLocationsWindow`, whose `dataLocationPathText LibraryDatabaseLocation` reads the library file's full path and whose `dataLocationPathText KitsLocation` reads `locations.kitsFolder`'s text (steps 192, 193); it and the launcher are then closed. (b) `acceptance: the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing` and (c) `acceptance: the committed absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing`, over `OpticsMuellerKit` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyKit` through one private function of the class: `TestAppScope.openCommittedReadOnly (FolderName \"WireUiFinalCompositionTests\") kit` (step 493: a start screen sending `OpenKitReadOnly` of the committed folder, against an empty library) answers the context, the Inverse window model and the recording; the model is mounted as `KitWindowTests` mounts its screens (step 312: `kitWindowView` over the model, dispatching through `updateTableAndElementRotation`, its shell `KitWindowShell.inert`) and shown; `kitCaptionText` contains ` (read-only)` (step 184); pressing each box of `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf InverseConstructor` shows the surface (a) names; then the window is closed, the kit is closed as `KitAcceptanceTests` closes it, and `TestAppScope.assertCommittedUnchanged` of the kit and the recording holds, so nothing was written under `data/`. The class's earlier facts keep their names and assertions. (4) The whole-tree proof (001 §V), by the gates this step runs whole: AT-1 and AT-2, the two committed kits equal to their builds and their read-only runs under kit-acceptance (`KitAcceptanceTests`, steps 421-440); the Planner's §M facts (`MeasurementPlannerTests`, steps 475, 481) and BerremanTests' unchanged numbers under unit-tests; the library in the database and the kit's files in its folder under (3)(a); zero warnings from our code and an empty `Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json` under build, elevation and elevation-full. The 001 §R removals are confirmed by `git grep -n -i -F \"ocproj\" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -F -e SceneProxy -e ExperimentCollectionProxy -e recent.json -e seedAll -e TestDbContext -e SolverHandoffView -e MuellerDataSet -e MuellerDataProxy -e Data/MuellerMatrix -e experimentRegex -e measuredElementOf -- Berreman/`, each finding nothing: the steps that removed them (S1.6, S2.1, steps 152, 161, 169, 254, 270, 330-331 and 416) deleted every mention, and the section invariants have held each name out since. No retry, sleep, timer, product seam or project-file comment is added.","acceptance":"After the root is closed, `Program.fs` and `AppContext.create` MUST compose the SQLite library over `DataLocations`, the catalogue import of every start, the start screen behind Main and Inverse, the kit window with its mode's flow-strip steps and the Data locations window, and their docs MUST say so; AGENTS.md MUST state the library database, kit folders and their layout, the start screen, the flow strip and the test locations; the composed app MUST go from the Launcher through the start screen to a kit under the test output and show every flow-strip step of each mode, and each committed kit MUST open read-only from the start screen and leave `data/` unchanged; `git grep -n -i -F \"ocproj\" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -F -e SceneProxy -e ExperimentCollectionProxy -e recent.json -e seedAll -e TestDbContext -e SolverHandoffView -e MuellerDataSet -e MuellerDataProxy -e Data/MuellerMatrix -e experimentRegex -e measuredElementOf -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; build MUST pass with zero warnings from our code; elevation and elevation-full MUST pass with `Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json` listing no finding; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass whole; ui-smoke MUST pass whole, including `acceptance: the composed app goes from the Launcher through the start screen to a kit under the test output and shows every flow-strip step of its mode`, `acceptance: the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing` and `acceptance: the committed absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing`, the count rising by 3; ui-tests MUST pass whole; unit-tests MUST pass whole with BerremanTests' numbers unchanged; kit-acceptance MUST pass whole; and the twenty-one s47 invariants MUST pass.","required_gates":["build","elevation","elevation-full","constructor-unit-tests","ui-smoke","ui-tests","unit-tests","kit-acceptance"],"gate_selection":{"constructor-unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"constructor-unit-tests"},"ui-smoke":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-smoke"},"ui-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"ui-tests"},"unit-tests":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"unit-tests"},"kit-acceptance":{"mode":"all_discovered","suite":"kit-acceptance"}},"effects":{"edits":["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs","AGENTS.md","Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs"],"tests":[{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests.acceptance: the composed app goes from the Launcher through the start screen to a kit under the test output and shows every flow-strip step of its mode","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["CLOSE-WIRE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests.acceptance: the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["CLOSE-WIRE"]},{"op":"create","suite":"ui-smoke","id":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests.acceptance: the committed absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing","path":"Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs","class":"OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests","discovery_gate":"ui-smoke","obligations":["CLOSE-WIRE"]}],"contracts":[],"packages":[],"checks":[]},"section":"Close -- the composition root and the whole-tree proof"}
